7 until July 13, 2010 of the ROSETTA orbiter magnetometerRPCMAG. The closest approach (CA) took place on July 10, 2010 at 15:45.The current version of the dataset is V9.0.The difference to the datasets of earlier versions is mainly a significantlyimproved sensor temperature model, more detailed documentation about magneticdisturbance sources, more data handling information for the user andalso an improved quality flagging system.','public','2026-03-13T16:53:35.545240','2026-03-13T16:53:35.545245','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','2c2f30de-8e54-4fc1-9576-fbdb18e18c7b','NASA Data.json','6a8b4cbb584ba0e6f6f925c1d10c0b334c913f9af35648f605386a1660380930','1.1','2026-03-13T16:53:35.545240','2026-03-13T16:53:35.545245','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('0e7f0efe-d0c7-46f9-af8f-aa5dea86014a','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 3 0896 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 3 phase 2015-07-01 to 2015-10-21. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-07-14T11:02:05.000 to 2015-07-14T14:20:12.000.','public','2026-03-13T16:51:19.142817','2026-03-13T16:51:19.142823','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','0c3e4ea2-5fc3-486b-9c8b-ee513063083c','NASA Data.json','ba5a84c29a845012c8dba5b125cceaf2b23f57fced15554157a04e037ad1a55e','1.1','2026-03-13T16:51:19.142817','2026-03-13T16:51:19.142823','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('0ea50165-5abb-4311-8ee0-0f54f0c2d4f4','NRC 834','Employee Reporting of Inappropriate Conduct Addressing Allegations of Retaliation for Raising Safety Concerns. Fillable form in Adobe Portable Document Format (PDF) with information submitted by NRC stakeholder - licensee, applicant, or NRC employee/contractor.','non-public','2026-03-20T19:43:21.976594','2026-03-20T19:43:21.976603','Nuclear Regulatory Commission','Jenna Saucerman','429:00','13bc4c95-14ad-44c5-b86a-3a0b60bfd7a2','NRC Data.json Harvest Source','4994793d22e42d352b88a939a