). This version V1.0 is the first version of this dataset: Lien corrected dataset after October 2018 PSA/PDS external peer review.','public','2026-03-13T17:35:43.007038','2026-03-13T17:35:43.007044','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','fe96c4b7-8f07-45c7-8452-1aa04a81ce00','NASA Data.json','f9d703396bc90aa385abcace4cf0f05980b0026fcbdfd568968bd785367d727d','1.1','2026-03-13T17:35:43.007038','2026-03-13T17:35:43.007044','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('19ef88d8-a2d7-44ca-a1f1-63dd8c79ccec','MARS EXPRESS SUN MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 5 3787 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2015-01-01 to 2016-12-31. It is a Solar Conjunction measurement and covers the time 2015-07-05T15:13:01 to 2015-07-05T17:34:00.','public','2026-03-13T18:15:04.047734','2026-03-13T18:15:04.047740','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','b6627e25-d28e-4ff7-99a3-5358f83c6674','NASA Data.json','cfd02aa72eb17fb37d67d0e0a15265dace27c001ad86d01d1766d690b0a6a618','1.1','2026-03-13T18:15:04.047734','2026-03-13T18:15:04.047740','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('19f313a4-f87f-4d97-a138-002a3b3be46e','Continuous Fixed Station Water Quality Measurements in Timucuan Ecological and Historic Preserve, January 2008 (Certified)','This dataset represents continuous water quality measurements that were taken at a fixed point in Timucuan Ecological and Historic Preserve during the month of January, 2008 as a part of the Fixed Station Water Quality Monitoring protocol that was developed by the Southeast Coast I&M Network (SECN). The measurements were taken by a YSI 6600 ESD Multi-Parameter Long Term Water Quality Monitoring Datasonde unit that serves as the standard fixed station water quality monitoring equipment for all similar operations conducted by the SECN. The following parameters were measured at 30 minute intervals during the time period that has been specified: Water Temperature, Specific Conductivity, Salinity, Dissolved Oxygen (DO), DO Concentration, Shallow Depth, pH Level, and Turbidity. Any anomalies noted regarding these parameters have also been noted in separate fields. Please note that these measurements have been certified by network personnel.','public','2026-03-26T05:33:45.231625','2026-03-26T05:33:45.231631','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','385da29e-f695-4402-a623-91dda12b5a9d','DOI NPS DCAT-US','4b9d1f9a727c7dd2034a1aaa96a3ba06b8415066d139e68eca8dd8f20e1aec3a','1.1','2026-03-26T05:33:45.231625','2026-03-26T05:33:45.231631','Vector Dataset','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('1a03a583-fa01-4f2e-b016-726ddcb16623','Kiana','Timeseries data from \'Kiana\' (raws_akakia)','public','2026-03-26T19:16:21.296213','2026-03-26T19:16:21.296223',NULL,NULL,NULL,'48c248a1-a5b5-4046-a61a-eedc41d0d654','ioos',NULL,NULL,'2026-03-26T19:16:21.296213','2026-03-26T19:16:21.296223',NULL,NULL,NULL,'noaa-gov'),('1a1ce5d4-c59e-4520-961f-1f8b5a1e21c6','MARS EXPRESS MARS MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 7 4159 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2019-01-01 to 2020-12-31. It is a Occultation measurement and covers the time 2020-11-29T09:03:55.399 to 2020-11-29T09:26:03.649.','public','2026-03-13T20:03:52.664555','2026-03-13T20:03:52.664560','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','95512990-9f15-4a42-8298-79ab98ade389','NASA Data.json','705df6cf5cd3f8c139393b129689633d441021437ab0b5175d22108702892a46','1.1','2026-03-13T20:03:52.664555','2026-03-13T20:03:52.664560','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('1a489878-f9c6-4f61-89cb-36423bfb9b6f','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSIWAC 3 ESC2-MTP017 RDR V3.0','This CODMAC level 3 data set contains radiometric calibrated image data in W/m^2/sr/nm, acquired by the OSIRIS Wide Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft during the COMET ESCORT 2 mission phase, covering the period from 2015-06-02T23:25:00.000 to 2015-06-30T23:24:59.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V3.0 supersedes previous deliveries of the same dataset with the following changes since the last version: Lien corrected dataset after the July and October 2018 PSA/PDS external peer reviews. Updated documentation and ancillary files, added document on bandpass filter. Updated SCIENCE_USER_GUIDE_V03.PDF to include one section about FAQ and one section about image data quality. Added shutter backtravel and readout issues to image quality map. Updated DATA_QUALITY_ID keyword in image header. Improved handling of images with missing packets. Included FITs files. Browse products changed to the same size as the original image.','public','2026-03-13T18:13:20.897396','2026-03-13T18:13:20.897401','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','435b7c94-5e34-45ac-86e3-f1d754a0b7d5','NASA Data.json','e72f3e4085590c8395d75717416a674a53401bf85ccae79adef3ce1ef9fe56cd','1.1','2026-03-13T18:13:20.897396','2026-03-13T18:13:20.897401','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('1a5c6d76-e301-454a-b806-5d5c490fe02c','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSIWAC 4 ESC2-MTP017 RDR-STR-REFL V1.0','This CODMAC level 4 data set contains solar stray light corrected, radiometric calibrated and geometric distortion corrected (resampled) image data in in reflectance units (normalized and thus without unit), acquired by the OSIRIS Wide Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft during the COMET ESCORT 2 mission phase, covering the period from 2015-06-02T23:25:00.000 to 2015-06-30T23:24:59.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V1.0 is the first version of this dataset: Lien corrected dataset after October 2018 PSA/PDS external peer review.','public','2026-03-13T18:13:13.099319','2026-03-13T18:13:13.099324','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','09efeac2-39aa-4b43-abe1-387784d4b974','NASA Data.json','4d2f728f44029c4052dd565c057ab621a7818d0a9545674629dfaecb1d98f65a','1.1','2026-03-13T18:13:13.099319','2026-03-13T18:13:13.099324','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('1a797cef-c040-4b97-be74-7f4eee560e3a','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 4 1161 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 4 phase 2015-10-22 to 2015-12-31. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-11-07T05:28:29.500 to 2015-11-07T12:29:04.000.','public','2026-03-13T17:43:21.553593','2026-03-13T17:43:21.553598','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','5c535e5b-29c9-4262-82c1-1e005c943246','NASA Data.json','955e60518822077183129809cdb3854c516f49e92727c74bffc62c3d2ffd8e25','1.1','2026-03-13T17:43:21.553593','2026-03-13T17:43:21.553598','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('1a8ad8d6-0f70-437b-a634-0ce55cc3867c','Continuous Fixed Station Water Quality Measurements in Canaveral National Seashore, May 2008 (Certified)','This dataset represents continuous water quality measurements that were taken at a fixed point in Canaveral National Seashore during the month of May, 2008 as a part of the Fixed Station Water Quality Monitoring protocol that was developed by the Southeast Coast I&M Network (SECN). The measurements were taken by a YSI 6600 ESD Multi-Parameter Long Term Water Quality Monitoring Datasonde unit that serves as the standard fixed station water quality monitoring equipment for all similar operations conducted by the SECN. The following parameters were measured at 30 minute intervals during the time period that has been specified: Water Temperature, Specific Conductivity, Salinity, Dissolved Oxygen (DO), DO Concentration, Shallow Depth, pH Level, and Turbidity. Any anomalies noted regarding these parameters have also been noted in separate fields. Please note that these measurements have been certified by network personnel.','public','2026-03-26T05:31:33.846176','2026-03-26T05:31:33.846181','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','67b8f72f-d830-42f0-a728-076f509e11a8','DOI NPS DCAT-US','4522800ec157dd0f88ab87622fd81d1987d075e282c6a5f4c53fce7807cd00fd','1.1','2026-03-26T05:31:33.846176','2026-03-26T05:31:33.846181','Vector Dataset','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('1aa5f368-2e03-45d9-a95c-b417f069fdfe','DC COVID 19 Total Positive Cases by Neighborhood','<div style=\"text-align:Left;\"><div><div><p>Retired on March 2, 2022. Data and metadata are provided as-is archive.</p><p><span>District of Columbia COVID-19 positive cases reported by DC Health Planning Neighborhoods. Due to rapidly changing nature of COVID-19, data for March 2020 is limited.</span></p><p><strong>General Guidelines for Interpreting Disease Surveillance Data</strong></p><p><span>During a disease outbreak, the health department will collect, process, and analyze large amounts of information to understand and respond to the health impacts of the disease and its transmission in the community. The sources of disease surveillance information include contact tracing, medical record review, and laboratory information, and are considered protected health information. When interpreting the results of these analyses, it is important to keep in mind that the disease surveillance system may not capture the full picture of the outbreak, and that previously reported data may change over time as it undergoes data quality review or as additional information is added. These analyses, especially within populations with small samples, may be subject to large amounts of variation from day to day. Despite these limitations, data from disease surveillance is a valuable source of information to understand how to stop the spread of COVID19.</span></p></div></div></div>','public','2026-04-01T08:42:28.275537','2026-04-01T08:42:28.275544','Office of the Chief Technology Officer','DCGISopendata',NULL,'698fc6b9-ae47-42f5-b3ad-3c2b4275add1','DC data','47710366863a0a46ef57fa9da88da375b3cf786b3551fca89870a77c021ce141','1.1','2026-04-01T08:42:28.275537','2026-04-01T08:42:28.275544','geospatial',NULL,0,'district-of-columbia'),('1aa7fe29-6623-4596-8071-273f6ba728e8','Lidar-derived elevation data for upper Barry Arm fjord, southcentral Alaska, collected October 14, 2022','Lidar-derived elevation data for upper Barry Arm fjord, southcentral Alaska, collected October 14, 2022, Raw Data File 2026-10, provides a lidar-derived classified point cloud, digital terrain model (DTM), surface model (DSM), and intensity model for Upper Barry Arm fjord with focus on the Barry Arm landslide, northeast of Whittier in Prince William Sound, southcentral Alaska, during near snow-free ground conditions. The goal of the survey is to provide snow-free surface elevation data to assess landslide movement using repeat surveys during snow-free conditions. Ground control was collected on July 27, 2022, and airborne data were collected on October 14, 2022, and subsequently processed in Terrasolid and ArcGIS. These data are provided as a Raw Data File under an open end-user license and are available on the DGGS website (http://doi.org/10.14509/32063).','public','2026-03-15T03:17:29.647797','2026-03-15T03:17:29.647803',NULL,NULL,NULL,'3894995a-9831-4fcc-a315-d538d83c3cd4','Alaska Division of Geological and Geophysical Surveys',NULL,NULL,'2026-03-15T03:17:29.647797','2026-03-15T03:17:29.647803',NULL,NULL,NULL,'state-of-alaska'),('1ab30e22-2ffe-4635-a803-ff73ced9ae74','myUSCIS - profile','Stores case receipt and HAC information on paper filed and ELIS cases. Also stores secure inbox messages.','non-public','2026-03-22T11:53:23.599406','2026-03-22T11:53:23.599411','Unspecified','Open Data (MGMT)','024:030','0b5ea230-a591-448f-8e0e-766ca6a25055','DHS datajson source','36366b1cf1e0b02eea97e89ba80ac221d863331f312f023282b3f7028a902d2f','1.1','2026-03-22T11:53:23.599406','2026-03-22T11:53:23.599411',NULL,'024:000',0,'dhs-gov'),('1adc7ca7-8089-460d-b25b-39c016a952aa','Atmospheric circulation constraints on future Southwest United States precipitation from CMIP6','This data file contains Python scripts for recreating the analysis presented in the manuscript. The manuscript figures are also included in this file. \n\nThis dataset is associated with the following publication:\nKelleher, M.K., P.E. Morefield, and K.M. Grise. Relationships Between Atmospheric Circulation and Southwestern United States 21st Century Precipitation Trends in Statistically Downscaled CMIP6 Models.   JOURNAL OF GEOPHYSICAL RESEARCH: ATMOSPHERES. American Geophysical Union, Washington, DC, USA, 131(6): e2025JD044419, (2026).','public','2026-03-21T12:04:08.303592','2026-03-21T12:04:08.303596','U.S. Environmental Protection Agency','Philip Morefield','020:00','40645697-1f35-4a10-a436-f03e09cb5fd3','EPA ScienceHub','98332a3a3c7d4029c0e1ea18f338cfa12549d1db3d2952b290fa0490c4063b52','1.1','2026-03-21T12:04:08.303592','2026-03-21T12:04:08.303596',NULL,'020:000',0,'epa-gov'),('1b3af324-b9ae-4d34-a40b-89d7c5d041b6','Ordinance 20040902-005','Ordinance 20040902-005','public','2026-03-25T14:34:01.055862','2026-03-25T14:34:01.055867','data.austintexas.gov','Haileigh.Meyers@austintexas.gov',NULL,'52b6888f-b259-4b2c-a843-be0f4997a27a','City of Austin Data.json','2b34ee3317c2a285c953a4689d8a1ae64074b8170fe3fca8c098add5530c536f','1.1','2026-03-25T14:34:01.055862','2026-03-25T14:34:01.055867',NULL,NULL,0,'city-of-austin'),('1b520d9c-d027-40bf-8242-2a5c09bb896e','MER1/MER2 MARS IMU ENTRY DESCENT & LANDING DERIVED DATA V1.0','Unknown','public','2026-03-13T17:04:50.710819','2026-03-13T17:04:50.710826','Planetary Atmospheres','Planetary Data System','026:00','ded9741d-6820-48cb-a6bc-2191422745c0','NASA Data.json','cbacd390d9fe49c176371b0e79d2af60b0582e308a06e07b79949f4e1aec3355','1.1','2026-03-13T17:04:50.710819','2026-03-13T17:04:50.710826','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('1b5c81f3-ade1-4a7f-88c0-a2029a7832a7','Product Data for Newly Reported Drugs in the Medicaid Drug Rebate Program 03-09-2026 to 03-15-2026','The data below contains newly reported, active covered outpatient drugs which were reported by participating drug manufacturers since the last quarterly update of the Drug Products in the Medicaid Drug Rebate Program (MDRP) database.','public','2026-03-17T16:47:54.074208','2026-03-19T17:34:01.810539','Centers for Medicare & Medicaid Services','Medicaid.gov','009:38','3e3a5f50-b98d-46c9-8301-bdaad38a8c93','Healthdata.gov','2d10f143a7c6c15d662533e86ccb7bc1af68d403ecd8addb687b5ad251b61d21','1.1','2026-03-17T16:47:54.074208','2026-03-19T17:34:01.810539','CMS','009:076',0,'hhs-gov'),('1b995631-ed90-48f5-90cf-fe4bb9d12a76','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSIWAC 4 EXT2-MTP029 RDR-STRLIGHT V1.0','This CODMAC level 4 data set contains solar stray light corrected, radiometric calibrated and geometric distortion corrected (resampled) image data in W/m^2/sr/nm, acquired by the OSIRIS Wide Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft during the ROSETTA EXTENSION 2 mission phase, covering the period from 2016-05-03T23:25:00.000 to 2016-05-31T23:24:59.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V1.0 is the first version of this dataset: Lien corrected dataset after October 2018 PSA/PDS external peer review.','public','2026-03-13T17:28:25.063424','2026-03-13T17:28:25.063429','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','8286fb48-6004-4441-8b41-b6abc758b658','NASA Data.json','461c08381700c9a095c9ca17b9ead8db7d2e6afc691790404a95d8f7c9ddfb43','1.1','2026-03-13T17:28:25.063424','2026-03-13T17:28:25.063429','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('1ba30a40-15e7-4f59-9001-2822ee02b3b2','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 3 0968 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 3 phase 2015-07-01 to 2015-10-21. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-08-17T21:32:20.000 to 2015-08-18T03:40:09.000.','public','2026-03-13T17:57:46.091764','2026-03-13T17:57:46.091769','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','f51103dc-53a4-49e1-827d-566da8a41792','NASA Data.json','ba79cd2ae7fa1e6d9b0bbcdce23c5dde676f64180fbba3c7457bc97c05c66d7e','1.1','2026-03-13T17:57:46.091764','2026-03-13T17:57:46.091769','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('1ba758f2-4008-41a6-9a69-7bf4a36cdc27','ARCSIX P-3B In-Situ Aerosol Data','ARCSIX_Aerosol_AircraftInSitu_P3B_Data is the in-situ aerosol data collected onboard the P-3B aircraft during the Arctic Radiation-Cloud-Aerosol-Surface Interaction EXperiment (ARCSIX) campaign. Data from the Nucleation Mode Aerosol Size Spectrometer, Portable Optical Particle Spetrometer (POPS), Ultra-High Sensitivity Aerosol Spectrometer (UHSAS), Time-of-Flight Aerosol Mass Spectrometer (ToF-AMS), Differential Aerosol Sizing and Hygroscopicity Spectrometer Probe (DASH-SP), Fast Integrated Mobility Spectrometer (FIMS), Aerodynamic Particle Sizer (APS), Cloud Condensation Nuclei Counter (CCN), TSI Condensation Particle Counter 3772 (TSI CPC-3772), TSI-3563 Nephelometer, and the Single Particle Soot Photometer (SP2) are featured in this collection. Data collection for this product is complete. The ARCSIX campaign is a NASA field investigation aimed at quantifying the contributions of surface properties, clouds, aerosol particles, and precipitation to the Arctic summer surface radiation budget and sea ice melt during the early melt season. Based out of Greenland, ARCSIX completed two deployments from May – June 2024 and July - August 2024 utilizing the NASA P-3B, LaRC G-III, and SPEC-Learjet aircraft. The P-3B was equipped with in situ and remote sensing payloads to acquire measurements of aerosols, cloud, and radiation properties. The high-flying LaRC G-III was equipped with remote sensing instrumentation, including the HALO, and HSRL, along with the AVAPS dropsonde system. The SPEC-Learjet acquired measurements of cloud microphysics. Data were also collected at the Thule High Arctic Atmospheric Observatory (THAAO) in Pituffik, Greenland. The primary objective of ARCSIX was to enhance long-term space-based monitoring and predictive capabilities of Arctic sea ice, cloud, and aerosols by validating and improving remote sensing algorithms and model parameterizations in the Arctic. ARCSIX science questions focused on examining the impact of the predominant summer Arctic cloud types on the radiative surface energy budget, what processes control the evolution and maintenance of the predominant cloud types in the summertime Arctic, and how do the two-way interactions between surface properties and atmospheric forcings affect sea ice evolution?','public','2026-03-13T16:45:37.861007','2026-03-13T16:45:37.861013','NASA/LARC/SD/ASDC','Earthdata Forum','026:00','5ca62e35-80e5-4300-8af1-72a2427f0815','NASA Data.json','6acc828742511509078a9c30fe648091e21c46634e251eaa03c89787c2090f95','1.1','2026-03-13T16:45:37.861007','2026-03-13T16:45:37.861013','Earth Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('1bf65bca-fe53-4ba4-ad61-2b22743e5c4e','ROSETTA-ORBITER CHECK GIADA 2 MARS MARSSWINGBY V1.0','This volume contains Experiment Data acquired by GIADA during \'Mars swing-by\' phase. More in detail it refers to the data provided during the following in-flight tests: \'Active Payload Checkout n. 4\' (PC4) held on 24/25-11-2006 and 04-12-2006; \'Passive Payload Checkout n. 5\' (PC5) held on 20/21-05-2007. It also contains documentation which describes the GIADA experiment. The data reported in this data set have been converted from ADC counts to engineering values. The quality of the Housekeeping and Calibration data is good. Scientific data are due to noise, as no grain event is expected during this mission phase. These data must be only considered to evaluate GIADA behaviour and not as real scientific data. Data reported by GDS and IS are due to noise as no dust event is expected during this mission phase. MBS frequency changes, once normalised for frequency vs. temperature dependence, if present, are due to deposition of contaminants existing in the S/C environment. Housekeeping and Calibration data from all GIADA sub-systems are useful to evaluate instrument health and behaviour when compared with similar data acquired during other mission phases.','public','2026-03-13T18:40:45.312278','2026-03-13T18:40:45.312283','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','dfca0e03-ab54-48a6-97fd-83482b0e01dd','NASA Data.json','555f89df71677bf91bbbfd854598e3d327615ea1274c14af755482dc7c7dceed','1.1','2026-03-13T18:40:45.312278','2026-03-13T18:40:45.312283','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('1c3bec07-b688-4d0c-883e-658739858435','MESSENGER MERCURY MDIS LEVEL 5 DEM V1.0','Abstract : The MESSENGER MDIS DEMs are derived products. A DEM is a gridded (raster) product that records elevation values of a given terrain in each pixel. Corresponding metadata include map projection information so pixels can be associated with latitude and longitude. Values are measured relative to the planetary geoid reference radius of 2,439.4 km (i.e. elevation). Generally, the MESSENGER DEM products described here are derived from MESSENGER MDIS image data. The DEMs are typically derived using stereo photogrammetry (i.e., stereo pairs or sets) techniques. The primary PDS product is a DEM provided in both PDS image (.IMG) and JPEG 2000 (.JP2) format files. Associated with some of the DEM products is a list of lower-level MDIS products provided either as an accompanying table (*.TAB) file or as text (*.TXT) files in the EXTRAS directory.','public','2026-03-13T19:15:23.726182','2026-03-13T19:15:23.726187','Imaging','Planetary Data System','026:00','0615456f-bd48-4947-98ca-ad41f9398fde','NASA Data.json','cf355219bb84ab8566867d0ca8918d75b258386c41c35c7f2b35fd877664a38e','1.1','2026-03-13T19:15:23.726182','2026-03-13T19:15:23.726187','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('1c62ec5f-396d-421f-9621-e9b88a13b635','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSIWAC 2 ESC2-MTP017 EDR V3.0','This CODMAC level 2 data set contains uncalibrated image data in DN unit, acquired by the OSIRIS Wide Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft during the COMET ESCORT 2 mission phase, covering the period from 2015-06-02T23:25:00.000 to 2015-06-30T23:24:59.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V3.0 supersedes previous deliveries of the same dataset with the following changes since the last version: Lien corrected dataset after the July and October 2018 PSA/PDS external peer reviews. Updated documentation and ancillary files, added document on bandpass filter. Updated SCIENCE_USER_GUIDE_V03.PDF to include one section about FAQ and one section about image data quality. Added shutter backtravel and readout issues to image quality map. Updated DATA_QUALITY_ID keyword in image header. Improved handling of images with missing packets. Included FITs files. Browse products changed to the same size as the original image.','public','2026-03-13T18:17:48.161300','2026-03-13T18:17:48.161305','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','17f7ed54-3f15-42b2-86aa-5747513c3ea8','NASA Data.json','33f48e592b0bf6fefc56769d302224d4faf778bd87eb68a637e732d13f021a86','1.1','2026-03-13T18:17:48.161300','2026-03-13T18:17:48.161305','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('1c6405f4-23ae-4544-8373-12c5af673ad2','LRO DLRE LEVEL 2 EDR V1.0','This data set consists of the Diviner Lunar Radiometer Experiment uncalibrated observations, also known as EDRs. The DLRE is a surface pushbroom mapper that  measures emitted thermal radiation and reflected solar radiation  from the surface of the moon. Two Diviner solar channels measure 0.3-3 micrometers reflected solar radiation. Three Diviner channels near 8 micrometers classify regolith mineralogy by mapping the location of the Christiansen feature. The remaining four Diviner channels measure surface temperature in four spectral bands ranging from 12.5 micrometers to beyond 200 micrometers.','public','2026-03-13T20:02:56.625763','2026-03-13T20:02:56.625769','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','7cfc4cd4-27ba-493f-8398-718b7d6e6aef','NASA Data.json','ef858cb349b4b6fd47a7e806cb3be25b4b3e252d313cf6657f9a40c0f3decec3','1.1','2026-03-13T20:02:56.625763','2026-03-13T20:02:56.625769','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('1c74d336-a8b8-4c05-b959-db8492c3e827','SPECTROPHOTOMETRY OF THE JOVIAN PLANETS AND TITAN','The best description of this data set can be found in [KARKOSCHKA1998]. The previous version (1993) of this data set is included as well. The reference for that portion of the data set is [KARKOSCHKA1994].','public','2026-03-13T18:30:01.185811','2026-03-13T18:30:01.185815','Planetary Atmospheres','Planetary Data System','026:00','836a2670-a225-458e-9bb7-482419d02202','NASA Data.json','13bf8ce7f82632c17a0595fa6968bf0f438f5290c86d673a43ff8a54e4146676','1.1','2026-03-13T18:30:01.185811','2026-03-13T18:30:01.185815','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('1c8df699-9356-474b-a404-650e3cf39027','EGIS - Enterprise Gateway Integration Services-EGIS Reference Data (RefData)','EGIS RefDaaS is an enterprise service to maintain and provide reference data across USCIS. It provides services to consumes reference data from authorized sources and make it available to services across USCIS. It provides services to translate reference data values between internal USCIS or external systems managed by agencies such DOS, CBP.','non-public','2026-03-22T11:54:19.425711','2026-03-22T11:54:19.425716','Unspecified','Open Data (MGMT)','024:030','733780dc-76da-43d2-ae50-3c53bdf76e14','DHS datajson source','ec237a3380cae9f03ae77e275e59f9a70a4d1914bdf45fff2f2aa6b1ffd8d093','1.1','2026-03-22T11:54:19.425711','2026-03-22T11:54:19.425716',NULL,'024:000',0,'dhs-gov'),('1ce46ce2-5dd9-4761-873e-5810579a889f','CASSINI ORBITER N/A UVIS IMAGE AT ONE WAVELENGTH','Imaging of the Saturn system at a wavelength in the far or extreme ultraviolet.','public','2026-03-13T18:18:02.529999','2026-03-13T18:18:02.530004','Planetary Atmospheres','Planetary Data System','026:00','869d973d-541f-41e9-aae7-a0fe2b57d2a9','NASA Data.json','e72da25453dd5320a0c86d37e6bce1c4bbc3dee2221ffb5141d880b17898f8a2','1.1','2026-03-13T18:18:02.529999','2026-03-13T18:18:02.530004','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('1cf1bac2-11de-4717-91df-b73c3d24b2d5','State Motor Fuel Tax Receipts (MF-201)','Motor fuel tax receipt totals by States from the Federal Highway Administration\'s Office of Policy Information\'s Highway Statistics Series.','public','2026-03-20T11:37:55.740863','2026-03-20T11:37:55.740870','Federal Highway Administration','Office of Highway Policy Information','021:15','1e260fb5-56b2-430b-ae4e-28c4ede5ad2b','DOT Socrata Data.json','cf1494b4f63b6b6901da13bd3966667e0c744f0932702b3fcf839b2e654c0acd','1.1','2026-03-20T11:37:55.740863','2026-03-20T11:37:55.740870','Roadways and Bridges','021:009',0,'dot-gov'),('1d54f71c-65d7-4cfc-9ff6-be29091f5e8f','US Forest Atlas FIA Forest Type Groups (Image Service)','<div><strong>Forest-type Groups:</strong></div><div>This dataset portrays the forest type group. Each group is a subset of the National Forest Type dataset which portrays 28 forest type groups across the contiguous United States. These data were derived from MODIS composite images from the 2002 and 2003 growing seasons in combination with nearly 100 other geospatial data layers, including elevation, slope, aspect, ecoregions, and PRISM climate data.</div>','public','2026-03-13T22:50:07.213287','2026-03-13T22:50:07.213293','U.S. Forest Service','USFSEnterpriseContent','005:96','bca8d70d-445c-47b4-83d6-9ed2b4194e0f','USDA JSON','be4098ebcd201e864671c282944ab862be5b659e6411e67a92a871d02d6be9b7','1.1','2026-03-13T22:50:07.213287','2026-03-13T22:50:07.213293','geospatial','005:059',0,'usda-gov'),('1d5799ca-07f6-4b9d-83d2-1d1919a4f807','ALOS_PALSAR_KMZ','ALOS PALSAR KMZ','public','2026-03-13T18:45:09.598232','2026-03-13T18:45:09.598238','ASF','Earthdata Forum','026:00','dbabb079-e270-46a0-a44e-c61f8847cc6a','NASA Data.json','ca0eb81f654e754d7b3153f65b46ba7c482c300c78a93887e4159d941774064f','1.1','2026-03-13T18:45:09.598232','2026-03-13T18:45:09.598238','Earth Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('1d61c764-eeef-4b3e-9cd3-51e485b9e56f','DAWN FC1 RAW (EDR) CRUISE  CHECKOUT/CALIBRATION IMAGES V1.0','Abstract  :  Framing Camera 1 is one of two identical units flying on Dawn  spacecraft. This dataset includes the Experiment Data Record (EDR)  version of all available images acquired during the initial checkout and all cruise phases (Earth to Mars, Mars to Vesta and Vesta to Ceres).  In addition to the imagery, anciliary information is stored within the  image headers. Calibration files needed for further processing are  archived as a separate data set.','public','2026-03-13T19:17:21.396116','2026-03-13T19:17:21.396125','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','8adca4e6-43a2-4b80-8283-8ead5342c1bd','NASA Data.json','62cb2f17acbe0f83c0fc2da29f70b2c850506e1f5b6d605b2943740c7ca9c88d','1.1','2026-03-13T19:17:21.396116','2026-03-13T19:17:21.396125','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('1d6afa52-5706-44de-8664-a0c363a39bd4','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSIWAC 5 EXT1-MTP026 DDR-GEO V1.0','This CODMAC level 5 data set contains derived data products that include pixel-precise georeferencing information, acquired by the OSIRIS Wide Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft during the ROSETTA EXTENSION 1 mission phase, covering the period from 2016-02-09T23:25:00.000 to 2016-03-08T23:24:59.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V1.0 is the first version of this dataset: Lien corrected dataset after October 2018 PSA/PDS external peer review.','public','2026-03-13T17:18:01.120376','2026-03-13T17:18:01.120380','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','4400ddb3-536e-4853-a8fc-83a412b11b79','NASA Data.json','31ae06f8936d0b8a49d43346b916ac2b46faa9a08ca3c07ffe9af89feb5323fe','1.1','2026-03-13T17:18:01.120376','2026-03-13T17:18:01.120380','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('1d6cc03f-ed25-47bf-9cd4-1368f84d0695','2023 NOAA Topbathy Lidar DEM: Whitefish Point Lake Superior, MI','The Digital Elevation Model includes the grounded classes of class 2, 40, and 43. This raster is tiled out into 23 5000 m x 5000 m tiles. The project AOI covers approximately 161.5 square kilometers, and includes the area from Whitefish Point to Bay Mills, MI in Eastern Lake Superior, the eastern portion of which falls within and EPA\'s St. Marys River area of concern.','public','2026-03-26T20:18:39.097958','2026-03-26T20:18:39.097964',NULL,NULL,NULL,'3142d390-6f66-4ea0-b590-43be82e81535','NOS OCM',NULL,NULL,'2026-03-26T20:18:39.097958','2026-03-26T20:18:39.097964',NULL,NULL,NULL,'noaa-gov'),('1d7d2316-3e08-46f6-b36a-fa0ed67daf7e','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P ROSINA 3 ESC2 V2.0','This data set contains CODMAC level 3 science data acquired by the DFMS and RTOF ROSINA sensors between 2015-03-11 and 2015-06-30 during the Escort phase 2 of the Rosetta mission to comet 67P/CG. V2.0 : Mass scale has been enhanced for a selection of masses which are now provided with 4 digits after the coma and the offset removal has been improved, corrupted files have been removed in the V2.0','public','2026-03-13T17:07:18.827949','2026-03-13T17:07:18.827954','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','e8a7cd35-2010-44db-9256-3efee4c4a65b','NASA Data.json','00792b146b91d136077a83ac924f7e26bb1aa9abd56e0c24741e1f09f897c5ee','1.1','2026-03-13T17:07:18.827949','2026-03-13T17:07:18.827954','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('1d8d9a17-5a6b-4c75-91d5-55d7f21db58a','Continuous Fixed Station Water Quality Measurements in Canaveral National Seashore, August 2005 (Certified)','This dataset represents continuous water quality measurements that were taken at a fixed point in Canaveral National Seashore during the month of August, 2005 as a part of the Fixed Station Water Quality Monitoring protocol that was developed by the Southeast Coast I&M Network (SECN). The measurements were taken by a YSI 6600 ESD Multi-Parameter Long Term Water Quality Monitoring Datasonde unit that serves as the standard fixed station water quality monitoring equipment for all similar operations conducted by the SECN. The following parameters were measured at 30 minute intervals during the time period that has been specified: Water Temperature, Specific Conductivity, Salinity, Dissolved Oxygen (DO), DO Concentration, Shallow Depth, pH Level, and Turbidity. Any anomalies noted regarding these parameters have also been noted in separate fields. Please note that these measurements have been certified by network personnel.','public','2026-03-26T05:28:58.482385','2026-03-26T05:28:58.482391','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','90ce890f-a165-48cb-b341-468d6264f238','DOI NPS DCAT-US','8ec1f3505d134ba9956c7574c3861c2c862e726667024421a1b8283c9db1ff87','1.1','2026-03-26T05:28:58.482385','2026-03-26T05:28:58.482391','Vector Dataset','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('1da7d04a-b5c6-42cf-a652-efd88ebf3b70','MIDAS - Microfilm Digitization Application System-Document Services Management System','This dataset represents warehouse inventory management for USCIS warehouses. The data includes order requests and fulfillment of all forms and other standard and secure Items from DHS warehouses to all the field offices across all the states and internationally.','non-public','2026-03-22T11:56:48.260788','2026-03-22T11:56:48.260792','Unspecified','Open Data (MGMT)','024:030','4d1ea868-ef93-4891-91a6-b3bb3f58908f','DHS datajson source','b3ed35537b74bd6d640564f8821287aa96a8dcf878cdc3880edf534c2d8be51e','1.1','2026-03-22T11:56:48.260788','2026-03-22T11:56:48.260792',NULL,'024:000',0,'dhs-gov'),('1dcb8095-f6bf-4fb4-ade2-e4c0b627de5a','EGIS - Enterprise Gateway Integration Services-Reference Data as a Service (RefDaaS)','EGIS RefDaaS is an enterprise service to maintain and provide reference data across USCIS. It provides services to consumes reference data from authorized sources and make it available to services across USCIS. It provides services to translate reference data values between internal USCIS or external systems managed by agencies such DOS, CBP.','non-public','2026-03-22T11:53:22.469891','2026-03-22T11:53:22.469896','Unspecified','Open Data (MGMT)','024:030','fbce595d-fb6d-41e4-b950-cbd0a2e4a5a2','DHS datajson source','63e7288fa7e2f1b82547c33fb52c4701a9441465f1d20c1fa53c45c4c34d745b','1.1','2026-03-22T11:53:22.469891','2026-03-22T11:53:22.469896',NULL,'024:000',0,'dhs-gov'),('1dd830bb-aadc-43e8-b555-47de79f3cef9','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P VIRTIS 2 ESCORT 3 MTP021 V1.0','This release contains the digital numbers (DN) contained in the telemetry (TM) packages of the VIRTIS instrument on board of the spacecraft Rosetta. This volume contains data at the vicinity of comet 67P, from the ESCORT 3 MTP021 phase, which occurred from 2015-09-23 to 2015-10-21','public','2026-03-13T17:01:44.206061','2026-03-13T17:01:44.206069','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','c6e901d8-c524-4fb4-bd56-63afae9b5907','NASA Data.json','37d2a0694ad9387a3a91ed9358df98e5f85afe2ce63da3c5569561b8b3d16fe2','1.1','2026-03-13T17:01:44.206061','2026-03-13T17:01:44.206069','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('1df810d3-05ce-4134-ba55-b91cc042472f','ROSETTA-ORBITER EARTH MIRO 2 EAR1 EARTH1 V1.0','This data set contains Spectroscopic, Continuum and Engineering data, in the form of table files, taken during the first Earth swing-by phase of the Rosetta mission by the MIRO instrument.','public','2026-03-13T18:37:25.336634','2026-03-13T18:37:25.336640','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','0dae3fee-d421-49a6-b3fc-8e84b0cf4f3f','NASA Data.json','2a754124466ac21ff6774068a54726e38c9f3cb6f974492d80f44d50af8c6159','1.1','2026-03-13T18:37:25.336634','2026-03-13T18:37:25.336640','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('1e0bb264-846c-4849-9caa-fe3346f8da3b','ROSETTA-ORBITER COMET ESCORT OSIWAC 3 RDR MTP 011 V1.0','This data set contains calibrated images acquired by the OSIRIS Wide AngleCamera during the escort phase of the Rosetta mission at the comet 67P,covering the period from 2014-12-19 to 2015-01-13.','public','2026-03-13T17:51:17.546163','2026-03-13T17:51:17.546169','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','3e98dc8a-e2e8-44a1-b302-811d8dab636c','NASA Data.json','a0534abbfe39cbe29f8de3bde435f8d4270cacdafdc4fc2ec8e1fe409f3fca76','1.1','2026-03-13T17:51:17.546163','2026-03-13T17:51:17.546169','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('1e4bc328-842d-4e1b-9e3e-4726fe866654','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 3 0966 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 3 phase 2015-07-01 to 2015-10-21. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-08-17T03:04:20.000 to 2015-08-17T09:56:21.500.','public','2026-03-13T19:39:14.057621','2026-03-13T19:39:14.057628','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','7b6bc4dd-b652-4fdd-8c36-db7c7652f0d4','NASA Data.json','4a221bcaebb162d13d46afaff0528abf89ff7fed14a2ef90e03b93a7e985e0d9','1.1','2026-03-13T19:39:14.057621','2026-03-13T19:39:14.057628','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('1e7af238-a0bf-4daa-b7f5-3f5335df6c60','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P NAVCAM 2 COMET ESCORT 2 MTP016 V1.1','This dataset contains ROSETTA NAVCAM RAW DATA of the Escort Phase 2 from 5th May 2015 to 2nd Jun 2015 when at the vicinity of target 67P/CG. This data set V1.1 supersedes the V1.0. It includes updates of the Browse images, adding of the FITS version, clarification of calibration target, document updates and resolve other minor outstanding errata.','public','2026-03-13T17:51:39.400203','2026-03-13T17:51:39.400208','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','01ed9f6a-3e87-4cf0-94a4-4a068ee19370','NASA Data.json','858cca987955546d834ad468c6c561bb086d80d8d4e2b1f20e981b8b933fdc61','1.1','2026-03-13T17:51:39.400203','2026-03-13T17:51:39.400208','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('1e969238-5039-43fb-bdce-566bb44e463b','PHX MARS THERMAL EVOLVED GAS ANALYZER 2 SCEDR V1.0','Raw, uncalibrated engineering, housekeeping and scientific data collected from the Thermal Evolved Gas Analyzer (TEGA) aboard the 2007 Mars Phoenix Lander.','public','2026-03-13T20:05:59.625000','2026-03-13T20:05:59.625007','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','d2534312-2287-4e62-89eb-a1b09275d9ce','NASA Data.json','3f54a74a4a9b327a7930369377af5161099aa1b75f5dc2f011039a3819d26122','1.1','2026-03-13T20:05:59.625000','2026-03-13T20:05:59.625007','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('1f16d3ed-932d-4889-8d28-028c98e1915b','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 4 1245 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 4 phase 2015-10-22 to 2015-12-31. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-12-08T18:23:35.000 to 2015-12-09T00:11:40.000.','public','2026-03-13T19:59:06.688191','2026-03-13T19:59:06.688196','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','025b8252-0d3e-4f2f-a9bd-9d5b9efef944','NASA Data.json','bcf38f00c2e1fe05231e9b81d25c7aaefe9a34d66f4211ccc3989c6d3a2b43f3','1.1','2026-03-13T19:59:06.688191','2026-03-13T19:59:06.688196','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('1f222ff5-3643-4da4-948d-29dfbb7657d4','ROSETTA-ORBITER LUTETIA/CAL ALICE 4 AST2 V1.0','This data set contains CODMAC level 4 data acquired by the Rosetta Orbiter ALICE UV Spectrometer during the Lutetia flyby mission phase, which took place between 2010-06-07 and 2010-09-10.','public','2026-03-13T17:26:39.153114','2026-03-13T17:26:39.153121','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','2e207937-c65c-46f9-8891-864211c9c202','NASA Data.json','f92eb5b70056d3d1ce99807694a242c3e8507838c58ab8237f9925d768d09e6d','1.1','2026-03-13T17:26:39.153114','2026-03-13T17:26:39.153121','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('1f35053a-34f7-41d6-8810-ca2e535e6c70','AIRS/Aqua L2 Near Real Time (NRT) Cloud-Cleared Infrared Radiances (AIRS-only) V006 (AIRS2CCF_NRT) at GES DISC','The Atmospheric Infrared Sounder (AIRS) Level 2 Near Real Time (NRT) Cloud-Cleared Infrared Radiances (AIRS-only) product (AIRS2CCF_NRT_006) differs from the routine product (AIRS2CCF_006) in four ways to meet the three hour latency requirements of the Land Atmosphere NRT Capability Earth Observing System (LANCE): (1) The NRT granules are produced without previous or subsequent granules if those granules are not available within 5 minutes, (2) the predictive ephemeris/attitude data are used rather than the definitive ephemeris/attitude, (3) if the forecast surface pressure is unavailable, a surface climatology is used, and (4) no ice cloud properties retrievals are performed. The consequences of these differences are described in the AIRS Near Real Time (NRT) data products document. The Atmospheric Infrared Sounder (AIRS) is a grating spectrometer (R = 1200) aboard the second Earth Observing System (EOS) polar-orbiting platform, EOS Aqua. In combination with the Advanced Microwave Sounding Unit (AMSU) and the Humidity Sounder for Brazil (HSB), AIRS constitutes an innovative atmospheric sounding group of visible, infrared, and microwave sensors. This product is produced using AIRS IR only because the radiometric noise in AMSU channel 4 started to increase significantly (since June 2007). Cloud-Cleared Radiances contain calibrated, geolocated channel-by-channel AIRS infrared radiances (milliWatts/m2/cm-1/steradian) that would have been observed within each AMSU footprint if there were no clouds in the FOV and produced along with the AIRS Standard Product, as they are the radiances used to retrieve the Standard Product. Nevertheless, they are an order of magnitude larger in data volume than the remainder of the Standard Products and, many Standard Product users are expected to have little interest in the Cloud Cleared Radiance. For these reasons they are a separate output file. The AIRS2CCF_NRT_006 products are stored in files (often referred to as \"granules\") that contain 6 minutes of data, 30 footprints across track by 45 lines along track.','public','2026-03-13T18:37:54.319592','2026-03-13T18:37:54.319597','NASA/GSFC/SED/ESD/TISL/GESDISC','Earthdata Forum','026:00','49568f1c-ec83-4097-9d28-2f142b0f4861','NASA Data.json','4634259a8bbb6f8be177929d492550fe1cfcf46dea9fae06058a1e232942a800','1.1','2026-03-13T18:37:54.319592','2026-03-13T18:37:54.319597','Earth Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('1f718506-c52c-4199-9b64-fa302a3aae0b','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 PRELANDING 0183 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the PRELANDING phase 2014-01-21 to 2014-11-18. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2014-08-06T15:42:05.000 to 2014-08-06T19:43:37.000.','public','2026-03-13T17:23:35.502338','2026-03-13T17:23:35.502343','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','0bfe60d2-96f7-4eae-b6ca-4d95db13acd5','NASA Data.json','211d1c663e121cbb150f527b899e78701317a4f71598d3325506fdc0b761f765','1.1','2026-03-13T17:23:35.502338','2026-03-13T17:23:35.502343','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('1fa498dd-2d58-4677-a76e-ba15ee57ee19','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P ROSINA 3 EXT1 V2.0','This data set contains CODMAC level 3 science data acquired by the DFMS and RTOF ROSINA sensors between 2016-01-13 and 2016-04-05 during the Extension phase 1 of the Rosetta mission to comet 67P/CG. V2.0 : Mass scale has been enhanced for a selection of masses which are now provided with 4 digits after the coma and the offset removal has been improved, corrupted files have been removed in the V2.0','public','2026-03-13T16:52:24.799979','2026-03-13T16:52:24.799986','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','857c0825-0ca1-4a31-bc4e-63a0e6b3039c','NASA Data.json','bd47735e4a763555d65a5bb645b69a3014bdebd5251dfe29914a843b3b762c66','1.1','2026-03-13T16:52:24.799979','2026-03-13T16:52:24.799986','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('1fb51c44-95d7-482b-ab86-aaeb0bb111d8','MARS EXPRESS MARS MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 8 4212 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2021-01-01 to 2022-12-31. It is a Occultation measurement and covers the time 2021-04-12T06:32:20.299 to 2021-04-12T07:14:06.399.','public','2026-03-13T16:50:24.133331','2026-03-13T16:50:24.133336','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','2f6522fc-2010-493d-91a7-8d64ec075b28','NASA Data.json','750277b0725301d111831c888cc2c13a78d2a3f94abdd372f1bf463db39cd0a3','1.1','2026-03-13T16:50:24.133331','2026-03-13T16:50:24.133336','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('1ffd1993-0702-4f9e-84b0-c91d2561290f','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 PRELANDING 0371 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the PRELANDING phase 2014-01-21 to 2014-11-18. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2014-10-19T15:15:40.000 to 2014-10-19T22:01:23.000.','public','2026-03-13T22:35:45.451167','2026-03-13T22:35:45.451175','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','567d6369-09a2-4f2b-be5f-cee876fca88b','NASA Data.json','3c1d0151fed19ecd504dab47fd5768042e97daf05727cc48a479c4bb41fdb311','1.1','2026-03-13T22:35:45.451167','2026-03-13T22:35:45.451175','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('202c112b-2df1-456f-a4cf-75aaa87e4be6','MARS EXPRESS MARS MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 7 4010 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2019-01-01 to 2020-12-31. It is a Occultation measurement and covers the time 2019-05-21T08:28:58.100 to 2019-05-21T08:51:06.349.','public','2026-03-13T18:24:46.929943','2026-03-13T18:24:46.929948','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','2fcbfb59-a5e5-4e7d-8b42-a053a1e97c33','NASA Data.json','23208c53d2ff9f34e447e17c1cf9ceca2654c1a4fd9ae8b33f46cb14008ed5ca','1.1','2026-03-13T18:24:46.929943','2026-03-13T18:24:46.929948','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('205dbaa1-03bc-4235-a7d7-7ad3643ce9b4','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 2 0761 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 2 phase 2015-03-11 to 2015-06-30. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-05-09T10:02:05.000 to 2015-05-09T12:25:08.500.','public','2026-03-13T18:13:49.241060','2026-03-13T18:13:49.241064','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','aad1d21d-ceb9-4262-82e1-cc8c21aa1fa1','NASA Data.json','d2fa62cfc4d180a1ed665f9ba5e4f7754abff24882799609ce9060c7a937eeba','1.1','2026-03-13T18:13:49.241060','2026-03-13T18:13:49.241064','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('207dcfc7-3146-4289-a932-c6bdee05cb6a','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSINAC 4 EXT1-MTP025 RDR V2.0','This CODMAC level 4 data set contains radiometric calibrated and geometric distortion corrected (resampled) image data in W/m^2/sr/nm, acquired by the OSIRIS Narrow Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft during the ROSETTA EXTENSION 1 mission phase, covering the period from 2016-01-12T23:25:00.000 to 2016-02-09T23:24:59.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V2.0 supersedes previous deliveries of the same dataset with the following changes since the last version: Lien corrected dataset after October 2018 PSA/PDS external peer review. Updated documentation and ancillary files, added document on bandpass filter. Updated SCIENCE_USER_GUIDE_V03.PDF to include one section about FAQ and one section about image data quality. Added shutter backtravel and readout issues to image quality map. Updated DATA_QUALITY_ID keyword in image header. Improved handling of images with missing packets.','public','2026-03-13T19:50:53.310361','2026-03-13T19:50:53.310366','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','a25c4005-15d3-43a1-81e2-a80cb26c5544','NASA Data.json','25e8d578008daa427df95597e26f32e07cfc8fee95afff1472276f1388b34e93','1.1','2026-03-13T19:50:53.310361','2026-03-13T19:50:53.310366','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('20aea718-4110-4577-955b-975251043941','ROSETTA-ORBITER COMET PRELANDING OSINAC 3 RDR MTP 007B V1.0','This data set contains calibrated images acquired by the OSIRIS Narrow AngleCamera during the prelanding phase of the Rosetta mission at the comet 67P,covering the period from 2014-09-16 to 2014-09-23.','public','2026-03-13T19:34:58.360658','2026-03-13T19:34:58.360664','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','9b588984-5917-4452-bb5f-74592f45a502','NASA Data.json','aca32c9a729b834b1ff5345a9d5cdf9c6b9af8003eb438b79fe947499a483ad3','1.1','2026-03-13T19:34:58.360658','2026-03-13T19:34:58.360664','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('20ecb005-a978-43a1-b103-0f269b7c75e8','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 4 1148 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 4 phase 2015-10-22 to 2015-12-31. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-11-01T08:32:30.000 to 2015-11-01T17:11:56.000.','public','2026-03-13T19:05:48.785300','2026-03-13T19:05:48.785307','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','70da13f3-2b77-4877-b4a5-7d8ea9562639','NASA Data.json','2e71ba47c32ab55b96eebe41cf6c4f93e4c5f4b392cf5555518e8159b13ce157','1.1','2026-03-13T19:05:48.785300','2026-03-13T19:05:48.785307','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('21073334-4102-48d7-b6e1-098ed2f50847','VG2 NEP CRS RESAMPLED SUMMARY D1 RATE ELEC 96SEC V1.0','This data set describes the counting rate from the D1 detector     in the Cosmic Ray System (CRS) electron telescope (TET) on     Voyager 2 during the Neptune encounter. The D1 detector nominally     responds to electrons with kinetic energies above approximately 1 MeV     (see detector description for details).','public','2026-03-13T17:24:35.794037','2026-03-13T17:24:35.794042','planetary plasma interactions','Planetary Data System','026:00','422d5a44-d1a7-4a29-a1e4-6f53e9a80428','NASA Data.json','30bdc6b9b3338e38f6a518bcf16917719d44f3e72dd850ddaafacf2503056f77','1.1','2026-03-13T17:24:35.794037','2026-03-13T17:24:35.794042','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('211419b0-167e-43b8-956e-2544311e30a6','VOYAGER 2 JUPITER MAGNETOMETER RESAMPLED DATA 9.60 SEC','This data set includes Voyager 2 Jupiter encounter magnetometer data that have been resampled at a 9.6 second sample rate. The data set is composed of 6 columns: 1) ctime - this column contains the data acquisition time. The time is always output in the ISO standard spacecraft event time format (yyyy-mm-dd-Thh:mm:ss.sss) but is stored internally in Cline time which is measured in seconds after 00:00:00.000 Jan 01, 1966, 2) br - this column contains the radial component of the magnetic field, 3) bphi - this column contains the phi component of the magnetic field, 4) btheta - this column contains the theta component of the magnetic field, 5) bmag - this column contains the magnitude of the magnetic field, 6) flag - a flag value that indicates either software error or spacecraft hardware interference reduced confidence in this record (flag value of 1 is bad , 0 is good or unchecked). All magnetic field observations are measured in nanoTeslas. The coordinate system for this dataset is Minus System III. All of the magnetic field data are calibrated (see the instrument calibration description for more details). The Jupiter System III coordinate system is defined in Dessler 1983 and the reference documents for this dataset are: Ness et al, 1979A Lepping et al, 1981 Connerney,Acuna,Ness, 1981 Behannon,Burlaga,Ness, 1981','public','2026-03-13T18:49:53.544070','2026-03-13T18:49:53.544075','Planetary Plasma Interactions','Planetary Data System','026:00','d1c90bf1-bc1f-4131-9fdf-38bf047917d4','NASA Data.json','819dc4a971109e0c823c7c93be91934d17f427100b356009bb98daf777cb50d7','1.1','2026-03-13T18:49:53.544070','2026-03-13T18:49:53.544075','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('211cafc0-985e-448e-9538-f834f33de5ea','KECK I LWS MID-IR IMAGES AND PHOTOMETRY OF 9P/TEMPEL 1','This data set contains raw and reduced mid-infrared images and photometry of comet 9P/Tempel 1, the target of the Deep Impact mission. Images were acquired on the night of 21 August 2000, about 7.5 months after perihelion, by Y. Fernandez, C. Lisse, M. A\'Hearn and M. Belton using the Long Wavelength Spectrometer instrument at the Keck I telescope.','public','2026-03-13T17:14:16.741465','2026-03-13T17:14:16.741471','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','68868f84-f1c0-4831-b3ae-5504425b821f','NASA Data.json','340d0f17892fde3b692ddae886fafc6a10327b09703bb8ba4194ff6d0bc78f23','1.1','2026-03-13T17:14:16.741465','2026-03-13T17:14:16.741471','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('214a3985-5809-404e-b509-82ed634dd377','AMES MARS GENERAL CIRCULATION MODEL 5 TIME VARIABLES V1.0','The Ames Mars General Circulation Model is a three dimensional model based on the primitive equations of meteorology. It includes the radiative effects of dust and carbon dioxide as well as other features such as large-scale topography (see [POLLACKETAL1990]','public','2026-03-13T19:35:16.847449','2026-03-13T19:35:16.847458','Planetary Atmospheres','Planetary Data System','026:00','45103a96-c249-4cdd-883d-a9452b9b3291','NASA Data.json','d2d627e33703c3d07dd8d0146d6b4af3f229fbad52b8256a6439a8925183c5eb','1.1','2026-03-13T19:35:16.847449','2026-03-13T19:35:16.847458','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('217de64e-6a4d-4a29-996a-923595e3e376','BLM ID Administrative Unit Office Locations','<div style=\'text-align:Left;font-size:12pt\'><div><div><div><p><span>Point features used to show the locations of BLM offices. Each office in this feature class is represented by a point, regardless of whether the office is co-located with others at the same location. One physical location may administer more than one administrative unit, and have multiple offices co-located in that location. Therefore, point features may be coincident. The feature class includes attributes to store feature level metadata information. Several attributes document the origin and characteristics of the points. The Bureau of Land Management uses a multiple tier organization to manage the land. With some exceptions, the land that the BLM manages is served by field offices. Most of these field offices are managed by district offices, which in turn are managed by State Offices.    For more information contact us at blm_id_stateoffice@blm.gov.</span></p></div></div></div></div>','public','2026-03-18T11:14:14.554264','2026-03-18T11:14:14.554271','Bureau of Land Management','Bureau of Land Management, id_so_information','010:04','f3562514-bc2b-4135-ab74-0bd896ef34e5','DOI BLM DCAT-US','1129349a2352598c95cedfab3898fd61ed4551ca152c7cb07538fa0de4658e96','1.1','2026-03-18T11:14:14.554264','2026-03-18T11:14:14.554271','geospatial','010:000',0,'doi-gov'),('21811651-1896-4e9e-8ceb-dc64a2e60ede','MARS EXPRESS MARS MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 8 4206 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2021-01-01 to 2022-12-31. It is a Occultation measurement and covers the time 2021-04-05T06:53:43.100 to 2021-04-05T07:29:43.449.','public','2026-03-13T16:47:51.246505','2026-03-13T16:47:51.246510','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','34824c88-5a88-4722-b010-0293bafe469d','NASA Data.json','f460ff19daadc6fc48ffc22738251d267fd72a5fb425fcbfb0db647e0a657eef','1.1','2026-03-13T16:47:51.246505','2026-03-13T16:47:51.246510','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('21877994-5f30-4fd5-9f2d-6fc3fff450c4','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 1 0464 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 1 phase 2014-11-20 to 2015-03-10. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2014-11-29T03:34:35.000 to 2014-11-29T13:08:47.000.','public','2026-03-13T19:53:48.312867','2026-03-13T19:53:48.312873','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','d5ad084b-6caa-4d8a-8c28-4aa5756597f7','NASA Data.json','52f4c5e693e39086e9c38516bb977ba8d2398707f3ea9d2637c8fb16305a123b','1.1','2026-03-13T19:53:48.312867','2026-03-13T19:53:48.312873','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('219c9567-e448-47ef-96a6-84da1d133457','Code for: Sensitivity of soil nutrient pools, but stability of microbial processes, under reduced rainfall and altered grazing management in northern mixed-grass prairie','<p dir=\"ltr\">Nutrient cycling is a key ecosystem service provided by soils, which may be impacted by global change-induced droughts and alterations to grazing pressure. While the belowground abiotic and biotic responses to drought are increasingly studied, linkages among plant, animal, and microbial responses to drought remain poorly understood. Here we used an innovative experimental approach to enable understanding the relative importance of rainfall reduction, bovine grazing, and their interplay on soil nutrient pools and processes during and after treatments. Specifically, we experimentally imposed a two-year drought of varying intensity (five levels) at two northern mixed-grass prairie sites in Montana and Wyoming. Crossed with this drought treatment, we also imposed a gradient of bovine grazing pressure during the two drought years and three years of recovery following the drought. We found that rainfall reductions at both sites resulted in reductions in soil available P and micronutrients during treatment application. Conversely, rainfall reductions caused both immediate and persistent increases in soil NO<sub>3</sub><sup>-</sup>. Soil nutrients were generally unaffected by grazing treatments. In contrast, biotic soil properties including the activities of six extracellular enzymes and bacterial and fungal community compositions were relatively resistant to rainfall reduction treatments. However, grazing treatments appeared to have a greater effect on extracellular enzyme activity potentials and soil microbial community composition. Overall, our results highlight the relative stability of belowground processes in semi-arid rangelands in the face of drought and land management strategies.</p><p dir=\"ltr\">The article utilizing this dataset is at <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.soilbio.2025.110071\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" target=\"_blank\">https://doi.org/10.1016/j.soilbio.2025.110071</a>.</p>','public','2026-03-13T22:47:43.408039','2026-03-13T22:47:43.408046','Agricultural Research Service','Komatsu, Kimberly J.','005:18','d9a25cc1-3274-424d-8f23-3b5318eff060','USDA JSON','0570a8574fc50110d0653ae64cc3c1ab75b718f8aa4b793233e6e1e0e560684f','1.1','2026-03-13T22:47:43.408039','2026-03-13T22:47:43.408046',NULL,'005:040',0,'usda-gov'),('21e9876c-66ea-4110-8f35-73b6001ffc35','Walton-Smith CTD, WS0718, WS0718_WS0718_005, 2007-07-08, 25.0933N 80.355W','Walton-Smith Conductivity, Temperature, Depth (CTD) - WS0718 - WS0718_WS0718_005 - 2007-07-08 - 25.0933N 80.355W. Hydrographic Measurements in the Gulf of Mexico. flags: 1 = good; 3 =  mean ÃÂ± 3*standard deviation; 4 = mean ÃÂ± 5*standard deviation; 9 = missing','public','2026-03-26T19:16:13.725572','2026-03-26T19:16:13.725578',NULL,NULL,NULL,'76486ad7-df7c-4001-9a40-f77bf45e8e59','ioos',NULL,NULL,'2026-03-26T19:16:13.725572','2026-03-26T19:16:13.725578',NULL,NULL,NULL,'noaa-gov'),('21f74a34-401d-44fc-a1e2-732d7c49851a','VOYAGER 1 JUPITER MAGNETOMETER RESAMPLED DATA 1.92 SEC','This data set includes Voyager 1 Jupiter encounter magnetometer data that have been resampled at a 1.92 second sample rate. The data set is composed of 6 columns: 1) ctime - this column contains the data acquisition time. The time is always output in the ISO standard spacecraft event time format (yyyy-mm-dd-Thh:mm:ss.sss) but is stored internally in Cline time which is measured in seconds after 00:00:00.000 Jan 01, 1966, 2) br - this column contains the radial component of the magnetic field, 3) bphi - this column contains the phi component of the magnetic field, 4) btheta - this column contains the theta component of the magnetic field, 5) bmag - this column contains the magnitude of the magnetic field, 6) flag - a flag value that indicates either software error or spacecraft hardware interference reduced confidence in this record (flag value of 1 is bad , 0 is good or unchecked). All magnetic field observations are measured in nanoTeslas. The coordinate system for this dataset is Minus System III. All of the magnetic field data are calibrated (see the instrument calibration description for more details). The Jupiter System III coordinate system is defined in Dessler 1983 and the reference documents for this dataset are: Ness et al, 1979 Lepping et al, 1981 Connerney,Acuna,Ness, 1981 Behannon,Burlaga,Ness, 1981','public','2026-03-13T19:22:59.407020','2026-03-13T19:22:59.407026','Planetary Plasma Interactions','Planetary Data System','026:00','c0aedaac-300b-4c71-a1de-2582a469df64','NASA Data.json','1cb4a8b3ffaaeddbd7128a8f9cd5fbe68c3344dd9ba9558e5dcd1d4d691132d0','1.1','2026-03-13T19:22:59.407020','2026-03-13T19:22:59.407026','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('2224c7f6-4e3a-427a-a0e2-9a16581b5886','FAST Eddy Sys 2  Transect 60, 150kHz kHz VMADCP','Program of vessel mount ADCP measurements comprising a combination of 75kHz and 150kHz ADCP data collected in the vicinity of the Loop Current and drilling blocks between 2009 and 2020.','public','2026-03-26T19:15:56.534280','2026-03-26T19:15:56.534286',NULL,NULL,NULL,'d31d3055-762a-4133-8693-d1f40becf7de','ioos',NULL,NULL,'2026-03-26T19:15:56.534280','2026-03-26T19:15:56.534286',NULL,NULL,NULL,'noaa-gov'),('228c5e41-7bc0-45aa-9a08-041e97032e2f','VENUS CLIMATE ORBITER LIR CALIBRATED DATA V1.0','The VCO LIR CDR data set contains products acquired by the LIR instrument onboard the Venus Climate Orbiter (VCO, also known as PLANET-C and AKATSUKI) spacecraft. The data files are provided in FITS format with an HDU as IMAGE extension, and it also contains metadata to the header of the HDU.','public','2026-03-13T16:39:02.735009','2026-03-13T16:39:02.735014','Planetary Atmospheres','Planetary Data System','026:00','8ab3a9c9-bd35-45b4-b726-ccded5334544','NASA Data.json','fc378eab8fa330379333c70c44e8d70a766d3b85b5c48febd8eccde8d4470fa6','1.1','2026-03-13T16:39:02.735009','2026-03-13T16:39:02.735014','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('22b60872-2883-46f6-a6c6-1e6011c22871','Continuous Fixed Station Water Quality Measurements in Timucuan Ecological and Historic Preserve, September 2008 (Certified)','This dataset represents continuous water quality measurements that were taken at a fixed point just outside of Timucuan Ecological and Historic Preserve during the month of September, 2008 as a part of the Fixed Station Water Quality Monitoring protocol that was developed by the Southeast Coast I&M Network (SECN). The measurements were taken by a YSI 6600 ESD Multi-Parameter Long Term Water Quality Monitoring Datasonde unit that serves as the standard fixed station water quality monitoring equipment for all similar operations conducted by the SECN. The following parameters were measured at 30 minute intervals during the time period that has been specified: Water Temperature, Specific Conductivity, Salinity, Dissolved Oxygen (DO), DO Concentration, Shallow Depth, pH Level, and Turbidity. Any anomalies noted regarding these parameters have also been noted in separate fields. Please note that these measurements have been certified by network personnel.','public','2026-03-26T05:33:58.402033','2026-03-26T05:33:58.402038','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','fe9ef0f7-a623-4680-89b9-a52146a8892a','DOI NPS DCAT-US','7ba17a165f65032cec01f8adaf541127adf70051f8685357dd1b89ed896d66a0','1.1','2026-03-26T05:33:58.402033','2026-03-26T05:33:58.402038','Vector Dataset','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('22d9b250-44bc-439b-a99c-638d09ee1203','\"NEGOM CTD - n9l11s16.nc - 27.5N, 85.23W - 2000-00-07\"','The Northeastern Gulf of Mexico Physical Oceanography Program (NEGOM) is supported by the Minerals Management Service (MMS) of the U.S. Department of the Interior. Through a contract between MMS and the Texas A&M Research Foundation, several components of the Texas A&M University System are conducting the Chemical Oceanography and Hydrography study of NEGOM (NEGOM-COH). This report covers activities from October 1997 through June 1998. Data were collected from hydrographic and acoustic Doppler current profiler (ADCP) surveys conducted in the Gulf of Mexico over the continental shelf and upper slope between the Mississippi delta and Tampa Bay in water depths of 10 to 1000 m. Additionally, historical and concurrent data from other programs in this region were collected. Two hydrographic/ADCP surveys, N1 and N2, were conducted with 94 and 98 hydrographic sampling stations and with 80 and 97 expendable bathythermograph stations on respective cruises. Each survey also included continuous ADCP measurements along the cruise track. At each hydrographic sampling station continuous profiles were made of conductivity, temperature, pressure, downwelling irradiance, fluorescence, and light transmission. Up to twelve water samples were taken at each station and analyzed for dissolved oxygen and six nutrients: nitrate, nitrite, phosphate, silicate, ammonium, and urea. At 51 stations on cruise N1 and 61 on N2, water samples were filtered and analyzed for phytoplankton pigments at the surface and from the chlorophyll maximum and the low light regime immediately below it. Pigments were determined using high performance liquid chromatography. At 60 stations on each cruise, water samples were filtered and analyzed for particulate matter concentrations at surface, middle, and bottom water depths and for particulate organic carbon concentrations at surface and bottom water depths. Bottle salinity was measured at every station on the first cruise and at the shallowest and deepest stations on each cross-shelf line on the second. The instrumentation as well as calibration and sampling procedures are described in this report. The collected data were subjected to stringent quality assurance/quality control procedures.','public','2026-03-26T19:17:20.200297','2026-03-26T19:17:20.200303',NULL,NULL,NULL,'567c3532-3ecd-46ed-bdbe-72bed50aa096','ioos',NULL,NULL,'2026-03-26T19:17:20.200297','2026-03-26T19:17:20.200303',NULL,NULL,NULL,'noaa-gov'),('231c9c22-0230-40d3-aed1-0a6626e1604b','ROSETTA-ORBITER CHECKOUT OSIWAC 2 CR1 EDR V1.0','This CODMAC level 2 data set contains uncalibrated image data in DN unit,  acquired by the OSIRIS Wide Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft  during the CRUISE 1 mission phase, covering the period  from 2004-06-07T00:00:00.000 to 2004-09-05T23:59:59.000. The prime objective was commissioning / calibration. Several targets of opportunity were observed, but none of them is identifiable as prime target. After the October 2018 PSA/PDS external peer review, the COMMISSIONING  data set was reprocessed and split into multiple data sets. This  version V1.0 is one part and supersedes the previous delivery.','public','2026-03-13T16:49:27.449159','2026-03-13T16:49:27.449166','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','be32c0e3-34ea-4a98-893b-d73f1def9509','NASA Data.json','3c3d321e932e121fbb88cf418b77c0413942941c4560fb56b406a828828869e2','1.1','2026-03-13T16:49:27.449159','2026-03-13T16:49:27.449166','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('234ac3cf-23c3-4ac3-baa5-ca91dda56c34','EGIS - Enterprise Gateway Integration Services-EGIS Common Audit Database (CAS)','CAS is the foundation infrastructure that provides the EGIS Microservices with DHS 4300 A compliant audit services.','non-public','2026-03-22T11:55:04.883228','2026-03-22T11:55:04.883234','Unspecified','Open Data (MGMT)','024:030','b0717cb9-eaf6-47f0-88c6-7f29013402f1','DHS datajson source','10c6dd4df946ca3f15f32761bf3f9cc5337cde1c0ce9be23fa8a04da2a648274','1.1','2026-03-22T11:55:04.883228','2026-03-22T11:55:04.883234',NULL,'024:000',0,'dhs-gov'),('2376ab20-c517-47a7-bd51-6bd4df810716','Ordinance 20060302-008','Ordinance 20060302-008','public','2026-03-25T14:42:32.707807','2026-03-25T14:42:32.707812','data.austintexas.gov','Haileigh.Meyers@austintexas.gov',NULL,'2bd9bca6-0e29-4aa4-844e-c993c660f3c3','City of Austin Data.json','8ea91674f1d58b5fe805102f2b9942eba907bc3ac948c42b4a9662392c0dde4b','1.1','2026-03-25T14:42:32.707807','2026-03-25T14:42:32.707812',NULL,NULL,0,'city-of-austin'),('237da9f7-fa8d-4c54-84b8-316f609dbdd9','AIRS/Aqua L1B Near Real Time (NRT) AMSU (A1/A2) geolocated and calibrated brightness temperatures V005 (AIRABRAD_NRT) at GES DISC','The AMSU-A Level 1B Near Real Time (NRT) product (AIRABRAD_NRT_005) differs from the routine product (AIRABRAD_005) in 2 ways to meet the three hour latency requirements of the Land Atmosphere NRT Capability Earth Observing System (LANCE): (1) The NRT granules are produced without previous or subsequent granules if those granules are not available within 5 minutes, (2) the predictive ephemeris/attitude data are used rather than the definitive ephemeris/attitude. The consequences of these differences are described in the AIRS Near Real Time (NRT) data products document. The Atmospheric Infrared Sounder (AIRS) is a grating spectrometer (R = 1200) aboard the second Earth Observing System (EOS) polar-orbiting platform, EOS Aqua. In combination with the Advanced Microwave Sounding Unit (AMSU) and the Humidity Sounder for Brazil (HSB), AIRS constitutes an innovative atmospheric sounding group of visible, infrared, and microwave sensors. The AMSU-A instrument is co-aligned with AIRS so that successive blocks of 3 x 3 AIRS footprints are contained within one AMSU-A footprint. AMSU-A is primarily a temperature sounder that provides atmospheric information in the presence of clouds, which can be used to correct the AIRS infrared measurements for the effects of clouds. This is possible because non-precipitating clouds are for the most part transparent to microwave radiation, in contrast to visible and infrared radiation which are strongly scattered and absorbed by clouds. AMSU-A1 has 13 channels from 50 - 90 GHz and AMSU-A2 has 2 channels from 23 - 32 GHz. The AIRABRAD_NRT_005 products are stored in files (often referred to as \"granules\") that contain 6 minutes of data, 30 footprints across track by 45 lines along track.','public','2026-03-13T19:08:59.445669','2026-03-13T19:08:59.445674','NASA/GSFC/SED/ESD/TISL/GESDISC','Earthdata Forum','026:00','4901dde6-a713-4842-a8a7-b4e09d669b68','NASA Data.json','60ec7dd2f85f8e37aee61253436aced6b278273b254ad96eaf9635279c626831','1.1','2026-03-13T19:08:59.445669','2026-03-13T19:08:59.445674','Earth Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('2386ba7c-740a-49a5-815c-ef8aac2d570b','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RPCICA 2 EXT1 UNCALIBRATED V2.0','This dataset contains RAW DATA from the RPCICA instrument onmission ROSETTA during Rosetta extension 1.Data contains measurements of solar wind interactionwith the atmosphere of target comet 67P.Data set version 2 replaces a previously delivered data set.Important changes are the the expansion of data to a uniform resolution,Inclusion of the mode variable and new quality flags in the data andmoving Information about software version, BAD_HV_MASK and SHADOW_MASKto the label.','public','2026-03-13T18:05:01.969736','2026-03-13T18:05:01.969743','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','47b285e9-e7ba-46b8-885e-3e36c10e0d46','NASA Data.json','7cdfb5f6ff9e191c2c63758d8f0fbe7285e824964e1474d3ca7425c8fec7debe','1.1','2026-03-13T18:05:01.969736','2026-03-13T18:05:01.969743','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('23a5e354-a14c-476a-8b6b-27b256fefdf9','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 2 0729 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 2 phase 2015-03-11 to 2015-06-30. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-04-24T21:15:55.000 to 2015-04-25T01:53:30.000.','public','2026-03-13T17:06:17.351941','2026-03-13T17:06:17.351950','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','a18c5df8-237c-4306-af34-4538524522c7','NASA Data.json','2cbcd71c2537ee1daf0feb30ac7e54e2b80849f8a2b52dafba4fd0c6f8e5f70d','1.1','2026-03-13T17:06:17.351941','2026-03-13T17:06:17.351950','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('23e35c53-bdc7-4009-815e-2c624dd182d4','AIRS/Aqua L1B Near Real Time (NRT) Visible/Near Infrared (VIS/NIR) quality assurance subset V005 (AIRVBQAP_NRT) at GES DISC','The AIRS Level 1B Near Real Time (NRT) product (AIRVBQAP_NRT_005) differs from the routine product (AIRVBQAP_005) in 2 ways to meet the three hour latency requirements of the Land Atmosphere NRT Capability Earth Observing System (LANCE): (1) The NRT granules are produced without previous or subsequent granules if those granules are not available within 5 minutes, (2) the predictive ephemeris/attitude data are used rather than the definitive ephemeris/attitude. The consequences of these differences are described in the AIRS Near Real Time (NRT) data products document. The Atmospheric Infrared Sounder (AIRS) Visible/Near Infrared (VIS/NIR) instrument in combination with the AIRS Infrared Spectrometer, the Advanced Microwave Sounding Unit (AMSU) and the Humidity Sounder for Brazil (HSB) constitute an innovative atmospheric sounding group aboard the Earth Observing System (EOS) Aqua platform in a near-polar Sun-synchronous orbit with a 1:30 AM/PM equator crossing time and an ~705 km altitude. The AIRS Visible/Near Infrared (VIS/NIR) Level 1B QA Subset contains Quality Assurance (QA) parameters that a may use of filter AIRS VIS/NIR Level 1B radiance data to create a subset of analysis. It includes \"state\" that user should check before using any VIS/NIR Level 1B data radiance and \"glintlat\", \"glintlon\", and \"sun_glint_distant\" that users can use to check for possibility of solar glint contamination. AIRS VIS/NIR Level 1B radiance data can be found in AIRVBRAD.','public','2026-03-13T19:09:16.370402','2026-03-13T19:09:16.370408','NASA/GSFC/SED/ESD/TISL/GESDISC','Earthdata Forum','026:00','df990742-ada3-4ceb-b354-abee01537121','NASA Data.json','6dbf5e93257a4b5f458f1bc9311e246a9f961ed9f7416a697264db5c3bfd071c','1.1','2026-03-13T19:09:16.370402','2026-03-13T19:09:16.370408','Earth Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('23ec50c1-4a24-4d92-876c-fac734821b4a','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSIWAC 2 PRL-MTP006 EDR V3.0','This CODMAC level 2 data set contains uncalibrated image data in DN unit, acquired by the OSIRIS Wide Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft during the PRELANDING mission phase, covering the period from 2014-08-01T10:00:00.000 to 2014-09-02T09:59:59.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V3.0 supersedes previous deliveries of the same dataset with the following changes since the last version: Lien corrected dataset after the July and October 2018 PSA/PDS external peer reviews. Updated documentation and ancillary files, added document on bandpass filter. Updated SCIENCE_USER_GUIDE_V03.PDF to include one section about FAQ and one section about image data quality. Added shutter backtravel and readout issues to image quality map. Updated DATA_QUALITY_ID keyword in image header. Improved handling of images with missing packets. Included FITs files. Browse products changed to the same size as the original image.','public','2026-03-13T16:41:19.369185','2026-03-13T16:41:19.369189','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','beb2e510-a7a1-4c04-ab34-1b7ebdbbc762','NASA Data.json','32c9424a635d21890d7ea046d212e39df2d0a75e0c4922f0f7f3525475f6cf40','1.1','2026-03-13T16:41:19.369185','2026-03-13T16:41:19.369189','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('241d4b09-65ba-4d44-b90e-a0f5bf2d3bf0','DEEP IMPACT 9P/TEMPEL ENCOUNTER - RAW HRII SPECTRA V1.0','This data set contains raw 9P/Tempel 1 and science calibration spectra acquired by the Deep Impact High Resolution Instrument Infrared Spectrometer during the 9P encounter phase of the mission.','public','2026-03-13T17:12:51.629095','2026-03-13T17:12:51.629101','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','4c2f956c-ab02-4958-96c6-8882456d2669','NASA Data.json','faeb27b27badc930ad110df2cf8bf2406c9578494288d09d4be5a4906a9681a1','1.1','2026-03-13T17:12:51.629095','2026-03-13T17:12:51.629101','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('242fdf61-1145-4154-aa05-9fb1dc6ac459','IHW COMET NNSN CALIBRATED EXPERIMENT DATA RECORD GZ V1.0','In preparation for the concerted international study of Comet Halley, the IHW conducted a trial run with observations of Comet Crommelin, largely during February and March of 1984.','public','2026-03-13T17:09:50.488378','2026-03-13T17:09:50.488383','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','59c06699-8509-4f05-be73-0ed71b58a83e','NASA Data.json','a5fbf442183fb578b6f5b7595140da09fd8c4bb4cc8ecb4f8f7534892dfc6709','1.1','2026-03-13T17:09:50.488378','2026-03-13T17:09:50.488383','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('2434a29f-fa82-4b78-82ca-5cdfe2ecf13f','ODYSSEY MARS MARIE REFORMATTED RAW DATA V1.0','The MARIE (Martian Radiation Environment Experiment), aboard the 2001       Mars Odyssey spacecraft, was launched on April 7, 2001, and arrived at       Mars on October 24, 2001.  Data were collected intermittently during       the cruise phase, starting in late April and ending in late July.  A       problem with MARIE&apos;s onboard computer occurred in early August,       and the instrument was turned off until early March 2002, after Odyssey       &apos;s mapping orbit had been established.  Data have been collected       from that time to the present without major interruption.  Routine       minor interruptions of up to 48 hours have occurred during the orbital       phase when the instrument&apos;s data is erased from local storage       (after having been downloaded).  MARIE is oriented to point in the       direction opposite Odyssey&apos;s velocity vector.  Space radiation is       for the most part isotropic, so the orientation of Odyssey is usually       not critical and references to external coordinate systems are not a       part of the data returned by MARIE.  There is one exception to the       statement that space radiation is isotropic: During the early stages of       solar particle events, there can be directionality in the particle       flux.','public','2026-03-13T19:13:40.658290','2026-03-13T19:13:40.658295','planetary plasma interactions','Planetary Data System','026:00','d828f9e9-20a8-499e-83a7-7969b2b7668d','NASA Data.json','a0416f9ecaa96aed6ecf517cde472f7b0a1a08b87b495669529ec8b9e079bc8f','1.1','2026-03-13T19:13:40.658290','2026-03-13T19:13:40.658295','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('24c10a42-4d3a-406c-bcaf-ec59b5bc8010','Okeanos Explorer (EX1503L1): Tropical Exploration							(Mapping I)','Multibeam data will be collected 24 hours a day and XBT casts\n					will be conducted at an interval defined by prevailing oceanographic conditions,\n					but not to exceed 6 hours. Additionally, EK60 single beam and sub-bottom profile\n					data will be collected 24 hours per day. Data will only be collected in foreign\n					waters where clearance has been granted. If no permit was obtained, all data\n					collection systems will be shut down in those foreign waters. All multibeam data\n					will be fully processed according to standard onboard\n					procedures.','public','2026-03-28T23:16:43.176140','2026-03-28T23:16:43.176146',NULL,NULL,NULL,'a47b82f3-a8c7-446e-9e5c-8a6da60c6cd8','NCDDC OER',NULL,NULL,'2026-03-28T23:16:43.176140','2026-03-28T23:16:43.176146',NULL,NULL,NULL,'noaa-gov'),('258246b0-5920-4de7-a602-d3ec0dd7b017','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RPCLAP 2 ESC3 MTP021 V1.0','This dataset contains EDITED data from Rosetta RPC-LAP, acquired during MTP21, part of the COMET ESCORT 3 mission phase. The primary target was comet 67P/C-G.','public','2026-03-13T20:00:38.850213','2026-03-13T20:00:38.850219','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','5d3eb89c-447f-4b57-962d-3c5f4a7ecb03','NASA Data.json','3f97a64d9eefc3630af43a1ee923e5490135483b1b8bb0b948d88d0ef5b564b4','1.1','2026-03-13T20:00:38.850213','2026-03-13T20:00:38.850219','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('25858aa8-92f4-4e0e-8c88-2afdaf5a830d','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 4 1126 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 4 phase 2015-10-22 to 2015-12-31. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-10-25T01:56:20.000 to 2015-10-25T05:08:18.000.','public','2026-03-13T16:57:17.662369','2026-03-13T16:57:17.662374','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','9a678942-94fa-4743-89ac-2a57d80ac26d','NASA Data.json','f299aade66a4718fb04756e06b34e53da5f50afa5ea6405c9ae1910f1d1981a3','1.1','2026-03-13T16:57:17.662369','2026-03-13T16:57:17.662374','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('258c8caf-357d-4d8d-b72e-555c877c514d','Okeanos Explorer (EX1710): Canal Transit and Gulf of							Mexico Mapping (Mapping)','Multibeam and splitbeam mapping operations will be conducted 24\n					hours a day throughout the cruise. Sub-bottom profile mapping will be conducted\n					24 hours a day at the discretion of the CO. XBT and/or Underway CTD sound\n					velocity casts in support of multibeam sonar mapping operations will be\n					conducted at an interval defined by prevailing oceanographic conditions, but not\n					to exceed 6 hours. All mapping data will be fully processed according to\n					standard procedures and will be archived with the National Centers for\n					Environmental Information (NCEI).','public','2026-03-28T23:17:22.586383','2026-03-28T23:17:22.586391',NULL,NULL,NULL,'5b39fa54-5fa7-4ded-994a-e81e3b9a16ad','NCDDC OER',NULL,NULL,'2026-03-28T23:17:22.586383','2026-03-28T23:17:22.586391',NULL,NULL,NULL,'noaa-gov'),('2593ac1b-dd4a-4c2d-b4d8-f20324fe2f28','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 2 0827 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 2 phase 2015-03-11 to 2015-06-30. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-06-05T09:28:55.000 to 2015-06-05T17:10:12.000.','public','2026-03-13T17:19:00.318457','2026-03-13T17:19:00.318465','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','ed608414-3995-4eb6-85bd-29c41300ef45','NASA Data.json','37a299c4c6b8119b24d27af525982b885837147bd75fedec399816552a7f06f9','1.1','2026-03-13T17:19:00.318457','2026-03-13T17:19:00.318465','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('25d150c0-a9e6-4130-b3a1-3a6271fb3bf5','MARS EXPRESS MARS MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 4 3585 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2013-01-01 to 2014-12-31. It is a Global Gravity measurement and covers the time 2013-06-10T04:20:13.000 to 2013-06-10T06:06:58.500.','public','2026-03-13T20:01:43.393239','2026-03-13T20:01:43.393244','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','b5ca6e08-c67b-446b-a3eb-8bf3432ef8b7','NASA Data.json','a41d8e9969802ca341a11e19cb241aee632bd796c9ac7073359a143c74a0c97c','1.1','2026-03-13T20:01:43.393239','2026-03-13T20:01:43.393244','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('25e7eb16-181d-4b9c-b12c-34cb63db3cd5','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 PRELANDING 0246 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the PRELANDING phase 2014-01-21 to 2014-11-18. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2014-08-26T23:02:45.000 to 2014-08-27T01:06:47.000.','public','2026-03-13T17:12:26.752122','2026-03-13T17:12:26.752129','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','f9d6ee40-1627-461b-8aca-01d8e43c7d8d','NASA Data.json','9b6c726df42a8a84f1989e501165187d8a91383783ebbbdab9fc9d38611f9aa2','1.1','2026-03-13T17:12:26.752122','2026-03-13T17:12:26.752129','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('26584b13-a941-4d89-af20-089eb295cb25','GALILEO ORBITER ASTEROID AND EARTH 2 SOLID STATE IMAGING 2 R','This data set has been generated by NASA\'s Galileo Project in order to distribute the images acquired by the Solid State Imaging (SSI) camera to the scientists and later to the Planetary Data System (PDS). The collection resides on volumes GO_0007 thru GO_0015 and consists of all images acquired by the Galileo spacecraft during the Gaspra and the second encounter with the Earth (Earth2). Included are images of Gaspra, the Earth\'s Moon and the Earth taken during the 1991 and 1992 encounters (SCLK 99757945 through 166324700), as well as additional star and calibration data.','public','2026-03-13T19:21:10.371135','2026-03-13T19:21:10.371141','Imaging','Planetary Data System','026:00','678eeaa1-39de-4a7f-9243-c63723916148','NASA Data.json','49808a82ba16de0d5a77bd89241814353c8fc42b71816b40d4470e05bb1119ff','1.1','2026-03-13T19:21:10.371135','2026-03-13T19:21:10.371141','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('2662f56c-2614-4d2c-89d2-19e176d94826','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 ROSETTA EXTENSION 1 1412 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the ROSETTA EXTENSION 1 phase 2016-01-01 to 2016-04-05. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2016-02-09T03:10:25.000 to 2016-02-09T12:20:36.500.','public','2026-03-13T18:43:56.615904','2026-03-13T18:43:56.615909','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','36393a94-0a85-4702-b7c7-04b8c8c8c546','NASA Data.json','0e834b1478b8fcf5960e13e611478a35dc3e3f7cfd20c36b0e1b9d3cce6c3f0f','1.1','2026-03-13T18:43:56.615904','2026-03-13T18:43:56.615909','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('266c27ee-2b8c-4ab2-b747-e44a8b20ad1f','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSINAC 4 ESC2-MTP017 RDR-INFLDSTR V1.0','This CODMAC level 4 data set contains solar stray-light corrected, in-field stray-light corrected,  radiometric calibrated and geometric distortion corrected  (resampled) image data in W/m^2/sr/nm,  acquired by the OSIRIS Narrow Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft  during the COMET ESCORT 2 mission phase, covering the period  from 2015-06-02T23:25:00.000 to 2015-06-30T23:24:59.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V1.0 is the first version of this dataset: Lien corrected dataset after September 2019 PSA/PDS external peer review.','public','2026-03-13T20:07:55.825990','2026-03-13T20:07:55.825997','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','6768314b-97e0-4631-8b2d-1bc7627ac733','NASA Data.json','b1d079a088ecaf242733b5edc162903f63af8da8cf14ee2f23eb92105c351d81','1.1','2026-03-13T20:07:55.825990','2026-03-13T20:07:55.825997','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('268065d6-c468-4386-ab05-bd6ef70f072e','Continuous Fixed Station Water Quality Measurements in Cape Lookout National Seashore, January 2009 (Certified)','This dataset represents continuous water quality measurements that were taken at a fixed point in Cape Lookout National Seashore during the month of January, 2009 as a part of the Fixed Station Water Quality Monitoring protocol that was developed by the Southeast Coast I&M Network (SECN). The measurements were taken by a YSI 6600 ESD Multi-Parameter Long Term Water Quality Monitoring Datasonde unit that serves as the standard fixed station water quality monitoring equipment for all similar operations conducted by the SECN. The following parameters were measured at 15 minute intervals during the time period that has been specified: Water Temperature, Specific Conductivity, Salinity, Dissolved Oxygen (DO), DO Concentration, Shallow Depth, pH Level, and Turbidity. Any anomalies noted regarding these parameters have also been noted in separate fields.  Please note that these measurements have been certified by network personnel.','public','2026-03-26T05:28:13.078713','2026-03-26T05:28:13.078718','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','5629d2ea-7656-49ec-ac50-34a7aa56dddb','DOI NPS DCAT-US','e490918efea41498663276a86ca3f119151cd1a03de51973d937a0da1a8e26be','1.1','2026-03-26T05:28:13.078713','2026-03-26T05:28:13.078718','Vector Dataset','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('2681c7ad-821f-4ca0-9d53-007e0c646c4f','US Forest Atlas FIA Forest Ownership (Image Service)','<p><span style=\'background-color:rgb(255,255,255); color:rgb(76,76,76); font-family:&quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:15px;\'><span style=\'display:inline !important; float:none; font-style:normal; font-variant-caps:normal; font-variant-ligatures:normal; font-weight:400; letter-spacing:normal; text-align:left; text-decoration-color:initial; text-decoration-style:initial; text-indent:0px; text-transform:none; word-spacing:0px;\'>This data publication contains 250 meter raster data depicting the spatial distribution of forest ownership types in the conterminous United States. The data are a modeled representation of forest land by ownership type, and include three types of public ownership: federal, state, and local; three types of private: family (includes individuals and families), corporate, and other private (includes conservation and natural resource organizations, and unincorporated partnerships and associations); as well as Native American tribal lands. The most up-to-date data available were used in creating this data publication. A plurality of the ownership data were from 2014, but some data were as old as 2004.</span></span></p>','public','2026-03-13T22:49:54.521977','2026-03-13T22:49:54.521984','U.S. Forest Service','USFSEnterpriseContent','005:96','35cc27b5-76b1-473e-b159-6efbab38041b','USDA JSON','3f457ec1d20030210dc364e8a29409d529347785a1d2f3d72c2f428af0332b3b','1.1','2026-03-13T22:49:54.521977','2026-03-13T22:49:54.521984','geospatial','005:059',0,'usda-gov'),('26a62af9-e26d-40ea-90ab-4f9a34a93630','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P VIRTIS 3 ESCORT 4 MTP022 V2.0','This release contains the calibrated data of the VIRTIS instrument on board of the spacecraft Rosetta. This volume contains data from the ESCORT 4 MTP022 phase, which occurred from 2015-10-21 to 2015-11-18 when at the vicinity of comet 67P. This data set V2.0 supersedes V1.0. It includes major updates on the data and documentation.','public','2026-03-13T17:41:21.075488','2026-03-13T17:41:21.075493','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','e55f41fb-e4e4-48ba-9c64-cac8597486ff','NASA Data.json','c9c82cdc6496a1c8aaa5738cc68859a76fb9b6f6ab7f65abe77f5bd50785bb81','1.1','2026-03-13T17:41:21.075488','2026-03-13T17:41:21.075493','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('26f01e40-3bb5-4e8b-8b42-75b88419d261','NIMS RADIANCE POINT SPECTRA OF IDA AND DACTYL V1.0','This data volume contains radiometrically corrected point spectra of asteroid 243 Ida and a spectrum of the asteroid satellite Dactyl (Ida I) as acquired by the Galileo spacecraft Near Infrared Mapping Spectrometer (NIMS) on August 28, 1993. They record the spectra collected as the Galileo spacecraft approached the 243 Ida system. These data are products of the calibration of the raw data number files idu002tn.qub, idu005tn.qub, idu006tn.qub, idu007tn.qub, idu019tn.qub, idu020tn.qub, idu022tn.qub, idu028tn.qub, idu032tn.qub, idu033tn.qub, and idu035tn.qub (DATA SET ID :\'GO-A-NIMS-3-TUBE-V1.0\') with calibration factors acquired during the Jovian tour of the Galileo mission. These raw data .qub files are archived in the Imaging Node of the NASA Planetary Data System (PDS). The calibrated spectra consist of radiance and incidence/flux measurements for wavelengths between 0.7 - 5.2 micrometers.','public','2026-03-13T16:58:21.392812','2026-03-13T16:58:21.392818','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','83439363-8e75-4fb4-9325-e597db983968','NASA Data.json','55b7dcef79b9941d0e72bbd43443502d167dc53e39dba965fd53d851fd7fcccc','1.1','2026-03-13T16:58:21.392812','2026-03-13T16:58:21.392818','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('2719f143-bd73-4487-bf1b-5dc9cdae5d4b','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 4 1267 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 4 phase 2015-10-22 to 2015-12-31. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-12-19T04:59:35.000 to 2015-12-19T08:40:48.000.','public','2026-03-13T17:31:59.196809','2026-03-13T17:31:59.196814','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','c4eccb33-5337-4680-9810-1bd52061454d','NASA Data.json','8a2058b7cca88f3c8a9bab1ad6d96b774471041ed9ab59c5790edbcbb37bd412','1.1','2026-03-13T17:31:59.196809','2026-03-13T17:31:59.196814','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('2779a79b-0e03-4ce2-bbd4-38bac7f036e5','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 4 1180 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 4 phase 2015-10-22 to 2015-12-31. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-11-14T02:27:15.000 to 2015-11-14T07:25:06.500.','public','2026-03-13T17:27:17.243929','2026-03-13T17:27:17.243935','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','b03f2b32-65e6-47c7-a927-12eeda54596d','NASA Data.json','bc2dc1e4ff5c2e7f2e56442be9f425568ae41db1c48f18e6f3065e53cf83be38','1.1','2026-03-13T17:27:17.243929','2026-03-13T17:27:17.243935','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('278656e0-7aa7-443f-a809-7a4c2dc687f6','Moving Violations Issued in February 2026','<p>Moving citation locations in the District of Columbia. The <a href=\'https://visionzero.dc.gov\' target=\'_blank\' rel=\'nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer\'>Vision Zero</a> data contained in this layer pertain to moving violations issued by the District of Columbia\'s Metropolitan Police Department (MPD) and partner agencies with the authority. For example, DC\'s enforcement camera program cites speeders, blocking the box, and other moving offenses. Moving violation locations are summarized ticket counts based on time of day, week of year, year, and category of violation. Data was originally extracted from the District Department of Motor Vehicle\'s eTIMS meter work order management system. Data was then loaded into the DC GIS, where the Office of the Chief Technology Officer (OCTO) geocoded citation data to the street segment level. Data are visualized using the street segment centroid coordinates.</p>','public','2026-03-25T08:44:33.743073','2026-03-25T08:44:33.743079','District Department of Transportation','DCGISopendata',NULL,'d7268ad1-a4b3-4b14-b444-8f1e6c6411ab','DC data','9a2c9d3dc8b31960cdcfe3c712bc37640b1db44d1d4f6ed623e1ffdcc920b289','1.1','2026-03-25T08:44:33.743073','2026-03-25T08:44:33.743079','geospatial',NULL,0,'district-of-columbia'),('278bfa1a-8d3c-4016-a905-adea2086e17d','Continuous Fixed Station Water Quality Measurements in Cape Lookout National Seashore, March 2009 (Certified)','This dataset represents continuous water quality measurements that were taken at a fixed point in Cape Lookout National Seashore during the month of March, 2009 as a part of the Fixed Station Water Quality Monitoring protocol that was developed by the Southeast Coast I&M Network (SECN). The measurements were taken by a YSI 6600 ESD Multi-Parameter Long Term Water Quality Monitoring Datasonde unit that serves as the standard fixed station water quality monitoring equipment for all similar operations conducted by the SECN. The following parameters were measured at 15 minute intervals during the time period that has been specified: Water Temperature, Specific Conductivity, Salinity, Dissolved Oxygen (DO), DO Concentration, Shallow Depth, pH Level, and Turbidity. Any anomalies noted regarding these parameters have also been noted in separate fields.  Please note that these measurements have been certified by network personnel.','public','2026-03-26T05:28:14.423174','2026-03-26T05:28:14.423180','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','a83a6837-10ec-4203-a196-ff7856d9f2d1','DOI NPS DCAT-US','c36ba05cb4eacaff7bd5afe5d0584cfcc21248a5a929cb38975d51be69dcce93','1.1','2026-03-26T05:28:14.423174','2026-03-26T05:28:14.423180','Vector Dataset','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('27b0b3e1-5953-406f-8b2a-bdf9affebff8','MARS EXPRESS MARS MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 3 3286 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2010-01-01 to 2012-12-31. It is a Global Gravity measurement and covers the time 2012-05-13T12:11:47.000 to 2012-05-13T15:39:44.500.','public','2026-03-13T17:34:21.913043','2026-03-13T17:34:21.913049','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','7c00aa78-9647-4275-9a20-004b6607aa66','NASA Data.json','6a641c690375dcc8d586c0aede6116a866b4149e4c4864947fd023dfdd552de4','1.1','2026-03-13T17:34:21.913043','2026-03-13T17:34:21.913049','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('27c226f8-6362-4bc8-b1aa-d3dd6f65bada','Walton-Smith CTD, WS19028, WS19028_Stn58, 2019-01-31, 25.1658N 81.6532W','Walton-Smith Conductivity, Temperature, Depth (CTD) - WS19028 - WS19028_Stn58 - 2019-01-31 - 25.1658N 81.6532W. Hydrographic Measurements in the Gulf of Mexico. flags: 1 = good; 3 =  mean ÃÂ± 3*standard deviation; 4 = mean ÃÂ± 5*standard deviation; 9 = missing. other','public','2026-03-26T19:16:44.194167','2026-03-26T19:16:44.194173',NULL,NULL,NULL,'0b2e12f9-77ec-4da7-a7c2-7947a9ecdd12','ioos',NULL,NULL,'2026-03-26T19:16:44.194167','2026-03-26T19:16:44.194173',NULL,NULL,NULL,'noaa-gov'),('27e56baf-3d12-46a8-b0a8-2e6c1e7daf9b','ROSETTA-ORBITER/ROSETTA-LANDER CAL CONSERT 3 EAR3 V2.0','This archive contains CALIBRATED data (CODMAC level 3) that refers to target CALIBRATION from the CONSERT instrument onboard ROSETTA Orbiter and Lander, acquired during the EAR3 phase. In addition to the scientific signal of interest, it contains all the values applied to the signal for calibration. It also contains documentation which describes the CONSERT experiment. The data archived in this data set conform to the Planetary Data System (PDS) Standards, Version 3.6. V2.0 of this dataset includes additional cruise operations which were missing in V1.0.','public','2026-03-13T17:14:28.305662','2026-03-13T17:14:28.305668','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','0abd666c-cc0e-4fe0-b1a8-e39627c7d24f','NASA Data.json','809922613aac3608d8c2ee39fd56b6d8422a7204b662fabbed62ec2809e57d86','1.1','2026-03-13T17:14:28.305662','2026-03-13T17:14:28.305668','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('27ea1bc7-fe8d-442d-89e3-b1517d74604e','BLM ID Right Of Way Line','These are Rights-of-Ways (ROW) on Idaho BLM land (and some other Federal agency land) as shown on Bureau of Land Management (BLM) Master Title Plats (MTP). Every GIS ROW feature has a \"CASEFILE\" value, also known as the serial number of the ROW. The ROW data that was digitized is what was present on the MTP at the time of the digitizing done for that township. The project was performed over several years. Therefore, the \"early\" townships digitized are more out of date regarding ROWs compared to the ones more recently digitized. Unfortunately, there is no attribute that indicates the digitizing sequence. Any updates to this ROW feature class should be sent to the BLM Idaho State Office GIS staff for incorporation into the statewide GIS ROW feature classes for improvement over time. For more information contact us at blm_id_stateoffice@blm.gov.','public','2026-03-26T12:40:15.713093','2026-03-26T12:40:15.713099','Bureau of Land Management','Bureau of Land Management, blm_id_stateoffice','010:04','5e28ebf5-b0a3-48da-a278-0a8331036b78','DOI BLM DCAT-US','971a4850d32766d1f345c76147be87e3701e2cf6dad304a1486439e29e6eefdb','1.1','2026-03-26T12:40:15.713093','2026-03-26T12:40:15.713099','geospatial','010:000',0,'doi-gov'),('27ef5946-5b9d-458c-94a1-2a31d3377fd9','AIRS/Aqua L1B Near Real Time (NRT) Visible/Near Infrared (VIS/NIR) geolocated and calibrated radiances V005 (AIRVBRAD_NRT) at GES DISC','The AIRS Visible/Near Infrared (VIS/NIR) Level 1B Near Real Time (NRT) product (AIRVBRAD_NRT_005) differs from the routine product (AIRVBRAD_005) in 2 ways to meet the three hour latency requirements of the Land Atmosphere NRT Capability Earth Observing System (LANCE): (1) The NRT granules are produced without previous or subsequent granules if those granules are not available within 5 minutes, (2) the predictive ephemeris/attitude data are used rather than the definitive ephemeris/attitude. The consequences of these differences are described in the AIRS Near Real Time (NRT) data products document. The AIRS VIS/NIR level 1B data set contains visible and near-infrared calibrated and geolocated radiances in W/m^2/micron/steradian for 4 channels in the 0.4 to 1.0 um region of the spectrum. The spectral range of the VIS/NIR channels are as follows: Channel 1 0.41 um - 0.44 um, Channel 2 0.58 um - 0.68 um, Channel 3 0.71 um - 0.92 um, Channel 4 0.49 um - 0.94 um. The AIRVBRAD_NRT_005 products are stored in files (often referred to as \"granules\") that contain 6 minutes of data, 90 footprints across track by 135 lines along track. The VIS/NIR granules are only produced in the daytime so there will always be fewer VIS/NIR granules than Infrared or microwave granules.','public','2026-03-13T18:40:18.473149','2026-03-13T18:40:18.473155','NASA/GSFC/SED/ESD/TISL/GESDISC','Earthdata Forum','026:00','a20f87d6-0955-4ac6-9d6b-5d3484be6a5e','NASA Data.json','5ae472c98341fa7178374e31c9870857cd690b1398ef86ae309a0a81665ffeb7','1.1','2026-03-13T18:40:18.473149','2026-03-13T18:40:18.473155','Earth Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('282885e5-6680-4674-96a0-f8b897a25a3f','ROSETTA-ORBITER EARTH OSINAC 3 EAR1 RDR V2.0','This CODMAC level 3 data set contains radiometric calibrated image data in W/m^2/sr/nm,  acquired by the OSIRIS Narrow Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft  during the EARTH SWING-BY 1 mission phase, covering the period  from 2004-10-17T00:00:00.000 to 2005-04-04T23:59:59.000. The prime target is planet Earth. This version V2.0 supersedes previous deliveries of the same dataset with the following changes since the last version: Reprocessed dataset after October 2018 PSA/PDS external peer review.','public','2026-03-13T17:16:42.370599','2026-03-13T17:16:42.370604','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','890cf3b0-8f90-4084-8a98-2495f7b0d4f7','NASA Data.json','cd0b6f5846050480bded498a88e775369296f72febde650d9507030cd3fb8869','1.1','2026-03-13T17:16:42.370599','2026-03-13T17:16:42.370604','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('282c60f9-5f7b-48ff-b515-cfbb4eb81606','JUNO DERIVED RADIO SCIENCE GRAVITY DATA V1.0','This data set contains archival results from gravity investigations conducted during the Juno mission while the spacecraft was in orbit around Jupiter. X- and Ka-band Radio measusrements were made using the Juno spacecraft and Earth-based stations of the NASA Deep Space Network (DSN). Version 1.0 includes a spherical harmonic model of Jupiter\'s gravity field produced by Sapienza University of Rome; these results were derived from raw radio tracking data.','public','2026-03-13T16:59:04.566064','2026-03-13T16:59:04.566073','Planetary Atmospheres','Planetary Data System','026:00','b63d2915-d428-455b-96f4-e27bf33b277b','NASA Data.json','ad132ddcc5b0f61d78976ed312bb7c521c2c1158affb27b7b6767e4c36f83584','1.1','2026-03-13T16:59:04.566064','2026-03-13T16:59:04.566073','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('289beb0e-c2ec-48a3-8652-8ea4c1924021','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSINAC 4 ESC4-MTP023 RDR-STRLIGHT V1.0','This CODMAC level 4 data set contains solar stray light corrected, radiometric calibrated and geometric distortion corrected (resampled) image data in W/m^2/sr/nm, acquired by the OSIRIS Narrow Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft during the COMET ESCORT 4 mission phase, covering the period from 2015-11-17T23:25:00.000 to 2015-12-15T23:24:59.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V1.0 is the first version of this dataset: Lien corrected dataset after October 2018 PSA/PDS external peer review.','public','2026-03-13T19:02:11.226223','2026-03-13T19:02:11.226231','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','a41af8b2-6c02-412a-847f-a34cc7867fd7','NASA Data.json','a194085a51495258789f61d82be11c549633fbf72cb58a2cd3d84e545c0e9799','1.1','2026-03-13T19:02:11.226223','2026-03-13T19:02:11.226231','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('29431bf7-65a6-4ecc-8a57-82d541b3f6ac','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSINAC 2 PRL-MTP009 EDR V3.0','This CODMAC level 2 data set contains uncalibrated image data in DN unit, acquired by the OSIRIS Narrow Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft during the PRELANDING mission phase, covering the period from 2014-10-24T10:00:00.000 to 2014-11-21T23:24:59.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V3.0 supersedes previous deliveries of the same dataset with the following changes since the last version: Lien corrected dataset after the July and October 2018 PSA/PDS external peer reviews. Updated documentation and ancillary files, added document on bandpass filter. Updated SCIENCE_USER_GUIDE_V03.PDF to include one section about FAQ and one section about image data quality. Added shutter backtravel and readout issues to image quality map. Updated DATA_QUALITY_ID keyword in image header. Improved handling of images with missing packets. Included FITs files. Browse products changed to the same size as the original image.','public','2026-03-13T18:05:20.439656','2026-03-13T18:05:20.439662','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','77f9e043-ac19-455d-b0fa-cf3297768f00','NASA Data.json','9a8dc59e8e40b3d3ff8cc3e767e28ba9b039595c10bd20bca972240b9a008009','1.1','2026-03-13T18:05:20.439656','2026-03-13T18:05:20.439662','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('29607c65-a041-4cf9-9355-a7b77c66503f','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P VIRTIS 3 ESCORT 3 MTP019 V2.0','This release contains the calibrated data of the VIRTIS instrument on board of the spacecraft Rosetta. This volume contains data from the ESCORT 3 MTP019 phase, which occurred from 2015-07-29 to 2015-08-26 when at the vicinity of comet 67P. This data set V2.0 supersedes V1.0. It includes major updates on the data and documentation.','public','2026-03-13T20:00:50.117849','2026-03-13T20:00:50.117855','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','fa26bedf-6506-437a-9df0-13f2ccf72e9a','NASA Data.json','e7e2325644e7ea5d0db27678047cd6dcfcb3e52587967957c419997f933bfd07','1.1','2026-03-13T20:00:50.117849','2026-03-13T20:00:50.117855','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('296d1ffb-311d-4f3a-b35a-1abe4c62896b','ROSETTA-LANDER 67P PTOLEMY 2 RBD V1.0','This archive contains edited data from the PTOLEMY instrument onboard ROSETTA Lander, acquired during the RBD mission phase. The primary target is the comet 67P/CHURYUMOV-GERASIMENKO. It also contains documentation which describes the PTOLEMY experiment. The data archived in this data set conform to the Planetary Data System (PDS) Standards, Version 3.6.','public','2026-03-13T16:55:05.819306','2026-03-13T16:55:05.819311','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','359002ff-df88-45c5-aca3-f6fcb9af9810','NASA Data.json','dbe3460153643039ded53622e37dab26642358b25be9d05bf75194c7328b6023','1.1','2026-03-13T16:55:05.819306','2026-03-13T16:55:05.819311','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('298f44f1-6039-4508-a288-80f24289fcee','NPS Visitor Use Statistics Data Package, 2025','The NPS Social Science Program is responsible for coordinating visitor use\nstatistics reporting for units administered by the NPS. ‘Visitor Use Statistics’\nrefers to a formal set of statistics collected by the National Park Service that\naddress how many people visit parks and how long they stay. Program staff work\nwith parks to develop appropriate data collection procedures and provide quality\ncontrol for visitor use data. Such coordination ensures that visitor use data\nare consistent and reliable throughout all units of the National Park System.\nThis data package contains data collected from 1979-2025.\n\nDetailed instructions for the units that collect data, monthly visitation\nsummaries, and reports displaying trends in park visitation are available on the\nNPS Visitor Use Statistics website (https://irma.nps.gov/Stats/).','public','2026-03-28T05:45:10.160281','2026-03-28T05:45:10.160285','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','88b663ad-2898-4576-a66f-d906fd2dd04a','DOI NPS DCAT-US','9e8167c7b6349e61513db26570540cf419bb8e8d88f8f4f89301eb321b8b8080','1.1','2026-03-28T05:45:10.160281','2026-03-28T05:45:10.160285','Data Package','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('29992be4-8cce-4567-94cd-0ddc79f5bff3','VEGA1 DUST PARTICLE COUNTER MASS ANALYSER DATA V1.0','Encounter Data for Vega-1 included two files: DSFAST17 and Dvega101. These files were submitted by the Univ of Chicago group with hard copy versions of the operating manual and a preprint of results. The following explanation of the contents of the two files is below.','public','2026-03-13T19:10:17.495536','2026-03-13T19:10:17.495556','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','cd72c399-e0fd-4ad0-9d4d-4e33617fbd5d','NASA Data.json','0f47f882ca910a940936640d3a5d846032f2035cb63bcd9e7770da1585fbc1d7','1.1','2026-03-13T19:10:17.495536','2026-03-13T19:10:17.495556','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('29999b5b-4d52-4c6d-80d9-3ca0e3fcf819','Laborshed - Internet Sites and Newspapers','Laborshed dataset containing counts of the internet sites and newspapers used for job searching. Data covers all laborshed in Iowa.','public','2026-03-28T21:58:03.104671','2026-03-28T21:58:03.104675','data.iowa.gov','svqueen',NULL,'4fac5c8c-a3d4-40b4-8366-2b96125e1d1e','Iowa metadata','b0296b328953d14649958c23d6671ebb9167288bdb1055d7ce5e7e371dd619aa','1.1','2026-03-28T21:58:03.104671','2026-03-28T21:58:03.104675','Economic Statistics',NULL,0,'state-of-iowa'),('29e002d0-845f-4a2d-a411-ca77a927bb08','Continuous Fixed Station Water Quality Measurements in Timucuan Ecological and Historic Preserve, August 2008 (Certified)','This dataset represents continuous water quality measurements that were taken at a fixed point in Timucuan Ecological and Historic Preserve during the month of August, 2008 as a part of the Fixed Station Water Quality Monitoring protocol that was developed by the Southeast Coast I&M Network (SECN). The measurements were taken by a YSI 6600 ESD Multi-Parameter Long Term Water Quality Monitoring Datasonde unit that serves as the standard fixed station water quality monitoring equipment for all similar operations conducted by the SECN. The following parameters were measured at 30 minute intervals during the time period that has been specified: Water Temperature, Specific Conductivity, Salinity, Dissolved Oxygen (DO), DO Concentration, Shallow Depth, pH Level, and Turbidity. Any anomalies noted regarding these parameters have also been noted in separate fields. Please note that these measurements have been certified by network personnel.','public','2026-03-26T05:33:36.433579','2026-03-26T05:33:36.433586','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','e5c83932-d1fb-4ce2-9b85-add1856870cf','DOI NPS DCAT-US','d249b7c53939afd5eb4f21c981f4be733a639408452d9dea81a590ede394e2b0','1.1','2026-03-26T05:33:36.433579','2026-03-26T05:33:36.433586','Vector Dataset','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('29f1f99c-4f0b-4b5d-b3f5-ebbcb638cb32','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSINAC 4 ESC4-MTP024 RDR V1.0','This CODMAC level 4 data set contains radiometric calibrated and geometric distortion corrected (resampled) image data in W/m^2/sr/nm acquired by the OSIRIS Narrow Angle Camera during the COMET ESCORT 4 phase of the Rosetta mission, covering the period from 2015-12-15T23:25:00.000 to 2016-01-12T23:24:59.000.','public','2026-03-13T19:09:53.828251','2026-03-13T19:09:53.828259','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','89414ac4-f4da-482b-a026-58baf9762a5c','NASA Data.json','6435e9d529555ba7f1dd5685314b105b02bdbdee820c32b52c0a72ce602b7ea1','1.1','2026-03-13T19:09:53.828251','2026-03-13T19:09:53.828259','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('2a646f43-74de-44e3-9644-26b6956bba16','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P NAVCAM 3 COMET ESCORT 4 MTP024 V1.0','This dataset contains ROSETTA NAVCAM RADIOMETRICALLY CALIBRATED DATA of the COMET ESCORT 4 MTP024 Phase from 16 Dec. 2015, 06:02:17 to 12 Jan. 2016, 23:02:20 when at the vicinity of target 67P/CG.','public','2026-03-13T19:16:41.795488','2026-03-13T19:16:41.795495','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','891ba91f-eace-4773-9744-141c248b379f','NASA Data.json','60f87657308c7149afeb3bf9e6c20bd205c437f883677365ebefc4e2393cee00','1.1','2026-03-13T19:16:41.795488','2026-03-13T19:16:41.795495','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('2a7a301a-5b76-46d3-b543-19cb5478f961','ROSETTA-ORBITER EARTH OSIWAC 2 EAR1 EDR V2.0','This CODMAC level 2 data set contains uncalibrated image data in DN unit,  acquired by the OSIRIS Wide Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft  during the EARTH SWING-BY 1 mission phase, covering the period  from 2004-10-17T00:00:00.000 to 2005-04-04T23:59:59.000. The prime target is planet Earth. This version V2.0 supersedes previous deliveries of the same dataset with the following changes since the last version: Reprocessed dataset after October 2018 PSA/PDS external peer review.','public','2026-03-13T16:45:44.333876','2026-03-13T16:45:44.333882','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','79c3c7cb-279a-4d6c-a64f-5a9264779eb2','NASA Data.json','77f4ae5d3f497c23f1d0969cd423334ec159a6b10245353c7daed9570020a0c8','1.1','2026-03-13T16:45:44.333876','2026-03-13T16:45:44.333882','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('2ac683b4-4731-4202-a0a2-1795b284aa68','Occupational Skills Data','Occupational Information Network (ONET) defines occupational skills by analyzing work activities, tasks, and skills required for roughly 900 occupations. This dataset contains the top skills for each occupation.','public','2026-03-28T22:01:26.949749','2026-03-28T22:01:26.949753','data.iowa.gov','Katie Green',NULL,'d4c59dcb-df6c-4036-890f-7333bf24ade3','Iowa metadata','ebe2f18d5695fb7540e23983281afd6e3d14aa0a98f4460587aba340160e7295','1.1','2026-03-28T22:01:26.949749','2026-03-28T22:01:26.949753','Workforce',NULL,0,'state-of-iowa'),('2aca39d3-6b52-44e6-ae36-8ee10832e582','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSIWAC 3 PRL-MTP005 RDR V3.0','This CODMAC level 3 data set contains radiometric calibrated image data in W/m^2/sr/nm, acquired by the OSIRIS Wide Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft during the PRELANDING mission phase, covering the period from 2014-07-02T08:35:00.000 to 2014-08-01T09:59:59.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V3.0 supersedes previous deliveries of the same dataset with the following changes since the last version: Lien corrected dataset after the July and October 2018 PSA/PDS external peer reviews. Updated documentation and ancillary files, added document on bandpass filter. Updated SCIENCE_USER_GUIDE_V03.PDF to include one section about FAQ and one section about image data quality. Added shutter backtravel and readout issues to image quality map. Updated DATA_QUALITY_ID keyword in image header. Improved handling of images with missing packets. Included FITs files. Browse products changed to the same size as the original image.','public','2026-03-13T18:20:58.697753','2026-03-13T18:20:58.697759','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','3f90d044-770e-4c37-8069-b83955aeb77b','NASA Data.json','670ca6a967dc1b91094c81f99e23c2e4dcb399d20337ac8b193322b68e87bed3','1.1','2026-03-13T18:20:58.697753','2026-03-13T18:20:58.697759','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('2acda84d-93fd-4656-8834-7efe7b7bd03f','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSIWAC 4 EXT2-MTP029 RDR-REFLECT V1.0','This CODMAC level 4 data set contains radiometric calibrated and geometric distortion corrected (resampled) image data in reflectance units (normalized and thus without unit), acquired by the OSIRIS Wide Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft during the ROSETTA EXTENSION 2 mission phase, covering the period from 2016-05-03T23:25:00.000 to 2016-05-31T23:24:59.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V1.0 is the first version of this dataset: Lien corrected dataset after October 2018 PSA/PDS external peer review.','public','2026-03-13T19:20:41.947322','2026-03-13T19:20:41.947331','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','f213dfee-e8f3-459b-b530-5f6851edc54b','NASA Data.json','461ba4aead3bd4c0e614df8d1d4420aaa1101b0505ec0c76547b7fe154a1edef','1.1','2026-03-13T19:20:41.947322','2026-03-13T19:20:41.947331','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('2ae5c934-34b1-4e28-afda-ec41f8c5819c','MARS EXPRESS MARS MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 7 4152 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2019-01-01 to 2020-12-31. It is a Occultation measurement and covers the time 2020-11-19T11:32:33.000 to 2020-11-19T11:54:41.500.','public','2026-03-13T16:59:56.698048','2026-03-13T16:59:56.698053','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','9453d8d0-b826-4a40-b6e2-a92947669da8','NASA Data.json','0def331d545f8b074395017d8e938367d6fa17a27838524f20d8c246e28665d5','1.1','2026-03-13T16:59:56.698048','2026-03-13T16:59:56.698053','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('2ae73f8c-d88b-4493-8227-afe44f78f66f','VL1/VL2 MARS LCS DERIVED ATMOSPHERIC OPTICAL DEPTH V1.0','Viking Lander camera images of the Sun were used to compute total normal atmospheric optical depth at the two landing sites over a period of about 900 Mars days. The data set contains 1044 measurements of optical depth and associated error estimates. The optical depths were derived from Sun diode images, which were obtained by the Lander cameras at a wavelength of 0.67 micrometers. Note that no images of Phobos were used in deriving this data set. Studies of diurnal, seasonal, and annual variations in optical depth, surface-based observations of great dust storms, and analyses of the contributions of ice haze and dust particles to the observed optical depth, have been carried out using these data. See COLBURN_ETAL_1989, POLLACK_ETAL_1977, and POLLACK_ETAL_1977 for further information on the derivation and interpretation of this data set.','public','2026-03-13T18:21:25.715003','2026-03-13T18:21:25.715011','Planetary Atmospheres','Planetary Data System','026:00','d5f96463-7c98-4934-ae28-0a992b0c8462','NASA Data.json','32bd6ee6a4b67407d1e230b4d2d1bd0397caae2177517ab637b2b927891ee75e','1.1','2026-03-13T18:21:25.715003','2026-03-13T18:21:25.715011','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('2b247904-229f-4b3e-85e6-6b7a3f65a419','Key Watersheds in the Southeast Coast I&M Network (SECN) - Individual Watershed/Subwatershed Boundaries','This dataset consists of the individual watersheds/subwatersheds that contain water features that flow or contribute to those that flow directly into SECN parks. The watersheds/subwatersheds are displayed and described at the HUC-10 (Watershed) or HUC-12 (Subwatershed) level; attributes have also been added to provide the HUC-2 (Region), HUC-4 (Subregion), HUC-6 (Basin), and HUC-8 (Subbasin) numbers and descriptions of each watershed/subwatershed. Furthermore, the individual watersheds/subwatersheds are grouped by park so as to create an overall custom drainage basin for each park. If individual watershed/subwatershed boundaries are not needed, please refer to the dataset titled \'Key Watersheds in the Southeast Coast I&M Network (SECN) - Custom Drainage Basin Boundaries\' in order to access the overall custom drainage basins as single polygon shapefiles. Note: for the purposes of this dataset and for the remainder of this metadata file, the term \"watershed\" will refer to individual watershed/subwatershed units while the term \"drainage basin\" will refer to the collection of individual watershed/subwatershed units that contribute to the condition of each park.','public','2026-03-26T05:33:06.413763','2026-03-26T05:33:06.413768','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','4a6d2c3a-6d31-4e1c-a11e-402733929eb6','DOI NPS DCAT-US','bca3ee15c7730660b896fe4f03b0cfb3fbb431a933134bbf6fa467cdb03f30ff','1.1','2026-03-26T05:33:06.413763','2026-03-26T05:33:06.413768','geospatial','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('2b2baf03-868b-4bf9-b428-951d40b28a83','Station RP3, South Florida Program Survey Cruises','Timeseries data from \'Station RP3, South Florida Program Survey Cruises\' (station-rp3-south-florida-progra)','public','2026-03-26T19:18:00.867077','2026-03-26T19:18:00.867087',NULL,NULL,NULL,'76b165a0-309f-4d90-aebc-5fbfce99f76c','ioos',NULL,NULL,'2026-03-26T19:18:00.867077','2026-03-26T19:18:00.867087',NULL,NULL,NULL,'noaa-gov'),('2b2c371a-7cf8-4637-8a45-2e743f46cf35','Coastal Mapping Program of  Ports of Bremerton and Manchester, WA, WA2502B-CS-N','These data provide an accurate high-resolution shoreline compiled from imagery of  Ports of Bremerton and Manchester, WA .  This vector shoreline data is based on an office interpretation of imagery that may be suitable as a geographic information system (GIS) data layer. This metadata describes information for both the line and point shapefiles. The NGS attribution scheme \'Coastal Cartographic Object Attribute Source Table (C-COAST)\' was developed to conform the attribution of various sources of shoreline data into one attribution catalog. C-COAST is not a recognized standard, but was influenced by the International Hydrographic Organization\'s S-57 Object-Attribute standard so the data would be more accurately translated into S-57.  This resource is a member of  https://inport.nmfs.noaa.gov/inport/item/39808','public','2026-03-26T20:18:30.227971','2026-03-26T20:18:30.227982',NULL,NULL,NULL,'913e0a5c-be0b-4e4d-88bc-b895ada3d53b','NOS NGS',NULL,NULL,'2026-03-26T20:18:30.227971','2026-03-26T20:18:30.227982',NULL,NULL,NULL,'noaa-gov'),('2b7cde5f-8bea-48d9-a415-245c662e8ef8','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 1 0621 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 1 phase 2014-11-20 to 2015-03-10. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-03-04T22:15:00.000 to 2015-03-05T04:07:46.500.','public','2026-03-13T18:22:24.404915','2026-03-13T18:22:24.404920','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','33c74f24-349b-470d-aaa5-a5faaa55e6ad','NASA Data.json','673ec67bd6f88ea7418d4526b9b4ef83e050f89bfb8533c3b786c8af5ad6e302','1.1','2026-03-13T18:22:24.404915','2026-03-13T18:22:24.404920','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('2b7d3a8e-bd5b-48e2-a85a-a882baf220d1','GIOTTO DUST IMPACT DETECTOR SYSTEM DATA V1.0','Dust Impact Detection System (DIDSY) consists of six independent subsystems with the primary aim of registering the impacts of all particulates of significant mass incident on the probe during the post-perihelion encounter with Comet Halley in 1986. Mounted on Giotto\'s front dust shield, the detectors will determine the mass spectrum of the dust, with a limiting sensitivity of some 10^^-17^^ g, increasing to the largest grain masses encountered along Giotto\'s trajectory through the cometary environment with an ultimate spatial resolution of some 70 km. An additional detector is located on the rear shield to monitor those dust particles (m > ~ 5 X 10^^-7^^ g) that are able to penetrate the front dust shield. An ambient plasma monitor is also incorporated into DIDSY to measure the inJpact plasma generated by both dust and gas impacts on the spacecraft. The system is controlled and its data processed by a microprocessor-based system that allows the wide range of anticipated impact rates (varying from a few per minute, to ~ 10^6 s^^-1^^ at closest approach) to be handled. The instrument weighs 2.26 kg and consumes 1.9 W of power during normal operation.','public','2026-03-13T18:05:49.366576','2026-03-13T18:05:49.366583','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','119de2c6-6f9a-457a-bf89-b8d92678f956','NASA Data.json','8daf30112b50d41cdcb5a2e9bcd5a8e7fdf6e3f054c6d22c1996d8b4c0f79e50','1.1','2026-03-13T18:05:49.366576','2026-03-13T18:05:49.366583','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('2bc138d9-b418-44d1-8f30-343bd259e63a','FTB EITC Summary of CA Residents Feb 2026','Produced by the Economic & Statistical Research Bureau, monthly tabulations of tax filings statistics for the Earned Income Tax Credit (EITC), Young Child Tax Credit (YCTC) and Foster Youth Tax Credit (FYTC) provide credit use by county, preparer type, credit amount allowed number of dependents and a many other useful cross-sections','public','2026-03-23T13:57:24.571959','2026-03-23T13:57:24.571964','California Franchise Tax Board','FTB Open Data',NULL,'2e14cae6-6395-419c-a629-648edcde5e7f','State of California','158fe274aa537c4caa67314ab98ad0c9bc546fc4370c9333366e6c56fd186bb7','1.1','2026-03-23T13:57:24.571959','2026-03-23T13:57:24.571964','Economy and Demographics',NULL,0,'ca-gov'),('2bdf5936-8a6e-4f87-852c-54ddf1171f3f','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 PRELANDING 0221 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the PRELANDING phase 2014-01-21 to 2014-11-18. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2014-08-19T07:11:45.000 to 2014-08-19T13:09:58.000.','public','2026-03-13T18:03:25.273235','2026-03-13T18:03:25.273240','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','6e666ce6-6c8c-4af9-adba-12037f476ca7','NASA Data.json','12fd2e8b815d621c54a6506ed99f3909ece918d56bab7884c489566b230af2e9','1.1','2026-03-13T18:03:25.273235','2026-03-13T18:03:25.273240','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('2bf4da35-19df-4a43-ac01-bd5eb67f8e5a','MARS EXPRESS SUN MRS 1/2/3                                     EXTENDED MISSION 8 4358 V1.0','This is a Mars Express                                     Radio Science data set, collected                                     during the extended mission phase                                     2023-01-01 to 2023-12-31.                                     It is a Solar Conjunction                                     measurement and covers the time                                     2023-11-01T05:50:39.000 to                                     2023-11-01T09:56:49.300.','public','2026-03-13T18:43:07.979887','2026-03-13T18:43:07.979893','geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','cf6d2eea-fedb-4e49-b06b-d31b2cc10058','NASA Data.json','10afb6149af4d5e4ad60cbcad53806872281139eeba2528e89e5b753aca5eb28','1.1','2026-03-13T18:43:07.979887','2026-03-13T18:43:07.979893','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('2bfe2ab6-24e6-4e89-8b46-0bd4e14b8734','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RPCIES 2 PRL V1.0','This dataset contains EDITED RAW DATA of the Rosetta RPCIES instrument taken during the Prelanding phase (PRL). The target of this phase was comet 67P/CHURYUMOV-GERASIMENKO 1 (1969 R1). Included are the data taken between 21 Jan 2014 and 20 Nov 2014.','public','2026-03-13T18:26:06.143133','2026-03-13T18:26:06.143138','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','00c15810-47a2-4267-988f-5d99211bf8cb','NASA Data.json','6f7758910a6cbd61541100eaad94afc2fecafd8cae74e81a6e7dd7213f57ddcc','1.1','2026-03-13T18:26:06.143133','2026-03-13T18:26:06.143138','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('2c02683a-1837-40b2-8444-8210ba2d9988','MARS EXPRESS MARS MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 8 4194 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2021-01-01 to 2022-12-31. It is a Occultation measurement and covers the time 2021-03-08T08:18:57.100 to 2021-03-08T08:41:05.449.','public','2026-03-13T19:42:42.445099','2026-03-13T19:42:42.445106','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','9c079642-9643-4b19-96b0-5796292cfca1','NASA Data.json','d3a5ec728fa25db9d818ed7c6f550c6754d3df6c952b39e5ab05303da65c0850','1.1','2026-03-13T19:42:42.445099','2026-03-13T19:42:42.445106','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('2c0ca0c6-739f-44e1-8618-12b9c047f89e','MARS EXPRESS MARS MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 3 3055 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2010-01-01 to 2012-12-31. It is a Global Gravity measurement and covers the time 2011-08-02T01:35:44.000 to 2011-08-02T02:00:26.949.','public','2026-03-13T17:35:03.559424','2026-03-13T17:35:03.559429','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','03952b45-c6d7-462b-915d-fc8cad62a2ad','NASA Data.json','4171c80252c5d568cf90c87bb29af9403af270d5933b07455cb9a190ebd96c5d','1.1','2026-03-13T17:35:03.559424','2026-03-13T17:35:03.559429','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('2c46f847-d5da-49f8-87d9-fce44793c5f2','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P GIADA 3 ESC1 COMET ESCORT 1 V1.1','The current data set (version V1.1) is superseding the previous released version of Comet Escort 1 data set (RO-C-GIA-3-ESC1-COMET-ESCORT-1-V1.0): an issue occurred in some tables was fixed; addressed all scientific RIDS. Comet Escort 1 Phase covers the period of time from the 21 November 2014 until the 10 March 2015. It started after Rosetta successfully completed the Prelanding Phase. The present DataSet collects the GIADA data of ESC1 phase. The GIADA Scientific phase started on 7 May 2014 and was devoted to the characterization of the 67P environment.','public','2026-03-13T17:16:48.472698','2026-03-13T17:16:48.472719','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','d000e828-68a9-4e2b-8fc5-b51ad7530560','NASA Data.json','38eaa860199c611260dc440b0224d7ab44762d01070319e5579ed64e32552bbc','1.1','2026-03-13T17:16:48.472698','2026-03-13T17:16:48.472719','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('2c554756-2cc1-4570-ba8c-3fb0d65fe124','EPOXI C/ISON (2012 S1) - HRII CALIBRATED SPECTRA V1.0','This dataset contains calibrated, 1.05- to 4.8-micron spectral images of comet C/ISON (2012 S1) acquired by the High Resolution Infrared Spectrometer on 16-17 February 2013 during the Cruise 3 phase of the EPOXI mission.','public','2026-03-13T19:53:05.936991','2026-03-13T19:53:05.936996','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','971193b0-f050-455d-9982-25c8310c64e4','NASA Data.json','2867d48c10e43d61634d7443d599e95650d6a788866750924a5f19d771d4d018','1.1','2026-03-13T19:53:05.936991','2026-03-13T19:53:05.936996','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('2c5e5632-f9e0-4009-9bad-767c5a44b492','NEW HORIZONS LEISA JUPITER ENCOUNTER V1.1','This data set contains Raw data taken by the New Horizons Linear Etalon Imaging Spectral Array instrument during the Jupiter encounter mission phase.','public','2026-03-13T19:43:18.590182','2026-03-13T19:43:18.590187','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','c79d02d0-edfc-47cf-b0d8-ebe4f6415fa0','NASA Data.json','cb506c0b6474ac6e1db16f820830bac8daacaad2595503791e7706e48bb6ab3a','1.1','2026-03-13T19:43:18.590182','2026-03-13T19:43:18.590187','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('2c74d83e-671f-4b8e-b925-6908599c0405','CASSINI RSS RAW DATA SET - TIGR7 V1.0','The Cassini Radio Science Titan Gravity Science Experiment (TIGR7) Raw Data Archive is a time-ordered collection of radio science raw data acquired on January 28, 30, March 25, 26 2007 during the Tour subphase of the Cassini mission.','public','2026-03-13T17:00:34.021226','2026-03-13T17:00:34.021233','Planetary Atmospheres','Planetary Data System','026:00','97c8e6e7-63e1-4f51-8661-0959806d2490','NASA Data.json','1f770a3ced8e8f233825f0876a75a35760fb47ea22c31abd743fb148a4622add','1.1','2026-03-13T17:00:34.021226','2026-03-13T17:00:34.021233','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('2c8335ce-6c96-45c5-9adb-ea3c56df10d9','ULY JUP URAP PLASMA FREQ REC AVERAGE E-FIELD 10 MIN','A. UDS data files -------------------                                      Eight files are provided that conform                                      to the UDS conventions regarding the                                      naming of files and the format of the                                      data. The eight files are divided into                                      4 pairs of files with each pair                                      consisting of a file containing data                                      averaged over a 10 minute period and                                      a file containing the maximum data                                      value during the same 10 minute period.                                      The 4 pairs of file contain data for                                      the RAR, the PFR, WFA - magnetic                                      field, and WFA - magnetic field.','public','2026-03-13T19:31:50.904270','2026-03-13T19:31:50.904276','planetary plasma interactions','Planetary Data System','026:00','a24de48f-45fe-4d80-99dd-cadc553ecf48','NASA Data.json','767ea23aa6415ab4308f3c6c8794239d304fc431690a32ccdbf4b47ef06326ad','1.1','2026-03-13T19:31:50.904270','2026-03-13T19:31:50.904276','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('2c851d0b-85c4-42ce-b7f2-5dd248333293','GALILEO ORBITER ASTEROID AND COMET SL9 SOLID STATE IMAGING 2','This data set has been generated by NASA\'s Galileo Project in order to distribute the images acquired by the Solid State Imaging (SSI) camera to the scientists and later to the Planetary Data System (PDS). The collection resides on volume GO_0016 and consists of all images acquired by the Galileo spacecraft during the period from the flyby of Ida through the Shoemaker-Levy 9 (SL9) comet impact on Jupiter. This includes data from SCLK 197327200 through 249221800 and contains the following targets: stars, Ida and Jupiter.','public','2026-03-13T18:23:53.171160','2026-03-13T18:23:53.171166','Imaging','Planetary Data System','026:00','aa948e22-d43c-4919-94ff-99bd03fac627','NASA Data.json','54b7e747e79d9fc1a997d361e682ae04e42c944060c875d59ccc423e872fa09e','1.1','2026-03-13T18:23:53.171160','2026-03-13T18:23:53.171166','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('2c9987ae-3502-4f25-b164-76506d193ce7','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 2 0736 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 2 phase 2015-03-11 to 2015-06-30. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-04-28T09:08:05.000 to 2015-04-28T15:21:53.500.','public','2026-03-13T17:58:41.650299','2026-03-13T17:58:41.650304','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','dacdc8f3-9fad-4ef9-9ebc-fb7b8e06a681','NASA Data.json','76401faf1d0d01f0555d9d64e015c59822dbea4a42e6f711a24fc5915fa545b3','1.1','2026-03-13T17:58:41.650299','2026-03-13T17:58:41.650304','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('2cb7d25e-aca0-4a91-8edd-9c5c9b103a2f','ROSETTA-ORBITER STEINS OSINAC 3 AST1 RDR V2.0','This CODMAC level 3 data set contains radiometric calibrated image data in W/m^2/sr/nm,  acquired by the OSIRIS Narrow Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft  during the STEINS FLY-BY mission phase, covering the period  from 2008-08-04T00:00:00.000 to 2008-10-05T23:59:59.000. The prime target is asteroid 2867 Steins. This version V2.0 supersedes previous deliveries of the same dataset with the following changes since the last version: Reprocessed dataset after October 2018 PSA/PDS external peer review.','public','2026-03-13T17:44:43.498879','2026-03-13T17:44:43.498884','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','46f4d0eb-f8e1-4fd4-8559-707bdc6c8c09','NASA Data.json','68bd9076ad28d2a6b2e370192bd32c81bd8bc26a50da0a0a3434f3d2e56e72b6','1.1','2026-03-13T17:44:43.498879','2026-03-13T17:44:43.498884','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('2ceab6e9-6d44-49d4-bd94-74da7672e2ef','Continuous Fixed Station Water Quality Measurements in Canaveral National Seashore, December 2008 (Certified)','This dataset represents continuous water quality measurements that were taken at a fixed point in Canaveral National Seashore during the month of December, 2008 as a part of the Fixed Station Water Quality Monitoring protocol that was developed by the Southeast Coast I&M Network (SECN). The measurements were taken by a YSI 6600 ESD Multi-Parameter Long Term Water Quality Monitoring Datasonde unit that serves as the standard fixed station water quality monitoring equipment for all similar operations conducted by the SECN. The following parameters were measured at 30 minute intervals during the time period that has been specified: Water Temperature, Specific Conductivity, Salinity, Dissolved Oxygen (DO), DO Concentration, Shallow Depth, pH Level, and Turbidity. Any anomalies noted regarding these parameters have also been noted in separate fields. Please note that these measurements have been certified by network personnel.','public','2026-03-26T05:32:26.708463','2026-03-26T05:32:26.708468','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','653ed515-6aad-489b-9941-e76b61b5707b','DOI NPS DCAT-US','d41c523083b1db2468b3c7a3532a42d3128ead5f0d55f72eeb57aa996eccbe3d','1.1','2026-03-26T05:32:26.708463','2026-03-26T05:32:26.708468','Vector Dataset','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('2d59e1fd-c628-4017-ac07-4ca7ca05a62d','DID(IT) - Facilities Automated Management System (FAMS)','FAMS (Facilities Automated Management System) is the modernization of the Facilities Connect (FACCON) application - a DID(it) ColdFusion application. FAMS is developed to manage and record facility, project, and budget data. FAMS integrates Real Property, Lease Administration, Space Planning, Lease Acquisition, Mapping, and Environment programs and provides the Facilities Management Division with a significant improvement in data management and efficiency with greater data integrity.','non-public','2026-03-22T11:52:26.638921','2026-03-22T11:52:26.638926','Unspecified','Open Data (MGMT)','024:030','f36a99b9-057f-44a1-bb9a-09d9f36d994a','DHS datajson source','2241232c17a9fd91eb19ca942e243d0c0d4afcc6cdd012dbfc37efc6ee9890b5','1.1','2026-03-22T11:52:26.638921','2026-03-22T11:52:26.638926',NULL,'024:000',0,'dhs-gov'),('2d7a1a2c-b408-4d23-bb18-521437b5d032','FAST Eddy Sys NA  Transect 21, 150kHz kHz VMADCP','Program of vessel mount ADCP measurements comprising a combination of 75kHz and 150kHz ADCP data collected in the vicinity of the Loop Current and drilling blocks between 2009 and 2020.','public','2026-03-26T19:17:21.194314','2026-03-26T19:17:21.194322',NULL,NULL,NULL,'b00da6ee-ac9d-473b-8d8c-7f28c36c5e43','ioos',NULL,NULL,'2026-03-26T19:17:21.194314','2026-03-26T19:17:21.194322',NULL,NULL,NULL,'noaa-gov'),('2d7ff809-8018-4cf2-9337-331997e1835d','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 2 0686 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 2 phase 2015-03-11 to 2015-06-30. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-04-01T06:42:05.000 to 2015-04-01T12:16:08.000.','public','2026-03-13T19:29:35.416279','2026-03-13T19:29:35.416286','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','f1bb299f-5ae9-4c8b-a767-fbc46c6504d2','NASA Data.json','eed46140a0a62f8e27bb386d410b2bbb428afded53a6ceee4feac7196dc5d59f','1.1','2026-03-13T19:29:35.416279','2026-03-13T19:29:35.416286','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('2d836053-35d1-4570-83b5-0149cb70ca18','Fatalities, Injuries, and Illnesses in Train Accidents, Highway-Rail Incidents, and Other Incidents (4.08)','This is the report for Fatalities, Injuries, and Illnesses in Train Accidents, Highway-Rail Incidents, and Other Incidents (4.08).','public','2026-03-26T12:49:05.189023','2026-03-26T12:49:05.189028','Federal Railroad Administration','FRA Safety Data Team','021:27','57dde5da-9458-4cee-ac58-44062a10b6af','DOT Socrata Data.json','dcb35b8320875644e05837b6583d1064a50ade57a8134369d8cf861b94bc0961','1.1','2026-03-26T12:49:05.189023','2026-03-26T12:49:05.189028','Railroads','021:037',0,'dot-gov'),('2d8fe10e-a96b-4193-b508-891f4058517e','Experimental Performance of a Laboratory-Scaled Oscillating Surge Wave Energy Converter','This data is a subset of the data from an experimental campaign (https://mhkdr.openei.org/submissions/603) to characterize the hydrodynamics and performance of a laboratory-scale oscillating surge wave energy converter (OSWEC). The device was 85 cm wide, 1.4 meters tall, and 14 cm thick and was tested in the Sea Wave Environmental Lab (SWEL) wave tank at the National Laboratory of the Rockies which is 2.5 meters wide with a water depth of 1.3 meters. The device included fifteen pressure sensors on the flap face, two 6-axis load cells at the hinge, an encoder to measure flap position, and a motor to emulate a power take-off (PTO) and absorb power.\n\nThis data set consists of a single sweep through power take-off damping values with post-processed data from the pressure sensor array, in addition to flap motion, forces, and torques. A README document is provided to explain data file structure and descriptions.','public','2026-03-26T12:42:59.153353','2026-03-26T12:42:59.153358','University of Washington','Brian Polagye','019:20','db1df408-4e59-413f-b847-e1b28d124f32','OpenEI data.json','3caa9dabb6bd8ae077ed97e128932726487a65bdf621cbd0ef86982468787c2f','1.1','2026-03-26T12:42:59.153353','2026-03-26T12:42:59.153358',NULL,'019:009',0,'doe-gov'),('2dc362de-6985-458a-8a02-540139db6c8d','DID(IT) - QADB - Dataset','QADB Dataset of users\' quality assurance review of cases','non-public','2026-03-22T11:55:20.442770','2026-03-22T11:55:20.442774','Unspecified','Open Data (MGMT)','024:030','e674189e-1944-41b7-89af-eec592c994ca','DHS datajson source','4f3716fefbc5a6fffc38a6a8ea3ff994fb1b80518835712f190fc68fc843b39e','1.1','2026-03-22T11:55:20.442770','2026-03-22T11:55:20.442774',NULL,'024:000',0,'dhs-gov'),('2de7e939-ed3d-44c3-82f1-6de227a6c1bd','MESSENGER E/V/H XRS UNCALIBRATED (EDR) DATA V1.0','Abstract : This data set consists of the MESSENGER XRS uncalibrated observations, also known as EDRs. Each XRS observation results in four X-ray spectra. When an X-ray interacts with one of the four detectors, a charge or voltage pulse is generated. This signal is converted into one of 2^8 (256) channels, which are correlated to energy. Over a commanded integration time period a histogram of counts as a function of energy (channel number) is recorded. The EDRs are the number of events in each channel of the four detectors accumulated over the integration period. Channels above or below the useful energy range of the detectors are not transmitted. The result is three 244-channel GPC histograms and one 231-channel solar monitor histogram, each of which is designated as a single X-ray spectrum. In addition to the science data, associated instrument parameters are included.','public','2026-03-13T19:16:57.318835','2026-03-13T19:16:57.318839','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','c9f21498-23de-4bfb-b07b-98006bfbee3b','NASA Data.json','f98b34d79590033163236293d27723846e9f94ee0c6de3f7b0fa0ebc24309920','1.1','2026-03-13T19:16:57.318835','2026-03-13T19:16:57.318839','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('2e11423c-a76b-4801-9578-7434943fb8e3','Exposure Activities Number of Activities','<div style=\"text-align:Left;\"><div><div><p>Retired on March 2, 2022. Data and metadata are provided as-is archive.</p><p><span>The “Number of Activities” chart indicates the number of activity types reported by interviewed positive cases during their exposure period. Activity types were considered moderate to high exposure activity types, and included personal care, dining out, social-, work-, travel-, faith-, gym/fitness-, and sports-related activities. Data is reported on a weekly basis from Friday to the following Thursday.</span></p><p><span>Note: Data subject to change on a daily basis. Data are restricted to positive cases with a completed contact tracing interview. Possible exposure data are collected during the contact tracing interview as self-reported activities occurring within the 2-week period before the date of symptom onset for symptomatic individuals or the date of test sample collection for asymptomatic individuals. Data collection methods were altered starting the week of Dec 11 for gym/fitness and sports, so should not be compared to previous values.</span></p><p><span>* High to Moderate Exposure Activity Types are not exhaustive and include travel, personal care, faith events, work, dining out, social events, gym/fitness, and sports.</span></p><p><span>Data is updated on a weekly basis.</span></p></div></div></div>','public','2026-04-01T08:42:28.279264','2026-04-01T08:42:28.279268','D.C. Office of the Chief Technology Officer','DCGISopendata',NULL,'4dacd2d1-4eda-4256-b23c-eeb442b5c8c0','DC data','7a33be8256bd8415ce4423625a4c636cc393606e12d972110d5005c42d63cac3','1.1','2026-04-01T08:42:28.279264','2026-04-01T08:42:28.279268','geospatial',NULL,0,'district-of-columbia'),('2e1efdec-af89-481c-938e-85c724d1b152','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P ROSINA 5 ESC1 V2.0','This data set contains CODMAC level 5 science data acquired by the DFMS and RTOF ROSINA sensors between 2014-11-19 and 2015-03-10 during the Escort phase 1 of the Rosetta mission at the comet 67P/CG. V2.0: Some minor species (CH4, NH3, HCN, H2CO, C2H6, CH3OH, H2S, C2H5OH, OCS, CS2) detected by DFMS were added.','public','2026-03-13T16:57:05.554653','2026-03-13T16:57:05.554658','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','e4cb7f14-9af6-4a91-8468-ab35d14593fd','NASA Data.json','d26a80761556b371ca34cb9abf44db3273037e4f37262c95eea46cb4a5a0681c','1.1','2026-03-13T16:57:05.554653','2026-03-13T16:57:05.554658','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('2e37fe43-1032-43ae-953b-94e77c0fc0dd','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RPCLAP 2EXT3 EDITED2 V1.0','This data set contains EDITEDdata from Rosetta RPC-LAP, acquired during the ROSETTA EXTENSION 3mission phase where the primary target was the comet67P/CHURYUMOV-GERASIMENKO 1 (1969 R1). It contains uncalibrated rawdata, i.e. the digital output of the instrument. This versionreorganizes the data into fewer files with longer time series and sortedby type of measurement. It also supersedes previous versions that weresplit into MTPs. The version number starts over from V1.0 due to achange in naming convention.','public','2026-03-13T18:00:43.891150','2026-03-13T18:00:43.891157','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','fba38b7a-8569-4b23-9300-756c3234729a','NASA Data.json','3adea83fde27f75af90030fd303df13e25a1aca9c820795bb2ca986900787992','1.1','2026-03-13T18:00:43.891150','2026-03-13T18:00:43.891157','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('2e3e14ea-fc29-4be3-b7d3-109448821db7','Fugro Cruise C16266 Line 0103, 300 kHz VMADCP','Program of vessel mount Acoustic Doppler Current Profiler (ADCP) measurements comprising a combination of 300kHz and 75kHz ADCP data collected in the vicinity of the Loop Current and drilling blocks between 2004 and 2007.','public','2026-03-26T19:16:55.952307','2026-03-26T19:16:55.952314',NULL,NULL,NULL,'c4907e8e-1686-4771-901d-c5642ca0af0c','ioos',NULL,NULL,'2026-03-26T19:16:55.952307','2026-03-26T19:16:55.952314',NULL,NULL,NULL,'noaa-gov'),('2e5ce52d-f9ed-4818-85d9-38ac907e730a','ROSETTA-ORBITER PRELANDING OSIWAC 3 RDR MTP007 V2.0','This data set contains images acquired by the OSIRIS Wide Angle Camera during the PRELANDING phase of the Rosetta mission at the comet 67P, covering the period from 2014-09-02T10:00:00.000 to 2014-09-23T09:59:59.000. This version V2.0 supersedes previous deliveries of the same dataset. Note that the two datasets RO-C-OSIWAC-3-PRL-67PCHURYUMOV-M07-V1.0 and RO-C-OSIWAC-3-PRL-67PCHURYUMOV-M07B-V1.0 have been merged into one dataset: RO-C-OSIWAC-3-PRL-67PCHURYUMOV-M07-V2.0 (and higher), that covers the full time period spanned by the two previously delivered datasets.','public','2026-03-13T18:22:28.922496','2026-03-13T18:22:28.922501','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','708d0960-75ba-48bb-99b1-798329b9e88d','NASA Data.json','caea60171e4724864f00afdeeac8712e486764ed2a721bc0274926ee5cd939a2','1.1','2026-03-13T18:22:28.922496','2026-03-13T18:22:28.922501','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('2e6bc230-67e1-4854-8264-3d54ec36cb97','DS1 MICAS VISCCD EDR IMAGES OF COMET 19P/BORRELLY, V1.0','This archive contains undocumented images acquired by the visible wavelength charged couple device (VISCCD) channel of the Miniature Integrated Camera Spectrometer (MICAS) housed on the Deep Space 1 (DS1) spacecraft. Specifically, select EDR images of the September 2001 approach and encounter of comet 19P/Borrelly are provided. The data are considered to be of highly questionable quality.','public','2026-03-13T19:10:05.008407','2026-03-13T19:10:05.008415','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','6477e94c-dc09-41a0-a409-fd88d792b729','NASA Data.json','fbe2aec2dcd03eb4180860f1b9afa291a4fe7bb68c1ecd0ed2141f149cab6f3d','1.1','2026-03-13T19:10:05.008407','2026-03-13T19:10:05.008415','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('2e6e06cb-c147-4bf8-9f9a-2089e8c480ad','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSIWAC 4 PRL-MTP008 RDR-STR-REFL V1.0','This CODMAC level 4 data set contains solar stray light corrected, radiometric calibrated and geometric distortion corrected (resampled) image data in in reflectance units (normalized and thus without unit), acquired by the OSIRIS Wide Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft during the PRELANDING mission phase, covering the period from 2014-09-23T10:00:00.000 to 2014-10-24T09:59:59.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V1.0 is the first version of this dataset: Lien corrected dataset after October 2018 PSA/PDS external peer review.','public','2026-03-13T19:56:01.709364','2026-03-13T19:56:01.709371','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','c61bed87-c7c8-4e0c-bbc4-69857a00c03b','NASA Data.json','cce34e2b1ff0a775b593f1243173239cbd5ea7f54f9b22f72aba213bd2824d01','1.1','2026-03-13T19:56:01.709364','2026-03-13T19:56:01.709371','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('2ed1ee6d-e36b-4e55-b319-ce27ad94f7a7','MAG UNCALIBRATED (EDR) DATA E/V/H/SW                                     V1.0','Abstract   ========     This data set consists of the MESSENGER MAG uncalibrated     observations, also known as EDRs.  The MAG experiment is a     miniature three-axis ring-core fluxgate magnetometer with     low-noise electronics.  There are eight MAG EDR data products,     including standard data, burst-mode data, and status and     housekeeping data.','public','2026-03-13T17:58:55.730105','2026-03-13T17:58:55.730110','planetary plasma interactions','Planetary Data System','026:00','3f3acb52-044e-4c0f-b105-57ed88a0a9fa','NASA Data.json','dd898e8e2e0771dd9f8fc5f6c07b8f06c9bbcefc9b617ace40b11e11b9729f0f','1.1','2026-03-13T17:58:55.730105','2026-03-13T17:58:55.730110','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('2ee0012f-5130-4eaf-908e-e1aba5fb66e3','HPMS County Summary 2024','State DOTs provide Local and Rural Minor Collector mileage summarized by county and ownership as a direct input to the Highway Performance Management System (HPMS).','public','2026-03-28T13:35:17.356614','2026-03-28T13:35:17.356619','Federal Highway Administration','Office of Highway Policy Information','021:15','179cb5b5-4766-4ab7-8e60-8e0b015b2dd4','DOT Socrata Data.json','f2d19b29e5ce51fbc8e2f1930b01c1aa76b781fc1cf6e51b2f468daa5d0870bb','1.1','2026-03-28T13:35:17.356614','2026-03-28T13:35:17.356619','Roadways and Bridges','021:009',0,'dot-gov'),('2eea1330-c538-426c-ae14-1881db7ad869','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 PRELANDING 0238 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the PRELANDING phase 2014-01-21 to 2014-11-18. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2014-08-24T13:10:25.000 to 2014-08-24T18:21:26.000.','public','2026-03-13T17:05:03.817741','2026-03-13T17:05:03.817746','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','f4437090-b184-4b05-a1f9-b68b3bfb9bf7','NASA Data.json','20f2fbdb4786d78177d27fae2166637c52583e39a9269274087ea9614b6ff8ce','1.1','2026-03-13T17:05:03.817741','2026-03-13T17:05:03.817746','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('2ef8068b-16bf-4263-a9b9-16b133a7837d','VEGA1 DUST PARTICLE IMPACT DETECTOR DATA V1.0','The SP-2 experiment on Vega spacecraft was intended for studying the spatial and mass distributions of dust particles in the cometary coma over the mass range 1.e-16 to 1.e-6 g. Covering such a broad mass range was made possible by using sensors of two types, namely, impact plasma and acoustic.','public','2026-03-13T18:10:31.543316','2026-03-13T18:10:31.543323','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','93020b90-ed67-4189-a2d2-600d7e8d9128','NASA Data.json','40914dcd72834a7bf7cbfc8f97521c276c7b2883f350a405ca39a1413c20b68e','1.1','2026-03-13T18:10:31.543316','2026-03-13T18:10:31.543323','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('2f202c66-7787-4477-993e-e0a7c70058cc','ROSETTA-ORBITER COMET ESCORT 1 OSINAC 2 EDR MTP013 V2.0','This data set contains images acquired by the OSIRIS Narrow Angle Camera during the COMET ESCORT 1 phase of the Rosetta mission at the comet 67P, covering the period from 2015-02-10T23:25:00.000 to 2015-03-10T23:24:59.000. This version V2.0 supersedes previous deliveries of the same dataset.','public','2026-03-13T18:44:33.608737','2026-03-13T18:44:33.608744','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','dde2cc2e-d0eb-4735-8763-47d2cff4899e','NASA Data.json','3210f3d4b9960bf8556df15544ec0e938413cd61ac7caaa9f5768ccf3ed69c2e','1.1','2026-03-13T18:44:33.608737','2026-03-13T18:44:33.608744','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('2f3abd6f-046b-4b31-a31f-1cba282ce001','Derivation and characterization of environmental hazard concentrations for chemical prioritization: a case study in the Great Lakes tributaries','Supplementary data for \"Derivation and characterization of environmental hazard concentrations for chemical prioritization: a case study in the Great Lakes tributaries\". \n\nThis dataset is associated with the following publication:\nMaloney, E., S. Corsi, M. Pronschinske, L. DeCicco, M. Nott, J. Frisch, N. Fuller, A. Baldwin, K. Kimbrough, M. Edwards, S. Hummel, N. Vinas, and D. Villeneuve. Derivation and characterization of environmental hazard concentrations for chemical prioritization: a case study in the Great Lakes tributaries.   ENVIRONMENTAL TOXICOLOGY AND CHEMISTRY. Society of Environmental Toxicology and Chemistry, Pensacola, FL, USA, 44(7): 2029-2047, (2025).','public','2026-03-20T11:47:29.875943','2026-03-20T11:47:29.875950','U.S. Environmental Protection Agency','Daniel Villeneuve','020:00','39fe3769-c65e-417f-8c39-4966c4fca9b6','EPA ScienceHub','b28fec64d5b0b194debf015ddcb1078c907f52aad02c5220ce296cdc0b207be7','1.1','2026-03-20T11:47:29.875943','2026-03-20T11:47:29.875950',NULL,'020:000',0,'epa-gov'),('2f5d8984-cec3-49af-b602-fb50074971b2','Predevelopment Recipient List','A list of organizations that received funding through Oregon Housing and Community Services predevelopment program.','public','2026-03-29T04:09:11.702218','2026-03-29T04:09:11.702225','data.oregon.gov','Fiona Bai',NULL,'9fd91205-53d9-4765-bb59-9ff6b0b45480','oregon json','6dfc9a61d7120090b8fbd714b6860c4044021df2568326feb7669c80649bf356','1.1','2026-03-29T04:09:11.702218','2026-03-29T04:09:11.702225',NULL,NULL,0,'state-of-oregon'),('2f929516-465d-455f-a7b5-43f3207614e7','DID(IT) - Asset Manager: Computer and Network Attribute Data','The Assessment Generator will help minimize the time it takes to produce an assessment by automating assessment creation. More specifically, the Asylum Officer will be guided through assessment writing by the assessment generator tool. The tool will help the AO to streamline the process and fill out the required data to produce the final assessment.','non-public','2026-03-22T11:54:05.537235','2026-03-22T11:54:05.537240','Unspecified','Open Data (MGMT)','024:030','ee663a38-83c2-49fb-a8a1-9473c14d12a4','DHS datajson source','85facb93a537d0b9208b9e607235662bdbbc515b6ce7564343c9302c05c32cc1','1.1','2026-03-22T11:54:05.537235','2026-03-22T11:54:05.537240',NULL,'024:000',0,'dhs-gov'),('2fabe036-dec4-429b-8736-d9ccfba6b3e2','ROSETTA-ORBITER/ROSETTA-LANDER CAL CONSERT 2 PDCS V1.0','This archive contains edited data (CODMAC level 2) from the CONSERT instrument onboard ROSETTA Orbiter and Lander, acquired during PDCS mission phase (Pre Delivery Calib Science) during its journey to comet 67P/C-G. It also contains documentation which describes the CONSERT experiment. The data archived in this data set conform to the Planetary Data System (PDS) Standards, Version 3.6.','public','2026-03-13T18:26:32.424647','2026-03-13T18:26:32.424653','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','3a8d48c1-056d-4940-82ca-7650217e5f50','NASA Data.json','a69ca5289e15744f4c39aad71a9a23985235c0b686abdebb63bb644fb5d6c3af','1.1','2026-03-13T18:26:32.424647','2026-03-13T18:26:32.424653','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('2fe1f2e9-5b55-4b3d-aaaa-ef1f9db12b6b','AIRS/Aqua L2 Near Real Time (NRT) Support Retrieval (AIRS-only) V006 (AIRS2SUP_NRT) at GES DISC','The Atmospheric Infrared Sounder (AIRS) Level 2 Near Real Time (NRT) Support Retrieval (AIRS-only) product (AIRS2SUP_NRT_006) differs from the routine product (AIRS2SUP_006) in four ways to meet the three hour latency requirements of the Land Atmosphere NRT Capability Earth Observing System (LANCE): (1) The NRT granules are produced without previous or subsequent granules if those granules are not available within 5 minutes, (2) the predictive ephemeris/attitude data are used rather than the definitive ephemeris/attitude, (3) if the forecast surface pressure is unavailable, a surface climatology is used, and (4) no ice cloud properties retrievals are performed. The consequences of these differences are described in the AIRS Near Real Time (NRT) data products document. The Atmospheric Infrared Sounder (AIRS) is a grating spectrometer (R = 1200) aboard the second Earth Observing System (EOS) polar-orbiting platform, EOS Aqua. In combination with the Advanced Microwave Sounding Unit (AMSU) and the Humidity Sounder for Brazil (HSB), AIRS constitutes an innovative atmospheric sounding group of visible, infrared, and microwave sensors. This product is product produced using AIRS IR only because the radiometric noise in AMSU channel 4 started to increase significantly (since June 2007). The Support Product includes higher vertical resolution profiles of the quantities found in the Standard Product, plus intermediate outputs (e.g., microwave-only retrieval), research products such as the abundance of trace gases, and detailed quality assessment information. The Support Product profiles contain 100 levels between 1100 and .016 mb; this higher resolution simplifies the generation of radiances using forward models, though the vertical information content is no greater than that in the Standard Product profiles. The intended users of the Support Product are researchers interested in generating forward radiance or in examining research products, and the AIRS algorithm development team. The Support Product is generated at all locations as Standard Products. An AIRS granule has been set as 6 minutes of data, 30 footprints cross track by 45 scanlines. There are 240 granules per day, with an orbit repeat cycle of approximately 16 day.','public','2026-03-13T18:38:52.997739','2026-03-13T18:38:52.997745','NASA/GSFC/SED/ESD/TISL/GESDISC','Earthdata Forum','026:00','d3c9907e-9ac7-4362-8395-096c7d4ae46e','NASA Data.json','f19a4750b1d3574753ccc5773510e79ce332b6016af567c2c3f10f0c3b606c6e','1.1','2026-03-13T18:38:52.997739','2026-03-13T18:38:52.997745','Earth Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('30a33916-0a8f-44a1-93d5-cb3b6f2cef46','CASSINI RSS RAW DATA SET - SROC22 V1.0','The Cassini Radio Science Saturn Ring and Atmospheric Occultation experiments (SROC22) Raw Data Archive is a time-ordered collection of radio science raw data acquired on July 24, 2016, during the Cassini Extended Extended Mission.','public','2026-03-13T18:41:54.725197','2026-03-13T18:41:54.725205','Planetary Atmospheres','Planetary Data System','026:00','f2958dfa-0d04-449f-85e8-1f15e3b2234c','NASA Data.json','e234158da19a5b1fbee9d751a9477461ab9ad1fd68f0cdd534c2887263e5120b','1.1','2026-03-13T18:41:54.725197','2026-03-13T18:41:54.725205','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('311cf0cd-030c-4a85-9f0c-c982bc3d2251','Continuous Fixed Station Water Quality Measurements in Timucuan Ecological and Historic Preserve, April 2008 (Certified)','This dataset represents continuous water quality measurements that were taken at a fixed point in Timucuan Ecological and Historic Preserve during the month of April, 2008 as a part of the Fixed Station Water Quality Monitoring protocol that was developed by the Southeast Coast I&M Network (SECN). The measurements were taken by a YSI 6600 ESD Multi-Parameter Long Term Water Quality Monitoring Datasonde unit that serves as the standard fixed station water quality monitoring equipment for all similar operations conducted by the SECN. The following parameters were measured at 30 minute intervals during the time period that has been specified: Water Temperature, Specific Conductivity, Salinity, Dissolved Oxygen (DO), DO Concentration, Shallow Depth, pH Level, and Turbidity. Any anomalies noted regarding these parameters have also been noted in separate fields. Please note that these measurements have been certified by network personnel.','public','2026-03-26T05:33:12.613655','2026-03-26T05:33:12.613661','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','c34f9d75-095f-4aa5-93a6-9f8b1e220338','DOI NPS DCAT-US','8389efa6fc42917c20b13ef52691935c64ff242f00665c9da78d29103895a39f','1.1','2026-03-26T05:33:12.613655','2026-03-26T05:33:12.613661','Vector Dataset','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('31262019-a862-4580-8908-535e89ef835d','SURVEY OF COMET LIGHTCURVES V1.0','This is a dataset that compiles the data from various papers, which reported observations of brightness changes in comets that allowed to produce the comet lightcurves. Specifically, the data were based on the references in the paper by Samarasinha et al. (2004), i.e. they are those lightcurves, which were used to find out the rotational properties of the comet nuclei (periods, rotation vector coordinates, spin mode, etc.) reported by Samarasinha et al. (2004).','public','2026-03-13T17:40:05.059066','2026-03-13T17:40:05.059071','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','e38df461-83e0-4b41-9042-c9329c93f5de','NASA Data.json','ffd1613fd2c1856aeaf705655c4d12b1270158e971e49bbc55bd19fed17deb8e','1.1','2026-03-13T17:40:05.059066','2026-03-13T17:40:05.059071','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('3144fb2d-2d0e-43ea-8220-28c48346c750','HPMS Non-Federal Aid Summary 2024','Contains information about travel on non-Federal-Aid roads (functionally classified as local or rural minor collector) for each adjusted urbanized area and rural areas. (Note: Urban ID 99998 represents small urban roadway sections, and 99999 represents rural sections.)','public','2026-03-28T13:35:05.813751','2026-03-28T13:35:05.813757','Federal Highway Administration','Office of Highway Policy Information','021:15','c36545dd-4370-4def-be24-bef3a2143450','DOT Socrata Data.json','6ddb3034c67e97f1632c1ba593096f7a653ebd7fcd5c60d6c8d2254f1ad9f22f','1.1','2026-03-28T13:35:05.813751','2026-03-28T13:35:05.813757','Roadways and Bridges','021:009',0,'dot-gov'),('31952bde-d451-41a8-9bb6-30ad0154cc3c','ROSETTA-LANDER CAL MUPUS 2 PHC V1.0','This archive contains edited data from the MUPUS instrument onboard ROSETTA Lander, acquired during the PHC phase. It also contains documentation which describes the MUPUS experiment. The data archived in this data set conform to the Planetary Data System Standards, Version 3.6.','public','2026-03-13T20:07:01.481846','2026-03-13T20:07:01.481851','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','2680d02a-10aa-475f-ab79-0ccdfeb197cb','NASA Data.json','0169f7144a23908e8bd29b05e021d17a4fb2a75d6dced93cdd7a7665bccc6c8e','1.1','2026-03-13T20:07:01.481846','2026-03-13T20:07:01.481851','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('319c7ca5-b04f-4d7b-bd15-ec53c4e03874','BLM ID Areas of Critical Environmental Concern ACEC Designated','<div style=\'text-align:Left;\'><div><div><div style=\'font-size:12pt\'><p><span>This feature class contains polygons and attributes describing Idaho\'s active Areas of Critical Environmental Concern (ACECs). ACEC polygons represent boundaries as initially described in Resource Management Plans (RMPs) and Management Framework Plans (MFPs) either in narrative form or via maps. These GIS boundaries do not reflect the final serialized and authorized ACEC boundary. For more information contact us at blm_id_stateoffice@blm.gov.</span></p><p><span /></p></div></div></div></div>','public','2026-03-14T10:01:15.922381','2026-03-14T10:01:15.922386','Bureau of Land Management','Bureau of Land Management, blm_id_infoaccesscenter','010:04','45ce89f3-cb86-44c7-a738-9ef747c5d9b2','DOI BLM DCAT-US','c6b06e5dc38fe38ba63ab02851af4c6421e465c37143717d3e8306a87415d574','1.1','2026-03-14T10:01:15.922381','2026-03-14T10:01:15.922386','geospatial','010:000',0,'doi-gov'),('31d8a053-41f5-4d84-ab29-5e6591f100a7','HPMS Roadway Events Data 2021','Roadway attributes datasets in the Highway Performance Monitoring System (HPMS) consist of three separate tables: the Road Designations Table, the Road Identifications Table, and the Road Events Table.  The Roads Event Table data items include Inventory, Lanes, Intersections, Traffic, Control, Pavement, Terrain, and Travel Time Code.','public','2026-03-28T13:38:22.776809','2026-03-28T13:38:22.776813','Federal Highway Administration','Office of Highway Policy Information','021:15','65320eee-fa65-48f3-b85f-987ba491f29e','DOT Socrata Data.json','42da0863cf307f93aaddd566bd4897240f796a58179da1ee4d2431bf2b7107c0','1.1','2026-03-28T13:38:22.776809','2026-03-28T13:38:22.776813','Roadways and Bridges','021:009',0,'dot-gov'),('3204d745-731a-4203-b261-46088fbfad55','Laborshed - Actively Seeking','Laborshed dataset containing information for those who are and are not actively seeking employment.','public','2026-03-28T22:02:35.834241','2026-03-28T22:02:35.834245','data.iowa.gov','svqueen',NULL,'02da31c9-8cc5-4b4d-b40e-4721b0fdcfdf','Iowa metadata','52772b10659b836e41d068e69b7aa9d589bdba1b71f14fd550635d7b9d291c73','1.1','2026-03-28T22:02:35.834241','2026-03-28T22:02:35.834245','Economic Statistics',NULL,0,'state-of-iowa'),('3207e47a-ad80-4e62-836a-0fdf0ff8ccaf','Continuous Fixed Station Water Quality Measurements in Canaveral National Seashore, September 2005 (Certified)','This dataset represents continuous water quality measurements that were taken at a fixed point in Canaveral National Seashore during the month of September, 2005 as a part of the Fixed Station Water Quality Monitoring protocol that was developed by the Southeast Coast I&M Network (SECN). The measurements were taken by a YSI 6600 ESD Multi-Parameter Long Term Water Quality Monitoring Datasonde unit that serves as the standard fixed station water quality monitoring equipment for all similar operations conducted by the SECN. The following parameters were measured at 30 minute intervals during the time period that has been specified: Water Temperature, Specific Conductivity, Salinity, Dissolved Oxygen (DO), DO Concentration, Shallow Depth, pH Level, and Turbidity. Any anomalies noted regarding these parameters have also been noted in separate fields. Please note that these measurements have been certified by network personnel.','public','2026-03-26T05:29:12.117725','2026-03-26T05:29:12.117730','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','893129c3-bdea-4153-935a-d3fe1ca94722','DOI NPS DCAT-US','cc36cacc673795ceea663e41616333b2986c2d0f98808686d4933891862eda62','1.1','2026-03-26T05:29:12.117725','2026-03-26T05:29:12.117730','Vector Dataset','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('320fc0b6-94e3-450e-8ea3-68a971c40464','TTC POMA Audit Report (APR)','This is an audit report that the Austin Public Health (APH) Internal Auditor has completed regarding the Austin Parks and Recreation’s (APR) Park Operations and Maintenance Agreement (POMA) with The Trail Conservancy (TTC), including Parkland Improvement Agreements (PIA) for Rainey Street Trailhead and Holly Street Project.','public','2026-03-25T14:31:37.247289','2026-03-25T14:31:37.247294','data.austintexas.gov','Austin Parks and Recreation Owners',NULL,'571f3020-3992-478b-b1d8-728b570aa686','City of Austin Data.json','558e60751224876c3cd4bbc2e12221e01ef6f0f9f78801733f44aa4b89bf274c','1.1','2026-03-25T14:31:37.247289','2026-03-25T14:31:37.247294','Recreation and Culture',NULL,0,'city-of-austin'),('325741ca-eefb-4b38-97dc-6cdc69916826','Data and code for Olson et al. Algal blooms in lakes increase after wildfire smoke events in the contiguous United States','Data and code for Olson et al. Algal blooms in lakes increase after wildfire smoke events in the contiguous United States. \n\nThis dataset is associated with the following publication:\nOlson, N.E., M.M. Brehob, R.D. Sabo, I. Pavlovic, K.I. Shank, S. Penry, A.M. Handler, M.J. Pennino, R.B. Rice, K.L. Boaggio, and S.D. LeDuc. Algal Blooms in Lakes Increase After Wildfire Smoke Events in the Contiguous United States.   Global Change Biology Communications. John Wiley & Sons, Inc., Hoboken, NJ, USA, 1(1): e70004, (2026).','public','2026-03-19T11:40:39.542491','2026-03-19T11:40:39.542496','U.S. Environmental Protection Agency','Nicole Olson','020:00','0e676187-f68a-48d5-b1e3-d9e9552a9a8e','EPA ScienceHub','777dfc3f68ba2b4737704db71b0b2599ae596861abda7506245a985d59412f21','1.1','2026-03-19T11:40:39.542491','2026-03-19T11:40:39.542496',NULL,'020:000',0,'epa-gov'),('3279e053-94bc-490b-b92d-850b388367c2','DQS National Post-acute and Long-term Care Providers','Health estimates of providers of post-acute and long-term care in the United States. Search, visualize, and download these and other estimates from a wide range of health topics with the NCHS Data Query System (DQS), available from: https://www.cdc.gov/nchs/dataquery/index.htm.','public','2026-03-26T18:18:33.376871','2026-03-26T18:18:33.376876','Centers for Disease Control and Prevention','National Center for Health Statistics','009:20','d57c77df-eb88-4cc2-a910-05a95d8e17a8','Healthdata.gov','26d9f1b13c355b604b0858adbf2ed38041d45043c8e45eae5acbae3af302a474','1.1','2026-03-26T18:18:33.376871','2026-03-26T18:18:33.376876','National Center for Health Statistics','009:020',0,'hhs-gov'),('32855078-a64c-4a27-b0d8-061a7a3f0a4c','VOYAGER 1 SOLAR WIND PLS FINE RES V1.0','Voyager 1 plasma data of the solar wind, fine resolution data.','public','2026-03-13T16:48:09.249193','2026-03-13T16:48:09.249199','planetary plasma interactions','Planetary Data System','026:00','e9f4ad4a-8ad0-4073-927c-7734d9643e90','NASA Data.json','22b302841eee7b4f80df294bae1e90dd7f932ab326f03bb466b4a3bc490c4813','1.1','2026-03-13T16:48:09.249193','2026-03-13T16:48:09.249199','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('32980f1b-4846-4dc6-a886-3f8318ef2cab','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P SREM 2 ESCORT 1 MTP010 V1.0','This data set contains count rates (1/s) as measured by the Standard Radiation Environment Monitor (SREM) instrument on the Rosetta spacecraft, along with their standard deviations. The primary target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko. These are CODMAC Level 2 Experiment Data Record data, and provide a measure of the radiation in the spacecraft environment during the Medium Term Plan 10 period of the ESCORT 1 mission phase.','public','2026-03-13T18:02:00.197999','2026-03-13T18:02:00.198007','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','f962f42f-2824-4942-846b-4136a07d3424','NASA Data.json','61a127aa000e001c8be869ca7b640f2b31e748a7a31585d264145adb60faa3d6','1.1','2026-03-13T18:02:00.197999','2026-03-13T18:02:00.198007','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('32b556b7-7cde-4581-9c0f-73671bf097d1','ROSETTA-ORBITER EARTH OSIWAC 4 EAR3 RDR V1.0','This CODMAC level 4 data set contains radiometric calibrated and geometric distortion corrected (resampled) image data in W/m^2/sr/nm,  acquired by the OSIRIS Wide Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft  during the EARTH SWING-BY 3 mission phase, covering the period  from 2009-09-14T00:00:00.000 to 2009-12-13T23:59:59.000. The prime target is planet Earth. This version V1.0 is the first version of this dataset.','public','2026-03-13T16:57:00.504128','2026-03-13T16:57:00.504134','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','43a5ae27-be51-4244-acb3-cac29931d794','NASA Data.json','f8505e467acba8e37736a19cfb13a54e198d57d8a6ffaf0c7489c8dba6499d76','1.1','2026-03-13T16:57:00.504128','2026-03-13T16:57:00.504134','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('32d8d047-b43c-4355-9c0c-59e42b77a70c','ROSETTA-ORBITER COMET PRELANDING OSIWAC 2 EDR MTP 007B V1.0','This data set contains raw EDR images acquired by the OSIRIS Wide AngleCamera during the prelanding phase of the Rosetta mission at the comet 67P,covering the period from 2014-09-16 to 2014-09-23.','public','2026-03-13T17:28:37.307928','2026-03-13T17:28:37.307933','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','29922143-61a6-4666-b4d4-6a4183e4661f','NASA Data.json','d436c7ed7fba5d61229be60cf1e56e486c7b9c6d08733d663f3537f84c9557cc','1.1','2026-03-13T17:28:37.307928','2026-03-13T17:28:37.307933','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('331035a6-5731-415d-8cba-45273ee758fa','BLM ID Field Office Administrative Unit Boundary','<div style=\'text-align:Left;\'><div><div style=\'font-size:12pt\'><p><span>This data set shows the Idaho Bureau of Land Management (BLM) Field Office, District Office and State Office boundaries and names as per the three-tier organization initiated in February 2007. A Bureau of Land Management (BLM) Administrative Unit is a geographic area in which an organizational unit of the BLM has distinct jurisdictional responsibility for land and resource management activities occurring on the public lands, the maintained rights of the United States (i.e. mineral estate) and actions relating to the Trust responsibilities of the U.S. Government as stipulated in Law or Treaty.The State Office is the top layer of the three-tier organization, with District Offices being the middle layer and providing coordination, oversight and support to the lowest level, the Field Office. Idaho has one State Office, four Districts and twelve Field Offices. This feature class documents the physical boundary of an administrative unit. In some cases, the administrative unit may manage areas outside of the boundary for other programs’ purposes - this datset does not show these areas. BLM Idaho administers a little land in Nevada also, which is included here.    For more information contact us at blm_id_stateoffice@blm.gov.</span></p></div></div></div>','public','2026-03-18T11:15:28.349130','2026-03-18T11:15:28.349138','Bureau of Land Management','Bureau of Land Management, id_so_information','010:04','6bf119c6-9990-4543-b0ca-ea5eaca922e8','DOI BLM DCAT-US','05866d94b7283e2d7225d2c2cbbc358249e3e2fcc9f6856a93fe40aca0088ded','1.1','2026-03-18T11:15:28.349130','2026-03-18T11:15:28.349138','geospatial','010:000',0,'doi-gov'),('3360223f-4282-4db6-a224-469a3b5e3ada','EGIS - Enterprise Gateway Integration Services-Service Center Operations Intake Support (SCOPS)','Service Center Operations representative drops PDF into NFS pre-defined folder relative to environment being used. EGIS pulls at regular scheduled interval the ESE Folders for unprocessed files. EGIS service will identify the unprocessed files based on what is in the EGIS  Folder(s).','non-public','2026-03-22T11:55:51.426714','2026-03-22T11:55:51.426719','Unspecified','Open Data (MGMT)','024:030','bf534913-3e80-4b93-b527-fc7467d01e4b','DHS datajson source','c93c51f061dec47ee1efe9ce3748d378e0de5bc2ea5b007960ca52632f6c6108','1.1','2026-03-22T11:55:51.426714','2026-03-22T11:55:51.426719',NULL,'024:000',0,'dhs-gov'),('33a78cc9-fe3a-4725-ad7c-72acb0cac698','WITHLACOOCHEE RIVER AT US 301 AT TRILBY, FL (USGS 02312000)','Timeseries data from \'WITHLACOOCHEE RIVER AT US 301 AT TRILBY, FL (USGS 02312000)\' (gov_usgs_nwis_02312000)','public','2026-03-26T19:15:38.941633','2026-03-26T19:15:38.941640',NULL,NULL,NULL,'ba5c2661-978d-4af9-8f7c-73704ef35bf6','ioos',NULL,NULL,'2026-03-26T19:15:38.941633','2026-03-26T19:15:38.941640',NULL,NULL,NULL,'noaa-gov'),('33dd6989-82d6-4b2b-b7a0-37c2b8bbc9c8','Thoms Point, AK','Timeseries data from \'Thoms Point, AK\' (noaa_nos_co_ops_9450970)','public','2026-03-26T19:15:00.555268','2026-03-26T19:15:00.555274',NULL,NULL,NULL,'83623791-d28c-41cf-9b35-213a60b093da','ioos',NULL,NULL,'2026-03-26T19:15:00.555268','2026-03-26T19:15:00.555274',NULL,NULL,NULL,'noaa-gov'),('3431f2ad-9a92-4237-ae7f-014f2640de5d','F00929: NOS Hydrographic Survey , 2026-01-22','The National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration (NOAA) has the statutory mandate to collect hydrographic data in support of nautical chart compilation for safe navigation and to provide background data for engineers, scientific, and other commercial and industrial activities. Hydrographic survey data primarily consist of water depths, but may also include features (e.g. rocks, wrecks), navigation aids, shoreline identification, and bottom type information.\n							NOAA is responsible for archiving and distributing the source data as described in this metadata record.','public','2026-03-14T22:46:32.516059','2026-03-21T22:56:31.434935',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2b31414b-ec7d-42a3-ab58-158738ed556b','NESDIS/NGDC/MGG/NOS/F00001-F02000',NULL,NULL,'2026-03-14T22:46:32.516059','2026-03-21T22:56:31.434935',NULL,NULL,NULL,'noaa-gov'),('343217e9-485e-4f96-abf8-c9ac964b7005','MESSENGER E/V/H MLA 4 GDR DATA V1.0','This data set contains gridded data products from the MESSENGER mission [SOLOMONETAL2007].','public','2026-03-13T19:40:05.309243','2026-03-13T19:40:05.309249','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','4b9ad01d-ff23-49e1-8d1c-db5196919722','NASA Data.json','f5af43b5b4294c25cec209f2250daebd7967b26bcd36b48918cba28175a17394','1.1','2026-03-13T19:40:05.309243','2026-03-13T19:40:05.309249','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('343c5b0f-824f-4420-a06f-bc2de17690dd','DID(IT) - Digital Innovation & Development - Information Technology-Employee Profile','Employee Profile is an Application Program Interface (API) micro service to provide an interface for DID(it) ePulse, which contains employee information including, but not limited to, employee name, employee id, employee organization id, and contact information.  All employee information is entered and maintained in ePulse.  Employee Profile does not support creating or updating employee information in ePulse.','non-public','2026-03-22T11:57:00.662737','2026-03-22T11:57:00.662741','Unspecified','Open Data (MGMT)','024:030','782428f3-ead8-4422-afd9-edb05536c06a','DHS datajson source','01b14524d78913216b76d221bd3fdd128200412b10c721e1d4651ff5eeb16532','1.1','2026-03-22T11:57:00.662737','2026-03-22T11:57:00.662741',NULL,'024:000',0,'dhs-gov'),('345c814e-b954-42d7-b028-c5af73279eb6','DID(IT) - Process Immigration Benefit Fees','The Exam Fee Receipt System  is an automated immigration system to process benefit fees.','non-public','2026-03-22T11:56:16.516472','2026-03-22T11:56:16.516477','Unspecified','Open Data (MGMT)','024:030','cc32c952-829a-47c8-be3c-79d8d9b6b5c4','DHS datajson source','73560a0decbeee0686486a4b9b157585a1269a692c9673c3da089a2b43174a46','1.1','2026-03-22T11:56:16.516472','2026-03-22T11:56:16.516477',NULL,'024:000',0,'dhs-gov'),('346d288a-4e8f-4ae7-bf48-2b5a61ce0ce2','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RPCMIP/RPCLAP 5 ESC4 V1.0','This archive contains cross-calibrated data from the RPC-MIP and RPC-LAP instruments on-board ROSETTA Orbiter acquired during the COMET ESCORT 4 mission phase. Observations are performed in the vicinity of comet 67P/C-G. It also contains documentation which describes the RPC-MIP experiment. The data archived in this data set conform to the Planetary Data System Standards, Version 3.6.','public','2026-03-13T16:38:25.144653','2026-03-13T16:38:25.144660','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','9fc8846d-1ae4-44d4-83ff-c4422058f23e','NASA Data.json','689e85ff59c7c4ff0a45a7e92f8403faab281ff6b089b1462b4a6ab1a4cbe1ce','1.1','2026-03-13T16:38:25.144653','2026-03-13T16:38:25.144660','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('34896e80-8e7f-47c9-8c10-2aa486aeb58b','MARS EXPRESS HRSC RADIOMETRIC RDR EXTENSION1 V4.0','This CODMAC level 3 data set contains radiometrically calibrated data products acquired by the HRSC camera on the Mars Express spacecraft, covering the orbits 2419 to 4918.','public','2026-03-13T17:54:56.786801','2026-03-13T17:54:56.786810','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','bbd330bc-bd59-45b0-bbb9-7d0a94de17fa','NASA Data.json','355ce29d3b183cdf140e503eaecae2bf5fcadcf0e8581cd469469e1192dffa6a','1.1','2026-03-13T17:54:56.786801','2026-03-13T17:54:56.786810','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('349c5fd2-1e0a-4c56-89c8-b7351c8d47bc','Leveraging invasive mussel contaminant survey data for stepwise prioritization of chemicals of potential concern in the Great Lakes basin','Supplementary data for \"Leveraging invasive mussel contaminant survey data for stepwise prioritization of chemicals of potential concern in the Great Lakes basin\". \n\nThis dataset is associated with the following publication:\nFuller, N., K. Kimbrough, M. Edwards, E. Maloney, S. Corsi, M. Pronschinske, L. DeCicco, J. Frisch, A. Baldwin, S. Hummel, N. Garcia Reyero, and D. Villeneuve. Leveraging invasive mussel contaminant survey data for stepwise prioritization of chemicals of potential concern in the Great Lakes basin.   ENVIRONMENTAL TOXICOLOGY AND CHEMISTRY. Society of Environmental Toxicology and Chemistry, Pensacola, FL, USA, 44(7): 2070-2087, (2025).','public','2026-03-21T12:04:03.792225','2026-03-21T12:04:03.792259','U.S. Environmental Protection Agency','Daniel Villeneuve','020:00','e792b38b-5e43-45a8-811b-9d0af38e114a','EPA ScienceHub','2058a0c52c4eb851f2e2bf6cf452f8cb5ae2791c1effecad61f9e407b216e7f3','1.1','2026-03-21T12:04:03.792225','2026-03-21T12:04:03.792259',NULL,'020:000',0,'epa-gov'),('34b8f9a9-e8a4-411d-a399-e04d66738fac','VG2 NEP PLS DERIVED RDR ION INBOUND S-WIND 48SEC V1.0','This data set gives the best available values for ion densities,      temperatures, and velocities near Neptune derived from data obtained      by the Voyager 2 plasma experiment.  All parameters are obtained by      fitting the observed spectra (current as a function of energy) with      Maxwellian plasma distributions, using a non-linear least squares      fitting routine to find the plasma parameters which, when coupled      with the full instrument response, best simulate the data.','public','2026-03-13T18:43:13.281957','2026-03-13T18:43:13.281963','planetary plasma interactions','Planetary Data System','026:00','d6ac8c8e-514c-44d3-ba90-bf032fb4d36e','NASA Data.json','258b9940b360c362560fafe0e4bdbebb8dbad3d5011ed1f614fe9704857a339d','1.1','2026-03-13T18:43:13.281957','2026-03-13T18:43:13.281963','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('34c84c26-d7df-489b-a1c2-32686c5dfc3c','NHTSA Investigations by Manufacturer','NHTSA Investigations by Manufacturer','public','2026-03-27T12:58:09.964116','2026-03-27T12:58:09.964122','National Highway Traffic Safety Administration','NHTSA-Datahub','021:18','7ecdca28-5aba-4b0c-9506-d525d7ef6b41','DOT Socrata Data.json','e767c0700106a35aa7f357c178226d559fb6a670f441dc08fdeb9451db9bc880','1.1','2026-03-27T12:58:09.964116','2026-03-27T12:58:09.964122','Automobiles','021:035',0,'dot-gov'),('34f3f6b1-731a-47fa-bc63-ac2f0e8aeb05','Data from: Haplotype-resolved genome assemblies for the New World screwworm, <i>Cochliomyia hominivorax</i> (Diptera: Calliphoridae), using the trio binning approach','<p dir=\"ltr\">These are supplemental data for producing haplotype-resolved genome assemblies of <i>C. hominivorax </i>using the trio-binning approach. Briefly, a single male progeny from the cross of a Panama line male with a production strain female was sequenced using PacBio HiFi and scaffolded using Hi-C chromatin conformation, while Illumina NextSeq 2000 was used for short read sequencing of both parents to facilitate trio-binning. We produced a linear haploid reference assembly by transferring a copy of the X chromosome and mitochondrial genome to the paternal haplotype. This assembly is comprised of five autosomes, two sex chromosomes, the mitogenome, and 75 unplaced scaffolds spanning 455.6 Mb, which is closer to the predicted size based on flow cytometry (443.8 Mb) than the previous assembly of 534.4 Mb. NCBI’s external Eukaryotic Genome Annotation Pipeline (EGAPx) was used to annotate the protein coding and non-coding genes in the linear haploid reference and the maternal haplotype assembly.</p><p dir=\"ltr\">This research used resources provided by the SCINet project and/or the AI Center of Excellence of the USDA Agricultural Research Service, ARS project numbers 0201-88888-003-000D and 0201-88888-002-000D.</p>','public','2026-03-13T22:46:47.922123','2026-03-13T22:46:47.922128','Agricultural Research Service','Hickner, Paul, V','005:18','24df6017-ae35-430b-b16c-f67d49a826e7','USDA JSON','5b4d0d6a5fafefc0f12e649b5df030e3b09d920a932f7b5a4eb73272db596762','1.1','2026-03-13T22:46:47.922123','2026-03-13T22:46:47.922128',NULL,'005:040',0,'usda-gov'),('350587f0-0500-42a1-bf51-5bb5f40800c9','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSINAC 4 ESC1-MTP013 RDR-STRLIGHT V1.0','This CODMAC level 4 data set contains solar stray light corrected, radiometric calibrated and geometric distortion corrected (resampled) image data in W/m^2/sr/nm, acquired by the OSIRIS Narrow Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft during the COMET ESCORT 1 mission phase, covering the period from 2015-02-10T23:25:00.000 to 2015-03-10T23:24:59.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V1.0 is the first version of this dataset: Lien corrected dataset after October 2018 PSA/PDS external peer review.','public','2026-03-13T18:04:16.245344','2026-03-13T18:04:16.245350','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','9cd26429-0c79-4372-8fd0-18cdf89a56c0','NASA Data.json','c68ea7527a38c86fb8ac3c19d139de2fe221624aed044dae7882e6b004e8e33d','1.1','2026-03-13T18:04:16.245344','2026-03-13T18:04:16.245350','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('3510513b-bd4d-4c76-8d5b-180c85ef8d2f','GIOTTO ION MASS SPECTROMETER HIGH ENERGY RANGE DATA V1.0','A wide range of ion species and velocity distributions are expected to be found as the Giotto spacecraft traverses the coma of Halley\'s Comet. The outer coma is characterized by the interaction between solar wind and cometary plasmas, the inner coma by the outflow of cometary neutrals and their ionization products. The resultant demands on instrument dynamic range preclude use of a single sensor for measurements of ion composition. The Giotto Ion Mass Spectrometer (IMS) therefore consists of two sensors: one optimized for the outer and the other for the inner coma, with each obtaining complementary information in the region for which it is not optimized. Both sensors feature mass imaging characteristics, thereby permitting simultaneous measurements of several ion species by means of multi-detector arrays. The prime objective of the High-Energy Range Spectrometer (HERS) is to measure the ion abundances and three-dimensional velocity distributions outside the cometary contact surface.','public','2026-03-13T18:27:55.748683','2026-03-13T18:27:55.748689','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','c0535e1e-a935-41ac-8a75-782ced2b54bc','NASA Data.json','3f9aabd21fc7790aed4f93add905167c9403b8d5d5e98545d041a343ab51c52a','1.1','2026-03-13T18:27:55.748683','2026-03-13T18:27:55.748689','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('351e0789-fc40-4e93-8f21-c6f71a819e72','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 3 1028 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 3 phase 2015-07-01 to 2015-10-21. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-09-12T10:01:10.000 to 2015-09-12T17:31:39.000.','public','2026-03-13T18:37:59.278867','2026-03-13T18:37:59.278872','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','e57a51c1-f316-43cc-ba5d-c218036d051e','NASA Data.json','c15167d16e8d313483e16e8b41808a1aab7cc71c3a6f8d78fac51e03a9d85d1e','1.1','2026-03-13T18:37:59.278867','2026-03-13T18:37:59.278872','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('354e118e-2a02-4036-b32f-751b3d3345c5','AIRS/Aqua L2 CO2 in the free troposphere (AIRS-only) V005 (AIRS2STC) at GES DISC','The Atmospheric Infrared Sounder (AIRS) is a grating spectrometer (R = 1200) aboard the second Earth Observing System (EOS) polar-orbiting platform, EOS Aqua. In combination with the Advanced Microwave Sounding Unit (AMSU) and the Humidity Sounder for Brazil (HSB), AIRS constitutes an innovative atmospheric sounding group of visible, infrared, and microwave sensors. The AIRS Carbon Dioxide (CO2) Standard Retrieval Product consists of retrieved estimates of CO2, plus estimates of the errors associated with the retrieval. In contrast to AIRX2RET, the horizontal resolution of this standard product is about 110 km (1x1 degree). An AIRS granule has been set as 6 minutes of data, 15 footprints cross track by 22 lines along track.','public','2026-03-13T19:10:57.564784','2026-03-13T19:10:57.564789','NASA/GSFC/SED/ESD/TISL/GESDISC','Earthdata Forum','026:00','88cdcfa8-2a73-4259-896e-d8d0b45ac0fb','NASA Data.json','a2bb8c1ccd1bdeaf8a7d65434deb1a51ffb7bcc050c5c77963467575048a5425','1.1','2026-03-13T19:10:57.564784','2026-03-13T19:10:57.564789','Earth Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('355678d3-db39-4caa-a306-da00c240699e','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 2 0781 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 2 phase 2015-03-11 to 2015-06-30. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-05-16T09:29:25.000 to 2015-05-16T12:08:18.000.','public','2026-03-13T18:28:32.461507','2026-03-13T18:28:32.461514','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','ba7c3bbb-d5c9-4dfb-adc6-7a96c8c3ce04','NASA Data.json','615f1200d12f87b0c0a96802adb21353fd538c663282772c68dca142da0e58a8','1.1','2026-03-13T18:28:32.461507','2026-03-13T18:28:32.461514','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('3566bcdd-a84b-4ff2-806d-692ab9bfb0e7','NRC 829','NRC Small Business Subcontracting Plan. Fillable form in Adobe Portable Document Format (PDF) with information submitted by NRC stakeholder - licensee, applicant, or NRC employee/contractor.','non-public','2026-03-20T19:43:21.935257','2026-03-20T19:43:21.935263','Nuclear Regulatory Commission','Tira Patterson','429:00','e5d7773a-d601-48ec-8d07-93ee1f63254e','NRC Data.json Harvest Source','083f7d6ee8f90b8f5ab4b5134d507576e05fce18cfea4c350bcfed45e984d1e6','1.1','2026-03-20T19:43:21.935257','2026-03-20T19:43:21.935263',NULL,'000:000',0,'nrc-gov'),('357cdcf6-0c27-4ebb-bac6-82caeadef073','Green Building Mandatory','This shapefile shows the areas of Austin where buildings are required to achieve an Austin Energy Green Building Rating. These areas may be PUDs, zoning cases, development agreements, or other.','public','2026-03-25T14:49:12.403281','2026-03-25T14:49:12.403289','data.austintexas.gov','Austin Energy GIS Team',NULL,'c34eab6c-7fc6-4adb-a792-ba9cd9195f42','City of Austin Data.json','262f573bb92f8ff621f537c88a600d365a0d4ef92d466dfe951ce1e13f45260f','1.1','2026-03-25T14:49:12.403281','2026-03-25T14:49:12.403289','Locations and Maps',NULL,0,'city-of-austin'),('35c0492f-5010-4593-ae72-79b16d6a75f7','Hydrographic and Impairment Statistics Database: NPS-WSR Obed Wild and Scenic River','Hydrographic and Impairment Statistics (HIS) is a National Park Service (NPS) Water Resources Division (WRD) project established to track certain goals created in response to the Government Performance and Results Act of 1993 (GPRA). One water resources management goal established by the Department of the Interior under GRPA requires NPS to track the percent of its managed surface waters that are meeting Clean Water Act (CWA) water quality standards. This goal requires an accurate inventory that spatially quantifies the surface water hydrography that each bureau manages and a procedure to determine and track which waterbodies are or are not meeting water quality standards as outlined by Section 303(d) of the CWA. This project helps meet this DOI GRPA goal by inventorying and monitoring in a geographic information system for the NPS: (1) CWA 303(d) quality impaired waters and causes; and (2) hydrographic statistics based on the United States Geological Survey (USGS) National Hydrography Dataset (NHD). Hydrographic and 303(d) impairment statistics were evaluated based on a combination of 1:24,000 (NHD) and finer scale data (frequently provided by state GIS layers).','public','2026-03-29T06:06:19.389985','2026-03-29T06:06:19.389991','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','f6a5df52-4408-40bc-b47f-c97daec967b5','DOI NPS DCAT-US','51acdddebe8715a14fddee275a4a8e40bbf11b4491c4babe71b16d6f709bda2f','1.1','2026-03-29T06:06:19.389985','2026-03-29T06:06:19.389991','geospatial','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('36053736-7072-4ef3-9834-907c0d25f483','CASSINI ORBITER SATURN UVIS CALIBRATION DATA 1.2','Observations of solar or stellar targets for the purpose of calibrating detector wavelength scale, photometric sensitivity and flat fields.','public','2026-03-13T18:18:34.783302','2026-03-13T18:18:34.783308','Planetary Atmospheres','Planetary Data System','026:00','059e9136-2ec6-4a42-8c48-397194291ba6','NASA Data.json','ae7a212deeda1e28a86704dca294d85ee6cc773cde031fd9bbb6ae63c7743490','1.1','2026-03-13T18:18:34.783302','2026-03-13T18:18:34.783308','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('3656a331-2b2a-4942-bded-ce4e181c23dd','CRACMMv1.0 study 2021 dataset version 1 for January, April, July, and October.','all input to run the CMAQ model, all files are in netCDF format. This dataset is not publicly accessible because: hosted by the corresponding authors, can be obtained through a request. It can be accessed through the following means: All data is available upon request from the corresponding authors. Format: input for the CMAQ model in netCDF format','public','2026-03-22T11:50:01.238230','2026-03-22T11:50:01.238235','U.S. Environmental Protection Agency','Cheung Wong','020:00','9b0b7cc4-95d5-4c17-99ac-c3e8ba7898af','EPA ScienceHub','5273fd9ab6f3d9520ab7fabc1a1a01aa522e8b6553d6206f5178f0d345f66012','1.1','2026-03-22T11:50:01.238230','2026-03-22T11:50:01.238235',NULL,'020:000',0,'epa-gov'),('36a83d26-493e-478d-935b-4fb81215f057','BLM CO Oil and Gas Lease Sale Q1 (March) 2026','<div style=\'text-align:Left;\'><div><div><p><span>This data set consists of digital mapping data describing polygon geometry and linked attribute data for BLM Colorado\'s Quarterly Oil and Gas Lease Sale Parcels in the State of Colorado, BLM. The polygons in this data set were generated using the legal land descriptions of the identified Oil and Gas Lease Sale parcels and the Geographic Coordinate Data Base (GCDB) survey grid to produce a mapped layer. In some cases an error file may come with this data set. The error file shows polygons that did not process through the automated procedure. In other cases the BLM GIS Specialist may have manually completed identified error polygons. Mapped parcels should be checked against the legal land description for the sale parcels in the sale notice to verify and validate data. These data are consolidated from Field Office inputs.</span></p></div></div></div>','public','2026-03-14T10:00:57.998141','2026-03-14T10:00:57.998147','Bureau of Land Management','Bureau of Land Management, blm_co_info','010:04','f0abe26a-b67f-4ccf-9cc7-0105c9c4d51d','DOI BLM DCAT-US','a5876df4804ef32f3f00916ff91d220f109f88b7b7b1dd7c56fa5fe6111893bf','1.1','2026-03-14T10:00:57.998141','2026-03-14T10:00:57.998147','geospatial','010:000',0,'doi-gov'),('36b80bf0-fa10-4340-a695-d2caeaed8afc','MARS EXPRESS MARS MARSIS DERIVED                                      SUBSURFACE TEC DATA V1.0','This dataset contains the  Level 5 data that have been processed to produce Total Electron  Count data from the MARSIS subsurface sounder on Mars Express.  Details of the calibration and processing reports are found  in the documntation associated with this data set.','public','2026-03-13T16:40:36.432388','2026-03-13T16:40:36.432393','planetary plasma interactions','Planetary Data System','026:00','571ccf5c-cef6-4674-968f-09a3a8bdf235','NASA Data.json','75fc7ff05ed8770957deaec03a255ab8cf240be2cc7d3bd6a16235429c57d72d','1.1','2026-03-13T16:40:36.432388','2026-03-13T16:40:36.432393','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('36c4690a-9d3c-42fa-9d12-62ca8f45379a','NEW HORIZONS      LEISA KEM2      CALIBRATED V1.0','This data set contains Calibrated data taken by      the New Horizons Linear Etalon Imaging Spectral Array      instrument during the KEM1 ENCOUNTER and KEM2 CRUISE      mission phases.  This is VERSION 1.0 of this data set.      This version includes data acquired by the spacecraft between      08/14/2018 and 04/30/2023. It only includes data downlinked before      05/01/2023 and after 04/30/2022. Future datasets may include more      data acquired by the spacecraft after 08/13/2018 but downlinked after      04/30/2023.      This dataset includes data cubes observed prior to the Arrokoth      encounter.','public','2026-03-13T17:57:19.185322','2026-03-13T17:57:19.185326','small bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','db87520c-cf98-4d7c-a9d3-f8fb350cd829','NASA Data.json','b4d584c1aa1a2327a87a4f4689f2a465bec528d0faf068c030d99fa4ada8f788','1.1','2026-03-13T17:57:19.185322','2026-03-13T17:57:19.185326','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('36ecc6c0-487d-4176-957f-4efc48ce4a8d','ROSETTA-ORBITER CAL RPCMIP 3 CR2 V1.0','This archive contains data from the RPC-MIP instrument onboard ROSETTA Orbiter acquired during the CRUISE 2 mission phase. It also contains documentation which describes the RPC-MIP experiment. The data archived in this data set conform to the Planetary Data System Standards, Version 3.6.','public','2026-03-13T19:05:13.876341','2026-03-13T19:05:13.876346','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','39d2ef3f-204f-432f-ae26-2d7feffb7336','NASA Data.json','a3edc6ef09ff1de81d551944e1be8c62f4a89f30a041c2c570b08ccdd72b628c','1.1','2026-03-13T19:05:13.876341','2026-03-13T19:05:13.876346','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('36ee16b8-3d0a-4d10-bfe1-e03248619c32','MARS EXPRESS MARS MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 3 3266 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2010-01-01 to 2012-12-31. It is a Global Gravity measurement and covers the time 2012-07-26T05:00:43.000 to 2012-07-26T07:31:13.000.','public','2026-03-13T16:54:49.807041','2026-03-13T16:54:49.807047','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','6528d7ab-4a63-4de3-9590-e5b2c8dfd174','NASA Data.json','8d58f4e6b3f813741ee9b49ff101fa17939b7f38333a4633c58a934aac38a9e1','1.1','2026-03-13T16:54:49.807041','2026-03-13T16:54:49.807047','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('36f98a8b-0d50-42b0-9930-94edf735129b','Fugro Cruise C16215 Line 0963, 75 kHz VMADCP','Program of vessel mount Acoustic Doppler Current Profiler (ADCP) measurements comprising a combination of 300kHz and 75kHz ADCP data collected in the vicinity of the Loop Current and drilling blocks between 2004 and 2007.','public','2026-03-26T19:15:48.283809','2026-03-26T19:15:48.283816',NULL,NULL,NULL,'8990cfe9-5228-4e16-a7ef-ad8e6ad8cdf2','ioos',NULL,NULL,'2026-03-26T19:15:48.283809','2026-03-26T19:15:48.283816',NULL,NULL,NULL,'noaa-gov'),('36f9e5c9-04dc-40e8-b366-6c9d4f1372f0','LA-ICP-MS uranium-lead zircon data from igneous rocks collected during the 2025 field season from the Steese-White Mountains and Chena project areas, Yukon-Tanana Upland, Alaska','LA-ICP-MS uranium-lead zircon data from igneous rocks collected during the 2025 field season from the Steese-White Mountains and Chena project areas, Yukon-Tanana Upland, Alaska, Raw Data File 2026-11, contains uranium-lead (U-Pb) geochronologic data and trace and rare-earth element (TREE) data from single zircon spots analyzed by laser-ablation inductively coupled plasma mass spectrometry (LA-ICP-MS). U-Pb ages and TREE concentrations were acquired simultaneously from the same zircon volumes. Zircon data from 14 igneous and meta-igneous rock samples, primarily collected during the 2025 White Mountains field season, in support of the United States Geological Survey\'s Earth Mapping Resources Initiative (USGS Earth MRI) Steese and Chena geologic mapping projects. These Earth MRI projects are part of the effort to modernize geologic mapping of the nation\'s surface and subsurface with a focus on collecting data in areas of potential critical mineral resources. The USGS selected the Yukon-Tanana Upland as the most likely area for new potential mineral resources in Alaska and has been the focus area of the DGGS Mineral Resources Section since 2019. Geologic mapping of the approximately 24,000 km2 study area was accomplished through a combination of new helicopter- and vehicle-supported field investigations and the integration of existing DGGS, USGS, industry, and academic data. The goal of this geochronologic dataset is to delineate the timing of igneous activity to support geologic mapping, tectonic interpretation, and mineralization studies throughout east-central Alaska. These data are provided as a Raw Data File under an open end-user license and are available on the DGGS website: http://doi.org/10.14509/32064.','public','2026-03-15T03:17:22.530915','2026-03-15T03:17:22.530920',NULL,NULL,NULL,'4ef0b93f-0f25-42f6-92e3-373a0ead7d04','Alaska Division of Geological and Geophysical Surveys',NULL,NULL,'2026-03-15T03:17:22.530915','2026-03-15T03:17:22.530920',NULL,NULL,NULL,'state-of-alaska'),('37142df6-3273-49c6-85f8-d6c8a0c7ecb5','CASSINI RSS RAW DATA SET - TBIS2 V1.0','The Cassini Radio Science Titan Bistatic Experiment (TBIS2) Raw Data Archive is a time-ordered collection of radio science raw data acquired on March 27, 2009, during the Cassini Extended Mission.','public','2026-03-13T18:42:05.288734','2026-03-13T18:42:05.288740','Planetary Atmospheres','Planetary Data System','026:00','005a8ce5-484d-4fbe-997e-b452abc0d194','NASA Data.json','ddc22eba578577e230d750658bfc0e7b2a6d2599324b92565ce08e941830e916','1.1','2026-03-13T18:42:05.288734','2026-03-13T18:42:05.288740','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('3731afd8-a6e4-4dda-a7ee-a50fea339f47','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSINAC 4 ESC4-MTP023 RDR-REFLECT V1.0','This CODMAC level 4 data set contains radiometric calibrated and geometric distortion corrected (resampled) image data in reflectance units (normalized and thus without unit), acquired by the OSIRIS Narrow Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft during the COMET ESCORT 4 mission phase, covering the period from 2015-11-17T23:25:00.000 to 2015-12-15T23:24:59.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V1.0 is the first version of this dataset: Lien corrected dataset after October 2018 PSA/PDS external peer review.','public','2026-03-13T19:25:41.345693','2026-03-13T19:25:41.345700','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','47a84600-ebf3-49c2-a315-115c2115ebd9','NASA Data.json','4ff3900017ba64cf0f3bdecaeec14a5119b2886e1d956ffb419d9330ec02759a','1.1','2026-03-13T19:25:41.345693','2026-03-13T19:25:41.345700','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('374453fa-f9bd-4ab7-abbf-1290c44e298b','Continuous Fixed Station Water Quality Measurements in Timucuan Ecological and Historic Preserve, April 2008 (Certified)','This dataset represents continuous water quality measurements that were taken at a fixed point just outside of Timucuan Ecological and Historic Preserve during the month of April, 2008 as a part of the Fixed Station Water Quality Monitoring protocol that was developed by the Southeast Coast I&M Network (SECN). The measurements were taken by a YSI 6600 ESD Multi-Parameter Long Term Water Quality Monitoring Datasonde unit that serves as the standard fixed station water quality monitoring equipment for all similar operations conducted by the SECN. The following parameters were measured at 30 minute intervals during the time period that has been specified: Water Temperature, Specific Conductivity, Salinity, Dissolved Oxygen (DO), DO Concentration, Shallow Depth, pH Level, and Turbidity. Any anomalies noted regarding these parameters have also been noted in separate fields. Please note that these measurements have been certified by network personnel.','public','2026-03-26T05:34:13.718316','2026-03-26T05:34:13.718322','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','5bb46328-90de-41c4-ba93-da71577975cc','DOI NPS DCAT-US','c2dba0c8719c6b415a7beba3092b4070fb4b16ae57b4945c0706b8b0853c8c51','1.1','2026-03-26T05:34:13.718316','2026-03-26T05:34:13.718322','Vector Dataset','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('3769a579-2bde-46f7-a191-a765713c674e','myUSCIS - case-service','Stores receipt numbers for cases. Caches beneficiary information on H-1B Registration.','non-public','2026-03-22T11:54:52.918438','2026-03-22T11:54:52.918442','Unspecified','Open Data (MGMT)','024:030','f0ceb7c7-b802-48ff-b9fa-8dba7ddba68e','DHS datajson source','ce101d4e292eafe5710d00e5dab7e1b481cc34165271492db4f13b8cbfd6b16e','1.1','2026-03-22T11:54:52.918438','2026-03-22T11:54:52.918442',NULL,'024:000',0,'dhs-gov'),('376adc22-ff9b-4cd2-b320-2ce123d5ff9e','NEAR EARTH ASTEROID LIGHTCURVES V1.1','This data set is a collection of photometric lightcurves for 42 near-earth asteroids obtained at Ondrejov Observatory from 1984 through 1998.','public','2026-03-13T18:00:14.127273','2026-03-13T18:00:14.127278','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','973d85c1-e21b-4de6-9cc7-373dc8249d40','NASA Data.json','ca47761abea05dc195af0390ab04d0e83684ccc08f8f363b8cfebe08ee3a6822','1.1','2026-03-13T18:00:14.127273','2026-03-13T18:00:14.127278','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('38069c27-cfc5-4744-9b3b-f19e36254eab','ACS Table B21005 - Labor Force','American Community Survey dataset that covers labor forces estimates in Iowa at the 1 year and 5 year timeframe.','public','2026-03-28T22:00:43.269647','2026-03-28T22:00:43.269653','data.iowa.gov','svqueen',NULL,'fe1c5de6-3bf0-4db0-bbf0-6c56b446a35c','Iowa metadata','1f9f30a073b193c2e983056b33c630fb165046da3bacf0548e0250a5f80411c1','1.1','2026-03-28T22:00:43.269647','2026-03-28T22:00:43.269653','Economic Statistics',NULL,0,'state-of-iowa'),('382d5873-5767-464a-a9cf-937fcf66d03b','MARS EXPRESS MARS MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 3 3290 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2010-01-01 to 2012-12-31. It is a Global Gravity measurement and covers the time 2012-05-18T06:54:34.000 to 2012-05-18T08:08:30.500.','public','2026-03-13T17:24:07.431928','2026-03-13T17:24:07.431937','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','4aae60fe-7529-4d54-b23d-c4fe1332461a','NASA Data.json','37b84c2b0400c23657c3c68ffe2907797516ebeed6feefb498af20bc70de7d67','1.1','2026-03-13T17:24:07.431928','2026-03-13T17:24:07.431937','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('3852ad57-0486-417b-8938-fac2d96dfb73','MARS EXPRESS SUN MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 8 4225 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2021-01-01 to 2022-12-31. It is a Solar Conjunction measurement and covers the time 2021-09-15T00:26:51.399 to 2021-09-15T03:17:58.500.','public','2026-03-13T17:00:09.362001','2026-03-13T17:00:09.362007','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','79d7a22e-73c5-4904-b144-7d9c3ac2c6cd','NASA Data.json','3fbc302d363bc7087fe77825e55cbe7e6dc69d79bd461298027f3043cf458c83','1.1','2026-03-13T17:00:09.362001','2026-03-13T17:00:09.362007','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('3874ca5f-0276-4619-abfd-32b648876594','Continuous Fixed Station Water Quality Measurements in Timucuan Ecological and Historic Preserve, May 2008 (Certified)','This dataset represents continuous water quality measurements that were taken at a fixed point in Timucuan Ecological and Historic Preserve during the month of May, 2008 as a part of the Fixed Station Water Quality Monitoring protocol that was developed by the Southeast Coast I&M Network (SECN). The measurements were taken by a YSI 6600 ESD Multi-Parameter Long Term Water Quality Monitoring Datasonde unit that serves as the standard fixed station water quality monitoring equipment for all similar operations conducted by the SECN. The following parameters were measured at 30 minute intervals during the time period that has been specified: Water Temperature, Specific Conductivity, Salinity, Dissolved Oxygen (DO), DO Concentration, Shallow Depth, pH Level, and Turbidity. Any anomalies noted regarding these parameters have also been noted in separate fields. Please note that these measurements have been certified by network personnel.','public','2026-03-26T05:33:19.621947','2026-03-26T05:33:19.621955','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','4e5006aa-fb6d-43c8-b813-8f2008c6f479','DOI NPS DCAT-US','b4b83e53f74c04264d2769ac81a7e67ba65124abe6b022256cb199ac7217e92b','1.1','2026-03-26T05:33:19.621947','2026-03-26T05:33:19.621955','Vector Dataset','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('387d2033-271a-43e2-bffd-eabc9f9a49d0','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RPCICA 4 ESC3 CORR V1.0','This dataset contains corrected and RESAMPLED CALIBRATED DATA fromthe RPCICA instrument on mission ROSETTA during Comet escort 3.Data contains measurements of solar wind interactionwith the atmosphere of target comet 67P.','public','2026-03-13T20:09:14.282264','2026-03-13T20:09:14.282271','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','0600977b-43fe-49bc-a499-9214dbe923c7','NASA Data.json','05e46eb90a44607c6e9140318a8cf16d11931d4f590d99a6499848904c61a132','1.1','2026-03-13T20:09:14.282264','2026-03-13T20:09:14.282271','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('38a19e81-0008-48bd-ab2e-5208b7324769','FIRST - FOIA Processing Data','This data represents FOIA cases, the metadata about files processed as part of those cases, and metadata about the case processing workflow.','non-public','2026-03-22T11:52:37.841564','2026-03-22T11:52:37.841568','Unspecified','Open Data (MGMT)','024:030','f5efff69-4751-4150-a07a-b75aa804e2b5','DHS datajson source','b7b4a4ab7a08ae93df37a5fcec5a2ea3d766f9d0f8178fa7ba9018d1ec0adcf8','1.1','2026-03-22T11:52:37.841564','2026-03-22T11:52:37.841568',NULL,'024:000',0,'dhs-gov'),('38ad0fd5-40f5-4bbb-9b3f-d827313eb82d','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSINAC 3 EXT1-MTP026 RDR V3.0','This CODMAC level 3 data set contains radiometric calibrated image data in W/m^2/sr/nm, acquired by the OSIRIS Narrow Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft during the ROSETTA EXTENSION 1 mission phase, covering the period from 2016-02-09T23:25:00.000 to 2016-03-08T23:24:59.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V3.0 supersedes previous deliveries of the same dataset with the following changes since the last version: Lien corrected dataset after the July and October 2018 PSA/PDS external peer reviews. Updated documentation and ancillary files, added document on bandpass filter. Updated SCIENCE_USER_GUIDE_V03.PDF to include one section about FAQ and one section about image data quality. Added shutter backtravel and readout issues to image quality map. Updated DATA_QUALITY_ID keyword in image header. Improved handling of images with missing packets. Replaced FITs file extension .FTS with .FIT. Browse products changed to the same size as the original image.','public','2026-03-13T16:51:02.099575','2026-03-13T16:51:02.099580','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','fd88b1fa-9a67-44ba-b84e-f0f7570c53e4','NASA Data.json','3acd96832df57ccb77e7d89fa392952c9b7d614f7787f18c13855c5ada4afabe','1.1','2026-03-13T16:51:02.099575','2026-03-13T16:51:02.099580','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('38dc6e99-fac0-4f85-8afa-9a25b29f5e62','MARS EXPRESS SUN MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 5 3763 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2015-01-01 to 2016-12-31. It is a Solar Conjunction measurement and covers the time 2015-06-11T00:22:15.000 to 2015-06-11T08:21:48.500.','public','2026-03-13T17:39:20.892236','2026-03-13T17:39:20.892242','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','d4fa05aa-847c-4beb-9568-95dfde12ecf0','NASA Data.json','d9d5ff9c88358585e46ff4c4b5e57eedb93ffd37df55732a0c4576efaed93c8f','1.1','2026-03-13T17:39:20.892236','2026-03-13T17:39:20.892242','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('39043a46-26cc-4316-8be8-65eb1db70b41','GOLDSTONE MARS RADIO TELESCOPE DERIVED ALTIMETRY V1.0','This data set consists of Martian radii and elevations (relative to the 6 millibar reference surface) measured relative to JPL ephemeris DE_118. The data were obtained by the Goldstone Solar System Radar during the oppositions of 1971-1982. Present form of table generated by R. Mehlman, UCLA/IGPP.','public','2026-03-13T19:58:32.767908','2026-03-13T19:58:32.767915','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','3f088fbe-ffc7-42e9-b29d-b56cc4970ad0','NASA Data.json','bd2cef56a529796431d8d89a5c05333cacd921ecc2a810d904508f9fb7328715','1.1','2026-03-13T19:58:32.767908','2026-03-13T19:58:32.767915','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('3917bf9d-728a-44cb-b4c6-f846f7ecc439','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 2 0837 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 2 phase 2015-03-11 to 2015-06-30. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-06-10T16:12:05.000 to 2015-06-10T18:26:29.000.','public','2026-03-13T17:47:32.707612','2026-03-13T17:47:32.707618','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','5deb1130-2528-497c-a664-5f1709fe5d5f','NASA Data.json','ea7b7cdb49bce5021d9606d700bcf54f8c7c0985d902b486aa96f9a75fe87014','1.1','2026-03-13T17:47:32.707612','2026-03-13T17:47:32.707618','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('392c8dee-3bef-4713-82a6-b1faa830b233','Hydrographic and Impairment Statistics Database: NPS-WSR White Clay Wild and Scenic River','Hydrographic and Impairment Statistics (HIS) is a National Park Service (NPS) Water Resources Division (WRD) project established to track certain goals created in response to the Government Performance and Results Act of 1993 (GPRA). One water resources management goal established by the Department of the Interior under GRPA requires NPS to track the percent of its managed surface waters that are meeting Clean Water Act (CWA) water quality standards. This goal requires an accurate inventory that spatially quantifies the surface water hydrography that each bureau manages and a procedure to determine and track which waterbodies are or are not meeting water quality standards as outlined by Section 303(d) of the CWA. This project helps meet this DOI GRPA goal by inventorying and monitoring in a geographic information system for the NPS: (1) CWA 303(d) quality impaired waters and causes; and (2) hydrographic statistics based on the United States Geological Survey (USGS) National Hydrography Dataset (NHD). Hydrographic and 303(d) impairment statistics were evaluated based on a combination of 1:24,000 (NHD) and finer scale data (frequently provided by state GIS layers).','public','2026-03-29T06:05:26.450605','2026-03-29T06:05:26.450610','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','8b512d7b-0e0a-4970-b4b5-7aa82c8d5b3e','DOI NPS DCAT-US','24d4fa82efc5777b3ab7503cbf9cb753a2ba6540388a9295ef7d06bdae67773a','1.1','2026-03-29T06:05:26.450605','2026-03-29T06:05:26.450610','geospatial','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('3970319f-f4cf-4953-a533-5b491f436d5a','\"Deepwater CTD - 00622442.bdo.nc - 21.03N, -95.24W - 1971-05-04\"','The Minerals Management Service (MMS) of the U. S. Department of the Interior funded the Deepwater Physical Oceanography Reanalysis and Synthesis of Historical Data Study in the Gulf of Mexico. MMS awarded the contract to the Texas A&M Research Foundation in July 1998. The basic study area is bounded by the shelf edge and the 25DGN latitude, which is the southern boundary; it extends from sea surface to sea floor. MMS has four objectives for the study. First is to create an inventory of physical oceanographic data and compile it into a single database on a CD-ROM. Second is to conduct analyses and interpretations of the physical oceanographic data to identify physical processes and phenomena. Third is to produce a climatology of the processes from available data and analyses and to prioritize the processes in terms of importance to improved understanding, simulation, and prediction of deepwater circulation. Fourth is to provide criteria and constraints useful in design of future field observations and numerical modeling efforts. Study results will provide MMS with information needed to direct its resources more efficiently and effectively in the review and assessment of potential environmental impacts of offshore oil and gas operations in the deepwater Gulf of Mexico.','public','2026-03-26T19:15:05.898709','2026-03-26T19:15:05.898717',NULL,NULL,NULL,'0c9ca351-81b0-4b7a-8a2a-d46ed30222b1','ioos',NULL,NULL,'2026-03-26T19:15:05.898709','2026-03-26T19:15:05.898717',NULL,NULL,NULL,'noaa-gov'),('39a36ee5-d204-41cd-9d33-d7527f3f54c9','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSIWAC 4 PRL-MTP008 RDR-INFLDSTR V1.0','This CODMAC level 4 data set contains solar stray-light corrected, in-field stray-light corrected,  radiometric calibrated and geometric distortion corrected  (resampled) image data in W/m^2/sr/nm,  acquired by the OSIRIS Wide Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft  during the PRELANDING mission phase, covering the period  from 2014-09-23T10:00:00.000 to 2014-10-24T09:59:59.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V1.0 is the first version of this dataset: Lien corrected dataset after September 2019 PSA/PDS external peer review.','public','2026-03-13T17:33:21.951595','2026-03-13T17:33:21.951600','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','cee874b2-4887-471e-9a65-6cfa4232c2e9','NASA Data.json','cfde80af7e46f7cc919f859bd61af2bc16426ed67efc64827a845cae45632250','1.1','2026-03-13T17:33:21.951595','2026-03-13T17:33:21.951600','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('39b76524-e9a3-40fd-ab44-e4cba246e82b','LRO MOON LASER ALTIMETER 2 EDR V1.0','This data set contains archival raw experiment data from the Lunar Orbiter Laser Altimeter instrument (LOLA).','public','2026-03-13T18:52:52.348651','2026-03-13T18:52:52.348656','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','c1eb4dc8-12fb-42c1-bde9-f6e99c17435e','NASA Data.json','964fd3b98df20b31bf5c272b840ed6baca5e62c3fff159f86e48085d649180ad','1.1','2026-03-13T18:52:52.348651','2026-03-13T18:52:52.348656','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('39bf164f-99be-4b06-9995-f0d4ce98f5c1','Laborshed - Availability','Laborshed dataset that contains data regarding the availability of those in the labor supply, and those who are likely to accept or change employment.','public','2026-03-28T21:58:10.594642','2026-03-28T21:58:10.594647','data.iowa.gov','svqueen',NULL,'1d13c7f8-8f0e-4d7a-a1fc-cc62e1c41ce9','Iowa metadata','84d28c09cb4c393d35114bf5d2fe2a5914d0bfe62804e0541ae025e1f1e511c4','1.1','2026-03-28T21:58:10.594642','2026-03-28T21:58:10.594647','Economic Statistics',NULL,0,'state-of-iowa'),('39c95dde-17f9-43d7-83b5-50a4462362b6','Continuous Fixed Station Water Quality Measurements in Timucuan Ecological and Historic Preserve, September 2008 (Certified)','This dataset represents continuous water quality measurements that were taken at a fixed point in Timucuan Ecological and Historic Preserve during the month of September, 2008 as a part of the Fixed Station Water Quality Monitoring protocol that was developed by the Southeast Coast I&M Network (SECN). The measurements were taken by a YSI 6600 ESD Multi-Parameter Long Term Water Quality Monitoring Datasonde unit that serves as the standard fixed station water quality monitoring equipment for all similar operations conducted by the SECN. The following parameters were measured at 30 minute intervals during the time period that has been specified: Water Temperature, Specific Conductivity, Salinity, Dissolved Oxygen (DO), DO Concentration, Shallow Depth, pH Level, and Turbidity. Any anomalies noted regarding these parameters have also been noted in separate fields. Please note that these measurements have been certified by network personnel.','public','2026-03-26T05:29:59.180288','2026-03-26T05:29:59.180293','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','23a1a903-8481-40d3-8ac5-7ada1ed3e546','DOI NPS DCAT-US','7e6bcf56c312b99735b2d0d5d91873b5ebc70bb6951366aa2c5a58877f348451','1.1','2026-03-26T05:29:59.180288','2026-03-26T05:29:59.180293','Vector Dataset','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('39f0f7b2-910c-4d69-b6f9-ba47e960aed1','Fugro Cruise C16185 Line 1438, 75 kHz VMADCP','Program of vessel mount Acoustic Doppler Current Profiler (ADCP) measurements comprising a combination of 300kHz and 75kHz ADCP data collected in the vicinity of the Loop Current and drilling blocks between 2004 and 2007.','public','2026-03-26T19:17:19.281334','2026-03-26T19:17:19.281340',NULL,NULL,NULL,'211dbd25-5a2b-4938-99ef-0f4b53be8d98','ioos',NULL,NULL,'2026-03-26T19:17:19.281334','2026-03-26T19:17:19.281340',NULL,NULL,NULL,'noaa-gov'),('3a25efb0-604d-4953-9289-0cd4ffcecf08','Continuous Fixed Station Water Quality Measurements in Timucuan Ecological and Historic Preserve, February 2008 (Certified)','This dataset represents continuous water quality measurements that were taken at a fixed point in Timucuan Ecological and Historic Preserve during the month of February, 2008 as a part of the Fixed Station Water Quality Monitoring protocol that was developed by the Southeast Coast I&M Network (SECN). The measurements were taken by a YSI 6600 ESD Multi-Parameter Long Term Water Quality Monitoring Datasonde unit that serves as the standard fixed station water quality monitoring equipment for all similar operations conducted by the SECN. The following parameters were measured at 30 minute intervals during the time period that has been specified: Water Temperature, Specific Conductivity, Salinity, Dissolved Oxygen (DO), DO Concentration, Shallow Depth, pH Level, and Turbidity. Any anomalies noted regarding these parameters have also been noted in separate fields. Please note that these measurements have been certified by network personnel.','public','2026-03-26T05:33:48.143029','2026-03-26T05:33:48.143034','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','593f7c0d-70d8-446e-8bff-cd28d38cf0e3','DOI NPS DCAT-US','5ace84fd04765c935cd3e0cc954b18e0e98a479e2749495a64669047842beb61','1.1','2026-03-26T05:33:48.143029','2026-03-26T05:33:48.143034','Vector Dataset','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('3a3ccc47-91d8-40de-b5f2-251f831eb6d4','Laborshed - Likeliness to Change or Accept Employment','Laborshed dataset containing data about the counts of the likeliness to change or accept employment for a given laborshed area by various demographic groups. Data spans across all laborsheds in Iowa.','public','2026-03-28T21:58:45.580418','2026-03-28T21:58:45.580422','data.iowa.gov','svqueen',NULL,'b45d9903-f825-4d16-b7ed-2424a1758c6c','Iowa metadata','0df101eb2ea0866642c231079a23e4afa85413dde387315c576f2697c2e71374','1.1','2026-03-28T21:58:45.580418','2026-03-28T21:58:45.580422','Economic Statistics',NULL,0,'state-of-iowa'),('3a6d11a2-0f42-4535-bd62-86683657ee41','MARS EXPRESS MARS MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 7 4118 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2019-01-01 to 2020-12-31. It is a Occultation measurement and covers the time 2020-09-02T03:20:00.000 to 2020-09-02T04:10:00.000.','public','2026-03-13T18:31:03.233116','2026-03-13T18:31:03.233123','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','5c2f7428-dce7-4e7f-8270-ad228254589b','NASA Data.json','66f81d2bfd0a9d1aafff6b48aacb582860cffcd850cf13bac2b2acef8a43f6d6','1.1','2026-03-13T18:31:03.233116','2026-03-13T18:31:03.233123','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('3a7e2819-d9c2-4654-9fdd-8a6eb24feb8b','ROSETTA-ORBITER CHECK GIADA 2 EAR3 EARTHSWINGBY3 V1.0','Payload Checkout 10 (PC10) was an active checkout where a target independent opportunity to perform interactive operations and to request spacecraft pointing was given to all Rosetta payload teams. All Rosetta payload took part in this scenario The Active Payload Checkout 10 ran for 12 consecutive days starting on the 21th September 2009 until the 2th October 2009. This is the allocated time of the active PC10 scenario that preceded it PC10 consists of two phases. The 1st phase is a passive test (GD01) similar to the previous Passive Payload Checkouts the 2nd phase is an active test; GD02 is dealt with GIADA/VIRTIS interference test, in GD03 we upload on-board of new Context File settings performing and checking new procedures, GD_INT is dealt with GIADA/ROSINA interference test. The passive test (GD01), which includes standard procedures and full functional verification, was executed by switching on Main and Redundant I/Fs in sequence and executing similar procedures for the two cases. GD02, GD03 and GD_INT were executed only on Main I/F. The data reported in this data set have been converted from ADC counts to engineering values. The quality of the Housekeeping and Calibration data is good. Scientific data are due to noise, as no grain event is expected during this mission phase. These data must be only considered to evaluate GIADA behaviour and not as real scientific data. Data reported by GDS and IS are due to noise as no dust event is expected during this mission phase. MBS frequency changes, once normalised for frequency vs. temperature dependence, if present, are due to deposition of contaminants existing in the S/C environment. Housekeeping and Calibration data from all GIADA sub-systems are useful to evaluate instrument health and behaviour when compared with similar data acquired during other mission phases.','public','2026-03-13T18:09:40.962843','2026-03-13T18:09:40.962851','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','4d9db2b7-be5d-43ba-bd18-37a165fdd0ff','NASA Data.json','db4b12705b7353c9dfd72f92a26f9539030676c28a4284d53aae0924039e0251','1.1','2026-03-13T18:09:40.962843','2026-03-13T18:09:40.962851','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('3a7fd0ab-c6a5-4ed8-90f2-4e0c95db9c7f','Walton-Smith CTD, WS17282, WS17282_WS17282_Stn17, 2017-10-10, 24.636N 81.1972W','Walton-Smith Conductivity, Temperature, Depth (CTD) - WS17282 - WS17282_WS17282_Stn17 - 2017-10-10 - 24.636N 81.1972W. Hydrographic Measurements in the Gulf of Mexico. flags: 1 = good; 3 =  mean ÃÂ± 3*standard deviation; 4 = mean ÃÂ± 5*standard deviation; 9 = missing. other','public','2026-03-26T19:16:15.066838','2026-03-26T19:16:15.066844',NULL,NULL,NULL,'22ab3ae7-2c5a-479f-894f-c7ee9b450038','ioos',NULL,NULL,'2026-03-26T19:16:15.066838','2026-03-26T19:16:15.066844',NULL,NULL,NULL,'noaa-gov'),('3ab1056a-1f06-4f21-a83f-23390c038b16','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P NAVCAM 3 PRELANDING MTP003 V1.0','This dataset contains ROSETTA NAVCAM RADIOMETRICALLY CALIBRATED DATA of the PRELANDING MTP003 Phase from 08 May. 2014, 13:18:02 to 04 Jun. 2014, 10:32:05 when at the vicinity of target 67P/CG.','public','2026-03-13T19:06:35.410225','2026-03-13T19:06:35.410231','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','266c542f-3a86-41ca-8b6a-ee27763d110d','NASA Data.json','0b21267c34aeaf877a4cbee928c19345cb7af6b072cb0b51d7d94ee6f56d843e','1.1','2026-03-13T19:06:35.410225','2026-03-13T19:06:35.410231','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('3ab2e5cd-b455-4481-bcaf-f9c3ad8c6605','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 ROSETTA EXTENSION 1 1311 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the ROSETTA EXTENSION 1 phase 2016-01-01 to 2016-04-05. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2016-01-04T01:32:35.000 to 2016-01-04T07:54:52.000.','public','2026-03-13T16:43:46.857338','2026-03-13T16:43:46.857343','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','c2a5b69b-7a3b-424d-b348-50ffabebedcf','NASA Data.json','a97c0d99cde895a80e36fad54c8a5170dcb96ba9370f8fb4bbe0faf162c2fbbe','1.1','2026-03-13T16:43:46.857338','2026-03-13T16:43:46.857343','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('3abb576a-9a71-421b-aced-83a879a02333','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 3 0871 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 3 phase 2015-07-01 to 2015-10-21. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-07-01T21:06:55.000 to 2015-07-02T03:00:23.500.','public','2026-03-13T20:04:05.580300','2026-03-13T20:04:05.580305','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','390cd604-0e83-49bc-a4f7-5c0ec2a5d533','NASA Data.json','a722c0a2a5843aa7235ceb97ec89e058305d6519f6daf8c6d6ec3dbd2fd93d20','1.1','2026-03-13T20:04:05.580300','2026-03-13T20:04:05.580305','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('3ad28cfa-d0b5-44db-889b-a71a57a03414','MEX SPICAM CRUISE/MARS UV EDR-RAW V2.0','The Mars Express SPICAM level 0A UV data set contains raw measurements from the ultra violet SPICAM spectrometer collected during the cruise and MARS phases','public','2026-03-13T18:06:49.563852','2026-03-13T18:06:49.563859','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','1c7f946b-6452-4bad-9747-0dabfac646b6','NASA Data.json','7a2baedc9fc28ac836e399d22be4f56aebffd03815acf469dbba412b41e81cba','1.1','2026-03-13T18:06:49.563852','2026-03-13T18:06:49.563859','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('3b43639d-3143-4d64-bf78-15463a0a6023','BLM ID Ground Transportation Linear Features','The purpose of the BLM ID Ground Transportation Linear Features (GTLF) is to provide a standardized transportation information for use in BLM programs and analysis. The ground transportation linear features gathered, inventoried, analyzed and recorded in a Travel Management Plan (TMP). The TMP analyzes transportation options and incorporates public participation to assist in determining travel routes, modes of travel, season of use on selected and surrounding BLM managed lands. The BLM ID only maintains only GTLF routes that have been recorded in a TMP. All other data is considered Non-BLM authoritive, administered and maintained transportation data and is provided only as spatial and tabular reference material. The BLM ID GTLF contains external routes that provides connectivity to BLM managed lands. The purpose for collecting and maintaining an Idaho state-wide route connectivity is to provide a broad overview of the transportation network for properly focused analysis or inventory purposes and to provide connectivity between BLM managed routes and the broader transportation networks.','public','2026-03-25T12:35:38.193077','2026-03-25T12:35:38.193085','Bureau of Land Management','Bureau of Land Management, blm_id_stateoffice','010:04','ae4acc3f-e30f-4317-a99e-cd984350badf','DOI BLM DCAT-US','b56b4d2dc9691be44895a9481639314c6a9f2b6d524bd91ae54c282c2b940d30','1.1','2026-03-25T12:35:38.193077','2026-03-25T12:35:38.193085','geospatial','010:000',0,'doi-gov'),('3b6fab33-8c24-4345-b54c-f96cce83d3d7','MARS EXPRESS ASPERA-3 CAL RDR ELECTRON SPECTROMTR EXT4 V1.0','This data set contains calibrated Mars Express ASPERA-3         Electron Spectrometer (ELS) data for the fourth mission         extension (January 1, 2013 - Dec. 31, 2014).  These data         are provided in units of Differential Number Flux (DNF):         cnts/(cm**2-sr-sec-eV)','public','2026-03-13T17:42:04.755126','2026-03-13T17:42:04.755133','planetary plasma interactions','Planetary Data System','026:00','dc1d94e3-66b4-4170-87a1-52e40266b221','NASA Data.json','80b2e7cddbf2932b7e315bb29f628b605b0224adac501e9a6e21b921cff87d71','1.1','2026-03-13T17:42:04.755126','2026-03-13T17:42:04.755133','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('3ba07795-820b-4849-9660-4fbfedb2a094','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 2 0693 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 2 phase 2015-03-11 to 2015-06-30. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-04-04T23:28:05.000 to 2015-04-05T01:29:10.000.','public','2026-03-13T17:19:38.425666','2026-03-13T17:19:38.425672','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','2afe0f7b-b486-4bea-b182-19374c6ac564','NASA Data.json','b850528ec3656ac39169ede33f85658310fda58ff0c3f8545ea571d5c168b93c','1.1','2026-03-13T17:19:38.425666','2026-03-13T17:19:38.425672','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('3ba197ef-1553-4d9f-ab67-4f78d5061418','ROSETTA-ORBITER COMET ESCORT OSINAC 2 EDR MTP 015 V1.0','This data set contains raw EDR images acquired by the OSIRIS Narrow AngleCamera during the escort phase of the Rosetta mission at the comet 67P,covering the period from 2015-04-08 to 2015-05-05.','public','2026-03-13T17:42:15.848403','2026-03-13T17:42:15.848410','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','2f95951c-5c8f-43e5-b3de-8e2f1cf18f55','NASA Data.json','a7652974ef6213593dda4b8e54f3a564f2f8f46105746597c510d221a5e1f98f','1.1','2026-03-13T17:42:15.848403','2026-03-13T17:42:15.848410','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('3bb391b1-e929-4f82-9fb0-68afd69eb8bd','MR9/VO1/VO2 MARS IMAGING SCIENCE SUBSYSTEM/VIS 5 CLOUD V1.0','This data set consists of a catalog of clouds observed in Mariner 9 and Viking Orbiter images. Seven \'cloud types\' were defined according to easily observable objective morphologic criteria. The entire Mariner 9 and Viking Orbiter image data sets (approximately 7400 and over 50000 images, respectively) were examined at least twice, by two separate observers. Cloud occurrences were compiled by examining images for specific cloud morphologies, examining the same area at different times, utilizing limb images, and consulting photomosaics to determine the spatial relations of cloud obscurations.','public','2026-03-13T16:42:44.299632','2026-03-13T16:42:44.299747','Planetary Atmospheres','Planetary Data System','026:00','b5732551-16bf-46cf-bd73-7ec94afa11aa','NASA Data.json','65d9775ee386c1741cc1312bfd383a33e7c2364c3b9889c03b4b956c72b8d721','1.1','2026-03-13T16:42:44.299632','2026-03-13T16:42:44.299747','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('3bbf6b1c-c050-41ef-9169-353e59cea445','ISIS 2 Topside Sounder Ionograms','These ionograms were digitized from the original ISIS-2 7-track analog telemetry tapes using the facilities of the former Data Evaluation Laboratory at the NASA/GSFC. This data restoration project is headed by Dr. R.F. Benson (NASA/GSFC). Ionograms were digitized at the rate of 40,000 16-bit samples/sec. This sample rate is higher than the Nyquist frequency of 30 kHz. The sample frequency of 40 kHz provides a measurement every 25 microseconds corresponding to an apparent range (c*t/2) interval of 3.75 km. Ionograms with this sample rate are designated as \"full\" ionograms because they have the full 3.75 km apparent-range resolution. The ionograms used for most analysis, and those available from CDAWeb, were produced by averaging every four samples of the sounder-receiver video amplitude output to yield an average value every 100 microseconds corresponding to an apparent-range resolution of 15 km. These ionogram files are referred to as \"average\" files with standard resolution. Each ionogram consists of a fixed-frequency and and a swept-frequency portion. The time resolution between ionograms is typically 14 or 22 seconds depending on the frequency sweep range.','public','2026-03-13T22:35:21.498274','2026-03-13T22:35:21.498282','NASA Space Physics Data Facility (SPDF) Data Services','NASA Space Physics Data Facility','026:00','b739e245-d531-43f1-8f02-50b18ec441c6','NASA Data.json','16c9afb24af46f7736baa66e1e45c2a40e5210905cca2950628ceabad60744e4','1.1','2026-03-13T22:35:21.498274','2026-03-13T22:35:21.498282','Heliophysics','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('3bfccb17-ef16-49ec-9913-1387f474b73b','MARS EXPRESS SUN MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 8 4223 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2021-01-01 to 2022-12-31. It is a Solar Conjunction measurement and covers the time 2021-09-08T01:32:07.100 to 2021-09-08T03:59:53.549.','public','2026-03-13T16:50:03.306988','2026-03-13T16:50:03.306994','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','d1472d3b-e53e-4415-89f7-0d674cc0d14d','NASA Data.json','8e7580e22a4288ebdbd6e98a75c6324666c84823d824ca64777c10800edc4c45','1.1','2026-03-13T16:50:03.306988','2026-03-13T16:50:03.306994','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('3c4c6df7-62e5-4f3e-8694-99a1da4d37a8','Service Request 20250101 to 20251231','<p><span style=\'background-color:rgb(255,255,255); color:rgb(64,65,57); font-family:&quot;Nunito Sans Light&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px;\'><span style=\'display:inline !important; float:none; font-style:normal; font-variant-caps:normal; font-variant-ligatures:normal; font-weight:400; letter-spacing:normal; text-align:start; text-decoration-color:initial; text-decoration-style:initial; text-indent:0px; text-transform:none; word-spacing:0px;\'>This information is from Hartford 311 which is a toll-free, non-emergency call center, designed to connect Hartford residents, businesses and visitors to City services, resources and information.</span></span></p>','public','2026-03-24T06:43:02.153628','2026-03-24T06:43:02.153634','City of Hartford','HartfordData',NULL,'3313ab6a-b9a1-4bdc-8e74-aad59d8bd2d4','Hartford Data.json','1f7c1c2a96f6df00c877edc64a2fab23b966ac9dde0959eef1487a0446d280dc','1.1','2026-03-24T06:43:02.153628','2026-03-24T06:43:02.153634','geospatial',NULL,0,'city-of-hartford'),('3c8c1b57-81a8-4de9-83fb-85ac3f2cab60','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RPCMIP 5 ESC1 V1.0','This archive contains derived data from the RPC-MIP instrument on-board ROSETTA Orbiter acquired during the COMET ESCORT 1 mission phase. Observations are performed in the vicinity of comet 67P/C-G. It also contains documentation which describes the RPC-MIP experiment. The data archived in this data set conform to the Planetary Data System Standards, Version 3.6.','public','2026-03-13T17:47:58.550290','2026-03-13T17:47:58.550296','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','f1c5df43-4b7b-4d18-8431-e38e9d9d0461','NASA Data.json','97b71220e1ca2c86f92011574707eea2700d4915cb8c31a579fb002cd3bbd02d','1.1','2026-03-13T17:47:58.550290','2026-03-13T17:47:58.550296','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('3c8dda0c-19b9-46b2-9a5c-0ef4da001824','Short-Term Industry Projections','Industry projections estimate the future performance and trends of industries over a defined period. These are 2-year projections for the State of Iowa and its six local workforce development areas (LWDA). Projections are are based on a combination of historical data, market analysis, economic indicators, and emerging trends.','public','2026-03-28T22:01:16.581425','2026-03-28T22:01:16.581430','data.iowa.gov','Katie Green',NULL,'d5756e11-e396-4658-872d-59789dc13c67','Iowa metadata','2820860e396a48c747d478904086bbbb17d133edc6192a68eb5bb30243c7d4cb','1.1','2026-03-28T22:01:16.581425','2026-03-28T22:01:16.581430','Workforce',NULL,0,'state-of-iowa'),('3c91e2fc-32ba-4a3a-ab7d-9ec82678de87','Phosphorus removal capacity, arsenic leaching, and PFAS content of drinking water treatment residuals with potential to enhance stormwater infrastructure in New England, USA','The data sets include results from analyzing drinking water treatment residuals (DWTRs) collected from 11 drinking water treatment facilities located in the Northeast Region. The goal of analyzing DWTRs are to understand their phosphorus (P) removal capacity, arsenic leaching, and PFAS content so that we can better utilize their potential for enhancing stormwater infrastructure in New England to achieve P reduction goal. \n\nThis dataset is associated with the following publication:\nKubow, M., T. Chin, A. Sherman, Y. Yuan, M. Voorhees, A. Traviglia, J. McCord, M. Strynar, S. Hurley, and E. Roy. Phosphorus Removal Capacity, Arsenic Leaching, and PFAS Content of Drinking Water Treatment Residuals with Potential to Enhance Stormwater Infrastructure in New England.   Journal of Sustainable Water in the Built Environment. American Society of Civil Engineers (ASCE), New York, NY, USA, 12(2): 1-9, (2026).','public','2026-03-15T10:22:37.097306','2026-03-15T10:22:37.097311','U.S. Environmental Protection Agency','Yongping Yuan','020:00','40cf4b17-44f1-4e90-8ba1-c474ac688c53','EPA ScienceHub','b606bab176d67a958f32f639a23bd0f7861b97cc33da085c7cca19e8568e277e','1.1','2026-03-15T10:22:37.097306','2026-03-15T10:22:37.097311',NULL,'020:000',0,'epa-gov'),('3cf13de0-1e31-4eee-af82-3cc38f22909b','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P MIRO 4 PRL V2.0','This data set contains Spectroscopic and Continuum level 4 data, in the form of table files, taken during the ROSETTA PRELANDING phase of the Rosetta mission to comet 67P/CHURYUMOV-GERASIMENKO by the MIRO instrument. The major updates with this version (V2.0) are the addition of a Level 4 continuum data product and the elimination of separate geometry files for the spectroscopic data.','public','2026-03-13T18:46:24.892956','2026-03-13T18:46:24.892961','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','d6ef8f7d-0ce0-4839-8a5c-d74a45a49c2f','NASA Data.json','e1c75d9e3cc3e3741fbf722ee30b622a8e1a481c9f2ab997c7a68b3f9f85971e','1.1','2026-03-13T18:46:24.892956','2026-03-13T18:46:24.892961','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('3cf9af64-975e-4076-8a20-3718deefe845','Bat Activity Inventory at Pearl Harbor National Memorial 2024 - Open Format Dataset','We examined ‘ōpe‘ape‘a, or Hawaiian hoary bat (Lasiurus semotus; Chiroptera: Vespertilionidae), acoustic activity and surveyed potential roost trees at the Ford Island Chief Petty Officer’s (CPO) Bungalows Neighborhood of Pearl Harbor National Memorial (PERL) on the island of O‘ahu. We established four acoustic monitoring stations (PERL1–PERL4) that operated nightly to survey for ‘ōpe‘ape‘a echolocation activity from June to December 2024. Tree physiognomy data were collected at 12 potential roost trees and included tree species, tree height, diameter at breast height (DBH), percent canopy cover, distance to nearest tree, elevation, and canopy geometry. We collected 357,802 acoustic files over 672 station-nights across the four acoustic monitoring stations. ‘Ōpe‘ape‘a echolocation activity was detected over a total of 26 (4%) station-nights and during each month of the survey period except June. Echolocation activity peaked in September and October 2024, which is during the post-lactation and fledging period. These results represent a baseline for assessing ‘ōpe‘ape‘a acoustic activity and potential roosting resources in PERL.','public','2026-03-27T05:28:48.407175','2026-03-27T05:28:48.407181','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','1b9d1f56-31ac-4bcf-824c-aac4f86fb5ef','DOI NPS DCAT-US','dee49a5f423db18ab317e10aee8cd776122f5d808993915259fbc0535731bf4f','1.1','2026-03-27T05:28:48.407175','2026-03-27T05:28:48.407181','Data Package','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('3cfd33b6-f05f-4a75-8c8d-72474d6cab8c','Continuous Fixed Station Water Quality Measurements in Timucuan Ecological and Historic Preserve, June 2008 (Certified)','This dataset represents continuous water quality measurements that were taken at a fixed point just outside of Timucuan Ecological and Historic Preserve during the month of June, 2008 as a part of the Fixed Station Water Quality Monitoring protocol that was developed by the Southeast Coast I&M Network (SECN). The measurements were taken by a YSI 6600 ESD Multi-Parameter Long Term Water Quality Monitoring Datasonde unit that serves as the standard fixed station water quality monitoring equipment for all similar operations conducted by the SECN. The following parameters were measured at 30 minute intervals during the time period that has been specified: Water Temperature, Specific Conductivity, Salinity, Dissolved Oxygen (DO), DO Concentration, Shallow Depth, pH Level, and Turbidity. Any anomalies noted regarding these parameters have also been noted in separate fields. Please note that these measurements have been certified by network personnel.','public','2026-03-26T05:34:26.764643','2026-03-26T05:34:26.764648','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','7d643f20-7132-4013-8986-e2b454369b94','DOI NPS DCAT-US','597a96cb4a34ef4f48f8a8692aec415fb349dfae2c813031cd6c79448147df5c','1.1','2026-03-26T05:34:26.764643','2026-03-26T05:34:26.764648','Vector Dataset','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('3d2003f3-7f00-4816-858d-c2ea648db21d','Trespassers (not at Highway-Rail Crossings), including Suicides (2.07)','This is a report for trespasser and suicide data, not at highway-rail crossings.','public','2026-03-26T12:45:41.994672','2026-03-26T12:45:41.994676','Federal Railroad Administration','FRA Safety Data Team','021:27','49f90cb0-01be-43ee-83de-78bcb757144f','DOT Socrata Data.json','b1bfdf1796f9949507916ce64fd2294f55228c3b7f4d41c339b91d702f978496','1.1','2026-03-26T12:45:41.994672','2026-03-26T12:45:41.994676','Railroads','021:037',0,'dot-gov'),('3d217069-a6c2-4b32-becc-0223e8f19e7c','Laborshed - Laborshed Area','Laborshed dataset containing information about the geographical reach of the node city (main city within the laborshed area), for every laborshed area.','public','2026-03-28T21:59:18.027452','2026-03-28T21:59:18.027457','data.iowa.gov','svqueen',NULL,'081ccc98-ab3e-4e22-af2c-182ea0cdebbc','Iowa metadata','f0f83b7bf042497a29693ad3e329a2ab6fea82a84d7164ebb2744e1fbac54e14','1.1','2026-03-28T21:59:18.027452','2026-03-28T21:59:18.027457','Economic Statistics',NULL,0,'state-of-iowa'),('3d3a7b63-1157-40ac-9e84-e42670b6ff09','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSIWAC 4 EXT1-MTP026 RDR-INF-REFL V1.0','This CODMAC level 4 data set contains solar stray-light corrected, in-field stray-light corrected,  radiometric calibrated and geometric distortion corrected  (resampled) image data in reflectance units (normalized  and thus without unit),  acquired by the OSIRIS Wide Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft  during the ROSETTA EXTENSION 1 mission phase, covering the period  from 2016-02-09T23:25:00.000 to 2016-03-08T23:24:59.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V1.0 is the first version of this dataset: Lien corrected dataset after September 2019 PSA/PDS external peer review.','public','2026-03-13T16:41:34.690629','2026-03-13T16:41:34.690648','Small Bodies','Tess Jaffe','026:00','c5de6df1-b0ca-4f95-8938-7b0d1e61485a','NASA Data.json','53cd90ab610172b0137c081129ce73cfca1757b31f58ca328e8008d63b273b86','1.1','2026-03-13T16:41:34.690629','2026-03-13T16:41:34.690648','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('3d3e923e-9179-4f49-8cd5-3500fddce6f6','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSIWAC 4 EXT1-MTP026 RDR-STR-REFL V1.0','This CODMAC level 4 data set contains solar stray light corrected, radiometric calibrated and geometric distortion corrected (resampled) image data in in reflectance units (normalized and thus without unit), acquired by the OSIRIS Wide Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft during the ROSETTA EXTENSION 1 mission phase, covering the period from 2016-02-09T23:25:00.000 to 2016-03-08T23:24:59.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V1.0 is the first version of this dataset: Lien corrected dataset after October 2018 PSA/PDS external peer review.','public','2026-03-13T17:48:39.769145','2026-03-13T17:48:39.769151','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','afad6208-b6ff-44e2-b793-3daae4d97897','NASA Data.json','c5bc1d9c363da2d59c7eadfe4e0905a5834edfe766136762eaf0dda3c134e51d','1.1','2026-03-13T17:48:39.769145','2026-03-13T17:48:39.769151','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('3d410c31-16b7-4c47-b810-2b716b2dfdf2','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 2 0700 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 2 phase 2015-03-11 to 2015-06-30. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-04-09T21:29:55.000 to 2015-04-10T06:04:07.500.','public','2026-03-13T20:02:19.613905','2026-03-13T20:02:19.613910','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','47845e2b-b700-44a3-9997-b890d1d345ac','NASA Data.json','5a307d10374967c65c036f2bcb7623463f72ea80d6832408ab8b7974d96a1fef','1.1','2026-03-13T20:02:19.613905','2026-03-13T20:02:19.613910','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('3d634d74-80e9-4054-a91b-c402b17e95b9','FAST Eddy Sys 2  Transect 93, 75kHz kHz VMADCP','Program of vessel mount ADCP measurements comprising a combination of 75kHz and 150kHz ADCP data collected in the vicinity of the Loop Current and drilling blocks between 2009 and 2020.','public','2026-03-26T19:15:29.718561','2026-03-26T19:15:29.718567',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2273c678-5c18-49d5-89ef-fa9eae416cff','ioos',NULL,NULL,'2026-03-26T19:15:29.718561','2026-03-26T19:15:29.718567',NULL,NULL,NULL,'noaa-gov'),('3d82a8a8-7dca-4548-bf65-af43cc0fa467','DEEP IMPACT 9P/TEMPEL ENCOUNTER - RAW HRIV DATA V1.0','This data set contains raw 9P/Tempel 1 and science calibration images acquired by the Deep Impact High Resolution Instrument Visible CCD during the 9P encounter phase of the mission.','public','2026-03-13T18:56:58.439929','2026-03-13T18:56:58.439938','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','21876871-4895-478d-bdc2-5bbb5fdd76b6','NASA Data.json','cdf775cf33eb79575e359d7bb30b933f65c97da58688dfc7630d38959121dc39','1.1','2026-03-13T18:56:58.439929','2026-03-13T18:56:58.439938','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('3d966eea-bb0d-4ef5-aead-7162e1c57c93','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P VIRTIS 2 PRELANDING MTP007 V1.0','This release contains the digital numbers (DN) contained in the telemetry (TM) packages of the VIRTIS instrument on board of the spacecraft Rosetta. This volume contains data at the vicinity of comet 67P, from the PRELANDING MTP007 phase, which occurred from 2014-09-02 to 2014-09-23','public','2026-03-13T17:43:21.565144','2026-03-13T17:43:21.565150','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','f1487db9-1c42-4beb-addf-5612ce572425','NASA Data.json','f710de518df2b76c1f6a8887c749a3a3d02ae236892aae08cad3d43dc18a9137','1.1','2026-03-13T17:43:21.565144','2026-03-13T17:43:21.565150','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('3d976baf-645c-4326-9bf6-a44abd2803d4','Continuous Fixed Station Water Quality Measurements in Canaveral National Seashore, December 2007 (Certified)','This dataset represents continuous water quality measurements that were taken at a fixed point in Canaveral National Seashore during the month of December, 2007 as a part of the Fixed Station Water Quality Monitoring protocol that was developed by the Southeast Coast I&M Network (SECN). The measurements were taken by a YSI 6600 ESD Multi-Parameter Long Term Water Quality Monitoring Datasonde unit that serves as the standard fixed station water quality monitoring equipment for all similar operations conducted by the SECN. The following parameters were measured at 30 minute intervals during the time period that has been specified: Water Temperature, Specific Conductivity, Salinity, Dissolved Oxygen (DO), DO Concentration, Shallow Depth, pH Level, and Turbidity. Any anomalies noted regarding these parameters have also been noted in separate fields. Please note that these measurements have been certified by network personnel.','public','2026-03-26T05:31:43.313234','2026-03-26T05:31:43.313239','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','7d77e059-a3ee-4e4b-b0c6-5a69e7c4faa9','DOI NPS DCAT-US','2cd4e8064fe5493c0ef4989d6e158aaef554c466a8da67089d36d7ee772863f5','1.1','2026-03-26T05:31:43.313234','2026-03-26T05:31:43.313239','Vector Dataset','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('3dde2802-b43e-4f9e-ae2a-a3eee8e41799','MARS EXPRESS SUN MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 7 4052 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2019-01-01 to 2020-12-31. It is a Solar Conjunction measurement and covers the time 2019-09-07T00:56:52.000 to 2019-09-07T04:05:38.500.','public','2026-03-13T17:21:39.823437','2026-03-13T17:21:39.823444','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','d3871b4f-01a7-45e2-b36f-e747e329443c','NASA Data.json','3a60f907e9afded9a30b9fdb540aa3e22fb599ff8e1e72a5569ec67ee6e86ca8','1.1','2026-03-13T17:21:39.823437','2026-03-13T17:21:39.823444','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('3e32892e-fba7-4a88-bb54-f3ece89ec017','Loop Current Observations in the Eastern Gulf of Mexico - PIES Data','Phsyical Oceanographic Circulation Study','public','2026-03-26T19:17:36.717113','2026-03-26T19:17:36.717119',NULL,NULL,NULL,'950cc7f5-0242-4ebc-849b-a31270768cd7','ioos',NULL,NULL,'2026-03-26T19:17:36.717113','2026-03-26T19:17:36.717119',NULL,NULL,NULL,'noaa-gov'),('3e346e36-fd95-4592-bf2f-f7e1aab6a817','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 2 0733 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 2 phase 2015-03-11 to 2015-06-30. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-04-26T23:42:05.000 to 2015-04-27T03:17:06.500.','public','2026-03-13T17:54:56.759892','2026-03-13T17:54:56.759896','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','94b18e92-d32c-48ab-8314-87a380fd1b5c','NASA Data.json','d0afd7bcdd8f345a20566e4894ff90d20cd70a04fefdea7bcb891002e51d707a','1.1','2026-03-13T17:54:56.759892','2026-03-13T17:54:56.759896','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('3e431550-bf11-468d-876c-c25e03277faa','MARS EXPRESS MARS MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 8 4265 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2021-01-01 to 2022-12-31. It is a Occultation measurement and covers the time 2022-05-23T07:58:02.000 to 2022-05-23T08:55:33.000.','public','2026-03-13T19:52:26.685527','2026-03-13T19:52:26.685534','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','eec967ac-d6d3-43ec-ae33-210756218a2e','NASA Data.json','cf8c9f05dc1fefba10747ab1bd474a594e3a017502eb267d209bd634dea01225','1.1','2026-03-13T19:52:26.685527','2026-03-13T19:52:26.685534','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('3e43935b-720b-423a-b01d-b8e14e3fdb6e','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P MIRO 4 EXT2 V2.0','This data set contains Spectroscopic and Continuum level 4 data, in the form of table files, taken during the ROSETTA EXTENSION 2 phase of the Rosetta mission to comet 67P/CHURYUMOV-GERASIMENKO by the MIRO instrument. The major updates with this version (V2.0) are the addition of a Level 4 continuum data product and the elimination of separate geometry files for the spectroscopic data.','public','2026-03-13T19:49:39.663462','2026-03-13T19:49:39.663469','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','3c611625-9273-4462-8ab4-c9e72c5a48bd','NASA Data.json','1611c6054f1115cb12b44d6b766980ec6a66eee8042e1804a1442fff76190dad','1.1','2026-03-13T19:49:39.663462','2026-03-13T19:49:39.663469','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('3e46c7e0-e77e-4fde-b0e7-90e0a5df061b','CASSINI RSS RAW DATA SET - SROC4B V1.0','The Cassini Radio Science Saturn and Ring Occultation Experiment (SROC4B) Raw Data Archive is a time-ordered collection of radio science raw data acquired on June 28, 2007, during the Tour subphase of the Cassini mission.','public','2026-03-13T19:28:45.027427','2026-03-13T19:28:45.027434','Planetary Atmospheres','Planetary Data System','026:00','dde44fa5-24ac-4ce0-b0d4-24981c78e6e7','NASA Data.json','45d550a71a1e41c850450b8c116080139790d998d261d9db1100c332705d935e','1.1','2026-03-13T19:28:45.027427','2026-03-13T19:28:45.027434','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('3e677bbe-3b31-4175-b517-bba3241fe935','DID(IT) - El Rescate, Index of Acccountability: Government and Rebel Forces Data','The El Rescate database is static and contains government and rebel forces information as it related to human rights violations.','non-public','2026-03-22T11:52:53.354521','2026-03-22T11:52:53.354525','Unspecified','Open Data (MGMT)','024:030','0cfe056e-fcc5-4e46-a813-4611dc1c0bf0','DHS datajson source','2335c7255586571d3a9ce3cfb91c32cc0be4e343dc870c8c2a3eb7ff18d2871c','1.1','2026-03-22T11:52:53.354521','2026-03-22T11:52:53.354525',NULL,'024:000',0,'dhs-gov'),('3e9efde7-414b-4b51-b85f-384ac2af03d9','Coastal Mapping Program of  Port of Everett, WA, WA2503-CS-N','These data provide an accurate high-resolution shoreline compiled from imagery of  Port of Everett, WA .  This vector shoreline data is based on an office interpretation of imagery that may be suitable as a geographic information system (GIS) data layer. This metadata describes information for both the line and point shapefiles. The NGS attribution scheme \'Coastal Cartographic Object Attribute Source Table (C-COAST)\' was developed to conform the attribution of various sources of shoreline data into one attribution catalog. C-COAST is not a recognized standard, but was influenced by the International Hydrographic Organization\'s S-57 Object-Attribute standard so the data would be more accurately translated into S-57.  This resource is a member of  https://inport.nmfs.noaa.gov/inport/item/39808','public','2026-03-26T20:18:29.920001','2026-03-26T20:18:29.920013',NULL,NULL,NULL,'b728272d-bec1-43c0-9ba4-40c417d67f0f','NOS NGS',NULL,NULL,'2026-03-26T20:18:29.920001','2026-03-26T20:18:29.920013',NULL,NULL,NULL,'noaa-gov'),('3eb1142f-83c3-46e4-b000-364098cac118','Oregon Balance Billing Protection - Ground Ambulance Service Organization Established Local Rates','A catalog of established local rates submitted by ground ambulance service organizations to the Oregon Division of Financial Regulation, per HB 3243.\n\nEstablished local rates are reported to DCBS by ground ambulance services organizations for transparency purposes. For billing purposes, the insurer and ground ambulance services organization will determine the payment amount based on the allowed amount at the time and place of the service.','public','2026-03-22T03:21:04.695309','2026-03-22T03:21:04.695314','data.oregon.gov','DCBS Research Unit',NULL,'41c685ea-f202-4ed8-b0f9-32121a25c1a6','oregon json','b0e8f7b59dbf11732d5431c0b8ea16b74496817c93e61704403aa561bde06509','1.1','2026-03-22T03:21:04.695309','2026-03-22T03:21:04.695314','business',NULL,0,'state-of-oregon'),('3ee6a0af-a0b5-4b71-9106-a576e16cd33a','\"Deepwater CTD - n4l06s13.ctd.nc - 29.13N, -86.79W - 1998-11-20\"','The Minerals Management Service (MMS) of the U. S. Department of the Interior funded the Deepwater Physical Oceanography Reanalysis and Synthesis of Historical Data Study in the Gulf of Mexico. MMS awarded the contract to the Texas A&M Research Foundation in July 1998. The basic study area is bounded by the shelf edge and the 25DGN latitude, which is the southern boundary; it extends from sea surface to sea floor. MMS has four objectives for the study. First is to create an inventory of physical oceanographic data and compile it into a single database on a CD-ROM. Second is to conduct analyses and interpretations of the physical oceanographic data to identify physical processes and phenomena. Third is to produce a climatology of the processes from available data and analyses and to prioritize the processes in terms of importance to improved understanding, simulation, and prediction of deepwater circulation. Fourth is to provide criteria and constraints useful in design of future field observations and numerical modeling efforts. Study results will provide MMS with information needed to direct its resources more efficiently and effectively in the review and assessment of potential environmental impacts of offshore oil and gas operations in the deepwater Gulf of Mexico.','public','2026-03-26T19:16:23.908382','2026-03-26T19:16:23.908387',NULL,NULL,NULL,'83f83965-0e0b-4728-a45d-ce168c5afc1d','ioos',NULL,NULL,'2026-03-26T19:16:23.908382','2026-03-26T19:16:23.908387',NULL,NULL,NULL,'noaa-gov'),('3f00686f-2ca8-43ba-b52a-7e4a6f716afc','BLM ID Right Of Way Line','These are Rights-of-Ways (ROW) on Idaho BLM land (and some other Federal agency land) as shown on Bureau of Land Management (BLM) Master Title Plats (MTP). Every GIS ROW feature has a \"CASEFILE\" value, also known as the serial number of the ROW. The ROW data that was digitized is what was present on the MTP at the time of the digitizing done for that township. The project was performed over several years. Therefore, the \"early\" townships digitized are more out of date regarding ROWs compared to the ones more recently digitized. Unfortunately, there is no attribute that indicates the digitizing sequence. Any updates to this ROW feature class should be sent to the BLM Idaho State Office GIS staff for incorporation into the statewide GIS ROW feature classes for improvement over time. For more information contact us at blm_id_stateoffice@blm.gov.','public','2026-03-26T12:41:43.712406','2026-03-26T12:41:43.712410','Bureau of Land Management','Bureau of Land Management, blm_id_stateoffice','010:04','5e28ebf5-b0a3-48da-a278-0a8331036b78','DOI BLM DCAT-US','971a4850d32766d1f345c76147be87e3701e2cf6dad304a1486439e29e6eefdb','1.1','2026-03-26T12:41:43.712406','2026-03-26T12:41:43.712410','geospatial','010:000',0,'doi-gov'),('3f1544f9-0b7c-4ea2-b01b-0adaafc1a86b','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 3 0974 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 3 phase 2015-07-01 to 2015-10-21. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-08-20T15:27:50.000 to 2015-08-20T17:26:42.000.','public','2026-03-13T19:04:52.412510','2026-03-13T19:04:52.412515','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','6e95ca32-a8a1-4198-a9c4-851e87d8ba19','NASA Data.json','12eda4f131b189ed42f92d80c428f4c94e8d106e0c924e3db543906539f8fe82','1.1','2026-03-13T19:04:52.412510','2026-03-13T19:04:52.412515','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('3f23af00-f673-4591-bbb9-a6fb60877179','MARS EXPRESS MARS MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 5 3860 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2015-01-01 to 2016-12-31. It is a Occultation measurement and covers the time 2016-11-17T23:32:12.000 to 2016-11-17T23:54:21.949.','public','2026-03-13T18:36:44.123166','2026-03-13T18:36:44.123172','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','4929cce9-025e-4abc-ac86-2bf42abf112f','NASA Data.json','c40fd848f6feba9dd48e4adcd6478f28e49e459c0aac978552c95bbc2c5eb878','1.1','2026-03-13T18:36:44.123166','2026-03-13T18:36:44.123172','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('3f36a61e-80d4-4e0b-82f3-d275c3fd03b2','ARECIBO MOON RADIO TELESC RESAMPLED 70 CM RADAR MOSAIC V1.0','High resolution radar map compiled from measurements made between 1981 and 1984 with the 70 cm wavelength radar at Arecibo Observatory. The data have resolutions ranging from 2 to 5 kilometers. The pixel spacing is 0.1 degrees in latitude and longitude. The point at line 1000 and sample 1000 corresponds to 0 degrees latitude and 0 degrees longitude. The pixel values are scaled to represent 20 * log10 (backscattered power). Observed power has been corrected for antenna beam, scattering area and scattering law. Observed power of 1000, which is the lunar average, thus has a value of 60 in the data set. Radar was transmitted in left-hand circular polarization, and both right-hand circular polarization (i.e. polarized) and left-hand circular polarization (i.e. depolarized) echoes were received.','public','2026-03-13T16:58:54.270112','2026-03-13T16:58:54.270117','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','4061f6a1-1795-48bf-a444-e5c11eef1c4e','NASA Data.json','b81af289dbe3c4dd4099238d4ca17eecff41158be4a14d16563fd1febbae6760','1.1','2026-03-13T16:58:54.270112','2026-03-13T16:58:54.270117','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('3f37bd5a-a741-4d48-bbc8-c38b2279c0fa','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSINAC 4 EXT2-MTP028 RDR V1.0','This CODMAC level 4 data set contains radiometric calibrated and geometric distortion corrected (resampled) image data in W/m^2/sr/nm acquired by the OSIRIS Narrow Angle Camera during the ROSETTA EXTENSION 2 phase of the Rosetta mission, covering the period from 2016-04-05T23:25:00.000 to 2016-05-03T23:25:00.000.','public','2026-03-13T19:01:51.522683','2026-03-13T19:01:51.522692','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','4191b135-78d8-4dba-a55c-838fcfb29ae8','NASA Data.json','ddc089ee688d5e87dbdb6a36aa5fd52fe179ce8ec7b26882bcd8da4cbd5216d8','1.1','2026-03-13T19:01:51.522683','2026-03-13T19:01:51.522692','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('3f805beb-3199-4498-a935-19d13b48779f','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSINAC 5 ESC1-MTP012 DDR-GEO V1.0','This CODMAC level 5 data set contains derived data products that include pixel-precise georeferencing information, acquired by the OSIRIS Narrow Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft during the COMET ESCORT 1 mission phase, covering the period from 2015-01-13T23:25:00.000 to 2015-02-10T23:24:59.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V1.0 is the first version of this dataset: Lien corrected dataset after October 2018 PSA/PDS external peer review.','public','2026-03-13T19:11:12.717634','2026-03-13T19:11:12.717640','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','fc9f11b2-fc81-476e-9f40-6b98d404bebf','NASA Data.json','c36b6dc211ad5dac04e1cf96c7f638fbeb18aceeeadc7a08f33c986082727e3b','1.1','2026-03-13T19:11:12.717634','2026-03-13T19:11:12.717640','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('3f8a05c8-a5b0-4b77-ab89-7912e65319e7','KBO AND CENTAUR ABSOLUTE MAGNITUDES V1.0','This data set contains absolute visual magnitudes of 90 Kuiper belt objects and Centaurs from Romanishin and Tegler (2005). The absolute magnitudes are derived from V magnitudes observed by Romanishin and Tegler and their collaborators, with geometry from the JPL Horizons data base. As a convenience, R-band absolute magnitudes derived from the V absolute magnitudes and published V-R colors are also provided.','public','2026-03-13T18:40:33.832995','2026-03-13T18:40:33.833000','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','f2023e5d-123e-4756-8676-b41d3f2af2fb','NASA Data.json','f9e72f199e2b4f074b149896516e561191d61d825fde84223a8cc26aaab5f7d5','1.1','2026-03-13T18:40:33.832995','2026-03-13T18:40:33.833000','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('3fa55375-9c0a-4df6-b2c7-f920afc39a23','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 PRELANDING 0329 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the PRELANDING phase 2014-01-21 to 2014-11-18. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2014-10-01T16:12:05.000 to 2014-10-02T00:10:09.000.','public','2026-03-13T16:37:45.955676','2026-03-13T16:37:45.955682','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','f1755738-2343-4310-9212-154c9fa26e4c','NASA Data.json','73b9590fe405b3695326319dd3dd113017f14b0a4aa468525644855116dec267','1.1','2026-03-13T16:37:45.955676','2026-03-13T16:37:45.955682','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('3fbb28ef-492c-4741-a347-6a611e18e5d2','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSIWAC 4 PRL-MTP008 RDR V1.0','This CODMAC level 4 data set contains radiometric calibrated and geometric distortion corrected (resampled) image data in W/m^2/sr/nm acquired by the OSIRIS Wide Angle Camera during the PRELANDING phase of the Rosetta mission, covering the period from 2014-09-23T10:00:00.000 to 2014-10-24T09:59:59.000.','public','2026-03-13T19:09:30.427727','2026-03-13T19:09:30.427733','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','0d1bdf58-b9b4-4084-8270-97639dbfd377','NASA Data.json','252612fd74682adcc15084d66d154214d3d4ef0ece59170e721895fd8491aa2d','1.1','2026-03-13T19:09:30.427727','2026-03-13T19:09:30.427733','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('3fddafea-22eb-45f4-951e-68c658844920','IHW COMET PPMAG CALIBRATED REDUCED DATA RECORD GZ V1.0','In preparation for the concerted international study of Comet Halley, the IHW conducted a trial run with observations of Comet Crommelin, largely during February and March of 1984.','public','2026-03-13T16:38:47.041321','2026-03-13T16:38:47.041327','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','e6389607-c391-452a-b741-43a8450340fe','NASA Data.json','92a6fe03d36bc40d1db4b4a0a8ea3bd1a7724e475995316d94564bef9d2deee6','1.1','2026-03-13T16:38:47.041321','2026-03-13T16:38:47.041327','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('400965b7-8d94-4944-b150-2a70ac1e404b','IMAGING OF JUPITER ASSOCIATED WITH SL9 IMPACT FLASHES','A global imaging campaign (GIC) was organized at sites during the impact of comet Shoemaker-levy 9 with Jupiter. These five sites were Queensland in Australia, the Cerro Tololo Interamerican Observatory, Lick Observatory, Mauna Kea Observatory and Reunion Island. All sites used a combination of high speed optical CCD systems with similar broad and narrow band filters.','public','2026-03-13T17:58:26.136113','2026-03-13T17:58:26.136121','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','728dc5c5-a6fa-42db-bba2-9429e36dee63','NASA Data.json','a0be2a27de1550cae451e1551971d2f5fd3406b350e528956b64c759ba238c75','1.1','2026-03-13T17:58:26.136113','2026-03-13T17:58:26.136121','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('400da7d7-f9d6-47ef-85c2-39c8832b9567','ROSETTA-ORBITER CHECK RPCMAG 2 CR4B CALIBRATED V9.0','This dataset contains RESAMPLED DATA (CODMAC LEVEL 4) of the Cruise 4-2phase, called CRUISE PHASE CR4B, of the ROSETTA orbiter magnetometer RPCMAG.Included are data from the Passive Checkout PC9 from January 31, 2009 untilFebruary 1, 2009.The current version of the dataset is V9.0.The difference to the datasets of earlier versions is mainly a significantlyimproved sensor temperature model, more detailed documentation about magneticdisturbance sources, more data handling information for the user andalso an improved quality flagging system.','public','2026-03-13T16:59:39.083789','2026-03-13T16:59:39.083794','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','91df89f8-6fd7-4135-b920-a5955f544314','NASA Data.json','b72fcb87397044959b59b3b79ba4a560a031923f981c49a1d5033ed89d02b178','1.1','2026-03-13T16:59:39.083789','2026-03-13T16:59:39.083794','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('4028cb1a-b316-4298-ab80-6c53afeaf1a7','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 2 0768 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 2 phase 2015-03-11 to 2015-06-30. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-05-11T22:03:05.000 to 2015-05-12T07:07:13.000.','public','2026-03-13T19:15:06.824492','2026-03-13T19:15:06.824509','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','b95b7fa3-0d55-4191-9048-a45e8c3558a7','NASA Data.json','1eec63e81aba0d248bf24d8162607714bb3096b7fbbd10a79614a008cad62243','1.1','2026-03-13T19:15:06.824492','2026-03-13T19:15:06.824509','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('407e88e8-3701-420c-8920-85dc2e598631','DID(IT) - Case and Activity Management for International Operations System','CAMINO allows USCIS International Operations personnel to process applications and petitions, adoptions, military naturalizations, issue Boarding Letters, and track current case dispositions at the overseas offices and domestic branches of HQ IO.','non-public','2026-03-22T11:51:54.877780','2026-03-22T11:51:54.877785','Unspecified','Open Data (MGMT)','024:030','c1874b6b-3c5e-478d-a185-668ac9a9edad','DHS datajson source','46d59840d177d356a878d40c86f96c273fdba398aab55ac43bcb1874564b93da','1.1','2026-03-22T11:51:54.877780','2026-03-22T11:51:54.877785',NULL,'024:000',0,'dhs-gov'),('40a2a6bf-9d37-45c6-8276-e344547ef454','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 2 0645 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 2 phase 2015-03-11 to 2015-06-30. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-03-14T23:48:05.000 to 2015-03-15T09:16:07.500.','public','2026-03-13T19:26:42.826592','2026-03-13T19:26:42.826599','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','1063ef2c-a90c-4711-91a8-0f1ea275ff4b','NASA Data.json','080de38ba1a6e81ee8d0ba7864d3cdd6d6c467d558f2ccca05084e21b4eea0c0','1.1','2026-03-13T19:26:42.826592','2026-03-13T19:26:42.826599','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('40d0de21-cf92-4ef6-a6c9-ea09a79b1383','PHOTOMETRY OF IO AND EUROPA DURING SL9 IMPACT FLASHES','This data set contains digitized photometry of the reflections off Io and Europa of the impact fireballs produced as the D, E, K, and N fragments of comet D/Shoemaker-Levy 9 hit Jupiter\'s atmosphere.','public','2026-03-13T17:05:05.199675','2026-03-13T17:05:05.199681','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','7c9e4eab-1e7a-4246-9417-ed2ab90c1d3c','NASA Data.json','52df9dccc66f394b684e35d5dc1c45926203b4be9c916bdf2bbe15fe302070de','1.1','2026-03-13T17:05:05.199675','2026-03-13T17:05:05.199681','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('40dda906-c965-4441-ba0b-ab0f2586aee2','MARS EXPRESS MARS MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 7 4011 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2019-01-01 to 2020-12-31. It is a Occultation measurement and covers the time 2019-05-22T05:26:20.000 to 2019-05-22T05:48:28.649.','public','2026-03-13T19:02:23.444980','2026-03-13T19:02:23.444986','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','6e1cb7e2-84d0-4099-9c5f-06406b4036d6','NASA Data.json','764a89713b2d7f0b14c9b8379c468ae00cd087c67e86d24831752872cb80e289','1.1','2026-03-13T19:02:23.444980','2026-03-13T19:02:23.444986','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('40e37d18-783e-4257-9b7f-38bfb9b0bd0d','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 ROSETTA EXTENSION 1 1399 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the ROSETTA EXTENSION 1 phase 2016-01-01 to 2016-04-05. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2016-02-04T23:33:05.000 to 2016-02-05T08:44:20.000.','public','2026-03-13T18:44:58.792158','2026-03-13T18:44:58.792164','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','694901db-52d2-4a36-bda6-07009ff13c64','NASA Data.json','8f5b2fa503330eda4a705c447f3ad9a33232917489aa5b7dc3290fd9cf7db6a5','1.1','2026-03-13T18:44:58.792158','2026-03-13T18:44:58.792164','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('41445d54-5477-474f-a62c-d432caccc600','Continuous Fixed Station Water Quality Measurements in Timucuan Ecological and Historic Preserve, March 2008 (Certified)','This dataset represents continuous water quality measurements that were taken at a fixed point in Timucuan Ecological and Historic Preserve during the month of March, 2008 as a part of the Fixed Station Water Quality Monitoring protocol that was developed by the Southeast Coast I&M Network (SECN). The measurements were taken by a YSI 6600 ESD Multi-Parameter Long Term Water Quality Monitoring Datasonde unit that serves as the standard fixed station water quality monitoring equipment for all similar operations conducted by the SECN. The following parameters were measured at 30 minute intervals during the time period that has been specified: Water Temperature, Specific Conductivity, Salinity, Dissolved Oxygen (DO), DO Concentration, Shallow Depth, pH Level, and Turbidity. Any anomalies noted regarding these parameters have also been noted in separate fields. Please note that these measurements have been certified by network personnel.','public','2026-03-26T05:33:16.012769','2026-03-26T05:33:16.012774','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','94e5638d-5fe1-45ff-9a26-1280754ce740','DOI NPS DCAT-US','0f9cd01c717cb543c65f416330d70ebe3dcd5ff1e72725e63070479f1b92c6a0','1.1','2026-03-26T05:33:16.012769','2026-03-26T05:33:16.012774','Vector Dataset','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('4147dfc9-6fa2-4e6c-a0bd-abcebac7c26c','LCROSS SUN 2ND NEAR IR SPECTROMETER 2 RAW V1.0','Raw, uncalibrated spectra from the Near Infrared Spectrometer 2 (NSP2) aboard the Lunar Crater Observation and Sensing Satellite (LCROSS).','public','2026-03-13T17:15:05.163339','2026-03-13T17:15:05.163347','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','f1153d63-2df9-4f51-9e6a-baaa17f0e699','NASA Data.json','6e0ab1512f90bec667518b2a173bdd3ac8bd47a497428a062211fd8f37eedfa9','1.1','2026-03-13T17:15:05.163339','2026-03-13T17:15:05.163347','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('41488556-3dd5-4318-96b1-bc0afbfdb852','Continuous Fixed Station Water Quality Measurements in Canaveral National Seashore, April 2007 (Certified)','This dataset represents continuous water quality measurements that were taken at a fixed point in Canaveral National Seashore during the month of April, 2007 as a part of the Fixed Station Water Quality Monitoring protocol that was developed by the Southeast Coast I&M Network (SECN). The measurements were taken by a YSI 6600 ESD Multi-Parameter Long Term Water Quality Monitoring Datasonde unit that serves as the standard fixed station water quality monitoring equipment for all similar operations conducted by the SECN. The following parameters were measured at 30 minute intervals during the time period that has been specified: Water Temperature, Specific Conductivity, Salinity, Dissolved Oxygen (DO), DO Concentration, Shallow Depth, pH Level, and Turbidity. Any anomalies noted regarding these parameters have also been noted in separate fields. Please note that these measurements have been certified by network personnel.','public','2026-03-26T05:31:11.177486','2026-03-26T05:31:11.177491','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','3a6a3fc5-2b2c-4246-8101-211aa6fc6f95','DOI NPS DCAT-US','93d1ebec9154adf563d45f648ea0fda0dd5bca53a5bbc2e954e958a6b967d555','1.1','2026-03-26T05:31:11.177486','2026-03-26T05:31:11.177491','Vector Dataset','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('4154439e-4713-473f-94b0-44814c99a2cf','GO JUPITER PWS EDITED EDR 80KHZ WAVEFORM RECEIVER V1.0','This data set includes wideband waveform measurements from the    Galileo plasma wave receiver obtained during Jupiter orbital    operations. These data were obtained during selected observation    periods near perijove, satellite encounters and other select times.    These measurements are electric waveforms obtained by rapidly    sampling the potential at the input to the receiver from the    electric dipole antenna.  The sample rates are 201,600/s, 25,200/s,    or 3,150/s taken through bandpass filters of 80, 10, or 1 kHz,    respectively.','public','2026-03-13T18:32:08.847587','2026-03-13T18:32:08.847592','planetary plasma interactions','Planetary Data System','026:00','b865fe01-b556-4667-9027-1f9732cada08','NASA Data.json','3da4cb1240d7bd5ce463f828c762e19e0a0cec5d908be520751c794be0a28b31','1.1','2026-03-13T18:32:08.847587','2026-03-13T18:32:08.847592','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('417207ba-b14e-4dce-9a2b-3e696aba7a7d','Hydrographic and Impairment Statistics Database: NPS-WSR Alatna Wild and Scenic River','Hydrographic and Impairment Statistics (HIS) is a National Park Service (NPS) Water Resources Division (WRD) project established to track certain goals created in response to the Government Performance and Results Act of 1993 (GPRA). One water resources management goal established by the Department of the Interior under GRPA requires NPS to track the percent of its managed surface waters that are meeting Clean Water Act (CWA) water quality standards. This goal requires an accurate inventory that spatially quantifies the surface water hydrography that each bureau manages and a procedure to determine and track which waterbodies are or are not meeting water quality standards as outlined by Section 303(d) of the CWA. This project helps meet this DOI GRPA goal by inventorying and monitoring in a geographic information system for the NPS: (1) CWA 303(d) quality impaired waters and causes; and (2) hydrographic statistics based on the United States Geological Survey (USGS) National Hydrography Dataset (NHD). Hydrographic and 303(d) impairment statistics were evaluated based on a combination of 1:24,000 (NHD) and finer scale data (frequently provided by state GIS layers).','public','2026-03-29T06:07:01.869912','2026-03-29T06:07:01.869920','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','bb5f4e04-b60a-407f-8bc6-652649542883','DOI NPS DCAT-US','2922221e5e096201123583520e21421a528e07b2e33c454f93192ee0e50a6072','1.1','2026-03-29T06:07:01.869912','2026-03-29T06:07:01.869920','geospatial','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('41738534-2b3b-4302-bc91-fb278b018c6c','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P VIRTIS 2 ESCORT 4 MTP023 V1.0','This release contains the digital numbers (DN) contained in the telemetry (TM) packages of the VIRTIS instrument on board of the spacecraft Rosetta. This volume contains data at the vicinity of comet 67P, from the ESCORT 4 MTP023 phase, which occurred from 2015-11-18 to 2015-12-16','public','2026-03-13T16:57:45.827791','2026-03-13T16:57:45.827796','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','9e1a4ba5-3fc2-4454-a742-5e4a3125ae82','NASA Data.json','f59ef2849e2b30d215e324eca29840e18cf82e3afb3c5869e5a07930ea57e3f6','1.1','2026-03-13T16:57:45.827791','2026-03-13T16:57:45.827796','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('418ca9de-e322-4f37-9082-ade6a228c991','MARS EXPRESS MARS MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 3 3336 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2010-01-01 to 2012-12-31. It is a Global Gravity measurement and covers the time 2012-07-05T00:13:12 to 2012-07-05T02:18:09.000.','public','2026-03-13T19:09:13.692329','2026-03-13T19:09:13.692336','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','efe3b9d9-62a6-40b4-a333-96418f392792','NASA Data.json','18ff3028e16747182d014f8ab840e686976fdc655bfe8d484f19285279b74981','1.1','2026-03-13T19:09:13.692329','2026-03-13T19:09:13.692336','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('41916ec0-a59f-423e-a9dd-7a699c72edf7','BLM ID CADNSDI PLSS Conflicted Areas','The conflicted areas feature class is a depiction of known overlaps or gaps resulting from two or more different surveys of the same area, this may also include an indication of canceled or suspended surveys. For more information contact us at blm_id_stateoffice@blm.gov.','public','2026-03-18T11:10:17.087998','2026-03-18T11:10:17.088004','Bureau of Land Management','Bureau of Land Management, blm_id_infoaccesscenter','010:04','e1bc9fc4-9bde-4daf-aa7a-8b326b62e7a6','DOI BLM DCAT-US','64186e5a577a944ea219cf7b18bceeb1d65c0d4b6ad9a4ceb5512868fe84de86','1.1','2026-03-18T11:10:17.087998','2026-03-18T11:10:17.088004','geospatial','010:000',0,'doi-gov'),('41bc92be-b6dd-4af9-ae2c-b6e94198b9ea','ROSETTA-ORBITER COMET ESCORT 3 OSIWAC 2 EDR MTP020 V1.0','This data set contains images acquired by the OSIRIS Wide Angle Camera during the COMET ESCORT 3 phase of the Rosetta mission at the comet 67P, covering the period from 2015-08-25T23:25:00.000 to 2015-09-22T23:24:59.000.','public','2026-03-13T18:18:56.917280','2026-03-13T18:18:56.917286','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','4357d3d3-1e6c-4678-bcc1-033ed581f06e','NASA Data.json','03fb87164d00f264896302aa65ac8fda7895ab7b5a000875f84f03b209707095','1.1','2026-03-13T18:18:56.917280','2026-03-13T18:18:56.917286','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('41f74148-f55f-46ab-9df3-a445b26f913d','HPMS Statewide Summaries 2018','The Highway Performance Management System (HPMS) Statewide Summaries table contains demographic and system length estimates for all Urban and Rural public roads, functionally classified as minor collector in rural areas or local in any area, summarized by State. In addition, this dataset contains daily vehicle-miles traveled (VMT) estimates for all public roads located in Small Urban areas, functionally classified as minor collector or local.','public','2026-03-28T13:38:28.839933','2026-03-28T13:38:28.839937','Federal Highway Administration','Office of Highway Policy Information','021:15','45b31b90-63d3-44d5-8dd0-b892de30823e','DOT Socrata Data.json','7f71c1f0040918ddb60c475b766a78da77258e2b7de07330608d2bd99c43785e','1.1','2026-03-28T13:38:28.839933','2026-03-28T13:38:28.839937','Roadways and Bridges','021:009',0,'dot-gov'),('41ff9ca9-21a6-433a-b788-499257c26aa8','Coastal Mapping Program of  Port of Grand Haven, MI, MI2406B-CS-N','These data provide an accurate high-resolution shoreline compiled from imagery of  Port of Grand Haven, MI .  This vector shoreline data is based on an office interpretation of imagery that may be suitable as a geographic information system (GIS) data layer. This metadata describes information for both the line and point shapefiles. The NGS attribution scheme \'Coastal Cartographic Object Attribute Source Table (C-COAST)\' was developed to conform the attribution of various sources of shoreline data into one attribution catalog. C-COAST is not a recognized standard, but was influenced by the International Hydrographic Organization\'s S-57 Object-Attribute standard so the data would be more accurately translated into S-57.  This resource is a member of  https://inport.nmfs.noaa.gov/inport/item/39808','public','2026-03-19T20:04:12.206724','2026-03-19T20:04:12.206733',NULL,NULL,NULL,'0bbdfba5-e16d-4844-9539-fde552f86dde','NOS NGS',NULL,NULL,'2026-03-19T20:04:12.206724','2026-03-19T20:04:12.206733',NULL,NULL,NULL,'noaa-gov'),('4215f959-3d2f-4472-b4ea-94996a106ad2','MARS EXPRESS MARS MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 7 4104 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2019-01-01 to 2020-12-31. It is a Occultation measurement and covers the time 2020-08-16T06:47:09.299 to 2020-08-16T07:09:17.250.','public','2026-03-13T19:12:51.894691','2026-03-13T19:12:51.894697','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','560e03c7-dbf4-42e8-ab12-6d26e9f60ecc','NASA Data.json','726c79988bceb71562ba8f0af09cad4db6c3753f589f9bc8dc201da279f90ced','1.1','2026-03-13T19:12:51.894691','2026-03-13T19:12:51.894697','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('425940a8-ac8f-4a54-86a4-2285c4fa4913','EPA Facility Registry Service (FRS): ER_FRP','This dataset contains location and facility identification information from EPA\'s Facility Registry System (FRS) for the subset of facilities that link to Facility Response Plan (FRP) in the Oil database. These facilities are subject to the requirements to prevent and respond to oil spills. FRP facilities are referred to as substantial harm facilities due to the quantities of oil stored and facility characteristics. FRS identifies and geospatially locates facilities, sites or places subject to environmental regulations or of environmental interest. Using vigorous verification and data management procedures, FRS integrates facility data from EPA\'s national program systems, other federal agencies, and State and tribal master facility records and provides EPA with a centrally managed, single source of comprehensive and authoritative information on facilities. This data set contains the subset of FRS integrated facilities that link to Oil FRP facilities once the Oil data has been integrated into the FRS database. Additional information on FRS is available at the EPA website https://www.epa.gov/enviro/facility-registry-service-frs. These data are considered sensitive and are restricted to internal use only. The download file and map service are accessible only on the EPA intranet. EPA Category: Mission Sensitive, NARA Category: Critical Infrastructure.','public','2026-03-27T15:37:51.947718','2026-03-31T16:39:46.532044',NULL,NULL,NULL,'3ab940c9-1c91-44a0-91ab-6f5d0146c9ef','Environmental Dataset Gateway ISO Geospatial Metadata',NULL,NULL,'2026-03-27T15:37:51.947718','2026-03-31T16:39:46.532044',NULL,NULL,NULL,'epa-gov'),('427a7ff9-0d54-4947-827a-c8807d56c85a','Citywide Mobility Survey - Vehicle 2024','The Citywide Mobility Survey (CMS) is NYC DOT\'s annual travel survey to assess the travel behavior, preferences, and attitudes of NYC residents. It is composed of 5 linked data tables.\n\nCitywide Mobility Survey (CMS) Vehicle table contains characteristics of each vehicle in the participant’s household.\n\n<b>Other 2024 Citywide Mobility Survey Datasets:</b>\n<a href=\"https://data.cityofnewyork.us/d/i2im-iqtt\">Citywide Mobility Survey - Person 2024 </a>\n<a href=\"https://data.cityofnewyork.us/d/5mb3-padx\">Citywide Mobility Survey - Household 2024</a>\n<a href=\"https://data.cityofnewyork.us/d/naav-ygga\">Citywide Mobility Survey - Day 2024</a>\n<a href=\"https://data.cityofnewyork.us/d/wgnh-qwsg\">Citywide Mobility Survey - Trip 2024</a>\n\nSee all the <a href=\"https://data.cityofnewyork.us/browse?sortBy=relevance&pageSize=20&Data-Collection_Data-Collection=Citywide+Mobility+Survey\">Citywide Mobility Survey Data</a>, including past surveys.','public','2026-03-29T04:43:34.936058','2026-03-29T04:43:34.936064','data.cityofnewyork.us','NYC OpenData',NULL,'543ff71e-a04a-4e8c-a80d-1033906a47e7','NYC JSON','8018e6f5131e133efc5f965f71cc87e6fb737b1abda4bcfc535dce753968cd19','1.1','2026-03-29T04:43:34.936058','2026-03-29T04:43:34.936064','Transportation',NULL,0,'city-of-new-york'),('42bceba0-7ea9-4162-9e83-acad4c1bf397','Employment Benefit Analysis: Cost of Health Insurance Premiums','The Employment Benefit Analysis was published in 2023. The data reported was collected through an employer survey in the State of Iowa.\n\nThis dataset shows estimated cost employers reported per employee for health insurance premiums. The data can be viewed by area (statewide, county, or LWDA), by industry of the employer, and by employer size.','public','2026-03-28T22:01:31.995944','2026-03-28T22:01:31.995949','data.iowa.gov','Katie Green',NULL,'077734dc-2ef1-48ed-8b38-b08c590e57b9','Iowa metadata','e154e1d95683b90b4cf19bfaec8e70f43ed11edd963fbef138861b736c670b59','1.1','2026-03-28T22:01:31.995944','2026-03-28T22:01:31.995949','Workforce',NULL,0,'state-of-iowa'),('42d68d1a-c47e-4d8d-b060-309e3e0abb55','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSIWAC 4 ESC3-MTP019 RDR-INF-REFL V1.0','This CODMAC level 4 data set contains solar stray-light corrected, in-field stray-light corrected,  radiometric calibrated and geometric distortion corrected  (resampled) image data in reflectance units (normalized  and thus without unit),  acquired by the OSIRIS Wide Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft  during the COMET ESCORT 3 mission phase, covering the period  from 2015-07-28T23:25:00.000 to 2015-08-25T23:24:59.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V1.0 is the first version of this dataset: Lien corrected dataset after September 2019 PSA/PDS external peer review.','public','2026-03-13T17:23:23.157561','2026-03-13T17:23:23.157566','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','adb3136d-ea8e-4d43-a351-065deaebdc7a','NASA Data.json','95dab65e0331cfb68e1d669fca975b915117f066b67c758eb46e21f4a2fe966d','1.1','2026-03-13T17:23:23.157561','2026-03-13T17:23:23.157566','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('42f9d629-de06-4870-89e9-3b5deeb3ca93','ROSETTA-ORBITER/ROSETTA-LANDER 67P CONSERT 4 SDL V1.0','This archive contains REFORMATTED data (CODMAC level 4) that refers to target 67P/CHURYUMOV-GERASIMENKO 1 (1969 R1) from the CONSERT instrument onboard ROSETTA Orbiter and Lander, acquired during the SDL phase. In addition to the scientific signal of interest, it contains all the values applied to the signal for calibration. It also contains documentation which describes the CONSERT experiment. The L4 dataset includes interpolated signals using a specific CONSERT method. It also provide fine propagation travel times of the signal between Philae and Rosetta. The data archived in this data set conform to the Planetary Data System (PDS) Standards, Version 3.6.','public','2026-03-13T19:03:51.742689','2026-03-13T19:03:51.742695','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','dc79e506-447f-45d1-9905-0ab517f06ace','NASA Data.json','fb1507adf9c85e868f48af1a77cfc9605bdee0148bf4c89a6258e9e4028f1ccc','1.1','2026-03-13T19:03:51.742689','2026-03-13T19:03:51.742695','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('43020a92-d543-406d-ba5b-7646837c8f37','NEAR MAG DATA FOR CRUISE3','NEAR MAG RDR volume sets contain a single data set, from one instrument and one mission phase (defined in the phase table in /AAREADME.TXT).','public','2026-03-13T19:59:41.275084','2026-03-13T19:59:41.275089','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','db5090d9-b0c1-46ed-9e4e-8a2809a93078','NASA Data.json','985b79af503a8f782919d12bf671faf80c640b4f5f5099665ec61f8d466c6b9f','1.1','2026-03-13T19:59:41.275084','2026-03-13T19:59:41.275089','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('43066f27-5540-4430-ac66-a90c0a716d83','ICE ENERGETIC PARTICLE ANISOTROPY SPECTROMETER DATA V1.0','In this G-Z dataset, observations from channels E1 to E5 (table below) are included since cometary ions were not detected in the higher energy channels. For each of these channels, particle counts are accumulated in eight azimuthal sectors of 45 deg. width in each telescope. The sectors are numbered from 1 to 8 anticlockwise when viewed from above the ecliptic, with Sector 1 centered on the sun- Earth line, i.e. it views in the sunward direction and detects ions streaming away from the Sun. At Giacobini-Zinner, a complete 3- dimensional distribution function was obtained at 32 s intervals during the main encounter phase, changing to 64 s at greater distances e.g. after 1830 UT on 12 September outbound.','public','2026-03-13T18:04:30.630576','2026-03-13T18:04:30.630582','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','84fc46f7-77a4-4206-99cc-cafe6c2020ae','NASA Data.json','37a380ed309805bc0307359386e3ac78d650d2e2b2f85d9e09a1294b714e97dc','1.1','2026-03-13T18:04:30.630576','2026-03-13T18:04:30.630582','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('432e452f-1f56-43e3-9778-45a6f445b211','ROSETTA-ORBITER X SREM 5 CRUISE 1 V1.0','This data set contains derived electron and proton flux energies in MeV from the Standard Radiation Environment Monitor (SREM) instrument on the Rosetta spacecraft. These are CODMAC Level 5 derived data, and measure the radiation in the spacecraft environment during the CRUISE 1 mission phase.','public','2026-03-13T18:32:43.132865','2026-03-13T18:32:43.132870','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','9e8c6ec5-7bcd-456a-992b-2b8438163315','NASA Data.json','d783d15e2d5bd4d2bcd47d9916ba8b6194c0dd3953ac1dffb3b9d94ade04577f','1.1','2026-03-13T18:32:43.132865','2026-03-13T18:32:43.132870','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('432ff8d4-8b91-4004-b53f-7c7cbe10c79c','MARS EXPRESS MARS MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 3 3380 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2010-01-01 to 2012-12-31. It is a Global Gravity measurement and covers the time 2012-12-02T04:43:06.000 to 2012-12-02T08:05:10.500.','public','2026-03-13T16:55:21.793313','2026-03-13T16:55:21.793320','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','ceb4f6dc-4ca0-42a6-b524-5a3171d65e83','NASA Data.json','fee77025b370483b7aa44c7271cc7b56510c69de9b1d111e1ce38e1932ae6b3e','1.1','2026-03-13T16:55:21.793313','2026-03-13T16:55:21.793320','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('43431e4d-8c48-4ba1-9c80-d3f060fd9b8c','MARS EXPRESS MARS MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 8 4203 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2021-01-01 to 2022-12-31. It is a Occultation measurement and covers the time 2021-04-03T06:20:33.600 to 2021-04-03T06:58:27.750.','public','2026-03-13T20:04:36.415190','2026-03-13T20:04:36.415197','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','ecc79d60-98dd-4308-b0da-6f85cb535125','NASA Data.json','f5211e22d70d49d236711b9b36aa2ac343209758b0fe083b1fc3ce7acf0f3182','1.1','2026-03-13T20:04:36.415190','2026-03-13T20:04:36.415197','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('434d76c0-69de-4e65-9e0c-1bcc62badded','ROSETTA-ORBITER LUTETIA RPCICA 2 AST2 UNCALIBRATED V2.0','This dataset contains RAW DATA from the RPCICA instrument onmission ROSETTA during the flyby of asteroid Lutetia. RPC-ICAsuffered an overheating event shortly after turn on, and did notobtain any measurements of value.Data set version 2 replaces a previously delivered data set.Important changes are the the expansion of data to a uniform resolution,Inclusion of the mode variable and new quality flags in the data andmoving information about software version, BAD_HV_MASK and SHADOW_MASKto the label.','public','2026-03-13T16:53:52.550049','2026-03-13T16:53:52.550055','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','7559fa32-abba-4ca3-8c9c-8ace01b01f39','NASA Data.json','d5d43748cfb851f76fa9ebe8076925d0e54a2c718ea7321c40adc40b63fd48b4','1.1','2026-03-13T16:53:52.550049','2026-03-13T16:53:52.550055','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('437beb9f-24dc-4938-978e-8745c52435c7','JUNO JUPITER RAW GRAVITY SCIENCE 1 V1.0','This data set contains archival raw, partially processed, and ancillary/supporting gravity science data acquired during the Juno Jupiter orbits starting in July 2016. The radio observations were  carried out using the Juno spacecraft and Earth-based receiving  stations of the NASA Deep Space Network (DSN). The data set was  designed primarily to determine the gravitational field of Jupiter.  Of most interest are likely to be the Orbit Data Files in the ODF  directory, which provided the raw input to gravity investigations,  as well as the tropospheric media calibration file produced by the Advanced Media Calibration (AMC) system.','public','2026-03-13T17:09:01.929023','2026-03-13T17:09:01.929031','Planetary Atmospheres','Planetary Data System','026:00','cfabe3ce-bedf-4502-98dd-9594988bceed','NASA Data.json','8b91e290dfe77e30ca8c94793da48e3fc0a472905e26572ef27dcbb975b4cdab','1.1','2026-03-13T17:09:01.929023','2026-03-13T17:09:01.929031','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('438d137f-f4b4-4452-8f64-2ff0e428d697','GALILEO ORBITER EUV JUPITER OPERATIONS EDR DATA','TBD','public','2026-03-13T17:42:40.695567','2026-03-13T17:42:40.695572','Planetary Atmospheres','Planetary Data System','026:00','a78ea64b-1763-4335-89a6-121b0ebfaffb','NASA Data.json','4cd7f554158882e986fb8928a2464c970a1e0876a75acbdcf2b3304efe81966a','1.1','2026-03-13T17:42:40.695567','2026-03-13T17:42:40.695572','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('43e5e33d-040d-4c56-8619-fec63ee69cb6','TEAMER: Numerical Modeling of the Pitching Inertial Pump (PIP) Wave Energy Capture Device','This project focused on further development of a Numerical Model of the iProTech Pitching Inertial Pump (PIP) wave energy converter (WEC) using the MATLAB/Simulink tool, WEC-Sim. The process involved parameterizing key design variables, running time-domain simulations, and performing sensitivity analyses to determine their impact on power output. The workflow, designed for the PIP device, is generalized and can be extended to optimize other WECs that can be simulated in WEC-Sim. This work establishes a foundation for future time-domain-based WEC design optimizations.\n\nIncluded in this submission are all figures from the final report and the model inputs required to generate them. This includes boundary element method (BEM) models, hydrodynamic coefficients, and the WEC-Sim models used for time-domain analyses. Although data for every single run is not included to save space, all of it can be reproduced using the provided models.\n','public','2026-03-31T14:23:22.852460','2026-03-31T14:23:22.852467','IProTech','Nick Wynn','019:20','f451e7cc-6db8-4069-8dad-fb164428ce7a','OpenEI data.json','18aa8b421a9e10d30024df966f1244c45162c40cd7370e3ad6d315b8dbbbc867','1.1','2026-03-31T14:23:22.852460','2026-03-31T14:23:22.852467',NULL,'019:009',0,'doe-gov'),('4437315e-61b3-4997-81c6-415082bc3fb0','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 1 0542 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 1 phase 2014-11-20 to 2015-03-10. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-01-19T11:41:30.000 to 2015-01-19T23:09:58.000.','public','2026-03-13T18:38:23.275526','2026-03-13T18:38:23.275531','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','689fea4c-1668-4539-bd8a-b052ab37ed03','NASA Data.json','2e0fc1999827d1e9660d1e23f8df2f1bcd13523be378eb21f5c14120d2052483','1.1','2026-03-13T18:38:23.275526','2026-03-13T18:38:23.275531','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('443ca6db-bbdc-47cd-a6cc-3a34bc966b5a','VG1 SAT MAG RESAMPLED KRONOGRAPHIC (L1)                                      COORDS 9.6SEC V1.0','This data set includes calibrated    magnetic field data acquired by the Voyager 1 Low Field Magnetometer    (LFM) during the Saturn encounter. Coverage begins in the solar wind    inbound to Saturn and continues past the last outbound bowshock crossing.    The data are in Kronographic (L1) coordinates and have been averaged    from the 1.92 second summary rate to a 9.6 second sample rate. All    magnetic field measurements are given in nanoTesla (nT). The magnetic    field data are calibrated (see the calibration description included in    the Voyager 1 Magnetometer instrument catalog file for details).','public','2026-03-13T18:02:13.450654','2026-03-13T18:02:13.450659','planetary plasma interactions','Planetary Data System','026:00','0c0fcc67-702b-40cf-8601-a98b6e82581e','NASA Data.json','82650d07a5af2edf6efda6f306326d7eb6f1e4deec9c2db0d26dc036f6ba230b','1.1','2026-03-13T18:02:13.450654','2026-03-13T18:02:13.450659','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('4460720a-61c6-4d71-91ac-b15f3e640271','VG2 NEP PLS DERIVED RDR 2 PROTON MAGSPHERE 48SEC V1.0','This data set gives the best available values for ion densities,      temperatures, and velocities near Neptune derived from data      obtained by the Voyager 2 plasma experiment.  All parameters are      obtained by fitting the observed spectra (current as a function      of energy) with Maxwellian plasma distributions, using a non-linear      least squares fitting routine to find the plasma parameters which,      when coupled with the full instrument response, best simulate the      data.  The PLS instrument measures energy/charge, so composition is      not uniquely determined but can be deduced in some cases by the      separation of the observed current peaks in energy (assuming the      plasma is co-moving).','public','2026-03-13T19:05:38.425351','2026-03-13T19:05:38.425357','planetary plasma interactions','Planetary Data System','026:00','73f0c884-db62-4d13-8dd7-265e4bf19361','NASA Data.json','51054bb6b1cad0dccdfd6faadcb4c28315102783027f6c817ade62c8da1a1511','1.1','2026-03-13T19:05:38.425351','2026-03-13T19:05:38.425357','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('44872949-1675-4b15-b1e5-50dc1158794e','VG2 URA MAG RESAMPLED RDR U1 COORDINATES                                      1.92SEC V1.0','This data set includes data from the          Low Field Magnetometer (LFM) in the during the Uranus encounter. The          encounter data (1986-01-24T07:00:00  -> 1986-01-25T04:00:00) have          been averaged from the 60ms instrument sample rate to a 1.92 second          resampled rate and are provided in the Uranus Longitude (U1)          coordinate system. Magnetometer data in the solar wind are given in          Heliographic coordinates.','public','2026-03-13T18:06:11.983294','2026-03-13T18:06:11.983299','planetary plasma interactions','Planetary Data System','026:00','b4c05ea0-5d21-49c3-9dd0-8b0302b525a8','NASA Data.json','4288e574ded073926a0a4de2432b652288da3e961766559f20db037fb61c8f76','1.1','2026-03-13T18:06:11.983294','2026-03-13T18:06:11.983299','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('44b128b6-9185-41b5-aac8-e0e4355371fe','FIELD EXP E GPSM DERIVED RDR TOPOGRAPHIC PROFILES V1.0','A field differential Geopositional Satellite (GPS) survey team which included Jim Garvin, Jack Bufton, Bill Krabill, and Earl B. Frederick deployed a pair of Motorola Eagle II GPS receivers to the southern flanks of the feature known as Mars Hill (an alluvial boulder field superimposed on a major lobe of alluvial and colluvial material in Eastern Death Valley) on Oct. 19, 1989. The objective was to measure the 5-20 cm scale microrelief of the boulder field at pixel scales (30-50 m long transects), with vertical control to the few cm level. These microterrain profiles were to be used to help calibrate radar scattering models, and to compare with helicopter stereo data (FEXP-E-HSTP-4 RDR-TOPOGRAPHIC-PROF-V1.0) for the same location.','public','2026-03-13T20:03:34.968853','2026-03-13T20:03:34.968859','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','75ffaf25-3032-4dc7-943d-e80c82880efc','NASA Data.json','d1ad72fea75f7ae19c0f38c516ba164dd445b7260e376b10f4b2f281d6256c67','1.1','2026-03-13T20:03:34.968853','2026-03-13T20:03:34.968859','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('44c35848-3b0f-4b5a-b2d3-395e7638fdcb','Hydrographic and Impairment Statistics Database: NPS-WSR Rio Grande Wild and Scenic River','Hydrographic and Impairment Statistics (HIS) is a National Park Service (NPS) Water Resources Division (WRD) project established to track certain goals created in response to the Government Performance and Results Act of 1993 (GPRA). One water resources management goal established by the Department of the Interior under GRPA requires NPS to track the percent of its managed surface waters that are meeting Clean Water Act (CWA) water quality standards. This goal requires an accurate inventory that spatially quantifies the surface water hydrography that each bureau manages and a procedure to determine and track which waterbodies are or are not meeting water quality standards as outlined by Section 303(d) of the CWA. This project helps meet this DOI GRPA goal by inventorying and monitoring in a geographic information system for the NPS: (1) CWA 303(d) quality impaired waters and causes; and (2) hydrographic statistics based on the United States Geological Survey (USGS) National Hydrography Dataset (NHD). Hydrographic and 303(d) impairment statistics were evaluated based on a combination of 1:24,000 (NHD) and finer scale data (frequently provided by state GIS layers).','public','2026-03-29T06:06:06.309558','2026-03-29T06:06:06.309566','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','f01f5ea1-add2-4852-ab2a-cfe313ea94ef','DOI NPS DCAT-US','a3e9595865cab3b56c00d23e5d854db4a1de9996a4aabcafc5ddb57d57003f5d','1.1','2026-03-29T06:06:06.309558','2026-03-29T06:06:06.309566','geospatial','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('44d2ab19-d71d-4500-a5d3-c16c777f6d58','MARS EXPRESS MARS MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 6 3917 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2017-01-01 to 2018-12-31. It is a Occultation measurement and covers the time 2018-03-12T07:35:14.000 to 2018-03-12T08:02:03.949.','public','2026-03-13T18:08:58.321038','2026-03-13T18:08:58.321043','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','fbf20ab6-2207-4d8c-9886-7e49087588f5','NASA Data.json','4ddee738f7ff86407afdea182b817d38fa2f1989e1a49dc44efa5258aee46433','1.1','2026-03-13T18:08:58.321038','2026-03-13T18:08:58.321043','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('44e53852-de7d-4b28-b0d3-a37cdad7565e','Walton-Smith CTD, WS15264, WS15264_WS15264sta16, 2015-09-22, 24.6745N 81.2032W','Walton-Smith Conductivity, Temperature, Depth (CTD) - WS15264 - WS15264_WS15264sta16 - 2015-09-22 - 24.6745N 81.2032W. Hydrographic Measurements in the Gulf of Mexico. flags: 1 = good; 3 =  mean ÃÂ± 3*standard deviation; 4 = mean ÃÂ± 5*standard deviation; 9 = missing. other','public','2026-03-26T19:17:12.193097','2026-03-26T19:17:12.193103',NULL,NULL,NULL,'a78b306c-1b89-452e-93c4-c5524b241048','ioos',NULL,NULL,'2026-03-26T19:17:12.193097','2026-03-26T19:17:12.193103',NULL,NULL,NULL,'noaa-gov'),('450ee43c-f8e5-467b-9be3-a12c3c0fc605','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 4 1120 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 4 phase 2015-10-22 to 2015-12-31. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-10-22T10:21:00.000 to 2015-10-22T17:21:22.500.','public','2026-03-13T17:07:03.810733','2026-03-13T17:07:03.810741','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','a92e9400-52cb-4d8f-8c7d-f8be7af07fad','NASA Data.json','d9700c1ff4e7547fed835ab127c461c9edb6fac0e07bdb80d4ff8344ff5cd990','1.1','2026-03-13T17:07:03.810733','2026-03-13T17:07:03.810741','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('4513ce61-b86f-41c4-bf92-ad374518e271','MARS EXPRESS MARS MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 5 3689 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2015-01-01 to 2016-12-31. It is a Global Gravity measurement and covers the time 2015-01-29T04:35:43.000 to 2015-01-29T08:15:13.500.','public','2026-03-13T19:40:28.497539','2026-03-13T19:40:28.497547','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','16678d2d-1210-48df-9f07-110c090f6eae','NASA Data.json','c8046dded17112384e63946c254423165772ea9597889f21945bffcd24c3a778','1.1','2026-03-13T19:40:28.497539','2026-03-13T19:40:28.497547','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('4522664c-6f98-4387-8e3b-78d387428532','ROSETTA-ORBITER CHECKOUT OSIWAC 4 CVP2 RDR V1.0','This CODMAC level 4 data set contains radiometric calibrated and geometric distortion corrected (resampled) image data in W/m^2/sr/nm,  acquired by the OSIRIS Wide Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft  during the COMMISSIONING 2 mission phase, covering the period  from 2004-09-06T00:00:00.000 to 2004-10-16T23:59:59.000. The prime objective was commissioning / calibration. Several targets of opportunity were observed, but none of them is identifiable as prime target. This version V1.0 is the first version of this dataset.','public','2026-03-13T16:59:37.719724','2026-03-13T16:59:37.719730','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','0b46ebef-256b-433b-b518-a04c9fe8ef4d','NASA Data.json','0eacd07b77b6099de96ab6f0243805bd29d73aa2a5d9c8c2342cbffea5656ea4','1.1','2026-03-13T16:59:37.719724','2026-03-13T16:59:37.719730','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('45540578-1b4f-4d5c-a4d5-eb6c342c5565','AIRSAR_POLSAR_SYNOPTIC_3_FREQ_POLARIMETRY','AIRSAR three-frequency polarimetric synoptic product','public','2026-03-13T19:03:40.442154','2026-03-13T19:03:40.442161','NASA/JPL/RDC;ASF','Earthdata Forum','026:00','a3b005c2-341d-4d0a-971b-1c688e51d1f9','NASA Data.json','b144b513a2cd8ddcdc74e7c46cff2cf075c6470eae18aad2fd011fc3dd8fe6e6','1.1','2026-03-13T19:03:40.442154','2026-03-13T19:03:40.442161','Earth Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('455f5bba-44fd-4384-a8b3-b80a3f96616e','2025 E-Government Annual Data','2025 E-Government Annual Data','public','2026-03-22T03:20:06.714565','2026-03-22T03:20:06.714568','data.oregon.gov','Roger Anderson',NULL,'666aacd9-d72d-4d14-aa8f-25c458d4b6fd','oregon json','12a89e5250f4bede2f86d6fcef663d8c9074608932b48403cfd3261e38946016','1.1','2026-03-22T03:20:06.714565','2026-03-22T03:20:06.714568',NULL,NULL,0,'state-of-oregon'),('45663ef2-a867-4a1c-b068-0d9b1b5babc4','DID(IT) - Electronic Personnel Universally Linked System','ePulse is an application that the Vermont Service Center (VSC) uses to perform administrative functions such as a Continuity of Operations (COOP) program, workflow planning and distribution, human resources operations, and telework operations. ePulse will store employee-related data such as address and contact information, assignment details, and other types of data used to complete human resources forms such as the Standard Form (SF)-52, Request for Personnel Action. ePulse does not actually contain SF-52 forms - only data that can be used to populate a SF-52. ePulse uses a role based system that limits access to enter, view, or edit information.','non-public','2026-03-22T11:56:53.913545','2026-03-22T11:56:53.913551','Unspecified','Open Data (MGMT)','024:030','9dc787ce-3bdd-435e-a2ca-ebc6aed121b5','DHS datajson source','aed48f53b0811a8ea6965c4a87f68a0685704cb30287a4ec3884220bd77b6653','1.1','2026-03-22T11:56:53.913545','2026-03-22T11:56:53.913551',NULL,'024:000',0,'dhs-gov'),('45765071-b0dc-4058-b2b8-e43ca6b49dc0','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 1 0491 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 1 phase 2014-11-20 to 2015-03-10. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2014-12-16T12:47:40.000 to 2014-12-16T15:00:10.000.','public','2026-03-13T19:26:20.393837','2026-03-13T19:26:20.393844','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','f397c88b-02eb-48c1-b1e3-3d89e6a2c6b7','NASA Data.json','b13ec2ee3b9d5aadad1ef9b908a6047e3e93eb28bbe70df4dfe7c395bb8bd075','1.1','2026-03-13T19:26:20.393837','2026-03-13T19:26:20.393844','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('457c4c55-e0ec-4337-bfb7-b1d08104f901','DID(IT) - Electronic Statistical Automated Activity Tracking (ESTAT)','The Electronic Statistical Automated Activity Tracking (ESTAT) is a web based centralized workflow solution for conducting Adjudication Performance, Statistical Analysis and Tracking. ESTAT collects user-centric production metrics along activity and operation lines in compliance with the requirements of the G-22/23 PRT feeder system as detailed in the USCIS Administrative Manual.','non-public','2026-03-22T11:52:08.137618','2026-03-22T11:52:08.137623','Unspecified','Open Data (MGMT)','024:030','0d4a6a7a-9e83-4304-80de-fcc1259b20bc','DHS datajson source','fef9f6462ba7d4c17a272522a71d38de7088db48afd4511d315a197ee87a2c26','1.1','2026-03-22T11:52:08.137618','2026-03-22T11:52:08.137623',NULL,'024:000',0,'dhs-gov'),('45a4e2fe-7821-41c7-89a2-57247e91dd6f','ROSETTA-ORBITER PRELANDING OSIWAC 2 EDR MTP003 V2.0','This data set contains images acquired by the OSIRIS Wide Angle Camera during the PRELANDING phase of the Rosetta mission at the comet 67P, covering the period from 2014-05-07T12:48:00.000 to 2014-06-04T10:49:59.000. This version V2.0 supersedes previous deliveries of the same dataset.','public','2026-03-13T16:43:11.754389','2026-03-13T16:43:11.754398','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','e6e4feb3-d305-45eb-b081-b7cd43fd5e15','NASA Data.json','0c8ed3a749c67de309239409cc71b72efc6e34a30563d36a7bdd140621db993e','1.1','2026-03-13T16:43:11.754389','2026-03-13T16:43:11.754398','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('45accdf3-f03e-4fd2-abc1-e26da1566f35','MISSION C NR MISSION ST NR SANTA BARBARA CA (USGS 11119750)','Timeseries data from \'MISSION C NR MISSION ST NR SANTA BARBARA CA (USGS 11119750)\' (gov_usgs_nwis_11119750)','public','2026-03-26T19:15:49.443684','2026-03-26T19:15:49.443691',NULL,NULL,NULL,'b1837824-f88b-4b34-9ea3-0ab1cf900aa8','ioos',NULL,NULL,'2026-03-26T19:15:49.443684','2026-03-26T19:15:49.443691',NULL,NULL,NULL,'noaa-gov'),('45db12f3-07b1-431f-9b82-206f7c1b68f3','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 ROSETTA EXTENSION 1 1368 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the ROSETTA EXTENSION 1 phase 2016-01-01 to 2016-04-05. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2016-01-25T01:01:40.000 to 2016-01-25T09:11:44.500.','public','2026-03-13T18:22:19.408774','2026-03-13T18:22:19.408782','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','be594e2b-7131-4d2d-b5b6-d2bd9525a6a2','NASA Data.json','c1a137dcf44010c01c3013dfe3064a589374b08edfd9fa7d60762634b6f52ff5','1.1','2026-03-13T18:22:19.408774','2026-03-13T18:22:19.408782','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('45ec9db1-56a0-4da6-b250-b8c6d468ceec','VG1 J/S/SS PWS EDITED SPECTRUM ANALYZER FULL RES V1.0','This data set includes nearly all measurements collected from the     spectrum analyzer component of the Plasma Wave Spectrometer (PWS)     onboard Voyager 1 for the entire mission.  Some noise lines during the     planetary encounters have been edited from the data set.  Each sweep of     the PWS spectrum analyzer records spectral densities in 16 frequency     channels from 50 Hz to 10 kHz.  The values in this data set are given     as instrument data numbers.  Instructions for producing calibrated     values are provided.  An example C-language program which reads this     data set and produces calibrated values is also provided.','public','2026-03-13T19:38:47.469258','2026-03-13T19:38:47.469263','planetary plasma interactions','Planetary Data System','026:00','0fe8547e-8d73-4b9f-8b2e-af3b72e3d168','NASA Data.json','d3d09aa3178d124a6d6dd4be1bc1efc27c5069fe1fd46d42495a8a97e9edd85b','1.1','2026-03-13T19:38:47.469258','2026-03-13T19:38:47.469263','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('463dd2b7-9fa8-47d6-ab32-244f7e7dfa6e','MARS EXPRESS MARS MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 8 4270 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2021-01-01 to 2022-12-31. It is a Occultation measurement and covers the time 2022-05-27T03:23:00.200 to 2022-05-27T03:45:08.549.','public','2026-03-13T17:42:30.646289','2026-03-13T17:42:30.646297','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','c1a9d621-e1e2-43d1-8cf3-ab41cb78b997','NASA Data.json','37e45f7369fe63ebe1d40802704efc00a6fcb86b7c7f2b7955c281cb33df8edb','1.1','2026-03-13T17:42:30.646289','2026-03-13T17:42:30.646297','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('468c20e8-fb74-4b2f-bb11-5ac3997cf01f','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSIWAC 3 EXT3-MTP033 RDR V3.0','This CODMAC level 3 data set contains radiometric calibrated image data in W/m^2/sr/nm, acquired by the OSIRIS Wide Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft during the ROSETTA EXTENSION 3 mission phase, covering the period from 2016-08-09T23:25:00.000 to 2016-09-02T06:39:59.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V3.0 supersedes previous deliveries of the same dataset with the following changes since the last version: Lien corrected dataset after the July and October 2018 PSA/PDS external peer reviews. Updated documentation and ancillary files, added document on bandpass filter. Updated SCIENCE_USER_GUIDE_V03.PDF to include one section about FAQ and one section about image data quality. Added shutter backtravel and readout issues to image quality map. Updated DATA_QUALITY_ID keyword in image header. Improved handling of images with missing packets. Corrected START_TIME and STOP_TIME for BALLISTIC_STACKED images. Improved calibration of WAC balistic mode images.','public','2026-03-13T17:40:53.936271','2026-03-13T17:40:53.936276','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','f605c20f-f01c-45ef-b3e9-c98eca0d6ae0','NASA Data.json','8028e3c75f9e182b0b54ac4f30fe8e2a10a87d0b638a2f0ae79653b39c000bc1','1.1','2026-03-13T17:40:53.936271','2026-03-13T17:40:53.936276','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('46c6f619-eca1-4825-9a3b-57f2591b2d19','Continuous Fixed Station Water Quality Measurements in Canaveral National Seashore, September 2007 (Certified)','This dataset represents continuous water quality measurements that were taken at a fixed point in Canaveral National Seashore during the month of September, 2007 as a part of the Fixed Station Water Quality Monitoring protocol that was developed by the Southeast Coast I&M Network (SECN). The measurements were taken by a YSI 6600 ESD Multi-Parameter Long Term Water Quality Monitoring Datasonde unit that serves as the standard fixed station water quality monitoring equipment for all similar operations conducted by the SECN. The following parameters were measured at 30 minute intervals during the time period that has been specified: Water Temperature, Specific Conductivity, Salinity, Dissolved Oxygen (DO), DO Concentration, Shallow Depth, pH Level, and Turbidity. Any anomalies noted regarding these parameters have also been noted in separate fields. Please note that these measurements have been certified by network personnel.','public','2026-03-26T05:30:58.157311','2026-03-26T05:30:58.157316','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','4bf4ad10-ec3f-45d2-ab4e-df6f911a5681','DOI NPS DCAT-US','97c738affbf98909ce7fbf2d01f6ad88be0b5ea7754a263a80f1ea5541c60c3b','1.1','2026-03-26T05:30:58.157311','2026-03-26T05:30:58.157316','Vector Dataset','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('46ea84bc-b987-46f5-b7ea-85c86c8db457','NEW HORIZONS SWAP JUPITER ENCOUNTER V2.0','This data set contains Raw data taken by the New Horizons Solar Wind Around Pluto instrument during the Jupiter encounter mission phase.','public','2026-03-13T17:36:13.967150','2026-03-13T17:36:13.967156','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','c1f95c72-caa4-463e-bf2e-60d2ed67fc19','NASA Data.json','ab1d1275c94b0e5bb3861b648aaf8c724c52c5f9faeedf71aa839cadcabccf8b','1.1','2026-03-13T17:36:13.967150','2026-03-13T17:36:13.967156','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('472da5b0-d01a-4ce6-8f09-fda77991925a','Building Permits Dataset Contact Columns Removed - 7/16/2019','Columns removed from building permits dataset.','public','2026-03-29T04:49:36.304407','2026-03-29T04:49:36.304411','data.cityofchicago.org','Maria Fiorillo',NULL,'5c8ac8ef-be71-4735-89e4-29aeff93df1e','Chicago JSON','6d0b228f7016707e0bb378d124c0a03a8216629c0cc1c1d2ce919f09e069c88b','1.1','2026-03-29T04:49:36.304407','2026-03-29T04:49:36.304411','Buildings',NULL,0,'city-of-chicago'),('472fc474-59ee-41c6-a038-86f863a73b89','Prince Rupert, B. C., BC (CYPR)','Timeseries data from \'Prince Rupert, B. C., BC (CYPR)\' (gov_noaa_awc_cypr)','public','2026-03-26T19:15:14.402466','2026-03-26T19:15:14.402472',NULL,NULL,NULL,'06ec7057-fbf3-42e8-934a-393381f967af','ioos',NULL,NULL,'2026-03-26T19:15:14.402466','2026-03-26T19:15:14.402472',NULL,NULL,NULL,'noaa-gov'),('475ffd08-38bf-4da5-a393-82d659d3e764','NEW HORIZONS ALICE POST-LAUNCH CHECKOUT V2.0','This data set contains Raw data taken by the New Horizons Alice UV Spectrograph instrument during the post-launch checkout mission phase.','public','2026-03-13T17:09:25.721879','2026-03-13T17:09:25.721887','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','f0dc5407-e7fd-4871-a12a-606897c01795','NASA Data.json','67d40bc6374d34b39b1a14dada78dddd4d3d066ec1b8d26680924e6128cdf063','1.1','2026-03-13T17:09:25.721879','2026-03-13T17:09:25.721887','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('477b7bf5-0705-4aa4-a1c6-08287366d270','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 PRELANDING 0272 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the PRELANDING phase 2014-01-21 to 2014-11-18. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2014-09-05T06:52:05.000 to 2014-09-05T17:31:17.000.','public','2026-03-13T19:49:26.678705','2026-03-13T19:49:26.678711','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','f1ccaf9e-9361-4dc1-8dd4-b58618068119','NASA Data.json','88327dfea3daab5281743b91e0294d5c82cf69d68ced2972b325affc4307ce63','1.1','2026-03-13T19:49:26.678705','2026-03-13T19:49:26.678711','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('47c0a95c-fce1-47c5-8fe8-33500fd67e44','ROSETTA-ORBITER COMET PRELANDING OSINAC 2 EDR DATA MTP 002','This data set contains raw EDR images acquired by the OSIRIS Narrow AngleCamera during the prelanding phase of the Rosetta mission at the comet 67P,covering the period from 2014-04-06 to 2014-05-07.','public','2026-03-13T16:56:50.833022','2026-03-13T16:56:50.833027','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','63dc1588-158b-4995-bbab-dfc0bbefb0cc','NASA Data.json','1c15ad7f7a3bec8fc229bb96c1fbea014b710a8e038c54600a08680e3b77fd7f','1.1','2026-03-13T16:56:50.833022','2026-03-13T16:56:50.833027','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('47c12277-87a1-40b2-90be-669e8dab8886','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RPCIES 3 ESC2 V1.0','This dataset contains CALIBRATED DATA of the Rosetta RPCIES instrument taken during the comet escort 2 phase (ESC2). The target of this phase was comet 67P/CHURYUMOV-GERASIMENKO 1 (1969 R1). Included are the data taken between 11 Mar 2015 and 30 Jun 2015.','public','2026-03-13T17:26:43.468909','2026-03-13T17:26:43.468915','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','e6822bfc-05b5-427b-8b7c-506d6625173d','NASA Data.json','2febe5490cbbcd81c0106bfb337cb56b1c301999427de67b71b84ae3d966cc23','1.1','2026-03-13T17:26:43.468909','2026-03-13T17:26:43.468915','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('47ca0a2d-0d64-4583-8790-41e6085f76d8','Hydrographic and Impairment Statistics Database: NPS-WSR Snake River Headwaters Wild and Scenic River','Hydrographic and Impairment Statistics (HIS) is a National Park Service (NPS) Water Resources Division (WRD) project established to track certain goals created in response to the Government Performance and Results Act of 1993 (GPRA). One water resources management goal established by the Department of the Interior under GRPA requires NPS to track the percent of its managed surface waters that are meeting Clean Water Act (CWA) water quality standards. This goal requires an accurate inventory that spatially quantifies the surface water hydrography that each bureau manages and a procedure to determine and track which waterbodies are or are not meeting water quality standards as outlined by Section 303(d) of the CWA. This project helps meet this DOI GRPA goal by inventorying and monitoring in a geographic information system for the NPS: (1) CWA 303(d) quality impaired waters and causes; and (2) hydrographic statistics based on the United States Geological Survey (USGS) National Hydrography Dataset (NHD). Hydrographic and 303(d) impairment statistics were evaluated based on a combination of 1:24,000 (NHD) and finer scale data (frequently provided by state GIS layers).','public','2026-03-29T06:05:23.900037','2026-03-29T06:05:23.900043','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','8e278cdf-ca7f-4dba-a9c7-cd8eaa3a650f','DOI NPS DCAT-US','fac948d9222278abdc846305e4b9840b48c167f92005874ee9a5b42e097c326f','1.1','2026-03-29T06:05:23.900037','2026-03-29T06:05:23.900043','geospatial','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('480839fa-d859-4be5-b9f9-671c81b9deec','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSINAC 4 ESC3-MTP018 RDR-INF-REFL V1.0','This CODMAC level 4 data set contains solar stray-light corrected, in-field stray-light corrected,  radiometric calibrated and geometric distortion corrected  (resampled) image data in reflectance units (normalized  and thus without unit),  acquired by the OSIRIS Narrow Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft  during the COMET ESCORT 3 mission phase, covering the period  from 2015-06-30T23:25:00.000 to 2015-07-28T23:24:59.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V1.0 is the first version of this dataset: Lien corrected dataset after September 2019 PSA/PDS external peer review.','public','2026-03-13T17:33:53.792380','2026-03-13T17:33:53.792386','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','b6a773a4-7a5c-47ac-80f9-3391f4107494','NASA Data.json','9e58ef7812afbd44e3a24cd6810da62154a0c884cbd89353ec6aca97b41aeeff','1.1','2026-03-13T17:33:53.792380','2026-03-13T17:33:53.792386','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('482ad4c0-d57d-41ef-bd3b-99e7557fa5fa','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 2 0641 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 2 phase 2015-03-11 to 2015-06-30. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-03-13T10:21:35.000 to 2015-03-13T12:23:37.000.','public','2026-03-13T16:52:23.324101','2026-03-13T16:52:23.324106','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','50114f71-8108-4d47-9d7a-e3af55d2637e','NASA Data.json','5d0d587ccb4fe41b20b89ae81160277dbd03ebeb6be95dca8e167fb6b292d9bc','1.1','2026-03-13T16:52:23.324101','2026-03-13T16:52:23.324106','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('48317ad6-bb86-4c0e-9ad2-86efda4ee2d8','VG2 JUP PLS DERIVED ION IN/OUTBNDMAGSHTH L-MODE 96SEC V1.0','This data set contains plasma parameters    from the Voyager 2 inbound magnetosheath and outbound data from the    magnetotail through the solar wind. Inbound Voyager 2 passed near noon    local time, so it sampled regions of the magnetosheath where flow is    generally subsonic. Distribution functions observed were well represented    by two convected isotropic proton Maxwellians, so this type of    distribution was used to derive the proton velocity, density and    temperature. Physically the two populations represent the thermal plasma    accelerated at the shock (the colder component) and ions reflected once at    the shock before entering the magnetosheath (the hotter component). The    PLS experiment could not resolve alpha particles in this region so no    alpha parameters are provided; the neglect of alpha made cause an    overestimate of the hot proton component of the plasma. One sigma errors    are provided for the fit parameters.','public','2026-03-13T18:21:57.175459','2026-03-13T18:21:57.175465','planetary plasma interactions','Planetary Data System','026:00','ed1aeb80-85f5-4fcb-bd08-b7e0495ff634','NASA Data.json','0ecdb6ad855be8dbd7ebf2d49bad3c096ba5c9a73ef4fae63a8cb7c3971960f3','1.1','2026-03-13T18:21:57.175459','2026-03-13T18:21:57.175465','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('483a5f31-fcde-4df9-b748-3261552dce57','Steller Cove','Timeseries data from \'Steller Cove\' (noaa_nos_co_ops_twc2319)','public','2026-03-26T19:14:59.746041','2026-03-26T19:14:59.746047',NULL,NULL,NULL,'4b63f933-7e56-45ed-af07-7fa1af6be807','ioos',NULL,NULL,'2026-03-26T19:14:59.746041','2026-03-26T19:14:59.746047',NULL,NULL,NULL,'noaa-gov'),('48682f75-6892-45fb-b19e-d8303aa1e64a','MARS EXPRESS SUN MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 7 4028 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2019-01-01 to 2020-12-31. It is a Solar Conjunction measurement and covers the time 2019-08-11T06:17:27.000 to 2019-08-11T09:10:16.500.','public','2026-03-13T17:16:26.227210','2026-03-13T17:16:26.227215','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','c1748183-8a42-4e41-8cc6-131bd19c6867','NASA Data.json','87be38c4216da8a3d66ff5544658e449fb605a56acf416b9dfe268f756a28d95','1.1','2026-03-13T17:16:26.227210','2026-03-13T17:16:26.227215','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('48851c82-6f3e-456f-a7b2-922b6586013a','HPMS Urban Area Summaries 2021','The Highway Performance Monitoring System Urban Area Summaries table contains daily travel and demographics data for all local functional system roads for each adjusted urbanized area.','public','2026-03-28T13:37:15.074173','2026-03-28T13:37:15.074177','Federal Highway Administration','Office of Highway Policy Information','021:15','966d7c24-9714-4ca1-a019-e45ee677ebcd','DOT Socrata Data.json','180816a2c67de43d7ed99629361fc05ffbf06dff30995c836cd69b8ab5b04b58','1.1','2026-03-28T13:37:15.074173','2026-03-28T13:37:15.074177','Roadways and Bridges','021:009',0,'dot-gov'),('48a8ad84-d73d-4f8d-8281-da82e24daa53','AMES MARS GENERAL CIRCULATION MODEL 5 LAT TIME VARIABLE V1.0','The Ames Mars General Circulation Model is a three dimensional model based on the primitive equations of meteorology. It includes the radiative effects of dust and carbon dioxide as well as other features such as large-scale topography (see [POLLACKETAL1990]','public','2026-03-13T16:46:40.582632','2026-03-13T16:46:40.582638','Planetary Atmospheres','Planetary Data System','026:00','944cd30b-0f87-4dc6-ac90-b5acb779bf2b','NASA Data.json','c02f1e7636f5bbefb039fd602107703388658a3ba2266633588eba62bd5c892b','1.1','2026-03-13T16:46:40.582632','2026-03-13T16:46:40.582638','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('48ab10b1-4e63-4f4c-8c2f-0db9d99a389a','MARS EXPRESS MARS MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 8 4256 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2021-01-01 to 2022-12-31. It is a Occultation measurement and covers the time 2022-05-15T02:50:19.000 to 2022-05-15T05:25:03.000.','public','2026-03-13T19:17:21.378997','2026-03-13T19:17:21.379002','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','792b01f7-fafd-4b82-9af0-33d49f25ae4e','NASA Data.json','1cad57931093395ef270e3d04dd4c92a22008b1382debd756027b69aff7515d0','1.1','2026-03-13T19:17:21.378997','2026-03-13T19:17:21.379002','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('48c813c4-fc06-4366-b2c4-54039b11dc55','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P NAVCAM 2 COMET ESCORT 3 MTP021 V1.0','This dataset contains ROSETTA NAVCAM RAW DATA of the Escort Phase 3 from 22nd Sep 2015 to 20th Oct 2015 when at the vicinity of target 67P/CG.','public','2026-03-13T17:55:25.518974','2026-03-13T17:55:25.518979','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','0f201a74-3640-4e30-8f2c-14a869faa8ad','NASA Data.json','c167c90aa0d6e7cf90039f59dfe41306a4354c352254a87e5a9d9ecbe100aac3','1.1','2026-03-13T17:55:25.518974','2026-03-13T17:55:25.518979','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('48de3bb2-07e4-4093-a172-7257847354de','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RPCMIP 3 EXT1 V1.0','This archive contains calibrated data from the RPC-MIP instrument onboard ROSETTA Orbiter, acquired during the ROSETTA EXTENSION part 1 mission phase. The primary target was comet 67P/C-G. It also contains documentation which describes the MIP experiment. The data archived in this data set conform to the Planetary Data System Standards, Version 3.6.','public','2026-03-13T16:59:40.485966','2026-03-13T16:59:40.485973','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','e8285e53-a51e-4de7-997b-a017f3ba5e2c','NASA Data.json','0a02f6be990fe0c04c09f8a989ffb7ea55bbd43a9b76eacd000c6934c854bd33','1.1','2026-03-13T16:59:40.485966','2026-03-13T16:59:40.485973','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('48ee327d-79ae-4bc5-97cd-907c6114b4a6','VEGA1 TV SYSTEM IMAGES V1.0','For the TV SYSTEM, 95 images were sent as a 7-d FITS file with little information in the FITS headers. In addition, to the size of the image (NAXIS1 and NAXIS2), the values for NAXIS3 and NAXIS4 were labeled \'TIME\' interpreted as exposure time in seconds. The following procedure was used to convert NAXIS3 information:','public','2026-03-13T17:29:02.855008','2026-03-13T17:29:02.855013','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','c41c63e6-987a-4d63-9ac9-3db92720a22e','NASA Data.json','3e1799c63b449744d4fb5973eb0b45d4c8a2886991ad024eecb76588b8e986ec','1.1','2026-03-13T17:29:02.855008','2026-03-13T17:29:02.855013','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('4939272f-2e8c-4287-821b-bda47b098b86','EGIS - Enterprise Gateway Integration Services-AAMVA Hub Service','The American Association of Motor Vehicle Administration (AAMVA) Hub Service supports messaging between AAMVA and the USCIS Verification Division. AHS acts as an interface between AAMVAnet and USCIS applications to enable a States’ Department of Motor Vehicles (DMV) system to interact with SAVE for alien verification and E-Verify for employment verification and vice versa.','non-public','2026-03-22T11:55:33.523622','2026-03-22T11:55:33.523626','Unspecified','Open Data (MGMT)','024:030','ee96203a-1d27-47ac-a51b-6949af7c87c9','DHS datajson source','218f18429c0f5c59bfbc7a3a18284400598dfba70e2282ad4a230171e737bbf4','1.1','2026-03-22T11:55:33.523622','2026-03-22T11:55:33.523626',NULL,'024:000',0,'dhs-gov'),('49721b70-0ce5-4bc5-9eca-7bc6735aa0de','Continuous Fixed Station Water Quality Measurements in Cape Lookout National Seashore, July 2009 (Certified)','This dataset represents continuous water quality measurements that were taken at a fixed point in Cape Lookout National Seashore during the month of July, 2009 as a part of the Fixed Station Water Quality Monitoring protocol that was developed by the Southeast Coast I&M Network (SECN). The measurements were taken by a YSI 6600 ESD Multi-Parameter Long Term Water Quality Monitoring Datasonde unit that serves as the standard fixed station water quality monitoring equipment for all similar operations conducted by the SECN. The following parameters were measured at 15 minute intervals during the time period that has been specified: Water Temperature, Specific Conductivity, Salinity, Dissolved Oxygen (DO), DO Concentration, Shallow Depth, pH Level, and Turbidity. Any anomalies noted regarding these parameters have also been noted in separate fields.  Please note that these measurements have been certified by network personnel.','public','2026-03-26T05:27:48.100348','2026-03-26T05:27:48.100353','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','3c99f08d-aa82-403b-b07a-497c37655dc0','DOI NPS DCAT-US','9ebf424664ca4b1a9a99b102cf8761f52edc3f10d6386605e3bf1071697b9445','1.1','2026-03-26T05:27:48.100348','2026-03-26T05:27:48.100353','Vector Dataset','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('498a16ab-61a4-41fc-81c3-9e1d8c65acf8','GALILEO PROBE LRD RAW DATA SET','Data from this instrument appear to have been lost due to the death of Co-Investigator Klaus Rinnert. Please refer to the following publications for results from this instrument.','public','2026-03-13T18:16:23.568007','2026-03-13T18:16:23.568012','Planetary Atmospheres','Planetary Data System','026:00','b5fa9626-9372-4d6e-924d-4128b1776324','NASA Data.json','2a24db6a16fd84a5b7f362e2d871a94a46afcd3110115f0f898b2bc0ba259162','1.1','2026-03-13T18:16:23.568007','2026-03-13T18:16:23.568012','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('498e77a0-1139-4027-89e0-42cf81805feb','Continuous Fixed Station Water Quality Measurements in Canaveral National Seashore, January 2007 (Certified)','This dataset represents continuous water quality measurements that were taken at a fixed point in Canaveral National Seashore during the month of January, 2007 as a part of the Fixed Station Water Quality Monitoring protocol that was developed by the Southeast Coast I&M Network (SECN). The measurements were taken by a YSI 6600 ESD Multi-Parameter Long Term Water Quality Monitoring Datasonde unit that serves as the standard fixed station water quality monitoring equipment for all similar operations conducted by the SECN. The following parameters were measured at 30 minute intervals during the time period that has been specified: Water Temperature, Specific Conductivity, Salinity, Dissolved Oxygen (DO), DO Concentration, Shallow Depth, pH Level, and Turbidity. Any anomalies noted regarding these parameters have also been noted in separate fields. Please note that these measurements have been certified by network personnel.','public','2026-03-26T05:30:36.059647','2026-03-26T05:30:36.059655','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','5420fbd3-c1fa-4044-b47a-b007d2c95a63','DOI NPS DCAT-US','bf7dc563f57f1e7dc307230c1f2998ab35bf87d55a89f2c53483491181467f53','1.1','2026-03-26T05:30:36.059647','2026-03-26T05:30:36.059655','Vector Dataset','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('49cab1f7-0f00-4e18-b027-b25a5c5ee940','JOLTS Tableau - LAUS-ALMA Dataset','Job Openings and Labor Turnover survey dataset that contains Local Area Unemployment Statistics data (produced by America\'s Labor Market Analyzer). Data includes but is not limited to labor force estimates, unemployment rates, and job openings for the state of Iowa.','public','2026-03-28T21:57:46.505278','2026-03-28T21:57:46.505284','data.iowa.gov','svqueen',NULL,'6b3698ce-e711-48e4-ae58-67dea0d96779','Iowa metadata','5d9d4a554e238478a54e3dc68dae819c684b62f654db7deb7eb9db2fea612d42','1.1','2026-03-28T21:57:46.505278','2026-03-28T21:57:46.505284','Economic Statistics',NULL,0,'state-of-iowa'),('49f15ae9-1209-4d7d-b1be-51810e74c139','ROSETTA-ORBITER SUN RSI 1/2/3 CRUISE 2 0023 V1.0','This is a Solar Conjunction measurement covering the time 2006-03-30T00:27:04.500 to 2006-03-30T03:37:16.500.','public','2026-03-13T18:01:15.727055','2026-03-13T18:01:15.727061','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','8e7ed406-defa-48ba-abb2-484499443f9e','NASA Data.json','dfa23aaa26f12553eb942a59f3a01e84558d0faf7a94b29a792427080e6010ad','1.1','2026-03-13T18:01:15.727055','2026-03-13T18:01:15.727061','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('4a504626-44f5-421d-a898-c9a3bc9b697c','PHOENIX MARS METEOROLOGICAL PRESSURE / TEMPERATURE RDR V1.0','The PHX METEOROLOGICAL DATA product contains calibrated temperature and pressure data. The temperature data was collected at 250, 500 and 1000mm above the Phoenix Lander deck, and the pressure data was collected at (nearly) the height of the Lander deck. Nominally the data was collected at 2 sec resolution, but is also provided at 512 sec averages (with distribution statistics). Owing to the placement of a heater near the pressure sensor, a corrected set of values was required, and is provided for the pressure data.','public','2026-03-13T18:10:44.672294','2026-03-13T18:10:44.672299','Planetary Atmospheres','Planetary Data System','026:00','1c38c03e-b0f1-4ca3-8eb0-f50b35e45292','NASA Data.json','b1a015f2159479f646614c04c8993c5e193ba596ce877cb7874fe86eb5739f96','1.1','2026-03-13T18:10:44.672294','2026-03-13T18:10:44.672299','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('4a69b8de-c192-4199-a113-0805a6a2bf5c','MARS EXPRESS SUN MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 5 3761 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2015-01-01 to 2016-12-31. It is a Solar Conjunction measurement and covers the time 2015-06-08T10:33:01 to 2015-06-08T17:34:00.','public','2026-03-13T17:58:28.716982','2026-03-13T17:58:28.716987','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','7a4e2829-5d8f-4e8e-ba03-ebf5e095e0d6','NASA Data.json','2986d92b1c13b296d80205b227c3739d2258a3dbc7f938e58e2fb1424ecd244d','1.1','2026-03-13T17:58:28.716982','2026-03-13T17:58:28.716987','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('4a8b8f92-8121-435a-b059-cf5412759f96','CASSINI RSS RAW DATA SET - SROC21 V1.0','The Cassini Radio Science Saturn Ring and Atmospheric Occultation experiments (SROC21) Raw Data Archive is a time-ordered collection of radio science raw data acquired on June 6, and June 30, 2016, during the Cassini Extended Extended Mission.','public','2026-03-13T18:07:07.354861','2026-03-13T18:07:07.354866','Planetary Atmospheres','Planetary Data System','026:00','8d981f6e-ec7b-431d-a515-150e1a1b10b6','NASA Data.json','bb663d925c21e431641e443f6136d3f7fd953089f7fd7318e9a40a1e3ad6d521','1.1','2026-03-13T18:07:07.354861','2026-03-13T18:07:07.354866','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('4ad1d5f0-8b4b-4e54-b4a9-28f9f56abfe7','Images and segmentation annotations of cranberry fruit from a postharvest imaging platform','<p dir=\"ltr\">This data set provides the raw images and annotations from a postharvest berry imaging platform that was used to train an instance segmentation model. Downstream image processing of segmented berries measures the color, size, shape, and uniformity in a sample. Images were collected using a Nikon D7500 DSLR camera using manual shutter speed, focal length, f-stop, and ISO settings. The imaging platform was a custom-build LED lightbox and sample tray. The dataset contains 210 images with accompanying annotations in YOLOv8 format.</p>','public','2026-03-13T22:44:31.900010','2026-03-13T22:44:31.900016','Agricultural Research Service','Neyhart, Jeffrey L.','005:18','b321926b-425e-47dc-9845-e271ec913265','USDA JSON','42a5259db05ad3d178fcd0b619f4500e97209ae1185bd8035645d52416d18cd5','1.1','2026-03-13T22:44:31.900010','2026-03-13T22:44:31.900016',NULL,'005:040',0,'usda-gov'),('4aed2850-e8d7-4e65-af51-9524fd07d296','ROSETTA-ORBITER MARS OSINAC 2 MARS EDR V2.0','This CODMAC level 2 data set contains uncalibrated image data in DN unit,  acquired by the OSIRIS Narrow Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft  during the MARS SWING-BY mission phase, covering the period  from 2006-07-29T00:00:00.000 to 2007-05-28T23:59:59.000. The prime target is planet Mars. This version V2.0 supersedes previous deliveries of the same dataset with the following changes since the last version: Reprocessed dataset after October 2018 PSA/PDS external peer review.','public','2026-03-13T18:12:08.743041','2026-03-13T18:12:08.743045','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','b65c97d4-014c-4bd6-8671-8a3d6e6dac86','NASA Data.json','d236301d6b048cac5ebaba4a5f567fd3e808df414e6d48918796250dab13edbf','1.1','2026-03-13T18:12:08.743041','2026-03-13T18:12:08.743045','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('4aee9dc8-28ff-41ec-a00e-f6bdbb22b7e5','NEW HORIZONS      LORRI KEM2      RAW V1.0','This data set contains Raw data taken by      the New Horizons Long Range Reconnaissance Imager instrument during the      KEM1 ENCOUNTER and KEM2 CRUISE mission phases.      This is VERSION 1.0 of this data set.      This version includes data acquired by the spacecraft between      08/14/2018 and 04/30/2023. It only includes data downlinked before      05/01/2023 and after 04/30/2022. Future datasets may include more      data acquired by the spacecraft after 08/13/2018 but downlinked after      04/30/2023.      This dataset includes empty sky images near Arrokoth.','public','2026-03-13T18:27:58.259376','2026-03-13T18:27:58.259381','small bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','08e7fa94-2f4b-4230-a005-1986e75a6e84','NASA Data.json','2dee5e9cd4e9c6d8275909d3630b0b7f247d61ead3723dd3267eeecc18dfd734','1.1','2026-03-13T18:27:58.259376','2026-03-13T18:27:58.259381','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('4b0e3f95-56b5-4f91-a330-7ac5a3c395c7','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSINAC 4 ESC2-MTP016 RDR V2.0','This CODMAC level 4 data set contains radiometric calibrated and geometric distortion corrected (resampled) image data in W/m^2/sr/nm, acquired by the OSIRIS Narrow Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft during the COMET ESCORT 2 mission phase, covering the period from 2015-05-05T23:25:00.000 to 2015-06-02T23:24:59.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V2.0 supersedes previous deliveries of the same dataset with the following changes since the last version: Lien corrected dataset after October 2018 PSA/PDS external peer review. Updated documentation and ancillary files, added document on bandpass filter. Updated SCIENCE_USER_GUIDE_V03.PDF to include one section about FAQ and one section about image data quality. Added shutter backtravel and readout issues to image quality map. Updated DATA_QUALITY_ID keyword in image header. Improved handling of images with missing packets.','public','2026-03-13T16:48:07.684182','2026-03-13T16:48:07.684189','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','d7a70f54-ba7b-42de-8063-cf30b5e76505','NASA Data.json','46465a4755fb39a6cc709b9c24a00542b012bb3390ff94e130659400ac267f88','1.1','2026-03-13T16:48:07.684182','2026-03-13T16:48:07.684189','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('4b23dbf8-dbfd-404a-b2a7-28431383ac9d','MARS EXPRESS MARS MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 7 3977 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2019-01-01 to 2020-12-31. It is a Occultation measurement and covers the time 2019-03-15T09:45:56.299 to 2019-03-15T10:08:04.700.','public','2026-03-13T19:54:41.026394','2026-03-13T19:54:41.026400','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','5e6c6454-8222-490c-8903-2996507d3f04','NASA Data.json','803fbc7fb1fd3c0685afea9510bf55995c9af7a50512106486d7233b12243bc7','1.1','2026-03-13T19:54:41.026394','2026-03-13T19:54:41.026400','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('4b44abef-3332-4df6-bd54-408212f31dda','Eastern Gulf of Mexico Circulation Study','Phsyical Oceanographic Circulation Study','public','2026-03-26T19:17:55.556416','2026-03-26T19:17:55.556422',NULL,NULL,NULL,'6c359d65-7bd9-4066-963b-6baba80cac1e','ioos',NULL,NULL,'2026-03-26T19:17:55.556416','2026-03-26T19:17:55.556422',NULL,NULL,NULL,'noaa-gov'),('4b470c2e-1256-4e31-a8b9-5f3d0fb3fde9','MARS EXPRESS MARS MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 4 3494 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2013-01-01 to 2014-12-31. It is a Global Gravity measurement and covers the time 2013-01-09T08:07:47.000 to 2013-01-09T10:59:26.500.','public','2026-03-13T17:40:33.176850','2026-03-13T17:40:33.176856','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','a3c0943e-7889-4303-8720-7bc4fc2fcd7e','NASA Data.json','357ef23339f58a1246299644bd2d01fcc003b4a75ada260534cae0382ff8846d','1.1','2026-03-13T17:40:33.176850','2026-03-13T17:40:33.176856','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('4b634753-6809-4aa3-8b46-539539b99d3d','MESSENGER E/V/H MASCS 4 UVVS DERIVED DATA V1.0','Abstract : This data set consists of the MESSENGER MASCS UVVS derived data records, also known as DDRs. There are three types of UVVS DDRs: surface, atmosphere, and atmospheric model. There are two surface DDR data products associated with each UVVS observation set: a science header table and a science data table. There are nine geometry-classified atmosphere DDR data products, consisting of three different observation types for each of sodium (Na), calcium (Ca), and magnesium (Mg). There are three orbit-level summary atmosphere DDR data products, one each for Na, Ca, and Mg. There are 3 atmospheric model data products, one each for observations of Na, Ca, and Mg.','public','2026-03-13T19:23:13.748439','2026-03-13T19:23:13.748443','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','3b6ad3c8-db67-4fb1-aa51-19be2b765e69','NASA Data.json','96093e9bedb32ca343b903cbd930154a3acaca1668765c503f79cd7d6788d582','1.1','2026-03-13T19:23:13.748439','2026-03-13T19:23:13.748443','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('4b6ca1f3-0a2a-4e59-a375-cad527aa3e71','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 2 0636 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 2 phase 2015-03-11 to 2015-06-30. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-03-11T01:58:00.000 to 2015-03-11T09:25:33.000.','public','2026-03-13T18:48:59.001229','2026-03-13T18:48:59.001234','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','bb35318a-709b-49fb-96fb-ac13b4fa02ab','NASA Data.json','5aef43aede27260627e38483b5664b2a600de3a4f3f5f60a5c9fd72ab9d328ae','1.1','2026-03-13T18:48:59.001229','2026-03-13T18:48:59.001234','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('4bfcc0c8-db0d-41f2-8279-b9a146367a5f','MARS EXPRESS MARS MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 5 3867 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2015-01-01 to 2016-12-31. It is a Occultation measurement and covers the time 2016-12-06T01:07:01 to 2016-12-06T01:52:00.','public','2026-03-13T18:39:36.609712','2026-03-13T18:39:36.609717','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','42cfd49d-5998-48c9-bb8e-bfb40a2bc605','NASA Data.json','7051906b570d74d230a683508dd729d16c00b92182e6285c47c5c0d03c1a0aac','1.1','2026-03-13T18:39:36.609712','2026-03-13T18:39:36.609717','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('4c2383cc-61cd-4971-a830-c3a48702fb5e','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 4 1301 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 4 phase 2015-10-22 to 2015-12-31. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-12-31T01:38:40.000 to 2015-12-31T07:32:55.000.','public','2026-03-13T19:58:43.938339','2026-03-13T19:58:43.938345','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','0b3e5fcc-c28a-4edb-96cc-f61ec540de1e','NASA Data.json','3bba0da32262b996a3c0f3f454fe2cf1d2eb2b9e0c293a0c6e54b55db81d6909','1.1','2026-03-13T19:58:43.938339','2026-03-13T19:58:43.938345','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('4c283275-033a-4c59-bf0d-16ad32d80039','TEAMER: Two Stage Ocean Current Turbine Reduced Order Modeling','The Equinox Ocean Current turbine is a groundbreaking new two-stage turbine design, enabling cost effective power generation at low water velocities. The data included in this submission can be used to reproduce the figures provided in the corresponding Post Access Report. The provided script \"EquinoxFigures.ipynb\" calls the appropriate datasets and generates the figures. Normalized performance, thrust, and blade load data for the Equinox Ocean Turbines two-stage device are given, including for the main and secondary rotors operating in isolation, as well as for the combined rotor. Data from multiple levels of model fidelity are included. Calculated induction factors, inflow plane velocities, and induced velocities are given as well.\n\nThis project is part of the TEAMER RFTS 12 (request for technical support) program.','public','2026-03-31T14:23:22.841620','2026-03-31T14:23:22.841625','National Laboratory of the Rockies','Hannah Ross','019:20','0bc303ea-8e87-43f7-b97c-dca273133590','OpenEI data.json','2c5367a55390936471fd50f61dceed0f8ddeca771039bbde15c79fe5acd1b332','1.1','2026-03-31T14:23:22.841620','2026-03-31T14:23:22.841625',NULL,'019:009',0,'doe-gov'),('4c2c8a88-6df8-45e9-b440-e0d31794bc55','Data from: Bringing cross-validation into the real world to evaluate transferability of satellite-based vegetation models','<p dir=\"ltr\">This tabular dataset supports findings reported in \"Bringing cross-validation into the real world to evaluate transferability of satellite-based vegetation models\" published in <i>Scientific Reports</i>. Data are from the Central Plains Experimental Range (CPER), near Nunn, Colorado, and contains nearly 10,000 ground samples collected from 2014 to 2023. Data are aggregated to the plot level (n=2,322), of which there are 4-6 in each pasture and also provided at the transect level (n=9,647), of which there are 4 in each plot. Data were used to train progressively more complex Machine learning algorithms (MLAs) to predict standing aboveground herbaceous biomass in grazinglands, such as those found at CPER. These data support an investigation of whether (1) do simpler geospatial MLAs have better transferability to ‘unseen’ conditions and ‘worst-case’ performance (i.e., under extreme conditions) compared to more complex MLAs and (2) are they more consistent when re-trained with new data. Data include (1) unique identifiers and blocking co-variates (2) in-situ ground-sampled herbaceous standing biomass estimated using visual obstruction (VO) methods, along with the VO readings themselves (3) geographic polygon bounding coordinates of each plot/transect (WKT format), and (4) satellite-derived indices and bands from the Harmonized Landsat Sentinel (HLS) data product. All in situ values and satellite derived indices are means for the respective plot and transect areas.</p><p dir=\"ltr\">This research used resources provided by the SCINet project and/or the AI Center of Excellence of the USDA Agricultural Research Service, ARS project numbers 0201-88888-003-000D and 0201-88888-002-000D.</p>','public','2026-03-13T22:48:08.661006','2026-03-13T22:48:08.661013','Agricultural Research Service','Porensky, Lauren','005:18','7808a485-0988-47aa-bace-564c92ea58f5','USDA JSON','f62b89362c2decaf78dacce77843133b478fe256486bd8db7155559bf3cd818e','1.1','2026-03-13T22:48:08.661006','2026-03-13T22:48:08.661013','geospatial','005:040',0,'usda-gov'),('4c35f679-82d7-44c0-b2e2-28de6d2c5423','Laborshed - Fields of Study','Laborshed dataset that contains information about the fields of study of those in the survey who have an education beyond high school. The data covers all laborshed areas in Iowa.','public','2026-03-28T22:01:57.077494','2026-03-28T22:01:57.077499','data.iowa.gov','svqueen',NULL,'e03e6497-b0f2-4b69-99b6-5cfbbc0b99a7','Iowa metadata','eea5989de6a318d595ef81076bb0002c86ff11860a6e3cb8f95cb05f27561db5','1.1','2026-03-28T22:01:57.077494','2026-03-28T22:01:57.077499','Economic Statistics',NULL,0,'state-of-iowa'),('4c462f8a-227c-4e10-96ef-a00a3c9cc924','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 1 0582 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 1 phase 2014-11-20 to 2015-03-10. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-02-16T08:43:25.000 to 2015-02-16T12:30:10.000.','public','2026-03-13T19:19:59.907057','2026-03-13T19:19:59.907062','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','0cc070e5-e447-4322-b2c0-237ad1bc1dc1','NASA Data.json','515fe0bf03a8d18f31822ca7bcefd78dcdb350597ac083a02c30ea304f504a6c','1.1','2026-03-13T19:19:59.907057','2026-03-13T19:19:59.907062','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('4c4acfae-1b32-4d48-9b05-715865891595','MARS EXPRESS ASPERA-3 RAW EDR ION MASS ANALYZER EXT5 V1.0','This data set contains Mars Express ASPERA-3 Ion Mass         Analyzer (IMA) data for the fifth mission extension         (January 1, 2015 - December 31, 2016).  These data are         provided in raw units of counts/accumulation.','public','2026-03-13T17:49:01.778099','2026-03-13T17:49:01.778105','planetary plasma interactions','Planetary Data System','026:00','05b389c1-a001-4b62-8163-286324303440','NASA Data.json','ed4e0b576f41bd0782bb67d9c9cf97d9d4c4de0c97c455aa3814ff90a3ebef3d','1.1','2026-03-13T17:49:01.778099','2026-03-13T17:49:01.778105','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('4c5f040b-b0d1-4545-afb8-0ff47730af60','Foy Lake Data','The dataset comprises a high-resolution sediment record spanning 7000 years from Foy Lake (Montana, USA). Foy Lake, situated at 48.1648°N, 114.3589°W and 1005 meters above sea level, is a deep freshwater lake within the drought-prone Flathead River Basin in the northern Rocky Mountains. Researchers collected percent abundances of 109 diatom taxa from a continuous lake sediment core, sampled approximately every 5–20 years, resulting in an extensive 7000-year record captured over 763 time-steps. \n\nThis dataset is associated with the following publication:\nAngeler, D., T. Eason, A. Garmestani, and C. Allen. Data sonification offers a novel approach for communicating Earth’s tipping points.   Ecology and Society. Resilience Alliance Publications, Waterloo,  CANADA, 31(1): 28, (2026).','public','2026-03-15T10:22:49.893625','2026-03-15T10:22:49.893630','U.S. Environmental Protection Agency','Ahjond Garmestani','020:00','d5c14900-f720-4581-9c44-c0c924e2e6b0','EPA ScienceHub','473f699b759c0085ad41b109145b3e2e12a83077999a82bbba0f8bbb923d6b71','1.1','2026-03-15T10:22:49.893625','2026-03-15T10:22:49.893630',NULL,'020:000',0,'epa-gov'),('4c7855fc-4b91-47dd-9dd0-e54b481eb7ae','BLM ID Field Office Administrative Unit Boundary','<div style=\'text-align:Left;\'><div><div style=\'font-size:12pt\'><p><span>This data set shows the Idaho Bureau of Land Management (BLM) Field Office, District Office and State Office boundaries and names as per the three-tier organization initiated in February 2007. A Bureau of Land Management (BLM) Administrative Unit is a geographic area in which an organizational unit of the BLM has distinct jurisdictional responsibility for land and resource management activities occurring on the public lands, the maintained rights of the United States (i.e. mineral estate) and actions relating to the Trust responsibilities of the U.S. Government as stipulated in Law or Treaty.The State Office is the top layer of the three-tier organization, with District Offices being the middle layer and providing coordination, oversight and support to the lowest level, the Field Office. Idaho has one State Office, four Districts and twelve Field Offices. This feature class documents the physical boundary of an administrative unit. In some cases, the administrative unit may manage areas outside of the boundary for other programs’ purposes - this datset does not show these areas. BLM Idaho administers a little land in Nevada also, which is included here.    For more information contact us at blm_id_stateoffice@blm.gov.</span></p></div></div></div>','public','2026-03-18T11:12:36.526268','2026-03-18T11:12:36.526274','Bureau of Land Management','Bureau of Land Management, id_so_information','010:04','6bf119c6-9990-4543-b0ca-ea5eaca922e8','DOI BLM DCAT-US','05866d94b7283e2d7225d2c2cbbc358249e3e2fcc9f6856a93fe40aca0088ded','1.1','2026-03-18T11:12:36.526268','2026-03-18T11:12:36.526274','geospatial','010:000',0,'doi-gov'),('4ccba7d2-da86-4dd3-b4a3-86110c35c3ab','ROSETTA-LANDER 67P SESAME 2 SDL V1.0','This archive contains edited data (CODMAC level 2) from the SESAME instrument onboard ROSETTA Lander, acquired during the SDL phase. It also contains documentation which describes the SESAME experiment. The primary target is the comet 67P/CHURYUMOV-GERASIMENKO. The data archived in this data set conform to the Planetary Data System (PDS) Standards, Version 3.6.','public','2026-03-13T20:09:25.924229','2026-03-13T20:09:25.924235','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','a625deb7-c2cd-450b-98bb-fabc1a1bbed1','NASA Data.json','b9aa3c541f95d9f59d51471a430e0980d11e019fe46998636608cd157328aabc','1.1','2026-03-13T20:09:25.924229','2026-03-13T20:09:25.924235','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('4cea3883-064b-4d58-b00e-27e14ebeedf4','KECK II ESI IMAGES OF 81P/WILD 2','CCD images of comet 81P/Wild 2 taken 2003 December 19-21 UT with the ESI instrument on Keck II in support of the Stardust encounter.','public','2026-03-13T16:56:20.946252','2026-03-13T16:56:20.946257','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','b7972636-4cd9-400e-891d-98bb2deff816','NASA Data.json','844cc5cdcdc7b6ffef9d5e6ed13f789153bfad0b5f380553ada9fd3fd62ebbc7','1.1','2026-03-13T16:56:20.946252','2026-03-13T16:56:20.946257','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('4cffdb6b-092b-4840-827e-ae7609e88849','BLM ID Grazing Allotments','This feature class depicts the boundaries of the livestock grazing allotments under the jurisdiction of the Idaho Bureau of Land Management. A pasture is a sub-unit of a grazing allotment; each allotment is comprised of at least one pasture. An allotment is an area of land designated and managed for grazing of livestock. An allotment may include private and state lands, in addition to public lands under the jurisdiction of the Bureau of Land Management and/or other federal agencies. All allotments and pastures are recorded and tracked in BLM\'s Rangeland Administrative System (RAS). This GIS feature class provides a spatial component to pastures and allotments.  For more information contact us at blm_id_stateoffice@blm.gov.','public','2026-03-25T12:31:30.775165','2026-03-25T12:31:30.775172','Bureau of Land Management','Bureau of Land Management, id_so_information','010:04','f19e2f13-822f-466b-bc2d-d2ac2ac10e32','DOI BLM DCAT-US','0a2a2849f4bfce3b3b29f9c9ae69205671951b9ecdc71186749ecaea65080b68','1.1','2026-03-25T12:31:30.775165','2026-03-25T12:31:30.775172','geospatial','010:000',0,'doi-gov'),('4d139c52-1821-4fe5-a2a9-54efa0dd205d','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSIWAC 4 ESC2-MTP016 RDR V2.0','This CODMAC level 4 data set contains radiometric calibrated and geometric distortion corrected (resampled) image data in W/m^2/sr/nm, acquired by the OSIRIS Wide Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft during the COMET ESCORT 2 mission phase, covering the period from 2015-05-05T23:25:00.000 to 2015-06-02T23:24:59.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V2.0 supersedes previous deliveries of the same dataset with the following changes since the last version: Lien corrected dataset after October 2018 PSA/PDS external peer review. Updated documentation and ancillary files, added document on bandpass filter. Updated SCIENCE_USER_GUIDE_V03.PDF to include one section about FAQ and one section about image data quality. Added shutter backtravel and readout issues to image quality map. Updated DATA_QUALITY_ID keyword in image header. Improved handling of images with missing packets.','public','2026-03-13T16:58:59.171919','2026-03-13T16:58:59.171925','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','b51499b2-a97e-4dfc-b464-38b6e98274c4','NASA Data.json','9da2e54eae640646a0058c827dc4b39cb3cabf36677b3e76438f7c48cfba2960','1.1','2026-03-13T16:58:59.171919','2026-03-13T16:58:59.171925','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('4d3925e7-1e5e-4726-94d4-c5b91dbb242b','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 3 0943 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 3 phase 2015-07-01 to 2015-10-21. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-08-05T04:58:45.000 to 2015-08-05T09:52:32.500.','public','2026-03-13T17:21:54.666843','2026-03-13T17:21:54.666849','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','304e190d-2c5b-4a25-873d-9db355dcabe1','NASA Data.json','2ddf3323db94ce9c2d5b4c5c1479411c43c0fd120272d4b05325f165cba224fd','1.1','2026-03-13T17:21:54.666843','2026-03-13T17:21:54.666849','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('4d528c9f-c950-4c41-82f9-48422bf46fd6','MARS EXPRESS MARS MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 4 3587 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2013-01-01 to 2014-12-31. It is a Global Gravity measurement and covers the time 2013-06-13T00:14:04.000 to 2013-06-13T02:59:30.500.','public','2026-03-13T17:43:36.137926','2026-03-13T17:43:36.137935','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','fb7f74e2-fe8b-4ed1-ba6f-d78e39a6f8c8','NASA Data.json','73083dea7e567d6dd7a09bfac97acb2f6337091de8f6fac420836bc1b4f28439','1.1','2026-03-13T17:43:36.137926','2026-03-13T17:43:36.137935','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('4d595ace-724d-45a8-b824-359f763843cf','FAST Eddy Sys 3  Transect 3, 150kHz kHz VMADCP','Program of vessel mount ADCP measurements comprising a combination of 75kHz and 150kHz ADCP data collected in the vicinity of the Loop Current and drilling blocks between 2009 and 2020.','public','2026-03-26T19:15:11.442667','2026-03-26T19:15:11.442676',NULL,NULL,NULL,'9bc8f096-756c-4828-8ebc-ad9a46be371c','ioos',NULL,NULL,'2026-03-26T19:15:11.442667','2026-03-26T19:15:11.442676',NULL,NULL,NULL,'noaa-gov'),('4d5d80a0-6ba3-4fa5-a421-35c4d38e45c7','ROSETTA-ORBITER COMET ESCORT OSINAC 2 EDR MTP 014 V1.0','This data set contains raw EDR images acquired by the OSIRIS Narrow AngleCamera during the escort phase of the Rosetta mission at the comet 67P,covering the period from 2015-03-10 to 2015-04-08.','public','2026-03-13T18:21:36.912282','2026-03-13T18:21:36.912287','Small Bodies','Earthdata Forum','026:00','3f5123af-180d-40e0-920a-b97c7ca06a16','NASA Data.json','056e7ac9441e6bb2d1424ecf5b40020071731814cf7f25ad8c285a4e49da9951','1.1','2026-03-13T18:21:36.912282','2026-03-13T18:21:36.912287','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('4d69622e-c319-4d81-985a-e9489df0c83a','MARS EXPRESS MARS MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 3 3368 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2010-01-01 to 2012-12-31. It is a Global Gravity measurement and covers the time 2012-10-20T02:54:01.000 to 2012-10-20T06:50:54.500.','public','2026-03-13T16:38:12.159327','2026-03-13T16:38:12.159336','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','3c8fb1e1-2427-4d32-b0f4-35813222a589','NASA Data.json','e55bcde2a6227b6932cc3bb70eb0feae4dff8f2083a9a3ae95556e1407a7f1e3','1.1','2026-03-13T16:38:12.159327','2026-03-13T16:38:12.159336','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('4d7ead38-aa2e-41e0-8afd-a4737e52fab4','24-COLOR ASTEROID SURVEY','This dataset is comprised of asteroid flux data measured in 26 filters using the McCord dual beam photometer, and covering the range 0.32 - 1.08 microns for 285 numbered asteroids, as published in Chapman & Gaffey (1979b) and McFadden, et al. (1984).','public','2026-03-13T18:03:46.541083','2026-03-13T18:03:46.541089','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','8343d0c7-7415-463f-a47e-27d3bd32215a','NASA Data.json','edd863050d9a2ff22c0185496d219c19f58902f54532a5bbafdd816d35798a65','1.1','2026-03-13T18:03:46.541083','2026-03-13T18:03:46.541089','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('4d980d7f-6f78-4356-90ba-078e5cbb2ab1','HPMS Roadway Sample 2024','State DOTs provide the Highway Performance Monitoring System (HPMS) with the location limits of highway sections used to represent statewide aggregations based on a statistically valid Sample Panel.','public','2026-03-28T13:33:46.860877','2026-03-28T13:33:46.860881','Federal Highway Administration','Office of Highway Policy Information','021:15','4b80c869-3760-46f4-a4b1-4433d0efb1fd','DOT Socrata Data.json','5f89b4c21f3b36e9f570b5fdcee738179ba0e73291b3221a2a22338a0f6975f3','1.1','2026-03-28T13:33:46.860877','2026-03-28T13:33:46.860881','Roadways and Bridges','021:009',0,'dot-gov'),('4daef352-198d-480e-b70c-ac9451f7f6fb','Hospital Utilization Trends','The datasets provide medical encounter counts across three hospital settings (Inpatient Discharges, Emergency Department visits, and Ambulatory Surgery). The data is categorized by healthcare system and facility, and further grouped by common health conditions (including anxiety, asthma, behavioral syndromes, cancer, cardiac arrest, chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD), COVID-19, depression, diabetes, homelessness, hypertension, mood disorders excluding depression, non-mood psychotic disorders, nonpsychotic disorders excluding anxiety, obesity, pneumonia, respiratory arrest/failure, sepsis, stroke, substance use disorders, and unspecified mental disorders), as well as demographic characteristics such as age group, race/ethnicity, assigned sex at birth, and expected payer.','public','2026-03-23T13:59:56.231677','2026-03-23T13:59:56.231682','Department of Health Care Access and Information','Department of Health Care Access and Information, Healthcare Analytics Branch',NULL,'c36a381c-9ecc-4511-b15e-85ba054cf145','State of California','1c5d144258f6998b8ac3132329c1f614b599cf096c2dc016996a8d7af4b0ff49','1.1','2026-03-23T13:59:56.231677','2026-03-23T13:59:56.231682','COVID-19',NULL,0,'ca-gov'),('4db1950e-f7c1-40b1-85e0-2720bbcfc8ee','MARS EXPRESS MARS MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 3 3358 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2010-01-01 to 2012-12-31. It is a Global Gravity measurement and covers the time 2012-09-21T07:32:19.000 to 2012-09-21T11:26:54.500.','public','2026-03-13T17:05:20.748507','2026-03-13T17:05:20.748512','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','f550310f-face-47fe-bf11-b00f1c59f0c9','NASA Data.json','d37003ff86d38a28f78d52024ad3a628d6d7d80363b386fb64a66fe7fe25a52b','1.1','2026-03-13T17:05:20.748507','2026-03-13T17:05:20.748512','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('4dd762cb-94c3-42c4-aaeb-658817bddd8e','Continuous Fixed Station Water Quality Measurements in Canaveral National Seashore, November 2005 (Certified)','This dataset represents continuous water quality measurements that were taken at a fixed point in Canaveral National Seashore during the month of November, 2005 as a part of the Fixed Station Water Quality Monitoring protocol that was developed by the Southeast Coast I&M Network (SECN). The measurements were taken by a YSI 6600 ESD Multi-Parameter Long Term Water Quality Monitoring Datasonde unit that serves as the standard fixed station water quality monitoring equipment for all similar operations conducted by the SECN. The following parameters were measured at 30 minute intervals during the time period that has been specified: Water Temperature, Specific Conductivity, Salinity, Dissolved Oxygen (DO), DO Concentration, Shallow Depth, pH Level, and Turbidity. Any anomalies noted regarding these parameters have also been noted in separate fields. Please note that these measurements have been certified by network personnel.','public','2026-03-26T05:29:14.696639','2026-03-26T05:29:14.696644','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','40c712b3-fdb4-4157-87e9-dbe489aac0fb','DOI NPS DCAT-US','b8ccb3f0afd8049ccd49837e4158cb1d7338d241b532305772e99ffbce662c97','1.1','2026-03-26T05:29:14.696639','2026-03-26T05:29:14.696644','Vector Dataset','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('4dd8d0d4-7d5e-4678-bbb5-d9258918c3e3','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 PRELANDING 0212 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the PRELANDING phase 2014-01-21 to 2014-11-18. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2014-08-16T13:37:05.000 to 2014-08-16T18:57:01.000.','public','2026-03-13T20:06:34.653029','2026-03-13T20:06:34.653037','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','b2a764b4-8523-4bd2-b55a-d810de5cba82','NASA Data.json','c0751a2a381f9abf2f8f3d4502c130ade031372213c9b15077b146a7e2644152','1.1','2026-03-13T20:06:34.653029','2026-03-13T20:06:34.653037','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('4e046518-e541-401a-ae67-82e659f69ee6','Data from: Metabolic plasticity of Mormon cricket Anabrus simplex eggs in three developmental stages','<p dir=\"ltr\">Many organisms have evolved means of dealing with dry periods, including surviving as seeds or eggs beneath the soil. Suppression of metabolism during developmental arrest is one means by which insects reduce maintenance costs and await more favorable conditions. Mormon crickets have a complex lifecycle that can endure more than 10 years with three potential stages for arrested development: prior to initiation of embryogenesis, when the embryo is half grown, and an obligate arrest when the embryo fills the egg. Using an experimental design of two incubating temperature treatments and two moisture levels, I examined whether Mormon crickets reduce their metabolic rate in response to drought to conserve water in these three stages of arrested development.</p><p dir=\"ltr\">Eggs from individual females were kept separate, and sixteen eggs per female were separated evenly into two incubating temperature programs: one averaging 24°C at which embryonic development typically proceeds to the ultimate diapause stage (stage 23), and one averaging 28°C at which embryonic development typically arrests at the penultimate diapause stage (stage 19). The eight eggs in each temperature treatment were separated evenly into two humidity treatments (dry and saturated air). In preliminary results, these two moisture treatments resulted in a broad range of changes in egg mass: those housed in a desiccation chamber lost 10% of initial mass, on average, whereas those housed in saturated air gained 15% of initial mass, on average.</p><p dir=\"ltr\">After 11 weeks of incubation, the eggs were removed from their respective treatments, brushed to remove any sand, weighed, examined under a dissecting scope for development, and placed in a closed metabolic chamber. The metabolic chamber comprised a 5 ml syringe with a three-way stopcock that was flushed with dry, CO<sub>2</sub>-free air for 5 min at 500 ml per min prior to closing to 4 ml volume. After approximately 24 h at room temperature (23.5±0.5°C), 3 ml of air from the chamber was plunged steadily into a Tygon hose with dry, CO<sub>2</sub>-free air flowing at 100 ml per min, which passed through a syringe of magnesium perchlorite to dry the air sample, and then into a FoxBox Respirometry System (Sable Systems, Las Vegas, Nevada) connected to a laptop computer, which recorded the total CO<sub>2</sub> respired by the egg during the time the chamber was closed. An empty chamber treated the same way served as a control. Total CO<sub>2</sub> was adjusted by time the chamber was closed and CO<sub>2</sub> that leaked into the control chamber during the same time period was subtracted. Respiration (in ml CO<sub>2</sub>/h) was divided by egg mass on the day metabolic measurement was initiated to yield ml CO<sub>2</sub>/h/g. Egg development was checked again after 18 weeks incubation (7 weeks later) and any changes in development stage were noted.</p><p dir=\"ltr\">Data are divided into separate text files based on the egg stage at which respirometry was measured. Developmental stages 18, 19, 20, 21, and 23 were observed with a standard dissecting scope. No visible development refers to those eggs that were assumed to be in stage 4 (the stage for egg diapause), which was verified with lack of visible development 7 weeks later. See the readme file for an explanation of column headings.</p>','public','2026-03-13T22:48:44.757445','2026-03-13T22:48:44.757451','Agricultural Research Service','Srygley, Robert B.','005:18','31e4e914-dda6-42cb-8e42-8c0c6f7fd330','USDA JSON','68068b833a76554a2629bc0497dc17f73a99f34dc0ecd3dd10348561a30e91c7','1.1','2026-03-13T22:48:44.757445','2026-03-13T22:48:44.757451','geospatial','005:040',0,'usda-gov'),('4e287018-b87b-473a-8817-5a4dbaee19b3','BLM ID Range Improvement Point','This geodatabase of point, line and polygon features is an effort to consolidate all of the range improvement locations on BLM-managed land in Idaho into one database. Currently, the point feature class has some data for all of the BLM field offices except the Coeur d\'Alene and Cottonwood field offices. Range improvements are structures intended to enhance rangeland resources, including wildlife, watershed, and livestock management. Examples of range improvements include water troughs, spring headboxes, culverts, fences, water pipelines, gates, wildlife guzzlers, artificial nest structures, reservoirs, developed springs, corrals, exclosures, etc. These structures were first tracked by the Bureau of Land Management (BLM) in the Job Documentation Report (JDR) System in the early 1960s, which was predominately a paper-based tracking system. In 1988 the JDRs were migrated into and replaced by the automated Range Improvement Project System (RIPS), and version 2.0 is currently being used today. It tracks inventory, status, objectives, treatment, maintenance cycle, maintenance inspection, monetary contributions and reporting. Not all range improvements are documented in the RIPS database; there may be some older range improvements that were built before the JDR tracking system was established. There also may be unauthorized projects that are not in RIPS. Official project files of paper maps, reports, NEPA documents, checklists, etc., document the status of each project and are physically kept in the office with management authority for that project area. In addition, project data is entered into the RIPS system to enable managers to access the data to track progress, run reports, analyze the data, etc. Before Geographic Information System technology most offices kept paper atlases or overlay systems that mapped the locations of the range improvements. The objective of this geodatabase is to migrate the location of historic range improvement projects into a GIS for geospatial use with other data and to centralize the range improvement data for the state. This data set is a work in progress and does not have all range improvement projects that are on BLM lands. Some field offices have not migrated their data into this database, and others are partially completed. New projects may have been built but have not been entered into the system. Historic or unauthorized projects may not have case files and are being mapped and documented as they are found. Many field offices are trying to verify the locations and status of range improvements with GPS, and locations may change or projects that have been abandoned or removed on the ground may be deleted. Attributes may be incomplete or inaccurate. This data was created using the standard for range improvements set forth in Idaho IM 2009-044, dated 6/30/2009. However, it does not have all of the fields the standard requires. Fields that are missing from the point feature class that are in the standard are: ALLOT_NO, MGMT_AGCY, ADMIN_ST, ADMIN_OFF, SRCE_AGCY, MAX_PDOP, MAX_HDOP, CORR_TYPE, RCVR_TYPE, GPS_TIME, UPDATE_STA, UNFILT_POS, FILT_POS, DATA_DICTI, GPS_HEIGHT, VERT_PREC, HORZ_PREC, and CONF_LEVEL. Several additional fields have been added that are not part of the standard: wrpt_idwrn, bird_laddr, and year_checked. There is no National BLM standard for GIS range improvement data at this time. For more information contact us at blm_id_stateoffice@blm.gov.','public','2026-03-24T12:06:03.555742','2026-03-24T12:06:03.555747','Bureau of Land Management','Bureau of Land Management, id_so_information','010:04','b98eaca7-f492-46e7-b447-0dc4dcede4ca','DOI BLM DCAT-US','34ee39f2a245a1c605606510817e2de347306d4d01f89ac0c6b12ccfef19d606','1.1','2026-03-24T12:06:03.555742','2026-03-24T12:06:03.555747','geospatial','010:000',0,'doi-gov'),('4e2e8b8c-7847-44a7-81d8-5ba2b7072a9d','DAWN GRAND MAP CERES IRON MAP V1.0','A global map of the  concentration of iron within the regolith of asteroid 1 Ceres  on twenty-degree quasi-equal-area pixels is provided. Iron  concentrations were determined from gamma ray counting data acquired  by Dawn\'s Gamma Ray and Neutron Detector (GRaND) in a low altitude  mapping orbit, about 385 km from Ceres\' surface (about 0.8 body radii  altitude). The concentrations are representative of Ceres\'s bulk  regolith to depths up to a few decimeters with a spatial resolution  of about 600-km full-width-at-half-maximum of arc length on the  surface. The methods used to determine iron concentration are  described by PRETTYMANETAL2017.','public','2026-03-13T18:13:36.316065','2026-03-13T18:13:36.316071','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','c507507c-024e-4199-b158-9f632a9c6727','NASA Data.json','22d32e838970b2987ace475480ff7c37720d1a686e75264b60aecd3b62b450fe','1.1','2026-03-13T18:13:36.316065','2026-03-13T18:13:36.316071','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('4e54218f-1dec-43fe-9a96-61e06236a8bd','ROSETTA-ORBITER MARS OSIWAC 4 MARS RDR V1.0','This CODMAC level 4 data set contains radiometric calibrated and geometric distortion corrected (resampled) image data in W/m^2/sr/nm,  acquired by the OSIRIS Wide Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft  during the MARS SWING-BY mission phase, covering the period  from 2006-07-29T00:00:00.000 to 2007-05-28T23:59:59.000. The prime target is planet Mars. This version V1.0 is the first version of this dataset.','public','2026-03-13T16:51:00.759472','2026-03-13T16:51:00.759477','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','7a1ceb63-b5d8-4575-bf49-59a82db88f04','NASA Data.json','9e405642a349a9e2c1c911b9006219a8b6c417076e486e568e345243d8ec5ef5','1.1','2026-03-13T16:51:00.759472','2026-03-13T16:51:00.759477','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('4e8714d3-c56c-4fca-bcf9-4e916dfffd66','Okeanos Explorer (EX1607): CAPSTONE Wake Island PRI MNM							(Mapping)','Operations will include 24 hour/day mapping operations using\n					the shipâs deep water mapping systems (Kongsberg EM302 multibeam sonar, EK60\n					split-beam fisheries sonars, ADCPs, and Knudsen 3260 chirp sub-bottom profiler\n					sonar), CTD rosette, and the shipâs high-bandwidth satellite connection for\n					real-time ship to shore communications. Operations for this cruise will include\n					24 hour mapping, and continuous telepresence-based remote participation in\n					mapping operations. Multibeam and singlebeam mapping operations will be\n					conducted 24 hours a day throughout the cruise. Sub-bottom profile mapping will\n					be conducted 24 hours a day at the discretion of the CO. XBT sound velocity\n					casts in support of multibeam sonar mapping operations will be conducted at an\n					interval defined by prevailing oceanographic conditions, but not to exceed 6\n					hours.','public','2026-03-28T23:17:09.376455','2026-03-28T23:17:09.376464',NULL,NULL,NULL,'3642336d-705d-497f-807d-b5969e30a4d3','NCDDC OER',NULL,NULL,'2026-03-28T23:17:09.376455','2026-03-28T23:17:09.376464',NULL,NULL,NULL,'noaa-gov'),('4ea05752-326b-47f4-a6d3-c32290b9c390','HPMS Roadway Sample 2021','State DOTs provide the Highway Performance Monitoring System (HPMS) with the location limits of highway sections used to represent statewide aggregations based on a statistically valid Sample Panel.','public','2026-03-28T13:34:51.844050','2026-03-28T13:34:51.844055','Federal Highway Administration','Office of Highway Policy Information','021:15','22bbf4a0-8f29-4b3c-8481-522582e17947','DOT Socrata Data.json','e72f58b2abb8cf14d2274e632b8c477bd032ce44aa5747a9f157b65162b90f2a','1.1','2026-03-28T13:34:51.844050','2026-03-28T13:34:51.844055','Roadways and Bridges','021:009',0,'dot-gov'),('4eba2532-d3d7-46ef-9d70-a1c6599a548f','myUSCIS - My Profile','The profile section of the authenticated myUSCIS account allows applicants and representatives to create and update their profile information. The profile data is stored in the appropriate Case Management System DB (ELIS, Claims 3, global) via the Profile Manager Service.','restricted public','2026-03-22T11:52:10.736368','2026-03-22T11:52:10.736373','Unspecified','Open Data (MGMT)','024:030','980c0585-a7b5-4798-828b-32c17a893a0f','DHS datajson source','8b198adbf96aab8c762d534fde79c2d4b18090352cf2b5e9340e3daa61362708','1.1','2026-03-22T11:52:10.736368','2026-03-22T11:52:10.736373',NULL,'024:000',0,'dhs-gov'),('4ed5df71-a03d-4cb4-8016-36a39e621441','MetaData_2025-01-27_Inhibition-of-Fin-Regeneration-in-Fathead-Minnow-(Pimephales-promelas)-by-a-Potent-Synthetic-Glucocorticoid-and-Development-of-Adverse-Outcome-Pathway-334','Metadata for both preliminary and definitive studies, including water quality parameters, experimental takedown data, fin measurements, and RT-PCR data. \n\nThis dataset is associated with the following publication:\nCole, A., G. Ankley, J. Cavallin, J. Collins, K. Jensen, M. Kahl, A. Kasparek, B.R. Kwon, Y. Shmaitelly, L. Langan, D. Villeneuve, and B. Brooks. Inhibition of Fin Regeneration in Fathead Minnow (Pimephales promelas) by a Potent Synthetic Glucocorticoid, and Development of Adverse Outcome Pathway 334.   ENVIRONMENTAL SCIENCE & TECHNOLOGY. American Chemical Society, Washington, DC, USA, 59(19): 9497-9506, (2025).','public','2026-03-28T13:39:46.796282','2026-03-28T13:39:46.796287','U.S. Environmental Protection Agency','Alexander Cole','020:00','7b76359f-2f1c-4574-aa3b-0b2f604ec7dc','EPA ScienceHub','8eebc0e108d39246fd560326addaf3cfca87a24fd04ecd9cd971de5c687626c3','1.1','2026-03-28T13:39:46.796282','2026-03-28T13:39:46.796287',NULL,'020:000',0,'epa-gov'),('4edd98ea-4deb-488c-9d7e-ceafda9d29ea','ROSETTA-ORBITER CHECKOUT OSIWAC 4 CR4A RDR V1.0','This CODMAC level 4 data set contains radiometric calibrated and geometric distortion corrected (resampled) image data in W/m^2/sr/nm,  acquired by the OSIRIS Wide Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft  during the CRUISE 4-1 mission phase, covering the period  from 2008-01-28T00:00:00.000 to 2008-08-03T23:59:59.000. The prime objective was commissioning / calibration. Several targets of opportunity were observed, but none of them is identifiable as prime target. This version V1.0 is the first version of this dataset.','public','2026-03-13T16:52:50.118799','2026-03-13T16:52:50.118804','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','da251dbb-6e1d-4d23-ac5f-a13c7d43144d','NASA Data.json','aaf2c475b8fe25d2c55fc353ace7dfe90ce3cca42549a32ec8a8b70a164c2395','1.1','2026-03-13T16:52:50.118799','2026-03-13T16:52:50.118804','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('4f08f00e-74ee-49ff-83df-847f01847355','MARS EXPRESS MARS MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 3 3279 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2010-01-01 to 2012-12-31. It is a Global Gravity measurement and covers the time 2012-05-06T11:43:19.000 to 2012-05-06T16:03:49.500.','public','2026-03-13T16:45:09.278826','2026-03-13T16:45:09.278834','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','1ad02ced-b09a-4542-8182-56475f265adc','NASA Data.json','058f7079ea65b62f7294e27288b367a4a06c59af0637c7b79f0ce6d3cdc205c3','1.1','2026-03-13T16:45:09.278826','2026-03-13T16:45:09.278834','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('4f0e7dd9-759c-49b5-b1d4-8141293eee37','SCATHA Science Full Resolution Data','SCATHA Science Full Resolution Data','public','2026-03-13T22:43:36.386698','2026-03-13T22:43:36.386705','The Virtual Radiation Belt Observatory Data Repository','NASA Space Physics Data Facility','026:00','444c39ee-7695-40bc-8c86-8539b795f56a','NASA Data.json','7ce2ca7ce1d6c07afae7e0a4cabb866ae26a8df740f01be339d5c3a4553e09ff','1.1','2026-03-13T22:43:36.386698','2026-03-13T22:43:36.386705','Heliophysics','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('4f13ecbf-8fc5-4970-aba7-4279d7479a4b','Ordinance 20140130-038','Ordinance 20140130-038','public','2026-03-25T14:33:53.303167','2026-03-25T14:33:53.303174','data.austintexas.gov','Haileigh.Meyers@austintexas.gov',NULL,'510270f0-72e5-4dd8-8393-cf1d5c4d46c4','City of Austin Data.json','b9f81a39d0e64cd994ebb5ddd5952c682ad4566b6918ad074a49982e20e02313','1.1','2026-03-25T14:33:53.303167','2026-03-25T14:33:53.303174',NULL,NULL,0,'city-of-austin'),('4f16f07f-61ae-41d6-803e-b9b2eacec49e','Continuous Fixed Station Water Quality Measurements in Canaveral National Seashore, March 2008 (Certified)','This dataset represents continuous water quality measurements that were taken at a fixed point in Canaveral National Seashore during the month of March, 2008 as a part of the Fixed Station Water Quality Monitoring protocol that was developed by the Southeast Coast I&M Network (SECN). The measurements were taken by a YSI 6600 ESD Multi-Parameter Long Term Water Quality Monitoring Datasonde unit that serves as the standard fixed station water quality monitoring equipment for all similar operations conducted by the SECN. The following parameters were measured at 30 minute intervals during the time period that has been specified: Water Temperature, Specific Conductivity, Salinity, Dissolved Oxygen (DO), DO Concentration, Shallow Depth, pH Level, and Turbidity. Any anomalies noted regarding these parameters have also been noted in separate fields. Please note that these measurements have been certified by network personnel.','public','2026-03-26T05:31:27.729232','2026-03-26T05:31:27.729237','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','a5f976fb-32b1-4975-84e1-7d6f11d6bbe8','DOI NPS DCAT-US','47342d7a4b401bac39b85d7ac69ce1d356bea29f50a73821afa173a55be1a5cf','1.1','2026-03-26T05:31:27.729232','2026-03-26T05:31:27.729237','Vector Dataset','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('4f26df98-f169-4775-9a5a-5f9b5a4a8956','Nitrogen Screening Project - N Sources','This geodatabase includes NH3 (as N) and NOx (as N) emissions data for point sources as well as Total N emissions as represented in the 2002 National Emissions Inventory (NEI) database.','public','2026-03-26T05:35:03.635317','2026-03-26T05:35:03.635324','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','319ecee7-6b0d-4cdd-968d-1049532102f8','DOI NPS DCAT-US','fed00f9a34c10a6fd36435ff675da58af07ad3ffa06b4e038fd24d7fcb7f11cd','1.1','2026-03-26T05:35:03.635317','2026-03-26T05:35:03.635324','geospatial','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('4f4b2249-b1eb-4916-a21e-502fbb9dfe53','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 3 0961 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 3 phase 2015-07-01 to 2015-10-21. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-08-14T10:12:50.000 to 2015-08-14T17:28:23.500.','public','2026-03-13T19:04:24.869019','2026-03-13T19:04:24.869025','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','d237631b-b8cf-412b-aa5a-250b64611db3','NASA Data.json','f715ddbfa5ed07f744ac36ec00016513449a99fbccbb5465ae47166013fdf8b5','1.1','2026-03-13T19:04:24.869019','2026-03-13T19:04:24.869025','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('4f669bcd-1341-490c-a5c5-cae5ca17e986','HPMS Roadway Events Data 2024','Roadway attributes datasets in the Highway Performance Monitoring System (HPMS) consist of three separate tables: the Road Designations Table, the Road Identifications Table, and the Road Events Table. The Roads Event Table data items include Inventory, Lanes, Intersections, Traffic, Control, Pavement, Terrain, and Travel Time Code.','public','2026-03-28T13:33:03.808151','2026-03-28T13:33:03.808154','Federal Highway Administration','Office of Highway Policy Information','021:15','f57172ca-8bb7-4052-a145-580f2e19c592','DOT Socrata Data.json','3e4e865a20589ebe5fd34b18e61a6a5b7514ff1fe74aae00a73245b245b73b94','1.1','2026-03-28T13:33:03.808151','2026-03-28T13:33:03.808154','Roadways and Bridges','021:009',0,'dot-gov'),('4f82196f-7b43-40d9-bc12-b778b550915b','Newberry Volcano Joint Active-Source and Teleseismic P-Wave Tomography Slowness Model and Processing Code','This dataset contains a three-dimensional seismic slowness model and MATLAB processing code derived from P-wave seismic data collected at Newberry Volcano in central Oregon. The associated study combines active-source first-arrival travel times with teleseismic P-wave delay times to jointly image upper-crustal velocity structure beneath the volcano (targeting the shallow crust to ~10 km depth).\n\nThe included workflow uses a one-dimensional velocity model and a three-dimensional slowness model to compute a fractional velocity perturbation (dv/v) volume and to plot horizontal slices and vertical sections. The script reads the 1D model, interpolates it onto the depth grid of the 3D model, converts the 1D velocity profile to slowness, and then forms dv/v by comparing the 1D slowness volume to the 3D slowness model before plotting results. A python version of the workflow is also included, which was used to create the provided 3D model grid CSV files.\n\nThese data have been used by and uploaded to the Geothermal Data Repository (GDR) as part of the DE-risking Exploration of geothermal Plays in magmatic ENvironments (DEEPEN) project. The data were originally produced through the 2008 Newberry Seismic Experiment, funded by a USGS Venture Capital grant and NSF grants (EAR-207670 and EAR-207671). Seismic data from the 2008 experiment and from earlier 1983 and 1984 USGS experiments are archived at the IRIS DMC. Please refer to the associated manuscript (linked below) for additional details on the original data collection and research acknowledgements.','public','2026-03-21T11:55:57.652265','2026-03-21T11:55:57.652270','University of Oregon','Emilie Hooft','019:20','85149fe2-169d-4cac-8552-e998fe08afc2','OpenEI data.json','7f7443cc084bedc0dad14795e0203b9f6fba5b7e2a33a3337497ba2ae29fa6d9','1.1','2026-03-21T11:55:57.652265','2026-03-21T11:55:57.652270',NULL,'019:006',0,'doe-gov'),('4f8fad37-aa88-42a5-9e58-0a71a8161cc4','PVO VENUS MAG CALIBRATED S/C COORDINATES HIGH RES V2.0','This dataset contains vectors collected by the Pioneer Venus Orbiter (previously Pioneer 12) Magnetometer. The data are provided in spacecraft coordinates. In one format, apoapsis B, the magnetometer can be commanded to return 3 vectors per minor frame. In most others it transmits one vector per minor frame. In one format, periapsis E, it has no words in a minor frame. At very low sampling rates at which time the sine wave due to spacecraft spin could not be resolved. The magnetometer values are despun, and averaged on board using a Walsh transform (square wave) in phase and in quadiatune with the sun.','public','2026-03-13T18:26:25.056015','2026-03-13T18:26:25.056021','Planetary Plasma Interactions','Planetary Data System','026:00','62c829e0-c732-4fa0-b325-d71c0b53c1e9','NASA Data.json','6b5e50387550bb2828787c1e8689b88a4505a34f15ba8762083fd9244a1ca2d4','1.1','2026-03-13T18:26:25.056015','2026-03-13T18:26:25.056021','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('4fa5e09b-b8e8-430c-b9ac-b528b8c89b86','MARS EXPRESS SUN MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 4 3488 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2013-01-01 to 2014-12-31. It is a Solar Conjunction measurement and covers the time 2013-03-25T05:53:15.000 to 2013-03-25T09:15:25.500.','public','2026-03-13T19:37:44.263834','2026-03-13T19:37:44.263841','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','f853e38f-024d-4d94-83f9-a13d785e0fdf','NASA Data.json','8b6d532523f586e2afe6139a2412c5ed454531647d41806446631c8daa331858','1.1','2026-03-13T19:37:44.263834','2026-03-13T19:37:44.263841','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('4fc45c06-2a61-4212-85cd-1840899d8160','DEEP IMPACT 9P/TEMPEL ENCOUNTER - REDUCED MRI IMAGES V3.0','This dataset contains calibrated images of comet 9P/Tempel 1 acquired by the Medium Resolution Instrument Visible CCD (MRI) from 01 May through 06 July 2005 during the encounter phase of the Deep Impact mission. Version 3.0 was calibrated by the EPOXI mission pipeline and includes corrected observation times with a maximum difference of about 40 milliseconds, a change to decompress the camera\'s zero-DN lookup table entry to the top of its range and flag the affected pixels as saturated, the replacement of the I-over-F data products by multiplicative constants for converting radiance products to I-over-F, and the application of a horizontal destriping process and improved absolute radiometric calibration constants.','public','2026-03-13T17:13:06.141353','2026-03-13T17:13:06.141359','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','5ed0b1cf-0f36-48d9-a0de-04b8070f8b55','NASA Data.json','177e7cabfe36ee466d0dc08136a0f4b5295a7bc13e12bc05e7d94a89df9932f2','1.1','2026-03-13T17:13:06.141353','2026-03-13T17:13:06.141359','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('4ff9efe9-5af3-4025-8278-4c7c15b39fdb','Dataset: Density-dependent behaviors shape spatial redistribution of mountain ungulate abundance after a population die-off','Data and R code herein was involved in the analytical work associated with the following abstract from the Landscape Ecology manuscript entitled \"Density-dependent behaviors shape spatial redistribution of mountain ungulate abundance after a population die-off\":\n\nContext\nDensity dependence can affect patterns of animal abundance and interact with environmental disturbances. Resource restrictions from environmental disturbances may increase competition to cause population die-offs, after which competition may decrease. For group-forming prey species, theory suggests reduced competition enables changes in density-dependent group formation and habitat selection. Because resources and environmental disturbances are heterogeneously dispersed in space, subsequent density-dependent behavioral shifts may be heterogeneous and drive spatial patterns of populations after die-offs.\n\nObjectives\nWe sought to: (1) assess density-dependent behavioral changes in group size and habitat selection before and after a die-off, and (2) explore the role of objective 1 on the spatial redistribution of population abundance after a die-off.\n\nMethods\nWe used a 15-year dataset on Dall’s sheep (Ovis dalli) within the Brooks Range in Alaska, USA. We fitted a joint hierarchical distance sampling model with posterior sampling via Markov chain Monte Carlo to track changes in group size, habitat selection, and spatial abundance.\n\nResults\nAfter a die-off (> 50% population reduction), we documented 62% and 33% increases in sizes of nursery and adult-only groups, respectively. Nursery-group occurrence was concentrated at higher elevations after the die-off, as predicted, and declined in areas with prolonged snow cover. Sheep abundance within nursery groups declined in areas with late snowmelt, while declines in sheep within adult groups were more homogeneous.\n\nConclusions\nSpatial heterogeneity of resources and environmental disturbances can interact in a density-dependent fashion to affect behavioral changes that shape spatial redistributions of populations after die-offs. Our findings support interactions between density-dependent theories on habitat selection and group formation and highlight a smaller core area that appears critical for sheep conservation after die-offs.','public','2026-03-28T05:45:21.665242','2026-03-28T05:45:21.665247','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','225b5221-76ab-4a82-9603-e7f7b4deff95','DOI NPS DCAT-US','15d1363b9eed8b95172da447eea9f2f0fe784b6b435a17e7c8f93d01a367a0f2','1.1','2026-03-28T05:45:21.665242','2026-03-28T05:45:21.665247','Tabular Dataset','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('50074b57-3968-44ac-aa40-c3bdf6150414','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSIWAC 3 EXT3-MTP035 RDR V3.0','This CODMAC level 3 data set contains radiometric calibrated image data in W/m^2/sr/nm, acquired by the OSIRIS Wide Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft during the ROSETTA EXTENSION 3 mission phase, covering the period from 2016-09-26T06:40:00.000 to 2016-10-01T00:00:00.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V3.0 supersedes previous deliveries of the same dataset with the following changes since the last version: Lien corrected dataset after the July and October 2018 PSA/PDS external peer reviews. Updated documentation and ancillary files, added document on bandpass filter. Updated SCIENCE_USER_GUIDE_V03.PDF to include one section about FAQ and one section about image data quality. Added shutter backtravel and readout issues to image quality map. Updated DATA_QUALITY_ID keyword in image header. Improved handling of images with missing packets. Corrected START_TIME and STOP_TIME for BALLISTIC_STACKED images. Improved calibration of WAC balistic mode images.','public','2026-03-13T17:46:08.960667','2026-03-13T17:46:08.960674','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','582c6e46-117d-4065-8d39-abf72ebff578','NASA Data.json','5ce94104e059256886c7c8de1144e77396a4372dcb1c74a1584db6f08fe6744d','1.1','2026-03-13T17:46:08.960667','2026-03-13T17:46:08.960674','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('5010cd18-c27d-4eb7-adaf-fddc133c11aa','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 1 0546 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 1 phase 2014-11-20 to 2015-03-10. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-01-22T23:21:30.000 to 2015-01-23T09:34:09.000.','public','2026-03-13T19:44:44.263264','2026-03-13T19:44:44.263271','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','d8f02a81-b1bb-4de3-b0f1-c4eec89e3f59','NASA Data.json','81796adbcf68af13fd4c88f433fe54280283216500bc63d49208000722b353c5','1.1','2026-03-13T19:44:44.263264','2026-03-13T19:44:44.263271','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('501258db-59c5-4b3d-be98-a14080d254cc','American Peregrine Falcon Predicted Habitat - CWHR B129a [ds3284]','<div style=\'text-align:Left;\'><div><div><p><span>CWHR Predicted Habitat Models represent areas of predicted suitable habitat for each species within its range. These models are built from the following principal inputs: </span></p><p><span>1) a statewide, best-available vegetation map (FVEG);  </span></p><p><span>2) GIS data representing a species’ range;  </span></p><p><span>3) the CWHR database of habitat suitability values for over 700 terrestrial vertebrate species. </span></p><p><span>Habitat suitability ranks of Low (non-zero values less than 0.34), Medium (0.34-0.66), and High (greater than 0.66) are based on the maximum suitability value across the 3 species life requisites: reproduction, feeding, and cover. Note that previous versions of these Predicted Habitat Models used an average across the 3 life requisites in order to obtain an overall suitability score for each habitat type and stage class.  Habitat suitability scores were developed based on habitat patch sizes greater than 40 acres in size and are best interpreted for habitat patches greater than 200 acres in size. The FVEG landcover dataset is an aggregation of multiple statewide landcover and regional vegetation mapping efforts, conducted at different points in time (approximately 1990 up to time of publishing) and at various resolutions, compiled by the California Department of Forestry and Fire Protection (CALFIRE). FVEG uses the most current and consistent data available for each region of the state. Decision rules were developed that controlled which layers were given priority in areas of overlap. Crosswalks were used to attribute the various data sources according to the CWHR habitat-type classification system. Attributing FVEG with CWHR habitat types allows for the extraction of areas with non-zero suitability values for each species within the bounds of its range, creating a series of maps of predicted suitable habitat which are species-specific. Because FVEG is an amalgam of disparate landcover assessment efforts across the state, the predictive power for determining suitable habitat will vary between species, and possibly even regionally for species which are widely distributed. While these maps represent CDFW’s best estimate of the presence of suitable habitat for any given species in the CWHR system, these maps are also limited by several factors: 1) the accuracy and resolution of vegetation maps in a given region; 2) the dynamic nature of the landscape in which fire and other disturbance events alter conditions at a greater frequency than mapping efforts can track; 3) the currency of expert knowledge, particularly as species adapt to changing land and climate conditions and the shifting of other species’ ranges; 4) the frequency of species-specific surveys across a representative sample of a species’ entire range; 5) metapopulation dynamics, which describes the shifting of populations within their environment as result of numerous types of interactions and responses. </span></p><p><span>CWHR GIS data representing predicted suitable habitat should not be used to indicate the presence or absence of a particular species at any specific site. CWHR predicted habitat models are named according to the 4-character alpha-numeric CWHR ID assigned to each species (5 characters in the case of subspecies or other sub-taxa). There is also a “CWHR Revision Tracking Table” containing a record for each species, its CWHR ID, scientific name, common name, and range and habitat model data revision history. CWHR species range models, predicted habitat models, and GIS data of the statewide distribution of all CWHR habitat types, along with the CWHR revision tracking table, are available for download at </span><a href=\'https://www.wildlife.ca.gov/Data/CWHR\' target=\'_blank\' style=\'text-decoration:underline;\' rel=\'nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer\'><span>https://www.wildlife.ca.gov/Data/CWHR</span></a><span>. </span></p></div></div></div>','public','2026-03-23T13:53:11.969661','2026-03-23T13:53:11.969665','California Department of Fish and Wildlife','BIOS_Admin',NULL,'7c6b9654-909c-4550-ba3a-4b6b6baf3ab2','State of California','0f4b1301a994ab46423662a26f9d71c84400eca5bf312ae12b6addf32113996f','1.1','2026-03-23T13:53:11.969661','2026-03-23T13:53:11.969665','Natural Resources',NULL,0,'ca-gov'),('50326fbb-071f-4f1d-bff6-d9f3589b403d','GALILEO MAGNETOMETER CRUISE EDR DATA','This data set contains data acquired by the Galileo            Magnetometer during the Interplanetary Cruise to Jupiter.            The data are at varying resolution depending on the            averaging constant applied to the instrument.  The EDR            files are given in IBM 370 binary representation and are            stored in an extremely compact format.','public','2026-03-13T19:39:02.165765','2026-03-13T19:39:02.165770','planetary plasma interactions','Tess Jaffe','026:00','81194036-2af2-4fa5-bdaa-984bf1612dde','NASA Data.json','4ab2ba758c1c10d2f27f0b17ef1bb432c05e21273dfb0bc1556b85aa61ebd4d3','1.1','2026-03-13T19:39:02.165765','2026-03-13T19:39:02.165770','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('503e896d-23c7-4d97-bd83-9053518e7882','Continuous Fixed Station Water Quality Measurements in Cape Lookout National Seashore, May 2009 (Certified)','This dataset represents continuous water quality measurements that were taken at a fixed point in Cape Lookout National Seashore during the month of May, 2009 as a part of the Fixed Station Water Quality Monitoring protocol that was developed by the Southeast Coast I&M Network (SECN). The measurements were taken by a YSI 6600 ESD Multi-Parameter Long Term Water Quality Monitoring Datasonde unit that serves as the standard fixed station water quality monitoring equipment for all similar operations conducted by the SECN. The following parameters were measured at 15 minute intervals during the time period that has been specified: Water Temperature, Specific Conductivity, Salinity, Dissolved Oxygen (DO), DO Concentration, Shallow Depth, pH Level, and Turbidity. Any anomalies noted regarding these parameters have also been noted in separate fields.  Please note that these measurements have been certified by network personnel.','public','2026-03-26T05:28:30.240124','2026-03-26T05:28:30.240129','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','ce7b196d-6f76-4905-9cf7-b25e7bc16534','DOI NPS DCAT-US','68b82c9c4278bc577043aa3a036494f00b78aa69719b32e593bfd0d5a52fe547','1.1','2026-03-26T05:28:30.240124','2026-03-26T05:28:30.240129','Vector Dataset','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('5061d359-8fae-43a6-aba9-42af631f0e66','Data from: How you start matters: Density, resource size, and life stage impact population levels for pest insects','<p dir=\"ltr\"><i>Tribolium castaneum</i>, the red flour beetle, is a key pest of cereal grains and products that routinely infests food processing facilities. Such facilities represent dynamic environments comprising patches of resources of variable size and quality. To understand the influence of resource availability, insect density, and initial life stage on population regulation in <i>T. castaneum</i>, this study assessed the carrying capacity and population growth rates of <i>T. castaneum </i>populations<i> </i>kept for 20 weeks in a closed environment on four different amounts of diet at four starting population levels, then compared <i>T. castaneum</i> attraction to, reproductive output on, and the volatile profiles of previously-infested (e.g., conditioned) flour. Resource availability (e.g. the amount of flour) interacted with founding population density and life stage to influence <i>T. castaneum </i>population dynamics. In resource-limited patches, carrying capacity estimates were similar across founding densities, but the effect of founding population density on carrying capacity increased with flour availability. The opposite was observed for population growth rate, which tended to be more variable for small patches but stabilized as resource availability increased. Interestingly, both effects were reduced for populations founded as larvae compared to those founded as adults. The volatile profile of conditioned flour was also influenced by the interaction of patch size, density, and life stage. The relative abundance of 1-pentadecene and benzoquinones tended to be reduced in the volatile profiles of large patches, whereas 4,8-dimethyldecanal comprised a higher proportion of the total volatile emissions. Conditioned flour from large patches tended to be more attractive to <i>T. castaneum </i>adults, although this effect decreased as founding density increased. By contrast, when populations were founded as larvae, the volatile profiles of <i>T. castaneum </i>attraction to, and <i>T. castaneum </i>fecundity on conditioned flours were similar. These findings expand our understanding of how resource limitation and density-dependent effects influence <i>T. castaneum </i>population regulation and behavior, with implications for long-term trap monitoring and population thresholds in stored products.</p>','public','2026-03-13T22:46:57.255420','2026-03-13T22:46:57.255426','Agricultural Research Service','Gerken, Alison R.','005:18','333a332e-e5c0-439f-8714-f7423c453ffd','USDA JSON','f03838a9221226b0680d5e2c1dd7bdf22be8b4184e2de18fd614b4d8b0ed8557','1.1','2026-03-13T22:46:57.255420','2026-03-13T22:46:57.255426',NULL,'005:040',0,'usda-gov'),('509bb50a-9e04-4bb4-8fef-eea8f5b49861','NEAR MSI IMAGES FOR EROS/FLY/BY','NEAR EDR volume sets contain a single data set, from one instrument and one mission phase (defined in the phase table in /AAREADME.TXT).','public','2026-03-13T19:39:36.624231','2026-03-13T19:39:36.624238','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','7f825789-2100-4a7a-a500-53db3acd98cf','NASA Data.json','e62e15a2b924c3af687135d54d68dc4c58b73c4c81efdc8b516223620cc51ea4','1.1','2026-03-13T19:39:36.624231','2026-03-13T19:39:36.624238','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('50ac30a3-74a7-43f7-b914-b00a4f9aa578','CPMS - Customer Profile Management System BET-Biometric Enrollment Tool','Biometrics Enrollment Tool (BET) is custom-built software in CPMS boundary that is used for the collection of biometric data, including photos, signatures and fingerprint images; these collection artifacts are used for record checks and identification purposes, as well as for USCIS card production. BET is used both domestically and abroad for biometric collections. The information captured is sent to the Office of Biometric Identify Management\'s (OBIM) Homeland Advance Recognition Technology System (HART)  to confirm and/or validate the identity of the benefit requestor.','non-public','2026-03-22T11:51:27.435779','2026-03-22T11:51:27.435784','Unspecified','Open Data (MGMT)','024:030','85aa7a7f-6eda-4845-b753-905f27872990','DHS datajson source','7f44098066424beac3b95f4ec9bb754185c90f4e5cdf3fd69f514be58cc6161a','1.1','2026-03-22T11:51:27.435779','2026-03-22T11:51:27.435784',NULL,'024:000',0,'dhs-gov'),('50b3014f-d879-44ed-b072-826c0d089ec2','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P VIRTIS 2 ESCORT 2 MTP016 V1.0','This release contains the digital numbers (DN) contained in the telemetry (TM) packages of the VIRTIS instrument on board of the spacecraft Rosetta. This volume contains data at the vicinity of comet 67P, from the ESCORT 2 MTP016 phase, which occurred from 2015-05-06 to 2015-06-03','public','2026-03-13T17:51:28.099803','2026-03-13T17:51:28.099809','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','74377a4a-9a97-4794-aa4e-60faea49471c','NASA Data.json','7e42ade6b698221e1bc4886803aad123571e3680c0e6ceb367b6854114517ba2','1.1','2026-03-13T17:51:28.099803','2026-03-13T17:51:28.099809','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('50dff6e6-e0d8-49b5-a517-513e5c839196','Continuous Fixed Station Water Quality Measurements in Canaveral National Seashore, February 2008 (Certified)','This dataset represents continuous water quality measurements that were taken at a fixed point in Canaveral National Seashore during the month of February, 2008 as a part of the Fixed Station Water Quality Monitoring protocol that was developed by the Southeast Coast I&M Network (SECN). The measurements were taken by a YSI 6600 ESD Multi-Parameter Long Term Water Quality Monitoring Datasonde unit that serves as the standard fixed station water quality monitoring equipment for all similar operations conducted by the SECN. The following parameters were measured at 30 minute intervals during the time period that has been specified: Water Temperature, Specific Conductivity, Salinity, Dissolved Oxygen (DO), DO Concentration, Shallow Depth, pH Level, and Turbidity. Any anomalies noted regarding these parameters have also been noted in separate fields. Please note that these measurements have been certified by network personnel.','public','2026-03-26T05:31:50.190258','2026-03-26T05:31:50.190266','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','06da7f4e-d8f3-4907-a36b-9ff2f62a960f','DOI NPS DCAT-US','3313effcf7b42a0a40c70701be1711efbbf7d07a7b060c9c83d4c1c76a04e42d','1.1','2026-03-26T05:31:50.190258','2026-03-26T05:31:50.190266','Vector Dataset','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('50e53936-1761-487e-a5d2-89178ede78b5','Washington School Improvement Framework (WSIF) 2025 Annual','2025 annual calculation of the Washington School Improvement Framework for Federal School Accountability under the Every Student Succeeds Act.','public','2026-03-22T03:14:42.518764','2026-03-22T03:14:42.518767','data.wa.gov','OSPI Data',NULL,'2bffca21-0c22-4681-8658-889319926a99','WA JSON','bd2edc2d2252558045cbedbb9460d53826973e8270240677cbdfe81db87d06e4','1.1','2026-03-22T03:14:42.518764','2026-03-22T03:14:42.518767','education',NULL,0,'state-of-washington'),('50f3964e-757d-4162-8c5b-b33781138efe','JUNO JUPITER UVS 3 REDUCED DATA RECORD V1.0','The Juno Ultraviolet Spectrograph (UVS) CODMAC Level 3 Reduced Data Recordis a collection of the far ultraviolet photon detections obtained by the UVSinstrument, corrected for instrumental effects, radiometrically calibrated,and correlated with the auxiliary information needed to locate theobservations in space and time. These data are organized, in a manner verysimilar to the RDR product files from which they are derived, intoextensions within files formatted according to the Flexible Image TransportSystem (FITS) standard, version 2.1b. The UVS RDR archive enablesreprocessing of the corrected and calibrated science data into farultraviolet map products as map processing routines improve. Investigatorsinterested in applying advanced mapping methods or needing to understandthe properties of the corrected and calibrated data will find the RDRproducts useful. Many investigators, however, will be interested in usingthe UVS CODMAC Level 5 far ultraviolet map products directly.','public','2026-03-13T19:30:10.386427','2026-03-13T19:30:10.386434','Planetary Atmospheres','Planetary Data System','026:00','d231fb7a-7b01-48fc-b069-91a3521a22bb','NASA Data.json','75286a65a85654656664f382ab9e84258e0ac4db41e4ef28a6fef0148c077466','1.1','2026-03-13T19:30:10.386427','2026-03-13T19:30:10.386434','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('51157735-8200-4446-9452-80f95058ddc7','Impervious Surface 2025','<DIV STYLE=\"text-align:Left;\"><DIV><DIV><P><SPAN>The dataset contains basemap features that are typically classified as impervious surface, captured in 2025.Some examples of Impervious Surfaces include: Airport Taxiways, Helipads, Buildings, Sidewalks, Roads, Alleys and Swimming Pools.</SPAN></P></DIV></DIV></DIV>','public','2026-04-01T08:55:49.085931','2026-04-01T08:55:49.085935','Office of the Chief Technology Officer','DCGISopendata',NULL,'07521dac-b2e8-4c04-a186-d0ff990f0196','DC data','98526ed86f61a0ec4bf9c05391d0892809d9167bdbf7608f1b0bfddc751fd0fb','1.1','2026-04-01T08:55:49.085931','2026-04-01T08:55:49.085935','geospatial',NULL,0,'district-of-columbia'),('51246d0b-1a8e-4b17-875f-97718b9ebb52','MARS EXPRESS SUN MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 4 3566 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2013-01-01 to 2014-12-31. It is a Solar Conjunction measurement and covers the time 2013-04-27T08:52:36 to 2013-04-28T15:41:40.999.','public','2026-03-13T18:56:16.322150','2026-03-13T18:56:16.322157','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','a2600558-ba58-4323-859c-72d22a24dcb9','NASA Data.json','007dad8a6e22a3c5d6548a4ba4308c68228b9abd6a808cafe2a9ce9fab9b3c00','1.1','2026-03-13T18:56:16.322150','2026-03-13T18:56:16.322157','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('515fcb1e-39d2-4d42-8aff-f2878dc65b84','BLM Utah Federal Minerals Estate','<div style=\'text-align:Left;font-size:12pt\'><div><div><p><span>These data represent the current Federal Mineral Estate in Utah. The minerals on Federal lands are divided into three categories, each subject to different laws and regulations. Locatable, which are subject to the Mining Law of 1872, as amended, include gold, silver, copper and other hard rock minerals. Leasable minerals, such as oil, gas, coal and a host of other commodities, are subject to various Mineral Leasing Acts. Saleable minerals, such as sand and gravel that are essential to construction and road building, are subject to the Materials Act of 1947, as amended.</span></p></div></div></div>','public','2026-03-19T11:32:03.857681','2026-03-19T11:32:03.857686','Bureau of Land Management','Bureau of Land Management, bwillig','010:04','ae94c743-d57e-4be2-a04c-d785c3f7eaf1','DOI BLM DCAT-US','98fb731d707b862a95bf7d37f836d74ee4250e2b20363ab91fcb2de8427f2878','1.1','2026-03-19T11:32:03.857681','2026-03-19T11:32:03.857686','geospatial','010:000',0,'doi-gov'),('51659b6e-9950-4be2-bd5b-07e35479707a','MEX SPICAM MARS CLEANED UV RDR V1.0','The Mars Express SPICAM level 1A UV dataset contains measurements from the ultra violet SPICAM spectrometer collected during MARS phase with some corrections and processing','public','2026-03-13T18:14:32.524602','2026-03-13T18:14:32.524609','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','c48fb265-b10e-4264-9bfd-79d9a0149822','NASA Data.json','a66f94c0edb3cae15c3b11b319f3874f4271e74c0a91afccd806339ecc2a4e86','1.1','2026-03-13T18:14:32.524602','2026-03-13T18:14:32.524609','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('5175e49e-a7f3-4055-93bc-e5cd7ca4c799','ROSETTA-ORBITER X SREM 5 MARS V1.0','This data set contains derived electron and proton flux energies in MeV from the Standard Radiation Environment Monitor (SREM) instrument on the Rosetta spacecraft. These are CODMAC Level 5 derived data, and measure the radiation in the spacecraft environment during the MARS mission phase.','public','2026-03-13T18:10:00.371638','2026-03-13T18:10:00.371644','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','7449d5b5-1ea9-4010-bc96-cb6c530afb67','NASA Data.json','9e3c929087f67970b035a0c38ed20577dc0e7b75143966dc30df95bb79911416','1.1','2026-03-13T18:10:00.371638','2026-03-13T18:10:00.371644','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('5176f59c-1271-42d7-bfb7-0d4cb9e36bd8','MEX EXT 1 SPICAM MARS UV EDR-RAW V2.0','The Mars Express SPICAM level 0A UV data set contains raw measurements from the ultra violet SPICAM spectrometer collected during the cruise and MARS phases','public','2026-03-13T18:01:54.862765','2026-03-13T18:01:54.862770','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','b6775539-8813-4509-8402-aac7b42dfb71','NASA Data.json','1bfd284f8064366d0e5238a0493b84eddabf58226067b4cce01266fe8214de3b','1.1','2026-03-13T18:01:54.862765','2026-03-13T18:01:54.862770','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('51944270-9b76-44d6-945a-7ba723d51912','Continuous Fixed Station Water Quality Measurements in Canaveral National Seashore, August 2008 (Certified)','This dataset represents continuous water quality measurements that were taken at a fixed point in Canaveral National Seashore during the month of August, 2008 as a part of the Fixed Station Water Quality Monitoring protocol that was developed by the Southeast Coast I&M Network (SECN). The measurements were taken by a YSI 6600 ESD Multi-Parameter Long Term Water Quality Monitoring Datasonde unit that serves as the standard fixed station water quality monitoring equipment for all similar operations conducted by the SECN. The following parameters were measured at 30 minute intervals during the time period that has been specified: Water Temperature, Specific Conductivity, Salinity, Dissolved Oxygen (DO), DO Concentration, Shallow Depth, pH Level, and Turbidity. Any anomalies noted regarding these parameters have also been noted in separate fields. Please note that these measurements have been certified by network personnel.','public','2026-03-26T05:31:58.464959','2026-03-26T05:31:58.464963','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','b9c44cde-b4b3-4530-8313-355c592df0db','DOI NPS DCAT-US','bf9bef5b87fbc58c1415cf46b62513cf5d0b9134baf3d081d9ebccae07113a1c','1.1','2026-03-26T05:31:58.464959','2026-03-26T05:31:58.464963','Vector Dataset','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('519708e5-5e16-4c47-b569-12f2808a518d','KSC Array, Station IR3, Bottom Temperature','Timeseries data from \'KSC Array, Station IR3, Bottom Temperature\' (org_secoora_ksc_ir3)','public','2026-03-26T19:16:29.111861','2026-03-26T19:16:29.111870',NULL,NULL,NULL,'1f436a53-e2d6-490f-8441-4d3f12cf2bfd','ioos',NULL,NULL,'2026-03-26T19:16:29.111861','2026-03-26T19:16:29.111870',NULL,NULL,NULL,'noaa-gov'),('519ae691-a71d-4f6c-bdd1-ce59c98beca9','Hydrographic and Impairment Statistics Database: NPS-WSR Tinayguk Wild and Scenic River','Hydrographic and Impairment Statistics (HIS) is a National Park Service (NPS) Water Resources Division (WRD) project established to track certain goals created in response to the Government Performance and Results Act of 1993 (GPRA). One water resources management goal established by the Department of the Interior under GRPA requires NPS to track the percent of its managed surface waters that are meeting Clean Water Act (CWA) water quality standards. This goal requires an accurate inventory that spatially quantifies the surface water hydrography that each bureau manages and a procedure to determine and track which waterbodies are or are not meeting water quality standards as outlined by Section 303(d) of the CWA. This project helps meet this DOI GRPA goal by inventorying and monitoring in a geographic information system for the NPS: (1) CWA 303(d) quality impaired waters and causes; and (2) hydrographic statistics based on the United States Geological Survey (USGS) National Hydrography Dataset (NHD). Hydrographic and 303(d) impairment statistics were evaluated based on a combination of 1:24,000 (NHD) and finer scale data (frequently provided by state GIS layers).','public','2026-03-29T06:36:56.976954','2026-03-29T06:36:56.976964','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','5ea830ed-d9ea-456d-a04d-0499464ca423','DOI NPS DCAT-US','d1beb32da304ee9b28bc4e2051a5ee13bb6c34f4c03f8eb7092b78994ac1f08c','1.1','2026-03-29T06:36:56.976954','2026-03-29T06:36:56.976964','geospatial','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('51ad7c5a-5fa8-4347-9603-b5fd4f533c09','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 ROSETTA EXTENSION 1 1332 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the ROSETTA EXTENSION 1 phase 2016-01-01 to 2016-04-05. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2016-01-11T11:43:25.000 to 2016-01-11T14:26:59.500.','public','2026-03-13T18:10:18.228960','2026-03-13T18:10:18.228965','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','32f33345-0654-4a14-8832-f7b6f26f2723','NASA Data.json','66afdb7583006b7b227427f90c0945d559e7accd96518be81a1d784a5b82163d','1.1','2026-03-13T18:10:18.228960','2026-03-13T18:10:18.228965','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('51aff362-2dae-45f5-ada0-f6f4039cab91','MAGELLAN BISTATIC RADAR CALIBRATED DATA V1.0','Calibrated data from three orbits of S-Band (13 cm wavelength) Magellan bistatic radar data collected with NASA antenna DSS 63 on 5 June 1994 when the specular point crossed Maxwell Montes. Similarly processed data were used by Pettengill et al. (SCIENCE, 272, 1628-1631, 1996) to infer existence of a semiconductor layer covering anomalously reflecting regions at high altitude on Venus. This new data set includes calibrated time samples of receiver output as well as calibrated power spectra and voltage cross spectra (between the two received polarizations). The data set was written to three DVD+R volumes for delivery to the NASA Planetary Data System (PDS).','public','2026-03-13T16:59:20.929386','2026-03-13T16:59:20.929391','Geosciences;Radio Science','Planetary Data System','026:00','7a5f7e14-25b0-454b-89e0-b2081ec4d8e4','NASA Data.json','3f698d9c3ce5f0b32f8555a51b19e757eefbf66f6afe8af524d440cd448f49b8','1.1','2026-03-13T16:59:20.929386','2026-03-13T16:59:20.929391','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('51d7378b-0f17-40ab-a162-8cdffd92e09f','HAYABUSA SPICE KERNELS V1.0','This data set includes the complete set of Hayabusa SPICE data files (``kernel files\'\') for the surveying and collection phases of the mission. The SPICE data files, which can be accessed using SPICE software, contain geometric and other ancillary information needed to recover the full value of the science instrument data. In particular SPICE kernels provide spacecraft and planetary ephemerides, instrument mounting alignments, spacecraft orientation, spacecraft sequences of events, and data needed for relevant time conversions.','public','2026-03-13T19:41:05.588949','2026-03-13T19:41:05.588954','Navigation and Ancillary Information Facility','Planetary Data System','026:00','39eddd14-d3ff-4570-a1e0-70f0f3d0e2bd','NASA Data.json','0c1effef3330df458f3ca5a7532641febb30b65182b84bfd7035c35a5f4a0645','1.1','2026-03-13T19:41:05.588949','2026-03-13T19:41:05.588954','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('51fb83e0-3fdc-4fa4-87bc-c3724dabd1e8','Laborshed - Job Search Resources','Laborshed dataset containing data that covers the job search resources used in every laborshed area in Iowa.','public','2026-03-28T22:02:38.104956','2026-03-28T22:02:38.104961','data.iowa.gov','svqueen',NULL,'65f759eb-f6d6-4823-9581-0a7123630f0d','Iowa metadata','dd1f99fe830d00ef329dcfd67aefe43be9358cf8d1843a791f7bd95eeefd9e33','1.1','2026-03-28T22:02:38.104956','2026-03-28T22:02:38.104961','Economic Statistics',NULL,0,'state-of-iowa'),('52211a8c-2608-488b-b0e8-877f90c48756','ANGLO-AUSTRALIAN OBSERVATORY DATA FROM SL9 IMPACTS','This SL9 data set contains imaging, spectroscopy, & spectral mapping of Jupiter from 1994Jul16 through 1994Jul23. This includes data from the C,D,G,K,N,R,V, and W impacts in addition to before and after observations for baseline and comparison.','public','2026-03-13T19:39:18.544385','2026-03-13T19:39:18.544392','Planetary Atmospheres;Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','8b2f8bf2-d366-40f4-ad7a-66e81365a0de','NASA Data.json','e840a75ba7ca37582b1e9a651c2d78e864afa66cf28c71dfbddd970be8808c27','1.1','2026-03-13T19:39:18.544385','2026-03-13T19:39:18.544392','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('5224742b-f039-407d-be2a-2cc54ac1a9d5','IHW COMET HALLEY NEAR NUCLEUS IMAGE DATA V1.0','NASA\'s International Halley Watch (IHW) has created a Comet Halley Archive. The collection of data spans the full wavelength range as submitted by scientists to the IHW. The observations belong to one of the following Disciplines: Amateur, Astrometry, Infrared Studies, Large-Scale Phenomena, Meteor Studies, Near-Nucleus Studies, Photometry and Polarimetry, Radio Studies, and Spectroscopy and Spectrophotometry. The data collected by these nine disciplines were augmented by Spacecraft measurements. The data were submitted to IHW, but the evaluation and selection for the Archive has been the primary responsibility of the Discipline Specialist Teams for each network in cooperation with the Lead Center. The data from the Near Nucleus Studies Network contains 3523 images of Halley. These data span dates 1982 October 16 through 1989 April 12.','public','2026-03-13T19:38:20.823859','2026-03-13T19:38:20.823864','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','c9c1a4ad-ae71-4f0a-b644-2ad051c742a5','NASA Data.json','c4a47b6a6e25dd4b4332c0450c094b675153961423fd5a478c6de97abbf311be','1.1','2026-03-13T19:38:20.823859','2026-03-13T19:38:20.823864','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('52496775-8d47-4fc1-b38c-3d7780024d77','MARS EXPRESS MARS MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 7 4008 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2019-01-01 to 2020-12-31. It is a Occultation measurement and covers the time 2019-05-18T02:15:00.000 to 2019-05-18T04:05:00.000.','public','2026-03-13T18:09:12.563584','2026-03-13T18:09:12.563589','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','c768dcd7-4848-44b3-ac13-829863468e53','NASA Data.json','4965eb1040a73801c006ad0cb640ea2638c7c670580898ca160d5ab1ef7d4239','1.1','2026-03-13T18:09:12.563584','2026-03-13T18:09:12.563589','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('52694aef-93cb-4666-bda1-9d9515ccd106','ARECIBO/NRAO VENUS RTLS/GBT 3 DELAY DOPPLER V1.0','This dataset contains Earth-based, polarimetric radar image data for Venus collected from 1988 onwards, using the Arecibo Observatory 12.6-cm (2380 MHz) transmitter and receivers at either Arecibo or the Green Bank Telescope in West Virginia.','public','2026-03-13T16:42:07.211869','2026-03-13T16:42:07.211875','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','7f0612c4-277c-4d2d-9389-adf90329b540','NASA Data.json','c559f0cf04560d8f4fc1468dfabced6649e856c4e6f0b4084ea226c1c66e3b92','1.1','2026-03-13T16:42:07.211869','2026-03-13T16:42:07.211875','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('52c2fc24-02e2-42a9-93ad-f1843de92589','EPA Facility Registry Service (FRS): ER_CONTACTS','To improve public health and the environment, the United States Environmental Protection Agency (USEPA) collects information about facilities, sites, or places subject to environmental regulation or of environmental interest. These data are considered sensitive and are restricted to internal use only. The download file and map service are accessible only on the EPA intranet. EPA Category: Mission Sensitive, NARA Category: Critical Infrastructure.','public','2026-03-27T15:37:59.179841','2026-03-31T16:39:51.200955',NULL,NULL,NULL,'758692a3-4ba4-4585-80c8-4ec67c7e7d59','Environmental Dataset Gateway ISO Geospatial Metadata',NULL,NULL,'2026-03-27T15:37:59.179841','2026-03-31T16:39:51.200955',NULL,NULL,NULL,'epa-gov'),('52c88183-ffd5-454e-b14e-48645ee657fe','Continuous Fixed Station Water Quality Measurements in Timucuan Ecological and Historic Preserve, October 2008 (Certified)','This dataset represents continuous water quality measurements that were taken at a fixed point in Timucuan Ecological and Historic Preserve during the month of October, 2008 as a part of the Fixed Station Water Quality Monitoring protocol that was developed by the Southeast Coast I&M Network (SECN). The measurements were taken by a YSI 6600 ESD Multi-Parameter Long Term Water Quality Monitoring Datasonde unit that serves as the standard fixed station water quality monitoring equipment for all similar operations conducted by the SECN. The following parameters were measured at 30 minute intervals during the time period that has been specified: Water Temperature, Specific Conductivity, Salinity, Dissolved Oxygen (DO), DO Concentration, Shallow Depth, pH Level, and Turbidity. Any anomalies noted regarding these parameters have also been noted in separate fields. Please note that these measurements have been certified by network personnel.','public','2026-03-26T05:30:05.751238','2026-03-26T05:30:05.751242','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','2aca4845-e5a3-4d9f-af56-2173b8e9d4d4','DOI NPS DCAT-US','64bf346a78db4140664c8c3b11fa430bc0d4754ee8dcacde7ee0f1b323b9b499','1.1','2026-03-26T05:30:05.751238','2026-03-26T05:30:05.751242','Vector Dataset','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('52d9ef12-693e-4873-a811-06df313cce5d','FIELD EXP E SIRIS RESAMP REDUCED DATA RECORD SPECTRUM V1.0','The SIRIS measurement objectives were: 1) to measure reflectance spectra of a bright and dark target at each GRSFE site for potential use in AVIRIS calibration characterize selected sites at the GRSFE modeling site (Lunar Lake, NV) using visible/infrared reflectance reflectance spectra for selected endmember materials at each of the GRSFE sites inter-instrument calibration.','public','2026-03-13T17:29:34.176413','2026-03-13T17:29:34.176418','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','4e6183d8-e84d-44e5-b5f5-633837849bd5','NASA Data.json','b510b4cad75b92c4ab750347dcdb44329701390ed9ddbf98289f80e1cc163f94','1.1','2026-03-13T17:29:34.176413','2026-03-13T17:29:34.176418','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('52f32095-6d27-43b4-8a1a-91d55ba93d20','ROSETTA INERTIAL MEASUREMENT PACKAGE  ENGINEERING DATA','This CODMAC level 3 data set contains the key parameters of the Inertial Measurement Package.   In particular, it provides information on the gyroscope attitude  measurements on a global scale and individual.   It covers the period from launch in 2004, through the 3 Earth and  1 Mars flyby, plus the hibernation phases, plus the asteroid flybys  and finally covers the Prelanding, comet escort & Extension phases  of the prime target of the mission.   The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1).   This version V1.0 is the first version of this dataset.','public','2026-03-13T16:47:36.325176','2026-03-13T16:47:36.325183','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','cba10380-b8af-46c4-993c-9e7f4db70ed7','NASA Data.json','1abf5184830ab3567557fa5094feddf14462a4914df7f5ee47fd5d4d969c8cbb','1.1','2026-03-13T16:47:36.325176','2026-03-13T16:47:36.325183','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('52ff59a4-5d3c-4e66-be97-35a152665401','MESSENGER MDIS EXPERIMENT DATA RECORD V1.0','Abstract : The Mercury Dual Imaging System (MDIS) consists of two cameras, a Wide Angle Camera (WAC) and a Narrow Angle Camera (NAC), mounted on a common pivot platform. This dataset includes the Experiment Data Record (EDR) version of all available images acquired during the cruise phase to Mercury and includes post- launch checkout images, flyby images of Earth, Venus, Mercury, and the Moon, images acquired from Mercury orbit, and inflight calibration images. In addition to the imagery, anciliary information (including calibration files needed to process the data further) is included.','public','2026-03-13T19:28:31.988635','2026-03-13T19:28:31.988642','Imaging','Planetary Data System','026:00','01a1a8fa-c046-456a-900b-46a66a4d6fa0','NASA Data.json','42cbc976732d4ab0a43191f1bd501ea3718a959f4b2893534a9e0d972ca4b120','1.1','2026-03-13T19:28:31.988635','2026-03-13T19:28:31.988642','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('5312eea6-6a98-4684-a757-b61fe74ce557','Continuous Fixed Station Water Quality Measurements in Canaveral National Seashore, July 2006 (Certified)','This dataset represents continuous water quality measurements that were taken at a fixed point in Canaveral National Seashore during the month of July, 2006 as a part of the Fixed Station Water Quality Monitoring protocol that was developed by the Southeast Coast I&M Network (SECN). The measurements were taken by a YSI 6600 ESD Multi-Parameter Long Term Water Quality Monitoring Datasonde unit that serves as the standard fixed station water quality monitoring equipment for all similar operations conducted by the SECN. The following parameters were measured at 30 minute intervals during the time period that has been specified: Water Temperature, Specific Conductivity, Salinity, Dissolved Oxygen (DO), DO Concentration, Shallow Depth, pH Level, and Turbidity. Any anomalies noted regarding these parameters have also been noted in separate fields. Please note that these measurements have been certified by network personnel.','public','2026-03-26T05:30:47.097395','2026-03-26T05:30:47.097401','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','40bf0ec3-f641-40be-9237-068613ad0b09','DOI NPS DCAT-US','cd838d23b3002b30f0645b60124c15b78d07fd70e8f5331b92cfcd02fd409cff','1.1','2026-03-26T05:30:47.097395','2026-03-26T05:30:47.097401','Vector Dataset','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('532b2832-2c2d-46cf-a466-438d27896d7a','CIS2 - myaccount.uscis.gov - Public User Online Accounts','This data set contains the online account details used to register and authenticate public users as well as a history of user account action and authentication events.','non-public','2026-03-22T11:57:11.585400','2026-03-22T11:57:11.585405','Unspecified','Open Data (MGMT)','024:030','9b09d5f5-573e-48cb-bb43-c7d1cbb69a0b','DHS datajson source','994706a95eaae8626cbc5f415843c787d16855b5d672e508b817e30e6280706f','1.1','2026-03-22T11:57:11.585400','2026-03-22T11:57:11.585405',NULL,'024:000',0,'dhs-gov'),('533b9277-47f9-48d5-b019-05aaf46763b2','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 4 1207 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 4 phase 2015-10-22 to 2015-12-31. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-11-23T19:04:55.000 to 2015-11-24T02:25:05.000.','public','2026-03-13T19:53:38.212080','2026-03-13T19:53:38.212086','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','c0c3b09e-7501-485c-b4bc-2ffee28471db','NASA Data.json','6c7745ab56b74066823688762ed436b2c747b08d8e3901fb433bf522374dd0e7','1.1','2026-03-13T19:53:38.212080','2026-03-13T19:53:38.212086','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('536f1770-3e2c-4d4a-bb15-e4543e4baa42','Fort Frederica National Monument - Fish Inventory Update','This dataset is a vector point shapefile representing fish inventory locations at Fort Frederica National Monument. These points were digitized from maps and location descripitions from the data collectors in the field.','public','2026-03-26T05:28:43.592623','2026-03-26T05:28:43.592627','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','28558e30-cf11-4a18-bf5a-42b7612d7379','DOI NPS DCAT-US','207684424427992a0521e9e99fb13ad08d897c88e968356dee433c86970ebc5c','1.1','2026-03-26T05:28:43.592623','2026-03-26T05:28:43.592627','geospatial','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('53965359-d7e6-4fb5-9941-e86218396434','ARCSIX LaRC G-III High Altitude Lidar Observatory (HALO) Data','ARCSIX_AircraftRemoteSensing_LaRC-G3_HALO_Data is the High Altitude Lidar Observatory (HALO) data collected onboard the LaRC G-III aircraft during the Arctic Radiation-Cloud-Aerosol-Surface Interaction EXperiment (ARCSIX) campaign. Data collection for this product is complete. The ARCSIX campaign is a NASA field investigation aimed at quantifying the contributions of surface properties, clouds, aerosol particles, and precipitation to the Arctic summer surface radiation budget and sea ice melt during the early melt season. Based out of Greenland, ARCSIX completed two deployments from May – June 2024 and July - August 2024 utilizing the NASA P-3B, LaRC G-III, and SPEC-Learjet aircraft. The P-3B was equipped with in situ and remote sensing payloads to acquire measurements of aerosols, cloud, and radiation properties. The high-flying LaRC G-III was equipped with remote sensing instrumentation, including the HALO, and HSRL, along with the AVAPS dropsonde system. The SPEC-Learjet acquired measurements of cloud microphysics. Data were also collected at the Thule High Arctic Atmospheric Observatory (THAAO) in Pituffik, Greenland. The primary objective of ARCSIX was to enhance long-term space-based monitoring and predictive capabilities of Arctic sea ice, cloud, and aerosols by validating and improving remote sensing algorithms and model parameterizations in the Arctic. ARCSIX science questions focused on examining the impact of the predominant summer Arctic cloud types on the radiative surface energy budget, what processes control the evolution and maintenance of the predominant cloud types in the summertime Arctic, and how do the two-way interactions between surface properties and atmospheric forcings affect sea ice evolution?','public','2026-03-13T16:49:22.331963','2026-03-13T16:49:22.331968','NASA/LARC/SD/ASDC','Earthdata Forum','026:00','354c11bf-3b79-4102-bcc8-285220495fb5','NASA Data.json','453bfea132f22def043e6c60037f71696570f86fe0e5326f4d11f22f2a0ac812','1.1','2026-03-13T16:49:22.331963','2026-03-13T16:49:22.331968','Earth Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('53d0c135-4292-4047-84ff-382288575e28','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 PRELANDING 0273 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the PRELANDING phase 2014-01-21 to 2014-11-18. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2014-09-05T17:48:10.000 to 2014-09-06T00:15:13.000.','public','2026-03-13T18:56:46.933417','2026-03-13T18:56:46.933423','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','bbe04d24-021b-491e-bc73-f1ae1f3c6a67','NASA Data.json','becc713fab7093dc2693da93759f504cda5aba3134bd5f0c1a8238fd4498d750','1.1','2026-03-13T18:56:46.933417','2026-03-13T18:56:46.933423','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('53d0e420-0351-44df-8cc1-2aecacb26715','Laborshed - Commute','Laborshed dataset that contains data on commute time and distance for all laborsheds in Iowa.','public','2026-03-28T22:02:49.704005','2026-03-28T22:02:49.704010','data.iowa.gov','svqueen',NULL,'6c38fa6a-8bf8-4883-abf0-d72d5d0f0e73','Iowa metadata','1a93d99c10ae25acdb302b240f42ebb6a478fc22374bc002bcdec9d65015e33e','1.1','2026-03-28T22:02:49.704005','2026-03-28T22:02:49.704010','Economic Statistics',NULL,0,'state-of-iowa'),('540fc957-c7cc-4a63-a571-8ca36afd28ab','MESSENGER E/V/H MASCS 3 VIRS CALIBRATED DATA V1.0','Abstract : This data set consists of the MESSENGER MASCS VIRS calibrated observations, also known as CDRs. The MASCS VIRS experiment is a  fixed concave grating spectrograph with a beam splitter that simultaneously disperses the spectrum onto two photodiode arrays.  There are two VIRS CDR data products, one for each array, which  result in coverage of the wavelength ranges of the visible (VIS)  and near infrared (NIR).','public','2026-03-13T22:35:32.768736','2026-03-13T22:35:32.768743','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','4ba45990-41d1-4dc0-8667-797b437970e3','NASA Data.json','efb35d73347bd4e0220671b1f4aaa4b96217da26533597e2691efe74c6e37fd9','1.1','2026-03-13T22:35:32.768736','2026-03-13T22:35:32.768743','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('5459a40c-a9ee-47e5-896a-a49b7e3100ef','BLM OR Fish Passage Barriers Point Hub','FPB_PUB_PT: The Fish Passage Barrier (FPB) dataset represents basic information about existing and potential human-caused barriers to fish passage in watercourses, e.g., dams, culverts, bridges, tide gates, and weirs. In addition to basic information about barriers, the dataset provides general passage status.','public','2026-03-31T14:21:28.514079','2026-03-31T14:21:28.514084','Bureau of Land Management','Bureau of Land Management, ekjohnson','010:04','8309e7eb-0c3c-41d1-b577-fcc671766a08','DOI BLM DCAT-US','263a88e97d765684a7222fd2e2f82f103f19b67fcac1a7fe4747c38f1d5c4268','1.1','2026-03-31T14:21:28.514079','2026-03-31T14:21:28.514084','geospatial','010:000',0,'doi-gov'),('54693f1c-631b-45ee-bf17-3692fdef0976','MOLA AGGREGATED EXPERIMENT DATA RECORD','The MOLA AEDR data set contains the raw altimetry measurements acquired by the Mars Orbiter Laser Altimeter on the Mars Global Surveyor spacecraft. The AEDR data are used as input to the MOLA Precision Experiment Data Record (PEDR) data set, in which the altimetry data have been corrected according to precise measurements of the orbit. The PEDR data set is preferred for science analysis.','public','2026-03-13T17:33:40.198508','2026-03-13T17:33:40.198517','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','8131b841-fd1b-4ff1-8ac5-3f5b42359700','NASA Data.json','d20c2dfb2657ab13d5dea617d0947788e38f9a826606b7d8e18210b98a87c8ac','1.1','2026-03-13T17:33:40.198508','2026-03-13T17:33:40.198517','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('547e8d29-6969-4cec-82c6-a2f26e487133','GASPRA GALILEO MAGNETOMETER/TRAJECTORY DATA V1.0','Galileo Magnetometer observations of the asteroid Gaspra, extracted from the Galileo archive.','public','2026-03-13T18:21:10.656918','2026-03-13T18:21:10.656924','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','8c3d4245-d5b7-4eb3-b089-1b5911385a8b','NASA Data.json','a16b197abd3a5fc6bc701a415f954a1c0654df7c172de74eff5587d5bc265102','1.1','2026-03-13T18:21:10.656918','2026-03-13T18:21:10.656924','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('54d4c9b9-a9ac-4199-a8d3-24def70d8d30','ROSETTA HIGH GAIN ANTENNA  ENGINEERING DATA','This CODMAC level 3 data set contains the key parameters of the HGA Housekeeping. In particular, it provides information on the measured Azimuth & Elevation angles, as well as different pointing errors and displacement errors.   It covers the period from launch in 2004, through the 3 Earth and  1 Mars flyby, plus the hibernation phases, plus the asteroid flybys  and finally covers the Prelanding, comet escort & Extension phases  of the prime target of the mission.   The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1).   This version V1.0 is the first version of this dataset.','public','2026-03-13T17:13:31.918602','2026-03-13T17:13:31.918608','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','e7d8ed74-ecb9-4d99-955a-fa4e07be9ba0','NASA Data.json','8870c12c8f3a91b4568f46b132c626b37a0ea44e464d3d7477015251125dcde1','1.1','2026-03-13T17:13:31.918602','2026-03-13T17:13:31.918608','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('54d996b8-a5cd-4ac6-a7b4-d47a46c2b5d8','VG2 URA PWS RAW EXPERIMENT WAVEFORM                                      60MS V1.0','This data set consists ofelectric field waveform samples from the Voyager 2 Plasma WaveReceiver waveform receiver obtained during the Uranus encounter.The waveforms are collections of 4-bit samples of the electricfield measured by the dipole electric antenna at a rate of 28,800samples per second.  1600 samples are collected in 55.56 msecfollowed by a 4.44-msec gap. Each 60-msec interval constitutes aline of waveform samples. The data set includes about 271 frames ofwaveform samples consisting of up to 800 lines, each.  Thetelemetry format for the waveform data is identical to that forimages, hence the use of line and frame as constructs in describingthe form of the data.  The waveform is sampled through a bandpassfilter with a passband of 40 Hz to 12 kHz.  The 4-bit samplesprovide sixteen digital values of the electric field with alinear amplitude scale, but the amplitude scale is arbitrarybecause of the automatic gain control used in the waveformreceiver.  The instantaneous dynamic range afforded by the 4bit samples is about 23 db, but the automatic gain control allowsthe dominant signal in the passband to be set at the optimumlevel to fit within the instantaneous dynamic range.  With the gaincontrol, the overall dynamic range of the waveform receiveris about 100 db.','public','2026-03-13T18:47:42.824183','2026-03-13T18:47:42.824188','planetary plasma interactions','Planetary Data System','026:00','bfba8227-1d85-42fd-b070-0f18b82861c6','NASA Data.json','d2ebb714404db7f7a165ea65f280919a9800d3f180fae8ae1e98f2f0416004f6','1.1','2026-03-13T18:47:42.824183','2026-03-13T18:47:42.824188','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('550d771d-8261-478a-a4c9-1dfade79358f','HPMS Roadway Events Data 2022','Roadway attributes datasets in the Highway Performance Monitoring System (HPMS) consist of three separate tables: the Road Designations Table, the Road Identifications Table, and the Road Events Table.  The Roads Event Table data items include Inventory, Lanes, Intersections, Traffic, Control, Pavement, Terrain, and Travel Time Code.','public','2026-03-28T13:35:32.850506','2026-03-28T13:35:32.850510','Federal Highway Administration','Office of Highway Policy Information','021:15','650c77d4-b277-460e-b995-ee3a172d6c8f','DOT Socrata Data.json','fdc347527b8c4c7f5bb4ea240c38efe0608736563a509515393a81706b1cddfc','1.1','2026-03-28T13:35:32.850506','2026-03-28T13:35:32.850510','Roadways and Bridges','021:009',0,'dot-gov'),('554da962-11d1-4502-9717-7deedc611e14','Ordinance 20101209-074','Ordinance 20101209-074','public','2026-03-25T14:39:47.726493','2026-03-25T14:39:47.726498','data.austintexas.gov','Haileigh.Meyers@austintexas.gov',NULL,'99b1422e-9e9b-4262-b7c7-79b73a10332d','City of Austin Data.json','669fdcf7d534e94da74af32e4d43a5e3f7620dade870f2c1c7aa428e52d022ce','1.1','2026-03-25T14:39:47.726493','2026-03-25T14:39:47.726498',NULL,NULL,0,'city-of-austin'),('55711740-92f6-4f44-8bc7-85f89f914d6d','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P/CAL ALICE 2 ESC4 V2.0','This data set contains CODMAC Level 2 data acquired by the Rosetta Orbiter ALICE UV Spectrometer during the comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko Comet Escort 4 mission phase, which took place between 2015-10-22 and 2015-12-31. The current V2.0 data set supersedes the previous V1.0 data set with improved documentation.','public','2026-03-13T18:51:56.909707','2026-03-13T18:51:56.909713','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','e2c2dd93-cdd4-469d-a0cf-ba65595ef8d0','NASA Data.json','9165941d7c4a7692e983254991aa17c58951ef920e56ba1c873a0134b0c13d8c','1.1','2026-03-13T18:51:56.909707','2026-03-13T18:51:56.909713','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('55715063-d554-49d0-af09-b94e18c69603','Source Attribution of PM2.5 Health Benefits over Northern Hemisphere Using Adjoint of Hemispheric CMAQ','Abstract copied from manuscript April 25:\n\nThe adjoint of the U.S. EPA’s Community Multiscale Air Quality (CMAQ) model is extended for hemispheric scale applications and is used to estimate location-specific health impacts from primary PM2.5, and PM2.5 precursor emissions (NH3, NOX and SO2). We estimate the monetized health burden due to mortality caused by chronic PM2.5 exposure among adults living in the northern hemisphere, using a generalized concentration-response function. The health impact sensitivities show large spatial variability over the northern hemisphere and exhibit a great deal of seasonal variability, especially for inorganic precursor emissions. The largest marginal impacts are seen for NH3 and primary PM2.5. The estimated health impacts for a 10% reduction in emissions reveal a hemispheric burden of 513,700 avoided mortality (0.9% of global mortality) and monetized health benefits at above 1.2 trillion USD2016. The largest regional contribution to hemispheric mortality is found to be in East and South Asia, particularly China and India. Monetized health burdens are estimated to be highest in China and Europe while it was relatively similar in India as in Canada and the United States. Sectoral source contribution analysis demonstrates that the sectoral emissions of agriculture and residential are the largest contributors to the northern hemispheric scale health burden, however, regional differences exist in the results. Examining location- and sector-specific health impacts can inform more effective regulatory measures. This dataset is not publicly accessible because: These files are too large for ScienceHub. It can be accessed through the following means: These are available from the corresponding author upon request. Format: CMAQ outputs formatted as IOAPI with attribution results. These are available from the corresponding author upon request. \n\nThis dataset is associated with the following publication:\nOztaner, Y.B., S. Zhao, B. Henderson, R. Mathur, and A. Hakami. Source Attribution of PM2.5 Health Benefits Over Northern Hemisphere Using Adjoint of Hemispheric CMAQ.   GeoHealth. American Geophysical Union, Washington, DC, USA, 10(1): e2025GH001533, (2026).','public','2026-03-22T11:50:02.641764','2026-03-22T11:50:02.641769','U.S. Environmental Protection Agency','Barron Henderson','020:00','452c499c-b7eb-4a51-91f2-206584840e07','EPA ScienceHub','389d95d4af1111ef70debe0e2ecc0e1242ad5007e8c8c7d8d2955fd34ec6082a','1.1','2026-03-22T11:50:02.641764','2026-03-22T11:50:02.641769',NULL,'020:000',0,'epa-gov'),('559d8f13-90ac-4da4-98d8-7940f95e0828','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 PRELANDING 0396 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the PRELANDING phase 2014-01-21 to 2014-11-18. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2014-10-30T14:42:40.000 to 2014-10-30T21:19:03.500.','public','2026-03-13T17:01:25.834983','2026-03-13T17:01:25.834992','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','b411141a-deca-415f-bdb4-1a4fa142eef7','NASA Data.json','0bade78aa31c7371796a265cb23369c8700e8957ade7090f0ccb82010944085b','1.1','2026-03-13T17:01:25.834983','2026-03-13T17:01:25.834992','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('55b15122-70d5-4145-b123-dfee28c9711a','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 2 0637 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 2 phase 2015-03-11 to 2015-06-30. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-03-11T10:24:05.000 to 2015-03-11T12:24:01.500.','public','2026-03-13T17:54:24.934532','2026-03-13T17:54:24.934537','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','15866c5e-c205-4725-bc78-c73d9b3aa5a4','NASA Data.json','e7e5d309a8d1189cfad00f4a06ed7573629ef2658868111f9c4f3a8e9120fb50','1.1','2026-03-13T17:54:24.934532','2026-03-13T17:54:24.934537','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('55b35478-611c-441e-af6b-daffddc9dcd9','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 PRELANDING 0226 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the PRELANDING phase 2014-01-21 to 2014-11-18. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2014-08-20T18:55:55.000 to 2014-08-21T01:32:53.000.','public','2026-03-13T19:44:53.407260','2026-03-13T19:44:53.407266','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','aef19452-ab29-48ef-9f32-f7c2d178dbf9','NASA Data.json','7b0a3cf6d1e1797da4583ff25e25f0088a530367429a8ddfae3f01b487c040cd','1.1','2026-03-13T19:44:53.407260','2026-03-13T19:44:53.407266','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('55cc4309-b27a-4ce3-8476-55e1582bfb73','Continuous Fixed Station Water Quality Measurements in Timucuan Ecological and Historic Preserve, December 2008 (Certified)','This dataset represents continuous water quality measurements that were taken at a fixed point just outside of Timucuan Ecological and Historic Preserve during the month of December, 2008 as a part of the Fixed Station Water Quality Monitoring protocol that was developed by the Southeast Coast I&M Network (SECN). The measurements were taken by a YSI 6600 ESD Multi-Parameter Long Term Water Quality Monitoring Datasonde unit that serves as the standard fixed station water quality monitoring equipment for all similar operations conducted by the SECN. The following parameters were measured at 30 minute intervals during the time period that has been specified: Water Temperature, Specific Conductivity, Salinity, Dissolved Oxygen (DO), DO Concentration, Shallow Depth, pH Level, and Turbidity. Any anomalies noted regarding these parameters have also been noted in separate fields. Please note that these measurements have been certified by network personnel.','public','2026-03-26T05:34:10.950860','2026-03-26T05:34:10.950867','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','c2556c71-39bf-4a8f-9920-b2b6481e14e6','DOI NPS DCAT-US','a62a831f23ea64b2549ececead5f39caf92b26afb35c525dc511ec7e6698e25c','1.1','2026-03-26T05:34:10.950860','2026-03-26T05:34:10.950867','Vector Dataset','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('55cd3dc8-715d-4ee7-8d3a-6a444c6e5808','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 3 0929 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 3 phase 2015-07-01 to 2015-10-21. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-07-30T10:40:20.000 to 2015-07-30T17:28:34.500.','public','2026-03-13T16:54:52.350897','2026-03-13T16:54:52.350903','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','028660db-7f4f-40f1-951f-98992a4adfff','NASA Data.json','2cad20b7a67c4fcfadab98a45e18ca1a062c9efbeebbd0baa8e3754ebdc5f0fc','1.1','2026-03-13T16:54:52.350897','2026-03-13T16:54:52.350903','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('55d6ec88-6bb4-402f-a782-32e5fd837a00','NEW HORIZONS LEISA KEM1 CALIBRATED V6.0','This data set contains Calibrated data taken by the New Horizons Linear Etalon Imaging Spectral Array instrument during the KEM1 ENCOUNTER mission phase. This is VERSION 6.0 of this data set. This data set contains LEISA observations taken for functional testing, Radiometric Calibration, Solar Illumination Assembly Flat Field, and Arrokoth Encounter operations, including a test of a slow scan rate. Many LEISA Composition and System Scans along with some LEISA Scans as a LORRI Rider. In all FITS data files in this dataset, non-finite (NaN and Inf) values have been replaced with INVALID_CONSTANT values. This version includes data acquired by the spacecraft between 08/14/2018 and 04/30/2022. It only includes data downlinked before 05/01/2022. Future datasets may include more data acquired by the spacecraft after 08/13/2018 but downlinked after 04/30/2022.','public','2026-03-13T18:17:41.123322','2026-03-13T18:17:41.123329','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','85de1653-70ee-4072-b43f-039ab8f46e0b','NASA Data.json','26f8640be50f7e915ff50cac35f43125cba60b0def841e637c0800bc595d552e','1.1','2026-03-13T18:17:41.123322','2026-03-13T18:17:41.123329','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('5627a531-4843-4907-8d4e-08f0c49fff7d','Hydrographic and Impairment Statistics Database: NPS-WSR York Wild and Scenic River','Hydrographic and Impairment Statistics (HIS) is a National Park Service (NPS) Water Resources Division (WRD) project established to track certain goals created in response to the Government Performance and Results Act of 1993 (GPRA). One water resources management goal established by the Department of the Interior under GRPA requires NPS to track the percent of its managed surface waters that are meeting Clean Water Act (CWA) water quality standards. This goal requires an accurate inventory that spatially quantifies the surface water hydrography that each bureau manages and a procedure to determine and track which waterbodies are or are not meeting water quality standards as outlined by Section 303(d) of the CWA. This project helps meet this DOI GRPA goal by inventorying and monitoring in a geographic information system for the NPS: (1) CWA 303(d) quality impaired waters and causes; and (2) hydrographic statistics based on the United States Geological Survey (USGS) National Hydrography Dataset (NHD). Hydrographic and 303(d) impairment statistics were evaluated based on a combination of 1:24,000 (NHD) and finer scale data (frequently provided by state GIS layers).','public','2026-03-29T06:05:37.829016','2026-03-29T06:05:37.829023','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','8553f0f9-cd8f-43ba-9fec-e0335de09702','DOI NPS DCAT-US','98ea35e028f1b371360b874d5238ebf1421a19753324d0f5414f1f519fedacf0','1.1','2026-03-29T06:05:37.829016','2026-03-29T06:05:37.829023','geospatial','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('562c6acd-7d2e-4298-9103-525237145442','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 4 1159 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 4 phase 2015-10-22 to 2015-12-31. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-11-05T19:49:25.000 to 2015-11-06T03:08:25.000.','public','2026-03-13T18:32:57.264100','2026-03-13T18:32:57.264105','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','bd9c9cbb-172a-4070-8247-cca08816e964','NASA Data.json','bca0722672cb3d22a76d66207d73228e8e10035a6e2f314cf093d6628ad24d0e','1.1','2026-03-13T18:32:57.264100','2026-03-13T18:32:57.264105','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('564a58ae-2a00-4af8-ba46-54d817f30677','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 2 0868 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 2 phase 2015-03-11 to 2015-06-30. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-06-30T10:12:15.000 to 2015-06-30T11:37:47.000.','public','2026-03-13T17:43:50.087715','2026-03-13T17:43:50.087721','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','8b2e46fb-ad13-4a5d-9c87-bcf91fcdd2ef','NASA Data.json','4ca30f93fcc9efa96ad222bfe571da49cd1b3552e9d6fb9d1fe86487c16ce5aa','1.1','2026-03-13T17:43:50.087715','2026-03-13T17:43:50.087721','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('5656e7ae-af88-4677-9a9f-3de0b1d36b56','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P COSIMA 3 V3.0','The Rosetta COSIMA data contains the operational history of the 72 dust collecting substrates from the installation inside the instrument. This dataset contains data from 2002-05-29 up to 2015-06-30. The operations are either expose, storage, spectra, total intensity, heating, imaging or grain lists. The data is grouped by the substrate and time. Up to the 2014-08 the aim of the data has been the instrument health and operational functionality, not statistically significant substrate background spectra. From 2014-08 onward the D0 substrate set was used to collect dust collected in the vicinity of 67P/CHURYUMOV GERASIMENKO 1 (1969 R1) and dust analysis with TOF-SIMS. From 2014-10-23 onward due to an instrument failure, the SIMS data became scientifically unusable. While other SIMS parameter sets were tested, substrates CF were exposed from mid 2015-12 and C7 from mid 2015-02. End of March 2015 SIMS became operational again. D1 and CD were exposed and SIMS was done with CD, CF and D1. This data set supersedes all previous COSIMA datasets, like RO-C-COSIMA-3-V1.0, RO-C-COSIMA-3-V2.0, RO-CAL-COSIMA-2-V1.0 and RO-CAL-COSIMA-3-V3.0 Also, in the above previous versions, the values of the temperature in the HK data where given in Celsius although Kelvin was written in the description of the table in the FMT file','public','2026-03-13T17:18:20.348430','2026-03-13T17:18:20.348435','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','daf91129-d05f-4048-90d1-dcb7fe831184','NASA Data.json','d4571395c6f71b390ae610af4f734d67f6485ccae1316f72b3608e25fe5b790f','1.1','2026-03-13T17:18:20.348430','2026-03-13T17:18:20.348435','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('569c0759-cc14-4953-b3ef-283c3c27308e','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P VIRTIS 2 ESCORT 2 MTP014 V2.0','This release contains the digital numbers (DN) contained in the telemetry (TM) packages of the VIRTIS instrument on board of the spacecraft Rosetta. This volume contains data at the vicinity of comet 67P, from the ESCORT 2 MTP014 phase, which occurred from 2015-03-11 to 2015-04-08. This version of the dataset (2.0) is produced by a fixed EGSE software. The old version of the software produced incomplete products, reduced by one line','public','2026-03-13T18:26:44.846171','2026-03-13T18:26:44.846177','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','401c0e1a-0c75-4922-8ef5-5b8626ab805c','NASA Data.json','3ce0cf2c7a51bafb16a06a814f15d854ffb71dca32f7983afc425d1ed1ae9ccc','1.1','2026-03-13T18:26:44.846171','2026-03-13T18:26:44.846177','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('5754057e-43c6-4605-8188-001019e50f01','DID(IT) - Facilities Data','FAMS holds facilities data including, but not limited to: record facility, project, and budget data.','non-public','2026-03-22T11:56:04.607874','2026-03-22T11:56:04.607879','Unspecified','Open Data (MGMT)','024:030','2496651a-fd9f-48a8-bce3-bd646125eeaf','DHS datajson source','d0f7d9c2096bf2b68f26652be8456016111005a3326dc99c421febbfb8dcb064','1.1','2026-03-22T11:56:04.607874','2026-03-22T11:56:04.607879',NULL,'024:000',0,'dhs-gov'),('579ae065-6094-411f-8b7f-49154319026b','Ordinance 20071018-002','Ordinance 20071018-002','public','2026-03-25T14:48:47.309728','2026-03-25T14:48:47.309733','data.austintexas.gov','Haileigh.Meyers@austintexas.gov',NULL,'e5950015-0cf0-4fbf-8d42-51c559a9f0ce','City of Austin Data.json','c02458b10b82985a89ef02699128766a5e83aaa9a82cc9dcc890e6daa7b6f614','1.1','2026-03-25T14:48:47.309728','2026-03-25T14:48:47.309733',NULL,NULL,0,'city-of-austin'),('57a03098-29c6-46ab-8360-d68a7c0861d0','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSINAC 3 ESC3-MTP020 RDR V3.0','This CODMAC level 3 data set contains radiometric calibrated image data in W/m^2/sr/nm, acquired by the OSIRIS Narrow Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft during the COMET ESCORT 3 mission phase, covering the period from 2015-08-25T23:25:00.000 to 2015-09-22T23:24:59.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V3.0 supersedes previous deliveries of the same dataset with the following changes since the last version: Lien corrected dataset after the July and October 2018 PSA/PDS external peer reviews. Updated documentation and ancillary files, added document on bandpass filter. Updated SCIENCE_USER_GUIDE_V03.PDF to include one section about FAQ and one section about image data quality. Added shutter backtravel and readout issues to image quality map. Updated DATA_QUALITY_ID keyword in image header. Improved handling of images with missing packets. Included FITs files. Browse products changed to the same size as the original image.','public','2026-03-13T19:37:57.827795','2026-03-13T19:37:57.827801','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','ae061498-5e4e-4e0d-bca6-ea1ca51300be','NASA Data.json','a5c1da8f1e58537af21a6fccc1093bb67d5eb8d4a6b2fc261df766b0a764717c','1.1','2026-03-13T19:37:57.827795','2026-03-13T19:37:57.827801','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('57a7972b-dcb2-4f43-9e4a-f93e8f002962','Continuous Fixed Station Water Quality Measurements in Timucuan Ecological and Historic Preserve, July 2008 (Certified)','This dataset represents continuous water quality measurements that were taken at a fixed point just outside of Timucuan Ecological and Historic Preserve during the month of July, 2008 as a part of the Fixed Station Water Quality Monitoring protocol that was developed by the Southeast Coast I&M Network (SECN). The measurements were taken by a YSI 6600 ESD Multi-Parameter Long Term Water Quality Monitoring Datasonde unit that serves as the standard fixed station water quality monitoring equipment for all similar operations conducted by the SECN. The following parameters were measured at 30 minute intervals during the time period that has been specified: Water Temperature, Specific Conductivity, Salinity, Dissolved Oxygen (DO), DO Concentration, Shallow Depth, pH Level, and Turbidity. Any anomalies noted regarding these parameters have also been noted in separate fields. Please note that these measurements have been certified by network personnel.','public','2026-03-26T05:34:30.006910','2026-03-26T05:34:30.006916','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','f642aa1d-00f8-48a7-8057-28b9b87f9efd','DOI NPS DCAT-US','79485b522521fa46ff5c4c935730b5665971528ec4fa9b3f23c936a4eff5929a','1.1','2026-03-26T05:34:30.006910','2026-03-26T05:34:30.006916','Vector Dataset','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('57e1e38b-3682-4b78-b489-a81ac9cce580','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RPCLAP 3ESC3 CALIB2 V1.0','This data set containsCALIBRATED data from Rosetta RPC-LAP, acquired during the COMET ESCORT 3mission phase where the primary target was the comet67P/CHURYUMOV-GERASIMENKO 1 (1969 R1). It contains instrument outputs involts and amperes, calibrated and corrected for instrument offsets.','public','2026-03-13T17:08:40.035426','2026-03-13T17:08:40.035430','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','331132ae-57f3-4e4c-85d8-f21057cdd8ac','NASA Data.json','fbab55760c0b76bf581a19112619a3fa0753f1f147d2741f20c852fbed1c8f30','1.1','2026-03-13T17:08:40.035426','2026-03-13T17:08:40.035430','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('5804a796-b8e3-4327-87b0-18a2a945c764','ROSETTA-ORBITER STEINS ROSINA 2 ENGINEERING V1.0','This data set present engineering data of the COPS and DFMS ROSINA sensors during the Steins flyby phase. There were no RTOF measurements','public','2026-03-13T17:21:47.642857','2026-03-13T17:21:47.642863','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','296a1f8d-985e-4a26-ad4e-365a7d5d53c3','NASA Data.json','eb44a3a230d629a87c714c2091b33f40f9711ea07e32f5c371350b0d47dac082','1.1','2026-03-13T17:21:47.642857','2026-03-13T17:21:47.642863','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('58200c4f-7380-4c1d-8489-2a18ca7ba588','ROSETTA-ORBITER EARTH OSIWAC 4 EAR2 RDR-REFLECT V1.0','This CODMAC level 4 data set contains radiometric calibrated and geometric distortion corrected (resampled)  image data in reflectance units (normalized and thus without unit),  acquired by the OSIRIS Wide Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft  during the EARTH SWING-BY 2 mission phase, covering the period  from 2007-09-13T00:00:00.000 to 2008-01-27T23:59:59.000. The prime target is planet Earth. This version V1.0 is the first version of this dataset.','public','2026-03-13T18:19:58.722931','2026-03-13T18:19:58.722937','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','1e743e0a-6ee5-4fe7-9a04-8de236c46b88','NASA Data.json','5700db2d44fcbdc4b551c4540aa21f5eeaa9c8e932035f4bfb733c67e8a75f71','1.1','2026-03-13T18:19:58.722931','2026-03-13T18:19:58.722937','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('584df68d-09ba-4ac7-92f7-46c6795830db','AIRSAR_TOPSAR_DEM_C','AIRSAR topographic SAR digital elevation model CTIF product','public','2026-03-13T19:02:21.134817','2026-03-13T19:02:21.134822','NASA/JPL/RDC;ASF','Earthdata Forum','026:00','304034bb-a30a-4ee0-881c-72284282d9b6','NASA Data.json','c2fbd1e4e26f230d1dddfd44125a8d8473074f9849a1d74cad85efc4c17dfec6','1.1','2026-03-13T19:02:21.134817','2026-03-13T19:02:21.134822','Earth Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('585a3665-a507-4b06-aa94-6d144501e457','Hydrographic and Impairment Statistics Database: NPS-WSR North Fork Koyukuk Wild and Scenic River','Hydrographic and Impairment Statistics (HIS) is a National Park Service (NPS) Water Resources Division (WRD) project established to track certain goals created in response to the Government Performance and Results Act of 1993 (GPRA). One water resources management goal established by the Department of the Interior under GRPA requires NPS to track the percent of its managed surface waters that are meeting Clean Water Act (CWA) water quality standards. This goal requires an accurate inventory that spatially quantifies the surface water hydrography that each bureau manages and a procedure to determine and track which waterbodies are or are not meeting water quality standards as outlined by Section 303(d) of the CWA. This project helps meet this DOI GRPA goal by inventorying and monitoring in a geographic information system for the NPS: (1) CWA 303(d) quality impaired waters and causes; and (2) hydrographic statistics based on the United States Geological Survey (USGS) National Hydrography Dataset (NHD). Hydrographic and 303(d) impairment statistics were evaluated based on a combination of 1:24,000 (NHD) and finer scale data (frequently provided by state GIS layers).','public','2026-03-29T06:06:21.402893','2026-03-29T06:06:21.402900','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','eba26f7b-b7c5-48ea-bbdf-cfaf62c433f7','DOI NPS DCAT-US','8afa59a3062564fbd18381fa310af79f9546225d02898de11a110f7f9dcd17da','1.1','2026-03-29T06:06:21.402893','2026-03-29T06:06:21.402900','geospatial','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('587c6808-62a9-4cd6-b587-f5b306df8923','Iowa Staffing Patterns','Staffing patterns, which are published in conjunction with the occupational projections, provide detailed information on which occupations are employed in each industry (sector/sub-sector)--and the reverse.','public','2026-03-28T22:01:20.492012','2026-03-28T22:01:20.492017','data.iowa.gov','Katie Green',NULL,'34bc9548-74fd-408c-96ce-14df6d4971b5','Iowa metadata','83ba8ac2d3f21122ba26c9d62298b765d1678873a760775deab0963d274376ca','1.1','2026-03-28T22:01:20.492012','2026-03-28T22:01:20.492017','Workforce',NULL,0,'state-of-iowa'),('58b6fee5-4b85-4c4c-9453-b13db8e5e727','LCROSS EARTH/MOON VISIBLE SPECTROMETER 3 CAL V1.0','Calibrated spectra from the Visible Spectrometer (VSP) aboard the Lunar Crater Observation and Sensing Satellite (LCROSS).','public','2026-03-13T18:12:00.972066','2026-03-13T18:12:00.972071','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','8897f597-c211-4601-a42a-8945a66f5304','NASA Data.json','6832d47784ca884cd9a6c3670e51b66e2fd69a7df218a492253436f68b5ce08b','1.1','2026-03-13T18:12:00.972066','2026-03-13T18:12:00.972071','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('58c79c2b-7059-4c6f-b47f-f8ba808e3140','Hydrographic and Impairment Statistics Database: NPS-WSR Alagnak Wild and Scenic River','Hydrographic and Impairment Statistics (HIS) is a National Park Service (NPS) Water Resources Division (WRD) project established to track certain goals created in response to the Government Performance and Results Act of 1993 (GPRA). One water resources management goal established by the Department of the Interior under GRPA requires NPS to track the percent of its managed surface waters that are meeting Clean Water Act (CWA) water quality standards. This goal requires an accurate inventory that spatially quantifies the surface water hydrography that each bureau manages and a procedure to determine and track which waterbodies are or are not meeting water quality standards as outlined by Section 303(d) of the CWA. This project helps meet this DOI GRPA goal by inventorying and monitoring in a geographic information system for the NPS: (1) CWA 303(d) quality impaired waters and causes; and (2) hydrographic statistics based on the United States Geological Survey (USGS) National Hydrography Dataset (NHD). Hydrographic and 303(d) impairment statistics were evaluated based on a combination of 1:24,000 (NHD) and finer scale data (frequently provided by state GIS layers).','public','2026-03-29T06:05:55.707183','2026-03-29T06:05:55.707189','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','be9b2269-7870-4fb2-9ab1-b4a1267c078f','DOI NPS DCAT-US','1ee34b71869ee5115c20c3fcf5ce3854b39baa9c490602b661142e7c7407aa61','1.1','2026-03-29T06:05:55.707183','2026-03-29T06:05:55.707189','geospatial','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('58d6b813-314b-419c-8ac4-a7065c05de0f','BLM CO Lands Inventoried with Wilderness Characteristics','<DIV STYLE=\"text-align:Left;\"><DIV><P><SPAN>This feature dataset represents the spatial extent and boundaries of inventoried and managed BLM Lands with Wilderness Characteristics. This dataset also also provides BLM and the public with information about naturalness, opportunities for solitude and/or primitive recreation, supplemental values and proximity to Wilderness Areas or Wilderness Study Areas.    BLM Inventoried Lands with Wilderness Characteristics is consistent with Section 201 of the Federal Land Policy and Management Act (FLPMA), which requires the BLM Colorado Inventoried Lands with Wilderness Characteristics is consistent with Section 201 of the Federal Land Policy and Management Act (FLPMA), which requires the Secretary of the Interior to “prepare and maintain on a continuing basis an inventory of all public lands and their resource and other values,” and the BLM Land Use Planning Handbook, BLM Colorado has identified and begun an assessment of BLM-managed lands with wilderness characteristics outside of existing WSAs. BLM Manual 6310 - Conducting Wilderness Characteristics Inventory on BLM Lands, provides the guidance from which BLM performs the wilderness characteristic inventory process.</SPAN></P></DIV></DIV>','public','2026-03-26T12:40:59.041406','2026-03-26T12:40:59.041412','Bureau of Land Management','Bureau of Land Management, pkeller','010:04','41f6175e-077d-4053-bd2f-7b17dfc6e7aa','DOI BLM DCAT-US','3bce2eb16f6cd1a879074629750dabba6b70fb87330c02cd7cf02a8d132e7e9d','1.1','2026-03-26T12:40:59.041406','2026-03-26T12:40:59.041412','geospatial','010:000',0,'doi-gov'),('58e2179b-161e-4287-9bd4-7bb03b3a563e','LECL Lewis and Clark NHT Trail Corridor','The Trail Corridor dataset is comprised of a 50-mile buffer on each side of the Lewis and Clark National Historic Trail congressionally designated route.\n\nThe Lewis and Clark National Historic Trail is approximately 4,900 miles long, extending from the Ohio River in Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania to the mouth of the Columbia River in Oregon, following both the outbound and inbound routes of the Lewis and Clark Expedition. The trail connects 16 states (Pennsylvania, West Virginia, Ohio, Indiana, Kentucky, Illinois, Missouri, Kansas, Nebraska, Iowa, South Dakota, North Dakota, Montana, Idaho, Washington, and Oregon) and was established by Congress in 1978 as part of the national trails system (NTS) as one of four original national historic trails. This trail commemorates the 1803-1806 expedition of Lewis and Clark and the Corps of Discovery, which explored the Louisiana Territory and beyond. This epic journey contributed to significant scientific knowledge and profound political, social, economic, cultural, and environmental changes to the lands and the peoples of the North American continent.','public','2026-03-13T22:34:46.359335','2026-03-13T22:34:46.359342','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','c8542cef-8fd1-4c47-a6ae-980ceb28c326','DOI NPS DCAT-US','7caa3ba415ac0760132dc6346ddd5ba4845546c6e7e960141a41563b64b3f8fd','1.1','2026-03-13T22:34:46.359335','2026-03-13T22:34:46.359342','geospatial','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('58fb5d00-fb09-4ea0-aa8d-4d600ebb6180','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSINAC 4 PRL-MTP001 RDR-INFLDSTR V1.0','This CODMAC level 4 data set contains solar stray-light corrected, in-field stray-light corrected,  radiometric calibrated and geometric distortion corrected  (resampled) image data in W/m^2/sr/nm,  acquired by the OSIRIS Narrow Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft  during the PRELANDING mission phase, covering the period  from 2014-01-20T10:00:00.000 to 2014-05-07T12:47:59.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V1.0 is the first version of this dataset: Lien corrected dataset after September 2019 PSA/PDS external peer review.','public','2026-03-13T19:29:58.306229','2026-03-13T19:29:58.306236','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','099883de-d393-4bfb-8f17-1b15a32fc3a7','NASA Data.json','20ffb73c2c2d3255756e5cfd1f81f6f71b4bd6f4a83ae47866e7cb90189dea38','1.1','2026-03-13T19:29:58.306229','2026-03-13T19:29:58.306236','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('58fe48fb-ace6-47a2-9ac1-b5042dceceba','ROSETTA-ORBITER COMET ESCORT OSINAC 2 EDR MTP 013 V1.0','This data set contains raw EDR images acquired by the OSIRIS Narrow AngleCamera during the escort phase of the Rosetta mission at the comet 67P,covering the period from 2015-02-10 to 2015-03-10.','public','2026-03-13T19:02:55.063108','2026-03-13T19:02:55.063113','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','22c2a9d0-34b3-4b97-98ea-1a6c565faf68','NASA Data.json','39fa52102a9d58dc88932cce09e2a8f505f1185fcb40919c8079e33e5d6952a4','1.1','2026-03-13T19:02:55.063108','2026-03-13T19:02:55.063113','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('591fc131-fa72-42bf-a942-67bb32ba4b83','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 4 1188 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 4 phase 2015-10-22 to 2015-12-31. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-11-16T12:07:05.000 to 2015-11-16T16:51:43.500.','public','2026-03-13T16:43:33.899339','2026-03-13T16:43:33.899344','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','e517e442-4801-41b7-8494-e82434f14be5','NASA Data.json','8508cf14c72fcfcf395527b7a272a49da07a6af1586a1ab41d476275ef07dd66','1.1','2026-03-13T16:43:33.899339','2026-03-13T16:43:33.899344','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('5935c598-b03f-42ab-b1e6-d78c13652883','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSINAC 2 EXT3-MTP033 EDR V3.0','This CODMAC level 2 data set contains uncalibrated image data in DN unit, acquired by the OSIRIS Narrow Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft during the ROSETTA EXTENSION 3 mission phase, covering the period from 2016-08-09T23:25:00.000 to 2016-09-02T06:39:59.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V3.0 supersedes previous deliveries of the same dataset with the following changes since the last version: Lien corrected dataset after the July and October 2018 PSA/PDS external peer reviews. Updated documentation and ancillary files, added document on bandpass filter. Updated SCIENCE_USER_GUIDE_V03.PDF to include one section about FAQ and one section about image data quality. Added shutter backtravel and readout issues to image quality map. Updated DATA_QUALITY_ID keyword in image header. Improved handling of images with missing packets.','public','2026-03-13T19:36:22.461239','2026-03-13T19:36:22.461247','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','ae7c6444-5f9d-4057-a579-ef878cdb6a3b','NASA Data.json','042b8e940f12541c2ca843061a95221e824c1a03183b3e531782a656fb707906','1.1','2026-03-13T19:36:22.461239','2026-03-13T19:36:22.461247','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('595f0c8e-5824-448e-ba81-90466347b49d','NEW HORIZONS      SWAP KEM2      CALIBRATED V1.0','This data set contains Calibrated data taken by the      New Horizons Solar Wind Around Pluto instrument during the      KEM1 ENCOUNTER and KEM2 CRUISE mission phases.      This is VERSION 1.0 of this data set.      This version includes data acquired by the spacecraft between      08/14/2018 and 04/30/2023. It only includes data downlinked before      05/01/2023 and after 04/30/2022. Future datasets may include more      data acquired by the spacecraft after 08/13/2018 but downlinked after      04/30/2023.      This dataset includes SWAP observations and plasma rolls taken after the      Arrokoth encounter.','public','2026-03-13T18:30:10.517869','2026-03-13T18:30:10.517874','small bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','a46e3197-925a-4692-8668-c284edc5507f','NASA Data.json','8eaadd7daa1191770dcf7d1d05ea29e342c6577ffa04151dbead54b354f90ace','1.1','2026-03-13T18:30:10.517869','2026-03-13T18:30:10.517874','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('597f576d-d888-4e10-95e3-e50d086650d9','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSIWAC 5 PRL-MTP006 DDR-GEO V1.0','This CODMAC level 5 data set contains derived data products that include pixel-precise georeferencing information, acquired by the OSIRIS Wide Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft during the PRELANDING mission phase, covering the period from 2014-08-01T10:00:00.000 to 2014-09-02T09:59:59.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V1.0 is the first version of this dataset: Lien corrected dataset after October 2018 PSA/PDS external peer review.','public','2026-03-13T17:03:31.884857','2026-03-13T17:03:31.884863','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','6ccdafc6-9598-49a2-8a6a-f7ee17c2e07c','NASA Data.json','ea201b1aee88473fa09b412cff3a37989cadecdc424acccb6d412b1436304561','1.1','2026-03-13T17:03:31.884857','2026-03-13T17:03:31.884863','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('598594fb-27bb-4743-8fc9-af3d5c106ede','Short-Term Occupational Projections','Occupational projections estimate the future performance and trends of occupations over a defined period. These are 2-year projections for the State of Iowa and its six local workforce development areas (LWDA). Projections are are based on a combination of historical data, market analysis, economic indicators, and emerging trends.','public','2026-03-28T21:57:50.914425','2026-03-28T21:57:50.914429','data.iowa.gov','Katie Green',NULL,'2a4049a7-c462-4b8c-81b4-819feedc04aa','Iowa metadata','06b593c100e9f4da6c372bb261739c1c3750790004208aac92ad4c6d369e2c35','1.1','2026-03-28T21:57:50.914425','2026-03-28T21:57:50.914429','Workforce',NULL,0,'state-of-iowa'),('59ad915a-ade0-43cd-a6cd-b71853b1c657','PLATE SHAPE MODEL OF COMET 9P/TEMPEL 1 V2.0','Plate shape model of comet 9P/Tempel 1, as derived from Deep Impact and Stardust NEXT images obtained around the times of closest approach to the comet.','public','2026-03-13T17:07:48.072235','2026-03-13T17:07:48.072241','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','02eea08e-f029-46d7-b4d7-541327a69dfd','NASA Data.json','198b5110e6edb035e2cf7cf5807827a133f234ad1ac396997938ffc861a99089','1.1','2026-03-13T17:07:48.072235','2026-03-13T17:07:48.072241','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('59af79eb-b1ff-47fb-bf33-06cec3d8659f','VEGA2 PLASMAG-1 PLASMA ENERGY ANALYSER DATA V1.0','The PLASMAG-1 instument package included six different sensors: A0 plasma impact detector for measuring neutral particle flux, (manufactured by R. Grard, ESA/ESTEC, Noordwijk, The Netherlands) A1 Faraday cup for measuring integral ion flux from solar direction, A2 Faraday cup for measuring integral ion flux and neutral particles from ram direction, A3 spherical electrostatic analyzer for measuring ions from ram direction in the energy range of 15 eV - 3.6 keV in 120 logarithmically spaced channels, A4 spherical electrostatic analyzer for measuring ions from solar direction in the energy range of 60 eV - 30 keV in 60 logarithmically spaced channels, A5 cylindrical electrostatic analyzer for measuring ions perpendicular to the ecliptic plane in the energy range of 2 eV - 10 keV in 30 logarithmically spaced channels.','public','2026-03-13T17:37:35.159178','2026-03-13T17:37:35.159184','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','0b2e4cba-6440-4d78-9017-fb7afd3ad49d','NASA Data.json','f31e144f6d56c9be3a6e9bed013fb2c38fc242a76db9fe2dc2ed72faa6f69cc0','1.1','2026-03-13T17:37:35.159178','2026-03-13T17:37:35.159184','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('59b0a206-04fe-4537-af39-8d7a6b42e0aa','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 1 0592 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 1 phase 2014-11-20 to 2015-03-10. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-02-20T00:28:05.000 to 2015-02-20T10:10:44.500.','public','2026-03-13T18:55:01.574483','2026-03-13T18:55:01.574489','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','6e892721-369a-4c8d-9c4f-5ba34e590fec','NASA Data.json','39180dc8d0cfd9806a03a50eee62dcc5cf51b739e2e29260412d1479f3a927fe','1.1','2026-03-13T18:55:01.574483','2026-03-13T18:55:01.574489','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('59b3b560-a267-452e-bcff-7bb7a1ed8bb5','CASSINI S MIMI CHEMS SENSOR CALIBRATED DATA V1.0','The Cassini Magnetospheric Imaging Instrument(MIMI) Charge Energy Mass      Spectrometer (CHEMS) contains a deflection system and an overall field      of view of 159 x 4 deg. that is comprised of three distinct energetic      particle telescopes each having a field of view of 53 x 4. All      telescopes share the same deflection mechanism, but each has its own      start and stop microchannel plate (MCP) and its own solid-state      detector (SSD). Much of the data returned by CHEMS is separated by      telescope. The deflection plate power supply (DPPS) has 32 different      voltages that can be applied across the deflection plates. For any      single DPPS step, the electrostatic analyzer only transmits incoming      ions within a narrow range of energy per charge (a 3% pass band).      The CHEMS calibrated data set includes the Pulse Height Analysis (PHA)      data collected during the Saturn tour. CHEMS PHA provides a list of      individually detected particles, with specific detection parameters      for each event, including TOF, energy deposited in the SSD, and      telescope number.      The energy per charge data for six ion species (H+, He+, H2+, He++,      O++, W+)  are presented in two forms. (The W+ water ion group includes      O+, OH+, H20+ and H30+). One form is a set of tables which are of      variable length and use a comma to separate various fields, and the      other is a PDF file containing the energy per charge spectrograms and      are based on CHEMS PHA data.      The original data has been decommutated and decoded by software at the      Applied Physics Laboratory (APL) and calibrated and further processed      by software at the University of Maryland.      This data set should be among the first used by a user of any of the      MIMI CHEMS archive as it will lead one to information required to      search for more detailed or highly specialized features in the      original data.','public','2026-03-13T17:52:59.610096','2026-03-13T17:52:59.610104','planetary plasma interactions','Planetary Data System','026:00','b5a5940b-2a76-4429-a415-0554c7913f81','NASA Data.json','ec4bc76cf134c6ec90edd287723208a0517ec8eb4f98624a2c0575e3d3a7923f','1.1','2026-03-13T17:52:59.610096','2026-03-13T17:52:59.610104','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('59b4a068-862d-4ecb-9320-300aa983b202','AIRSAR_TOPSAR_DEM','AIRSAR topographic SAR digital elevation model product','public','2026-03-13T19:02:34.039885','2026-03-13T19:02:34.039891','NASA/JPL/RDC;ASF','Earthdata Forum','026:00','afa906d3-db27-4f52-8c53-0960bce3aeb9','NASA Data.json','4ad1e2ea153589da3333b64ab75f19d66d0b74680a053d5d56099f5f9eac76d0','1.1','2026-03-13T19:02:34.039885','2026-03-13T19:02:34.039891','Earth Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('59ba5822-c08a-474d-a025-5d0422a442c4','VG2 JUP PLS DERIVED ION INBOUND SOLARWIND 96SEC V1.0','This data set contains solar wind plasma     data upstream of Jupiter before the Voyager 2 encounter. Fit and moment     parameters are given; the fit parameters assume a convected isotropic     proton Maxwellian distribution. Use of fit parameters is recommended as     these are normally more accurate. Since only the first 72 or last 72     energy/charge channels are telemetered to Earth from each M-mode spectra,     derived parameters change significantly only every other set of spectra     so the effective time resolution is 196 s.','public','2026-03-13T19:54:24.745185','2026-03-13T19:54:24.745193','planetary plasma interactions','Planetary Data System','026:00','46855c1e-d3c2-4b08-94cc-6853b41fdc39','NASA Data.json','90879a4e003b77848e319f0456c63a4b9f7eb37cd96a2c04676eab0446436929','1.1','2026-03-13T19:54:24.745185','2026-03-13T19:54:24.745193','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('59c57616-6b9b-4a6f-bb50-b9bac1da1656','HST SATURN WFPC2 3 RING PLANE CROSSING V1.0','UNK','public','2026-03-13T17:09:52.732039','2026-03-13T17:09:52.732047','Planetary Rings','Planetary Data System','026:00','f3cd5272-0502-4c6a-935a-c22c3924e87c','NASA Data.json','6a4814cfe3d7ad521dccf200f27b817ceb4d032dad9af9b86c98f8d01db2c6fe','1.1','2026-03-13T17:09:52.732039','2026-03-13T17:09:52.732047','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('59dd33a1-732e-4ac2-83ee-d3bd034f77be','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 3 1029 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 3 phase 2015-07-01 to 2015-10-21. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-09-13T03:07:50.000 to 2015-09-13T09:43:10.500.','public','2026-03-13T19:57:53.207082','2026-03-13T19:57:53.207091','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','f488c638-2432-48e5-a61e-94a85cdc3fbe','NASA Data.json','bddb419805306b87741c66f4fe7a918c07b318c533fca7d1dfb3110c210a574f','1.1','2026-03-13T19:57:53.207082','2026-03-13T19:57:53.207091','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('5a3dff0f-fc8c-41cc-a8ae-7ddc9e5eeafd','Okeanos Explorer (EX1804): NESDIS VIIRS Satellite','While this Okeanos Explorer mission will be managed by NESDIS\'s Visible Infrared Imaging Radiometer Suite (VIIRS) Satellite project, OER will have a mapping lead, Mike White, onboard to perform opportunistic multibeam surveying. OER data management will manage these data in the same manner as other Okeanos missions.','public','2026-03-28T23:16:55.312823','2026-03-28T23:16:55.312829',NULL,NULL,NULL,'1be0aa3e-929f-4b62-8f43-bdb80491941b','NCDDC OER',NULL,NULL,'2026-03-28T23:16:55.312823','2026-03-28T23:16:55.312829',NULL,NULL,NULL,'noaa-gov'),('5a5c4dd1-d00c-458e-9381-dd8f16ee78ad','Data from: Carbon and water dynamics of Old World Bluestem in the U.S. Southern Great Plains','<p dir=\"ltr\">The dataset includes daily fluxes of net ecosystem CO2 exchange (NEE, g C m-2 d-1), gross primary production (GPP, g C m-2 d-1), ecosystem respiration (ER, g C m-2 d-1), and evapotranspiration (ET, mm d-1) from 2021 to 2024 for an Old World Bluestem pasture at the USDA-ARS, El Reno, Oklahoma.</p><p dir=\"ltr\">The study site, Old World Bluestem (OWB) pasture (~63 ha), was established in the 1980s on a native tallgrass prairie site. It is located at the United States Department of Agriculture – Agricultural Research Service (USDA-ARS), Oklahoma and Central Plains Agricultural Research Center, El Reno (35.5467º N, 98.0452º W, and 435 masl), Oklahoma.</p><p dir=\"ltr\">The eddy covariance (EC) tower was equipped with an open-path infrared gas analyzer (LI-7500 RS, LI-COR Biosciences, Lincoln, NE, USA) integrated with a three-dimensional sonic anemometer (CSAT3, Campbell Scientific Inc., Logan, UT, USA). These sensors were mounted at a height of ~2.8 m above the ground surface. The tower had enough fetch extending several hundred meters in all directions to ensure representative flux measurements from the OWB pasture.</p><p dir=\"ltr\">Raw high-frequency EC data were processed using EddyPro software (version 7.0.6, LI-COR Biosciences, Lincoln, NE, USA) in its Express configuration to compute half-hourly (30-min) fluxes. Gap-filling of half-hourly eddy fluxes and meteorological variables, as well as the partitioning of NEE (using nighttime partitioning) into its component fluxes (GPP and ER), was conducted using the REddyProc (https://www.bgc-jena.mpg.de/REddyProc/ui/REddyProc.php).</p>','public','2026-03-13T22:47:17.860153','2026-03-13T22:47:17.860160','Agricultural Research Service','Wagle, Pradeep','005:18','7ce76e50-5a54-43e7-bfbc-d70550a3b319','USDA JSON','5fa8c30caa64f84a5dca7264e32801cf89087567b01cf347ef8080b437e0add2','1.1','2026-03-13T22:47:17.860153','2026-03-13T22:47:17.860160',NULL,'005:040',0,'usda-gov'),('5a70e13d-b8a2-48e2-8188-51aaaed3b3ac','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 1 0456 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 1 phase 2014-11-20 to 2015-03-10. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2014-11-25T02:48:05.000 to 2014-11-25T13:18:11.500.','public','2026-03-13T18:36:02.341772','2026-03-13T18:36:02.341778','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','c2ee1044-a873-4ce5-9490-da88b9143a65','NASA Data.json','a7791dbb1e8a43dc87ed804bda04735db38e110813a5d89a3437eea3acd6af81','1.1','2026-03-13T18:36:02.341772','2026-03-13T18:36:02.341778','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('5a8cf7fa-a882-4571-80da-7e08045b5f5c','ROSETTA-ORBITER/ROSETTA-LANDER CAL CONSERT 2 CVP2 V1.0','This archive contains edited data from the CONSERT instrument onboard ROSETTA Orbiter and Lander, acquired during the Commissioning 2 phase. It also contains documentation which describes the CONSERT experiment. The data archived in this data set conform to the Planetary Data System (PDS) Standards, Version 3.6. This data set supersedes RO/RL-CAL-CONSERT-2-CVP-V1.0.','public','2026-03-13T20:08:56.855377','2026-03-13T20:08:56.855382','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','f786b1eb-2ec1-4af7-ad81-e7a9e8da9b90','NASA Data.json','60dfbf956ff440c87f98a4a34a67f627166c805148572df55fe52c61772a5b0d','1.1','2026-03-13T20:08:56.855377','2026-03-13T20:08:56.855382','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('5a95954b-8884-4a43-ae7a-7b5f60461f85','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 2 0809 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 2 phase 2015-03-11 to 2015-06-30. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-05-26T06:57:00.000 to 2015-05-26T09:11:07.000.','public','2026-03-13T17:10:18.177503','2026-03-13T17:10:18.177508','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','ac380e91-e507-435a-a8fb-65efab90f198','NASA Data.json','bb3d990f1a410b31f077d6b427058ccd2791b550dbb01ecefcc19dcc6ffba27d','1.1','2026-03-13T17:10:18.177503','2026-03-13T17:10:18.177508','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('5a9f3e91-e674-439a-b86b-ec11e3cf3f04','Continuous Fixed Station Water Quality Measurements in Canaveral National Seashore, July 2005 (Certified)','This dataset represents continuous water quality measurements that were taken at a fixed point in Canaveral National Seashore during the month of July, 2005 as a part of the Fixed Station Water Quality Monitoring protocol that was developed by the Southeast Coast I&M Network (SECN). The measurements were taken by a YSI 6600 ESD Multi-Parameter Long Term Water Quality Monitoring Datasonde unit that serves as the standard fixed station water quality monitoring equipment for all similar operations conducted by the SECN. The following parameters were measured at 30 minute intervals during the time period that has been specified: Water Temperature, Specific Conductivity, Salinity, Dissolved Oxygen (DO), DO Concentration, Shallow Depth, pH Level, and Turbidity. Any anomalies noted regarding these parameters have also been noted in separate fields. Please note that these measurements have been certified by network personnel.','public','2026-03-26T05:28:57.246621','2026-03-26T05:28:57.246628','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','6ca44048-4b47-44c2-bad1-59983f614642','DOI NPS DCAT-US','45b66f12df507da3805282112f6132b5e74490a94b7c5379f9fa5868b23266b3','1.1','2026-03-26T05:28:57.246621','2026-03-26T05:28:57.246628','Vector Dataset','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('5abd0936-09b0-4947-85e2-ca2270e6e28b','VG1 JUP PLASMA DERIVED ELECTRON MOMENTS                                         96.0 SEC V1.1','Voyager 1 Plasma Experiment (PLS) averaged electron moments 96.0 second data at Jupiter.','public','2026-03-13T18:58:04.816832','2026-03-13T18:58:04.816839','planetary plasma interactions','Planetary Data System','026:00','b71df667-99cc-4f35-9a3f-3126f083982b','NASA Data.json','8b54bf0d87d4c3ee5d7a55a9b675e862657706f8a6d86d1c7036b5ac92d1cd9d','1.1','2026-03-13T18:58:04.816832','2026-03-13T18:58:04.816839','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('5acfea78-1484-4479-b669-ce900b1cc778','Geospatial data for the Vegetation Mapping Inventory Project of Organ Pipe Cactus National Monument','The files linked to this reference are the geospatial data created as part of the completion of the baseline vegetation inventory project for the NPS park unit. Current format is ArcGIS file geodatabase but older formats may exist as shapefiles.\n\nFrom 2017 to 2020, the Sonoran Desert Network conducted a vegetation mapping and characterization project at Organ Pipe Cactus National Monument (ORPI) to update the 1981 vegetation map (Warren et al. 1981). This work, which is part of the National Park Service (NPS) Vegetation Mapping Inventory Program, aimed to provide park managers with a digital vegetation map meeting national standards for spatial and thematic accuracy and supporting regional and national comparisons.\nThe 1981 map, which described 29 vegetation community types using the Brown, Lowe, and Pase classification system (Brown et al. 1979), served as a baseline for the update. Using fine-scale (30 cm) aerial imagery from ca. 2008, modern mapping methods, and new relevé plot data, vegetation communities were reclassified under the United States National Vegetation Classification System (USNVCS) at the association level. Map unit boundaries were aligned with the adjacent Cabeza Prieta National Wildlife Refuge (CPNWR) vegetation map boundaries where applicable and possible. The study area covers approximately 347,058 hectares (857,600 ac) of ORPI.\nField surveys occurred primarily in winter 2017 and spring 2018, with two additional sampling rounds in spring 2019 and fall 2020 targeting under-sampled areas. Crews collected 323 classification plots and 1,065 photo points, resulting in the identification or update of 34 vegetation types at the USNVC association level.','public','2026-03-21T04:25:20.135558','2026-03-21T04:25:20.135563','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','a835ef38-f7f8-4eeb-8989-da875fd7ca5b','DOI NPS DCAT-US','34cd59311975c33952ddfbc4898ca7020e6b52755499596da8af3864fde4e7c9','1.1','2026-03-21T04:25:20.135558','2026-03-21T04:25:20.135563','geospatial','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('5af98912-a085-4381-a6d6-95791c638ecf','FRA Regulated Mode Major Security Events','This file includes event data reported to the National Transit Database (NTD) for Commuter Rail (CR) and Alaska Railroad (AR) modes, as well as Heavy Rail (HR) service reported for Port Authority Trans Hudson (NTD ID: 20098), Hybrid Rail (YR) service for the Tri-County Metropolitan Transportation District of Oregon (NTD ID: 00008),  Hybrid Rail (YR) service for Denton County Transportation Authority (NTD ID: 60101), and Hybrid Rail (YR) service for Capital Metropolitan Transportation Authority (NTD ID: 60048). Because these services fall under the safety oversight of the Federal Railroad Administration, the agencies are not required to report Safety Events (e.g., collisions, derailments, etc.) to the Federal Transit Administration through the NTD. Security events occurring on transit-owned property for these entities are reported to NTD, but excluded from other files to preserve the integrity of those datasets. They are presented in this file for completeness and should be considered by any user attempting to understand the scope and scale of reportable Security Events reported by public transit operators.','public','2026-03-24T12:09:03.455726','2026-03-24T12:09:03.455732','Federal Transit Administration','NTD Program Support','021:36','6df28b21-af55-4664-97e9-05027f8b4e0b','DOT Socrata Data.json','1c616bb0a08e400811777eaa6e3f08b22ec52aff92a5c773c5f98f6d845656b0','1.1','2026-03-24T12:09:03.455726','2026-03-24T12:09:03.455732','Public Transit','021:061',0,'dot-gov'),('5afa89e6-5db8-485f-a4b7-ff828d866098','VG2 LECP 6 MINUTE NEPTUNE STEP DATA','This data set consists of 6.4 minute step    proton and ion counting rate data from the LECP experiment on VOYAGER 2    from the Neptune far encounter.','public','2026-03-13T20:00:21.686011','2026-03-13T20:00:21.686017','planetary plasma interactions','Planetary Data System','026:00','c2c3d469-478c-4566-b44d-a5411658ee51','NASA Data.json','ff4c6c3463496da85fdc29f96da012304296347a0871f9170a0659e2229f4d8c','1.1','2026-03-13T20:00:21.686011','2026-03-13T20:00:21.686017','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('5b1d6593-b42a-413a-95f1-158d485ee01a','MARS EXPRESS HRSC RADIOMETRIC RDR EXTENSION6 V4.0','This CODMAC level 3 data set contains radiometrically calibrated data products acquired by the HRSC camera on the Mars Express spacecraft, covering the orbits 16469 to 18975.','public','2026-03-13T17:27:43.971892','2026-03-13T17:27:43.971897','Geosciences','Earthdata Forum','026:00','8cb6cf5a-9b6d-4a91-8994-16d9dac7e6c6','NASA Data.json','f3ecbb0109e6a88d40fd1c5aacad821cd7d10e7a5d77538d99e69c59d5f55bff','1.1','2026-03-13T17:27:43.971892','2026-03-13T17:27:43.971897','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('5b429834-cb88-418c-b816-8411f4e25151','MARS EXPRESS MARS MARSIS EXPERIMENT DATA RECORD EXT 4 V1.0','This dataset contains the                    scientific telemetry produced by the MARSIS                    instrument after editing for duplicated and                    corrupted packets, together with geometric                    information computed on ground to locate                    observations in space and time. Both subsurface                    and ionosphere sounding data are included in                    the dataset.','public','2026-03-13T18:15:18.904283','2026-03-13T18:15:18.904290','planetary plasma interactions','Planetary Data System','026:00','0bd76d4c-ef94-4d73-91d1-4b45d2041239','NASA Data.json','cfe68eefca5ef54106f4fea4ff14775d4b85296bcef469b31b6578e320917479','1.1','2026-03-13T18:15:18.904283','2026-03-13T18:15:18.904290','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('5b531bba-2f66-4417-8098-f841a1c92897','PHOENIX MARS MECA OPTICAL MICROSCOPE 2 EDR  VERSION 1.0','The Microscopy, Electrochemistry, and  Conductivity Analyzer (MECA) experiment on the Mars Phoenix Lander  consists of four instrument components plus command electronics. This  MECA Imaging EDR data set contains data from one of the four  MECA components, the Optical Microscope (OM).','public','2026-03-13T16:37:56.083449','2026-03-13T16:37:56.083457','Imaging','Planetary Data System','026:00','7ee57bec-410c-45e4-87a6-1216d9d02524','NASA Data.json','e1bbc6c85c3d12f9aead8b7d12fb8e6d2a3289451ae4e6749d97225faedad75a','1.1','2026-03-13T16:37:56.083449','2026-03-13T16:37:56.083457','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('5b53a2ed-9726-4e10-aa9e-37e32bf1834e','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSIWAC 4 PRL-MTP003 RDR V2.0','This CODMAC level 4 data set contains radiometric calibrated and geometric distortion corrected (resampled) image data in W/m^2/sr/nm, acquired by the OSIRIS Wide Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft during the PRELANDING mission phase, covering the period from 2014-05-07T12:48:00.000 to 2014-06-04T10:49:59.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V2.0 supersedes previous deliveries of the same dataset with the following changes since the last version: Lien corrected dataset after October 2018 PSA/PDS external peer review. Updated documentation and ancillary files, added document on bandpass filter. Updated SCIENCE_USER_GUIDE_V03.PDF to include one section about FAQ and one section about image data quality. Added shutter backtravel and readout issues to image quality map. Updated DATA_QUALITY_ID keyword in image header. Improved handling of images with missing packets.','public','2026-03-13T18:54:02.214362','2026-03-13T18:54:02.214367','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','576545cf-e32a-4619-ba53-41d608dd98ba','NASA Data.json','73ca20add7788320a30d4da455c518b2bfb98a3cb2c5195a619d9cee79c32564','1.1','2026-03-13T18:54:02.214362','2026-03-13T18:54:02.214367','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('5b629c46-97fe-4af9-8113-78e95626d769','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSINAC 4 ESC3-MTP021 RDR-INFLDSTR V1.0','This CODMAC level 4 data set contains solar stray-light corrected, in-field stray-light corrected,  radiometric calibrated and geometric distortion corrected  (resampled) image data in W/m^2/sr/nm,  acquired by the OSIRIS Narrow Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft  during the COMET ESCORT 3 mission phase, covering the period  from 2015-09-22T23:25:00.000 to 2015-10-20T23:24:59.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V1.0 is the first version of this dataset: Lien corrected dataset after September 2019 PSA/PDS external peer review.','public','2026-03-13T19:46:38.165070','2026-03-13T19:46:38.165076','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','b39249aa-7e7e-43b1-9cf5-8ecc08736473','NASA Data.json','a7a16cb01124d25753416beed1f1f3ab3aa6abebcf63088ace9dea79d62287ce','1.1','2026-03-13T19:46:38.165070','2026-03-13T19:46:38.165076','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('5b81431c-61b6-4c08-8990-7a3e244bbc14','MARS EXPRESS MARS MRS 5 OCCULTATION 9101 V1.0','This data set contains ionospheric electron density profiles as well as neutral atmospheric temperature, pressure and number density profiles derived from the MEX Radio Science experiment MaRS. The data set covers measurements from the occultation season 01.','public','2026-03-13T17:46:25.467881','2026-03-13T17:46:25.467889','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','68e85f2f-6c16-4582-a6b5-16c24354b448','NASA Data.json','8508eca4992075fd51c70702f08db7c4d24717a1ac557f82c983765628a67108','1.1','2026-03-13T17:46:25.467881','2026-03-13T17:46:25.467889','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('5b83acb4-d587-44b5-b63e-0757cd4da3e3','Data Access for Highway Performance Monitoring System (HPMS)','This story provides data access for highway performance monitoring system (HPMS).','public','2026-03-20T11:38:21.770647','2026-03-20T11:38:21.770652','data.transportation.gov','FHWA-Datahub','021:15','74cb04f7-fca7-4741-9b7f-08e612b0123f','DOT Socrata Data.json','4adc59fc25d18a8381438aa47ff9c2cc6876c4fed631a8f70518c3df214ead45','1.1','2026-03-20T11:38:21.770647','2026-03-20T11:38:21.770652','Roadways and Bridges','021:009',0,'dot-gov'),('5b8d4174-2fdc-4cec-b423-7be523038dff','Loop Current Observations in the Eastern Gulf of Mexico - SAIC Mooring Data (Scalars)','Phsyical Oceanographic Circulation Study','public','2026-03-26T19:16:52.711846','2026-03-26T19:16:52.711852',NULL,NULL,NULL,'94df2094-857e-4d16-8919-2f9ab6298cc3','ioos',NULL,NULL,'2026-03-26T19:16:52.711846','2026-03-26T19:16:52.711852',NULL,NULL,NULL,'noaa-gov'),('5b9f10b8-47a5-426a-8e47-e12de33e0668','HPMS Urban Area Summaries 2023','The Highway Performance Monitoring System Urban Area Summaries table contains daily travel and demographics data for all local functional system roads for each adjusted urbanized area.','public','2026-03-28T13:33:10.800663','2026-03-28T13:33:10.800670','Federal Highway Administration','Office of Highway Policy Information','021:15','ec0263a4-3332-44a1-b1cb-0a39b7f2d17d','DOT Socrata Data.json','c722e7730258bc66f0ceb50b1fdd77bc4ec2b6bf64abd328bcd0927f06ab6bdf','1.1','2026-03-28T13:33:10.800663','2026-03-28T13:33:10.800670','Roadways and Bridges','021:009',0,'dot-gov'),('5bae9525-7ea5-446c-ac3c-53b0d6bbb820','Inventory of Major Medical Equipment in Missouri','This report is prepared by the Certificate of Need (CON) Program and does not include all medical equipment in Missouri. Refer to other reliable sources to obtain numbers of existing units for CON proposals.','public','2026-03-22T03:21:40.251730','2026-03-22T03:21:40.251734','data.mo.gov','Alison Dorge',NULL,'7cd4591f-2b9b-4478-9224-b434dd787975','MO JSON','fc3a6a8d2b53ffec277e0119271926b70eae68d971a03f92de09a330251582c6','1.1','2026-03-22T03:21:40.251730','2026-03-22T03:21:40.251734',NULL,NULL,0,'state-of-missouri'),('5bbca2df-89af-43c3-acbb-90446c6ec940','VG1 SAT MAG RESAMPLED HELIOGRAPHIC (RTN)                                      COORDS 48.0SEC V1.0','This data set includes calibrated    magnetic field data acquired by the Voyager 1 Low Field Magnetometer (LFM)    during the Saturn encounter. Coverage begins in the solar wind inbound to    Saturn and continues past the last outbound bowshock crossing. The data    are in Heliographic (RTN) coordinates and have been averaged from the 9.6    second summary rate to a 48 second sample rate. All magnetic field    measurements are given in nanoTesla (nT). The magnetic field data    are calibrated (see the calibration description included in the    Voyager 1 Magnetometer instrument catalog file for details).','public','2026-03-13T17:39:45.924071','2026-03-13T17:39:45.924076','planetary plasma interactions','Planetary Data System','026:00','ff3937fc-0e95-488b-9a80-85c63fcc34c6','NASA Data.json','4acdd1ad7630efedce08e9f1cbfde51666a686c1fd690b71d4f3a419e8f2b198','1.1','2026-03-13T17:39:45.924071','2026-03-13T17:39:45.924076','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('5bc7a030-8412-45ca-8b35-b645c85fa935','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P/CAL ALICE 3 PRL V1.0','This data set contains CODMAC level 3 data acquired by the Rosetta Orbiter ALICE UV Spectrometer during the comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko prelanding mission phase, which took place between 2014-01-21 and 2014-11-18.','public','2026-03-13T19:12:41.545015','2026-03-13T19:12:41.545022','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','56ef8178-307f-454c-a594-ce54417bbf01','NASA Data.json','273d813ea90f5edea4a9b8115bc521ebdabc0cd07907e211565f14bd96815830','1.1','2026-03-13T19:12:41.545015','2026-03-13T19:12:41.545022','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('5bc939d3-1382-4773-aedc-ff5e6d702869','Geologic map of the West Susitna area, parts of the Tyonek C-3, C-4, D-4, and D-5 quadrangles, Alaska','Geologic map of the West Susitna area, parts of the Tyonek C-3, C-4, D-4, and D-5 quadrangles, Alaska, Preliminary Interpretive Report 2026-1, prevents surficial and bedrock geology for approximately 500 mi2 of the Tyonek C-3, C-4, D-4, and D-5 quadrangles in western Cook Inlet. These products summarize findings of the West Susitna STATEMAP project, a 1:50,000-scale geologic mapping campaign across an area north of Cook Inlet that has attracted interest for resource development, alternative energy, and recreation. The map area includes approximately 50 miles of the West Susitna Access Corridor, which is proposed to connect Anchorage to the Happy River valley on the western margin of the Susitna Basin. Previous surficial and bedrock geologic mapping in the region has primarily been reconnaissance-level and limited to 1:250,000-scale detail. Field data were collected during a helicopter-supported program from July 16-28, 2024. Surficial geology, initially interpreted through a desktop study in ArcGIS, was verified in the field during the 2024 campaign. The desktop study incorporated new interpretations of remotely sensed imagery combined with previously published geologic mapping and relevant literature. Together, these datasets form the basis for updated geologic unit definitions, geomorphic interpretations, and structural observations presented in this map series. This mapping offers stakeholders information about geologic hazards, including those associated with seismic activity, near the proposed corridor alignment. The resulting surficial and bedrock framework further supports refined interpretations of Quaternary and bedrock geologic history in the western Susitna Basin region. The map is published on two sheets to accommodate its scale and geographic extent. The dataset provides geologic, structural, stratigraphic, and geochronologic information organized according to the GeMS and AK GeMS mapping schemas. The complete report, geodatabase, and ESRI fonts and style files are available from the Alaska Division of Geological & Geophysical Surveys website: http://doi.org/10.14509/32075.','public','2026-03-15T03:17:25.298562','2026-03-15T03:17:25.298569',NULL,NULL,NULL,'fd424654-5581-40ec-8f16-30c20a7eb91c','Alaska Division of Geological and Geophysical Surveys',NULL,NULL,'2026-03-15T03:17:25.298562','2026-03-15T03:17:25.298569',NULL,NULL,NULL,'state-of-alaska'),('5bf2a423-4772-43f9-b32f-22f7b2f4bf75','NRC 825','NRC Health Center Consent for Release of Medical Records. Fillable form in Adobe Portable Document Format (PDF) with information submitted by NRC stakeholder - licensee, applicant, or NRC employee/contractor.','non-public','2026-03-20T19:43:49.435489','2026-03-20T19:43:49.435493','Nuclear Regulatory Commission','Ilka Solorio','429:00','0523cae2-82f7-49cc-8899-931e78c0ec20','NRC Data.json Harvest Source','303fcd8e862c4512828908516d5329fd86c38e5045cef2cab7ae20b67422f769','1.1','2026-03-20T19:43:49.435489','2026-03-20T19:43:49.435493',NULL,'000:000',0,'nrc-gov'),('5c06f7f4-dd43-47ae-afe5-63aed43ec919','APL_visitor_count','Visitor count at APL locations','public','2026-03-25T14:45:41.911005','2026-03-25T14:45:41.911012','data.austintexas.gov','Austin Public Library Owners',NULL,'ba29c508-fdf3-463a-93e6-ac77b16b0ddf','City of Austin Data.json','b67a800e9390491063d10ec64145259eeb83d813633d2f507cabbbb2db33aa0c','1.1','2026-03-25T14:45:41.911005','2026-03-25T14:45:41.911012','Recreation and Culture',NULL,0,'city-of-austin'),('5c0c21cc-06f0-4b1c-b50c-a049e13d3481','DAWN VIR RAW (EDR) CERES VISIBLE SPECTRA  V1.0','This volume contains the digitalnumbers (DN) contained in the telemetry (TM) packages of the VIR-VISinstrument on board of the spacecraft DAWN. The data are from theCeres Encounter and Extended mission phases, which occurred 2014-12-26to 2017-04-29.','public','2026-03-13T19:24:51.064123','2026-03-13T19:24:51.064129','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','1330e751-c8e3-4626-890d-023a119e916e','NASA Data.json','a7da51706694a0958ea653b381d23706969303a23980d33773583c5c143ab06a','1.1','2026-03-13T19:24:51.064123','2026-03-13T19:24:51.064129','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('5c173ee0-4969-46cf-8d16-2b44d7cfc8f3','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSINAC 4 ESC2-MTP015 RDR-STR-REFL V1.0','This CODMAC level 4 data set contains solar stray light corrected, radiometric calibrated and geometric distortion corrected (resampled) image data in in reflectance units (normalized and thus without unit), acquired by the OSIRIS Narrow Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft during the COMET ESCORT 2 mission phase, covering the period from 2015-04-08T11:25:00.000 to 2015-05-05T23:24:59.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V1.0 is the first version of this dataset: Lien corrected dataset after October 2018 PSA/PDS external peer review.','public','2026-03-13T18:06:21.774764','2026-03-13T18:06:21.774771','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','1c3aa948-141d-4e79-80dc-ee8cbbfe7c76','NASA Data.json','98e0071ed4c4af3e38eee39d28787a7e28175ecc155ebd3838d75c3b82af3640','1.1','2026-03-13T18:06:21.774764','2026-03-13T18:06:21.774771','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('5c479ecf-6935-44bb-9b5f-2fa4035133a8','NEW HORIZONS  REX JUPITER ENCOUNTER  RAW V1.0','This data set contains Raw data taken by the New Horizons  Radio Science Experiment  instrument during the  Jupiter encounter  mission phase. This is VERSION 1.0 of this data set.','public','2026-03-13T18:34:22.205883','2026-03-13T18:34:22.205889','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','5572314f-262b-4bf2-81ae-f94398e2bf6b','NASA Data.json','37778ecd6dc31b514403fac8e503d4a7ab12555a6197e252c34740daaffa099f','1.1','2026-03-13T18:34:22.205883','2026-03-13T18:34:22.205889','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('5c4860be-ab81-4df1-8f30-6186fe52a265','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P MIRO 3 EXT1 V3.0','This data set contains Spectroscopic and Continuum, level 3 data, in the form of table files, taken during the ROSETTA COMET EXTENSION 1 phase of the Rosetta mission to comet 67P/CHURYUMOV-GERASIMENKO by the MIRO instrument. It supercedes data sets with a lower version number. The updates include a new calibration algorithm and modified documentation.','public','2026-03-13T17:01:25.724068','2026-03-13T17:01:25.724074','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','e878f778-83be-44fc-8790-ceaec6c8816b','NASA Data.json','af4afa621e86f525ca91dba76a1a0a6d2af0cbbb933e0f7d5b710440e89f4e6d','1.1','2026-03-13T17:01:25.724068','2026-03-13T17:01:25.724074','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('5c5cec83-99af-454a-bb4d-06c459266a88','MARS EXPRESS MARS MRS 1/2/3                                     EXTENDED MISSION 8 4323 V1.0','This is a Mars Express                                     Radio Science data set, collected                                     during the extended mission phase                                     2023-01-01 to 2023-12-31.                                     It is a Occultation                                     measurement and covers the time                                     2023-08-15T14:15:12.000 to                                     2023-08-15T18:32:00.000.','public','2026-03-13T18:39:42.872093','2026-03-13T18:39:42.872100','geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','440f8269-27ec-488b-93e7-fbce78da1265','NASA Data.json','ecb802109e81f4be90f83fe2d164b1995e152ad2494aa170a04efde16273e2ce','1.1','2026-03-13T18:39:42.872093','2026-03-13T18:39:42.872100','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('5c72d8c4-5469-4d1c-a6d0-8e419cc5c0e4','NLR HPC Eagle Jobs Data and Additional Energy Metrics','Dataset DescriptionThis dataset contains anonymized job-level records from the Eagle high-performance computing (HPC) system. Each record represents a Slurm batch job and includes scheduling metadata, resource requests, resource utilization, CPU and GPU energy consumption measurements, and computed efficiency metrics. Personally identifiable fields (user, account, and job name) have been replaced with cryptographic hashes. Energy metrics include both TDP-estimated CPU energy and measured node-level and GPU-level energy from iLO and Ganglia monitoring systems.Developed byNational Laboratory of the Rockies (NLR), ROR: https://ror.org/036266993Contributed byHPC Operations and Data Analytics teams at NLR.Dataset short descriptionAnonymized Slurm job records from the NLR Eagle HPC system, including job scheduling, resource allocation, CPU and GPU energy measurements, and efficiency metrics.Over what timeframe was the data collected or generated? Does this timeframe align with when the underlying phenomena or events occurred?The dataset covers the operational lifetime of the Eagle HPC system, with timestamps in Mountain Time zone. Slurm data was processed nightly after midnight, so the database was always current through the prior day. The collection timeframe aligns directly with the underlying job scheduling events as they occurred on the Eagle system.What resources were used?Facilities:Eagle HPC System, National Laboratory of the Rockies (NLR), ROR: https://ror.org/036266993Funding:U.S. Department of Energy, Office of Energy Efficiency and Renewable Energy (EERE).Other Supporting Entities:N/ASharing/Access InformationReuse restrictions placed on the data:The dataset has been anonymized by hashing sensitive fields (user, account, and job name). Reuse is subject to the license specified in this datacard. Users should not attempt to re-identify individuals from hashed fields.Provide DOIs, and bibtex citations to publications that cite or use the data.N/AProvide DOIs, citations, or links to other publicly accessible locations of the data.N/AProvide DOIs, citations, or links and descriptions of relationships to ancillary data sets.This dataset is derived from the Eagle schema of the NLR HPC job database.Data &amp; File OverviewList all files contained in the dataset.Format: File | Descriptionesif.hpc.eagle.job-anon.zip | Zipped Hive-partitioned Apache Parquet dataset containing anonymized job records from the Eagle Slurm scheduler. Each row is a parent job record with scheduling metadata, resource requests/usage, CPU and GPU energy measurements, and computed efficiency metrics.esif.hpc.eagle.job-anon-energy-metrics.zip | Zipped Hive-partitioned Apache Parquet dataset containing anonymized job records from the Eagle Slurm scheduler. Each row is a parent job record with scheduling metadata, resource requests/usage, CPU and GPU energy measurements, computed efficiency metrics, and addtional energy metrics calculated from iLO and Ganglia.datacard.md | This datacard file describing the dataset.Describe the relationship(s) between files.The Parquet dataset is the primary data file. The datacard provides documentation. In the source database, each job record may have associated job_step records (not included here) that contain finer-grained per-step resource usage data including TRESUsage fields.Describe any additional related data collected that was not included in the current data package.The source database contains additional tables not included in this extract including job_step (per-step resource usage including TRESUsage fields). Raw Slurm slurm_data JSONB fields have also been excluded.Are there multiple versions of this dataset?N/AMethodological InformationHow was the data for each instance obtained or generated?Each instance is a parent job record collected from the Slurm workload manager on the Eagle HPC system via the sacct command. The data represents real job submissions, scheduling decisions, and resource consumption. Calculated fields (efficiency metrics, energy measurements) are derived from the raw Slurm data through database triggers and batch functions. Energy data is enriched from two additional sources: node-level power from iLO (Integrated Lights-Out) monitoring, and GPU-level power from Ganglia monitoring.For each instrument, facility, or source used to generate and collect the data, what mechanisms or procedures were used?Slurm data was collected via the sacct command and ingested through the following pipeline: Eagle Jobs API → Redpanda message queue (hpc-eagle-job topic) → StreamSets on Snowy → HPCMON API → Sage PostgreSQL database. Slurm data was processed nightly after midnight. Node-level energy data was collected from iLO (HP Integrated Lights-Out) management interfaces. GPU energy data was collected from Ganglia monitoring. Both energy sources were joined to job records via node lists and time ranges.To create the final dataset, was any preprocessing/cleaning/labeling of raw data done?Yes. ','public','2026-03-21T11:56:17.284843','2026-03-21T11:56:17.284848','Computational Science','Struan Clark','019:20','87d101ad-730f-4327-b8cb-39f872d341b7','OpenEI data.json','063ac500735b60fb027754e69d48651920172bca686ad862049f1d98fe6f5c84','1.1','2026-03-21T11:56:17.284843','2026-03-21T11:56:17.284848',NULL,'019:023',0,'doe-gov'),('5c8fbab7-243a-4ff1-9b5c-57265378f273','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P NAVCAM 3 COMET ESCORT 3 MTP018 V1.0','This dataset contains ROSETTA NAVCAM RADIOMETRICALLY CALIBRATED DATA of the COMET ESCORT 3 MTP018 Phase from 01 Jul. 2015, 04:38:43 to 28 Jul. 2015, 23:02:19 when at the vicinity of target 67P/CG.','public','2026-03-13T18:55:12.299898','2026-03-13T18:55:12.299903','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','d97c7dd9-758f-4973-b84d-59ac4c625956','NASA Data.json','52f0cac635bd768194007cb3812d2576cc22e94270dbf7cbb904fdbe9a97b55d','1.1','2026-03-13T18:55:12.299898','2026-03-13T18:55:12.299903','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('5c9612c9-9fb1-4ff0-a650-5dc38085c43a','GIOTTO ION MASS SPECTROMETER HIGH INTENSITY DATA V1.0','A wide range of ion species and velocity distributions are expected to be found as the Giotto spacecraft traverses the coma of Halley\'s Comet. The outer coma is characterized by the interaction between solar wind and cometary plasmas, the inner coma by the outflow of cometary neutrals and their ionization products. The resultant demands on instrument dynamic range preclude use of a single sensor for measurements of ion composition. The Giotto Ion Mass Spectrometer (IMS) therefore consists of two sensors: one optimized for the outer and the other for the inner coma, with each obtaining complementary information in the region for which it is not optimized. Both sensors feature mass imaging characteristics, thereby permitting simultaneous measurements of several ion species by means of multi-detector arrays. The High Intensity Spectrometer (HIS) was designed to complement the HERS in the inner coma.','public','2026-03-13T18:16:57.898376','2026-03-13T18:16:57.898381','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','b79981ae-8073-4494-acb9-d278b7a49efd','NASA Data.json','29b461440dafb939d7b3565634d076c6177bb13bed3090b5363a340b81118399','1.1','2026-03-13T18:16:57.898376','2026-03-13T18:16:57.898381','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('5ca5684e-08ba-4db0-9c36-f838e28cd86b','Continuous Fixed Station Water Quality Measurements in Timucuan Ecological and Historic Preserve, October 2008 (Certified)','This dataset represents continuous water quality measurements that were taken at a fixed point in Timucuan Ecological and Historic Preserve during the month of October, 2008 as a part of the Fixed Station Water Quality Monitoring protocol that was developed by the Southeast Coast I&M Network (SECN). The measurements were taken by a YSI 6600 ESD Multi-Parameter Long Term Water Quality Monitoring Datasonde unit that serves as the standard fixed station water quality monitoring equipment for all similar operations conducted by the SECN. The following parameters were measured at 30 minute intervals during the time period that has been specified: Water Temperature, Specific Conductivity, Salinity, Dissolved Oxygen (DO), DO Concentration, Shallow Depth, pH Level, and Turbidity. Any anomalies noted regarding these parameters have also been noted in separate fields. Please note that these measurements have been certified by network personnel.','public','2026-03-26T05:33:27.447887','2026-03-26T05:33:27.447892','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','5b076732-2e9b-4410-b3c5-5843882624d5','DOI NPS DCAT-US','ef2937580a1d9350615cf622fa02aaa95dfeaf1edf61de9fc7765343aa84603a','1.1','2026-03-26T05:33:27.447887','2026-03-26T05:33:27.447892','Vector Dataset','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('5cacc28e-a513-45f9-ba81-d9b8c53d413e','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 3 1043 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 3 phase 2015-07-01 to 2015-10-21. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-09-19T10:19:40.000 to 2015-09-19T17:32:59.000.','public','2026-03-13T16:38:23.833801','2026-03-13T16:38:23.833806','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','df2265b5-70c2-4535-a3d5-447be236b372','NASA Data.json','4bcb8f694e6aec9b4d42d397a28aebe7a5e60c75349c893f1c62803ba25e13ed','1.1','2026-03-13T16:38:23.833801','2026-03-13T16:38:23.833806','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('5ce086fe-a9f9-4ac3-96cf-cb0fc24ef9ff','MPFL MARS ATM STRUCT INST AND MET PKG RAW SURFACE V1.0','Mars Pathfinder bounced down and rolled to a stop on the surface of Mars on July 4, 1997. It landed in an ancient floodplain in the Ares Vallis region of Chryse Planitia at 19.17 degrees North latitude, and 33.21 degrees West longitude.','public','2026-03-13T17:15:30.057966','2026-03-13T17:15:30.057972','Planetary Atmospheres','Planetary Data System','026:00','597f7353-a91d-4397-b0e6-68655ed6d0bc','NASA Data.json','6963130bf9f831692e73058318a097d55ee0053bf2725ecac2449b2e85b82dbe','1.1','2026-03-13T17:15:30.057966','2026-03-13T17:15:30.057972','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('5cebad1f-5db0-45a7-b2c0-70e35f01eb47','MARS EXPRESS MARS MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 7 4111 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2019-01-01 to 2020-12-31. It is a Occultation measurement and covers the time 2020-08-22T01:50:00.000 to 2020-08-22T02:40:00.000.','public','2026-03-13T17:25:38.625927','2026-03-13T17:25:38.625932','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','528b98cb-c818-4e53-8a7a-722576d1cf5c','NASA Data.json','41fba16765c515685c3d84ccb6c3ded0f58ff75a7ccfdb51c610a379719fb08f','1.1','2026-03-13T17:25:38.625927','2026-03-13T17:25:38.625932','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('5cfa7d92-eebc-4b0c-93dc-f19b6b24daa1','myUSCIS - accounts-data','Backend cache and aggregation store leveraged by the myUSCIS user interface applications. Pulls data from various microservices and temporarily caches locally in a database to improve performance.','non-public','2026-03-22T11:54:21.721577','2026-03-22T11:54:21.721582','Unspecified','Open Data (MGMT)','024:030','1ca2ad47-8e97-4c2b-b407-b776d08715fd','DHS datajson source','3e4c5d68ec3095d349dc49d66c35f0b1fff1707c312f4997f4fa130fea63e4a6','1.1','2026-03-22T11:54:21.721577','2026-03-22T11:54:21.721582',NULL,'024:000',0,'dhs-gov'),('5d0b49a7-7710-4208-b870-84f7fd1f0884','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSIWAC 4 ESC4-MTP024 RDR-STRLIGHT V1.0','This CODMAC level 4 data set contains solar stray light corrected, radiometric calibrated and geometric distortion corrected (resampled) image data in W/m^2/sr/nm, acquired by the OSIRIS Wide Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft during the COMET ESCORT 4 mission phase, covering the period from 2015-12-15T23:25:00.000 to 2016-01-12T23:24:59.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V1.0 is the first version of this dataset: Lien corrected dataset after October 2018 PSA/PDS external peer review.','public','2026-03-13T16:53:05.254061','2026-03-13T16:53:05.254065','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','b922ff88-254e-48e3-9374-102134699635','NASA Data.json','810ed9c15087f7a5f6f96b939e31be4ff68984daab612c5f7ada267eb27ea6c9','1.1','2026-03-13T16:53:05.254061','2026-03-13T16:53:05.254065','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('5d273755-a523-4b68-b902-e1d6264ff9fe','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P NAVCAM 2 ROSETTA EXTENSION 3 MTP033 V1.0','This dataset contains ROSETTA NAVCAM RAW DATA of the Escort Phase Ext3 from 9th Aug 2016 to 2nd Sep 2016 when at the vicinity of target 67P/CG.','public','2026-03-13T16:55:23.204232','2026-03-13T16:55:23.204237','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','0f5b3634-47a7-4bad-ab86-6d3c650d2906','NASA Data.json','2604d4e6b64ec6819b70f57dfc7a1ad5422091bbc418e15ca12c21c7a51545dd','1.1','2026-03-13T16:55:23.204232','2026-03-13T16:55:23.204237','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('5d62673a-5809-4cc5-8db3-efbafefbf4dd','MARS EXPRESS MARS MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 8 4201 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2021-01-01 to 2022-12-31. It is a Occultation measurement and covers the time 2021-04-02T09:32:19.200 to 2021-04-02T10:01:16.649.','public','2026-03-13T19:08:48.191541','2026-03-13T19:08:48.191547','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','1eed565e-42a0-4b4c-80db-5b17eb247ff4','NASA Data.json','49a85fcf842c7072115185113e6fb83276c0aefb1bee3b5c4e124047cd80ad0b','1.1','2026-03-13T19:08:48.191541','2026-03-13T19:08:48.191547','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('5d6796d3-69ef-4247-b5a4-b6ac03e30faa','IMESD Board Meeting','IMESD Regular Board Meeting\nWednesday, March 18 5:00 pm\n2001 SW Nye Ave. Pendleton OR. 97801','public','2026-03-15T02:12:01.863671','2026-03-15T02:12:01.863675','data.oregon.gov','Danielle Sackett',NULL,'615adf78-c96a-48c8-9389-4410ce8707d6','oregon json','ce5aa6282fcca8fe77dd3a604e1777aef6223de07c7ff3d0780f429503ce6ac7','1.1','2026-03-15T02:12:01.863671','2026-03-15T02:12:01.863675','education',NULL,0,'state-of-oregon'),('5d6b7d21-ba79-4bc0-9fdc-8523d3558289','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RPCICA 3 EXT1 CALIB V1.0','This dataset contains CALIBRATED DATA from the RPCICA instrument onmission ROSETTA during Rosetta extension 1.Data contains measurements of solar wind interactionwith the atmosphere of target comet 67P.','public','2026-03-13T18:29:28.585319','2026-03-13T18:29:28.585328','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','f675e4f5-870d-44db-b7ba-5775dfff19c5','NASA Data.json','cce51151bc5c5c4727696f2eb27b27a3eb674210bd1eefb2c5bea7c37470eb87','1.1','2026-03-13T18:29:28.585319','2026-03-13T18:29:28.585328','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('5d74a572-578c-4b37-b30c-9652cbadadea','MARS EXPRESS MARSIS RDR ACTIVE IONOSPHERE SOUNDING EXT3 V1.0','The Mars Express MARSIS Active Ionospheric Sounder (AIS) full      resolution data set includes all spectral information      calibrated in units of spectral density for the Mars Express      third extended mission, EXT3.  The data set consists of a      transmit frequency followed by a time series of spectral density      measurements of the received power.  Browse products contain      a spectrogram overview plot and individual ionograms for each      sounding  activity.','public','2026-03-13T18:25:47.170672','2026-03-13T18:25:47.170680','planetary plasma interactions','Planetary Data System','026:00','3127e0fe-928c-4209-b30d-da3c74526c48','NASA Data.json','05cb41bb56bb7ade2f9423713d13f225710e6ccea354e8a3eb810bc883ccc058','1.1','2026-03-13T18:25:47.170672','2026-03-13T18:25:47.170680','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('5d7d9567-053b-4388-bc35-ca292eefb0ff','BLM ID Right of Way Point','These are Rights-of-Ways (ROW) on Idaho BLM land (and some other Federal agency land) as shown on Bureau of Land Management (BLM) Master Title Plats (MTP). Every GIS ROW feature has a \"CASEFILE\" value, also known as the serial number of the ROW. The ROW data that was digitized is what was present on the MTP at the time of the digitizing done for that township. The project was performed over several years. Therefore, the \"early\" townships digitized are more out of date regarding ROWs compared to the ones more recently digitized. Unfortunately, there is no attribute that indicates the digitizing sequence. Any updates to this ROW feature class should be sent to the BLM Idaho State Office GIS staff for incorporation into the statewide GIS ROW feature classes for improvement over time. For more information contact us at blm_id_stateoffice@blm.gov.','public','2026-03-26T12:40:28.630702','2026-03-26T12:40:28.630708','Bureau of Land Management','Bureau of Land Management, blm_id_stateoffice','010:04','fb18b788-642e-454d-9e14-e3ed62574472','DOI BLM DCAT-US','748075d3ee89333648824e1985921e60ce78bbdba1e132dbfe722cd22055d5b9','1.1','2026-03-26T12:40:28.630702','2026-03-26T12:40:28.630708','geospatial','010:000',0,'doi-gov'),('5db3a89d-0891-4871-87d9-63d284809732','Report Card 1003 Funds 2024-25 School Year','This data provides a list of all the school districts and schools that received funds under section 1003 of ESSA in the 2024-25 school year, including the amount of funds each school received and the types of strategies implemented in each school with using these funds.','public','2026-03-22T03:13:44.790872','2026-03-22T03:13:44.790877','data.wa.gov','thomas.mankovich',NULL,'1f00ba89-76e9-4981-89a3-e94185438264','WA JSON','109bca82067347756555d343b146c3618c99e876e864b2c98d099f87ff806346','1.1','2026-03-22T03:13:44.790872','2026-03-22T03:13:44.790877','education',NULL,0,'state-of-washington'),('5ddc591e-4e18-40ee-9b53-8da15e90e9ef','MDDNR, Station Riverside','At continuous monitoring sites throughout Maryland, water quality is monitored at shallow water sites located in Chesapeake Bay, Chesapeake Bay tributaries and Maryland Coastal Bay tributaries. YSI (6600 V2 or EXO2) data loggers sample seven environmental parameters: water temperature, specific conductance, dissolved oxygen concentration, oxygen percent saturation, pH, turbidity and fluorescence. Water depth is measured at stations where loggers were deployed at fixed depths. Salinity and chlorophyll are derived from specific conductance and fluorescence, respectively. Each parameter is generally sampled at 15-minute intervals. Most continuous monitoring sites are deployed during the SAV growing season (April-October) with a few sites deployed year-round.','public','2026-03-26T19:15:21.393778','2026-03-26T19:15:21.393784',NULL,NULL,NULL,'a35d3400-28c3-4c16-b506-c9f96c3c8788','ioos',NULL,NULL,'2026-03-26T19:15:21.393778','2026-03-26T19:15:21.393784',NULL,NULL,NULL,'noaa-gov'),('5def0c12-559a-43ac-97eb-9ef3a9d9b144','MSX LUNAR ECLIPSE OBSERVATION V1.0','The Midcourse Space Experiment (MSX) lunar eclipse observation on September 27, 1996 resulted in six 4.3 micron brightness temperature maps of the moon. In addition, qualitative observations were made at 8.3 microns.','public','2026-03-13T16:41:51.389098','2026-03-13T16:41:51.389104','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','a2e1820a-fb65-4c97-bb6c-569f4c19613c','NASA Data.json','e93d897fa15398502303acfe170e48c24fbe3bb811f1f33d4e4ebaa1e5c887d7','1.1','2026-03-13T16:41:51.389098','2026-03-13T16:41:51.389104','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('5e311b23-61b7-41dc-8fca-5028076ca395','BLM CO Lands Inventoried with Wilderness Characteristics','<DIV STYLE=\"text-align:Left;\"><DIV><P><SPAN>This feature dataset represents the spatial extent and boundaries of inventoried and managed BLM Lands with Wilderness Characteristics. This dataset also also provides BLM and the public with information about naturalness, opportunities for solitude and/or primitive recreation, supplemental values and proximity to Wilderness Areas or Wilderness Study Areas.    BLM Inventoried Lands with Wilderness Characteristics is consistent with Section 201 of the Federal Land Policy and Management Act (FLPMA), which requires the BLM Colorado Inventoried Lands with Wilderness Characteristics is consistent with Section 201 of the Federal Land Policy and Management Act (FLPMA), which requires the Secretary of the Interior to “prepare and maintain on a continuing basis an inventory of all public lands and their resource and other values,” and the BLM Land Use Planning Handbook, BLM Colorado has identified and begun an assessment of BLM-managed lands with wilderness characteristics outside of existing WSAs. BLM Manual 6310 - Conducting Wilderness Characteristics Inventory on BLM Lands, provides the guidance from which BLM performs the wilderness characteristic inventory process.</SPAN></P></DIV></DIV>','public','2026-03-26T12:42:15.610949','2026-03-26T12:42:15.610967','Bureau of Land Management','Bureau of Land Management, pkeller','010:04','41f6175e-077d-4053-bd2f-7b17dfc6e7aa','DOI BLM DCAT-US','3bce2eb16f6cd1a879074629750dabba6b70fb87330c02cd7cf02a8d132e7e9d','1.1','2026-03-26T12:42:15.610949','2026-03-26T12:42:15.610967','geospatial','010:000',0,'doi-gov'),('5e41a710-5815-4b1b-9ae8-dcadb94e812c','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSINAC 5 PRL-MTP005 DDR-GEO V1.0','This CODMAC level 5 data set contains derived data products that include pixel-precise georeferencing information, acquired by the OSIRIS Narrow Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft during the PRELANDING mission phase, covering the period from 2014-07-02T08:35:00.000 to 2014-08-01T09:59:59.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V1.0 is the first version of this dataset: Lien corrected dataset after October 2018 PSA/PDS external peer review.','public','2026-03-13T17:54:01.551927','2026-03-13T17:54:01.551931','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','8f1a36d0-ffc3-4b4d-a3ee-71975dbb7775','NASA Data.json','bd71f62795f7ed69857e7c333569251aa5ce52af999db1d283e569b7fa2acacf','1.1','2026-03-13T17:54:01.551927','2026-03-13T17:54:01.551931','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('5e5b7e0a-e657-43b4-9036-0d3f998ccf6f','Continuous Fixed Station Water Quality Measurements in Timucuan Ecological and Historic Preserve, February 2008 (Certified)','This dataset represents continuous water quality measurements that were taken at a fixed point in Timucuan Ecological and Historic Preserve during the month of February, 2008 as a part of the Fixed Station Water Quality Monitoring protocol that was developed by the Southeast Coast I&M Network (SECN). The measurements were taken by a YSI 6600 ESD Multi-Parameter Long Term Water Quality Monitoring Datasonde unit that serves as the standard fixed station water quality monitoring equipment for all similar operations conducted by the SECN. The following parameters were measured at 30 minute intervals during the time period that has been specified: Water Temperature, Specific Conductivity, Salinity, Dissolved Oxygen (DO), DO Concentration, Shallow Depth, pH Level, and Turbidity. Any anomalies noted regarding these parameters have also been noted in separate fields. Please note that these measurements have been certified by network personnel.','public','2026-03-26T05:30:22.243577','2026-03-26T05:30:22.243584','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','2eaafccc-aa30-42fd-ad1b-6a18b3ea00f3','DOI NPS DCAT-US','67d64003979d2204f03929bf7e6d8d84b1e62972778f8c2a6862668819fb0412','1.1','2026-03-26T05:30:22.243577','2026-03-26T05:30:22.243584','Vector Dataset','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('5edd67a0-7621-4570-8dff-7a6ed3e6d5ae','Continuous Fixed Station Water Quality Measurements in Cape Lookout National Seashore, February 2009 (Certified)','This dataset represents continuous water quality measurements that were taken at a fixed point in Cape Lookout National Seashore during the month of February, 2009 as a part of the Fixed Station Water Quality Monitoring protocol that was developed by the Southeast Coast I&M Network (SECN). The measurements were taken by a YSI 6600 ESD Multi-Parameter Long Term Water Quality Monitoring Datasonde unit that serves as the standard fixed station water quality monitoring equipment for all similar operations conducted by the SECN. The following parameters were measured at 15 minute intervals during the time period that has been specified: Water Temperature, Specific Conductivity, Salinity, Dissolved Oxygen (DO), DO Concentration, Shallow Depth, pH Level, and Turbidity. Any anomalies noted regarding these parameters have also been noted in separate fields.  Please note that these measurements have been certified by network personnel.','public','2026-03-26T05:28:15.857928','2026-03-26T05:28:15.857934','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','9931e6ae-8b54-4f24-8a69-cdf58cb3533a','DOI NPS DCAT-US','dc2101a6f3524d4910dcfc4d2d75eb068687a29843476565439b2f03f10b82c0','1.1','2026-03-26T05:28:15.857928','2026-03-26T05:28:15.857934','Vector Dataset','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('5ee18799-0894-4388-a48e-5a259e42ab0b','MARS EXPRESS MARS MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 5 3814 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2015-01-01 to 2016-12-31. It is a Occultation measurement and covers the time 2015-09-08T09:15:54.000 to 2015-09-08T09:39:44.949.','public','2026-03-13T18:24:59.018445','2026-03-13T18:24:59.018450','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','d74eacf7-e9c5-4ed8-b702-8bfeb35d6ada','NASA Data.json','dc6ec51ab64872889c567423ded9c8c91cc75d8897ec63d7fd5419daba3907d0','1.1','2026-03-13T18:24:59.018445','2026-03-13T18:24:59.018450','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('5f06f29a-3f32-41ed-a750-6d34b62ff3d6','ROSETTA-ORBITER CAL MIDAS 3 CVP FULL V1.0','The Micro-Imaging Dust Analysis System (MIDAS) is an instrument on the ROSETTA Orbiter that will provide 3D images and statistical parameters of pristine cometary particles hitting the detector. This data set includes all data from the COMMISSIONING mission phase.','public','2026-03-13T17:44:09.419764','2026-03-13T17:44:09.419769','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','16709af1-fff4-4bbf-854a-23c1332e64cc','NASA Data.json','3c68f62d3397e573cde5ec92e4c34809e816de5700391ea2ff54f8f19608b4bd','1.1','2026-03-13T17:44:09.419764','2026-03-13T17:44:09.419769','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('5f07c52c-6e13-4d2a-aa41-58e884105073','MARS EXPRESS MARS MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 6 3963 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2017-01-01 to 2018-12-31. It is a Occultation measurement and covers the time 2018-09-29T17:00:43.000 to 2018-09-29T17:29:12.549.','public','2026-03-13T18:53:49.611652','2026-03-13T18:53:49.611661','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','cabd29ae-1ce7-45f9-86d8-abda7f36131f','NASA Data.json','923790b27ba782f7046223fbba1a192d3d38091d9f530859a49fc42b27727971','1.1','2026-03-13T18:53:49.611652','2026-03-13T18:53:49.611661','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('5f35728f-6f23-49e6-bade-a23f31e529f1','Dataset for development and evaluation of a qPCR method modification that mitigates DNA recovery losses for analyses of E. coli fecal indicator bacteria in Great Lakes region recreational waters','Results previously reported by EPA/ORD on the modified method have led to its adoption into a Standard Operating Procedure for labs performing qPCR analyses for E. coli at recreational beaches in the state of Michigan. This dataset provides further documentation of the performance and applicability of the modified method for recreational beach water testing including data from an extensive survey that can be used to determine when and where unacceptable levels of DNA losses may occur with and without this method modification in the Great Lakes region.\n\nPlease see the attached dataset description document for additional information. ','public','2026-03-22T11:49:52.725396','2026-03-22T11:49:52.725401','U.S. Environmental Protection Agency','Shawn Siefring','020:00','5377cc47-3477-4af5-8ee9-f6bc182862d7','EPA ScienceHub','ed434948ff5bfcbee69e3a4aba90da770c259018b9b3089297db33d0a509fa94','1.1','2026-03-22T11:49:52.725396','2026-03-22T11:49:52.725401',NULL,'020:000',0,'epa-gov'),('5f43b5df-3045-4b14-bd34-3cc62bf76c18','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSIWAC 4 EXT2-MTP028 RDR-REFLECT V1.0','This CODMAC level 4 data set contains radiometric calibrated and geometric distortion corrected (resampled) image data in reflectance units (normalized and thus without unit), acquired by the OSIRIS Wide Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft during the ROSETTA EXTENSION 2 mission phase, covering the period from 2016-04-05T23:25:00.000 to 2016-05-03T23:25:00.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V1.0 is the first version of this dataset: Lien corrected dataset after October 2018 PSA/PDS external peer review.','public','2026-03-13T19:23:57.454179','2026-03-13T19:23:57.454186','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','f3beec0c-178f-4951-96e6-759148d494e5','NASA Data.json','b5fefd0befc9b96b5dc84fdfb4521201c94920b0d0f1b02aedd0402538200bc6','1.1','2026-03-13T19:23:57.454179','2026-03-13T19:23:57.454186','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('5f54f5af-f6aa-4c19-8a38-e999833435e1','ROSETTA-ORBITER COMET PRELANDING OSIWAC 2 EDR MTP 005 V1.0','This data set contains raw EDR images acquired by the OSIRIS Wide AngleCamera during the prelanding phase of the Rosetta mission at the comet 67P,covering the period from 2014-07-02 to 2014-08-01.','public','2026-03-13T17:00:21.698735','2026-03-13T17:00:21.698743','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','9110e21c-9e35-46e7-9aa3-70e92ac35b98','NASA Data.json','1db9713ff660578be3ead5b72861afe04b72811070d405fa2f5b7fb2d50f62c4','1.1','2026-03-13T17:00:21.698735','2026-03-13T17:00:21.698743','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('5f7b589d-ba35-4cc9-ab6a-c8e175349942','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P VIRTIS 2 PRELANDING MTP004 V1.0','This release contains the digital numbers (DN) contained in the telemetry (TM) packages of the VIRTIS instrument on board of the spacecraft Rosetta. This volume contains data from the PRELANDING MTP004 phase, which occurred from 2014-06-18 to 2014-07-02','public','2026-03-13T17:31:59.226304','2026-03-13T17:31:59.226310','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','18859ec0-7c9d-433a-9905-0113850d6b4d','NASA Data.json','d03aee1566678a0b24dd0766fd2c0d4d5db602be15d3d6397652b0cd3ada9233','1.1','2026-03-13T17:31:59.226304','2026-03-13T17:31:59.226310','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('5f8b5e3c-1982-438d-ada0-0930ad7934be','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 PRELANDING 0394 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the PRELANDING phase 2014-01-21 to 2014-11-18. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2014-10-29T14:45:30.000 to 2014-10-29T22:29:54.500.','public','2026-03-13T19:07:18.482831','2026-03-13T19:07:18.482838','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','82bffdfc-ba3f-455a-aa6b-47cedaa47366','NASA Data.json','afe187737534701367b0141f62e32ed63de069aeaba23a83cb4eb02e08866a3b','1.1','2026-03-13T19:07:18.482831','2026-03-13T19:07:18.482838','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('5fa3ad3b-6ab4-407b-b101-0d5487cf8e57','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 ROSETTA EXTENSION 1 1326 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the ROSETTA EXTENSION 1 phase 2016-01-01 to 2016-04-05. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2016-01-09T20:13:35.000 to 2016-01-10T00:56:38.500.','public','2026-03-13T16:51:20.672520','2026-03-13T16:51:20.672526','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','b0016f2d-fd78-46bd-a48a-72a7b5a4c062','NASA Data.json','a867d28de686d11529875fae93fc949eb3859783a69b177710d8e77a56dd0c8b','1.1','2026-03-13T16:51:20.672520','2026-03-13T16:51:20.672526','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('5fdf2ad0-b953-4a70-b2d1-a616e632ef0b','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 3 0918 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 3 phase 2015-07-01 to 2015-10-21. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-07-24T21:22:20.000 to 2015-07-25T04:37:30.000.','public','2026-03-13T16:54:17.306597','2026-03-13T16:54:17.306603','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','1e210cde-7601-408a-9b23-b52ee6055bc5','NASA Data.json','a97af6880bee53c5aa772654ac7cbf88d22bd5ba334d685ae7289181f8e95417','1.1','2026-03-13T16:54:17.306597','2026-03-13T16:54:17.306603','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('60112b39-4445-4850-9fc1-6d68caa777c7','ROSETTA-ORBITER X SREM 5 EARTH 2 V1.0','This data set contains derived electron and proton flux energies in MeV from the Standard Radiation Environment Monitor (SREM) instrument on the Rosetta spacecraft. These are CODMAC Level 5 derived data, and measure the radiation in the spacecraft environment during the EARTH 2 mission phase.','public','2026-03-13T19:49:50.471827','2026-03-13T19:49:50.471833','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','5dd5c9ac-e358-44b2-a6f5-88456ce4e3d4','NASA Data.json','acdebe33ebfe9078b4b3192da4856f9383e390e50c217f9d1d1440daaf199d66','1.1','2026-03-13T19:49:50.471827','2026-03-13T19:49:50.471833','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('6053dca9-f67c-48da-b2f6-9438e7818bcb','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSIWAC 4 EXT3-MTP031 RDR-STRLIGHT V1.0','This CODMAC level 4 data set contains solar stray light corrected, radiometric calibrated and geometric distortion corrected (resampled) image data in W/m^2/sr/nm, acquired by the OSIRIS Wide Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft during the ROSETTA EXTENSION 3 mission phase, covering the period from 2016-06-28T23:25:00.000 to 2016-07-26T23:24:59.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V1.0 is the first version of this dataset: Lien corrected dataset after October 2018 PSA/PDS external peer review.','public','2026-03-13T17:56:16.870331','2026-03-13T17:56:16.870338','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','6167b583-b225-4013-907a-33d3762b2316','NASA Data.json','6de9292b64713c42ed3c5d98f0994cd4f03d463b310cfdcec1035a50372054eb','1.1','2026-03-13T17:56:16.870331','2026-03-13T17:56:16.870338','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('60e5f3c3-be79-4c9c-a87c-5b11d8983853','Voyager 1 Saturn Planetary Radio Astronomy (PRA) Calibrated Low-Frequency Receiver Band, Version 1.0, 6 s High Resolution Data','* Data Set Overview\n* =================\n\nThis Data Set (VG1-S-PRA-3-RDR-LOWBAND-6SEC-V1.0) contains Data acquired by the Voyager 1 Planetary Radio Astronomy (PRA) Instrument during the Saturn Encounter. Since the PRA Instrument is able to observe Planetary Phenomenon at much larger Ranges than other Fields and Particles Experiments, thus the PRA Data cover a variable and longer Encounter Period. PRA Low Band Data provided here cover the entire Saturn Encounter Phase (1980-08-22 to 1980-12-14).\n\nVG1-S-PRA-3-RDR-LOWBAND-6SEC-V1.0 contains Data at the highest Time Resolution possible during Normal Operations. The Normal Mode of PRA Operations during the Planetary Encounters was to Sweep through the two Radio Receiver Bands, High Band (40.5 MHz to 1.5 MHz in 128 Channels spaced 0.3072 MHz apart) and Low Band (1326.0 kHz to 1.2 kHz in 70 Channels spaced 19.2 kHz apart) in a Period of 6 s. The Receivers measured, on alternate Samples, the left hand circular And right hand circular (radio definition) Power.\n\n* Measured Parameters\n* ===================\n\nThe Data here are from the Low Frequency Receiver Band and are \"packaged\" into Spacecraft Major Frame Records. Each Major Frame is 48 s long or eight Sweeps through the PRA Receiver. The Data are calibrated and are given in Units of \"millibels\" or mB, which is 1000 times the Log of the received Power. Zero mB corresponds to approximately 1.4×10^-21 W m^-2 Hz^-1, however, this Value is never seen in practice. The minimum Values detected, which includes Receiver internal and Spacecraft generated Noise, are about 2300 mB to 2400 mB, or about 3.5×10^-19 W m^-2 Hz^-1; even higher Values are seen at the very lowest Frequencies.\n\nThe Data Format is ASCII and consists of a Time Indicator followed by an Array containing the eight Low Band Sweeps. Time is Spacecraft Event Time (SCET) which is basically Universal Time at the Spacecraft. Specifically, Time is in the Form of YYMMDD and Seconds into YYMMDD. Both are written as I6. Example: July 1, 1979 at 12:00 SCET would be 790701, 43200. The Seconds corresponds, to the nearest Second, to the Start of the Sweep (which occurs in PRA High Band). The first Value in Low Band (1326.0 kHz) occurs some 3.9 s after this Time and Samples at successively lower Frequencies are spaced 0.03 s apart. Only one Time is given for the entire Major Frame, thus the Start of each Sweep is the Time given plus 6 times the Sweep Number minus 1 (i.e., 0 through 7).\n\nThe Data Array is dimensioned as 71 × 8 and written as I4 Format (i.e., 568I4). The \"8\" corresponds to the eight PRA Sweeps. The lowest 68 of the 70 Low Band Channels (1287.6 kHz to 1.2 kHz) are in Positions 2 to 69. Positions 70 and 71 should be ignored. Missing or Bad Data Values are set to Zero. In Position 1 of each Sweep is a Status Word where the 12 least significant Bits have used, although not all 12 have meaning for the PRA Low Band. Numbering those Bits 0 for least significant to 11 for most significant, the Bits that have meaning are as follows:\n\n* Bit Value(s)\n- 0: 15 dB Attenuator in use when equal to 1\n- 1: 30 dB Attenuator in use when equal to 1\n- 2: 45 dB Attenuator in use when equal to 1\n- 9 and 10 together: Polarization of first Channel sampled (1326.0 kHz) according to the Scheme:\n\n+-------------------------------------------------------+\n|                 | Value Bit 10 = 0 | Value Bit 10 = 1 |\n---------------------------------------------------------\n| Value Bit 9 = 0 | R                | L                |\n| Value Bit 9 = 1 | L                | R                |\n+-------------------------------------------------------+\n\nPolarization at successively lower Frequencies is opposite to the Frequency above it, i.e., either a LRLR or an RLRL Pattern. Successive 6 s Sweeps start on the opposite Polarization as the previous Sweep as indicated in the Status Bits. Note that this Polarization is the received Polarization, not necessarily the emitted Polarization. Correct Interpretation of the received Polarization depends on the Antenna Plane Orientation relative to the Radio Source. A good Description of this Concept can be found in (Le Blanc et al., 1987).\n\nMissing or Bad Data Values are set to Zero. If the Status Word is Zero, any Data in that Receiver Sweep should be discarded.','public','2026-03-13T22:35:03.219236','2026-03-13T22:35:03.219243','PDS PPI','NASA Space Physics Data Facility','026:00','0593c10a-4b8b-4d5e-bfab-927eb59637fa','NASA Data.json','5d92719560b7eaed1848889b5eead5d3269f3de369005c1cc6dd9bd8ecff0104','1.1','2026-03-13T22:35:03.219236','2026-03-13T22:35:03.219243','Heliophysics','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('6116b560-02a7-45dd-abf9-310f8c80c0c6','USCIS RAILS','The RAILS data tracks the location, movement, and location history of immigrant and receipt files. RAILS replaced the now decommissioned National File Tracking System (NFTS).','non-public','2026-03-22T11:51:27.439860','2026-03-22T11:51:27.439864','Unspecified','Open Data (MGMT)','024:030','81498e51-23f3-48fa-b3e8-5380f676d255','DHS datajson source','1baf78091237c6aa6e252c2acd35f236a70420b705ab7edeff2ed9a4967a652f','1.1','2026-03-22T11:51:27.439860','2026-03-22T11:51:27.439864',NULL,'024:000',0,'dhs-gov'),('611a9eb4-50a1-49a6-96a2-a0d6c29575e8','Pelagic Cormorant Predicted Habitat - CWHR B047 [ds2038]','<div style=\'text-align:Left;\'><div><div><p><span>CWHR Predicted Habitat Models represent areas of predicted suitable habitat for each species within its range. These models are built from the following principal inputs: </span></p><p><span>1) a statewide, best-available vegetation map (FVEG);  </span></p><p><span>2) GIS data representing a species’ range;  </span></p><p><span>3) the CWHR database of habitat suitability values for over 700 terrestrial vertebrate species. </span></p><p><span>Habitat suitability ranks of Low (non-zero values less than 0.34), Medium (0.34-0.66), and High (greater than 0.66) are based on the maximum suitability value across the 3 species life requisites: reproduction, feeding, and cover. Note that previous versions of these Predicted Habitat Models used an average across the 3 life requisites in order to obtain an overall suitability score for each habitat type and stage class.  Habitat suitability scores were developed based on habitat patch sizes greater than 40 acres in size and are best interpreted for habitat patches greater than 200 acres in size. The FVEG landcover dataset is an aggregation of multiple statewide landcover and regional vegetation mapping efforts, conducted at different points in time (approximately 1990 up to time of publishing) and at various resolutions, compiled by the California Department of Forestry and Fire Protection (CALFIRE). FVEG uses the most current and consistent data available for each region of the state. Decision rules were developed that controlled which layers were given priority in areas of overlap. Crosswalks were used to attribute the various data sources according to the CWHR habitat-type classification system. Attributing FVEG with CWHR habitat types allows for the extraction of areas with non-zero suitability values for each species within the bounds of its range, creating a series of maps of predicted suitable habitat which are species-specific. Because FVEG is an amalgam of disparate landcover assessment efforts across the state, the predictive power for determining suitable habitat will vary between species, and possibly even regionally for species which are widely distributed. While these maps represent CDFW’s best estimate of the presence of suitable habitat for any given species in the CWHR system, these maps are also limited by several factors: 1) the accuracy and resolution of vegetation maps in a given region; 2) the dynamic nature of the landscape in which fire and other disturbance events alter conditions at a greater frequency than mapping efforts can track; 3) the currency of expert knowledge, particularly as species adapt to changing land and climate conditions and the shifting of other species’ ranges; 4) the frequency of species-specific surveys across a representative sample of a species’ entire range; 5) metapopulation dynamics, which describes the shifting of populations within their environment as result of numerous types of interactions and responses. </span></p><p><span>CWHR GIS data representing predicted suitable habitat should not be used to indicate the presence or absence of a particular species at any specific site. CWHR predicted habitat models are named according to the 4-character alpha-numeric CWHR ID assigned to each species (5 characters in the case of subspecies or other sub-taxa). There is also a “CWHR Revision Tracking Table” containing a record for each species, its CWHR ID, scientific name, common name, and range and habitat model data revision history. CWHR species range models, predicted habitat models, and GIS data of the statewide distribution of all CWHR habitat types, along with the CWHR revision tracking table, are available for download at </span><a href=\'https://www.wildlife.ca.gov/Data/CWHR\' target=\'_blank\' style=\'text-decoration:underline;\' rel=\'nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer\'><span>https://www.wildlife.ca.gov/Data/CWHR</span></a><span>. </span></p></div></div></div>','public','2026-03-23T13:55:23.109382','2026-03-23T13:55:23.109386','California Department of Fish and Wildlife','BIOS_Admin',NULL,'18336627-efec-4284-a16a-fa8fd887cfa3','State of California','00bd55aef628bc6fc79064982e277a70c7b8e3c3f58ea799b577d694488d7df0','1.1','2026-03-23T13:55:23.109382','2026-03-23T13:55:23.109386','Natural Resources',NULL,0,'ca-gov'),('615c3f34-9936-44e8-9ba2-a35dc545a15e','ROSETTA-ORBITER PRELANDING OSINAC 3 RDR MTP009 V2.0','This data set contains images acquired by the OSIRIS Narrow Angle Camera during the PRELANDING phase of the Rosetta mission at the comet 67P, covering the period from 2014-10-24T10:00:00.000 to 2014-11-21T23:24:59.000. This version V2.0 supersedes previous deliveries of the same dataset.','public','2026-03-13T17:53:49.589441','2026-03-13T17:53:49.589447','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','4dd64f0e-ecf1-4a54-8fe5-4e00948d35a2','NASA Data.json','7ddddb1a09fb405915d0a59b1adfc508f7f5003ff948eda553b1e8adb02697ff','1.1','2026-03-13T17:53:49.589441','2026-03-13T17:53:49.589447','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('61655a4f-f355-40c4-b9c4-708e7e647f0a','Continuous Fixed Station Water Quality Measurements in Timucuan Ecological and Historic Preserve, August 2008 (Certified)','This dataset represents continuous water quality measurements that were taken at a fixed point just outside of Timucuan Ecological and Historic Preserve during the month of August, 2008 as a part of the Fixed Station Water Quality Monitoring protocol that was developed by the Southeast Coast I&M Network (SECN). The measurements were taken by a YSI 6600 ESD Multi-Parameter Long Term Water Quality Monitoring Datasonde unit that serves as the standard fixed station water quality monitoring equipment for all similar operations conducted by the SECN. The following parameters were measured at 30 minute intervals during the time period that has been specified: Water Temperature, Specific Conductivity, Salinity, Dissolved Oxygen (DO), DO Concentration, Shallow Depth, pH Level, and Turbidity. Any anomalies noted regarding these parameters have also been noted in separate fields. Please note that these measurements have been certified by network personnel.','public','2026-03-26T05:33:54.820097','2026-03-26T05:33:54.820103','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','8ddd0900-d7b7-43c0-aa20-b95a67010ff5','DOI NPS DCAT-US','2ebacb6883e6132b982000e04cceeb79eaa20933f6ba71150acc89f31f91cfac','1.1','2026-03-26T05:33:54.820097','2026-03-26T05:33:54.820103','Vector Dataset','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('6171f0d0-1184-4c83-83df-143005dc6209','2026 Open Data Annual Report --Featured Accomplishments','Featured Accomplishments page showcased the projects that Open Data team worked on last year.','public','2026-03-15T02:19:27.086792','2026-03-15T02:19:27.086797','opendata.maryland.gov','Helen Bai',NULL,'a328a351-e672-4b3a-9c33-7e069433dad3','md json','def96b54b9dd6dcf0c26382bead71994766840ba6c6a7efdb2d1e4a7e228d7bd','1.1','2026-03-15T02:19:27.086792','2026-03-15T02:19:27.086797',NULL,NULL,0,'state-of-maryland'),('61819a62-4e82-468b-99fe-382e0baec12d','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RPCMIP 3 PRL2 V3.0','This archive contains data from the RPC-MIP instrument onboard ROSETTA Orbiter acquired during the PRELANDING mission phase between 2014/07/25 and 2014/10/16. The primary target was comet 67P/C-G. It also contains documentation which describes the RPC-MIP experiment. The data archived in this data set conform to the Planetary Data System Standards, Version 3.6. This is V3.0 updated after Science Review.','public','2026-03-13T19:37:10.228770','2026-03-13T19:37:10.228775','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','ec2ffa81-cf55-433c-8b2b-cde97a073a9a','NASA Data.json','72c6b2bdde20f16adfc1ec051eb44140b5140749052b49a9acffd204a8eea8bf','1.1','2026-03-13T19:37:10.228770','2026-03-13T19:37:10.228775','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('61870568-af48-4ab4-b9d6-22fca3cf7bf7','VG1 JUP MAG RESAMPLED SYSTEM III (1965) COORDS 48.0SEC V1.1','not applicable','public','2026-03-13T18:23:13.962969','2026-03-13T18:23:13.962974','Planetary Plasma Interactions','Planetary Data System','026:00','22f82f8f-cc54-44dc-a4a0-2e8b15806ea0','NASA Data.json','dc328eb99cce4b81c583bbb97b96ee66f7751a27468af0fb07fc2cca87c20657','1.1','2026-03-13T18:23:13.962969','2026-03-13T18:23:13.962974','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('6187f4fb-7587-4cdd-ba2a-87306cfc9531','Next Generation Accountable Care Organization Model Data','The Next Generation Accountable Care Organization (NGACO) dataset includes summary‑level information on organizational performance, including aligned beneficiary counts, spending benchmarks, performance‑year expenditures, shared savings or losses, quality performance, and high‑level breakdowns of Medicare service‑category spending.','public','2026-03-28T19:04:51.024858','2026-03-28T19:04:51.024865','Centers for Medicare & Medicaid Services','CMS Innovation Center - CMMI','009:38','b302bd46-fca1-4a41-a221-646f31b414a5','Healthdata.gov','606d70cd64ec4e59a7f98f513e7eb88b520675ca1db47288fc6a1442cbcbf244','1.1','2026-03-28T19:04:51.024858','2026-03-28T19:04:51.024865','Medicare','009:000',0,'hhs-gov'),('61909a8f-9296-4e9b-8552-2076793111c5','FLKEYS Array, Station RHA04, Bottom Temperature','Timeseries data from \'FLKEYS Array, Station RHA04, Bottom Temperature\' (org_secoora_flkeys_rha04)','public','2026-03-26T19:16:16.608709','2026-03-26T19:16:16.608715',NULL,NULL,NULL,'16fc086e-2379-4e9b-bf34-24251a84eae9','ioos',NULL,NULL,'2026-03-26T19:16:16.608709','2026-03-26T19:16:16.608715',NULL,NULL,NULL,'noaa-gov'),('6199d2a8-bc5f-4633-9666-040d9f3c6331','AIRSAR_TOPSAR_P-BAND_STOKES','AIRSAR topographic SAR digital elevation model P_Stokes product','public','2026-03-13T19:01:28.648750','2026-03-13T19:01:28.648756','NASA/JPL/RDC;ASF','Earthdata Forum','026:00','5bd39cdd-96de-423a-9fe3-a80abd91aa7c','NASA Data.json','6af02a420b7b317dbd1c3f1a173af741ee28893fe896ed3af8f5dac94fdc6ce2','1.1','2026-03-13T19:01:28.648750','2026-03-13T19:01:28.648756','Earth Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('61aeb5fe-ec19-4be1-be9b-38f75ec47f2b','VG2 JUP PLASMA DERIVED ELECTRON MOMENTS96.0 SEC V1.1','This data set contains derived values    of the electron density and moment temperature at Jupiter during the    Voyager 2 encounter in the PLS voltage range (10-5950 eV/q). Adjacent low    and high energy electron measurements are combined to form a composite    spectra which is used for the moment calculation. These assume isotropic    distributions and correct for positive spacecraft charge when applicable    and interpolate electron spectra below the 10 eV instrument threshold    before performing the integration over velocity. Data format: column 1 is    time (yyyy-mm-ddThh:mm:ss.sssZ), column 2 is the moment density in cm^-3,    column 3 the temperature in eV. Each row has format (a24, 2(1x,1pe9.2)).    Values of -9.99e+10 indicate that the parameter could not be obtained from    the data using the standard analysis technique. Additional information    about this data set and the instrument which produced it can be found    elsewhere in this catalog.','public','2026-03-13T18:18:16.286676','2026-03-13T18:18:16.286681','planetary plasma interactions','Planetary Data System','026:00','ce806847-e910-4964-a71b-a5fd7c959f73','NASA Data.json','3532068a2953ecc52153b4595e683d41e843c41972c7cc1fae0129ba0abb3a55','1.1','2026-03-13T18:18:16.286676','2026-03-13T18:18:16.286681','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('61dc9b73-54b5-4b4b-9dac-bf69524e9147','ROSETTA-ORBITER CHECK RPCMAG 3 CR5 CALIBRATED V9.0','This dataset contains CALIBRATED (CODMAC LEVEL 3) DATA of the CRUISE 5(CR5) phase from February 24, 2010 until April 27, 2010 of the ROSETTAorbiter magnetometer RPCMAG.The current version of the dataset is V9.0.The difference to the datasets of earlier versions is mainly a significantlyimproved sensor temperature model, more detailed documentation about magneticdisturbance sources, more data handling information for the user andalso an improved quality flagging system.','public','2026-03-13T19:49:20.475286','2026-03-13T19:49:20.475291','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','a0ce1380-a8cf-40c6-b02b-324cb975fbd7','NASA Data.json','fc507a945f37d9956275571bb83e6187b6e0748d98b0c08fb0b744692d3f981b','1.1','2026-03-13T19:49:20.475286','2026-03-13T19:49:20.475291','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('61eb6764-8093-4445-98ce-cd8c965c9cd5','Steep Slope 10 ft','<p><strong>Overview</strong></p><p>This Feature Service provides detailed geographic information on steep slope areas within the state of Connecticut. This layer was derived from the 2023 Digital Elevation Model from the <a target=\'_blank\' href=\'https://maps.cteco.uconn.edu/data/flight2023/\' rel=\'nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer\'>2023 Spring imagery and lidar capture</a>. It is developed to support planning, environmental management, and risk assessment related to slope stability.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Details about layer development: <a target=\'_blank\' href=\'https://github.com/ctgisoffice/steep_slopes\' rel=\'nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer\'>https://github.com/ctgisoffice/steep_slopes</a></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Feature Layers</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Steep Slope 10 ft</strong>: This layer maps areas with steep slopes derived from a 10-feet per pixel DEM, providing details such as slope percentage, municipality, and council of governments (COG) region. It offers data for assessing terrain steepness over larger vertical intervals.</li><li><strong>Steep Slope 2 ft</strong>: This layer captures steep slopes derived from a 10-feet per pixel DEM, allowing for more detailed slope analysis at a smaller vertical resolution. Similar attribute details like slope percent, municipality, and COG are included, supporting higher-resolution terrain studies.</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Geographic Coverage</strong></p><p>The data covers the landscape of Connecticut, focusing on areas with significant slope gradients that may impact land use and development.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p style=\'line-height:125%;\'><span><strong>Classifications</strong></span></p><ul><li><p style=\'margin-bottom:0in; margin-right:0in; margin-top:0in;\'><span>Agency: OPM</span></p></li><li><p style=\'margin-bottom:0in; margin-right:0in; margin-top:0in;\'><span>Sensitivity: Public</span></p></li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p style=\'line-height:125%;\'><span><strong>Currency </strong>(time)</span></p><ul><li><p style=\'margin-bottom:0in; margin-right:0in; margin-top:0in;\'><span>Created Data: 2026</span></p></li><li><p style=\'margin-bottom:0in; margin-right:0in; margin-top:0in;\'><span>Update Frequency (estimated): none</span></p></li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p style=\'line-height:125%;\'><span><strong>Lineage</strong></span></p><ul><li><span>Originated: D</span>erived from the 2023 Digital Elevation Model from the <a target=\'_blank\' href=\'https://maps.cteco.uconn.edu/data/flight2023/\' rel=\'nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer\'>2023 Spring imagery and lidar capture</a></li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p style=\'line-height:125%;\'><strong>Attributes</strong></p><ul><li><p style=\'line-height:125%;\'><strong>Slope_Percent </strong>- The category of percent steep slope. Moderate (10%-15%), Steep (15%-20%), Very Steep (20%+).</p></li><li><p style=\'line-height:125%;\'><strong>Muni </strong>- Municipality</p></li><li><p style=\'line-height:125%;\'><strong>COG </strong>- Council of Governments</p></li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p>','public','2026-03-29T03:55:59.809140','2026-03-29T03:55:59.809146','State of Connecticut','ctgisoffice',NULL,'fddabc3f-102f-4cf5-85b8-d48f1a7fb2ab','Connecticut Data.json','03f5937f9c18a24f1ec73a41226e65ca7ac1fcb42ad1de41a465ab115a2ddf14','1.1','2026-03-29T03:55:59.809140','2026-03-29T03:55:59.809146','geospatial',NULL,0,'state-of-connecticut'),('61f400a5-d7ce-4708-8e9e-4e93e993384a','MARS EXPRESS MARS MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 4 3471 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2013-01-01 to 2014-12-31. It is a Global Gravity measurement and covers the time 2013-01-03T00:45:08.000 to 2013-01-03T03:17:14.500.','public','2026-03-13T18:42:21.369015','2026-03-13T18:42:21.369021','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','db5f97f6-6f85-4726-a83c-a5e6442da62d','NASA Data.json','7b93fa7e5a9572d23eb7cfb91d60522b791120133fb5641210ca26a286059505','1.1','2026-03-13T18:42:21.369015','2026-03-13T18:42:21.369021','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('62066b67-dde6-4dd8-82ab-7127899842c7','MARS EXPRESS MARS MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 3 3321 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2010-01-01 to 2012-12-31. It is a Global Gravity measurement and covers the time 2012-08-04T05:45:02.000 to 2012-08-04T08:15:01.500.','public','2026-03-13T16:44:10.466819','2026-03-13T16:44:10.466825','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','785712a1-d9ca-403e-b994-cc7b9e97a7bb','NASA Data.json','41e9527208023b3b17173858dec9e8b862d065630b0f2e6149c2064bb959735d','1.1','2026-03-13T16:44:10.466819','2026-03-13T16:44:10.466825','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('62188075-357a-47c4-b482-3cbf3f426924','ROSETTA-ORBITER PRELANDING OSIWAC 3 RDR MTP004 V2.0','This data set contains images acquired by the OSIRIS Wide Angle Camera during the PRELANDING phase of the Rosetta mission at the comet 67P, covering the period from 2014-06-04T10:50:00.000 to 2014-07-02T08:34:59.000. This version V2.0 supersedes previous deliveries of the same dataset. Note that the two datasets RO-C-OSIWAC-3-PRL-67PCHURYUMOV-M04-V1.0 and RO-C-OSIWAC-3-PRL-67PCHURYUMOV-M04B-V1.0 have been merged into one dataset: RO-C-OSIWAC-3-PRL-67PCHURYUMOV-M04-V2.0 (and higher), that covers the full time period spanned by the two previously delivered datasets.','public','2026-03-13T19:28:08.284740','2026-03-13T19:28:08.284747','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','de7cb821-3561-452b-87eb-e4aab1588e19','NASA Data.json','17dfcda8a636d6e6b7969e5bdbfdc9fa8678a8c7da54f0bcd29e350a4aaa35eb','1.1','2026-03-13T19:28:08.284740','2026-03-13T19:28:08.284747','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('62229933-962f-49e4-956d-a56635f1345e','PHOENIX MARS MECA OPTICAL MICROSCOPE 3  RADIOMETRIC SCI V1.0','The Microscopy, Electrochemistry, and  Conductivity Analyzer (MECA) experiment on the Mars Phoenix Lander  consists of four instrument components plus command electronics. This  MECA Imaging Science RDR data set contains data from one of the four  MECA components, the Optical Microscope (OM).','public','2026-03-13T19:16:32.645946','2026-03-13T19:16:32.645953','Imaging','Planetary Data System','026:00','af1d7ec6-1a71-4f9e-a78b-fbc21c6a7a7d','NASA Data.json','a290371836c7c526347d53af04911f761c47923029ff48aa782b5d660ac1d842','1.1','2026-03-13T19:16:32.645946','2026-03-13T19:16:32.645953','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('62990a7c-1686-44ee-b2de-0840f98beca4','MARS EXPRESS MARS MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 3 3323 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2010-01-01 to 2012-12-31. It is a Global Gravity measurement and covers the time 2012-08-05T03:31:55.000 to 2012-08-05T05:52:22.500.','public','2026-03-13T18:27:14.068858','2026-03-13T18:27:14.068865','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','23d23ff6-1ad8-488c-8767-f1420c145312','NASA Data.json','1cff22c4265b57c3f298568e069ff664389ae75dc07d64c30d19f3067cab8bab','1.1','2026-03-13T18:27:14.068858','2026-03-13T18:27:14.068865','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('63015619-05f8-45c2-bcb7-2abd8cafab1b','BLM ID Boise District Orchard Training Area Military Impact Area Poly','The Artillery Impact Area is a training space within the Orchard Training Center\'s Impact Area. It is used by the Idaho Army National Guard (IDARNG). This area is the primary target area for artillery. Various weapons are discharged in this area. This area contains the bulk of the unexploded ordinance found within the larger Impact Area. It contains a live round target area. There may be unexploded warheads in this area. There is no public access to this area and recreation and grazing are not allowed in this area. This is the boundary of the Orchard Training Area Artillery Impact Area in the Morley Nelson Snake River Birds of Prey (BOP) National Conservation Area (NCA). This area is within the Orchard Training Area Impact Area. This data set is limited to the BOP area. This dataset was updated using 2009 NAIP Photography in May 2011 making it current to May 2011. Data Attributes include: District Name, Field Office Name, District Code, Field Office Code, Area Name and Acres. For more information contact us at blm_id_stateoffice@blm.gov.','public','2026-03-25T12:33:37.300073','2026-03-25T12:33:37.300078','Bureau of Land Management','Bureau of Land Management, blm_id_stateoffice','010:04','79bde17d-0386-4636-9ffd-9cbf2f51609e','DOI BLM DCAT-US','1fb82dad419a95f62fb6840cea723196860b3c3fd77307fed304b45eefc11487','1.1','2026-03-25T12:33:37.300073','2026-03-25T12:33:37.300078','geospatial','010:000',0,'doi-gov'),('63d0b393-11c7-4b74-a62c-62f4bdbd3b45','ACS Table B21005 - Age','This data comes from the American Community Survey, specifically table B21005, broken out by age groups. Contains 1 year and 5 year estimates.','public','2026-03-28T21:59:07.837038','2026-03-28T21:59:07.837043','data.iowa.gov','svqueen',NULL,'f9dc5fa2-f1f7-44f0-b920-b9c63632fca5','Iowa metadata','6c6df87782d725a23789a5251077d09f86331e5c8cd7f376b25bc70d968c75b0','1.1','2026-03-28T21:59:07.837038','2026-03-28T21:59:07.837043','Economic Statistics',NULL,0,'state-of-iowa'),('63d0ee87-0722-4496-ac0c-b34d6322fcc5','GALILEO PROBE NMS RAW DATA SET','This Galileo Probe Mass Spectrometer (GPMS) data set includes: (1) Jupiter atmospheric entry data from December 7, 1995; (2) Instrument characterization data; March - April, 1985; (3) Residual background data from Earth testing; 1985 - 1989; (4) Residual background data from space; 1989, 1990, 1992; (5) Characterization data from the refurbished Engineering Unit (NOT YET AVAILABLE - December, 1998); (6) Sequence and conversion tables necessary to process the data.','public','2026-03-13T17:50:39.227980','2026-03-13T17:50:39.227985','Planetary Atmospheres','Planetary Data System','026:00','3da5e307-23d6-4fed-a3cf-cf3cf3068d26','NASA Data.json','f1e098369ca2b7c6212dee94a399b5658fdbab3ccdd42304c90144255c5f5831','1.1','2026-03-13T17:50:39.227980','2026-03-13T17:50:39.227985','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('63f2472d-1b99-4102-a76d-d928e8265122','Employee on Duty Fatalities, Injuries, and Illnesses (2.04 & 2.05)','This is the report for Employee on Duty Fatalities, Injuries, and Illnesses','public','2026-03-26T12:46:37.840865','2026-03-26T12:46:37.840871','Federal Railroad Administration','FRA Safety Data Team','021:27','08cab0a2-040a-4a87-b10d-ca8ff55e0554','DOT Socrata Data.json','9884cd75aaad6ec94e0868fb6e3d9b1df0d6f5bd79d84190a53ebcd0c9102f25','1.1','2026-03-26T12:46:37.840865','2026-03-26T12:46:37.840871','Railroads','021:037',0,'dot-gov'),('63f6df6c-8133-4d48-9268-4e127b164101','ROSETTA-LANDER 67P ROMAP 2 RBD MAG V1.0','This archive contains edited data that refers to target 67P (CODMAC level 2) from the ROMAP-MAG instrument onboard ROSETTA Lander, acquired during the RBD (Rebounds) phase. It also contains documentation which describes the ROMAP experiment. The data archived in this data set conform to the Planetary Data System (PDS) Standards, Version 3.6.','public','2026-03-13T19:46:25.825707','2026-03-13T19:46:25.825713','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','dcf6a613-f72c-4725-a3fe-546f0efdc59b','NASA Data.json','6d04f29c23fe2e1c4037c5ebde51960f20f4500b0558f14370f09e14de6549a3','1.1','2026-03-13T19:46:25.825707','2026-03-13T19:46:25.825713','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('6417a26f-c166-417f-b22d-8b7ca37ec75b','myUSCIS - draft-benefits','Temporarily stores non-ELIS case draft data for systems such as Claims 3, Global, and BenefitsHub.','non-public','2026-03-22T11:54:06.787671','2026-03-22T11:54:06.787677','Unspecified','Open Data (MGMT)','024:030','2e22f29b-0c76-4f5f-bce5-df1f2cf0b062','DHS datajson source','ea9fcd8f63d5c9bc994b0a70a4a1d7472be49bfa19c9ac0489e5a570039227b7','1.1','2026-03-22T11:54:06.787671','2026-03-22T11:54:06.787677',NULL,'024:000',0,'dhs-gov'),('6425502d-9983-4cb2-a637-45d200e7f028','California Brown Pelican Range - CWHR B043a [ds3282]','<div style=\'text-align:Left;\'><div><div><p style=\'margin:0 0 14 0;\'><span><span>Vector datasets of CWHR range maps are one component of California Wildlife Habitat Relationships (CWHR), a comprehensive information system and predictive model for California\'s wildlife. The CWHR System was developed to support habitat conservation and management, land use planning, impact assessment, education, and research involving terrestrial vertebrates in California. CWHR contains information on life history, management status, geographic distribution, and habitat relationships for wildlife species known to occur regularly in California. Range maps represent the maximum, current geographic extent of each species within California. They were originally delineated at a scale of 1:5,000,000 by species-level experts and have gradually been revised at a scale of 1:1,000,000. For more information about CWHR, visit the CWHR webpage (</span><a href=\'https://www.wildlife.ca.gov/Data/CWHR\' style=\'text-decoration:underline;\' rel=\'nofollow ugc\'><span>https://www.wildlife.ca.gov/Data/CWHR</span></a><span>). The webpage provides links to download CWHR data and user documents such as a look up table of available range maps including species code, species name, and range map revision history; a full set of CWHR GIS data; .pdf files of each range map or species life history accounts; and a User Guide.</span></span></p></div></div></div>','public','2026-03-23T13:56:14.540156','2026-03-23T13:56:14.540160','California Department of Fish and Wildlife','BIOS_Admin',NULL,'a4afec1c-b25b-49a2-afab-9d251004918b','State of California','68f2b2b51d3ea3ad9c3596c7c8d5387d1371d614579c03f271bfd096136d32bd','1.1','2026-03-23T13:56:14.540156','2026-03-23T13:56:14.540160','Natural Resources',NULL,0,'ca-gov'),('644a80b0-65f3-4789-a4d2-38f89a575618','VG2 URA MAG RESAMPLED RDR U1 COORDINATES                                      9.6SEC V1.0','This data set includes data from the          Low Field Magnetometer (LFM) in the solar wind during the Uranus          encounter. The encounter data (1986-01-24T07:00:00  ->          1986-01-25T04:00:00) have been averaged from the 1.92 second          averaged data to a 9.6 second resampled rate and are provided in          the Uranus Longitude (U1) coordinate system. Magnetometer data          in the solar wind are given in Heliographic coordinates.','public','2026-03-13T19:54:13.291695','2026-03-13T19:54:13.291703','planetary plasma interactions','Planetary Data System','026:00','9f653483-e334-40b8-afb0-30bb367c6aca','NASA Data.json','23d6f61f7b99acfd130a24a3f67d463226e36f2fcb5ba908f90eadbb1e6eb768','1.1','2026-03-13T19:54:13.291695','2026-03-13T19:54:13.291703','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('64a9cde5-1eb6-42f0-b6c9-9ca942087cd4','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 2 0648 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 2 phase 2015-03-11 to 2015-06-30. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-03-16T11:33:05.000 to 2015-03-16T13:10:15.000.','public','2026-03-13T17:29:10.509784','2026-03-13T17:29:10.509790','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','178108a0-484f-4a31-ab22-7a76c8b68c18','NASA Data.json','1c31d8c728e2766f501ab55ddec14413e7e94372d61b730846ab22a9dee8119d','1.1','2026-03-13T17:29:10.509784','2026-03-13T17:29:10.509790','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('64fe3d9f-dfea-4f4f-8c64-ef791b5cdaec','MARS EXPRESS SUN MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 5 3770 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2015-01-01 to 2016-12-31. It is a Solar Conjunction measurement and covers the time 2015-06-17T14:18:01 to 2015-06-17T17:29:00.','public','2026-03-13T18:34:24.975412','2026-03-13T18:34:24.975417','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','1dfc968d-6de3-473e-bb2d-2f7509af8881','NASA Data.json','4fe9518a5d2a815211b5741f278efc4f6601e79b6ce12fe5eeb6b163af1bbacd','1.1','2026-03-13T18:34:24.975412','2026-03-13T18:34:24.975417','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('65160672-b700-4e1a-9832-bb5947b73b0a','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSINAC 4 ESC1-MTP010 RDR-REFLECT V1.0','This CODMAC level 4 data set contains radiometric calibrated and geometric distortion corrected (resampled) image data in reflectance units (normalized and thus without unit), acquired by the OSIRIS Narrow Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft during the COMET ESCORT 1 mission phase, covering the period from 2014-11-21T23:25:00.000 to 2014-12-19T23:24:59.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V1.0 is the first version of this dataset: Lien corrected dataset after October 2018 PSA/PDS external peer review.','public','2026-03-13T17:39:00.559988','2026-03-13T17:39:00.559993','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','7dd6e869-6d53-4cf6-b5f4-9364eb285fb3','NASA Data.json','98b9508ee499a41924a610ca4469e32b2104709f06dde135f985d8a12cb5ff98','1.1','2026-03-13T17:39:00.559988','2026-03-13T17:39:00.559993','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('653fd2d8-d7a1-4ffc-8897-c17837976219','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RPCLAP 2 ESC3 MTP019 V1.0','This dataset contains EDITED data from Rosetta RPC-LAP, acquired during MTP19, part of the COMET ESCORT 3 mission phase. The primary target was comet 67P/C-G.','public','2026-03-13T19:40:15.920428','2026-03-13T19:40:15.920436','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','722c1b9d-177c-42e8-8e64-0a9329d9b92d','NASA Data.json','f4d8bba6a3276b2f19570917708439075ca5e107645e17a8b18474170eab5503','1.1','2026-03-13T19:40:15.920428','2026-03-13T19:40:15.920436','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('6578a9f2-bf0c-435d-9edd-8fa13ce57e51','Continuous Fixed Station Water Quality Measurements in Cape Lookout National Seashore, September 2009 (Certified)','This dataset represents continuous water quality measurements that were taken at a fixed point in Cape Lookout National Seashore during the month of September, 2009 as a part of the Fixed Station Water Quality Monitoring protocol that was developed by the Southeast Coast I&M Network (SECN). The measurements were taken by a YSI 6600 ESD Multi-Parameter Long Term Water Quality Monitoring Datasonde unit that serves as the standard fixed station water quality monitoring equipment for all similar operations conducted by the SECN. The following parameters were measured at 15 minute intervals during the time period that has been specified: Water Temperature, Specific Conductivity, Salinity, Dissolved Oxygen (DO), DO Concentration, Shallow Depth, pH Level, and Turbidity. Any anomalies noted regarding these parameters have also been noted in separate fields.  Please note that these measurements have been certified by network personnel.','public','2026-03-26T05:27:59.315708','2026-03-26T05:27:59.315713','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','751851a4-0259-4299-b3de-42160e910b4e','DOI NPS DCAT-US','95cde9d14dbd94e7848c0a78d0abe00ac816282686573d65ecd2b33c87e3aae2','1.1','2026-03-26T05:27:59.315708','2026-03-26T05:27:59.315713','Vector Dataset','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('65ad209e-bf79-46ee-a594-ced266b79081','VG2 JUP PLS PLASMA DERIVED ION MOMENTS    96.0 SEC V1.0','This data set contains the best    estimates of the total ion density from Voyager 2 at Jupiter in the PLS    voltage range (10-5950 eV/Q). It is calculated using the method of    which to first order consists of taking the total measured current and    dividing by the collector area and plasma bulk velocity. This method is    only accurate for high mach number flows directly into the detector, and    may result in underestimates of the total density of a factor of 2 in the    outer magnetosphere. Thus absolute densities should be treated with    caution, but density variations in the data set can be trusted. The low    resolution mode density is used at all times except day 190 2100-2200 when    the larger of the high and low resolution mode densities in a 96 sec    period is used. Corotation is assumed inside L=17.5, and a constant    velocity component of 200 km/s into the D cup is used outside of this.    Data format: column 1 is time (yyyy-mm-ddThh:mm:ss.sssZ), column 2 is    the moment density in cm^-3. Each row has format (a24, 1x, 1pe9.2). Values    of -9.99e+10 indicate that the parameter could not be obtained from the    data using the standard analysis technique. Additional information about    this data set and the instrument which produced it can be found elsewhere    in this catalog.','public','2026-03-13T17:41:51.254764','2026-03-13T17:41:51.254771','planetary plasma interactions','Planetary Data System','026:00','c977e432-07fe-4327-88ae-75c9edd2bf40','NASA Data.json','556818188bfe28c55edacda02804fdd8007fa9b54314dd0813886d8deb95a023','1.1','2026-03-13T17:41:51.254764','2026-03-13T17:41:51.254771','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('65d1b0d6-e76a-49f6-8ada-4b4a76bf9ec3','ROSETTA-ORBITER PRELANDING OSINAC 2 EDR MTP003 V2.0','This data set contains images acquired by the OSIRIS Narrow Angle Camera during the PRELANDING phase of the Rosetta mission at the comet 67P, covering the period from 2014-05-07T12:48:00.000 to 2014-06-04T10:49:59.000. This version V2.0 supersedes previous deliveries of the same dataset.','public','2026-03-13T18:03:34.489145','2026-03-13T18:03:34.489149','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','5f15be31-0da5-4504-af4e-1c8980cb46a1','NASA Data.json','65de1aad5c720f8d43b0828cba5ffcc5d2178c3dcc844e7712b7a6ac003dabbf','1.1','2026-03-13T18:03:34.489145','2026-03-13T18:03:34.489149','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('66021a4a-6e8d-4090-be75-116f15de66c1','DAWN CERES RAW GRAVITY SCIENCE V2.0','This data set contains archival raw, partially processed, and ancillary/supporting gravity science data acquired during the Dawn mission while the spacecraft was in orbit around the asteroid Ceres. The radio observations were carried out using the Dawn spacecraft and Earth-based receiving stations of the NASA Deep Space Network (DSN). The data set was designed primarily to support generation of high-resolution gravity field models for Ceres. Of most interest are likely to be the Orbit Data Files in the ODF directory and Tracking and Navigation Files in the TNF directory, which provided the raw input to gravity investigations, as well as the ionospheric and tropospheric media calibration files in the ION and TRO directories, respectively.','public','2026-03-13T19:53:13.863061','2026-03-13T19:53:13.863067','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','9b38eade-ad34-42b0-a742-9cddd7b679d1','NASA Data.json','3d4d8ae94eee9a5a8196608f691c64bf80100b96b2872446416decc7f416a508','1.1','2026-03-13T19:53:13.863061','2026-03-13T19:53:13.863067','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('661c86e6-673a-4f80-97a0-8b01d90a3597','Graduation Pathways Completion Rates (2019-20 to 2024-25)','In 2019, House Bill 1599 established different graduation pathways as part of statewide high school graduation requirements. The bill also required the Office of Superintendent of Public Instruction (OSPI) to annually report on the number of students completing each pathway. In accordance with legislation, this dataset features pathway completion rates for all four-year graduation cohorts since the Class of 2020. An accompanying data display is available at the source link below.','public','2026-03-22T03:15:01.970868','2026-03-29T04:04:58.581870','data.wa.gov','Andrew Nelson',NULL,'32b90da8-2508-418a-aa51-c60f79917ee3','WA JSON','b7967cb3d7312519b307df6d48a56b8c8274e5c52e6990a59f051138036bc959','1.1','2026-03-22T03:15:01.970868','2026-03-29T04:04:58.581870','education',NULL,0,'state-of-washington'),('661cfa36-e15b-48f7-9f6a-9823e5d59400','Estuarine and Nearshore Marine Sediment Quality Measurements in Fort Pulaski National Monument (2007)','This dataset represents sediment quality measurements that were taken in Fort Pulaski National Monument during 2007 as a part of the marine water and sediment quality assessment protocol that was developed by the Southeast Coast I&M Network (SECN). The protocol is modeled after the EPA\'s National Coastal Assessment Program (www.epa.gov/emap/nca) and it consists of conducting sediment sampling every 10 years based on a probabilistic sampling design that was also designed by the EPA. Thirty sites were selected within the Savannah River, South Channel Savannah River, Bull River, Shad River, Lazaretto Creek, and Tybee Creek at which sediments were sampled using a Van Veen sampler and composited for analysis as described in the National Coastal Assessment Quality Assurance Project Plan (www.epa.gov/emap/nca/html/docs/qaprojplan.html). The final analyses of the sediment samples were conducted by GPL Laboratories, LLC (now Centauri Labs); please refer to their website (www.centaurilabs.com) or the documents listed in the Cross Reference section for more information about the analytical process. Please note that each sampling location contains multiple sediment parameters that are recorded individually.','public','2026-03-26T05:28:01.791907','2026-03-26T05:28:01.791913','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','539ec895-f2c4-477c-ac77-847fbaa8d2aa','DOI NPS DCAT-US','7524487598c66e57bd50beb1628ca10c086bb1e757db47731af4c44f243dd4b0','1.1','2026-03-26T05:28:01.791907','2026-03-26T05:28:01.791913','Vector Dataset','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('6634953d-95dd-4ebf-94fa-90b20bc1a7fb','Data from: Evaluating the Long-Term Efficacy of Four Active Ingredients against <i>Rhyzopertha dominica </i>(F.) (Coleoptera: Bostrichidae) and <i>Sitophilus oryzae </i>(L.) (Coleoptera: Curculionidae) on Stored Sorghum','<p dir=\"ltr\">The objective of this study was to determine the residual efficacy of four commercially available grain protectants, Gravista<sup>®</sup> (deltamethrin + methoprene + PBO), Diacon<sup>®</sup> IGR (methoprene), Sensat™ (spinosad), and EverGreen<sup>®</sup> (pyrethrin), applied to sorghum and held for each of eight storage periods spanning 28 weeks, against <i>Rhyzopertha dominica</i> and <i>Sitophilus oryzae</i>. Subsamples were collected every 4 weeks (up to 28 post grain protectant application) and infested with 10 adults of either <i>R. dominica</i> or <i>S. oryzae.</i> The initial adult mortality was assessed 7 d post-exposure to the treated grain. After adult mortality was determined, the sorghum was held for 8 weeks and adult progeny were counted. Additionally the amount of frass and insect damaged kernels were also evaluated. </p>','public','2026-03-13T22:47:06.216291','2026-03-13T22:47:06.216297','Agricultural Research Service','Scheff, Deanna, S','005:18','35080c27-f474-4f2b-8e3d-1a0ac9ec6650','USDA JSON','8baae7aec25be7ab41967c67b05db560da2130b77800a41f217ec0cfe4c7e478','1.1','2026-03-13T22:47:06.216291','2026-03-13T22:47:06.216297',NULL,'005:040',0,'usda-gov'),('67105691-57bd-4ac7-9ad7-ac92a0bc8bc4','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 3 1106 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 3 phase 2015-07-01 to 2015-10-21. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-10-17T04:58:30.000 to 2015-10-17T10:01:41.000.','public','2026-03-13T17:15:46.023386','2026-03-13T17:15:46.023391','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','93b9b1cd-1198-4965-aa63-af141223950c','NASA Data.json','e65c8c83844869e7d731035a634459847ab3a274748268adced83ee37e0a3621','1.1','2026-03-13T17:15:46.023386','2026-03-13T17:15:46.023391','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('672a4383-7680-4959-b23b-2a2e0785dee8','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 4 1244 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 4 phase 2015-10-22 to 2015-12-31. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-12-08T12:00:15.000 to 2015-12-08T16:08:51.500.','public','2026-03-13T18:24:40.561812','2026-03-13T18:24:40.561818','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','95f981a3-6526-44a2-859e-fac8f46f4da2','NASA Data.json','29553011d8ce296693babbb39d1d23361fc2ec62393858886e5d907c5bc41a29','1.1','2026-03-13T18:24:40.561812','2026-03-13T18:24:40.561818','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('6743db09-e8a2-436c-9347-487a56b1f587','NEAR NIS SPECTRA FOR CRUISE1','This data set contains the NEAR infrared spectrometer (NIS) data for the CRUISE1 phase. The data set begins on 1996-02-20T00:00:00.000 and ends 1997-06-24T23:59:59.999 . The data are raw telemetry data, provided in engineering units, that have been reformatted into FITS file format (NASA Office of Science and Technology (NOST), 100-1.0). In addition to the raw spectrometer data, a calibration file and algorithm are available. This data set is archived as a set of CDROM images as a part of the NEAR EDR volume set.','public','2026-03-13T18:02:29.430517','2026-03-13T18:02:29.430522','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','36cfdf47-c1dd-48f2-99eb-101cc61600b1','NASA Data.json','68e9208309409584c8e71179bc23b48ccf95f39e109142d332350d470b6f1e59','1.1','2026-03-13T18:02:29.430517','2026-03-13T18:02:29.430522','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('6766cb25-9c07-4cac-a3ae-47d3c9008889','NEW HORIZONS REX PLUTO CRUISE CALIBRATED V1.0','This data set contains Calibrated data taken by the New Horizons Radio Science Experiment instrument during the pluto cruise mission phase. This is VERSION 1.0 of this data set. The REX datasets over the mission include calibrations using known radio sources, Jupiter, and cold sky measurements; operational readiness tests (ORTs); internal test pattern calibration; and prime science radiometry and occultation observations during the Pluto Encounter.','public','2026-03-13T18:44:25.198500','2026-03-13T18:44:25.198507','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','c7a8cc00-6335-4b50-b98d-b25a487fb947','NASA Data.json','7972eb3222d8c75f9d3209c2238c425e77016cf705f9fd5d565d4315d46891f7','1.1','2026-03-13T18:44:25.198500','2026-03-13T18:44:25.198507','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('67708ac2-2614-461b-bf12-ecad85df70c5','Citywide Mobility Survey - Trip 2024','The Citywide Mobility Survey (CMS) is NYC DOT\'s annual travel survey to assess the travel behavior, preferences, and attitudes of NYC residents. It is composed of 5 linked data tables.\n\nCitywide Mobility Survey (CMS) Trip table contains characteristics of each trip made by the participants, including origins and destinations, mode, purpose, transportation related fees such as transit, parking, or taxi pay, parking location for the bikes or micromobility devices, number of travelers, trip duration, and trip distance.\n\n<b>Other 2024 Citywide Mobility Survey Datasets:</b>\n<a href=\"https://data.cityofnewyork.us/d/i2im-iqtt\">Citywide Mobility Survey - Person 2024 </a>\n<a href=\"https://data.cityofnewyork.us/d/5mb3-padx\">Citywide Mobility Survey - Household 2024</a>\n<a href=\"https://data.cityofnewyork.us/d/naav-ygga\">Citywide Mobility Survey - Day 2024</a>\n<a href=\"https://data.cityofnewyork.us/d/qhkz-4dqm\">Citywide Mobility Survey - Vehicle 2024</a>\n\nSee all the <a href=\"https://data.cityofnewyork.us/browse?sortBy=relevance&pageSize=20&Data-Collection_Data-Collection=Citywide+Mobility+Survey\">Citywide Mobility Survey Data</a>, including past surveys.','public','2026-03-29T04:45:53.676141','2026-03-29T04:45:53.676146','data.cityofnewyork.us','NYC OpenData',NULL,'1fa5bf7a-0569-4420-832c-6e6f015a7e44','NYC JSON','00fbc7bd0fc529acab2891b4cf871a28f2ac4ea1c25f806d8af1fc682cf8b26c','1.1','2026-03-29T04:45:53.676141','2026-03-29T04:45:53.676146','Transportation',NULL,0,'city-of-new-york'),('682ce1c5-85d1-452a-8887-027db3b0adcb','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 1 0600 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 1 phase 2014-11-20 to 2015-03-10. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-02-24T10:44:20.000 to 2015-02-24T15:20:09.500.','public','2026-03-13T19:41:51.950928','2026-03-13T19:41:51.950934','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','aa293dee-282c-45f3-b918-bcf1739c1c68','NASA Data.json','1da8522fe9e20f5d5888e800afe796382b550b589d3e3921746cb3843d7e72a6','1.1','2026-03-13T19:41:51.950928','2026-03-13T19:41:51.950934','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('6840352a-78d7-4b1b-8e7b-727dccb68ab0','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 