 EXT2 SPICAM MARS CLEANED IR RDR V1.0','The Mars Express SPICAM level 1A IR data set contains clean measurements from the infrared SPICAM spectrometer collected during the nominal MARS phases','public','2026-03-13T19:46:12.956313','2026-03-13T19:46:12.956318','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','8bfee47d-ef37-41a9-b867-deb37eb27708','NASA Data.json','79647c7ea5a0786d80d87c6b3f190df9c444d59aad7c2c69451aeddb54cfcf99','1.1','2026-03-13T19:46:12.956313','2026-03-13T19:46:12.956318','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('68f7c655-d658-41fc-9f0e-b0165af6b690','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 1 0471 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 1 phase 2014-11-20 to 2015-03-10. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2014-12-03T13:16:25.000 to 2014-12-03T21:45:08.000.','public','2026-03-13T16:46:10.754000','2026-03-13T16:46:10.754006','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','b2029d62-160c-4721-ba75-2e0f891c40c6','NASA Data.json','a1f9514a2530fd4303626f15f31e81ba650cb36528f83d11bba7692c516d4c03','1.1','2026-03-13T16:46:10.754000','2026-03-13T16:46:10.754006','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('69002dc8-b0c7-4295-8ef5-7eea3eb90493','V-safe COVID-19','Users of the V-safe data are required to adhere to the following standards for the analysis and reporting of research data. All research results must be presented and/or published in a manner that protects the confidentiality of participants. V-safe data will not be presented and/or published in any way in which an individual can be identified. Therefore, users will:\n<ol>\n<li>Not attempt to link or permit others to link the data with individually identified records in another database.</li>\n<li>Not attempt to learn the identity of any participant in the data and will not deliberately combine these data with other CDC or non-CDC data for the purpose of matching records to identify individuals. If you should inadvertently discover the identity of any participant, you will ensure the identity of any participant is kept confidential, and will not be used in any publications and/or presentations.</li>\n<li>Not imply or state, either in written or oral form, that interpretations based on analysis of the data reflect official CDC policies or positions.</li>\n<li>Understand that sub-national analyses are not appropriate for this national sample and will not be conducted. </li>\n<li>Understand that V-safe is a voluntary self-enrollment program requiring smartphone access; therefore, information from V-safe might not be representative or generalizable to the US population.</li></ol>\nBy clicking on the weblink below to download and use these V-safe data, you signify your agreement to comply with the above-stated terms.\n\nV-safe is a voluntary U.S. active safety surveillance system established by CDC to characterize local and systemic side effects of new vaccines administered after U.S. authorization or licensure. V-safe participants are not a random sample of all vaccinated persons in the United States and data might not be generalizable to the full U.S. vaccinated population. Participants may have been more likely to complete surveys if experiencing symptoms post-vaccination. All V-safe measures are self-reported, therefore there may be some misclassification of outcomes, vaccine-related information, or demographics.\n\nFor participants who requested corrections (i.e. vaccination date or vaccine manufacturer) to their vaccination record, data may be missing for one or more doses.  Requested corrections were applied to ‘Enrollment’, ‘Vaccination’, and ‘Dose History’ files. The old vaccination records are located in the ‘Vaccination (Old Records)’ file while the corrected vaccine records are in the ‘Vaccination’ file. Mobile outages or technical malfunctions may have caused a small number of missing surveys or collection of incorrect survey type. Occasional system outages and attrition over time also contribute to incomplete reporting. \n\nV-safe COVID-19 public data includes enrollment, vaccination information, and daily and weekly surveys collected from 1/22/2024 to 3/23/2025. Corresponding V-safe Registration public data (de-identified demographic data) can be downloaded at data.cdc.gov. Please review the V-safe data user agreement before analyzing any V-safe data.','public','2026-03-20T17:40:23.962186','2026-03-20T17:40:23.962191','Centers for Disease Control and Prevention','Vsafe@cdc.gov','009:15','9f5562a5-8439-4872-827f-89c29efbcf2e','Healthdata.gov','7eac1c257e36d83d2c9997f145eb33ac86c9c33d564041a1cde5ce68fad00613','1.1','2026-03-20T17:40:23.962186','2026-03-20T17:40:23.962191','National Center for Emerging and Zoonotic Infectious Diseases','009:028',0,'hhs-gov'),('692c17ba-ea1a-4466-b362-7d960648d170','LCROSS SUN 2ND NEAR IR SPECTROMETER 3 CAL V1.0','Calibrated spectra from the Near Infrared Spectrometer 2 (NSP2) aboard the Lunar Crater Observation and Sensing Satellite (LCROSS).','public','2026-03-13T17:42:23.015220','2026-03-13T17:42:23.015225','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','86ee9722-f72f-4200-9afb-2918802c1098','NASA Data.json','79c37fef7a7dc48d50f9504b094f6184ac5cd35fea31da6b2a61a11fc2f6b5c7','1.1','2026-03-13T17:42:23.015220','2026-03-13T17:42:23.015225','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('692d54f3-2db6-4a1c-9c4e-d0d0dd9f9c34','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 3 1038 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 3 phase 2015-07-01 to 2015-10-21. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-09-16T21:17:30.000 to 2015-09-17T05:26:15.500.','public','2026-03-13T17:11:27.863800','2026-03-13T17:11:27.863806','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','ef961c12-f856-4cd3-90b8-e123896dd520','NASA Data.json','4775fdb2f76007d10d0ac90b31aa51964d1a2f8e9610344fd51ac0f105afca40','1.1','2026-03-13T17:11:27.863800','2026-03-13T17:11:27.863806','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('6932e643-ed99-4a55-985e-2793049814b0','Hydrographic and Impairment Statistics Database: JOFL','Hydrographic and Impairment Statistics (HIS) is a National Park Service (NPS) Water Resources Division (WRD) project established to track certain goals created in response to the Government Performance and Results Act of 1993 (GPRA). One water resources management goal established by the Department of the Interior under GRPA requires NPS to track the percent of its managed surface waters that are meeting Clean Water Act (CWA) water quality standards. This goal requires an accurate inventory that spatially quantifies the surface water hydrography that each bureau manages and a procedure to determine and track which waterbodies are or are not meeting water quality standards as outlined by Section 303(d) of the CWA. This project helps meet this DOI GRPA goal by inventorying and monitoring in a geographic information system for the NPS: (1) CWA 303(d) quality impaired waters and causes; and (2) hydrographic statistics based on the United States Geological Survey (USGS) National Hydrography Dataset (NHD). Hydrographic and 303(d) impairment statistics were evaluated based on a combination of 1:24,000 (NHD) and finer scale data (frequently provided by state GIS layers).','public','2026-03-29T06:06:34.726059','2026-03-29T06:06:34.726065','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','c961e573-a980-460b-b86b-dd794d8c867a','DOI NPS DCAT-US','df60f7e2c2b32097f3b244028a7df0fca61d7d85f781ca5234dd811dce7037c3','1.1','2026-03-29T06:06:34.726059','2026-03-29T06:06:34.726065','geospatial','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('693db846-1c9c-4b3c-a4f3-90e5fc55bb0a','PHOBOS 2 MARS VSK-FREGAT EDR V1.0','This data set consists of the set of images obtained by the VSK-Fregat experiment on the Phobos 2 spacecraft. This data set is saved for historical reasons, but is not considered to be of archival quality.','public','2026-03-13T18:58:45.638306','2026-03-13T18:58:45.638313','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','12c938e6-6089-49aa-b507-acf02b27ac89','NASA Data.json','4a1187184a0e8ec7717da7958407aa80bbc195a4ac38463c7e8a62473bcad36c','1.1','2026-03-13T18:58:45.638306','2026-03-13T18:58:45.638313','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('69402923-27b2-4d06-ba20-778e31bc10f4','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 1 0503 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 1 phase 2014-11-20 to 2015-03-10. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2014-12-24T00:19:40.000 to 2014-12-24T12:14:13.000.','public','2026-03-13T16:51:34.640933','2026-03-13T16:51:34.640938','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','f131aea3-b483-41e7-a5e4-4396b29adb0f','NASA Data.json','ad29a8b26cc5862d168b7a687941e9e8c7a28aa746c08206c6d180e6e400f79e','1.1','2026-03-13T16:51:34.640933','2026-03-13T16:51:34.640938','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('6943b486-b402-4c59-a2f8-e64a3ce4ac96','MSX ZODIACAL DUST DATA V1.0','The Midcourse Space Experiment (MSX) mid-infrared emission measurements from the zodiacal dust cloud in spectral bands centered at 8.3 12, 15, and 21 microns.','public','2026-03-13T18:08:52.031927','2026-03-13T18:08:52.031932','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','57fa384a-d05c-4486-9457-bf92d353a4c0','NASA Data.json','4c38bdaa1a2e3b2706bf7af058b4232f141bf474daef84cef27845a94a94589e','1.1','2026-03-13T18:08:52.031927','2026-03-13T18:08:52.031932','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('69467521-3c7c-44cc-9e0d-91229b9c12d2','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 PRELANDING 0385 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the PRELANDING phase 2014-01-21 to 2014-11-18. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2014-10-25T12:21:15.000 to 2014-10-25T14:39:58.500.','public','2026-03-13T20:05:04.509956','2026-03-13T20:05:04.509964','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','8b6c038f-5b27-462a-ae4e-dd36979b1e73','NASA Data.json','5b9e0e131355126522d63056a8823c2722ce358d07a2dae90fbfcfaa6cbb7fb3','1.1','2026-03-13T20:05:04.509956','2026-03-13T20:05:04.509964','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('69508438-3be1-4028-9749-cab613fa87d8','Hydrographic and Impairment Statistics Database: NPS-WSR Chilikadrotna Wild and Scenic River','Hydrographic and Impairment Statistics (HIS) is a National Park Service (NPS) Water Resources Division (WRD) project established to track certain goals created in response to the Government Performance and Results Act of 1993 (GPRA). One water resources management goal established by the Department of the Interior under GRPA requires NPS to track the percent of its managed surface waters that are meeting Clean Water Act (CWA) water quality standards. This goal requires an accurate inventory that spatially quantifies the surface water hydrography that each bureau manages and a procedure to determine and track which waterbodies are or are not meeting water quality standards as outlined by Section 303(d) of the CWA. This project helps meet this DOI GRPA goal by inventorying and monitoring in a geographic information system for the NPS: (1) CWA 303(d) quality impaired waters and causes; and (2) hydrographic statistics based on the United States Geological Survey (USGS) National Hydrography Dataset (NHD). Hydrographic and 303(d) impairment statistics were evaluated based on a combination of 1:24,000 (NHD) and finer scale data (frequently provided by state GIS layers).','public','2026-03-29T06:05:58.068121','2026-03-29T06:05:58.068128','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','51c9cbf6-8470-42c4-b77d-8bef0c8b776b','DOI NPS DCAT-US','be25f24ae3c1c00bf4b2143e26c0fb955485d825f8a1f98dc4215fb04622cf08','1.1','2026-03-29T06:05:58.068121','2026-03-29T06:05:58.068128','geospatial','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('6964e68c-8e79-46ad-88d3-91844a469af0','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSIWAC 4 PRL-MTP001 RDR-INF-REFL V1.0','This CODMAC level 4 data set contains solar stray-light corrected, in-field stray-light corrected,  radiometric calibrated and geometric distortion corrected  (resampled) image data in reflectance units (normalized  and thus without unit),  acquired by the OSIRIS Wide Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft  during the PRELANDING mission phase, covering the period  from 2014-01-20T10:00:00.000 to 2014-05-07T12:47:59.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V1.0 is the first version of this dataset: Lien corrected dataset after September 2019 PSA/PDS external peer review.','public','2026-03-13T19:06:29.522111','2026-03-13T19:06:29.522116','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','d41a78e4-cb28-473c-ac7f-a61ccb3e8935','NASA Data.json','4d965a5d9a40a6f7a8ffb32a2a9ea96c0125526652ddc9bd9cbe00fb3ad1c114','1.1','2026-03-13T19:06:29.522111','2026-03-13T19:06:29.522116','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('69a8a429-1033-460b-97fe-a1258ee1d79a','Accident Detail Listing (3.18)','This is the page for Accident Detail Listing (3.18).','public','2026-03-26T12:48:33.178946','2026-03-26T12:48:33.178952','Federal Railroad Administration','FRA Safety Data Team','021:27','60ce4c27-b441-4e89-91fb-557efd58fe5a','DOT Socrata Data.json','7a2063c5d1050e4ea1cde54624b833a2e1f97c33692930cb7051577ecc2cff49','1.1','2026-03-26T12:48:33.178946','2026-03-26T12:48:33.178952','Railroads','021:037',0,'dot-gov'),('69abd360-90db-432b-ba96-d3abd3d7cc06','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 2 0783 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 2 phase 2015-03-11 to 2015-06-30. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-05-17T05:07:20.000 to 2015-05-17T06:57:14.500.','public','2026-03-13T16:57:12.743273','2026-03-13T16:57:12.743279','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','d39773f5-3fc6-4aad-9338-4486d22a3676','NASA Data.json','e82aa678b2f53eb25f02a4ddcd719bff783c207956fbf84e541744f79c361512','1.1','2026-03-13T16:57:12.743273','2026-03-13T16:57:12.743279','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('69bf0dfe-e37e-42c2-9e70-894e248e78c0','\"Deepwater CTD - 94g077a.ctd.nc - 26.0N, -90.6W - 1994-00-17\"','The Minerals Management Service (MMS) of the U. S. Department of the Interior funded the Deepwater Physical Oceanography Reanalysis and Synthesis of Historical Data Study in the Gulf of Mexico. MMS awarded the contract to the Texas A&M Research Foundation in July 1998. The basic study area is bounded by the shelf edge and the 25DGN latitude, which is the southern boundary; it extends from sea surface to sea floor. MMS has four objectives for the study. First is to create an inventory of physical oceanographic data and compile it into a single database on a CD-ROM. Second is to conduct analyses and interpretations of the physical oceanographic data to identify physical processes and phenomena. Third is to produce a climatology of the processes from available data and analyses and to prioritize the processes in terms of importance to improved understanding, simulation, and prediction of deepwater circulation. Fourth is to provide criteria and constraints useful in design of future field observations and numerical modeling efforts. Study results will provide MMS with information needed to direct its resources more efficiently and effectively in the review and assessment of potential environmental impacts of offshore oil and gas operations in the deepwater Gulf of Mexico.','public','2026-03-26T19:17:54.610007','2026-03-26T19:17:54.610014',NULL,NULL,NULL,'1eb904ff-01d0-4012-82db-c3e01ec12cd2','ioos',NULL,NULL,'2026-03-26T19:17:54.610007','2026-03-26T19:17:54.610014',NULL,NULL,NULL,'noaa-gov'),('69bf8eeb-ada0-41d5-bfcf-309a274c6e23','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RPCMIP 3 EXT2 V1.0','This archive contains calibrated data from the RPC-MIP instrument onboard ROSETTA Orbiter, acquired during the ROSETTA EXTENSION part 2 mission phase. The primary target was comet 67P/C-G. It also contains documentation which describes the MIP experiment. The data archived in this data set conform to the Planetary Data System Standards, Version 3.6.','public','2026-03-13T17:00:55.690401','2026-03-13T17:00:55.690406','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','945f88b8-aa46-44f0-b247-1c696457c9b6','NASA Data.json','9a1d9529c24e7ee126276f292224612fd01601cde3305e775e07291047cc7c95','1.1','2026-03-13T17:00:55.690401','2026-03-13T17:00:55.690406','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('69d167ac-86ec-4636-86d8-5faf35bb64f2','Continuous Fixed Station Water Quality Measurements in Cape Lookout National Seashore, March 2008 (Certified)','This dataset represents continuous water quality measurements that were taken at a fixed point in Cape Lookout National Seashore during the month of March, 2008 as a part of the Fixed Station Water Quality Monitoring protocol that was developed by the Southeast Coast I&M Network (SECN). The measurements were taken by a YSI 6600 ESD Multi-Parameter Long Term Water Quality Monitoring Datasonde unit that serves as the standard fixed station water quality monitoring equipment for all similar operations conducted by the SECN. The following parameters were measured at 15 minute intervals during the time period that has been specified: Water Temperature, Specific Conductivity, Salinity, Dissolved Oxygen (DO), DO Concentration, Shallow Depth, pH Level, and Turbidity. Any anomalies noted regarding these parameters have also been noted in separate fields.  Please note that these measurements have been certified by network personnel.','public','2026-03-26T05:34:43.188502','2026-03-26T05:34:43.188507','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','83dc75f2-0b69-481b-86f8-e8a3fa847de6','DOI NPS DCAT-US','2d251eb30c114fd264438373901e697400178c18280052cb998d76533dfd1232','1.1','2026-03-26T05:34:43.188502','2026-03-26T05:34:43.188507','Vector Dataset','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('6a04e1e0-865e-4339-b91b-868f4cec4c44','\"Deepwater CTD - 00578552.bdo.nc - 24.81N, -94.21W - 1969-07-29\"','The Minerals Management Service (MMS) of the U. S. Department of the Interior funded the Deepwater Physical Oceanography Reanalysis and Synthesis of Historical Data Study in the Gulf of Mexico. MMS awarded the contract to the Texas A&M Research Foundation in July 1998. The basic study area is bounded by the shelf edge and the 25DGN latitude, which is the southern boundary; it extends from sea surface to sea floor. MMS has four objectives for the study. First is to create an inventory of physical oceanographic data and compile it into a single database on a CD-ROM. Second is to conduct analyses and interpretations of the physical oceanographic data to identify physical processes and phenomena. Third is to produce a climatology of the processes from available data and analyses and to prioritize the processes in terms of importance to improved understanding, simulation, and prediction of deepwater circulation. Fourth is to provide criteria and constraints useful in design of future field observations and numerical modeling efforts. Study results will provide MMS with information needed to direct its resources more efficiently and effectively in the review and assessment of potential environmental impacts of offshore oil and gas operations in the deepwater Gulf of Mexico.','public','2026-03-26T19:17:05.568757','2026-03-26T19:17:05.568764',NULL,NULL,NULL,'4dc4abea-fd33-44f6-b884-9de4a8d65ba0','ioos',NULL,NULL,'2026-03-26T19:17:05.568757','2026-03-26T19:17:05.568764',NULL,NULL,NULL,'noaa-gov'),('6a0d8864-cca7-4f3e-b220-bc994b05b909','EPA Facility Registry Service (FRS): ER_RMP','This web feature service contains location and facility identification information from EPA\'s Facility Registry System (FRS) for the subset of facilities that link to the Risk Management Plan (RMP) database. RMP stores the risk management plans reported by companies that handle, manufacture, use, or store certain flammable or toxic substances, as required under section 112(r) of the Clean Air Act (CAA). FRS identifies and geospatially locates facilities, sites or places subject to environmental regulations or of environmental interest. Using vigorous verification and data management procedures, FRS integrates facility data from EPA\'s national program systems, other federal agencies, and State and tribal master facility records and provides EPA with a centrally managed, single source of comprehensive and authoritative information on facilities. This data set contains the subset of FRS integrated facilities that link to RMP facilities once the RMP data has been integrated into the FRS database. Additional information on FRS is available at the EPA website https://www.epa.gov/enviro/facility-registry-service-frs. These data are considered sensitive and are restricted to internal use only. The download file and map service are accessible only on the EPA intranet. EPA Category: Mission Sensitive, NARA Category: Critical Infrastructure.','public','2026-03-27T15:37:49.276277','2026-03-31T16:39:57.292555',NULL,NULL,NULL,'392e3669-fbf6-406e-a189-6afc04dac60e','Environmental Dataset Gateway ISO Geospatial Metadata',NULL,NULL,'2026-03-27T15:37:49.276277','2026-03-31T16:39:57.292555',NULL,NULL,NULL,'epa-gov'),('6a2d856e-4684-4421-a798-5e7791876a89','IHW COMET IRFTAB EDITED REDUCED DATA RECORD CROMMELIN V1.0','In preparation for the concerted international study of Comet Halley, the IHW conducted a trial run with observations of Comet Crommelin, largely during February and March of 1984.','public','2026-03-13T18:59:02.759937','2026-03-13T18:59:02.759943','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','859b9f00-c6da-4155-a407-c64654b68239','NASA Data.json','cf028de98aee532fa945797af7a5ca13a4fa8f8381a95c8cfe9a45a637a8929b','1.1','2026-03-13T18:59:02.759937','2026-03-13T18:59:02.759943','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('6a496111-5ad6-4001-b695-d812a7a241f2','ROSETTA-ORBITER CHECK RPCMAG 2 CR4B RAW V9.0','This dataset contains EDITED RAW DATA (CODMAC LEVEL 2) of the Cruise 4-2phase, called CRUISE PHASE CR4B, of the ROSETTA orbiter magnetometer RPCMAG.Included are data from the Passive Checkout PC9 from January 31, 2009 untilFebruary 1, 2009.The current version of the dataset is V9.0.The difference to the datasets of earlier versions is mainly a significantlyimproved sensor temperature model, more detailed documentation about magneticdisturbance sources, more data handling information for the user andalso an improved quality flagging system.This applies mainly to CALIBRATED and RESAMPLED datasets. The RAW dataset,however, has been updated as well in order provide all datasets at thesame stage, although RAW data proper did not change.','public','2026-03-13T18:33:09.059540','2026-03-13T18:33:09.059545','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','49c807ff-33b5-452a-9dc4-4636d6a27615','NASA Data.json','77b6a2fcd2a5c1ac334a6c6194d754c2989cbf19656757edbfbe05bf50b73e98','1.1','2026-03-13T18:33:09.059540','2026-03-13T18:33:09.059545','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('6a68d779-ce20-42b5-80b4-da617ce50038','STARDUST NAVCAM RAW IMAGES OF ANNEFRANK - VERSION 3.0','This data set contains EDR (raw) pre-encounter and encounter images taken by the Stardust Navigation Camera of asteroid 5535 Annefrank. This is a new version of a subset of an existing data set, based on work done during the Stardust-NExT mission. The updated calibration from the Stardust-NExT mission was applied to these data in a separate data set (similar name: Level 3; RDR). Changes in the calibration of the NAVCAM instrument, between these prime mission data and those of the Stardust-NExT mission, are a possibility and are addressed in [KLAASENETAL2011B].','public','2026-03-13T17:11:04.386141','2026-03-13T17:11:04.386146','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','c408c7aa-e1c0-4852-aaee-3223f38c06b6','NASA Data.json','4893bd950c13699aa0530a13eace4216f312b185b94f58ecccb7f91612bbb58b','1.1','2026-03-13T17:11:04.386141','2026-03-13T17:11:04.386146','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('6a936166-309e-40b6-b333-b0a1410fc6ef','Fugro Cruise C16185 Line 1156, 75 kHz VMADCP','Program of vessel mount ADCP measurements comprising a combination of 300kHz and 75kHz ADCP data collected in the vicinity of the Loop Current and drilling blocks between 2004 and 2007.','public','2026-03-26T19:16:04.456659','2026-03-26T19:16:04.456665',NULL,NULL,NULL,'7055dfb3-8673-439b-b89b-19a10a48df40','ioos',NULL,NULL,'2026-03-26T19:16:04.456659','2026-03-26T19:16:04.456665',NULL,NULL,NULL,'noaa-gov'),('6a94daa7-9fc1-4259-b5c3-ef714b3eba49','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P NAVCAM 3 COMET ESCORT 1 MTP013 V1.0','This dataset contains ROSETTA NAVCAM RADIOMETRICALLY CALIBRATED DATA of the COMET ESCORT 1 MTP013 Phase from 11 Feb. 2015, 04:38:06 to 10 Mar. 2015, 23:22:54 when at the vicinity of target 67P/CG.','public','2026-03-13T19:31:27.647010','2026-03-13T19:31:27.647017','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','666cb4f0-2067-4017-83ed-c5e53df095bf','NASA Data.json','411a5ac9910b28335f6794e6625d06f8640936ad769184901fb337c978c028f5','1.1','2026-03-13T19:31:27.647010','2026-03-13T19:31:27.647017','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('6aa437a7-d311-432c-ba4d-3697c702d746','MARS EXPRESS MARS MARSIS EXPERIMENT DATA RECORD EXT 3 V1.0','This dataset contains the                    scientific telemetry produced by the MARSIS                    instrument after editing for duplicated and                    corrupted packets, together with geometric                    information computed on ground to locate                    observations in space and time. Both subsurface                    and ionosphere sounding data are included in                    the dataset.','public','2026-03-13T17:53:18.862909','2026-03-13T17:53:18.862918','planetary plasma interactions','Planetary Data System','026:00','5338afdc-31c9-4112-8b9e-cd241cb81758','NASA Data.json','cb60000b05c075ce79d79c73e5741aada08e642937de8c809b991e17de2d11e0','1.1','2026-03-13T17:53:18.862909','2026-03-13T17:53:18.862918','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('6ac0c175-88db-4057-ab7c-6342f2f7eb6c','Continuous Fixed Station Water Quality Measurements in Timucuan Ecological and Historic Preserve, July 2008 (Certified)','This dataset represents continuous water quality measurements that were taken at a fixed point in Timucuan Ecological and Historic Preserve during the month of July, 2008 as a part of the Fixed Station Water Quality Monitoring protocol that was developed by the Southeast Coast I&M Network (SECN). The measurements were taken by a YSI 6600 ESD Multi-Parameter Long Term Water Quality Monitoring Datasonde unit that serves as the standard fixed station water quality monitoring equipment for all similar operations conducted by the SECN. The following parameters were measured at 30 minute intervals during the time period that has been specified: Water Temperature, Specific Conductivity, Salinity, Dissolved Oxygen (DO), DO Concentration, Shallow Depth, pH Level, and Turbidity. Any anomalies noted regarding these parameters have also been noted in separate fields. Please note that these measurements have been certified by network personnel.','public','2026-03-26T05:29:52.110029','2026-03-26T05:29:52.110034','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','9fbe08a6-1cc0-4e4d-96b3-8bb020d3d277','DOI NPS DCAT-US','56be58321a9fbed67614abc217356e00a1ddf1b8a35da35cfceb85677f589053','1.1','2026-03-26T05:29:52.110029','2026-03-26T05:29:52.110034','Vector Dataset','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('6adfd26a-fd00-4d6e-9d32-b6c9cbdc0d79','Inyo Mountains Slender Salamander Predicted Habitat - CWHR A019 [ds3281]','<div style=\'text-align:Left;\'><div><div><p><span>CWHR Predicted Habitat Models represent areas of predicted suitable habitat for each species within its range. These models are built from the following principal inputs: </span></p><p><span>1) a statewide, best-available vegetation map (FVEG);  </span></p><p><span>2) GIS data representing a species’ range;  </span></p><p><span>3) the CWHR database of habitat suitability values for over 700 terrestrial vertebrate species. </span></p><p><span>Habitat suitability ranks of Low (non-zero values less than 0.34), Medium (0.34-0.66), and High (greater than 0.66) are based on the maximum suitability value across the 3 species life requisites: reproduction, feeding, and cover. Note that previous versions of these Predicted Habitat Models used an average across the 3 life requisites in order to obtain an overall suitability score for each habitat type and stage class.  Habitat suitability scores were developed based on habitat patch sizes greater than 40 acres in size and are best interpreted for habitat patches greater than 200 acres in size. The FVEG landcover dataset is an aggregation of multiple statewide landcover and regional vegetation mapping efforts, conducted at different points in time (approximately 1990 up to time of publishing) and at various resolutions, compiled by the California Department of Forestry and Fire Protection (CALFIRE). FVEG uses the most current and consistent data available for each region of the state. Decision rules were developed that controlled which layers were given priority in areas of overlap. Crosswalks were used to attribute the various data sources according to the CWHR habitat-type classification system. Attributing FVEG with CWHR habitat types allows for the extraction of areas with non-zero suitability values for each species within the bounds of its range, creating a series of maps of predicted suitable habitat which are species-specific. Because FVEG is an amalgam of disparate landcover assessment efforts across the state, the predictive power for determining suitable habitat will vary between species, and possibly even regionally for species which are widely distributed. While these maps represent CDFW’s best estimate of the presence of suitable habitat for any given species in the CWHR system, these maps are also limited by several factors: 1) the accuracy and resolution of vegetation maps in a given region; 2) the dynamic nature of the landscape in which fire and other disturbance events alter conditions at a greater frequency than mapping efforts can track; 3) the currency of expert knowledge, particularly as species adapt to changing land and climate conditions and the shifting of other species’ ranges; 4) the frequency of species-specific surveys across a representative sample of a species’ entire range; 5) metapopulation dynamics, which describes the shifting of populations within their environment as result of numerous types of interactions and responses. </span></p><p><span>CWHR GIS data representing predicted suitable habitat should not be used to indicate the presence or absence of a particular species at any specific site. CWHR predicted habitat models are named according to the 4-character alpha-numeric CWHR ID assigned to each species (5 characters in the case of subspecies or other sub-taxa). There is also a “CWHR Revision Tracking Table” containing a record for each species, its CWHR ID, scientific name, common name, and range and habitat model data revision history. CWHR species range models, predicted habitat models, and GIS data of the statewide distribution of all CWHR habitat types, along with the CWHR revision tracking table, are available for download at </span><a href=\'https://www.wildlife.ca.gov/Data/CWHR\' target=\'_blank\' style=\'text-decoration:underline;\' rel=\'nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer\'><span>https://www.wildlife.ca.gov/Data/CWHR</span></a><span>. </span></p></div></div></div>','public','2026-03-23T13:56:00.197069','2026-03-23T13:56:00.197075','California Department of Fish and Wildlife','BIOS_Admin',NULL,'2f481737-cb02-460f-b55e-a11c0251b112','State of California','4e5736ee43a4eb68d155f9036ae14af02b0792b9272c8da45e859fdc505b6299','1.1','2026-03-23T13:56:00.197069','2026-03-23T13:56:00.197075','Natural Resources',NULL,0,'ca-gov'),('6b33c69c-da59-486a-8ed3-28cd5a7a178f','MAGELLAN RADIO OCCULTATION RAW DATA RECORDS V2.0','The Magellan (MGN) Radio Occultation (ROCC) Raw Data Archive (RDA) is a time-ordered collection of raw and partially processed data from radio occultation experiments conducted using the Magellan spacecraft while it orbited Venus.','public','2026-03-13T19:30:23.829876','2026-03-13T19:30:23.829882','Planetary Atmospheres','Planetary Data System','026:00','3cd69548-14ea-4607-bab7-46ec3b6e8c72','NASA Data.json','0de2053309d2093d9048ca33d9d8423d6da5f486cdc126b68e75317a9a6ab232','1.1','2026-03-13T19:30:23.829876','2026-03-13T19:30:23.829882','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('6b3a479b-49c4-41bf-8d97-6b0c87fdbc12','Pacific Tailed Frog Predicted Habitat - CWHR A026 [ds1992]','<div style=\'text-align:Left;\'><div><div><p><span>CWHR Predicted Habitat Models represent areas of predicted suitable habitat for each species within its range. These models are built from the following principal inputs: </span></p><p><span>1) a statewide, best-available vegetation map (FVEG);  </span></p><p><span>2) GIS data representing a species’ range;  </span></p><p><span>3) the CWHR database of habitat suitability values for over 700 terrestrial vertebrate species. </span></p><p><span>Habitat suitability ranks of Low (non-zero values less than 0.34), Medium (0.34-0.66), and High (greater than 0.66) are based on the maximum suitability value across the 3 species life requisites: reproduction, feeding, and cover. Note that previous versions of these Predicted Habitat Models used an average across the 3 life requisites in order to obtain an overall suitability score for each habitat type and stage class.  Habitat suitability scores were developed based on habitat patch sizes greater than 40 acres in size and are best interpreted for habitat patches greater than 200 acres in size. The FVEG landcover dataset is an aggregation of multiple statewide landcover and regional vegetation mapping efforts, conducted at different points in time (approximately 1990 up to time of publishing) and at various resolutions, compiled by the California Department of Forestry and Fire Protection (CALFIRE). FVEG uses the most current and consistent data available for each region of the state. Decision rules were developed that controlled which layers were given priority in areas of overlap. Crosswalks were used to attribute the various data sources according to the CWHR habitat-type classification system. Attributing FVEG with CWHR habitat types allows for the extraction of areas with non-zero suitability values for each species within the bounds of its range, creating a series of maps of predicted suitable habitat which are species-specific. Because FVEG is an amalgam of disparate landcover assessment efforts across the state, the predictive power for determining suitable habitat will vary between species, and possibly even regionally for species which are widely distributed. While these maps represent CDFW’s best estimate of the presence of suitable habitat for any given species in the CWHR system, these maps are also limited by several factors: 1) the accuracy and resolution of vegetation maps in a given region; 2) the dynamic nature of the landscape in which fire and other disturbance events alter conditions at a greater frequency than mapping efforts can track; 3) the currency of expert knowledge, particularly as species adapt to changing land and climate conditions and the shifting of other species’ ranges; 4) the frequency of species-specific surveys across a representative sample of a species’ entire range; 5) metapopulation dynamics, which describes the shifting of populations within their environment as result of numerous types of interactions and responses. </span></p><p><span>CWHR GIS data representing predicted suitable habitat should not be used to indicate the presence or absence of a particular species at any specific site. CWHR predicted habitat models are named according to the 4-character alpha-numeric CWHR ID assigned to each species (5 characters in the case of subspecies or other sub-taxa). There is also a “CWHR Revision Tracking Table” containing a record for each species, its CWHR ID, scientific name, common name, and range and habitat model data revision history. CWHR species range models, predicted habitat models, and GIS data of the statewide distribution of all CWHR habitat types, along with the CWHR revision tracking table, are available for download at </span><a href=\'https://www.wildlife.ca.gov/Data/CWHR\' target=\'_blank\' style=\'text-decoration:underline;\' rel=\'nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer\'><span>https://www.wildlife.ca.gov/Data/CWHR</span></a><span>. </span></p></div></div></div>','public','2026-03-23T13:57:32.375089','2026-03-23T13:57:32.375094','California Department of Fish and Wildlife','BIOS_Admin',NULL,'7a1af65b-1fa0-46af-a8d4-28b5af301c9b','State of California','838ff496ad67b17b8afd36d185b40869afddd43ea1dbbdff430ad95b4809b491','1.1','2026-03-23T13:57:32.375089','2026-03-23T13:57:32.375094','Natural Resources',NULL,0,'ca-gov'),('6b4c6819-6228-4b15-9ac9-d2e2d494819d','2018-2019 All Road Network Of Linear Data (ARNOLD)','This is a data story about 2018-2019 All Road Network Of Linear Data (ARNOLD).','public','2026-03-20T11:41:47.457632','2026-03-20T11:41:47.457637','data.transportation.gov','FHWA-Datahub','021:15','bfd8c285-8f02-4578-8691-d80254bb7660','DOT Socrata Data.json','a96ed0fca508d7438e39e4c2e6a565aefb95a3a0728cd43ee0d318fb21ed4a2d','1.1','2026-03-20T11:41:47.457632','2026-03-20T11:41:47.457637','Roadways and Bridges','021:009',0,'dot-gov'),('6b5a100c-04cb-448a-bb6c-7c34552cae0c','Data from: Systematic Color Correction Pipeline for Controlled-Environment Imaging','<p dir=\"ltr\">Raw data set to evaluate a stepwise color correction (CC) pipeline for controlled imaging environments. The workflow integrates flat-field correction (FFC), gamma correction (GC), and white-balance correction (WB), followed by a color-mapping (CM) stage using machine-learning regression—linear, partial least squares (PLS), and neural networks (NN)—to deliver reliable CC in digital images. The pipeline reduces perceptual color differences in the corrected images. An NN with a second-degree polynomial expansion consistently outperformed other CM methods, yielding the lowest color errors and robust performance across varying imaging conditions.</p><p dir=\"ltr\">Tests showed that illumination quality and placement are critical: although the common 45° geometry produces favorable uncorrected images, top-mounted area lighting combined with FFC yielded the best corrected color. Imaging-environment materials also mattered; object background color and sidewalls affected fidelity, with diffusely reflective white performing best. Applied to various colored fruit samples, the proposed pipeline produced more consistent fruit colors across illuminants. An open-source Python package (https://github.com/collinswakholi/ColorCorrectionPackage) and an interactive user interface (https://github.com/collinswakholi/ColorCorrectionPackage_UI) implementing this pipeline is available, enabling reproducible analyses and straightforward adaptation to other controlled imaging tasks. Overall, the pipeline improved color reproduction and measurement in digital images and helped bridge the gap between sophisticated CC methods and practical, routine applications.</p>','public','2026-03-13T22:44:37.854291','2026-03-13T22:44:37.854297','Agricultural Research Service','Rippner, Devin, A.','005:18','61ab4ae7-7919-4a3e-a348-b66320baf380','USDA JSON','6eac63ff8196135b3dfc4496f0ea1d4dc6e0a429b08d2c6256f57c56a07d7257','1.1','2026-03-13T22:44:37.854291','2026-03-13T22:44:37.854297',NULL,'005:040',0,'usda-gov'),('6b6d5b1b-031e-44af-a786-1dd5cc5e54c7','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 3 1089 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 3 phase 2015-07-01 to 2015-10-21. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-10-08T20:46:30.000 to 2015-10-09T01:17:36.500.','public','2026-03-13T19:42:09.168683','2026-03-13T19:42:09.168689','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','97dd1a30-89b4-4ed1-ba5b-21faf72764b7','NASA Data.json','6c311cda9d2c96c11a26cc638ad2fe5a500b7e3e7ac5db560da7e64d602df42e','1.1','2026-03-13T19:42:09.168683','2026-03-13T19:42:09.168689','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('6b7ffa9a-1a0b-474e-b662-55ef85131d75','CASSINI RSS RAW DATA SET - SAGR15 V1.0','The Cassini Radio Science Saturn Gravity Science Experiment (SAGR15) Raw Data Archive is a time-ordered collection of radio science raw data acquired on January 17 and 19, 2013, during the Cassini Extended Extended Mission.','public','2026-03-13T19:05:25.033722','2026-03-13T19:05:25.033729','Planetary Atmospheres','Planetary Data System','026:00','4bbfd548-062b-4089-8730-e539e37be0bd','NASA Data.json','77ffee55e5adbce6de8461a6e73c3e514099cc8fd02c190d5cdafc370a570a07','1.1','2026-03-13T19:05:25.033722','2026-03-13T19:05:25.033729','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('6b916186-c445-405d-abe9-f4b66e68441b','2026 Open Data Annual Report','The introductory page of Maryland\'s Open Data Annual Report. It states our vision and mission.','public','2026-03-15T02:21:38.556088','2026-03-15T02:21:38.556092','opendata.maryland.gov','Helen Bai',NULL,'46f029b0-3498-44b5-b4eb-cf4aa74d6af0','md json','1215c697a3d774990217c6a45df538e4b65b8ca7aa84871dca83c2b36c20aefb','1.1','2026-03-15T02:21:38.556088','2026-03-15T02:21:38.556092',NULL,NULL,0,'state-of-maryland'),('6bb024bc-9f77-4b40-9b59-64f90d24930f','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 4 1162 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 4 phase 2015-10-22 to 2015-12-31. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-11-07T08:18:10.000 to 2015-11-07T12:29:07.000.','public','2026-03-13T19:36:37.618016','2026-03-13T19:36:37.618025','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','bd2189d1-92b6-4494-8fe4-74666040d763','NASA Data.json','044b0965512b1c4672dafa09800b1640a4eadff224724f01b7d7b2e107b8ab6b','1.1','2026-03-13T19:36:37.618016','2026-03-13T19:36:37.618025','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('6bbe1efd-2f1f-45c0-8e22-76808a55e2c2','Fugro Cruise C16295 Line 0324, 75 kHz VMADCP','Program of vessel mount ADCP measurements comprising a combination of 300kHz and 75kHz ADCP data collected in the vicinity of the Loop Current and drilling blocks between 2004 and 2007.','public','2026-03-26T19:16:05.349241','2026-03-26T19:16:05.349247',NULL,NULL,NULL,'de26d9b4-db14-44d3-9585-cde30c8355e0','ioos',NULL,NULL,'2026-03-26T19:16:05.349241','2026-03-26T19:16:05.349247',NULL,NULL,NULL,'noaa-gov'),('6bbea508-4f37-4487-8e77-506bafb0998a','Southern California Slender Salamander Predicted Habitat - CWHR A013 [ds1980]','<div style=\'text-align:Left;\'><div><div><p><span>CWHR Predicted Habitat Models represent areas of predicted suitable habitat for each species within its range. These models are built from the following principal inputs: </span></p><p><span>1) a statewide, best-available vegetation map (FVEG);  </span></p><p><span>2) GIS data representing a species’ range;  </span></p><p><span>3) the CWHR database of habitat suitability values for over 700 terrestrial vertebrate species. </span></p><p><span>Habitat suitability ranks of Low (non-zero values less than 0.34), Medium (0.34-0.66), and High (greater than 0.66) are based on the maximum suitability value across the 3 species life requisites: reproduction, feeding, and cover. Note that previous versions of these Predicted Habitat Models used an average across the 3 life requisites in order to obtain an overall suitability score for each habitat type and stage class.  Habitat suitability scores were developed based on habitat patch sizes greater than 40 acres in size and are best interpreted for habitat patches greater than 200 acres in size. The FVEG landcover dataset is an aggregation of multiple statewide landcover and regional vegetation mapping efforts, conducted at different points in time (approximately 1990 up to time of publishing) and at various resolutions, compiled by the California Department of Forestry and Fire Protection (CALFIRE). FVEG uses the most current and consistent data available for each region of the state. Decision rules were developed that controlled which layers were given priority in areas of overlap. Crosswalks were used to attribute the various data sources according to the CWHR habitat-type classification system. Attributing FVEG with CWHR habitat types allows for the extraction of areas with non-zero suitability values for each species within the bounds of its range, creating a series of maps of predicted suitable habitat which are species-specific. Because FVEG is an amalgam of disparate landcover assessment efforts across the state, the predictive power for determining suitable habitat will vary between species, and possibly even regionally for species which are widely distributed. While these maps represent CDFW’s best estimate of the presence of suitable habitat for any given species in the CWHR system, these maps are also limited by several factors: 1) the accuracy and resolution of vegetation maps in a given region; 2) the dynamic nature of the landscape in which fire and other disturbance events alter conditions at a greater frequency than mapping efforts can track; 3) the currency of expert knowledge, particularly as species adapt to changing land and climate conditions and the shifting of other species’ ranges; 4) the frequency of species-specific surveys across a representative sample of a species’ entire range; 5) metapopulation dynamics, which describes the shifting of populations within their environment as result of numerous types of interactions and responses. </span></p><p><span>CWHR GIS data representing predicted suitable habitat should not be used to indicate the presence or absence of a particular species at any specific site. CWHR predicted habitat models are named according to the 4-character alpha-numeric CWHR ID assigned to each species (5 characters in the case of subspecies or other sub-taxa). There is also a “CWHR Revision Tracking Table” containing a record for each species, its CWHR ID, scientific name, common name, and range and habitat model data revision history. CWHR species range models, predicted habitat models, and GIS data of the statewide distribution of all CWHR habitat types, along with the CWHR revision tracking table, are available for download at </span><a href=\'https://www.wildlife.ca.gov/Data/CWHR\' target=\'_blank\' style=\'text-decoration:underline;\' rel=\'nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer\'><span>https://www.wildlife.ca.gov/Data/CWHR</span></a><span>. </span></p></div></div></div>','public','2026-03-23T13:59:35.890882','2026-03-23T13:59:35.890889','California Department of Fish and Wildlife','BIOS_Admin',NULL,'6372dd6a-037a-4f82-afac-e7624550559e','State of California','1fefb93ddd9fc59d535eb0949f6f7e40ac67fa1961a4e26e70d4223a81db6c27','1.1','2026-03-23T13:59:35.890882','2026-03-23T13:59:35.890889','Natural Resources',NULL,0,'ca-gov'),('6bc47fe1-1d94-4f4c-b99b-bac381f32d0e','MARS EXPRESS MARS MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 8 4191 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2021-01-01 to 2022-12-31. It is a Occultation measurement and covers the time 2021-02-11T07:34:57.000 to 2021-02-11T07:57:05.349.','public','2026-03-13T18:08:13.443678','2026-03-13T18:08:13.443685','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','2efea764-1376-4d91-81a4-331ff3049c7c','NASA Data.json','42457a596678d00f61622a30d0f6fc742e3ed4595514f914c0dab89046a7d9cd','1.1','2026-03-13T18:08:13.443678','2026-03-13T18:08:13.443685','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('6c1e17ca-cc13-4d0f-aff0-257876927ee5','MESSENGER E/V/H GRNS 3 GAMMA RAY SPECTROMETER CALIBDATA V1.0','Abstract : This data set consists of the MESSENGER GRS calibrated observations (CDRs) and the reduced data product (RDR). The GRS experiment is a gamma ray spectrometer designed to observe spectra of gamma rays emitted from Mercury\'s surface in the energy range from 0.1 to 10 MeV. There are seven basic GRS CDR data products: the Ge raw spectra data (GRS_CAL_RAW), the anti-coincidence spectra data (GRS_CAL_AC), the shield spectra data (GRS_CAL_SH, GRS_CAL_SH2, GRS_CAL_SH3), the shield count rate (GRS_CAL_SCR) and the engineering data (GRS_ENG). There is one GRS RDR product (GRS_RDR_SUM), a spectral sum of the GRS_CAL_RAW and GRS_CAL_AC spectra.','public','2026-03-13T18:33:15.739188','2026-03-13T18:33:15.739195','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','fa6afa9d-cc14-459f-8d71-448d1e4c7a1e','NASA Data.json','9514552911a330893f1a2f462083698fc2c0ccbe40b84210c4c18e8335eb9a22','1.1','2026-03-13T18:33:15.739188','2026-03-13T18:33:15.739195','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('6c46eef8-be18-483c-a6a8-f412d2e4cda1','DID(IT) - Investigations Division Case Management System','IDCMS is a case management system that supports evaluating and conducting investigations pertaining to allegations of USCIS employee or contractor misconduct. IDCMS also supports the management inquiry process. Some of its capabilities include case tracking, case reporting, case correspondence management, management inquiry tracking, management report of action tracking and knowledge management to respond to customer service queries.','non-public','2026-03-22T11:56:44.042269','2026-03-22T11:56:44.042274','Unspecified','Open Data (MGMT)','024:030','ab0fac2f-44a8-4934-b198-ddda9b216519','DHS datajson source','3d8d650554f7a596f36663e2461b435815e34e36ef9371f6a25ebc8151906532','1.1','2026-03-22T11:56:44.042269','2026-03-22T11:56:44.042274',NULL,'024:000',0,'dhs-gov'),('6c479b4a-b587-45a3-99ba-de27f46a7b59','ROSETTA-ORBITER SW RPCLAP 3RVM1 CALIB2 V1.0','This data set containsCALIBRATED data from Rosetta RPC-LAP, acquired during the RENDEZVOUSMANOEUVRE 1 mission phase where the primary target was the SOLAR WIND.It contains instrument outputs in volts and amperes, calibrated andcorrected for instrument offsets.','public','2026-03-13T18:10:50.764660','2026-03-13T18:10:50.764665','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','3ccf6bb2-c722-4692-acc6-f7ccab9b7294','NASA Data.json','4e69611d1a56bd05086978b2ad30a1e69950553288411deafc9b39addcf89b58','1.1','2026-03-13T18:10:50.764660','2026-03-13T18:10:50.764665','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('6c588e2c-e7a5-47ab-8c39-3778582e01d1','MRO MARS CRISM 4 TYPE SPECTRA  LIBRARY V1.0','This dataset includes spectral  data from type spectra of phases identified using the CRISM  (Compact Reconnaissance Imaging Spectrometer for Mars)  instrument on MRO. Type locations for the diversity of  currently identified mineral spectral signatures have been  compiled into this library of spectra. The type spectra  assembled into the MICA library represent the results of over  seven years of measurements from CRISM of the surface of Mars and represent the compilation of many researchers\' efforts.','public','2026-03-13T18:19:15.874429','2026-03-13T18:19:15.874433','Small Bodies','Tess Jaffe','026:00','c81a99ce-4f1c-4135-a989-51bfaf1918ee','NASA Data.json','b9d43e93f9bbe603a7c95bbec23b058b2a639cc2e04d769e73bff17b0b664ee9','1.1','2026-03-13T18:19:15.874429','2026-03-13T18:19:15.874433','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('6c82b998-591c-49fe-b076-ba0a1024db1f','American Peregrine Falcon Range - CWHR B129a [ds3283]','<div style=\'text-align:Left;\'><div><div><p style=\'margin:0 0 14 0;\'><span><span>Vector datasets of CWHR range maps are one component of California Wildlife Habitat Relationships (CWHR), a comprehensive information system and predictive model for California\'s wildlife. The CWHR System was developed to support habitat conservation and management, land use planning, impact assessment, education, and research involving terrestrial vertebrates in California. CWHR contains information on life history, management status, geographic distribution, and habitat relationships for wildlife species known to occur regularly in California. Range maps represent the maximum, current geographic extent of each species within California. They were originally delineated at a scale of 1:5,000,000 by species-level experts and have gradually been revised at a scale of 1:1,000,000. For more information about CWHR, visit the CWHR webpage (</span><a href=\'https://www.wildlife.ca.gov/Data/CWHR\' style=\'text-decoration:underline;\' rel=\'nofollow ugc\'><span>https://www.wildlife.ca.gov/Data/CWHR</span></a><span>). The webpage provides links to download CWHR data and user documents such as a look up table of available range maps including species code, species name, and range map revision history; a full set of CWHR GIS data; .pdf files of each range map or species life history accounts; and a User Guide.</span></span></p></div></div></div>','public','2026-03-23T13:53:25.110637','2026-03-23T13:53:25.110642','California Department of Fish and Wildlife','BIOS_Admin',NULL,'a30d9a85-2fdd-41e8-87bc-dae9ae025ccb','State of California','b7d2f3f9a83fdba1e1065c3ac84ea08e03672c5269f1e9775f55ca53c20340be','1.1','2026-03-23T13:53:25.110637','2026-03-23T13:53:25.110642','Natural Resources',NULL,0,'ca-gov'),('6c8bbe98-416b-4b4e-bd27-388b4d979570','NRC 826','NRC Health Center Agreement to Participate in NRC Wellness Program. Fillable form in Adobe Portable Document Format (PDF) with information submitted by NRC stakeholder - licensee, applicant, or NRC employee/contractor.','non-public','2026-03-20T19:43:36.493109','2026-03-20T19:43:36.493114','Nuclear Regulatory Commission','Ilka Solorio','429:00','e10c2ac7-4ace-459e-839a-ae98ff0deac4','NRC Data.json Harvest Source','a99193b50ab3b9558dba5fd8433d4051d5fc019dc46069221e2c99ddbf3bff85','1.1','2026-03-20T19:43:36.493109','2026-03-20T19:43:36.493114',NULL,'000:000',0,'nrc-gov'),('6cbd65af-8801-40ae-981b-64d87ffdead7','MARS EXPRESS SUN MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 7 4056 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2019-01-01 to 2020-12-31. It is a Solar Conjunction measurement and covers the time 2019-09-13T01:41:24.000 to 2019-09-13T04:12:45.500.','public','2026-03-13T18:37:37.647394','2026-03-13T18:37:37.647399','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','8d43d576-db48-4b28-8633-e33223ccb40b','NASA Data.json','61be3d48b5daf2164fe5b35d92d91ea849fc5cbf35bdb42c1e83c6e3e525356b','1.1','2026-03-13T18:37:37.647394','2026-03-13T18:37:37.647399','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('6cec5fc9-8891-4988-abfc-63f147c8e0d0','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSINAC 4 EXT2-MTP028 RDR-STR-REFL V1.0','This CODMAC level 4 data set contains solar stray light corrected, radiometric calibrated and geometric distortion corrected (resampled) image data in in reflectance units (normalized and thus without unit), acquired by the OSIRIS Narrow Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft during the ROSETTA EXTENSION 2 mission phase, covering the period from 2016-04-05T23:25:00.000 to 2016-05-03T23:25:00.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V1.0 is the first version of this dataset: Lien corrected dataset after October 2018 PSA/PDS external peer review.','public','2026-03-13T19:31:12.285221','2026-03-13T19:31:12.285227','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','49599ed7-6e99-45d3-ae7b-a8b2a8ef6951','NASA Data.json','166b81d65afbb0549fef1ad371b6036f1a51ae1c880e56869e80dcbc0cc22140','1.1','2026-03-13T19:31:12.285221','2026-03-13T19:31:12.285227','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('6d280008-e9cc-4e31-a8de-531d0af8b8a5','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 PRELANDING 0292 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the PRELANDING phase 2014-01-21 to 2014-11-18. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2014-09-13T22:12:03.000 to 2014-09-14T01:25:11.000.','public','2026-03-13T19:50:43.244741','2026-03-13T19:50:43.244746','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','e2fe7da8-bd5c-4313-9abc-599e02782938','NASA Data.json','148b2dda9c1b608482eb12194c3928448148e7ad02399dc2973adc4021d9289b','1.1','2026-03-13T19:50:43.244741','2026-03-13T19:50:43.244746','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('6d3f0996-1a2b-4827-93c1-7330a224e06d','EPOXI C/ISON (2012 S1) - MRI RAW IMAGES V1.0','This dataset contains raw clear-filter, CN, OH and dust continuum images of comet C/ISON (2012 S1) acquired by the Medium Resolution Visible CCD (MRI) from 17 January through 06 March 2013 during the Cruise 3 phase of the EPOXI mission.','public','2026-03-13T18:02:46.006738','2026-03-13T18:02:46.006742','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','5de6ae72-86e4-4c11-bb32-7042ca9ae2f7','NASA Data.json','adfb64551e0f93e3b0a4341d630e812189b126113ea0beeac50c29d68c48f3a3','1.1','2026-03-13T18:02:46.006738','2026-03-13T18:02:46.006742','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('6d76c886-f392-4278-bcae-4ae92ea69c0e','MARS EXPRESS MARS MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 5 3858 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2015-01-01 to 2016-12-31. It is a Occultation measurement and covers the time 2016-11-14T06:30:00 to 2016-11-14T11:54:39.500.','public','2026-03-13T17:39:25.548689','2026-03-13T17:39:25.548695','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','3e851ae2-3206-4588-b170-73c75fb82911','NASA Data.json','75b36f5aa7f929a81c3d88c50c833181a59765096aaf448072992845bb079806','1.1','2026-03-13T17:39:25.548689','2026-03-13T17:39:25.548695','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('6d81942e-3b88-4572-9650-d9279533cc48','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P SREM 2 ESCORT 4 MTP022 V1.0','This data set contains count rates (1/s) as measured by the Standard Radiation Environment Monitor (SREM) instrument on the Rosetta spacecraft, along with their standard deviations. The primary target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko. These are CODMAC Level 2 Experiment Data Record data, and provide a measure of the radiation in the spacecraft environment during the Medium Term Plan 22 period of the ESCORT 4 mission phase.','public','2026-03-13T19:41:18.437425','2026-03-13T19:41:18.437431','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','20adc9f1-adc1-4d65-9573-a651b68ba54a','NASA Data.json','997f93538f266828b971a11c2236ef4b62a5351a5338304a6390da1ae80f30b4','1.1','2026-03-13T19:41:18.437425','2026-03-13T19:41:18.437431','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('6de8b3be-4e6d-423e-81d5-cde1d4b6c5f1','FTB EITC Summary of CA Residents Year Comparison Jan 2026','Produced by the Economic & Statistical Research Bureau, monthly tabulations of tax filings statistics for the Earned Income Tax Credit (EITC), Young Child Tax Credit (YCTC) and Foster Youth Tax Credit (FYTC) provide credit use by county, preparer type, credit amount allowed number of dependents and a many other useful cross-sections.','public','2026-03-23T13:57:13.773717','2026-03-23T13:57:13.773722','California Franchise Tax Board','FTB Open Data',NULL,'ff6c5223-da9c-4857-89a8-bf8f7d09968b','State of California','3bba8d5ec52c6215f40e7082eedb214cb09e26d77c5ddcb4482db1c0d1022751','1.1','2026-03-23T13:57:13.773717','2026-03-23T13:57:13.773722','Economy and Demographics',NULL,0,'ca-gov'),('6e1b3b32-1ee5-47c9-8909-0c205427f23e','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSINAC 4 PRL-MTP001 RDR-REFLECT V1.0','This CODMAC level 4 data set contains radiometric calibrated and geometric distortion corrected (resampled) image data in reflectance units (normalized and thus without unit), acquired by the OSIRIS Narrow Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft during the PRELANDING mission phase, covering the period from 2014-01-20T10:00:00.000 to 2014-05-07T12:47:59.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V1.0 is the first version of this dataset: Lien corrected dataset after October 2018 PSA/PDS external peer review.','public','2026-03-13T17:15:05.078994','2026-03-13T17:15:05.079000','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','eacf5dd3-5ec5-43a2-b0f3-3b510ce5439b','NASA Data.json','cbb4b518bc51028df891a8c5f833ccd44230bd54bb7c8496880fa039566a4db8','1.1','2026-03-13T17:15:05.078994','2026-03-13T17:15:05.079000','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('6e5a163a-5dd6-4298-96e5-bc470fe3df3c','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSINAC 4 PRL-MTP005 RDR-STR-REFL V1.0','This CODMAC level 4 data set contains solar stray light corrected, radiometric calibrated and geometric distortion corrected (resampled) image data in in reflectance units (normalized and thus without unit), acquired by the OSIRIS Narrow Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft during the PRELANDING mission phase, covering the period from 2014-07-02T08:35:00.000 to 2014-08-01T09:59:59.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V1.0 is the first version of this dataset: Lien corrected dataset after October 2018 PSA/PDS external peer review.','public','2026-03-13T18:47:59.864200','2026-03-13T18:47:59.864205','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','5599a09f-432c-46d4-829c-4055b8ed5387','NASA Data.json','450abe8409e90186188a1f3f5b2cc625ed95811ae9758ff09016e313ccfdd6f6','1.1','2026-03-13T18:47:59.864200','2026-03-13T18:47:59.864205','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('6e69878c-c661-4ce5-b097-d4ed47f01229','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 3 0874 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 3 phase 2015-07-01 to 2015-10-21. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-07-03T21:08:05.000 to 2015-07-04T00:18:16.000.','public','2026-03-13T17:23:12.913395','2026-03-13T17:23:12.913401','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','0032990f-b54e-4ea1-b440-e9a2d6782992','NASA Data.json','242120b5318e689a0efd59ebd47f8584a8635c07f85d8eea89f38c98666158ef','1.1','2026-03-13T17:23:12.913395','2026-03-13T17:23:12.913401','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('6e7f39da-7960-4c13-89c5-1bf9dffb7f93','ROSETTA-ORBITER LUTETIA/CAL NAVCAM 2 LUTETIA FLY-BY V1.1','This dataset contains RAW DATA of the LUTETIA flyby Phase from 30 May 2010 until 10 July 2010. The closest approach (CA) took place on 10 July 2010 at 15:45. This data set V1.1 supersedes the V1.0. It includes updates of the Browse images, adding of the FITS version, clarification of calibration target, document updates and resolve other minor outstanding errata.','public','2026-03-13T17:45:39.010737','2026-03-13T17:45:39.010743','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','c714b5e0-5aa5-41ba-8c11-5be34a9f6d50','NASA Data.json','ba74e9afd440b6a3a632992b4c0a0af37d0db0ebbede79314a7f29ee6598e8da','1.1','2026-03-13T17:45:39.010737','2026-03-13T17:45:39.010743','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('6e964cea-2b9e-4420-8611-22216fd6e65f','ODYSSEY THEMIS VIS ABR V1.0','The THEMIS VIS-ABR data set contains the apparent brightness records, derived from the calibrated visible observations. Each image header includes basic parameters describing the observation and geometric parameters for the center of the observation.','public','2026-03-13T19:31:59.850987','2026-03-13T19:31:59.850993','Imaging','Planetary Data System','026:00','70a0483b-24fd-441f-8c5a-4abc8fd8be9f','NASA Data.json','a90f188e54446266ed8a94a0b9c072078ea560904aa6b0a05eeefa10dab6f360','1.1','2026-03-13T19:31:59.850987','2026-03-13T19:31:59.850993','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('6eb63f23-3a4b-4181-8926-6b254ea0d74d','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P SREM 2 EXTENSION 2 MTP029 V1.0','This data set contains count rates (1/s) as measured by the Standard Radiation Environment Monitor (SREM) instrument on the Rosetta spacecraft, along with their standard deviations. The primary target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko. These are CODMAC Level 2 Experiment Data Record data, and provide a measure of the radiation in the spacecraft environment during the Medium Term Plan 29 period of the EXTENSION 2 mission phase.','public','2026-03-13T17:46:53.665764','2026-03-13T17:46:53.665769','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','4e2e6a71-9a63-435d-a2c6-369c46f40ccc','NASA Data.json','27db39930903c2b0d1009603baa84d96fc9cdebf428c920eb7e91c030694363e','1.1','2026-03-13T17:46:53.665764','2026-03-13T17:46:53.665769','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('6ed1cf7c-24c7-442d-9834-8c6f149e9169','Hydrographic and Impairment Statistics Database: NPS-WSR Missisquoi & Trout Wild and Scenic River','Hydrographic and Impairment Statistics (HIS) is a National Park Service (NPS) Water Resources Division (WRD) project established to track certain goals created in response to the Government Performance and Results Act of 1993 (GPRA). One water resources management goal established by the Department of the Interior under GRPA requires NPS to track the percent of its managed surface waters that are meeting Clean Water Act (CWA) water quality standards. This goal requires an accurate inventory that spatially quantifies the surface water hydrography that each bureau manages and a procedure to determine and track which waterbodies are or are not meeting water quality standards as outlined by Section 303(d) of the CWA. This project helps meet this DOI GRPA goal by inventorying and monitoring in a geographic information system for the NPS: (1) CWA 303(d) quality impaired waters and causes; and (2) hydrographic statistics based on the United States Geological Survey (USGS) National Hydrography Dataset (NHD). Hydrographic and 303(d) impairment statistics were evaluated based on a combination of 1:24,000 (NHD) and finer scale data (frequently provided by state GIS layers).','public','2026-03-29T06:05:52.326169','2026-03-29T06:05:52.326175','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','11308ca5-a401-4e7d-baab-f7d223443e8f','DOI NPS DCAT-US','c5e2a71c42406dea6b04869e55bd8a2a449f858c75347a0db5bdf3bdd18b199c','1.1','2026-03-29T06:05:52.326169','2026-03-29T06:05:52.326175','geospatial','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('6ee6b60c-8481-421e-9da7-e757aa613819','MGS SOLAR CONJUNCTION RAW                                      DATA SET - ROCC V1.0','The Mars Global Surveyor (MGS) Solar Conjunction Raw Data Archive is a time-ordered collection of raw data acquired during the Solar Conjunction in 2000, while MGS was  in its Mars Mapping (MAP) mission phase.','public','2026-03-13T18:50:25.673375','2026-03-13T18:50:25.673380','planetary plasma interactions','Planetary Data System','026:00','94c57fa7-16d9-4fbe-a15d-919ffe0850ef','NASA Data.json','00ef03696636e15e441ea793622768f05fec79f1442bc85e91f2de789e10b4b7','1.1','2026-03-13T18:50:25.673375','2026-03-13T18:50:25.673380','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('6f1ba6db-c2e8-41e1-b5d7-f1c3ea15f33d','MARS EXPRESS MARS MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 5 3854 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2015-01-01 to 2016-12-31. It is a Occultation measurement and covers the time 2016-11-08T01:27:01 to 2016-11-08T02:09:00.','public','2026-03-13T22:43:09.860580','2026-03-13T22:43:09.860588','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','8617d3fb-12c3-4f9f-a30e-f249edb9d150','NASA Data.json','166341dfc9df3f2d027ce389fd0052d59fc4a39a84a1365a93ead9372d73347b','1.1','2026-03-13T22:43:09.860580','2026-03-13T22:43:09.860588','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('6f33edad-c138-4b0f-aee5-4feaf98ec0e7','FIRST - Freedom of Information Records System','The Freedom of Information Record System (FIRST) supports the processing of FOIA/PA requests from the public.  It is used to scan and capture electronic copies of FOIA/PA request and response documents; create and manage cases based on requests; transfer requests to other USCIS units or other government agencies; locate, review, redact, and process requested documents or records for disclosure; create standard correspondence letters to the requestors; process payments; print final action letters and redacted responsive records.  FIRST users are located within the National Records Center, where requests under the FOIA/PA are processed.','non-public','2026-03-22T11:51:40.604051','2026-03-22T11:51:40.604058','Unspecified','Open Data (MGMT)','024:030','d9af0cf4-0bf9-4b66-a0ce-95b32dbe34fd','DHS datajson source','09f2fa0188da8f33e486ef22c3f00847a49fe8016986f3189eae85f3f4c420d2','1.1','2026-03-22T11:51:40.604051','2026-03-22T11:51:40.604058',NULL,'024:000',0,'dhs-gov'),('6f3c3090-f9d0-4aff-bf27-8a707a6f20e7','CASSINI RSS RAW DATA SET - RHGR1 V1.0','The Cassini Radio Science Rhea Gravity Experiment (RHGR1) Raw Data Archive is a time-ordered collection of radio science raw data acquired on November 25, 26, 27, 2005 during the Tour subphase of the Cassini mission.','public','2026-03-13T18:07:19.432920','2026-03-13T18:07:19.432926','Planetary Atmospheres','Planetary Data System','026:00','672af8ec-bd61-40ae-a9fb-c065f1b12a40','NASA Data.json','005a2832cb1e8e1690bdec68d3398818755b7dd102a1f8acea2538a6acee5840','1.1','2026-03-13T18:07:19.432920','2026-03-13T18:07:19.432926','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('6f512858-da3a-47c2-acb9-5c44005e38b1','ARECIBO/NRAO MOON RTLS/GBT 5 12.6CM V1.0','Radar backscatter power from the lunar surface was collected at a wavelength of 12.6 cm, using the 305 m Radio Telescope at Arecibo to transmit and the NRAO\'s 105 m Robert C. Byrd Green Bank Telescope to receive.','public','2026-03-13T19:14:15.623742','2026-03-13T19:14:15.623751','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','d2b48a21-4bc1-4b5e-b02f-0bb91a3ff8bd','NASA Data.json','2880acb9cd61b60b204995896835f8e2a6ce99d222fb4fdd70850cdde401c6c1','1.1','2026-03-13T19:14:15.623742','2026-03-13T19:14:15.623751','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('6f75fb8c-d0d5-4637-b18e-32643932422c','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P MIDAS 3 EXT3 SAMPLES V2.0','The Micro-Imaging Dust Analysis System (MIDAS) is an instrument on theROSETTA Orbiter that will provide 3D images and statistical parametersof pristine cometary particles, collected in the vicinity of comet67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko. This data set includes all data from theROSETTA EXTENSION 3 mission phase.The current release is based on the results of the Comet ScienceReviews held in Feb 2016 and Oct 2017 and supersedes version 1.0.','public','2026-03-13T17:00:47.417569','2026-03-13T17:00:47.417575','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','4429ae72-e1d5-41d6-80f7-4136d0ca8274','NASA Data.json','a6ec5737d872f1f922e0dcff213b6f2e26175f121d234dcccc37cb32151e080b','1.1','2026-03-13T17:00:47.417569','2026-03-13T17:00:47.417575','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('6f9cc1f7-cd31-42a4-afc3-22f0518b49cc','EGIS - Enterprise Gateway Integration Services-Refugee Asylum Support Services (RASS)','RASS interfaces with DoS WRAPS, CBP/NCTC and USCIS CAMINO allows for a more efficient refugee application request intake through the automation of an Interagency Check (IAC) request data process  and granting case adjudications will be performed by USCIS immigrations officers using the CAMINO application. ','non-public','2026-03-22T11:56:00.815342','2026-03-22T11:56:00.815349','Unspecified','Open Data (MGMT)','024:030','7d94dc3d-83cc-43a1-aa9d-ad498770cace','DHS datajson source','2fdf899fe8516a009e53ef1f0fb4e8b7619bddb9cff2b7f4570069d1c5c224b5','1.1','2026-03-22T11:56:00.815342','2026-03-22T11:56:00.815349',NULL,'024:000',0,'dhs-gov'),('6fbeadb4-e155-4b91-a91c-376f2ce80e3e','Fatality, Injury, and Illness Map (4.07)','This is the report for Fatality, Injury, and Illness Map (4.07).','public','2026-03-25T12:36:54.073357','2026-03-26T12:43:36.109317','Federal Railroad Administration','FRA Safety Data Team','021:27','9764625e-94d1-4918-a599-1c59eba863d8','DOT Socrata Data.json','946fc6bf6427eb585d803ce54e4aa771b9dac521419bb6289d448917f0d73ff4','1.1','2026-03-25T12:36:54.073357','2026-03-26T12:43:36.109317','Railroads','021:037',0,'dot-gov'),('6fcc6b8e-100e-4543-9dbb-8218f1fba846','Highway Revenue Forecasting Model','This is a Highway Revenue Forecasting Model.','public','2026-03-28T13:33:01.668823','2026-03-28T13:33:01.668829','Federal Highway Administration','Viktoriia Dunleavy','021:15','b81ba3ee-a254-4220-9cd8-a0311312a2b6','DOT Socrata Data.json','32c17262543406d11b5c788b2253f3f6a2e4816695e450f5bdb7d6fc2a54e901','1.1','2026-03-28T13:33:01.668823','2026-03-28T13:33:01.668829','Roadways and Bridges','021:009',0,'dot-gov'),('700e4624-c1f0-4a6e-8ef6-4a8733c33e0b','NEAR SPICE KERNELS V1.0','This data set includes the complete set of NEAR SPICE data files (``kernel files\'\'), which can be accessed using SPICE software. The SPICE data contain geometric and other ancillary information needed to recover the full value of science instrument data. In particular SPICE kernels provide spacecraft and planetary ephemerides, instrument mounting alignments, spacecraft orientation, and data needed for relevant time conversions.','public','2026-03-13T19:20:52.474138','2026-03-13T19:20:52.474143','Navigation and Ancillary Information Facility','Planetary Data System','026:00','b2882c30-0794-4ade-b10f-c0c6723204bf','NASA Data.json','1e2677db18f83e3563712dae62e7e200b5844e6159501a7cb19c5b83e98b186e','1.1','2026-03-13T19:20:52.474138','2026-03-13T19:20:52.474143','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('705ea969-97a2-49d1-ac97-5191a7c4854a','ROSETTA-ORBITER CHECK MIDAS 3 EAR1 PC0 V1.0','The Micro-Imaging Dust Analysis System (MIDAS) is an instrument on the ROSETTA Orbiter that will provide 3D images and statistical parameters of pristine cometary particles hitting the detector. This data set includes all data from the EARTH SWING-BY 1 mission phase.','public','2026-03-13T18:44:09.660292','2026-03-13T18:44:09.660297','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','cdf14852-9ed0-4909-a604-9df516e4352d','NASA Data.json','3fc8f8a6b45cff738e552631aa40dfad7c73ad1f119b1a682fccf20e2797cb7e','1.1','2026-03-13T18:44:09.660292','2026-03-13T18:44:09.660297','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('7079982a-a11b-4bb0-9b81-e0d5e6dca916','MRO CRISM TARGETED EMPIRICAL RECORD V1.0','This volume contains the CRISM Targeted Empirical Record (TER) archive, a collection of multiband image cubes derived from targeted (gimbaled) observations of Mars\' surface acquired by the Compact Reconnaissance Imaging Spectrometer for Mars (CRISM) instrument on the Mars Reconnaissance Orbiter (MRO) spacecraft. Post-processing attempts to represent the spectrum the instrument would have measured looking at the surface of Mars at a standard illumination geometry, in the absence of atmospheric gases, with aerosol scattering normalized to that at the geometry within the observation that is closest to nadir, in the absence of instrument artifacts. A series of value added products represent spatial variability in signatures of minerals of interest. The data are still in sensor space, allowing map projection using terrain models of the Martian surface that are of better accuracy or spatial resolution than was used to generate the companion Map-projected Targeted Reduced Data Record (MTR) archive.','public','2026-03-13T17:19:59.673161','2026-03-13T17:19:59.673169','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','3a1e7aff-3862-4ba6-b662-8cf9faa5828b','NASA Data.json','b9f780179a01468cbc1df9695c4e54afd2d3a6eb3e3eabccbc2588417a569b05','1.1','2026-03-13T17:19:59.673161','2026-03-13T17:19:59.673169','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('70ba4d0b-36fa-4258-bf22-4c529786cfd2','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RPCMIP 3 PRL2 V2.0','This archive contains data from the RPC-MIP instrument onboard ROSETTA Orbiter, acquired during the prelanding part 2 phase at the vicinity of the comet 67P/CG. It also contains documentation which describes the MIP experiment. This is V2.0 updated after Science Review.','public','2026-03-13T17:22:42.168542','2026-03-13T17:22:42.168549','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','2b6c5416-81bc-4927-bee3-8927c683c677','NASA Data.json','d2a4d47e6939e98a3c10792ffd0cdecbe625dd3fd4878b93791fca2a82ae35f3','1.1','2026-03-13T17:22:42.168542','2026-03-13T17:22:42.168549','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('70eab44a-7094-4914-b185-44bcd5fd21bc','BLM ID Range Improvement Line','<div style=\'text-align:Left;font-size:12pt\'><div><div><p><span>This geodatabase of point, line and polygon features is an effort to consolidate all of the range improvement locations on BLM-managed land in Idaho into one database. Currently, the line feature class has some data for all of the BLM field offices except the Coeur d\'Alene and Cottonwood field offices. Range improvements are structures intended to enhance rangeland resources, including wildlife, watershed, and livestock management. Examples of range improvements include water troughs, spring headboxes, culverts, fences, water pipelines, gates, wildlife guzzlers, artificial nest structures, reservoirs, developed springs, corrals, exclosures, etc. These structures were first tracked by the Bureau of Land Management (BLM) in the Job Documentation Report (JDR) System in the early 1960s, which was predominately a paper-based tracking system. In 1988 the JDRs were migrated into and replaced by the automated Range Improvement Project System (RIPS), and version 2.0 is currently being used today. It tracks inventory, status, objectives, treatment, maintenance cycle, maintenance inspection, monetary contributions and reporting. Not all range improvements are documented in the RIPS database; there may be some older range improvements that were built before the JDR tracking system was established. There also may be unauthorized projects that are not in RIPS. Official project files of paper maps, reports, NEPA documents, checklists, etc., document the status of each project and are physically kept in the office with management authority for that project area. In addition, project data is entered into the RIPS system to enable managers to access the data to track progress, run reports, analyze the data, etc. Before Geographic Information System technology most offices kept paper atlases or overlay systems that mapped the locations of the range improvements. The objective of this geodatabase is to migrate the location of historic range improvement projects into a GIS for geospatial use with other data and to centralize the range improvement data for the state. This data set is a work in progress and does not have all range improvement projects that are on BLM lands. Some field offices have not migrated their data into this database, and others are partially completed. New projects may have been built but have not been entered into the system. Historic or unauthorized projects may not have case files and are being mapped and documented as they are found. Many field offices are trying to verify the locations and status of range improvements with GPS, and locations may change or projects that have been abandoned or removed on the ground may be deleted. Attributes may be incomplete or inaccurate. This data was created using the standard for range improvements set forth in Idaho IM 2009-044, dated 6/30/2009. However, it does not have all of the fields the standard requires. Fields that are missing from the line feature class that are in the standard are: ALLOT_NO, MGMT_AGCY, ADMIN_ST, ADMIN_OFF, SRCE_AGCY, MAX_PDOP, MAX_HDOP, CORR_TYPE, RCVR_TYPE, GPS_TIME, UPDATE_STA, UNFILT_POS, FILT_POS, DATA_DICTI, GPS_LENGTH, GPS_3DLGTH, AVE_VERT_P, AVE_HORZ_P, WORST_VERT, WORST_HORZ and CONF_LEVEL. Several additional fields have been added that are not part of the standard: top_fence, btm_fence, admin_fo_line and year_checked. There is no National BLM standard for GIS range improvement data at this time.  For more information contact us at blm_id_stateoffice@blm.gov.</span></p></div></div></div>','public','2026-03-24T12:06:04.671818','2026-03-24T12:06:04.671824','Bureau of Land Management','Bureau of Land Management, id_so_information','010:04','d27caefe-1347-479c-91bd-28ef3eaa6186','DOI BLM DCAT-US','7ff07d13f43915b83ac56137b6bee14b3909e60dd19d0f62e8f32ae393e063c2','1.1','2026-03-24T12:06:04.671818','2026-03-24T12:06:04.671824','geospatial','010:000',0,'doi-gov'),('70fd941a-0e53-4dfd-b9a7-919d39a6589b','F00911: NOS Hydrographic Survey , 2024-10-12','The National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration (NOAA) has the statutory mandate to collect hydrographic data in support of nautical chart compilation for safe navigation and to provide background data for engineers, scientific, and other commercial and industrial activities. Hydrographic survey data primarily consist of water depths, but may also include features (e.g. rocks, wrecks), navigation aids, shoreline identification, and bottom type information.\n							NOAA is responsible for archiving and distributing the source data as described in this metadata record.','public','2026-03-14T22:46:32.510836','2026-03-14T22:46:32.510840',NULL,NULL,NULL,'cfbefb88-c916-4e10-a7f8-8ddac8c93b23','NESDIS/NGDC/MGG/NOS/F00001-F02000',NULL,NULL,'2026-03-14T22:46:32.510836','2026-03-14T22:46:32.510840',NULL,NULL,NULL,'noaa-gov'),('715c400e-28b4-492f-aba1-2b1762b9044c','Continuous Fixed Station Water Quality Measurements in Timucuan Ecological and Historic Preserve, December 2008 (Certified)','This dataset represents continuous water quality measurements that were taken at a fixed point in Timucuan Ecological and Historic Preserve during the month of December, 2008 as a part of the Fixed Station Water Quality Monitoring protocol that was developed by the Southeast Coast I&M Network (SECN). The measurements were taken by a YSI 6600 ESD Multi-Parameter Long Term Water Quality Monitoring Datasonde unit that serves as the standard fixed station water quality monitoring equipment for all similar operations conducted by the SECN. The following parameters were measured at 30 minute intervals during the time period that has been specified: Water Temperature, Specific Conductivity, Salinity, Dissolved Oxygen (DO), DO Concentration, Shallow Depth, pH Level, and Turbidity. Any anomalies noted regarding these parameters have also been noted in separate fields. Please note that these measurements have been certified by network personnel.','public','2026-03-26T05:32:50.234919','2026-03-26T05:32:50.234923','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','481f1f1c-0209-4f90-be1c-a22f26067d90','DOI NPS DCAT-US','d9718f92d172e5dc1054cecc254ff3a68faa7c3e2cbdf3ca7310c8191f77d6e7','1.1','2026-03-26T05:32:50.234919','2026-03-26T05:32:50.234923','Vector Dataset','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('719b033d-60c4-4fe5-b103-874173e1e2ed','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 4 1294 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 4 phase 2015-10-22 to 2015-12-31. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-12-28T17:22:00.000 to 2015-12-29T01:01:34.000.','public','2026-03-13T19:04:40.297219','2026-03-13T19:04:40.297224','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','6af1de0c-fe84-4671-ae35-579e7412feee','NASA Data.json','3120543b9ed71465a71936a922233a02ed53242a535d0d3c81e122e137dadd74','1.1','2026-03-13T19:04:40.297219','2026-03-13T19:04:40.297224','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('71a5fad3-db8a-45db-a7ad-db1255d326f1','VG1 LECP 0.4 SEC HIGH RESOLUTION JUPITER NEAR ENCOUNTER DATA','This near encounter data set consists of electron and ion        counting rate data from the Low Energy Charged Particle (LECP)        experiment on Voyager 1 while the spacecraft was within the        very close vicinity of Jupiter. This instrument measures the        intensities of in-situ charged particles ( >15 keV electrons        and >30 keV ions) with various levels of discrimination based        on energy range and mass species.  The LECP data are        globally calibrated to the extent possible.        Particles include low energy electrons, protons, alpha        particles, medium energy protons and ions, high energy and        intensity protons, electrons, alpha particles, and Z >= nuclei.','public','2026-03-13T18:52:48.761198','2026-03-13T18:52:48.761204','planetary plasma interactions','Earthdata Forum','026:00','cee5b1a6-bdf1-41a5-b41b-bde423eb7ed2','NASA Data.json','beba26192ac50fdbadb0275724822d9c595a47f272ada54949ad2ea4b72e0b71','1.1','2026-03-13T18:52:48.761198','2026-03-13T18:52:48.761204','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('71ade980-0fed-4edc-a3ce-ec80410710aa','Ecosys EcoMapSections 2025','<DIV STYLE=\"text-align:Left;\"><DIV><P><SPAN>The Ecomap 2025 contains a feature class for five different levels of the National Hierarchical Framework of Ecological Units (the Hierarchy. FSM 2060): Ecological Domains, Ecological Divisions, Ecological Provinces, Ecological Sections, and Ecological Subsections. The Ecomap 2025 data set describes the ecological hierarchy within the conterminous United States. Each feature class contains polygons attributed with the code and name of the ecological unit along with the codes and names of broader scale units into which a given ecological unit is nested. It contains regional geographic delineations for analysis of ecological relationships across ecological units. ECOMAP is the term used for a USDA Forest Service initiative to map ecological units and encourage their use in ecosystem-based approaches to forest and range land conservation and management. This is a collaborative effort with many partners. It is coordinated at the national and regional levels by USDA Forest Service staff and implemented in cooperation with State forestry agencies and others. ECOMAP mapping criteria are outlined in the National Hierarchical Framework of Ecological Units (Cleland et al. 1997, FSM 2060). The framework systematically divides the country into progressively smaller areas that have similar geophysical and biological characteristics and ecological processes.</SPAN></P></DIV></DIV>','public','2026-03-13T22:49:31.152316','2026-03-13T22:49:31.152322','U.S. Forest Service','USFSEnterpriseContent','005:96','caa88cbf-716a-4b2d-ac8c-0a65ce9a6291','USDA JSON','06fbd93c93eba08260aa05a7af63aa6f9464aef7625502c4e15da02ce519d980','1.1','2026-03-13T22:49:31.152316','2026-03-13T22:49:31.152322','geospatial','005:059',0,'usda-gov'),('71e16e0f-1fea-47b4-a850-6ca82d302ec8','MARINER 10 MERC POS M3 FLYBY TRAJ 42SEC V1.0','Mariner 10 trajectory (POS)  M3 FLYBY 42 second data at Mercury.','public','2026-03-13T18:34:09.415270','2026-03-13T18:34:09.415277','planetary plasma interactions','Planetary Data System','026:00','b303bdfc-e4d1-4d9d-8d10-67e560dbef79','NASA Data.json','dc7086d208469abec2f6a40e42156e1171ff3ae0eaafe0c0662d92869b8a753f','1.1','2026-03-13T18:34:09.415270','2026-03-13T18:34:09.415277','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('71f96e2e-0787-487a-b2fc-ed1d9d11709e','JOLTS TABLEAU - Separations','Job Openings and Labor Turnover survey dataset that contains data specifically about separations by geography.','public','2026-03-28T21:59:49.450437','2026-03-28T21:59:49.450442','data.iowa.gov','svqueen',NULL,'6f0c21ac-bd48-44c1-951c-b44794047ed3','Iowa metadata','fe6bd24af25175bd989678b7f7cf0cc2d2a16c3029766c3d7f92ed4a3bc9002f','1.1','2026-03-28T21:59:49.450437','2026-03-28T21:59:49.450442','Economic Statistics',NULL,0,'state-of-iowa'),('721cf7a1-22bd-4b33-a7d3-ec419ccd64cf','ROSETTA-ORBITER LUTETIA RPCMAG 3 AST2 CALIBRATED V9.0','This dataset contains CALIBRATED (CODMAC LEVEL 3) DATA of the LUTETIA flybyphase from July 7 until July 13, 2010 of the ROSETTA orbiter magnetometerRPCMAG. The closest approach (CA) took place on July 10, 2010 at 15:45.The current version of the dataset is V9.0.The difference to the datasets of earlier versions is mainly a significantlyimproved sensor temperature model, more detailed documentation about magneticdisturbance sources, more data handling information for the user andalso an improved quality flagging system.','public','2026-03-13T16:53:34.239285','2026-03-13T16:53:34.239291','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','9ab4a657-cd75-4ac2-907e-92bf6a845aa8','NASA Data.json','209a45951f66bf656decde5f273a703c76c8cee3b1f7ff03131c79d8266c40a4','1.1','2026-03-13T16:53:34.239285','2026-03-13T16:53:34.239291','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('72358091-b475-4a86-871e-f80b9aabc54e','GO V PWS RESAMP SUMMARY VENUS SPECTRUM ANALYZER 60S V1.0','This data set includes 1-minute averages of the electric and magnetic    wave spectra obtained during the ~ 53-minute period that the Galileo    plasma wave receiver was operated at Venus.','public','2026-03-13T18:43:20.960100','2026-03-13T18:43:20.960107','planetary plasma interactions','Planetary Data System','026:00','2a8d9a48-3839-4ea1-bf01-c0d2cee43c6f','NASA Data.json','4d39240ab8b7c7051cd9a82ddc1c0ca8dfd9f7d0af93595c2d4fa137d6c2e8e3','1.1','2026-03-13T18:43:20.960100','2026-03-13T18:43:20.960107','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('7258ebca-abc1-4edd-a756-a7bdc03b58c3','EGIS - Enterprise Gateway Integration Services-Person Centric Query System','PCQS is a read-only system that temporarily displays data from linked DHS and external agency systems based on a user query and is not a system of record for any response data from any external system.','non-public','2026-03-22T11:56:32.406073','2026-03-22T11:56:32.406077','Unspecified','Open Data (MGMT)','024:030','ec5d421d-383f-49fd-b573-c26c879a17b0','DHS datajson source','2f446039b88330aeccfffd2fe5a883b8df820110fc746d807cda0462589b473a','1.1','2026-03-22T11:56:32.406073','2026-03-22T11:56:32.406077',NULL,'024:000',0,'dhs-gov'),('72f04df1-322e-42b7-a737-217c3f072a83','ROSETTA-ORBITER ROSETTA EXTENSION 1 OSINAC 3 RDR MTP025 V1.0','This data set contains images acquired by the OSIRIS Narrow Angle Camera during the ROSETTA EXTENSION 1 phase of the Rosetta mission at the comet 67P, covering the period from 2016-01-12T23:25:00.000 to 2016-02-09T23:24:59.000.','public','2026-03-13T19:30:53.484470','2026-03-13T19:30:53.484477','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','6f8a1620-2fcc-49f9-afc2-2bad6ebe8d9a','NASA Data.json','bbe6e3e4bb0316306f6a0b76f259d46410be80b0602818fefbd8f4281cafb01b','1.1','2026-03-13T19:30:53.484470','2026-03-13T19:30:53.484477','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('733c5fdc-474c-49d2-bd73-6805cb0c8352','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 4 1166 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 4 phase 2015-10-22 to 2015-12-31. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-11-09T03:25:35.000 to 2015-11-09T07:13:25.000.','public','2026-03-13T18:43:40.182276','2026-03-13T18:43:40.182282','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','a224a22e-1a72-4991-bae6-ddba91104a7b','NASA Data.json','80de1738a8a9adb00b9ca10d79825bd82090f84d5411dfb9917d7758101f550a','1.1','2026-03-13T18:43:40.182276','2026-03-13T18:43:40.182282','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('737e4947-b873-48dd-ad4e-4992cd0da101','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSINAC 4 EXT3-MTP031 RDR-REFLECT V1.0','This CODMAC level 4 data set contains radiometric calibrated and geometric distortion corrected (resampled) image data in reflectance units (normalized and thus without unit), acquired by the OSIRIS Narrow Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft during the ROSETTA EXTENSION 3 mission phase, covering the period from 2016-06-28T23:25:00.000 to 2016-07-26T23:24:59.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V1.0 is the first version of this dataset: Lien corrected dataset after October 2018 PSA/PDS external peer review.','public','2026-03-13T19:47:26.080186','2026-03-13T19:47:26.080194','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','c97c3655-0378-44ef-9a3d-b567a0d95479','NASA Data.json','fda0090fc1ee1fdf845d48806df70d45783e0dbac554f28ec562142e63fa4a2a','1.1','2026-03-13T19:47:26.080186','2026-03-13T19:47:26.080194','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('73a1a82c-c59c-4c37-9038-2c0754d927c6','2026 Open Data Annual Report -- Year In Review','Year In Review page summarized the progress of Open Data project.','public','2026-03-15T02:20:47.200829','2026-03-15T02:20:47.200834','opendata.maryland.gov','Helen Bai',NULL,'deb07263-0284-46b7-ab38-1773c8ed9db4','md json','03cd4eaa8ae4143b0857f76c3ff0eeaf1e937e926d3cbaf42a16862966ace21e','1.1','2026-03-15T02:20:47.200829','2026-03-15T02:20:47.200834',NULL,NULL,0,'state-of-maryland'),('73a820b8-56b1-4dc8-a8bf-d9ccc2d6915e','Thyroid Hormone Insufficiency Alters the Pattern of Expression of the Ca2+-Binding Proteins in the Rat Neonatal Cortex','Dataset includes various results from two studies: the first study being a pilot study (M1123) and the second including dose response (M1224). In both studies, pregnant rats were dosed with Propylthiouracil (PTU) through drinking water with either 0 and 3ppm PTU (M1123) or 0, 0.5, 1, and 3ppm PTU (M1224) and tissue collected from both pups at various ages and dams on postnatal day 23. Specific results include serum thyroid hormone measures (RIA for thyroid stimulating hormone and LC-MS/MS for the remaining thyroid hormones), cortical thyroid hormone measures (LC-MS/MS), cortical gene expression data (qPCR), body weights, and immunohistochemical cell count data for four stains (DAB staining): parvalbumin, GAD-67, calbindin, and calretinin. Also included are the results for periventricular heterotopia volume measures (NeuN staining with DAB). Cell counts and volume measures for the periventricular heterotopia were conducted using Aperio ImageScope software.','public','2026-03-14T10:21:47.212981','2026-03-14T10:21:47.212985','U.S. Environmental Protection Agency','Tammy Stoker','020:00','b097fbbf-1dc4-439e-86ed-1b68c421cffc','EPA ScienceHub','e10b1e14e97ce0337c67a06c724e68b5378e8eb6492947bc0afaa49daa6d3bc2','1.1','2026-03-14T10:21:47.212981','2026-03-14T10:21:47.212985',NULL,'020:000',0,'epa-gov'),('73cad321-a05b-4608-a2b8-19c6c49a3228','MARS EXPRESS MARS MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 5 3852 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2015-01-01 to 2016-12-31. It is a Occultation measurement and covers the time 2016-10-31T11:31:01 to 2016-10-31T12:14:00.','public','2026-03-13T18:09:17.458889','2026-03-13T18:09:17.458895','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','73342fe0-0b63-49f3-8f1f-43b88e755dd1','NASA Data.json','447ddcc8b83ff36cc0f7e498fa8ebf553421fa419c8b0ec433c5db7d4a693b66','1.1','2026-03-13T18:09:17.458889','2026-03-13T18:09:17.458895','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('73d1551a-67a8-47a6-aa37-17518192a90c','APL_public_computer_use','Public computer use at APL locations','public','2026-03-25T14:36:27.167142','2026-03-25T14:36:27.167147','data.austintexas.gov','Austin Public Library Owners',NULL,'832fcd91-984b-4d9c-a023-ee6cb5ec8ffc','City of Austin Data.json','a562598e77f53bbae29ad4f11fa6866716be0aaa0b503ad90c9b74d306d426e5','1.1','2026-03-25T14:36:27.167142','2026-03-25T14:36:27.167147','Recreation and Culture',NULL,0,'city-of-austin'),('73de465f-f295-4b2f-8bc0-beb77a020f9a','EPOXI 103P/HARTLEY2 ENCOUNTER - HRIV CALIBRATED IMAGES V1.0','This dataset contains calibrated clear-filter images of comet 103/P Hartley 2 acquired by the High Resolution Visible CCD (HRIV) from 05 September through 26 November 2010 during the Hartley 2 encounter phase of the EPOXI mission. Four color-filter sets (350-950 nm) were acquired during the hour about closest approach.','public','2026-03-13T17:34:41.936769','2026-03-13T17:34:41.936774','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','ac848978-f8da-400e-afe1-99ef5b68318e','NASA Data.json','46f3bbc8b137b31adfd4efc9c1c0d9f0a649e82ebc61177c47c7ee063964a91e','1.1','2026-03-13T17:34:41.936769','2026-03-13T17:34:41.936774','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('74305053-f14e-4f90-818a-76dec1c7a6d9','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 2 0816 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 2 phase 2015-03-11 to 2015-06-30. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-05-29T09:28:00.000 to 2015-05-29T11:34:07.500.','public','2026-03-13T19:18:56.028750','2026-03-13T19:18:56.028755','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','cbfa94d1-86e6-44ac-af38-a62463d03366','NASA Data.json','40ffb347f8d0a05f93c7d1ae2697399e6726c29a171bddc8f8d29ea25ff0002a','1.1','2026-03-13T19:18:56.028750','2026-03-13T19:18:56.028755','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('74631522-0ee5-40e8-b42b-64fbff94401d','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 PRELANDING 0408 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the PRELANDING phase 2014-01-21 to 2014-11-18. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2014-11-04T20:57:05.000 to 2014-11-04T23:24:48.000.','public','2026-03-13T16:46:02.529820','2026-03-13T16:46:02.529826','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','9336e1f1-027f-432c-b768-73f1b5327377','NASA Data.json','3d32d0df1b5e4ccc65cab9c078a5329ff3978fb1b0c88928ce6877674fe5c897','1.1','2026-03-13T16:46:02.529820','2026-03-13T16:46:02.529826','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('74a82235-1c37-48b0-9e55-240695b3b836','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P NAVCAM 2 COMET ESCORT 3 MTP020 V1.0','This dataset contains ROSETTA NAVCAM RAW DATA of the Escort Phase 3 from 25th Aug 2015 to 22nd Sep 2015 when at the vicinity of target 67P/CG.','public','2026-03-13T18:21:39.552411','2026-03-13T18:21:39.552418','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','29729d2a-9af2-43d1-a656-75a8f2343869','NASA Data.json','1174b45adc0e3746305d0a8c6212dfdcde0be43b62129b29de8f560ace8f3215','1.1','2026-03-13T18:21:39.552411','2026-03-13T18:21:39.552418','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('74d8aa95-0b29-4b6a-b7ce-51659434fd0a','DAWN VESTA GRAVITY SCIENCE DERIVED  SCIENCE DATA V1.0','This data set contains archival results from gravity investigations conducted during the Dawn mission while the spacecraft was in orbit around the asteroid Vesta. Radio measurements were made using the Dawn spacecraft and Earth-based stations of the NASA Deep Space Network (DSN). The data set includes a spherical harmonic model of Vesta\'s gravity field generated by the Jet Propulsion Laboratory  and radial gravity acceleration map; these results were derived from raw radio tracking data.','public','2026-03-13T18:22:37.043195','2026-03-13T18:22:37.043201','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','98d1dedf-bc0f-4a5a-b91d-507a1b20e53b','NASA Data.json','3d7d643202f91deaf7f16ea3a3ede0b7cb2da55b10d7dae11aed04f6db694c90','1.1','2026-03-13T18:22:37.043195','2026-03-13T18:22:37.043201','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('7503ed23-4f08-4dc6-bf86-dae06789e9b9','2025 FTB EITC Summary of CA Residents','Produced by the Economic & Statistical Research Bureau, year-end tabulations of tax filings statistics for the Earned Income Tax Credit, (EITC), Young Child Tax Credit (YCTC) and Foster Youth Tax Credit (FYTC) provide credit use by county, preparer type, credit amount allowed number of dependents and a many other useful cross-sections.','public','2026-03-23T13:52:22.372007','2026-03-23T13:52:22.372011','California Franchise Tax Board','FTB Open Data',NULL,'fe9faee2-b79f-4484-8ba3-f1a4814618e8','State of California','6d9a3c7116b87f0f57e0ef7aaae033eaee41599b3f223ba11745b253871c64bb','1.1','2026-03-23T13:52:22.372007','2026-03-23T13:52:22.372011','Economy and Demographics',NULL,0,'ca-gov'),('7505202a-327b-4454-94d5-779a581ba97b','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSIWAC 3 ESC2-MTP015 RDR V3.0','This CODMAC level 3 data set contains radiometric calibrated image data in W/m^2/sr/nm, acquired by the OSIRIS Wide Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft during the COMET ESCORT 2 mission phase, covering the period from 2015-04-08T11:25:00.000 to 2015-05-05T23:24:59.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V3.0 supersedes previous deliveries of the same dataset with the following changes since the last version: Lien corrected dataset after the July and October 2018 PSA/PDS external peer reviews. Updated documentation and ancillary files, added document on bandpass filter. Updated SCIENCE_USER_GUIDE_V03.PDF to include one section about FAQ and one section about image data quality. Added shutter backtravel and readout issues to image quality map. Updated DATA_QUALITY_ID keyword in image header. Improved handling of images with missing packets. Included FITs files. Browse products changed to the same size as the original image.','public','2026-03-13T19:59:53.918942','2026-03-13T19:59:53.918948','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','988c1385-d5c2-4e84-8ae2-0c8b6f7fe594','NASA Data.json','f45283e45eb63a4c9f562c923107e43ad925ca72cf6c83777ce19f68e80f44ae','1.1','2026-03-13T19:59:53.918942','2026-03-13T19:59:53.918948','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('75355c3a-19b0-4317-9b76-cfd079b7c0bc','CASSINI ORBITER SATURN UVIS SPATIAL SPECTRAL IMAGE CUBE 1.2','Spectrographic observations of Jupiter, Saturnian rings, satellites, atmospheres and the interplanetary medium in the far and extreme ultraviolet.','public','2026-03-13T18:15:55.222638','2026-03-13T18:15:55.222654','Planetary Atmospheres','Planetary Data System','026:00','6268d810-62f2-4dbb-9c6e-c06cfb743462','NASA Data.json','db492e03b50ab1ff83f67721235ca2699833815d77e4113cde120ab564bbcad5','1.1','2026-03-13T18:15:55.222638','2026-03-13T18:15:55.222654','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('7546b738-7c61-4055-9390-71c377378016','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 1 0522 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 1 phase 2014-11-20 to 2015-03-10. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-01-04T23:55:20.000 to 2015-01-05T02:40:07.500.','public','2026-03-13T20:05:30.543746','2026-03-13T20:05:30.543754','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','55ea0aff-e012-4a86-986c-8c72d32cc846','NASA Data.json','13a6bea8e5a427a8534050bda3cc463bd49af7b0a45dbb3b34f9d0b3c2ca1ac6','1.1','2026-03-13T20:05:30.543746','2026-03-13T20:05:30.543754','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('7551c417-a4db-43ba-8672-814bec07c934','SMAP_L1A_RADAR_RECEIVE_ONLY_QA_V002','SMAP Level 1A Radar Receive Only Data Quality Information Version 2','public','2026-03-13T22:33:38.257605','2026-03-13T22:33:38.257611','NASA/JPL/SMAP;ASF','Earthdata Forum','026:00','2c1431f0-f2b0-4369-bf48-2efd086c25ab','NASA Data.json','3fbda86ad91d9fc5883c922d35ca43b30eb2fda2756e01ccba337d8a69d5ff9d','1.1','2026-03-13T22:33:38.257605','2026-03-13T22:33:38.257611','Earth Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('757ec38d-2de2-419f-89fd-90707411d3f0','ROSETTA-ORBITER X SREM 2 CRUISE 5 V1.0','This data set contains count rates (1/s) as measured by the Standard Radiation Environment Monitor (SREM) instrument on the Rosetta spacecraft, along with their standard deviations. These are CODMAC Level 2 Experiment Data Record data, and provide a measure of the radiation in the spacecraft environment during the CRUISE 5 mission phase.','public','2026-03-13T19:27:19.174738','2026-03-13T19:27:19.174744','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','a83ef167-846a-4ffb-890d-42b7bb0a3d03','NASA Data.json','8edaea89e7044b02fa79a3dca155d0d49ff9dfb34e02f2d3be3a51e352bf553b','1.1','2026-03-13T19:27:19.174738','2026-03-13T19:27:19.174744','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('758516e9-4be4-43f0-95e6-b20557973d41','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 1 0544 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 1 phase 2014-11-20 to 2015-03-10. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-01-21T04:19:50.000 to 2015-01-21T11:23:33.500.','public','2026-03-13T17:54:42.353744','2026-03-13T17:54:42.353752','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','f4c527eb-2c0e-4064-9425-1e4e70df0fce','NASA Data.json','a5e09075b30a5188eea13536fcb9f4e748bd921ffeb448278df94285cac8b976','1.1','2026-03-13T17:54:42.353744','2026-03-13T17:54:42.353752','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('758f458f-40e8-4ed8-9971-7db79bb61e7b','DE 1 Plasma Waves Instrument (PWI) Low Frequency Receiver B data','Plasma Waves Instrument Low Frequency Receiver B data','public','2026-03-13T22:35:38.031780','2026-03-13T22:35:38.031787','UCLA DE1','NASA Space Physics Data Facility','026:00','4ddb6469-82ab-41df-9a78-96954195c632','NASA Data.json','bc5d8b32cf2a29325057185ecf8ef1ddc867a6fb0729ba4f1898eee6d329ad07','1.1','2026-03-13T22:35:38.031780','2026-03-13T22:35:38.031787','Heliophysics','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('75ce0213-183b-47d2-a827-25fb4292833d','MARS EXPRESS ASPERA-3 CAL RDR ELECTRON SPECTROMTR EXT6 V1.0','This data set contains calibrated Mars Express ASPERA-3         Electron Spectrometer (ELS) data for the sixth mission         extension (January 1, 2017 - Dec. 31, 2018).  These data         are provided in units of Differential Number Flux (DNF):         cnts/(cm**2-sr-sec-eV)','public','2026-03-13T19:34:15.608123','2026-03-13T19:34:15.608130','planetary plasma interactions','Planetary Data System','026:00','cdb2c060-b228-4da0-9a34-ad4f544d3f50','NASA Data.json','4e2044807312dafd77d352c8e4c67be231e2c72200df61f563e51c8ee3d39104','1.1','2026-03-13T19:34:15.608123','2026-03-13T19:34:15.608130','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('75d9ca84-3fb9-4119-b4e4-64dd41b07970','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 PRELANDING 0357 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the PRELANDING phase 2014-01-21 to 2014-11-18. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2014-10-14T04:37:05.000 to 2014-10-14T15:12:59.000.','public','2026-03-13T18:36:56.916733','2026-03-13T18:36:56.916738','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','480008a1-bc07-4