,'2026-03-26T19:17:46.643708','2026-03-26T19:17:46.643716',NULL,NULL,NULL,'noaa-gov'),('76762051-4f05-450c-b19a-bd8621e8ba12','MARS EXPRESS MARS MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 7 3996 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2019-01-01 to 2020-12-31. It is a Occultation measurement and covers the time 2019-04-17T19:45:00.000 to 2019-04-17T21:30:00.000.','public','2026-03-13T19:40:00.015436','2026-03-13T19:40:00.015443','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','a035bdd4-6161-4a44-8b93-3046da57e33c','NASA Data.json','35b863cb9f93c6d09734eee267c43cd4ea3e904020c7519d41c034f5b3ddae98','1.1','2026-03-13T19:40:00.015436','2026-03-13T19:40:00.015443','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('767da94e-8a50-429d-b8d3-1ffca2ef7f71','Help America Vote Verification (HAVV) Transactions by State - Week Ending February 28, 2026','This dataset represents the results of the 4-digit match performed using the Social Security - Help America Vote Verification (HAVV) system. Report for week ending February 28, 2026.','public','2026-03-31T17:19:20.032809','2026-03-31T17:19:20.032814','Social Security Administration','Open Data','016:00','5734515a-68e7-44f0-9e07-38c78632e156','SSA JSON','0392dc6c1d0eb37484648f4d9e39f3ae98e27af1749519d8ef3d782dbc828a51','1.1','2026-03-31T17:19:20.032809','2026-03-31T17:19:20.032814',NULL,'016:000',0,'ssa-gov'),('767e44e7-0e2f-410e-84dd-f2596efdd695','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 3 1053 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 3 phase 2015-07-01 to 2015-10-21. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-09-24T03:07:20.000 to 2015-09-24T09:30:14.000.','public','2026-03-13T17:45:13.582702','2026-03-13T17:45:13.582709','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','07364893-6d4c-4c44-994f-c7356051f7cf','NASA Data.json','a536bfbb59eeb37e6a6e60e1970ed1c9a9b0edb98a7ee14b8d4eed5b5ed6b879','1.1','2026-03-13T17:45:13.582702','2026-03-13T17:45:13.582709','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('7688921b-3a88-4206-aaad-e47c779f1cf3','Floodplains from 2020','<div style=\'text-align:Left;\'><p><span>Insurance applications include enforcement of the mandatory purchase requirement of the Flood Disaster Protection Act, which requires the purchase of flood insurance by property owners who are being assisted by Federal programs or by Federally supervised, regulated or insured agencies or institutions in the acquisition or improvement of land facilities located or to be located in identified areas having special flood hazards, Section 2 (b) (4) of the Flood Disaster Protection Act of 1973. In addition to the identification of Special Flood Hazard Areas (SFHAs), the risk zones shown on the FIRMs are the basis for the establishment of premium rates for flood coverage offered through the NFIP. The DFIRM Database presents the flood risk information depicted on the FIRM in a digital format suitable for use in electronic mapping applications. The DFIRM database is a subset of the Digital FIS database that serves to archive the information collected during the FIS. For more information, visit </span><a target=\'_blank\' href=\'https://msc.fema.gov/portal/home\' rel=\'nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer\'><span><u>https://msc.fema.gov/portal/home</u></span></a><span>.</span></p></div>','public','2026-04-01T08:50:06.510678','2026-04-01T08:50:06.510683','Federal Emergency Management Agency','DCGISopendata',NULL,'83309288-cb6b-41d2-aa9c-0c1f76ae928e','DC data','ea00119fd0ba6ca804adde1bf653a03b4d460bf9bf5b56dfeb97e56d6b7f0ff9','1.1','2026-04-01T08:50:06.510678','2026-04-01T08:50:06.510683','geospatial',NULL,0,'district-of-columbia'),('76accacd-9edc-49f9-8ce9-7a9d572dc50d','San Francisco Municipal Energy Benchmarking','<strong>This dataset will replace the <u><a href=\"https://data.sfgov.org/d/k3fc-45qw/\">previous version of this dataset</a></u>, which will no longer be updated.</strong>\n\n<strong>A. SUMMARY</strong>\nSan Francisco’s Existing Buildings Energy Performance Ordinance requires owners of non-residential buildings over 10,000 square feet to annually benchmark and disclose energy performance. On behalf of City agencies, the San Francisco Public Utilities Commission (SFPUC) benchmarks and reports energy use for a portfolio of approximately 500 public facilities buildings. The performance of public facilities can be examined in an interactive report at https://bit.ly/SFMunicipalBenchmarking, and annual reports from 2011-present are available there as well.\n\nThis dataset presents the energy performance and basic characteristics for public facilities that is visualized by the SFPUC’s interactive report.\n\nIn addition, energy performance data for non-municipal buildings (i.e. commercial buildings of 10,000 square feet or larger, and multifamily & mixed-use buildings of 50,000 square feet or larger) is available at: https://bit.ly/ExistingBuildingsReport\n\n<strong>B. HOW THE DATASET IS CREATED</strong>\nIn compliance with California Energy Benchmarking Regulations (CA Public Resources Code Section 25402.10 and CCR Title 20 Section 1680), and San Francisco Existing Buildings Energy Ordinance (Environment Code Chapter 20), the San Francisco Public Utilities Commission provides energy benchmarking services on behalf of municipal facilities. Details for public facilities are compiled from city records, and energy usage is compiled from utility records; related metrics such as energy use intensity are calculated from the combination of such records. Data is subjected to quality assurance validation prior to publication. For additional information regarding data sources and assumptions, please review the \"Data Sources and Assumptions\" page of the Municipal Facilities Energy Benchmarking dashboard: https://bit.ly/SFMunicipalBenchmarking.\n\n<strong>C. UPDATE PROCESS</strong>\nUpdated Annually, but any adjustments may be made throughout the year.\n\n<strong>E. RELATED DATASETS</strong>\n<u><a href=\"https://data.sfgov.org/d/96ck-qcfe/\">Existing Buildings Energy Performance Ordinance Report</a></u>','public','2026-03-22T04:15:24.564606','2026-03-22T04:15:24.564611','data.sfgov.org','OpenData',NULL,'1257911e-08ce-49a8-bf37-2cbcf1d9f23b','SFO JSON','66df8e4906b57385e49f8d7e00b4a3367627492844856f5bd0e07c06ffcb6c55','1.1','2026-03-22T04:15:24.564606','2026-03-22T04:15:24.564611','Energy and Environment',NULL,0,'city-of-san-francisco'),('76b6c8a7-a208-47fa-8008-9e39a1c258ac','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RPCIES 3 PRL V2.0','This dataset contains CALIBRATED DATA of the Rosetta RPCIES instrument taken during the Prelanding phase (PRL). The target of this phase was comet 67P/CHURYUMOV-GERASIMENKO 1 (1969 R1). Included are the data taken between 21 Jan 2014 and 19 Nov 2014. This version of the data has been reprocessed to remove an error introduced in the previous version.','public','2026-03-13T17:39:06.101587','2026-03-13T17:39:06.101594','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','0bf8b03b-8235-4510-b233-14eb6e844d03','NASA Data.json','47034e1c5b1bce20389b194f227e57c115b9852108c1a3bc338598553b355a7e','1.1','2026-03-13T17:39:06.101587','2026-03-13T17:39:06.101594','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('76ccccec-c80a-4988-9cd3-1fbaf7df01d5','Oral Health Professional Supply and Non-Traumatic Dental Emergency Department Visits','These datasets contain emergency department visit rates for non-traumatic dental conditions as well as dentists and other oral health professionals who treat these conditions per county. Rates are displayed per 100,000 population. Higher emergency department visit rates for non-traumatic dental conditions may indicate a need for greater access to quality outpatient dental care. Lower dentist supply rates and oral health professional supply rates may indicate a greater need for oral health professionals in the area. Funding sources by condition are shown as percentages of dental-related emergency department visits. Counties are also grouped according to the Office of Health Workforce Development (OHWD) regions. See the diagnosis group to dentist and oral health professional list below to see which specialists would be needed to prevent/and or treat each dental-related diagnosis group.','public','2026-03-23T13:54:13.978662','2026-03-23T13:54:13.978670','Department of Health Care Access and Information','Department of Health Care Access and Information, Healthcare Analytics Branch',NULL,'97cb3028-53b8-4ca7-8814-98e9d84130b7','State of California','2a11bed9e91d24d045a0e92e1e6ae6e985d912902780d34257609b65dd10a4af','1.1','2026-03-23T13:54:13.978662','2026-03-23T13:54:13.978670','Health and Human Services',NULL,0,'ca-gov'),('770fa056-1f7b-480e-baa2-d9c46dad5020','Data from: The importance of vertically stratified, multi-year sampling for understanding native bee assemblages in southeastern temperate deciduous forests','<p dir=\"ltr\">We sampled and compared the bee assemblages of a temperate deciduous forest (Tuskegee National Forest, Tuskegee, Macon County, Alabama, USA) in both canopy and understory from April-October 2021 and March-October 2022. Blue vane traps were deployed at four sites across Tuskegee National Forest with four replicates per site. Each replicate had a blue vane in the understory (1m) and in the upper canopy (20 m average). In total, we captured 1,494 bees representing 38 taxa belonging to 15 genera and 5 families (Andrenidae, Apidae, Colletidae, Halictidae, and Megachilidae). Abundance varied seasonally and by year. The canopy traps produced 70% of all captures and there were almost three times as many bees in the canopy as in the understory. The four most commonly captured species (Lasioglossum bruneri, Melissodes bimaculatus, Augochlora pura, and Bombus impatiens) were present in significantly higher abundances in the canopy. We found no significant differences in species richness between the canopy and understory, but found that Simpson diversity was significantly different between strata. Interestingly, while overall and in 2021 Simpson diversity was higher in the canopy, in 2022 it was higher in the understory. </p>','public','2026-03-13T22:46:42.180335','2026-03-13T22:46:42.180341','Agricultural Research Service','Campbell, Joshua, W','005:18','ec892889-1cb1-4629-bea6-55c612ef2539','USDA JSON','e1b37dfe6609ca5a4623a658cfbd80a1aed72fecd4b3bd25970ff130ae776c0c','1.1','2026-03-13T22:46:42.180335','2026-03-13T22:46:42.180341',NULL,'005:040',0,'usda-gov'),('771e7c6d-95b7-4e58-897e-8c246d7ec8c0','DEEP IMPACT 9P/TEMPEL ENCOUNTER - REDUCED ITS NAV IMGS V1.0','This data set contains calibrated images of comet 9P/Tempel 1 acquired by the Deep Impact Impactor Targeting Sensor Visible CCD during the encounter phase of the mission. These observations were used for optical and autonomous navigation (NAV) of the impactor spacecraft as well as for scientific investigations. These data were collected on 3-4 July 2005.','public','2026-03-13T17:10:18.241257','2026-03-13T17:10:18.241265','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','c5655271-74ea-4fc4-ad86-e743695c43cc','NASA Data.json','57bc8920437766d49bb4e96f1d3aedce779bb486a5f7164fb6598034e88c45ec','1.1','2026-03-13T17:10:18.241257','2026-03-13T17:10:18.241265','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('773a53b2-74dd-43bd-be33-e39596e4363a','MARS EXPRESS MARS MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 3 3278 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2010-01-01 to 2012-12-31. It is a Global Gravity measurement and covers the time 2012-05-05T08:07:31.000 to 2012-05-05T11:49:55.500.','public','2026-03-13T19:32:28.801591','2026-03-13T19:32:28.801596','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','85374ed9-49b5-445c-8f51-97dab9abb466','NASA Data.json','a806ca8c5c540276e32fb986102df2204ce4ed217e924976239585eae25f906f','1.1','2026-03-13T19:32:28.801591','2026-03-13T19:32:28.801596','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('775e0d92-ecf3-4148-a8c0-95f2f87a5ccc','NEW HORIZONS REX POST-LAUNCH CHECKOUT CALIBRATED V1.0','This data set contains Calibrated data taken by the New Horizons Radio Science Experiment instrument during the post-launch checkout mission phase. This is VERSION 1.0 of this data set. The REX datasets over the mission include calibrations using known radio sources, Jupiter, and cold sky measurements; operational readiness tests (ORTs); internal test pattern calibration; and prime science radiometry and occultation observations during the Pluto Encounter.','public','2026-03-13T16:41:34.718608','2026-03-13T16:41:34.718615','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','ec9574c7-b376-4607-a1cf-2e769b38b1e6','NASA Data.json','4ce67391840ca2a1d62d2b0d972483f30ff24317574caf1f312ad537ab0b97a9','1.1','2026-03-13T16:41:34.718608','2026-03-13T16:41:34.718615','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('7768672d-09b7-4d21-9c30-b9e60575c861','BLM ID District Office Administrative Unit Boundary','<div style=\'text-align:Left;\'><div><div style=\'font-size:12pt\'><p><span>This data set shows the Idaho BLM District boundaries and names as per the Organization Refinement for FY 2004, which became official on October 1, 2003 (FY04), plus subsequent edits. This dataset has been updated over time. A Bureau of Land Management (BLM) Administrative Unit is a geographic area in which an organizational unit of the BLM has distinct jurisdictional responsibility for land and resource management activities occurring on the public lands, the maintained rights of the United States (i.e. mineral estate) and actions relating to the Trust responsibilities of the U.S. Government as stipulated in Law or Treaty. District Offices are the middle tier of BLM\'s three-tier organization, providing coordination, oversight and support to the lowest level, the Field Office, and overseen by the State Office.  For more information contact us at blm_id_stateoffice@blm.gov.</span></p></div></div></div>','public','2026-03-18T11:15:05.369359','2026-03-18T11:15:05.369364','Bureau of Land Management','Bureau of Land Management, id_so_information','010:04','3e7af677-9eb7-467c-b59f-05b5e76b4c7b','DOI BLM DCAT-US','a1ccf45e3b9b6a5688bf6e9f332e6ac1fd8842be16845005f9307e53ff796a62','1.1','2026-03-18T11:15:05.369359','2026-03-18T11:15:05.369364','geospatial','010:000',0,'doi-gov'),('7775a179-fc38-4ddc-a43b-6c343527875c','PHX MARS THERMAL EVOLVED GAS ANALYZER 4 EGSRDR V1.0','Calibrated or converted engineering, housekeeping and scientific data collected from the Thermal Evolved Gas Analyzer (TEGA) aboard the 2007 Mars Phoenix Lander.','public','2026-03-13T17:32:30.454392','2026-03-13T17:32:30.454398','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','13844799-43ca-459a-a909-434d623bf3bc','NASA Data.json','e8f24e4e5c58fe30dd72e2d49fcc805099f97b0b0bc50e568aa97b839f8153ae','1.1','2026-03-13T17:32:30.454392','2026-03-13T17:32:30.454398','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('779bdb4b-67d5-4243-9024-4a9ad2e0a057','ROSETTA-ORBITER 9P MIRO 3 CR2 9P-TEMPEL1 V1.1','This data set contains Spectroscopic and Continuum data taken by the Microwave Instrument for the Rosetta Orbiter (MIRO) during the second cruise phase of the mission. The data consist entirely of observations of comet 9P/Tempel 1 before, during and after the planned collision of the Deep Impact mission impactor spacecraft with that comet in July 2005. These data have been calibrated to antenna temperatures and are presented as a series of binary table files. Version 1.1 added UTC to the data files, added a GEOMETRY directory and incorporated a number of minor documentation additions and corrections.','public','2026-03-13T17:43:07.973863','2026-03-13T17:43:07.973871','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','d75b61da-fa65-4a90-9d0b-5be81846b95b','NASA Data.json','c82974501a26ad8b84d9c4a1a265215b94bab098827ef2a25e9a4673fdb49127','1.1','2026-03-13T17:43:07.973863','2026-03-13T17:43:07.973871','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('7835dfa3-f3a9-48da-81e8-d18f46870d14','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSINAC 4 ESC2-MTP016 RDR-INFLDSTR V1.0','This CODMAC level 4 data set contains solar stray-light corrected, in-field stray-light corrected,  radiometric calibrated and geometric distortion corrected  (resampled) image data in W/m^2/sr/nm,  acquired by the OSIRIS Narrow Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft  during the COMET ESCORT 2 mission phase, covering the period  from 2015-05-05T23:25:00.000 to 2015-06-02T23:24:59.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V1.0 is the first version of this dataset: Lien corrected dataset after September 2019 PSA/PDS external peer review.','public','2026-03-13T19:12:24.035901','2026-03-13T19:12:24.035906','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','d889f507-17bc-40f0-9e96-5b99539a1b0c','NASA Data.json','6872e8c746789d2c92074f4e8be541c3283a272e6d336798de534865c626ad23','1.1','2026-03-13T19:12:24.035901','2026-03-13T19:12:24.035906','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('784250a5-3907-409a-8256-a9d44d5e2037','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 PRELANDING 0331 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the PRELANDING phase 2014-01-21 to 2014-11-18. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2014-10-02T16:08:45.000 to 2014-10-02T22:55:08.500.','public','2026-03-13T18:33:28.417506','2026-03-13T18:33:28.417513','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','819512cf-0b96-404a-989d-09d2e3f58543','NASA Data.json','02f7cfd5207b452bd56b282dc77e10b1b6f9d6ecb2bbbaf91e6c503831aea715','1.1','2026-03-13T18:33:28.417506','2026-03-13T18:33:28.417513','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('787f7201-faf1-4edd-ab66-363c4013aa14','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P NAVCAM 3 ROSETTA EXTENSION 2 MTP029 V1.0','This dataset contains ROSETTA NAVCAM RADIOMETRICALLY CALIBRATED DATA of the ROSETTA EXTENSION 2 MTP029 Phase from 04 May. 2016, 06:04:22 to 31 May. 2016, 23:17:53 when at the vicinity of target 67P/CG.','public','2026-03-13T18:52:14.182784','2026-03-13T18:52:14.182789','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','1990003a-8e71-4f8f-baf3-c80626efb3a5','NASA Data.json','080a4b3c7f6bf72a5e77bf53867e96e6576897f50f7197ea453f6a6f91ffc5c1','1.1','2026-03-13T18:52:14.182784','2026-03-13T18:52:14.182789','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('789768e0-1c52-4ce7-b408-99ff11029160','MARS EXPRESS MARS MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 6 3882 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2017-01-01 to 2018-12-31. It is a Occultation measurement and covers the time 2017-01-08T20:47:01 to 2017-01-08T21:32:00.','public','2026-03-13T18:11:55.453962','2026-03-13T18:11:55.453967','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','3e963372-2a2e-4034-aac3-fd8747394212','NASA Data.json','d5bb8a272143132f98f8535dfce0ede5b0820e69c5d1a242b230078ac601548f','1.1','2026-03-13T18:11:55.453962','2026-03-13T18:11:55.453967','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('78a6ae3b-d87d-407f-9f4a-75d3e4cb392e','Test UTF-8','Test','public','2026-03-25T18:20:03.165286','2026-03-25T18:20:03.165290','Centers for Medicare & Medicaid Services','Medicaid.gov','009:38','0b3c034b-20bd-4580-a396-0fa9fa0f7c37','Healthdata.gov','b83e8e2ba2e041d441be52e942caa513602961926c110425a7980654d56fb0d3','1.1','2026-03-25T18:20:03.165286','2026-03-25T18:20:03.165290','CMS','009:076',0,'hhs-gov'),('78da8ccf-10b0-4b81-91fd-720c23bfe3b3','Continuous Fixed Station Water Quality Measurements in Timucuan Ecological and Historic Preserve, November 2008 (Certified)','This dataset represents continuous water quality measurements that were taken at a fixed point in Timucuan Ecological and Historic Preserve during the month of November, 2008 as a part of the Fixed Station Water Quality Monitoring protocol that was developed by the Southeast Coast I&M Network (SECN). The measurements were taken by a YSI 6600 ESD Multi-Parameter Long Term Water Quality Monitoring Datasonde unit that serves as the standard fixed station water quality monitoring equipment for all similar operations conducted by the SECN. The following parameters were measured at 30 minute intervals during the time period that has been specified: Water Temperature, Specific Conductivity, Salinity, Dissolved Oxygen (DO), DO Concentration, Shallow Depth, pH Level, and Turbidity. Any anomalies noted regarding these parameters have also been noted in separate fields. Please note that these measurements have been certified by network personnel.','public','2026-03-26T05:32:46.680543','2026-03-26T05:32:46.680550','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','ade5b3f4-b21f-444e-a4cf-57980fa53315','DOI NPS DCAT-US','203444dfbecf8244dce2ff633014491b93e8067bb86f418c0b9604f18cd2ad02','1.1','2026-03-26T05:32:46.680543','2026-03-26T05:32:46.680550','Vector Dataset','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('78e0f3fb-94c2-455b-a5c3-27e610cff5b4','Continuous Fixed Station Water Quality Measurements in Timucuan Ecological and Historic Preserve, October 2008 (Certified)','This dataset represents continuous water quality measurements that were taken at a fixed point just outside of Timucuan Ecological and Historic Preserve during the month of October, 2008 as a part of the Fixed Station Water Quality Monitoring protocol that was developed by the Southeast Coast I&M Network (SECN). The measurements were taken by a YSI 6600 ESD Multi-Parameter Long Term Water Quality Monitoring Datasonde unit that serves as the standard fixed station water quality monitoring equipment for all similar operations conducted by the SECN. The following parameters were measured at 30 minute intervals during the time period that has been specified: Water Temperature, Specific Conductivity, Salinity, Dissolved Oxygen (DO), DO Concentration, Shallow Depth, pH Level, and Turbidity. Any anomalies noted regarding these parameters have also been noted in separate fields. Please note that these measurements have been certified by network personnel.','public','2026-03-26T05:34:06.117217','2026-03-26T05:34:06.117225','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','536899af-baf4-48ce-b2f1-661eab9c1098','DOI NPS DCAT-US','b1cb65a4d0c1cc56ec7d04f8f62b3bd316842b651ade0b4cd70ca55659301c39','1.1','2026-03-26T05:34:06.117217','2026-03-26T05:34:06.117225','Vector Dataset','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('790245be-87d3-4445-bae9-edf4b4ecaf73','Product Data for Newly Reported Drugs in the Medicaid Drug Rebate Program 03-16-2026 to 03-22-2026','The data below contains newly reported, active covered outpatient drugs which were reported by participating drug manufacturers since the last quarterly update of the Drug Products in the Medicaid Drug Rebate Program (MDRP) database.','public','2026-03-25T18:17:10.829516','2026-03-25T18:17:10.829522','Centers for Medicare & Medicaid Services','Medicaid.gov','009:38','ea8a1edb-cb93-4020-a364-825f685e2460','Healthdata.gov','994cf14b1350a58c6fdcf1086c5fce48fda597db94de81d9b68aeff009b66247','1.1','2026-03-25T18:17:10.829516','2026-03-25T18:17:10.829522','CMS','009:076',0,'hhs-gov'),('7935bddf-5e09-4d20-b535-931ea1ccde72','MARS EXPRESS MARS MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 4 3501 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2013-01-01 to 2014-12-31. It is a Global Gravity measurement and covers the time 2013-01-21T08:35:03.000 to 2013-01-21T11:10:30.500.','public','2026-03-13T17:19:45.034621','2026-03-13T17:19:45.034627','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','66a7cac7-3b10-4e5d-9b7b-41c6e3f07846','NASA Data.json','d9d25649ad502524118990a62ebb1ca4c39592d6a8506e1add5b5defee1d5d20','1.1','2026-03-13T17:19:45.034621','2026-03-13T17:19:45.034627','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('7965789d-74bf-4b17-920b-0ac4b5c5a986','EGIS - Enterprise Gateway Integration Services-Lockbox Intake Service','LIS is a composite service that receives immigration applications and petitions along with supporting documents from the JPMC Lockbox Service Provider via USCIS EGIS. The applications data is then transmitted to USCIS backend systems. ','non-public','2026-03-22T11:52:25.476203','2026-03-22T11:52:25.476210','Unspecified','Open Data (MGMT)','024:030','6c889625-e071-41b6-adcb-3a0231ad3426','DHS datajson source','a9429af6aa60593bfbd45c40491e0bec663933616d211a319f5a3cfe963ab266','1.1','2026-03-22T11:52:25.476203','2026-03-22T11:52:25.476210',NULL,'024:000',0,'dhs-gov'),('79719c4d-a282-4901-8494-fdbf03700a6f','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSINAC 3 ESC1-MTP013 RDR V3.0','This CODMAC level 3 data set contains radiometric calibrated image data in W/m^2/sr/nm, acquired by the OSIRIS Narrow Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft during the COMET ESCORT 1 mission phase, covering the period from 2015-02-10T23:25:00.000 to 2015-03-10T23:24:59.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V3.0 supersedes previous deliveries of the same dataset with the following changes since the last version: Lien corrected dataset after the July and October 2018 PSA/PDS external peer reviews. Updated documentation and ancillary files, added document on bandpass filter. Updated SCIENCE_USER_GUIDE_V03.PDF to include one section about FAQ and one section about image data quality. Added shutter backtravel and readout issues to image quality map. Updated DATA_QUALITY_ID keyword in image header. Improved handling of images with missing packets. Included FITs files. Browse products changed to the same size as the original image.','public','2026-03-13T17:08:04.398327','2026-03-13T17:08:04.398334','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','09163703-7604-4743-bebf-d8fdc69446d8','NASA Data.json','69e8cf04e09e7b2eede24c02dca506c6be11559f40f6218c19eb96d5b1b4fa85','1.1','2026-03-13T17:08:04.398327','2026-03-13T17:08:04.398334','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('79b45886-7299-4f5a-8334-d14d290788f4','MARS EXPRESS MARS MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 3 3454 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2010-01-01 to 2012-12-31. It is a Global Gravity measurement and covers the time 2012-11-03T02:37:49.000 to 2012-11-03T06:35:04.500.','public','2026-03-13T19:11:32.038900','2026-03-13T19:11:32.038906','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','10214911-3f8f-479b-8afd-158afeaca077','NASA Data.json','8ca5ba1b14be3b597b9c02a22e54ecd4ea8050a75e15c8bb275e395d232d0196','1.1','2026-03-13T19:11:32.038900','2026-03-13T19:11:32.038906','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('79fa87cb-2744-49fd-aaba-5fedfd1dc236','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 1 0598 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 1 phase 2014-11-20 to 2015-03-10. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-02-23T10:45:45.000 to 2015-02-23T22:11:29.000.','public','2026-03-13T19:02:39.260145','2026-03-13T19:02:39.260150','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','024742fa-e466-4b49-aeec-01ea649033ef','NASA Data.json','ae55debf7fa7b91d33010cae07c6cf73ac161723163515ac40fc66de638b0205','1.1','2026-03-13T19:02:39.260145','2026-03-13T19:02:39.260150','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('7a0bcaad-420a-4c27-9df0-1fb9485c7980','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P NAVCAM 2 ROSETTA EXTENSION 3 MTP034 V1.1','This dataset contains ROSETTA NAVCAM RAW DATA of the Extension 3 Phase phase from 2nd Sep 2016 to 26th Sep 2016 when at the vicinity of target 67P/CG. This data set V1.1 supersedes the V1.0. It includes document updates and resolve other outstanding errata.','public','2026-03-13T16:46:23.351596','2026-03-13T16:46:23.351601','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','7c66c535-5869-4e47-984a-ddf0f0b79c76','NASA Data.json','6202e268504c14100829d12818d470ac8c10005d8e933d51f9069397afb40d1c','1.1','2026-03-13T16:46:23.351596','2026-03-13T16:46:23.351601','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('7a2ece4f-f6ea-498c-b426-b2f12060d715','MARS EXPRESS SUN MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 5 3746 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2015-01-01 to 2016-12-31. It is a Solar Conjunction measurement and covers the time 2015-05-27T09:03:01 to 2015-05-27T13:04:00.','public','2026-03-13T18:48:15.534043','2026-03-13T18:48:15.534049','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','e02ab0f2-0d59-44e6-b963-d3c37373176b','NASA Data.json','9fdc2e18b0193e3992e648943d58a5d829c50c4604752025940a9831b51cbfbc','1.1','2026-03-13T18:48:15.534043','2026-03-13T18:48:15.534049','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('7a41ce3f-1fe4-4f2a-b30f-3e1907a313ba','IHW COMET PPMAG CALIB REDUCED DATA RECORD CROMMELIN V1.0','In preparation for the concerted international study of Comet Halley, the IHW conducted a trial run with observations of Comet Crommelin, largely during February and March of 1984.','public','2026-03-13T17:30:17.673675','2026-03-13T17:30:17.673683','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','1c8ca325-499f-4434-bc25-300d769c07fa','NASA Data.json','16c659d16047edf46634b35dcade8416d85dc84b7fbcd5e2205238796300fd0a','1.1','2026-03-13T17:30:17.673675','2026-03-13T17:30:17.673683','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('7a52dcf3-0d3d-4c86-b2ff-d38c8cdd7e2e','AIRSAR_ALONGTRACK_INTERFEROMETRY_JPG','AIRSAR along-track interferometric browse product JPG','public','2026-03-13T18:37:01.637145','2026-03-13T18:37:01.637151','NASA/JPL/RDC;ASF','Earthdata Forum','026:00','4aaaccc2-bc28-4892-bde4-9bfeb37dbf62','NASA Data.json','655f33262ddf93c71b9ac918f8fd82f5722445e3ecf560f94a32af0d616a3d35','1.1','2026-03-13T18:37:01.637145','2026-03-13T18:37:01.637151','Earth Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('7a59c73c-bb81-4c0a-90c4-eab2de9be89e','MARS EXPRESS SUN MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 7 4067 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2019-01-01 to 2020-12-31. It is a Solar Conjunction measurement and covers the time 2019-09-21T05:12:48.000 to 2019-09-21T08:49:49.500.','public','2026-03-13T19:35:38.043817','2026-03-13T19:35:38.043822','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','1bff873b-75c1-4746-b187-75f028b48e1f','NASA Data.json','e2a487c3199ceee191911d06fc5193c137099d5d3e96a81ac5ff84658d0b679f','1.1','2026-03-13T19:35:38.043817','2026-03-13T19:35:38.043822','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('7a8a43d2-f422-477a-87da-1e5d773e9e5c','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P NAVCAM 3 COMET ESCORT 1 MTP010 V1.0','This dataset contains ROSETTA NAVCAM RADIOMETRICALLY CALIBRATED DATA of the COMET ESCORT 1 MTP010 Phase from 22 Nov. 2014, 04:19:32 to 19 Dec. 2014, 22:35:03 when at the vicinity of target 67P/CG.','public','2026-03-13T19:37:22.997067','2026-03-13T19:37:22.997072','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','83d2a3d5-a0d9-4852-bdca-89108f9d59f9','NASA Data.json','5bf850ca4088d35f41b6588a5955ebc27aff6bc78a913a598acc2c7140c7b165','1.1','2026-03-13T19:37:22.997067','2026-03-13T19:37:22.997072','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('7ad0681e-0bda-4390-8fff-2136c340895b','EPA Facility Registry Service (FRS): ER_TRI','This web feature service contains location and facility identification information from EPA\'s Facility Registry System (FRS) for the subset of facilities that link to the Toxic Release Inventory (TRI) System. TRI is a publicly available EPA database reported annually by certain covered industry groups, as well as federal facilities. It contains information about more than 650 toxic chemicals that are being used, manufactured, treated, transported, or released into the environment, and includes information about waste management and pollution prevention activities. FRS identifies and geospatially locates facilities, sites or places subject to environmental regulations or of environmental interest. Using vigorous verification and data management procedures, FRS integrates facility data from EPA\'s national program systems, other federal agencies, and State and tribal master facility records and provides EPA with a centrally managed, single source of comprehensive and authoritative information on facilities. This data set contains the subset of FRS integrated facilities that link to TRI facilities once the TRI data has been integrated into the FRS database. Additional information on FRS is available at the EPA website https://www.epa.gov/enviro/facility-registry-service-frs. These data are considered sensitive and are restricted to internal use only. The download file and map service are accessible only on the EPA intranet. EPA Category: Mission Sensitive, NARA Category: Critical Infrastructure.','public','2026-03-27T15:37:48.871591','2026-03-31T16:40:04.683815',NULL,NULL,NULL,'d3b58178-c36e-45ae-a750-62d2703306b2','Environmental Dataset Gateway ISO Geospatial Metadata',NULL,NULL,'2026-03-27T15:37:48.871591','2026-03-31T16:40:04.683815',NULL,NULL,NULL,'epa-gov'),('7ae9be74-cec9-430d-ae7e-39658db20506','NEW HORIZONS SWAP POST-LAUNCH CHECKOUT V2.0','This data set contains Calibrated data taken by the New Horizons Solar Wind Around Pluto instrument during the post-launch checkout mission phase.','public','2026-03-13T19:32:10.997767','2026-03-13T19:32:10.997775','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','b7d387b2-1680-410e-831f-893147bb13e1','NASA Data.json','aa6c6c013309159a813c054f6236216f223c7063c17b2fc7a9992ec190a760a7','1.1','2026-03-13T19:32:10.997767','2026-03-13T19:32:10.997775','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('7b4e749d-5b4b-4ac3-b9f7-69dbc2809b2e','MARS EXPRESS MARS MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 4 3604 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2013-01-01 to 2014-12-31. It is a Global Gravity measurement and covers the time 2013-10-04T22:50:12.000 to 2013-10-05T01:17:47.500.','public','2026-03-13T18:31:19.470919','2026-03-13T18:31:19.470925','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','17ce5974-2ee7-4f7a-a1b3-f889713c76de','NASA Data.json','cee888672b8d3eb1d697016748b863a7687232ff1e1ceb4e46715245110086ba','1.1','2026-03-13T18:31:19.470919','2026-03-13T18:31:19.470925','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('7bf7de59-e42b-4ef1-a52d-97adfeb3c3f8','Fugro Cruise C16185 Line 1371, 75 kHz VMADCP','Program of vessel mount ADCP measurements comprising a combination of 300kHz and 75kHz ADCP data collected in the vicinity of the Loop Current and drilling blocks between 2004 and 2007.','public','2026-03-26T19:14:37.123338','2026-03-26T19:14:37.123344',NULL,NULL,NULL,'06b47791-ed94-43c8-85c1-2933e35e7153','ioos',NULL,NULL,'2026-03-26T19:14:37.123338','2026-03-26T19:14:37.123344',NULL,NULL,NULL,'noaa-gov'),('7bff0eb5-2123-44b8-bcc8-7db2436ce086','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 PRELANDING 0204 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the PRELANDING phase 2014-01-21 to 2014-11-18. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2014-08-13T13:51:05.000 to 2014-08-13T19:10:41.500.','public','2026-03-13T16:38:47.028642','2026-03-13T16:38:47.028649','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','76fed129-e9b1-4052-bb65-da41e7b67784','NASA Data.json','98599d2d98850471026adc05d0781b6e6caca44fb48a04c362dd11491bc0cecb','1.1','2026-03-13T16:38:47.028642','2026-03-13T16:38:47.028649','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('7c369549-42fb-4735-ba40-c1642fcb004c','Continuous Fixed Station Water Quality Measurements in Timucuan Ecological and Historic Preserve, January 2009 (Certified)','This dataset represents continuous water quality measurements that were taken at a fixed point in Timucuan Ecological and Historic Preserve during the month of January, 2009 as a part of the Fixed Station Water Quality Monitoring protocol that was developed by the Southeast Coast I&M Network (SECN). The measurements were taken by a YSI 6600 ESD Multi-Parameter Long Term Water Quality Monitoring Datasonde unit that serves as the standard fixed station water quality monitoring equipment for all similar operations conducted by the SECN. The following parameters were measured at 30 minute intervals during the time period that has been specified: Water Temperature, Specific Conductivity, Salinity, Dissolved Oxygen (DO), DO Concentration, Shallow Depth, pH Level, and Turbidity. Any anomalies noted regarding these parameters have also been noted in separate fields. Please note that these measurements have been certified by network personnel.','public','2026-03-26T05:32:54.275447','2026-03-26T05:32:54.275453','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','70144172-7d78-4a17-be42-79608b8a3c36','DOI NPS DCAT-US','3ccb3af9fc3f7decd197013e6d61330c8f437bc134806931925fef3b6e133cf8','1.1','2026-03-26T05:32:54.275447','2026-03-26T05:32:54.275453','Vector Dataset','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('7c4d2bcb-363b-4d39-adb6-c9e0767898c5','US Forest Atlas FIA Modeled Abundance (Image Service)','<p><strong>FIA Modeled Abundance:</strong></p><div>This dataset portrays the live tree mean basal area (square feet per acre) of the species across the contiguous United States. The underlying data publication contains raster maps of live tree basal area for each tree species along with corresponding assessment data. An efficient approach for mapping multiple individual tree species over large spatial domains was used to develop these raster datasets. The method integrates vegetation phenology derived from MODIS imagery and raster data describing relevant environmental parameters with extensive field plot data of tree species basal area to create maps of tree species abundance and distribution at a 250-meter (m) pixel size for the contiguous United States. The approach uses the modeling techniques of k-nearest neighbors and canonical correspondence analysis, where model predictions are calculated using a weighting of nearest neighbors based on proximity in a feature space derived from the model. The approach also utilizes a stratification derived from the 2001 National Land-Cover Database tree canopy cover layer.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div><p>This data depicts current species abundance and distribution across the contiguous United States, modeled by using FIA field plot data. Although the absolute values associated with the maps differ from species to species, the highest values within each map are always associated with darker colors. This is a digital representation of maps by Elbert L. Little, Jr., published between 1971 and 1977. These maps were based on botanical lists, forest surveys, field notes and herbarium specimens.</p></div>','public','2026-03-13T22:50:09.699497','2026-03-13T22:50:09.699503','U.S. Forest Service','USFSEnterpriseContent','005:96','f1c7c804-f06a-4836-912f-498a306f1865','USDA JSON','fa488f70cebf8a2e978ef0018dbf1ff9f2a5dec553c5496938bbca892fb9856c','1.1','2026-03-13T22:50:09.699497','2026-03-13T22:50:09.699503','geospatial','005:059',0,'usda-gov'),('7c8539da-db33-4eb4-9321-2d529f251839','Highway-Rail Grade Crossing Incidents Within Quiet Zones Detail Listing','This is the report page for Highway-Rail Grade Crossing Incidents Within Quiet Zones Detail Listing.','public','2026-03-26T12:46:24.783169','2026-03-26T12:46:24.783174','Federal Railroad Administration','FRA Safety Data Team','021:27','5b4ff2fb-8f01-400f-9c8c-4859cfa04af3','DOT Socrata Data.json','9aca747b733cdee675877bf46c42ad8a5914bf6349248d043e590a08ea24ab3f','1.1','2026-03-26T12:46:24.783169','2026-03-26T12:46:24.783174','Railroads','021:037',0,'dot-gov'),('7c8f54fa-db6f-4d58-b43e-7051cbbd1b66','COVID-19 Probable Cases (ARCHIVED)','__Note:__ This dataset is no longer being updated due to the end of the COVID-19 Public Health Emergency.\n\n__Note:__ On 2/16/22, 17,467 cases based on at-home positive test results were excluded from the probable case counts. Per national case classification guidelines, cases based on at-home positive results are now classified as “suspect” cases. The majority of these cases were identified between November 2021 and February 2022. \n\nCDPH tracks both probable and confirmed cases of COVID-19 to better understand how the virus is impacting our communities. Probable cases are defined as individuals with a positive antigen test that detects the presence of viral antigens. Antigen testing is useful when rapid results are needed, or in settings where laboratory resources may be limited. Confirmed cases are defined as individuals with a positive molecular test, which tests for viral genetic material, such as a PCR or polymerase chain reaction test. Results from both types of tests are reported to CDPH.\n\nDue to the expanded use of antigen testing, surveillance of probable cases is increasingly important. The proportion of probable cases among the total cases in California has increased.  To provide a more complete picture of trends in case volume, it is now more important to provide probable case data in addition to confirmed case data. The Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC) has begun publishing probable case data for states. \n\nTesting data is updated weekly. Due to small numbers, the percentage of probable cases in the first two weeks of the month may change. Probable case data from San Diego County is not included in the statewide table at this time. \n\nFor more information, please see https://www.cdph.ca.gov/Programs/CID/DCDC/Pages/COVID-19/Probable-Cases.aspx','public','2026-03-23T14:05:02.784063','2026-03-23T14:05:02.784069','California Department of Public Health','COVID-19 Response Data, Informatics, Surveillance, Clinical and Outbreaks (DISCO) Team',NULL,'31dc3a44-aa4f-429a-bbd7-87b7991908b8','State of California','e213971983de077f31afb17738db0d1af5bc792a9e6337e01693a1de6f6383e5','1.1','2026-03-23T14:05:02.784063','2026-03-23T14:05:02.784069','COVID-19',NULL,0,'ca-gov'),('7caf93f0-ee26-4010-9b7d-5e0676c6b1d3','Continuous Fixed Station Water Quality Measurements in Timucuan Ecological and Historic Preserve, September 2008 (Certified)','This dataset represents continuous water quality measurements that were taken at a fixed point in Timucuan Ecological and Historic Preserve during the month of September, 2008 as a part of the Fixed Station Water Quality Monitoring protocol that was developed by the Southeast Coast I&M Network (SECN). The measurements were taken by a YSI 6600 ESD Multi-Parameter Long Term Water Quality Monitoring Datasonde unit that serves as the standard fixed station water quality monitoring equipment for all similar operations conducted by the SECN. The following parameters were measured at 30 minute intervals during the time period that has been specified: Water Temperature, Specific Conductivity, Salinity, Dissolved Oxygen (DO), DO Concentration, Shallow Depth, pH Level, and Turbidity. Any anomalies noted regarding these parameters have also been noted in separate fields. Please note that these measurements have been certified by network personnel.','public','2026-03-26T05:33:39.433653','2026-03-26T05:33:39.433657','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','cc2fcf34-7083-4ab5-a415-e8e6adc701bc','DOI NPS DCAT-US','c06aa0e5c3c7b464d04dc90d25f86a81047182ee6c217b388f099b1c3df184e6','1.1','2026-03-26T05:33:39.433653','2026-03-26T05:33:39.433657','Vector Dataset','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('7d5bc3a3-c764-4837-8e8a-b08dce1d6e97','VG1 JUP PLS DERIVED ION INBOUND SOLAR                                        WIND 96SEC V1.0','Voyager 1 Plasma Experiment (PLS)averaged ion inbndswind 96 second data at Jupiter.','public','2026-03-13T19:00:16.321245','2026-03-13T19:00:16.321252','planetary plasma interactions','Planetary Data System','026:00','e02f7f41-81df-4dae-946e-05e07082ced5','NASA Data.json','91752173bbe4aeb1b55f2f5396aeb438e7bdf92d2ac8ffae823e076cdbccbbd1','1.1','2026-03-13T19:00:16.321245','2026-03-13T19:00:16.321252','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('7d878e2f-1853-430a-9346-8aafc5d509cb','HPMS Roadway Sample 2020','State DOTs provide the Highway Performance Monitoring System (HPMS) with the location limits of highway sections used to represent statewide aggregations based on a statistically valid Sample Panel.','public','2026-03-28T13:37:06.130372','2026-03-28T13:37:06.130376','Federal Highway Administration','Office of Highway Policy Information','021:15','7670c376-16fe-4082-bc90-0eb00b086c07','DOT Socrata Data.json','63f9385d28277f6666d6507a0650f71dc185d46e9784fb6ff99f743723596cca','1.1','2026-03-28T13:37:06.130372','2026-03-28T13:37:06.130376','Roadways and Bridges','021:009',0,'dot-gov'),('7d8ec0ef-0e1f-4402-aa98-ab326e5a1133','AIRSAR_TOPSAR_L-BAND_STOKES','AIRSAR topographic SAR digital elevation model L_Stokes product','public','2026-03-13T18:35:09.670694','2026-03-13T18:35:09.670699','NASA/JPL/RDC;ASF','Earthdata Forum','026:00','891c46f5-c2d7-4a6c-ade1-471edd6f7231','NASA Data.json','6b24923b91c67aac7699133104c0e3fe7c9dc053c6492db8d8d2f28441256498','1.1','2026-03-13T18:35:09.670694','2026-03-13T18:35:09.670699','Earth Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('7ddec5c7-efb6-4af9-9d08-7553e6d1d6fc','Iowa 4.0 Work Zone Data Exchange Feed Example','This dataset provides archived lane closure occurrences within the Iowa Department of Transportation (IDOT) highway system in a tabular format.\n\nThe ITS JPO has collections from 23 states including Iowa covering various parts of the time period from 10/2019 to 08/2024 depending on when the feed was active. The data is split into two archive files, the raw data contains the collection of .json or .geojson files exactly as they were on the individual state’s WZDx feed at the time of collection. The processed data is organized by work zone, so that as information about the work zone changed through feed updates they would be collected in a single file for that work zone. To request access fill out the form here.','public','2026-03-25T12:38:23.331183','2026-03-25T12:38:23.331228','Federal Highway Administration','Elina Zlotchenko','021:15','bc4a8f95-a3f1-46e1-b96b-a9792d277439','DOT Socrata Data.json','3702c3f4283bebcf1a4358789e77aa6a9105a5bedef96e032d1ba6de8f547f20','1.1','2026-03-25T12:38:23.331183','2026-03-25T12:38:23.331228','Roadways and Bridges','021:042',0,'dot-gov'),('7ddec8db-62c8-4df1-97c9-3a949ea30a14','ASTEROID BIBLIOGRAPHY V2.0','Compilation of asteroid and asteroid-related references, covering the period 1621-1993.','public','2026-03-13T16:58:11.387005','2026-03-13T16:58:11.387009','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','416f78e3-dbf8-49f3-a2cb-2f4d5f4d7e87','NASA Data.json','339a8cb56dd85f77293b50bf2f4199a349187eeaf2ea45aecd547531f9c81a7e','1.1','2026-03-13T16:58:11.387005','2026-03-13T16:58:11.387009','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('7e36dff4-1d6c-435a-be22-3b9d95dbf202','HID Amendment','HID Amendment','public','2026-03-25T14:22:29.621549','2026-03-25T14:22:29.621556','data.austintexas.gov','Haileigh.Meyers@austintexas.gov',NULL,'be30d1c8-ac1d-47a9-ae5b-bb8e62ed32ca','City of Austin Data.json','c5f3c64921a342a8ec0c3eab3079b08c8fdfe70fa7374110e77424b4768d21f2','1.1','2026-03-25T14:22:29.621549','2026-03-25T14:22:29.621556',NULL,NULL,0,'city-of-austin'),('7e383d74-c99e-4359-8feb-9ac934399fd2','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P VIRTIS 3 EXTENSION 1 MTP025 V2.0','This release contains the calibrated data of the VIRTIS instrument on board of the spacecraft Rosetta. This volume contains data from the EXTENSION 1 MTP025 phase, which occurred from 2016-01-13 to 2016-02-10 when at the vicinity of comet 67P. This data set V2.0 supersedes V1.0. It includes major updates on the data and documentation.','public','2026-03-13T18:39:18.492603','2026-03-13T18:39:18.492609','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','a7031c06-3bed-4187-b950-ae4d707b0a1c','NASA Data.json','464c864dce557fda30e15fc2664edefdba971ac940cc154557163ddd990467d3','1.1','2026-03-13T18:39:18.492603','2026-03-13T18:39:18.492609','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('7e5be9f7-018d-4d40-8c4a-4626aa1a3353','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 4 1289 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 4 phase 2015-10-22 to 2015-12-31. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-12-26T17:28:35.000 to 2015-12-27T00:40:07.500.','public','2026-03-13T17:54:27.373438','2026-03-13T17:54:27.373444','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','06b89191-d273-48cb-a0a8-f3cb20ffc892','NASA Data.json','37c7e48cf9b2bf32d9f7c12bd40eeef48bced9e771f80c53c0e8319864254dff','1.1','2026-03-13T17:54:27.373438','2026-03-13T17:54:27.373444','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('7e7dcc59-105b-41c1-b847-a6e0907d78e6','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 4 1221 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 4 phase 2015-10-22 to 2015-12-31. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-11-29T06:25:35.000 to 2015-11-29T09:20:11.000.','public','2026-03-13T18:47:43.981332','2026-03-13T18:47:43.981337','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','c8277b7c-7762-4ae3-b3d9-20c2e8074afa','NASA Data.json','8fc56bb8047489ab21e45de689b431f3f31883e30b6383a780432984f0a36045','1.1','2026-03-13T18:47:43.981332','2026-03-13T18:47:43.981337','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('7e8448e7-78fd-47de-ab7f-b164958ac95e','MARS EXPRESS ASPERA-3 RAW EDR ELECTRON SPECTROMTR EXT3 V1.0','This data set contains Mars Express ASPERA-3 Electron         Spectrometer (ELS) data for the second mission extension         (January 1, 2010 - Dec. 31, 2012). These data are provided         in raw units of counts/accumulation.','public','2026-03-13T18:11:12.680134','2026-03-13T18:11:12.680141','planetary plasma interactions','Planetary Data System','026:00','5256b187-33cd-4212-a85e-c3e77228560d','NASA Data.json','76192165c23d4d66897a0858f68c8a845751e72ef239feed6069200adcba2ef1','1.1','2026-03-13T18:11:12.680134','2026-03-13T18:11:12.680141','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('7e99cbcd-9c8e-483d-ab28-3a2270b37b29','BLM Natl Recreation Site Points','This feature class represents the point features that show the physical locations of BLM National Recreation Sites. The general types of recreation point features targeted by this feature class include information center sites, water-based sites, overnight sites, day use sites, restrooms, water access, recreational access, parking areas, airplane landing strips, etc.\n\nThis dataset is based on an interim data standard and will be republished in the future.\n\nThis dataset is a subset of the official national dataset, containing features and attributes intended for public release and has been optimized for online map service performance. ','public','2026-03-18T11:13:57.371987','2026-03-18T11:13:57.371995','Bureau of Land Management','Bureau of Land Management, dbyrd','010:04','269d8f64-067f-4628-8d95-cd45c7910af9','DOI BLM DCAT-US','2cb03d30756b7be3ce65316ba21aef488dbb4c6d1d2e2d7f190ea3fa751bb292','1.1','2026-03-18T11:13:57.371987','2026-03-18T11:13:57.371995','geospatial','010:000',0,'doi-gov'),('7ea586ed-9ae9-4c98-a978-9739adaeeb0a','ROSETTA-ORBITER CAL ALICE 3 CR5 V1.0','This data set contains CODMAC level 3 data acquired by the Rosetta Orbiter ALICE UV Spectrometer during the Cruise 5 mission phase, which took place between 2009-12-14 and 2010-06-06, and includes Payload Checkout #12.','public','2026-03-13T17:24:41.697376','2026-03-13T17:24:41.697382','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','c113b726-3583-444b-8746-eb5d06cb9a46','NASA Data.json','d99585adda00c8768a9d09bafabf23e4968a8cceaab0d8ff23c7ff5143454473','1.1','2026-03-13T17:24:41.697376','2026-03-13T17:24:41.697382','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('7eebfd9b-16aa-4aba-993e-801fe6801183','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 2 0807 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 2 phase 2015-03-11 to 2015-06-30. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-05-25T12:03:05.000 to 2015-05-25T18:57:06.500.','public','2026-03-13T16:42:15.761224','2026-03-13T16:42:15.761231','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','a2b6e364-7df4-446c-b808-ee3aa33cfe78','NASA Data.json','727634825cc1bad727ffcc754503ed40220bb55fb36e5497bef09c26a56953f0','1.1','2026-03-13T16:42:15.761224','2026-03-13T16:42:15.761231','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('7eff68a9-8709-418a-9184-e7cac034fe04','Continuous Fixed Station Water Quality Measurements in Cape Lookout National Seashore, October 2008 (Certified)','This dataset represents continuous water quality measurements that were taken at a fixed point in Cape Lookout National Seashore during the month of October, 2008 as a part of the Fixed Station Water Quality Monitoring protocol that was developed by the Southeast Coast I&M Network (SECN). The measurements were taken by a YSI 6600 ESD Multi-Parameter Long Term Water Quality Monitoring Datasonde unit that serves as the standard fixed station water quality monitoring equipment for all similar operations conducted by the SECN. The following parameters were measured at 15 minute intervals during the time period that has been specified: Water Temperature, Specific Conductivity, Salinity, Dissolved Oxygen (DO), DO Concentration, Shallow Depth, pH Level, and Turbidity. Any anomalies noted regarding these parameters have also been noted in separate fields.  Please note that these measurements have been certified by network personnel.','public','2026-03-26T05:28:56.122751','2026-03-26T05:28:56.122756','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','8ee6e7c9-7c25-41fe-a6cf-a712a277e8a5','DOI NPS DCAT-US','5bf973cfe2b969776c77453d48c143329cefb15c41b29082391dbdd218b27e00','1.1','2026-03-26T05:28:56.122751','2026-03-26T05:28:56.122756','Vector Dataset','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('7f01fe8e-5dbb-4735-a44e-331487f42ba7','V-safe RSV for Pregnant Women','Users of the V-safe data are required to adhere to the following standards for the analysis and reporting of research data. All research results must be presented and/or published in a manner that protects the confidentiality of participants. V-safe data will not be presented and/or published in any way in which an individual can be identified. Therefore, users will:\n<ol>\n<li>Not attempt to link or permit others to link the data with individually identified records in another database.</li>\n<li>Not attempt to learn the identity of any participant in the data and will not deliberately combine these data with other CDC or non-CDC data for the purpose of matching records to identify individuals. If you should inadvertently discover the identity of any participant, you will ensure the identity of any participant is kept confidential, and will not be used in any publications and/or presentations.</li>\n<li>Not imply or state, either in written or oral form, that interpretations based on analysis of the data reflect official CDC policies or positions.</li>\n<li>Understand that sub-national analyses are not appropriate for this national sample and will not be conducted. </li>\n<li>Understand that V-safe is a voluntary self-enrollment program requiring smartphone access; therefore, information from V-safe might not be representative or generalizable to the US population.</li></ol>\nBy clicking on the weblink below to download and use these V-safe data, you signify your agreement to comply with the above-stated terms.\n\nV-safe is a voluntary U.S. active safety surveillance system established by CDC to characterize local and systemic side effects of new vaccines administered after U.S. authorization or licensure. V-safe participants are not a random sample of all vaccinated persons in the United States and data might not be generalizable to the full U.S. vaccinated population. Participants may have been more likely to complete surveys if experiencing symptoms post-vaccination. All V-safe measures are self-reported, therefore there may be some misclassification of outcomes, vaccine-related information, or demographics.\n\nMobile outages or technical malfunctions may have caused a small number of missing surveys or collection of incorrect survey type. Occasional system outages and attrition over time also contribute to incomplete reporting. \n\nV-safe RSV for Pregnant Women public data includes enrollment, vaccination information, and daily and weekly surveys collected from 11/28/2023 to 3/23/2025. Corresponding V-safe Registration public data (de-identified demographic data) can be downloaded at data.cdc.gov. Please review the V-safe data user agreement before analyzing any V-safe data.','public','2026-03-20T17:35:36.476043','2026-03-20T17:35:36.476048','Centers for Disease Control and Prevention','Vsafe@cdc.gov','009:20','a7e12243-3e9d-4962-aaed-310854fdbd97','Healthdata.gov','b61b41d0dccfcff7463b2de3741c70dad7fcd7e9fb1ed455fc9a30572912205f','1.1','2026-03-20T17:35:36.476043','2026-03-20T17:35:36.476048','National Center for Emerging and Zoonotic Infectious Diseases','009:028',0,'hhs-gov'),('7f022da7-43df-4838-a357-f65155d74c8b','MARS EXPRESS SUN MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 7 4053 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2019-01-01 to 2020-12-31. It is a Solar Conjunction measurement and covers the time 2019-09-08T04:52:56.000 to 2019-09-08T08:01:42.500.','public','2026-03-13T19:18:40.147239','2026-03-13T19:18:40.147245','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','fd59ddcb-eb2e-4d66-ac82-cf4fc5666e93','NASA Data.json','4381e8497a56db8f91b38842d3e297ff8003e956cfb9e64613fa4d21370fd64b','1.1','2026-03-13T19:18:40.147239','2026-03-13T19:18:40.147245','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('7f1331f7-3e8c-4bc3-8877-6831b17990f3','ROSETTA-ORBITER COMET ESCORT 4 OSINAC 2 EDR MTP023 V1.0','This data set contains images acquired by the OSIRIS Narrow Angle Camera during the COMET ESCORT 4 phase of the Rosetta mission at the comet 67P, covering the period from 2015-11-17T23:25:00.000 to 2015-12-15T23:24:59.000.','public','2026-03-13T17:34:04.223997','2026-03-13T17:34:04.224003','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','7593d94e-f955-42f5-b27f-5dfd7ad20abc','NASA Data.json','275964c9bdbd11d080df0b4530aa4a324c8cb104fa343feede4adfa0eed8ba4a','1.1','2026-03-13T17:34:04.223997','2026-03-13T17:34:04.224003','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('7f170dd3-efb8-4a0b-81ff-21495d237174','ROSETTA-ORBITER STEINS OSIWAC 4 AST1 RDR-STRLIGHT V1.0','This CODMAC level 4 data set contains solar stray light corrected, radiometric calibrated and geometric distortion corrected (resampled) image data in W/m^2/sr/nm,  acquired by the OSIRIS Wide Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft  during the STEINS FLY-BY mission phase, covering the period  from 2008-08-04T00:00:00.000 to 2008-10-05T23:59:59.000. The prime target is asteroid 2867 Steins. This version V1.0 is the first version of this dataset.','public','2026-03-13T17:55:53.906469','2026-03-13T17:55:53.906475','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','7362c4f8-f142-4824-a7c1-bf454d72bee7','NASA Data.json','e7adc92b437c9aa48a0db9b22030e563cea1b4ffe8dc2db84d4247931a49c5c6','1.1','2026-03-13T17:55:53.906469','2026-03-13T17:55:53.906475','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('7f2b5efe-3f7b-441d-a58c-7cac322ac314','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 PRELANDING 0232 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the PRELANDING phase 2014-01-21 to 2014-11-18. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2014-08-22T18:47:05.000 to 2014-08-23T00:05:34.000.','public','2026-03-13T18:49:22.832812','2026-03-13T18:49:22.832818','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','6bd70ae7-022f-4073-9987-889a7768af8f','NASA Data.json','9af3abbd1f372c3a9405a2b3356d5f6802cd6c148006b1f81fb5ea157c3a83bd','1.1','2026-03-13T18:49:22.832812','2026-03-13T18:49:22.832818','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('7f56ce22-24c3-447d-8402-7e7d71b25e8a','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSIWAC 5 ESC1-MTP011 DDR-GEO V1.0','This CODMAC level 5 data set contains derived data products that include pixel-precise georeferencing information, acquired by the OSIRIS Wide Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft during the COMET ESCORT 1 mission phase, covering the period from 2014-12-19T23:25:00.000 to 2015-01-13T23:24:59.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V1.0 is the first version of this dataset: Lien corrected dataset after October 2018 PSA/PDS external peer review.','public','2026-03-13T18:57:08.889519','2026-03-13T18:57:08.889525','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','83cca238-617a-43fa-a878-c82ab8f8b86b','NASA Data.json','d241667e41c0dc7fff37df77c53c530a6ae4f3288dd2a720b4600276f35f9c04','1.1','2026-03-13T18:57:08.889519','2026-03-13T18:57:08.889525','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('7f5d67b1-5089-4028-8e7d-454a75c496e2','2026 City of Austin Demographic Profiles','These are the data for the Demographic Profiles displayed on austintexas.gov/demographics. These profiles were published in 2026, but display data from 2024 and 2025.\n\nMost data are from the 2024 American Community Survey (the most recent available at the time of publication), but some data have other sources. All data come from the American Community Survey estimates except for:\n\nTotal Population - City of Austin Planning (2024) (City and Council Districts only)\nPopulation Low-Moderate Income - Dept. of Housing and Urban Development LMISD Summary Data (5 year 2016-2020)\nOccupied Housing Units - City of Austin Planning (2024) (City and Council Districts only)\nMedian Home Closing Price - Austin Board of Realtors (2025)\nAverage Monthly Rent - ApartmentTrends.com by Austin Investor Interests (Q4 2025)\nIncome Restricted Units - City of Austin Affordable Housing Inventory (February 2026)\nHousing Units - City of Austin Planning (2024)(City and Council Districts only)\nPopulation Density - Esri Updated Demographics (2025) (County, MSA, Council Districts)\nDaytime Population Density - Esri Updated Demographics (2025) (County, MSA, Council Districts)\nPopulation Density - Calculation derived from 2024 Population Estimates, City of Austin Demographics & Data Division (City only)\nDaytime Population Density - 2024 Population Estimates, City of Austin Demographics & Data Division (City only)\nSelected Land Use Percentages - City of Austin Land Use Inventory (2025)\nTransit Stops - Capital Metro (January 2026)\n\nCity, County, and MSA data are 1-Year ACS estimates. Council Districts are 5-year ACS estimates.\n\nSome datapoints may not be available for all geographies.\n\nMore information and links to these alternate sources, when available, can be found at austintexas.gov/demographics.\n\nThese profiles are updated annually.\n\nCity of Austin Open Data Terms of Use – https://data.austintexas.gov/stories/s/ranj-cccq','public','2026-03-25T14:18:05.734141','2026-03-25T14:18:05.734145','data.austintexas.gov','Austin Planning Owners',NULL,'8938717f-1ef3-4f19-acab-df66b9062802','City of Austin Data.json','5e3b6a798573c1bd1ec4569dbe7b2977a55864a88491aa75996bb7d5310f8ddd','1.1','2026-03-25T14:18:05.734141','2026-03-25T14:18:05.734145','City Government',NULL,0,'city-of-austin'),('7f723cc9-0850-461d-9d41-5e7ac86f6e29','EGIS - Enterprise Gateway Integration Services-VIBE Service','The Validation Instrument for Business Enterprises (VIBE) is a tool used to reduce benefits fraud on employment-based visas through verification of petitioner (company) information using an independent information broker.','non-public','2026-03-22T11:56:50.549025','2026-03-22T11:56:50.549029','Unspecified','Open Data (MGMT)','024:030','65b4f5a8-d431-440c-85ba-0721e454d2d4','DHS datajson source','e1dee057ae7ef3cafca7e4d4cd91506ba09d4400b1650b39aa4df553da244ce5','1.1','2026-03-22T11:56:50.549025','2026-03-22T11:56:50.549029',NULL,'024:000',0,'dhs-gov'),('7f73407c-2e01-4aef-a182-4f501f5eff26','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSIWAC 4 ESC3-MTP019 RDR V2.0','This CODMAC level 4 data set contains radiometric calibrated and geometric distortion corrected (resampled) image data in W/m^2/sr/nm, acquired by the OSIRIS Wide Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft during the COMET ESCORT 3 mission phase, covering the period from 2015-07-28T23:25:00.000 to 2015-08-25T23:24:59.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V2.0 supersedes previous deliveries of the same dataset with the following changes since the last version: Lien corrected dataset after October 2018 PSA/PDS external peer review. Updated documentation and ancillary files, added document on bandpass filter. Updated SCIENCE_USER_GUIDE_V03.PDF to include one section about FAQ and one section about image data quality. Added shutter backtravel and readout issues to image quality map. Updated DATA_QUALITY_ID keyword in image header. Improved handling of images with missing packets.','public','2026-03-13T18:58:17.887787','2026-03-13T18:58:17.887793','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','bd85c2fe-d277-485f-a43f-b5f273befe65','NASA Data.json','d46e93a7f2f7c4e37a4e317b9fe927fdbe94e47d0d1719e75b238192614e2ff5','1.1','2026-03-13T18:58:17.887787','2026-03-13T18:58:17.887793','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('8032c1de-bf14-4fce-a9d6-d41b4aad291e','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 3 0947 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 3 phase 2015-07-01 to 2015-10-21. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-08-06T21:29:30.000 to 2015-08-07T05:22:32.500.','public','2026-03-13T19:56:20.294837','2026-03-13T19:56:20.294843','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','d44696c5-1640-4354-ba23-87e37ffff856','NASA Data.json','4f8b5b81c16591a9dcfa54cb7233e2f7a58c4fd28b62f39e253b32bf8b674d18','1.1','2026-03-13T19:56:20.294837','2026-03-13T19:56:20.294843','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('806066e2-ce8e-43c7-883b-5383cfc74633','LP MOON MAG LEVEL 5 SURFACE MAGNETIC FIELD MAPS V1.0','Lunar Prospector magnetometer (MAG) Level 4 Data (CODMAC Level 5).Large-Scale Vector Field Maps at a Common Altitude of 37 km.The spatial resolution of the grid (0.25 x 0.25 degrees) is muchless than the mean S/C altitude.','public','2026-03-13T19:21:51.290907','2026-03-13T19:21:51.290912','planetary plasma interactions','Planetary Data System','026:00','0bdab9e4-1a69-4e1b-954e-607b78dea946','NASA Data.json','14bc6a00b66390b67d3f509cba2d30e96683ddfa5009653d92a919fa0b5cd782','1.1','2026-03-13T19:21:51.290907','2026-03-13T19:21:51.290912','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('806d3005-6bae-478f-8c41-8e1aa0a61ac8','Ecosys EcomapSubsections 2025','<DIV STYLE=\"text-align:Left;\"><DIV><P><SPAN>The Ecomap 2025 contains a feature class for five different levels of the National Hierarchical Framework of Ecological Units (the Hierarchy. FSM 2060): Ecological Domains, Ecological Divisions, Ecological Provinces, Ecological Sections, and Ecological Subsections. The Ecomap 2025 data set describes the ecological hierarchy within the conterminous United States. Each feature class contains polygons attributed with the code and name of the ecological unit along with the codes and names of broader scale units into which a given ecological unit is nested. It contains regional geographic delineations for analysis of ecological relationships across ecological units. ECOMAP is the term used for a USDA Forest Service initiative to map ecological units and encourage their use in ecosystem-based approaches to forest and range land conservation and management. This is a collaborative effort with many partners. It is coordinated at the national and regional levels by USDA Forest Service staff and implemented in cooperation with State forestry agencies and others. ECOMAP mapping criteria are outlined in the National Hierarchical Framework of Ecological Units (Cleland et al. 1997, FSM 2060). The framework systematically divides the country into progressively smaller areas that have similar geophysical and biological characteristics and ecological processes.</SPAN></P></DIV></DIV>','public','2026-03-13T22:49:35.130649','2026-03-13T22:49:35.130655','U.S. Forest Service','USFSEnterpriseContent','005:96','12f36e61-f792-4773-a941-2997e3bcdf2a','USDA JSON','0d2326f8147d5f95be0787d2c3d590c189ecc2fd54ef88a7fbcafb16cad10d45','1.1','2026-03-13T22:49:35.130649','2026-03-13T22:49:35.130655','geospatial','005:059',0,'usda-gov'),('80d5bfac-b0ef-45b2-b529-f9f2abbef103','V-safe RSV for Adults','Users of the V-safe data are required to adhere to the following standards for the analysis and reporting of research data. All research results must be presented and/or published in a manner that protects the confidentiality of participants. V-safe data will not be presented and/or published in any way in which an individual can be identified. Therefore, users will:<ol>\n<li>Not attempt to link or permit others to link the data with individually identified records in another database.\n<li>Not attempt to learn the identity of any participant in the data and will not deliberately combine these data with other CDC or non-CDC data for the purpose of matching records to identify individuals. If you should inadvertently discover the identity of any participant, you will ensure the identity of any participant is kept confidential, and will not be used in any publications and/or presentations.\n<li>Not imply or state, either in written or oral form, that interpretations based on analysis of the data reflect official CDC policies or positions.\n<li>Understand that sub-national analyses are not appropriate for this national sample and will not be conducted. \n<li>Understand that V-safe is a voluntary self-enrollment program requiring smartphone access; therefore, information from V-safe might not be representative or generalizable to the US population.</li></ol>\nBy clicking on the weblink below to download and use these V-safe data, you signify your agreement to comply with the above-stated terms.\n\nV-safe is a voluntary U.S. active safety surveillance system established by CDC to characterize local and systemic side effects of new vaccines administered after U.S. authorization or licensure. V-safe participants are not a random sample of all vaccinated persons in the United States and data might not be generalizable to the full U.S. vaccinated population. Participants may have been more likely to complete surveys if experiencing symptoms post-vaccination. All V-safe measures are self-reported, therefore there may be some misclassification of outcomes, vaccine-related information, or demographics.\n\nFor participants who requested corrections (i.e. vaccination date or vaccine manufacturer) to their vaccination record, data may be missing or incorrect for one or more doses. Requested corrections were applied to ‘Enrollment’ and ‘Vaccination’ files. The old vaccination records are located in the ‘Vaccination (Old Records)’ file while the corrected vaccine records are in the ‘Vaccination’ file. Mobile outages or technical malfunctions may have caused a small number of missing surveys or collection of incorrect survey type. Occasional system outages and attrition over time also contribute to incomplete reporting. \n\nV-safe RSV for Adults public data includes enrollment, vaccination information, and daily and weekly surveys collected from 10/20/2023 to 3/23/2025. Corresponding V-safe Registration public data (de-identified demographic data) can be downloaded at data.cdc.gov. Please review the V-safe data user agreement before analyzing any V-safe data.','public','2026-03-20T17:38:25.112763','2026-03-20T17:38:25.112770','Centers for Disease Control and Prevention','Vsafe@cdc.gov','009:20','e616423c-e3cc-4818-9af6-ba19814f62cb','Healthdata.gov','b1c35132a92be4a83780deba6ba141241ca5a99b054990e7b063fa37330cd4b4','1.1','2026-03-20T17:38:25.112763','2026-03-20T17:38:25.112770','National Center for Emerging and Zoonotic Infectious Diseases','009:028',0,'hhs-gov'),('8100999e-acf7-4136-85d1-bddff944f546','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RPCLAP 2 ESC3 MTP018 V1.0','This dataset contains EDITED data from Rosetta RPC-LAP, acquired during MTP18, part of the COMET ESCORT 3 mission phase. Primary target was comet 67P/C-G.','public','2026-03-13T18:51:32.238602','2026-03-13T18:51:32.238608','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','c36a8dc3-d828-422c-96bb-2a47a74e0034','NASA Data.json','eb41a538d573004d25d62e10f24dc7c7a8f828a76cbd0efcc417cffec994f566','1.1','2026-03-13T18:51:32.238602','2026-03-13T18:51:32.238608','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('8104c1d7-5ac8-400f-ab94-60f76fccc865','BLM CO Oil and Gas Lease Sale Q3 (September) 2026','This data set consists of digital mapping data describing polygon geometry and linked attribute data for BLM Colorado\'s Quarterly Oil and Gas Lease Sale Parcels in the State of Colorado, BLM. The polygons in this data set were generated using the legal land descriptions of the identified Oil and Gas Lease Sale parcels and the Geographic Coordinate Data Base (GCDB) survey grid to produce a mapped layer. Mapped parcels should be checked against the legal land description for the sale parcels in the sale notice to verify and validate data. These data are consolidated from field office inputs.','public','2026-03-14T10:00:20.041305','2026-03-25T12:33:36.243418','Bureau of Land Management','Bureau of Land Management, blm_co_info','010:04','b8952832-1d6d-4770-8067-67f3474301b2','DOI BLM DCAT-US','646be4cc5ba0bcad7d83ea00337f1292c439455d03351885359a056ed6e50ce3','1.1','2026-03-14T10:00:20.041305','2026-03-25T12:33:36.243418','geospatial','010:000',0,'doi-gov'),('811f390c-0d82-49e7-a0d9-a87aabae9be1','Iowa Licensed Occupations','Data designed to provide job seekers, career counselors, and other interested individuals with information concerning occupations in Iowa that require a license, certificate or commission issued at the State level.','public','2026-03-28T22:00:19.472781','2026-03-28T22:00:19.472787','data.iowa.gov','Katie Green',NULL,'6551a310-70aa-4508-bbd2-10a556338f43','Iowa metadata','b7937e1ef27eadcb744289626e9f3edb50700f8bf0d68c5e7fea8ea237af12ee','1.1','2026-03-28T22:00:19.472781','2026-03-28T22:00:19.472787','Workforce',NULL,0,'state-of-iowa'),('8136a78f-162b-49e1-b6c0-42b352b3b706','Life history diversity of Oncorhynchus mykiss in the Elwha River during and fallowing dam removal','Data for the paper published by Frontiers in Ecology and Evolution special issue on intensively monitored watersheds','public','2026-03-13T22:36:20.154728','2026-03-13T22:36:20.154734','U.S. Fish and Wildlife Service','Todd Sutherland','010:18','929f05a0-5275-476f-9c1d-8cb822e649e9','DOI FWS DCAT-US','e00c44d350f9ed6c53ec756c3694f46ff321446d4321cf2053ee896e0efef3da','1.1','2026-03-13T22:36:20.154728','2026-03-13T22:36:20.154734','Tabular Dataset','010:028',0,'doi-gov'),('813b40d8-5891-43bb-bf9c-4cc1f4dbfc70','Continuous Fixed Station Water Quality Measurements in Cape Lookout National Seashore, October 2009 (Certified)','This dataset represents continuous water quality measurements that were taken at a fixed point in Cape Lookout National Seashore during the month of October, 2009 as a part of the Fixed Station Water Quality Monitoring protocol that was developed by the Southeast Coast I&M Network (SECN). The measurements were taken by a YSI 6600 ESD Multi-Parameter Long Term Water Quality Monitoring Datasonde unit that serves as the standard fixed station water quality monitoring equipment for all similar operations conducted by the SECN. The following parameters were measured at 15 minute intervals during the time period that has been specified: Water Temperature, Specific Conductivity, Salinity, Dissolved Oxygen (DO), DO Concentration, Shallow Depth, pH Level, and Turbidity. Any anomalies noted regarding these parameters have also been noted in separate fields.  Please note that these measurements have been certified by network personnel.','public','2026-03-26T05:27:48.101050','2026-03-26T05:27:48.101056','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','f0728fa7-3be2-4cae-8530-524de45d77c1','DOI NPS DCAT-US','3f400fbc7576ace4b3c75f497e68fb1822ef1c2dc0f64b935fa5b361253c2c74','1.1','2026-03-26T05:27:48.101050','2026-03-26T05:27:48.101056','Vector Dataset','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('81769b27-4895-4c37-b40b-c0a762803ad2','GALILEO ORBITER EARTH MAG SUMM EARTH2 SUMMARY V1.0','Galileo Orbiter Magnetometer (MAG) calibrated 20             second averaged data from the Earth-2 flyby in             spacecraft, GSE, and GSM coordinates. These data             cover the interval 1992-11-03 to 1992-12-19.','public','2026-03-13T17:22:28.810115','2026-03-13T17:22:28.810122','planetary plasma interactions','Planetary Data System','026:00','63400f77-2fae-4a8f-a60e-4bae8ab3868b','NASA Data.json','946dfbf91256e31140dcc4129cc694bed384baeb9a18d9c7d57f35abbb0b6305','1.1','2026-03-13T17:22:28.810115','2026-03-13T17:22:28.810122','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('820bd422-124f-4bb6-970c-162109216876','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 2 0854 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 2 phase 2015-03-11 to 2015-06-30. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-06-22T21:05:55.000 to 2015-06-23T04:20:23.000.','public','2026-03-13T18:34:46.267139','2026-03-13T18:34:46.267145','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','bec0b6e0-1f22-4575-86ae-1ad1e69a1c9d','NASA Data.json','8625585c137fae71ca7ba506bf47c11e5c3db14d169ac6d4b5d5b52ab615817a','1.1','2026-03-13T18:34:46.267139','2026-03-13T18:34:46.267145','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('82616126-522e-4697-b181-cd3343e1a48b','ROSETTA-ORBITER CHECK MIDAS 3 EAR1 PC0 V3.0','The Micro-Imaging Dust Analysis System (MIDAS) is an instrument on theROSETTA Orbiter that will provide 3D images and statistical parametersof pristine cometary particles, collected in the vicinity of comet67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko. This data set includes all data from theEARTH SWING-BY 1 mission phase.This release supersedes version 1.0. Version 2.0 was never generatedfor pre-comet phases.','public','2026-03-13T17:41:35.945253','2026-03-13T17:41:35.945261','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','59745327-9298-476d-8544-746eb2af5ba1','NASA Data.json','b8e4abe7c9a364be2b8c56d54ed70129c81f66490b8f6d60feffa90b1d91aa3e','1.1','2026-03-13T17:41:35.945253','2026-03-13T17:41:35.945261','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('8280c3e1-eade-4206-9de7-69ca7bb09721','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSINAC 2 ESC4-MTP024 EDR V3.0','This CODMAC level 2 data set contains uncalibrated image data in DN unit, acquired by the OSIRIS Narrow Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft during the COMET ESCORT 4 mission phase, covering the period from 2015-12-15T23:25:00.000 to 2016-01-12T23:24:59.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V3.0 supersedes previous deliveries of the same dataset with the following changes since the last version: Lien corrected dataset after the July and October 2018 PSA/PDS external peer reviews. Updated documentation and ancillary files, added document on bandpass filter. Updated SCIENCE_USER_GUIDE_V03.PDF to include one section about FAQ and one section about image data quality. Added shutter backtravel and readout issues to image quality map. Updated DATA_QUALITY_ID keyword in image header. Improved handling of images with missing packets. Included FITs files. Browse products changed to the same size as the original image.','public','2026-03-13T17:12:12.071345','2026-03-13T17:12:12.071351','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','d3426c66-c190-4c66-8773-11dfbf2c392c','NASA Data.json','fa009bbd13c678b9f6d70e421bc5413486825cc89eaa4a2ab47f08f5f70bc5e8','1.1','2026-03-13T17:12:12.071345','2026-03-13T17:12:12.071351','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('82a1a186-1e6e-48bf-bad7-462dcb63eef1','BLM ID CADNSDI PLSS Metadata Glance','This is a graphic representation of the data stewards based on PLSS Townships in PLSS areas. In non-PLSS areas the metadata at a glance is based on a data steward defined polygons such as a city or county or other units. The identification of the data steward is a general indication of the agency that will be responsible for updates and providing the authoritative data sources. In other implementations this may have been termed the alternate source, meaning alternate to the BLM. But in the shared environment of the NSDI the data steward for an area is the primary coordinator or agency responsible for making updates or causing updates to be made. The data stewardship polygons are defined and provided by the data steward. For more information contact us at blm_id_stateoffice@blm.gov.','public','2026-03-19T11:32:52.778951','2026-03-19T11:32:52.778957','Bureau of Land Management','Bureau of Land Management, blm_id_infoaccesscenter','010:04','19f98b7c-3a99-4325-a2e4-ce0cdf594fa6','DOI BLM DCAT-US','2ae131fa5f525a7d0c525897148155d3777386b22213b4b68697551e02a28a60','1.1','2026-03-19T11:32:52.778951','2026-03-19T11:32:52.778957','geospatial','010:000',0,'doi-gov'),('82b9ecac-7ec2-42d2-9890-daa98c54373e','NEW HORIZONS  MVIC PLUTO ENCOUNTER  RAW V1.0','This data set contains Raw data taken by the New Horizons  Multispectral Visible Imaging Camera  instrument during the  Pluto encounter  mission phase. This is VERSION 1.0 of this data set.','public','2026-03-13T16:38:10.736762','2026-03-13T16:38:10.736767','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','03b4b04e-74cb-4141-96e0-39380eeef479','NASA Data.json','cb5d2a87ce74e9e8407795b25dc4b08ff52d5283bf3b9572f1562758f1b223c9','1.1','2026-03-13T16:38:10.736762','2026-03-13T16:38:10.736767','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('83027d61-190f-4ff0-bb51-1f585b9dcbff','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RPCICA 2 ESC3 UNCALIBRATED V3.0','This dataset contains RAW DATA from the RPCICA instrument onmission ROSETTA during Comet escort 3.Data contains measurements of solar wind interactionwith the atmosphere of target comet 67P. Data set version 3 replaces a previously delivered data set.Important changes are the the expansion of data to a uniform resolution,Inclusion of the mode variable and new quality flags in the data andmoving information about software version, BAD_HV_MASK and SHADOW_MASKto the label.','public','2026-03-13T19:52:04.212026','2026-03-13T19:52:04.212034','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','ba722af8-9e4c-49aa-9adf-9fa95fc06166','NASA Data.json','fc0e480033a90432481e380998e2dedcf5a063da40516212f0dd1496a2a69af1','1.1','2026-03-13T19:52:04.212026','2026-03-13T19:52:04.212034','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('8317e5d3-4143-4c19-ac20-20de01c396e3','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 PRELANDING 0298 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the PRELANDING phase 2014-01-21 to 2014-11-18. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2014-09-16T17:05:04.000 to 2014-09-16T23:25:10.500.','public','2026-03-13T18:15:37.494571','2026-03-13T18:15:37.494576','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','bf640d9f-2c16-4ac2-bd39-c9751ebeb24e','NASA Data.json','b9044e9d087966c05b10219bcedb1d01c2202d119c7f059e6513df9c24d5b314','1.1','2026-03-13T18:15:37.494571','2026-03-13T18:15:37.494576','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('83445544-5fcd-4ad0-8c2c-d721574f7612','MARS EXPRESS PHOBOS MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 4 3648 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2013-01-01 to 2014-12-31. It is a Phobos Gravity measurement and covers the time 2013-12-29T01:30:06 to 2013-12-29T11:25:56.000.','public','2026-03-13T19:33:11.607365','2026-03-13T19:33:11.607372','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','7cbffcee-f66b-4df9-b957-3457372340db','NASA Data.json','2a822b356745654fd8c3778e2cfd720450207e591e9fb6067a228e74f11fd29e','1.1','2026-03-13T19:33:11.607365','2026-03-13T19:33:11.607372','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('834bdcbd-7eb8-4e09-abc5-9267529fe95c','MARS EXPRESS SUN MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 5 3754 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2015-01-01 to 2016-12-31. It is a Solar Conjunction measurement and covers the time 2015-06-03T21:53:01 to 2015-06-04T02:09:00.','public','2026-03-13T19:06:47.182783','2026-03-13T19:06:47.182792','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','8f526663-f2db-432a-be36-e0f829eec97f','NASA Data.json','c930758aaf4561438294f71ec4a755a541ba83aaa64344865425448af37a384f','1.1','2026-03-13T19:06:47.182783','2026-03-13T19:06:47.182792','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('839385b5-c29f-4cbf-afd7-ed0cb4a732fb','National Coral Reef Monitoring Program: Benthic Images Collected from Climate Stations across the Hawaiian Archipelago since 2013','Photoquadrat benthic images were collected at NCRMP climate stations and permanent sites identified by the Ocean and Climate Change team across the Hawaiian archipelago since 2013 according to protocols established by the Coral Reef Ecosystem Program (CREP), now know as the Ecosystem Sciences Division (ESD), and the NOAA National Coral Reef Monitoring Program (NCRMP). The imagery allows for a quantitative analysis using image analysis software to derive an estimate of benthic percent cover.\n\nClimate stations are 3-4 sites per island that were selected in a stratified random fashion to be roughly equally spaced around the island, along the 15 m contour, on hard bottom, and at least 1 km away from a river mouth or embayment. Once selected we assess multiple features of the coral reef environment including in-situ temperature (STR), seawater carbonate, net carbonate accretion (CAU), and bioerosion (BMU). In 2013 and 2016, cryptobiota diversity (ARMS) was also assessed.\n\nThese data can be accessed online via the NOAA National Centers for Environmental Information (NCEI) Ocean Archive.','public','2026-03-21T23:13:24.078127','2026-03-21T23:13:24.078133',NULL,NULL,NULL,'81ff037f-ca03-4a47-b0f6-027b9eee743b','NMFS PIFSC',NULL,NULL,'2026-03-21T23:13:24.078127','2026-03-21T23:13:24.078133',NULL,NULL,NULL,'noaa-gov'),('83a10cfc-71f2-452e-83d4-5ccd4cf912bc','ROSETTA-LANDER CAL SESAME 3 PDCS V1.0','This archive contains calibrated data (CODMAC level 3) from the SESAME instrument onboard ROSETTA Lander, acquired during the PDCS phase. It also contains documentation which describes the SESAME experiment. The data archived in this data set conform to the Planetary Data System (PDS) Standards, Version 3.6.','public','2026-03-13T19:50:31.515092','2026-03-13T19:50:31.515099','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','91cd8aa9-effa-46bd-9aa9-ce46295ed673','NASA Data.json','82f8bb7a3c0c3ccab221d8403b81fc62acabf900c10d3fd4eea24f93470b4b77','1.1','2026-03-13T19:50:31.515092','2026-03-13T19:50:31.515099','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('83d29836-579f-4675-b6cc-0aff4921cae6','VG1 J PLASMA WAVE SPECTROMETER DENSITY 1S V1.0','Electron plasma density data set      for Jupiter\'s outer magnetosphere derived from high-resolution      wideband measurements of low-frequency radio and plasma waves      obtained by Voyagers 1 and 2 during their 1979 flybys.  Density      data were measured at 1-second intervals.','public','2026-03-13T22:35:58.070783','2026-03-13T22:35:58.070790','planetary plasma interactions','Planetary Data System','026:00','f3e6643a-4136-44ac-b878-323e1b089875','NASA Data.json','e72c8bb451eea0a022781b6e927bfbe5d7dbff71bd3fa342018b8556a47f6442','1.1','2026-03-13T22:35:58.070783','2026-03-13T22:35:58.070790','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('83ddd306-ab3a-40a4-b625-c365056ede94','ROSETTA-ORBITER STEINSRPCLAP 2 AST1 EDITED2 V1.0','This data set contains EDITEDdata from Rosetta RPC-LAP, acquired during the STEINS FLY-BY missionphase where the primary target was the asteroid 2867 STEINS. It containsuncalibrated raw data, i.e. the digital output of the instrument.','public','2026-03-13T20:04:21.526889','2026-03-13T20:04:21.526895','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','f55fa3b1-2f30-4048-906c-ea5bd2d7703f','NASA Data.json','58644275c7208edd8e7b876857d00f6ad02f2690fc443df043754848dab9dbe1','1.1','2026-03-13T20:04:21.526889','2026-03-13T20:04:21.526895','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('84094fc9-6516-4b70-ac67-c85b26fefd0a','MESSENGER E/V/H/SW EPPS CALIBRATED EPS DDR V1.0','Abstract    ========      This data set consists of the MESSENGER Energetic Particle and      Plasma Spectrometer (EPPS) advanced data products, also known      as DDR/DAPs. The system encompasses 2 instrument subsystems - the      Energetic Particle Spectrometer (EPS) and the Fast Imaging Plasma      Spectrometer (FIPS). This data set contains EPS instrument data.      EPS covers the energy range of 25 to > 500 keV for electrons, and      10 keV/nucleon to ~3 MeV total energy for ions. There is one      DDR data product for EPS','public','2026-03-13T18:16:33.895168','2026-03-13T18:16:33.895174','planetary plasma interactions','Planetary Data System','026:00','b898e319-21ab-4c73-adb2-827e22733570','NASA Data.json','a0aa79b970178ca98b4ba2d87c08dfd9f44a033c198ad555ef8fab86d904547e','1.1','2026-03-13T18:16:33.895168','2026-03-13T18:16:33.895174','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('840d1ddd-65ab-4f7a-9876-c1bee666ad13','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P COSIMA 3 V1.0','The Rosetta COSIMA data contains the operational history of the 72 dust collecting substrates from the installation inside the instrument. The operations are either spectra, total intensity, heating, imaging or grain lists. The data is grouped by the substrate and time. Up to the 2014-08 the aim of the data has been the instrument calibration and operational functionality, not statistically good substrate background spectra. From 2014-08 onward the D0 substrate set was used to collect dust taken in the vicinity of 67P/CHURYUMOV GERASIMENKO 1 (1969 R1) and dust analysis with SIMS. From 2014-10-23 onward due to an instrument effect, the SIMS data became scientifically unusable. This data set supersedes RO-CAL-COSIMA-3-V3.0.','public','2026-03-13T17:05:19.486094','2026-03-13T17:05:19.486100','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','9a4fb452-a89d-4002-b330-aa42cdd9f353','NASA Data.json','e150bde9180a6e90d3aa74c11221e153096fde873442d4bb74600340056452c8','1.1','2026-03-13T17:05:19.486094','2026-03-13T17:05:19.486100','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('84300012-afaf-4d9e-a979-d7e6142c2d1c','Hydrographic and Impairment Statistics Database: MAPR','Hydrographic and Impairment Statistics (HIS) is a National Park Service (NPS) Water Resources Division (WRD) project established to track certain goals created in response to the Government Performance and Results Act of 1993 (GPRA). One water resources management goal established by the Department of the Interior under GRPA requires NPS to track the percent of its managed surface waters that are meeting Clean Water Act (CWA) water quality standards. This goal requires an accurate inventory that spatially quantifies the surface water hydrography that each bureau manages and a procedure to determine and track which waterbodies are or are not meeting water quality standards as outlined by Section 303(d) of the CWA. This project helps meet this DOI GRPA goal by inventorying and monitoring in a geographic information system for the NPS: (1) CWA 303(d) quality impaired waters and causes; and (2) hydrographic statistics based on the United States Geological Survey (USGS) National Hydrography Dataset (NHD). Hydrographic and 303(d) impairment statistics were evaluated based on a combination of 1:24,000 (NHD) and finer scale data (frequently provided by state GIS layers).','public','2026-03-29T06:06:52.681629','2026-03-29T06:06:52.681634','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','cf7a1728-03af-4e1e-80cd-f5b50b23664b','DOI NPS DCAT-US','e2827d6f24df365bb79efdff52ce9383a944bef7d536ab594e1effda07edf964','1.1','2026-03-29T06:06:52.681629','2026-03-29T06:06:52.681634','geospatial','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('84463f84-9ad0-411d-8e85-5c95d0a839df','GO JUP SSD DERIVED ELECTRON FLUX V1.0','The Galileo star scanner is providing data on the instantaneous      flux of 1.5 to 30 MeV electrons in the Jovian environment. It is      able to measure fluxes of ~1 x 105 electrons cm-2 sec-1 or greater      which generally means the data are usable inside of about 12 and      rarely as far out as 16.5 Jovian Radii (RJ). Typically, the data      points are spaced about 400 or 80 seconds apart with infrequent      periods of more rapid data depending upon the operational mode.      It should be noted that data are generally accurate in time to      only within 20 seconds without special processing. Pitch angle      information generally cannot be extracted from this data set.      Separate files exist for the Jovian insertion event (J0) and      all subsequent perijove passes except J5 which occurred during      a period of solar conjunction.','public','2026-03-13T19:57:29.651726','2026-03-13T19:57:29.651733','planetary plasma interactions','Planetary Data System','026:00','5cd93f10-6dcf-4ceb-81c1-1ad2c8bb07c8','NASA Data.json','a476436b219101671d5561e20e7dd5d2c47fd44ee0c6b8f9ae3d6b1b48f366d5','1.1','2026-03-13T19:57:29.651726','2026-03-13T19:57:29.651733','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('847acf0f-6a15-4d7a-907b-8c78c6a89867','Laborshed - Occupational Reports Map','Laborshed dataset containing occupational reports data that feeds into the map seen in the occupational reports dashboard. This dataset covers the counts of each occupation within each laborshed area across Iowa.','public','2026-03-28T21:58:12.498212','2026-03-28T21:58:12.498217','data.iowa.gov','svqueen',NULL,'f142bec7-2662-46ec-a1a0-53eccceb0a2f','Iowa metadata','78d9b685a5b7ca6c78e377405b3f5a7d20b455d545bee9927466ebd05f317772','1.1','2026-03-28T21:58:12.498212','2026-03-28T21:58:12.498217','Economic Statistics',NULL,0,'state-of-iowa'),('848905e6-68ba-48dc-ba5e-c68ce6713e39','NIMS SPECTRAL IMAGE TUBES OF VENUS','Unknown','public','2026-03-13T19:52:48.892471','2026-03-13T19:52:48.892477','Imaging','Planetary Data System','026:00','8ace30a1-21c4-4f07-8247-14b3ab3a84a1','NASA Data.json','106926a604ab1c09c5294c5c9731aa0b8c85f05330da7cc6fafd6b6fba461a1d','1.1','2026-03-13T19:52:48.892471','2026-03-13T19:52:48.892477','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('84ad08c0-fbc8-4d4a-a233-19a544c12dc5','Okeanos Explorer (EX1709): Eastern Pacific Mapping							(Telepresence Mapping)','Operations for this cruise will include 24 hour mapping, and\n					continuous telepresence-based remote participation in mapping operations.\n					Multibeam and splitbeam mapping operations will be conducted 24 hours a day\n					throughout the cruise, except during CTD operations. Sub-bottom profile mapping\n					will be conducted 24 hours a day at the discretion of the CO. XBT and Underway\n					CTD sound velocity casts in support of multibeam sonar mapping operations will\n					be conducted at an interval defined by prevailing oceanographic conditions, but\n					not to exceed 6 hours.','public','2026-03-28T23:16:55.314650','2026-03-28T23:16:55.314655',NULL,NULL,NULL,'f6f60a82-dee0-4097-baf0-f3590bbe09d9','NCDDC OER',NULL,NULL,'2026-03-28T23:16:55.314650','2026-03-28T23:16:55.314655',NULL,NULL,NULL,'noaa-gov'),('852aeee6-5b9b-47cc-9cea-44698c6fdce6','NEW HORIZONS SDC KEM1 RAW V6.0','This data set contains Raw data taken by the New Horizons Student Dust Counter instrument during the KEM1 ENCOUNTER mission phase. This is VERSION 6.0 of this data set. This version includes data acquired by the spacecraft between 08/14/2018 and 04/30/2022. It only includes data downlinked before 05/01/2022. Future datasets may include more data acquired by the spacecraft after 08/13/2018 but downlinked after 04/30/2022. This version includes Dust Counts from prior to, during, and after the Arrokoth Encounter.','public','2026-03-13T19:22:08.208346','2026-03-13T19:22:08.208353','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','b31b1b76-cdc4-4af0-a2e1-3e7baf1b61ed','NASA Data.json','66b5bd6e11efa2433caca580cfaf8cfda4bd98df7589dfb133b7431609275314','1.1','2026-03-13T19:22:08.208346','2026-03-13T19:22:08.208353','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('8535ae7c-2646-490f-b37e-521bd5b040cc','MESSENGER E/V/H MASCS 5 VIRS DERIVED ANALYSIS DATA V1.0','Abstract : This data set consists of the MESSENGER MASCS VIRS derived analysis product, also known as the DAP. The DAP is a 500 meter  per pixel mosaic map of 1 wavelength (750 nm) of VIRS spectral  data for footprints covering the planet Mercury. Data products  are derived from science data collected by the VIRS detector  during orbital operations of Mercury.','public','2026-03-13T18:20:45.293247','2026-03-13T18:20:45.293253','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','696cf7a1-34fe-4cd6-a402-b1f0a157c281','NASA Data.json','003d8eca91f509c42a567f5d274f5f306e2904583fa685773df0758f1708da4c','1.1','2026-03-13T18:20:45.293247','2026-03-13T18:20:45.293253','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('85392377-a8d3-43d2-a8b5-06fd52b08fab','VOYAGER 2 DAILY POSITION V1.0','This dataset contains Voyager 2 trajecotyr data from the      interplanetary cruise sampled daily in Solar Ecliptic and Heliographic      coordinates.','public','2026-03-13T18:18:21.823730','2026-03-13T18:18:21.823737','planetary plasma interactions','Planetary Data System','026:00','6e858aa1-bfe5-46fe-8f00-364090802334','NASA Data.json','1c6f200827eb0dea40da231a45d046215abee272915080385f1f082ff674936c','1.1','2026-03-13T18:18:21.823730','2026-03-13T18:18:21.823737','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('8548cc79-e3dd-4a02-af26-839b46145829','Long-Term Industry Projections','Industry projections estimate the future performance and trends of industries over a defined period. These are 10-year projections for the State of Iowa and its six local workforce development areas (LWDA). Projections are are based on a combination of historical data, market analysis, economic indicators, and emerging trends.','public','2026-03-28T22:00:05.628209','2026-03-28T22:00:05.628213','data.iowa.gov','Katie Green',NULL,'ea6dbe5f-f654-419f-8d04-af78b9dbcb26','Iowa metadata','81607c28cac73e5c8c3ec78141c29e146b43c5e37ff00d28ac1f8032c1c8fbcd','1.1','2026-03-28T22:00:05.628209','2026-03-28T22:00:05.628213','Workforce',NULL,0,'state-of-iowa'),('85cfcd0d-5ce5-4e5c-a7ad-283d20105c0b','Land Acquisition Revolving Loan Program Recipient List','Organizations that received funding from the Land Acquisition Revolving Loan Program (LAP), a funding program administered by the Oregon Housing and Community Services','public','2026-03-22T03:19:28.748981','2026-03-22T03:19:28.748986','data.oregon.gov','Fiona Bai',NULL,'62dd34a2-7169-4896-8c8b-939eed9855f8','oregon json','39f1715bf5c378fbdecd22e8ff0121b978885513bad5e4d58d946bdb832c9b17','1.1','2026-03-22T03:19:28.748981','2026-03-22T03:19:28.748986',NULL,NULL,0,'state-of-oregon'),('85fb315a-399a-44ec-aa29-69b72cbc2c2c','DID(IT) - Scheduler: Personnel Check in and Check out Data','Personnel check in and check out from their work locations','non-public','2026-03-22T11:55:51.416861','2026-03-22T11:55:51.416866','Unspecified','Open Data (MGMT)','024:030','72e87e16-fb04-4d18-b4dd-fc90d9510d79','DHS datajson source','599bc35f071c82c7d9b8814cf474af71e880cdb68031766c499ab740a15ac07c','1.1','2026-03-22T11:55:51.416861','2026-03-22T11:55:51.416866',NULL,'024:000',0,'dhs-gov'),('860bb4a7-c97b-4296-b630-a1c6a6e96128','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 4 1296 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 4 phase 2015-10-22 to 2015-12-31. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-12-29T22:09:40.000 to 2015-12-30T00:16:04.000.','public','2026-03-13T19:08:35.726688','2026-03-13T19:08:35.726693','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','dfa6a6af-12dd-4298-839f-0390f265f59b','NASA Data.json','e8e322ad7efd115fb778e1fd6fb6862fbde7decbc0979c073f103358b6db1f85','1.1','2026-03-13T19:08:35.726688','2026-03-13T19:08:35.726693','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('861d0d7f-36c3-4119-b91b-eb9a53533548','GO E PWS RESAMP SUMMARY EARTH 1 SPECTRUM ANALYZER 60S V1.0','This data set includes 1-minute averages of the electric and magnetic    wave spectra obtained during the period that the Galileo plasma wave    receiver was operated during the first flyby of Earth.  The parameter    provided for the electric field spectrum is the electric field spectral    density in units of V^2/m^2/Hz. The magnetic field spectrum is provided    in units of magnetic field spectral density, nT^2/Hz.','public','2026-03-13T18:15:23.883235','2026-03-13T18:15:23.883242','planetary plasma interactions','Planetary Data System','026:00','772d34ba-af17-4b8f-a459-c2b7a27ff30b','NASA Data.json','40030da6c65eae823945dc067cbc2bf8a035c9e4868851ee379fb3936bbabfa8','1.1','2026-03-13T18:15:23.883235','2026-03-13T18:15:23.883242','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('86412523-b3dd-4480-a7be-b6c2dc0b6388','Continuous Fixed Station Water Quality Measurements in Canaveral National Seashore, March 2007 (Certified)','This dataset represents continuous water quality measurements that were taken at a fixed point in Canaveral National Seashore during the month of March, 2007 as a part of the Fixed Station Water Quality Monitoring protocol that was developed by the Southeast Coast I&M Network (SECN). The measurements were taken by a YSI 6600 ESD Multi-Parameter Long Term Water Quality Monitoring Datasonde unit that serves as the standard fixed station water quality monitoring equipment for all similar operations conducted by the SECN. The following parameters were measured at 30 minute intervals during the time period that has been specified: Water Temperature, Specific Conductivity, Salinity, Dissolved Oxygen (DO), DO Concentration, Shallow Depth, pH Level, and Turbidity. Any anomalies noted regarding these parameters have also been noted in separate fields. Please note that these measurements have been certified by network personnel.','public','2026-03-26T05:31:07.753859','2026-03-26T05:31:07.753866','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','fef09111-06ba-4fbc-be78-3e5da2634c49','DOI NPS DCAT-US','d16907a6a819e106c17dbed6f2f95c39d2a31a4af77960139c7745dab4dd9349','1.1','2026-03-26T05:31:07.753859','2026-03-26T05:31:07.753866','Vector Dataset','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('8667b2c4-0190-491d-8b01-a66f50d2b028','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P NAVCAM 2 ROSETTA EXTENSION 1 MTP025 V1.0','This dataset contains ROSETTA NAVCAM RAW DATA of the Extension 1 from 12th Jan 2016 to 9th Feb 2016 when at the vicinity of target 67P/CG.','public','2026-03-13T17:52:18.525667','2026-03-13T17:52:18.525673','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','fb605d0d-8e12-4875-8eb5-92b156092129','NASA Data.json','9c0945ba1da92a4772a2c59572be8ffac96e5fa5b204a6c32b8d76fd92941f7c','1.1','2026-03-13T17:52:18.525667','2026-03-13T17:52:18.525673','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('8667bd75-9079-4ead-8fa1-f158858a7725','Continuous Fixed Station Water Quality Measurements in Timucuan Ecological and Historic Preserve, April 2008 (Certified)','This dataset represents continuous water quality measurements that were taken at a fixed point in Timucuan Ecological and Historic Preserve during the month of April, 2008 as a part of the Fixed Station Water Quality Monitoring protocol that was developed by the Southeast Coast I&M Network (SECN). The measurements were taken by a YSI 6600 ESD Multi-Parameter Long Term Water Quality Monitoring Datasonde unit that serves as the standard fixed station water quality monitoring equipment for all similar operations conducted by the SECN. The following parameters were measured at 30 minute intervals during the time period that has been specified: Water Temperature, Specific Conductivity, Salinity, Dissolved Oxygen (DO), DO Concentration, Shallow Depth, pH Level, and Turbidity. Any anomalies noted regarding these parameters have also been noted in separate fields. Please note that these measurements have been certified by network personnel.','public','2026-03-26T05:29:41.246788','2026-03-26T05:29:41.246793','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','4e42a1ac-16b5-43f2-a6f9-1463c59d32c9','DOI NPS DCAT-US','332b4064a3a320fc9903df69d636828a927b5b79a8579dd44b972ad9e72830e6','1.1','2026-03-26T05:29:41.246788','2026-03-26T05:29:41.246793','Vector Dataset','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('866ea2d4-f9b3-4033-8b1e-6720756ba692','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RPCICA 5 ESC4 MOMENT V1.0','This dataset contains DERIVED MOMENT data of ion density and ion bulkvelocity for masses 1,2,4 and 18 amu / e, from the RPCICAinstrument on mission ROSETTA during Comet escort 4.Data contains measurements of solar wind interactionwith the atmosphere of target comet 67P.','public','2026-03-13T17:48:25.701817','2026-03-13T17:48:25.701823','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','89d17061-5771-46c6-8564-d2f5d9df5a94','NASA Data.json','4f353be5a350d16f5b6ed80ce7ab9702882365a3b43993a03a6a78bedca94505','1.1','2026-03-13T17:48:25.701817','2026-03-13T17:48:25.701823','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('86893278-7f4e-4791-b8b1-e49d59f8077f','VOYAGER 1 SATURN PLASMA DERIVED ELECTRON BROWSE 96 SEC','THIS DATA SET CONTAINS THE THERMAL ELECTRON DENSITY AND TEMPERATURE IN THE PLS ENERGY RANGE (10-5950 EV) FROM VOYAGER 1 AT SATURN DERIVED BY FITTING THE LOW ENERGY ELECTRON COMPONENT WITH A MAXWELLIAN DISTRIBUTION, AND THE MOMENT DENSITY AND TEMPERATURE OF THE HOT ELECTRONS CALCULATED AFTER THE SIGNAL FROM THE THERMAL COMPONENT IS SUBTRACTED FROM THE ELECTRON SPECTRA. IT IS A SUBSET OF THE DATA SET VG1-S-PLS-5-ELE-FIT-96.0SEC WHICH SHOULD BE OBTAINED BEFORE THIS DATA IS USED. SPACECRAFT CHARGING MAY RESULT IN FACTOR OF 2-3 ERRORS IN THE THERMAL ELECTRON DENSITY. THE FIRST SIX COLUMNS ARE THE TIME TAG (YEAR, DAY, HOUR, MIN, SEC, MSEC), COLUMN 7 AND 8 ARE THE FIT DENSITY AND TEMPERATURE OF THE THERMAL ELECTRON COMPONENT, AND 9 AND 10 ARE THE MOMENT DENSITY AND TEMPERATURE OF THE SUPRATHERMAL ELECTRONS. EACH ROW HAS THE FORMAT (6I5,4E12.4). VALUES OF 1.E32 INDICATE THAT THE PARAMETER COULD NOT BE OBTAINED FROM THE DATA USING THE STANDARD ANALYSIS TECHNIQUE. ADDITIONAL INFORMATION ABOUT THIS DATASET AND THE INSTRUMENT WHICH PRODUCED IT CAN BE FOUND ELSEWHERE IN THIS CATALOG. AN OVERVIEW OF THE DATA IN THIS DATA SET CAN BE FOUND IN SITTLER ET AL. (1983) AND A COMPLETE INSTRUMENT DESCRIPTION CAN BE FOUND IN BRIDGE (1977).','public','2026-03-13T19:56:40.398116','2026-03-13T19:56:40.398121','Planetary Plasma Interactions','Planetary Data System','026:00','316aa6f6-2d9b-4f49-a3d1-838e44125191','NASA Data.json','95ee1ca86ac9307e9784dcab704683634c89df9605134f4432ce3f0b502bc943','1.1','2026-03-13T19:56:40.398116','2026-03-13T19:56:40.398121','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('8695280e-29b6-42f2-9f6e-b12ea2fa9d6c','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 PRELANDING 0231 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the PRELANDING phase 2014-01-21 to 2014-11-18. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2014-08-22T13:10:05.000 to 2014-08-22T18:30:12.000.','public','2026-03-13T18:18:45.016750','2026-03-13T18:18:45.016755','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','baa66422-471b-4299-9fcd-7f2f3f6bf2e9','NASA Data.json','762caf826fe6a4c5eaa16bea9db9f325cd08a77388a160d86aaf32965e9b255f','1.1','2026-03-13T18:18:45.016750','2026-03-13T18:18:45.016755','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('86b8a812-adb4-4b05-a7c1-7184b28b58b8','MARS EXPRESS MARS MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 4 3507 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2013-01-01 to 2014-12-31. It is a Global Gravity measurement and covers the time 2013-01-30T09:01:37.000 to 2013-01-30T11:07:28.500.','public','2026-03-13T18:51:03.552630','2026-03-13T18:51:03.552635','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','15dc8d3b-e29c-4d03-998e-e304c9523f51','NASA Data.json','7990b5a9718cea6ba146d6535975bef311b07abc4e61043794d38921fd2ad203','1.1','2026-03-13T18:51:03.552630','2026-03-13T18:51:03.552635','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('8778da0f-3f81-4fc2-bc36-f1ac240b5a14','ULYSSES JUPITER EPAC OMNI-DIRECTIONAL                                        PROTON FLUX 1 HR AVG','This data set contains Ulysses Energetic Particle Composition      Experiment (EPAC) 1 hour averaged omni-directional proton flux      data from the Ulysses Jupiter encounter 1992-Jan-25 to      1992-Feb-28. These data were recorded by Omni-directional      Protons Spin Averages Telescopes (OPTL) 1-4.','public','2026-03-13T17:48:56.374881','2026-03-13T17:48:56.374888','planetary plasma interactions','Planetary Data System','026:00','4dde4cca-54d7-4802-9e79-301374d5e4cd','NASA Data.json','31e02bd7e7218c4350c8233b1f38762731d34787392504d69735dc3ca413478d','1.1','2026-03-13T17:48:56.374881','2026-03-13T17:48:56.374888','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('8778e30c-c2b0-48ff-a8d5-2f2b0a6d3dcb','F00927: NOS Hydrographic Survey , 2025-12-18','The National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration (NOAA) has the statutory mandate to collect hydrographic data in support of nautical chart compilation for safe navigation and to provide background data for engineers, scientific, and other commercial and industrial activities. Hydrographic survey data primarily consist of water depths, but may also include features (e.g. rocks, wrecks), navigation aids, shoreline identification, and bottom type information.\n							NOAA is responsible for archiving and distributing the source data as described in this metadata record.','public','2026-03-14T22:46:32.541873','2026-03-14T22:46:32.541877',NULL,NULL,NULL,'614f553d-b30a-4ed3-8b49-8a0ac3ea9b3e','NESDIS/NGDC/MGG/NOS/F00001-F02000',NULL,NULL,'2026-03-14T22:46:32.541873','2026-03-14T22:46:32.541877',NULL,NULL,NULL,'noaa-gov'),('879089ff-4aa4-480d-a9a5-b38dc446474c','ROSETTA-ORBITER 9P MIRO 2 CR2 9P-TEMPEL1 V1.0','This data set contains Spectroscopic, Continuum and Engineering data taken by the Microwave Instrument for the Rosetta Orbiter (MIRO) during the second cruise phase of the mission. The data consist primarily of observations of comet 9P/Tempel 1 before, during and after the planned collision of the Deep Impact mission impactor spacecraft with that comet in July 2005. The data are presented as a series of binary table files.','public','2026-03-13T18:26:14.550541','2026-03-13T18:26:14.550547','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','46ced7b8-da23-4400-8cc1-000f6f0e7eac','NASA Data.json','4de04566a4a95af4874f9b76dec5ebc85c31028d7fbdbeeb9539d40c59288474','1.1','2026-03-13T18:26:14.550541','2026-03-13T18:26:14.550547','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('87954d1e-ad15-45c3-b096-6753a8e922d2','Hydrographic and Impairment Statistics Database: NPS-WSR Salmon Wild and Scenic River','Hydrographic and Impairment Statistics (HIS) is a National Park Service (NPS) Water Resources Division (WRD) project established to track certain goals created in response to the Government Performance and Results Act of 1993 (GPRA). One water resources management goal established by the Department of the Interior under GRPA requires NPS to track the percent of its managed surface waters that are meeting Clean Water Act (CWA) water quality standards. This goal requires an accurate inventory that spatially quantifies the surface water hydrography that each bureau manages and a procedure to determine and track which waterbodies are or are not meeting water quality standards as outlined by Section 303(d) of the CWA. This project helps meet this DOI GRPA goal by inventorying and monitoring in a geographic information system for the NPS: (1) CWA 303(d) quality impaired waters and causes; and (2) hydrographic statistics based on the United States Geological Survey (USGS) National Hydrography Dataset (NHD). Hydrographic and 303(d) impairment statistics were evaluated based on a combination of 1:24,000 (NHD) and finer scale data (frequently provided by state GIS layers).','public','2026-03-29T06:07:04.360001','2026-03-29T06:07:04.360008','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','a5dc8f0a-7760-45dd-af40-56ae1fb682e5','DOI NPS DCAT-US','14b0de7d05f3f163aac7361b7dfdace78b36fe2b74f511586f37c4de15a529a1','1.1','2026-03-29T06:07:04.360001','2026-03-29T06:07:04.360008','geospatial','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('87b6d17a-506b-4b35-9345-28ae380f263a','VG2 URA TRAJECTORY DERIV SUMM                                      HELIOGRAPHIC COORDS 48SEC V1.0','This dataset contains Voyager 2        position vectors relative to the Sun in both cartesian and        spherical Heliographic coordinates for the time when Voyager 2        was near Uranus but not within its magnetosphere. The position        vectors are given every 48 seconds. The units of the vector        components are Au and degrees.  Vectors are stored as 4-byte floating        point values.','public','2026-03-13T19:48:35.982399','2026-03-13T19:48:35.982405','planetary plasma interactions','Planetary Data System','026:00','49186ee7-8045-41ca-8998-bba9d8df485d','NASA Data.json','1ec41d8e43f9f15169682c894a0fa28dc92f9fb9b89eacd8d1e5267b347cb604','1.1','2026-03-13T19:48:35.982399','2026-03-13T19:48:35.982405','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('87b74214-b2f7-4227-9eb8-03b5a0abc7c7','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSIWAC 4 ESC1-MTP013 RDR-STR-REFL V1.0','This CODMAC level 4 data set contains solar stray light corrected, radiometric calibrated and geometric distortion corrected (resampled) image data in in reflectance units (normalized and thus without unit), acquired by the OSIRIS Wide Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft during the COMET ESCORT 1 mission phase, covering the period from 2015-02-10T23:25:00.000 to 2015-03-10T23:24:59.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V1.0 is the first version of this dataset: Lien corrected dataset after October 2018 PSA/PDS external peer review.','public','2026-03-13T18:57:42.191424','2026-03-13T18:57:42.191429','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','b372b351-43cd-4491-9e96-27e63cbb4f5d','NASA Data.json','953606e8af636a82fc615e4825937040008f9a823140f1781f86272d65841d72','1.1','2026-03-13T18:57:42.191424','2026-03-13T18:57:42.191429','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('87d5f43d-7ef0-43fb-ac45-bcea9a092774','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P VIRTIS 3 EXTENSION 3 MTP035 V2.0','This release contains the calibrated data of the VIRTIS instrument on board of the spacecraft Rosetta. This volume contains data from the EXTENSION 3 MTP035 phase, which occurred from 2016-09-26 to 2016-09-29 when at the vicinity of comet 67P. This data set V2.0 supersedes V1.0. It includes major updates on the data and documentation.','public','2026-03-13T16:58:37.413577','2026-03-13T16:58:37.413582','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','72af7a20-2313-4a03-8ba1-a4d1a8d77e11','NASA Data.json','e129057bda08f9838d7d4069ab7dc6a2a806f8dce0d18bfe5fb9f5c8fe660b6f','1.1','2026-03-13T16:58:37.413577','2026-03-13T16:58:37.413582','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('87e2244d-e086-4a75-91eb-940df721dd0c','ROSETTA-LANDER CAL SESAME 2 PHC V1.0','This archive contains edited data (CODMAC level 2) from the SESAME instrument onboard ROSETTA Lander, acquired during the PHC phase. It also contains documentation which describes the SESAME experiment. The data archived in this data set conform to the Planetary Data System (PDS) Standards, Version 3.6.','public','2026-03-13T17:08:51.024327','2026-03-13T17:08:51.024334','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','ac082a3c-4872-4904-85bb-b8bf76de274c','NASA Data.json','f9b0c7f2b710873c0cc6ad92616049374e077ea7c2abb702f48928a0897170fa','1.1','2026-03-13T17:08:51.024327','2026-03-13T17:08:51.024334','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('87edf40a-34ef-43ce-8cf4-3d80a814bc5c','ROSETTA-ORBITER SW RPCICA 4 CR2 CORR-CTS V1.0','This dataset contains corrected and RESAMPLED RAW DATA fromthe RPCICA instrument on mission ROSETTA during Cruise phase 2.The data has been corrected for cross-talk using an automatic algorithm,and noise has been treated to be even regardless of onward noisesuppression. The data is the same as L4 CORR but in counts, not physicalunits. The data may due to noise treatment have negative values.Data of the solar wind was obtained.','public','2026-03-13T18:36:29.735582','2026-03-13T18:36:29.735589','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','adc7af1f-9390-4e66-bd2c-795b15f3fc28','NASA Data.json','5f9849eecd876ecca336c5f4760b81a5dabe57a68e26ac331d3c2cb92ba2090c','1.1','2026-03-13T18:36:29.735582','2026-03-13T18:36:29.735589','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('8811cad0-b715-4408-96e6-4b2c18e83206','MARS EXPRESS MARS MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 5 3682 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2015-01-01 to 2016-12-31. It is a Global Gravity measurement and covers the time 2015-01-05T08:21:07.000 to 2015-01-05T10:29:58.500.','public','2026-03-13T18:53:20.786367','2026-03-13T18:53:20.786375','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','e007d4e7-014b-4cf9-826a-e41e9230211b','NASA Data.json','9907eb1af401ae660f615b891524b8fc620c9ae95bf7d76f8daee38e5f63d1ff','1.1','2026-03-13T18:53:20.786367','2026-03-13T18:53:20.786375','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('881efad3-a34d-4e5a-afae-6d3927665362','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 3 1057 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 3 phase 2015-07-01 to 2015-10-21. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-09-25T09:44:50.000 to 2015-09-25T17:32:29.500.','public','2026-03-13T18:13:52.003756','2026-03-13T18:13:52.003760','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','de9df876-4a49-4eb9-9af0-da29199afe08','NASA Data.json','6ae314c91039dee3b793371f80c424a13939ac85dc124c475a5367b73b0b9412','1.1','2026-03-13T18:13:52.003756','2026-03-13T18:13:52.003760','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('88285636-3518-4c9a-8f03-5d33ce3d461c','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSINAC 4 ESC1-MTP012 RDR V1.0','This CODMAC level 4 data set contains radiometric calibrated and geometric distortion corrected (resampled) image data in W/m^2/sr/nm acquired by the OSIRIS Narrow Angle Camera during the COMET ESCORT 1 phase of the Rosetta mission, covering the period from 2015-01-13T23:25:00.000 to 2015-02-10T23:24:59.000.','public','2026-03-13T19:01:15.748537','2026-03-13T19:01:15.748544','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','b0a45d7e-5ce8-49cc-8203-c417abe0b93c','NASA Data.json','e6c1be67681d63ddc3788d7fb6902fa11d1d36bcd57e80433b372631f0bb6816','1.1','2026-03-13T19:01:15.748537','2026-03-13T19:01:15.748544','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('8883cb99-4d0e-4267-9b75-52d5b59dcc0e','MARS EXPRESS MARS MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 4 3509 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2013-01-01 to 2014-12-31. It is a Global Gravity measurement and covers the time 2013-02-02T08:04:20.000 to 2013-02-02T10:08:15.500.','public','2026-03-13T17:02:52.452845','2026-03-13T17:02:52.452852','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','d3130416-7946-4da4-8e6e-5b529a815939','NASA Data.json','d94428cb01d8019c870d4a7e667b7420853b5e8be50bc62d01b01c4f4c497bca','1.1','2026-03-13T17:02:52.452845','2026-03-13T17:02:52.452852','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('88915d80-fcc1-496a-8466-1792d432729c','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 1 0480 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 1 phase 2014-11-20 to 2015-03-10. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2014-12-09T00:52:20.000 to 2014-12-09T12:45:59.000.','public','2026-03-13T18:56:41.168657','2026-03-13T18:56:41.168662','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','18505b7f-4fa8-4c22-9415-570cc2d6f700','NASA Data.json','471951fbe94868de6c762a7a0d3c535c6962788c01bf02d36861c826190e3355','1.1','2026-03-13T18:56:41.168657','2026-03-13T18:56:41.168662','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('88aadc87-f3b0-4888-ad29-054fc27ecdda','DAWN VIR CAL (RDR) VESTA INFRARED SPECTRA V2.0','This data set contains the spectral  radiance (W/(m**2*sr*micron)) data from the Dawn VIR instrument  infrared channel for all Vesta encounter mission phases. The data in  this version of the data set have been produced using an updated  calibration. The data cover the time period between 2011-05-03 and  2012-07-18.','public','2026-03-13T17:26:19.397495','2026-03-13T17:26:19.397501','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','b1858b96-88ab-4175-ac96-b6623d8853c0','NASA Data.json','2311e0a8a1acc202e2d3bbc5d2ccc7f873ab3e96e41df1bda05d235ea4dfd5e6','1.1','2026-03-13T17:26:19.397495','2026-03-13T17:26:19.397501','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('88f01f1e-41b7-45f3-a196-e50ee164a189','MARS EXPRESS MARS MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 3 3383 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2010-01-01 to 2012-12-31. It is a Global Gravity measurement and covers the time 2012-08-31T07:16:07.000 to 2012-08-31T09:59:31.500.','public','2026-03-13T17:06:24.232515','2026-03-13T17:06:24.232520','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','791acaf9-dace-4acc-aa36-e4797e5efeac','NASA Data.json','88a342e015755c7b97fef6697cb8e9429ec3975ee7f6a18493c24fa8f71dbada','1.1','2026-03-13T17:06:24.232515','2026-03-13T17:06:24.232520','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov');
INSERT INTO `datasets` VALUES ('8900c250-093e-4b8d-84f9-52e7779a2548','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSINAC 2 ESC2-MTP014 EDR V3.0','This CODMAC level 2 data set contains uncalibrated image data in DN unit, acquired by the OSIRIS Narrow Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft during the COMET ESCORT 2 mission phase, covering the period from 2015-03-10T23:25:00.000 to 2015-04-08T11:24:59.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V3.0 supersedes previous deliveries of the same dataset with the following changes since the last version: Lien corrected dataset after the July and October 2018 PSA/PDS external peer reviews. Updated documentation and ancillary files, added document on bandpass filter. Updated SCIENCE_USER_GUIDE_V03.PDF to include one section about FAQ and one section about image data quality. Added shutter backtravel and readout issues to image quality map. Updated DATA_QUALITY_ID keyword in image header. Improved handling of images with missing packets. Included FITs files. Browse products changed to the same size as the original image.','public','2026-03-13T16:55:39.900406','2026-03-13T16:55:39.900411','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','fe1c8083-57c2-43cd-8f57-0db8cbb5f903','NASA Data.json','33577f3fb53a638c3312ed89b302b8020fcc2b3385844e7453704596a97ce942','1.1','2026-03-13T16:55:39.900406','2026-03-13T16:55:39.900411','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('89068eb1-69c7-4e08-bb6a-2950a4d3aaa1','ROSETTA-ORBITER 2002T7/CAL/CHECK ALICE 3 CVP1 V1.0','This data set contains CODMAC level 3 cometary, calibration, and instrument checkout data acquired by the Rosetta Orbiter ALICE UV Spectrometer during the first commissioning phase of the Rosetta mission, which occurred March 5, 2004 to June 6, 2004.','public','2026-03-13T18:11:43.447975','2026-03-13T18:11:43.447980','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','0cff392d-8a12-4750-9203-5e0f0cf58af2','NASA Data.json','eca4e180e20ab05857f99543308f452e6b69da4d367fee4637ee54526427e127','1.1','2026-03-13T18:11:43.447975','2026-03-13T18:11:43.447980','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('890c0a51-120d-411d-8ac7-fd3c4bd780af','ROSETTA-ORBITER SUN RSI 1/2/3 CRUISE 2 0016 V1.0','This is a Solar Conjunction measurement covering the time 2006-03-15T00:41:33.500 to 2006-03-15T07:52:20.000.','public','2026-03-13T18:01:00.735554','2026-03-13T18:01:00.735561','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','cf9dd6f3-67bf-43ed-a71f-59718b55c460','NASA Data.json','068563282a4546629657944da028738c5bd154d06bd45a8c40257d9adc278059','1.1','2026-03-13T18:01:00.735554','2026-03-13T18:01:00.735561','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('89142ca0-e81e-468d-836b-78eab8f22476','IMAGES OF 9P/TEMPEL 1 FROM 2005 AROUND THE DI ENCOUNTER V1.0','The data set consists of ground-based images of comet 9P/Tempel 1 in the broadband R and narrowband HB filters taken at the Kitt Peak Mayall 4m telescope with the MOSAIC camera from July 2-9, 2005 around the Deep Impact encounter.','public','2026-03-13T17:10:37.541043','2026-03-13T17:10:37.541048','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','256d0022-5134-4329-be69-fe116db2f36b','NASA Data.json','aa465e6154f42ead893847943e4202a799658c346b07837040e6fd99f2a5002a','1.1','2026-03-13T17:10:37.541043','2026-03-13T17:10:37.541048','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('8926b92b-b316-418f-bd3d-5b96925345ff','CASSINI HIGH RATE DETECTOR V17.0','The High Rate Detector (HRD) from the University of Chicago is an independent part of the CDA instrument on the Cassini Orbiter that measures the dust flux and particle mass distribution of dust particles hitting the HRD detectors. This data set includes all data from the HRD through December 31, 2016. Please refer to Srama et al. (2004) for a detailed HRD description.','public','2026-03-13T18:35:12.312726','2026-03-13T18:35:12.312732','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','3a3e7247-c69b-4611-a91c-91baa1e5157a','NASA Data.json','9190e95d9f8995dad33a8933a4846bd28d68dc6e4fe2dc8a2881a1d0cf188e82','1.1','2026-03-13T18:35:12.312726','2026-03-13T18:35:12.312732','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('8952b3d6-93c9-4f6d-a7dd-30b00537869b','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSINAC 4 EXT1-MTP026 RDR-INF-REFL V1.0','This CODMAC level 4 data set contains solar stray-light corrected, in-field stray-light corrected,  radiometric calibrated and geometric distortion corrected  (resampled) image data in reflectance units (normalized  and thus without unit),  acquired by the OSIRIS Narrow Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft  during the ROSETTA EXTENSION 1 mission phase, covering the period  from 2016-02-09T23:25:00.000 to 2016-03-08T23:24:59.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V1.0 is the first version of this dataset: Lien corrected dataset after September 2019 PSA/PDS external peer review.','public','2026-03-13T18:08:23.634179','2026-03-13T18:08:23.634186','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','f3710444-0e2d-4664-8459-4483a94a0492','NASA Data.json','32c0e59bcafe5f9fd8ffcfbcbee8ba046a3922b6093b7a3f44d3af3c49b5340c','1.1','2026-03-13T18:08:23.634179','2026-03-13T18:08:23.634186','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('89838031-d7c5-42e1-ad40-5b5bc2a11396','ROSETTA-ORBITER SW RPCICA 4 CR2 CORR V1.0','This dataset contains corrected and RESAMPLED CALIBRATED DATA fromthe RPCICA instrument on mission ROSETTA during Cruise phase 2.Data of the solar wind was obtained.','public','2026-03-13T18:01:09.438944','2026-03-13T18:01:09.438949','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','9f8835fc-1002-47f7-aa89-66f4e033c061','NASA Data.json','89ee0f72790b955561425703ae7aa0cc79b763bb0e51224ba7916a0f5d3bc4fd','1.1','2026-03-13T18:01:09.438944','2026-03-13T18:01:09.438949','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('89930363-38e8-4744-aefc-42bde62c20de','Long-Term Occupational Projections','Occupational projections estimate the future performance and trends of occupations over a defined period. These are 10-year projections for the State of Iowa and its six local workforce development areas (LWDA). Projections are are based on a combination of historical data, market analysis, economic indicators, and emerging trends.','public','2026-03-28T21:59:27.742086','2026-03-28T21:59:27.742091','data.iowa.gov','Katie Green',NULL,'49ceed30-c7e6-49b9-9307-525b1c477e1c','Iowa metadata','fcf8c1b29655723496fa0211a54fa813d64a70ed75aade36719f5571e403a5ef','1.1','2026-03-28T21:59:27.742086','2026-03-28T21:59:27.742091','Workforce',NULL,0,'state-of-iowa'),('89a0f819-974c-4674-b319-b7abcc24b56d','CASSINI RSS RAW DATA SET - TIGR4 V1.0','The Cassini Radio Science Titan Gravity Science Experiment (TIGR4) Raw Data Archive is a time-ordered collection of radio science raw data acquired on April 29, May 1, 19, and 21, 2006 during the Tour subphase of the Cassini mission.','public','2026-03-13T18:34:46.250530','2026-03-13T18:34:46.250535','Planetary Atmospheres','Planetary Data System','026:00','99ba8d0c-d143-480d-88b5-83e790ed2609','NASA Data.json','e26e926e11d02d1e265f427211164255a899943f985dea7ed76c3abda634de69','1.1','2026-03-13T18:34:46.250530','2026-03-13T18:34:46.250535','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('89ae7ec7-86ef-4827-af11-81c2acf18afd','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSIWAC 5 EXT3-MTP031 DDR-GEO V1.0','This CODMAC level 5 data set contains derived data products that include pixel-precise georeferencing information, acquired by the OSIRIS Wide Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft during the ROSETTA EXTENSION 3 mission phase, covering the period from 2016-06-28T23:25:00.000 to 2016-07-26T23:24:59.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V1.0 is the first version of this dataset: Lien corrected dataset after October 2018 PSA/PDS external peer review.','public','2026-03-13T18:51:58.134139','2026-03-13T18:51:58.134145','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','0cd7435f-4e54-4335-9c4f-309449c3cc4b','NASA Data.json','f7fbb619e741255ef639a3ce731f99ad0705ef0c41d5b797ad2c992790b2d562','1.1','2026-03-13T18:51:58.134139','2026-03-13T18:51:58.134145','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('89fd998b-2c1a-48d1-bfc1-321c1716e379','ROSETTA-ORBITER PRELANDING OSIWAC 3 RDR MTP006 V2.0','This data set contains images acquired by the OSIRIS Wide Angle Camera during the PRELANDING phase of the Rosetta mission at the comet 67P, covering the period from 2014-08-01T10:00:00.000 to 2014-09-02T09:59:59.000. This version V2.0 supersedes previous deliveries of the same dataset.','public','2026-03-13T18:54:22.636387','2026-03-13T18:54:22.636393','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','8bf77a8b-af08-4224-ae4a-2f446e83b8be','NASA Data.json','5c9a189aa1917c210fd9be3efa2cbe3b1eb6ecdfac426d2d2c1c59027200033f','1.1','2026-03-13T18:54:22.636387','2026-03-13T18:54:22.636393','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('8a112d29-3ef2-4c82-817c-4fd11a8ecf86','ROSETTA-ORBITER EARTH RPCICA 4 EAR3 CORR-CTS V1.0','This dataset contains corrected and RESAMPLED RAW DATA fromthe RPCICA instrument on mission ROSETTA during the third flyby of Earth.The data has been corrected for cross-talk using an automatic algorithm,and noise has been treated to be even regardless of onward noisesuppression. The data is the same as L4 CORR but in counts, not physicalunits. The data may due to noise treatment have negative values.The data contains observations of the solar wind in the vicinity ofEarth and a passage through the Earth\'s magnetosphere, including someradiation belt data.','public','2026-03-13T18:06:27.186378','2026-03-13T18:06:27.186384','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','929b49a1-ee1b-496e-9515-8332d64e8cd6','NASA Data.json','7c2abceaf820b3ebb9a7744f5c81fbbdc138a08b6e30891e3d9c1e2f55378a7a','1.1','2026-03-13T18:06:27.186378','2026-03-13T18:06:27.186384','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('8a120f4c-1131-4aa9-abb1-f13ccbc21337','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSINAC 3 ESC4-MTP024 RDR V3.0','This CODMAC level 3 data set contains radiometric calibrated image data in W/m^2/sr/nm, acquired by the OSIRIS Narrow Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft during the COMET ESCORT 4 mission phase, covering the period from 2015-12-15T23:25:00.000 to 2016-01-12T23:24:59.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V3.0 supersedes previous deliveries of the same dataset with the following changes since the last version: Lien corrected dataset after the July and October 2018 PSA/PDS external peer reviews. Updated documentation and ancillary files, added document on bandpass filter. Updated SCIENCE_USER_GUIDE_V03.PDF to include one section about FAQ and one section about image data quality. Added shutter backtravel and readout issues to image quality map. Updated DATA_QUALITY_ID keyword in image header. Improved handling of images with missing packets. Included FITs files. Browse products changed to the same size as the original image.','public','2026-03-13T17:47:19.482788','2026-03-13T17:47:19.482794','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','daaaa653-6954-4229-8fe8-1072f9848891','NASA Data.json','09d7645056e2501b5506ca6990a684d9bf97a2be172bc8dcdbbaca374e0660d4','1.1','2026-03-13T17:47:19.482788','2026-03-13T17:47:19.482794','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('8a2d2934-2922-4eee-b054-329b9cdbfc91','Continuous Fixed Station Water Quality Measurements in Cape Lookout National Seashore, November 2009 (Certified)','This dataset represents continuous water quality measurements that were taken at a fixed point in Cape Lookout National Seashore during the month of November, 2009 as a part of the Fixed Station Water Quality Monitoring protocol that was developed by the Southeast Coast I&M Network (SECN). The measurements were taken by a YSI 6600 ESD Multi-Parameter Long Term Water Quality Monitoring Datasonde unit that serves as the standard fixed station water quality monitoring equipment for all similar operations conducted by the SECN. The following parameters were measured at 15 minute intervals during the time period that has been specified: Water Temperature, Specific Conductivity, Salinity, Dissolved Oxygen (DO), DO Concentration, Shallow Depth, pH Level, and Turbidity. Any anomalies noted regarding these parameters have also been noted in separate fields.  Please note that these measurements have been certified by network personnel.','public','2026-03-26T05:28:00.436634','2026-03-26T05:28:00.436639','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','e6bca30c-ac28-4df4-baed-2b91d94dc97d','DOI NPS DCAT-US','aef22f228e23f55d5e5d897154cba171457a8c1cbfb1532c70393ef5c39dc3e0','1.1','2026-03-26T05:28:00.436634','2026-03-26T05:28:00.436639','Vector Dataset','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('8a568196-534d-4790-b433-f6ca3df4404d','IHW COMET IRIMAG CALIBRATED EXPERIMENT DATA RECORD GZ V1.0','In preparation for the concerted international study of Comet Halley, the IHW conducted a trial run with observations of Comet Crommelin, largely during February and March of 1984.','public','2026-03-13T18:59:23.108625','2026-03-13T18:59:23.108630','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','61dcbabb-f111-4c9c-afec-b0d4e2aab868','NASA Data.json','20f933c47f46244883873cbbe0a1113de2a74b7f4352e3a02e7f8322f5057e6d','1.1','2026-03-13T18:59:23.108625','2026-03-13T18:59:23.108630','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('8a656782-cd94-4475-a75e-45363ab34651','MARS EXPRESS MARS MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 7 4173 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2019-01-01 to 2020-12-31. It is a Occultation measurement and covers the time 2020-12-25T13:49:52.200 to 2020-12-25T14:12:01.549.','public','2026-03-13T17:36:41.935337','2026-03-13T17:36:41.935343','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','534d6f62-1394-4711-a566-4c64835f154e','NASA Data.json','f73832a00156168aa3a07c7a087fba3ce0039ca40a865d41d35a3e0290895998','1.1','2026-03-13T17:36:41.935337','2026-03-13T17:36:41.935343','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('8a8c2a90-b73a-41a9-860e-dcb02b4ed37f','MARS EXPRESS MARS MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 4 3468 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2013-01-01 to 2014-12-31. It is a Global Gravity measurement and covers the time 2013-01-02T08:48:17.000 to 2013-01-02T10:46:01.500.','public','2026-03-13T17:13:31.894372','2026-03-13T17:13:31.894376','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','22184ede-3a2d-4792-93d1-23ef251bc1e8','NASA Data.json','e5d1b6bfc2504e49955218306fe7934a679c5339fe20cc0b01ff3b81f844fb14','1.1','2026-03-13T17:13:31.894372','2026-03-13T17:13:31.894376','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('8abe0112-cd51-45fe-b438-0d6afb774f2c','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P SREM 2 EXTENSION 1 MTP025 V1.0','This data set contains count rates (1/s) as measured by the Standard Radiation Environment Monitor (SREM) instrument on the Rosetta spacecraft, along with their standard deviations. The primary target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko. These are CODMAC Level 2 Experiment Data Record data, and provide a measure of the radiation in the spacecraft environment during the Medium Term Plan 25 period of the EXTENSION 1 mission phase.','public','2026-03-13T19:30:15.496997','2026-03-13T19:30:15.497004','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','81e56416-616d-4877-94a4-64802a054a7b','NASA Data.json','a99a01c8df519ab10ef834e8bf55d8fff0109d9ae57b2ac3535c3e512d57de18','1.1','2026-03-13T19:30:15.496997','2026-03-13T19:30:15.497004','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('8ac2466c-7cc8-4ed3-a276-4792f5a6517c','Texas Commission on Environmental Quality - Water Quality Individual Permits Active/Pending','This dataset includes basic information about the stormwater and wastewater individual permits administered by the TCEQ Water Quality Division. The authorizations covered in this dataset are as follows: Concentrated Animal Feeding Operations (CAFO), Conventional Water Treatment, Municipal Separate Storm Sewer System (MS4) Phase I, Industrial Stormwater, Industrial Wastewater, Public Domestic Wastewater, Private Domestic Wastewater, and Reverse Osmosis Water Treatment.','public','2026-03-25T14:23:22.122949','2026-03-25T14:23:22.122955','data.austintexas.gov','TCEQ Information Resources Division',NULL,'6f4f6ee0-fdab-466c-9d9d-37b3602a516e','City of Austin Data.json','e261550229772050ebc7e7ab396a34eda697af5b067a60c466ca5b8dd8cd3037','1.1','2026-03-25T14:23:22.122949','2026-03-25T14:23:22.122955',NULL,NULL,0,'city-of-austin'),('8ae09035-fc32-497d-ae07-705af0e00f4b','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P MIRO 3 EXT2 V3.0','This data set contains Spectroscopic and Continuum, level 3 data, in the form of table files, taken during the ROSETTA EXTENSION 2 phase of the Rosetta mission to comet 67P/CHURYUMOV-GERASIMENKO by the MIRO instrument. It supercedes data sets with a lower version number. The updates include a new calibration algorithm and modified documentation.','public','2026-03-13T17:00:05.605682','2026-03-13T17:00:05.605687','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','28927f4e-17eb-43bc-8c62-6d6edf320faf','NASA Data.json','105bccac2be05d2f25095f3c815f89d3108a0facecea8c30e64a5f61d2908264','1.1','2026-03-13T17:00:05.605682','2026-03-13T17:00:05.605687','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('8b071579-93b4-4041-9783-fbf98c71fca0','MARS EXPRESS MARS MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 3 3283 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2010-01-01 to 2012-12-31. It is a Global Gravity measurement and covers the time 2012-05-09T10:12:52.000 to 2012-05-09T14:07:56.000.','public','2026-03-13T20:07:25.023931','2026-03-13T20:07:25.023937','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','7f35af9f-9e41-4e40-953a-03d1fc0dc44e','NASA Data.json','4f7bbac66f25cf5223872ce41fc2bf841bba72469d27e52d429ffb088dcc7002','1.1','2026-03-13T20:07:25.023931','2026-03-13T20:07:25.023937','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('8b1a261c-44c2-47a0-8a7e-2370d78fcd35','Citywide Mobility Survey - Person 2024','The Citywide Mobility Survey (CMS) is NYC DOT\'s annual travel survey to assess the travel behavior, preferences, and attitudes of NYC residents. It is composed of 5 linked data tables.\n\nCitywide Mobility Survey (CMS) Person table contains characteristics of individual members of the participant’s household, including age, race, gender, disability status, education, employment, remote work, typical commute mode, biking frequency, shared services, and other demographic and transportation-related information.\n\n<b>Other 2024 Citywide Mobility Survey Datasets:</b>\n<a href=\"https://data.cityofnewyork.us/d/5mb3-padx\">Citywide Mobility Survey - Household 2024</a>\n<a href=\"https://data.cityofnewyork.us/d/naav-ygga\">Citywide Mobility Survey - Day 2024</a>\n<a href=\"https://data.cityofnewyork.us/d/wgnh-qwsg\">Citywide Mobility Survey - Trip 2024</a>\n<a href=\"https://data.cityofnewyork.us/d/qhkz-4dqm\">Citywide Mobility Survey - Vehicle 2024</a>\n\nSee all the <a href=\"https://data.cityofnewyork.us/browse?sortBy=relevance&pageSize=20&Data-Collection_Data-Collection=Citywide+Mobility+Survey\">Citywide Mobility Survey Data</a>, including past surveys.','public','2026-03-29T04:40:31.274862','2026-03-29T04:40:31.274868','data.cityofnewyork.us','NYC OpenData',NULL,'0e8f31e0-5aba-478a-b23f-435a4d16f536','NYC JSON','95ac16c49bf9748a6ed1c6dade968d7110d0cac3b3dcacf63e23ecaf667032bc','1.1','2026-03-29T04:40:31.274862','2026-03-29T04:40:31.274868','Transportation',NULL,0,'city-of-new-york'),('8b21b5a1-fbd9-4627-a4a7-be076bf8ad6d','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSIWAC 2 ESC3-MTP020 EDR V3.0','This CODMAC level 2 data set contains uncalibrated image data in DN unit, acquired by the OSIRIS Wide Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft during the COMET ESCORT 3 mission phase, covering the period from 2015-08-25T23:25:00.000 to 2015-09-22T23:24:59.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V3.0 supersedes previous deliveries of the same dataset with the following changes since the last version: Lien corrected dataset after the July and October 2018 PSA/PDS external peer reviews. Updated documentation and ancillary files, added document on bandpass filter. Updated SCIENCE_USER_GUIDE_V03.PDF to include one section about FAQ and one section about image data quality. Added shutter backtravel and readout issues to image quality map. Updated DATA_QUALITY_ID keyword in image header. Improved handling of images with missing packets. Included FITs files. Browse products changed to the same size as the original image.','public','2026-03-13T18:17:35.557257','2026-03-13T18:17:35.557262','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','6b834ddb-d4d1-481a-a89e-68ffcadb0b9d','NASA Data.json','af9411a90e4c3c539b74839b392fdc81525a2c86ecf6f1e1aaccf56d4943a882','1.1','2026-03-13T18:17:35.557257','2026-03-13T18:17:35.557262','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('8b76abca-65be-4ea4-a385-65d243842399','ROSETTA-ORBITER X SREM 2 MARS V1.0','This data set contains count rates (1/s) as measured by the Standard Radiation Environment Monitor (SREM) instrument on the Rosetta spacecraft, along with their standard deviations. These are CODMAC Level 2 Experiment Data Record data, and provide a measure of the radiation in the spacecraft environment during the MARS mission phase.','public','2026-03-13T19:33:20.886836','2026-03-13T19:33:20.886842','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','968d54bf-e8df-48ae-b487-011a41cb4d84','NASA Data.json','6abe87fcf18816c9152ffef51e591c75ad02eb51bac2051fd7e067995b24718b','1.1','2026-03-13T19:33:20.886836','2026-03-13T19:33:20.886842','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('8c3dbc38-97b4-4de3-aa58-4951aeae93d7','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RPCMIP 5 ESC4 V1.0','This archive contains derived data from the RPC-MIP instrument on-board ROSETTA Orbiter acquired during the COMET ESCORT 4 mission phase. Observations are performed in the vicinity of comet 67P/C-G. It also contains documentation which describes the RPC-MIP experiment. The data archived in this data set conform to the Planetary Data System Standards, Version 3.6.','public','2026-03-13T17:01:07.718484','2026-03-13T17:01:07.718490','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','ca4269e9-e56c-4502-92f5-5ae33a508092','NASA Data.json','150b4e2911cc07e93b1dbda609b11a5dd9674ddf01b9224a224ed2cf26e8ca51','1.1','2026-03-13T17:01:07.718484','2026-03-13T17:01:07.718490','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('8c66eb05-c0ea-4702-8354-812dd08cfc2f','ROSETTA-ORBITER CHECK ROSINA 2 ENGINEERING V1.0','This data set present engineering data of the three ROSINA sensors during the commissioning phases','public','2026-03-13T16:38:09.173205','2026-03-13T16:38:09.173210','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','c78f4801-141a-4ad1-a9a9-8f40b4c70aff','NASA Data.json','ec6edfd5bc2cbb81abfe5bbf171ef9ac30ca5b3fb14613b1c4aca1ce66c3f520','1.1','2026-03-13T16:38:09.173205','2026-03-13T16:38:09.173210','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('8c7457bb-7170-4c25-a832-5d88ced1de3e','NEAR GRS SPECTRA FOR CRUISE 4 PHASE','This data set contains Gamma Ray Spectrometer (GRS) observations made during the fourth cruise phase of the NEAR mission. The individual observations are combined into a single file per day for each sensor.','public','2026-03-13T16:55:24.701885','2026-03-13T16:55:24.701892','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','caddd305-5d86-4345-88c0-8e9418ec2941','NASA Data.json','06a24068e2e47cfa63fa562c46645f1620894a1476c424c84f37b9824bae05d9','1.1','2026-03-13T16:55:24.701885','2026-03-13T16:55:24.701892','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('8cc001b2-8445-412d-b9b9-ebe179c7a8b1','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSIWAC 4 PRL-MTP009 RDR-STR-REFL V1.0','This CODMAC level 4 data set contains solar stray light corrected, radiometric calibrated and geometric distortion corrected (resampled) image data in in reflectance units (normalized and thus without unit), acquired by the OSIRIS Wide Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft during the PRELANDING mission phase, covering the period from 2014-10-24T10:00:00.000 to 2014-11-21T23:24:59.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V1.0 is the first version of this dataset: Lien corrected dataset after October 2018 PSA/PDS external peer review.','public','2026-03-13T17:22:28.803655','2026-03-13T17:22:28.803660','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','7961003a-b7cd-4a83-ad04-8e3fc64d2fb0','NASA Data.json','f35cd4fb2bf6e3568d2ec57680e576e2f53bc7379095953f110589bc10f8014b','1.1','2026-03-13T17:22:28.803655','2026-03-13T17:22:28.803660','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('8cdecf8a-f2cf-4bb0-9e9f-a4ec59eb0c31','CASSINI RSS RAW DATA SET - SROC3 V1.0','The Cassini Radio Science Saturn and Ring Occultation Experiment (SROC3) Raw Data Archive is a time-ordered collection of radio science raw data acquired on September 15-17, 2006, during the Tour subphase of the Cassini mission.','public','2026-03-13T17:21:11.967130','2026-03-13T17:21:11.967136','Planetary Atmospheres','Planetary Data System','026:00','d02d0e85-60ce-40b4-be26-66d5c531f485','NASA Data.json','0c3b3faec0015ec9334387ad89fd1bcc8b6ef6e2dfbe11002352b1bd472e5915','1.1','2026-03-13T17:21:11.967130','2026-03-13T17:21:11.967136','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('8cec9299-1235-451b-afc4-31a7ee32897c','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 PRELANDING 0197 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the PRELANDING phase 2014-01-21 to 2014-11-18. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2014-08-11T07:48:25.000 to 2014-08-11T13:46:11.000.','public','2026-03-13T18:06:51.500589','2026-03-13T18:06:51.500595','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','be0654be-77cb-4e03-a89b-7bcf4fec9634','NASA Data.json','889498c2af2d1a7ff241ff094033c5a5c02d554aabf9d01fe16264625fc15f0b','1.1','2026-03-13T18:06:51.500589','2026-03-13T18:06:51.500595','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('8ced03bd-0293-4ac2-8a19-13b1db1da6da','BLM ID Right of Way Point','These are Rights-of-Ways (ROW) on Idaho BLM land (and some other Federal agency land) as shown on Bureau of Land Management (BLM) Master Title Plats (MTP). Every GIS ROW feature has a \"CASEFILE\" value, also known as the serial number of the ROW. The ROW data that was digitized is what was present on the MTP at the time of the digitizing done for that township. The project was performed over several years. Therefore, the \"early\" townships digitized are more out of date regarding ROWs compared to the ones more recently digitized. Unfortunately, there is no attribute that indicates the digitizing sequence. Any updates to this ROW feature class should be sent to the BLM Idaho State Office GIS staff for incorporation into the statewide GIS ROW feature classes for improvement over time. For more information contact us at blm_id_stateoffice@blm.gov.','public','2026-03-26T12:41:52.997309','2026-03-26T12:41:52.997314','Bureau of Land Management','Bureau of Land Management, blm_id_stateoffice','010:04','fb18b788-642e-454d-9e14-e3ed62574472','DOI BLM DCAT-US','748075d3ee89333648824e1985921e60ce78bbdba1e132dbfe722cd22055d5b9','1.1','2026-03-26T12:41:52.997309','2026-03-26T12:41:52.997314','geospatial','010:000',0,'doi-gov'),('8d45afdd-bbb8-4dfd-ba29-853dcd5031f9','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RPCLAP 3PRL CALIB2 V1.0','This data set containsCALIBRATED data from Rosetta RPC-LAP, acquired during the PRELANDINGmission phase where the primary target was the comet67P/CHURYUMOV-GERASIMENKO 1 (1969 R1). It contains instrument outputs involts and amperes, calibrated and corrected for instrument offsets. Thisversion reorganizes the data into fewer files with longer time seriesand sorted by type of measurement. The version number starts over fromV1.0 due to a change in naming convention.','public','2026-03-13T20:03:04.521511','2026-03-13T20:03:04.521519','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','8917e0ac-24f3-4436-8816-81f3dbdd6414','NASA Data.json','f64d8cf891fb9f1193796dcf0b9a79ae5b78a9668d3388208712ed7f908c7d68','1.1','2026-03-13T20:03:04.521511','2026-03-13T20:03:04.521519','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('8d7ad184-61f5-4347-8f53-3ae53715fe76','ROSETTA-ORBITER EARTH/CHECK NAVCAM 2 CRUISE 1 V1.1','This dataset contains RAW DATA of the CRUISE 1 Phase from 25 July 2004 until 1 August 2004. This data set V1.1 supersedes the V1.0. Details can be found in DATA_SET_DESC.','public','2026-03-13T16:51:34.657128','2026-03-13T16:51:34.657133','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','3be69ada-38b7-46f4-bb00-023d208c619c','NASA Data.json','2483ce8947502afee7342f55664dc7b8602f4857bc2b60cd78bfa72e2e065d15','1.1','2026-03-13T16:51:34.657128','2026-03-13T16:51:34.657133','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('8db1c7f8-15f0-4ce5-9151-9d186f054978','Soybean aphid,<i> Aphis glycines</i>, field abundance from field collection and corresponding vgsc-h1 genotypes','<p dir=\"ltr\">Data collected for soybean aphid, <i>Aphis glycines</i>, on soybean, <i>Glycine max</i>, in field efficacy trials conducted at the Iowa State University Northwest Research Farm, Sutherland, IA in 2023. Comprised of field aphid abundance (counts) from 10 sampled plants before and after insecticidal treatments, and corresponding genotypes of aphids at the voltage-gated sodium channel subunit h1 gene (<i>vgsc-h1</i>) encoding amino acid changes from a methionine at the <i>vgsc-h1</i> protein position 918 to either isoleucine (M918I) or leucine (M918L), a  leucine to methionine substitution at the 925<sup> </sup>position (L925M), and leucine to phenylalanine change at position 1014 (L1014F).</p>','public','2026-03-13T22:48:00.025249','2026-03-13T22:48:00.025255','Agricultural Research Service','Coates, Brad S.','005:18','45134e41-947a-47a8-8cf5-2cd46d982afa','USDA JSON','dbab0960a74f9c98f77c9dd61cb209ac6d622248a0efda0cd0b0ced935c28add','1.1','2026-03-13T22:48:00.025249','2026-03-13T22:48:00.025255',NULL,'005:040',0,'usda-gov'),('8db38983-701b-4711-a0bb-b88e64007c27','ROSETTA-ORBITER EARTH OSINAC 4 EAR1 RDR V1.0','This CODMAC level 4 data set contains radiometric calibrated and geometric distortion corrected (resampled) image data in W/m^2/sr/nm,  acquired by the OSIRIS Narrow Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft  during the EARTH SWING-BY 1 mission phase, covering the period  from 2004-10-17T00:00:00.000 to 2005-04-04T23:59:59.000. The prime target is planet Earth. This version V1.0 is the first version of this dataset.','public','2026-03-13T16:39:30.098183','2026-03-13T16:39:30.098190','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','4f19d863-68ab-4565-9496-7b72f96cc973','NASA Data.json','cb45ba9971e0bcc15d096a6bc58ba13a7eaf2e5a06570e4917684cea10e93570','1.1','2026-03-13T16:39:30.098183','2026-03-13T16:39:30.098190','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('8dee272f-1d97-4079-a76b-a410421ee04e','EPOXI C/ISON (2012 S1) - HRII RAW SPECTRA V1.0','This dataset contains raw, 1.05- to 4.8-micron spectral images of comet C/ISON (2012 S1) acquired by the High Resolution Infrared Spectrometer on 16-17 February 2013 during the Cruise 3 phase of the EPOXI mission.','public','2026-03-13T18:48:53.683746','2026-03-13T18:48:53.683751','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','f13fd069-0f57-45f8-8831-2ee0d0608f30','NASA Data.json','0ec7ba23720beebec24594027fecc011cab9998ab2e3fa0cfc0178b16b236c55','1.1','2026-03-13T18:48:53.683746','2026-03-13T18:48:53.683751','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('8df94520-9a2b-4438-ae6a-6c5690721726','DC COVID 19 Testing Overall','<div style=\'text-align:Left;\'><p><span>On March 2, 2022 DC Health announced the District’s new COVID-19 Community Level key metrics and reporting. COVID-19 cases are now reported on a </span><a href=\'https://opendata.dc.gov:443/datasets/dc-covid-19-weekly-cases/about\' style=\'text-decoration:underline;\' target=\'_blank\' rel=\'nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer\'><span>weekly basis</span></a><span>. More information available at https://coronavirus.dc.gov.</span></p><p><span>Data for overall Coronavirus cases and testing results. Demographics are presented by race, gender, ethnicity and age. Additional variables for personnel in the public safety, medical and human service workforce. District agencies are Metropolitan Police Department (MPD), Fire and Emergency Medical Services (FEMS), Department of Corrections (DOC), Department of Youth Rehabilitation Services (DYRS) and Department of Human Services (DHS). Data for Saint Elizabeth\'s Hospital available. DYRS, DOC and DHS further report on its resident populations. Visit https://coronavirus.dc.gov/page/coronavirus-data for interpretation analysis.</span></p><p><span style=\'font-weight:bold;\'>General Guidelines for Interpreting Disease Surveillance Data</span></p><p><span>During a disease outbreak, the health department will collect, process, and analyze large amounts of information to understand and respond to the health impacts of the disease and its transmission in the community. The sources of disease surveillance information include contact tracing, medical record review, and laboratory information, and are considered protected health information. When interpreting the results of these analyses, it is important to keep in mind that the disease surveillance system may not capture the full picture of the outbreak, and that previously reported data may change over time as it undergoes data quality review or as additional information is added. These analyses, especially within populations with small samples, may be subject to large amounts of variation from day to day. Despite these limitations, data from disease surveillance is a valuable source of information to understand how to stop the spread of COVID19.</span></p></div>','public','2026-04-01T08:42:45.248674','2026-04-01T08:42:45.248682','Office of the Chief Technology Officer','DCGISopendata',NULL,'d0792812-4eb5-4340-9f89-ea98e0d6defb','DC data','a2ebab5d24efcadf1738dabd2128afc80559d4ebd7f7aa28cb695573b5f15aaf','1.1','2026-04-01T08:42:45.248674','2026-04-01T08:42:45.248682','geospatial',NULL,0,'district-of-columbia'),('8e04c29f-c1e1-440c-ab2c-577eef3e7924','Ordinance 20030515-004','Ordinance 20030515-004','public','2026-03-25T14:31:14.170303','2026-03-25T14:31:14.170308','data.austintexas.gov','Haileigh.Meyers@austintexas.gov',NULL,'8bcac52a-09e0-410b-bc26-fb988df77ff8','City of Austin Data.json','b354b9dec35e1c5ad2172e5b59baba4d3c11d617fe4b76d9cde13752f49551c6','1.1','2026-03-25T14:31:14.170303','2026-03-25T14:31:14.170308',NULL,NULL,0,'city-of-austin'),('8e500d53-a8bf-4454-ae18-ce5167a95d95','VG2 URA LECP RESAMPLED RDR STEPPING                                      SECTOR 12.8MIN V1.0','This data consists of resampled datafrom the Low Energy Charged Particle (LECP) Experiment on the Voyager 2Spacecraft for the period when Voyager 2 was in the vicinity of the planetUranus.','public','2026-03-13T19:31:41.321637','2026-03-13T19:31:41.321644','planetary plasma interactions','Planetary Data System','026:00','519ed2f2-5a8e-44a6-b734-84019a0487b2','NASA Data.json','72502840b6d605af683f4507c0dd35cb5a184b7cd7aa793acb8d4a7c4260fdb1','1.1','2026-03-13T19:31:41.321637','2026-03-13T19:31:41.321644','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('8e619086-1d96-47a1-8898-da21159eec59','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 4 1128 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 4 phase 2015-10-22 to 2015-12-31. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-10-25T10:22:50.000 to 2015-10-25T17:18:53.500.','public','2026-03-13T16:39:45.923473','2026-03-13T16:39:45.923478','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','9c9273e9-5a86-4ec7-81bc-f40c996fe061','NASA Data.json','743777b1d1d4dcf2c96f08c3528745eca2e438aa161f7b004ebbb3812fa7b7dc','1.1','2026-03-13T16:39:45.923473','2026-03-13T16:39:45.923478','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('8e6227fa-a832-418e-a09d-24f08e03d119','MARS EXPRESS MARS MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 7 3978 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2019-01-01 to 2020-12-31. It is a Occultation measurement and covers the time 2019-03-22T09:23:10.200 to 2019-03-22T09:45:18.700.','public','2026-03-13T16:50:33.804138','2026-03-13T16:50:33.804143','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','bf5e287a-2c5f-4293-8162-4a296b92375f','NASA Data.json','7338ee267455f1a45571a8efccc16626bfebf87d0fc5a0e6d63e95d1141cfe3e','1.1','2026-03-13T16:50:33.804138','2026-03-13T16:50:33.804143','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('8e75dd0f-6d68-4a13-bdc6-79baba050cef','Groundwater Trading','The Water Resiliency Portfolio (2020) tasked the four State agencies to “create flexibility for GSAs to trade water within basins by enabling and incentivizing transactional approaches, including groundwater markets, with rules that safeguard natural resources, small- and medium-size farms, and water supply and quality for disadvantaged communities.” This direction is spelled out as Action 3.6. In 2021, the California Water Commission (Commission) was tasked to take initial steps to advance Action 3.6, and in 2022, the Commission\'s White Paper (https://cwc.ca.gov/-/media/CWC-Website/Files/Documents/2022/05_May/May2022_Item_10_Attach_1_WhitePaper_Final.pdf) identifies potential State actions and suggests that “with DWR as the lead agency, [the four State agencies] develop a workplan for implementing Action 3.6…”.','public','2026-03-23T14:01:55.886432','2026-03-23T14:01:55.886437','California Department of Water Resources','Sustainable Groundwater Management Office',NULL,'f5c52955-9f5d-4f34-9a06-bce0e5101e6c','State of California','5ee985662f53e140a25d5019b60ce4a243d2364ef21e7e3ba0db76aee24e9734','1.1','2026-03-23T14:01:55.886432','2026-03-23T14:01:55.886437','Natural Resources',NULL,0,'ca-gov'),('8e872981-007c-4f89-879e-532cc3ab4b75','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSINAC 5 ESC2-MTP016 DDR-GEO V1.0','This CODMAC level 5 data set contains derived data products that include pixel-precise georeferencing information, acquired by the OSIRIS Narrow Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft during the COMET ESCORT 2 mission phase, covering the period from 2015-05-05T23:25:00.000 to 2015-06-02T23:24:59.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V1.0 is the first version of this dataset: Lien corrected dataset after October 2018 PSA/PDS external peer review.','public','2026-03-13T16:57:25.720251','2026-03-13T16:57:25.720256','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','1e3d2b66-91e7-4f8a-a777-73c854f93f46','NASA Data.json','e940852909e8b70df96bd653350f81898df89606c0ae6231fa5bdf6213c67700','1.1','2026-03-13T16:57:25.720251','2026-03-13T16:57:25.720256','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('8e95ceab-e3bb-4331-ae53-aec11355e57d','MARS EXPRESS MARS MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 5 3818 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2015-01-01 to 2016-12-31. It is a Occultation measurement and covers the time 2015-09-12T11:08:42.000 to 2015-09-12T11:32:34.949.','public','2026-03-13T17:23:42.270409','2026-03-13T17:23:42.270420','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','0c89b110-fe24-4ecc-9cd9-80d840f20e18','NASA Data.json','0b88e757e530f9bbe14d13a2fead7985037f9a20e170fc3cef7ef8cae4567d88','1.1','2026-03-13T17:23:42.270409','2026-03-13T17:23:42.270420','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('8e9f548e-4e7e-4ce2-878a-c5f93ce0c326','MARINER 10 IMAGING ARCHIVE EXPERIMENT DATA RECORD','This series of fifteen CDs was produced by JPL\'s Science Digital Data Preservation Task (SDDPT) by migrating the original Mariner Ten image EDRs from old, deteriorating','public','2026-03-13T19:15:53.051144','2026-03-13T19:15:53.051150','Imaging','Planetary Data System','026:00','df73918d-e729-4403-8352-1268f590fe24','NASA Data.json','9206e5f64f5d648894d69257cc6406121d4e8f180a3209c252b10938b4c38eb8','1.1','2026-03-13T19:15:53.051144','2026-03-13T19:15:53.051150','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('8efb2248-36d8-4876-aa9f-3b44ea7da694','Soil lead conversion to plumbojarosite remains stable following lime addition and supports grass growth','Pb/As totals and IVBA. \n\nThis dataset is associated with the following publication:\nBlackmon, M., T. Sowers, A. Betts, C. Jiang, and K. Bradham. Lead transformation to plumbojarosite remains stable following lime addition for lead and arsenic contaminated soils.   JOURNAL OF HAZARDOUS MATERIALS. Elsevier Science Ltd, New York, NY, USA, 506: 141540, (2026).','public','2026-03-16T10:41:38.931749','2026-03-16T10:41:38.931756','U.S. Environmental Protection Agency','Matthew Blackmon','020:00','e18b5001-5dbd-4f3c-9aea-3d42cd71fddd','EPA ScienceHub','f07e97b6dae043bc6619247e837615f1815158e13c859d76c56e118deca27c89','1.1','2026-03-16T10:41:38.931749','2026-03-16T10:41:38.931756',NULL,'020:000',0,'epa-gov'),('8f3319d8-8146-454a-b25f-7fb8b731d553','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 2 0779 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 2 phase 2015-03-11 to 2015-06-30. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-05-15T23:03:05.000 to 2015-05-16T06:59:17.000.','public','2026-03-13T19:07:51.817861','2026-03-13T19:07:51.817868','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','7a410a36-1902-4ec4-83b2-a6108f46133e','NASA Data.json','a56f61bbde37f454748b25a71ac902921aba89f0e3ea7d6c8b5d8018a9e14b5e','1.1','2026-03-13T19:07:51.817861','2026-03-13T19:07:51.817868','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('8f402f79-73ce-457b-b843-b34ab5a36aca','2002 Turbidity and Total Suspended Solids Measurements of Glacial Streams in Yukon-Charley Rivers National Preserve and Wrangell-St. Elias National Park and Preserve, Alaska','This data release consists of water chemistry and quality data from glacial streams in Yukon-Charley Rivers National Preserve and Wrangell-St. Elias National Park and Preserve, Alaska. The data were collected by the National Park Service, Central Alaska Inventory and Monitoring Program as part of water inventory work in 2002.','public','2026-03-18T02:25:00.966071','2026-03-18T02:25:00.966077','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','029c06e2-5633-40f2-95f8-cea53cfde9a7','DOI NPS DCAT-US','7652939807c37ccc5efba429ab0e9e6d5ff0f9f75db016436ed70a6fb3b41f2b','1.1','2026-03-18T02:25:00.966071','2026-03-18T02:25:00.966077','Tabular Dataset','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('8f4f1d56-bcd6-4e22-bf73-93f31196c76e','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSINAC 4 ESC2-MTP014 RDR-INF-REFL V1.0','This CODMAC level 4 data set contains solar stray-light corrected, in-field stray-light corrected,  radiometric calibrated and geometric distortion corrected  (resampled) image data in reflectance units (normalized  and thus without unit),  acquired by the OSIRIS Narrow Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft  during the COMET ESCORT 2 mission phase, covering the period  from 2015-03-10T23:25:00.000 to 2015-04-08T11:24:59.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V1.0 is the first version of this dataset: Lien corrected dataset after September 2019 PSA/PDS external peer review.','public','2026-03-13T19:38:21.976415','2026-03-13T19:38:21.976420','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','4c61c6a6-3d8e-4727-8fff-992cbbc9d59c','NASA Data.json','ceb0cb77e89af4a2065e8c137e764caf5cfd4a4f5ca28b17ce2564e625366eb6','1.1','2026-03-13T19:38:21.976415','2026-03-13T19:38:21.976420','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('8fa8d7b4-2ef0-4901-a1de-0e7600c89197','Aqua MODIS Level-Regional Regional 11µm Day/Night Sea Surface Temperature (SST) Data, version R2019.0','MODIS (or Moderate-Resolution Imaging Spectroradiometer) is a key instrument aboard the Terra (EOS AM) and Aqua (EOS PM) satellites. Terra\'s orbit around the Earth is timed so that it passes from north to south across the equator in the morning, while Aqua passes south to north over the equator in the afternoon. Terra MODIS and Aqua MODIS are viewing the entire Earth\'s surface every 1 to 2 days, acquiring data in 36 spectral bands, or groups of wavelengths (see MODIS Technical Specifications). These data will improve our understanding of global dynamics and processes occurring on the land, in the oceans, and in the lower atmosphere. MODIS is playing a vital role in the development of validated, global, interactive Earth system models able to predict global change accurately enough to assist policy makers in making sound decisions concerning the protection of our environment.','public','2026-03-13T17:54:12.281111','2026-03-13T17:54:12.281116','OBPG;NASA/GSFC/SED/ESD/GCDC/OB.DAAC','Earthdata Forum','026:00','b6ed3b86-d179-4706-b94b-3a5a8f90cc9b','NASA Data.json','ebd000c4f3ab54cfaf36a2be92c25388ba28fe2f9928d05a2a641c86a29c3b5c','1.1','2026-03-13T17:54:12.281111','2026-03-13T17:54:12.281116','Earth Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('8fcb6914-3c31-4d05-b4fb-805441067dd9','Road Length by Measured Pavement Roughness, 2000-2024 (HM-64)','Annual road length by measured pavement roughness using the IRI (International Roughness Index) by functional class for the 50 states, DC, and PR from the Highway Statistics Series table HM-64.  Note: Missing 2010 and 2021,','public','2026-03-20T11:37:21.628535','2026-03-27T12:56:24.679386','Federal Highway Administration','Office of Highway Policy Information','021:15','e6f73119-f5c6-4935-81af-96075b9c3d5b','DOT Socrata Data.json','a2c26559dedf3c0e5d48e983f3d8e1c6fad4b51682df8c597c174fc96c2c8337','1.1','2026-03-20T11:37:21.628535','2026-03-27T12:56:24.679386','Transportation','021:009',0,'dot-gov'),('8fdf82a9-2e2f-44b2-94b8-0d2c49e3dbd2','MARS EXPRESS MARS MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 7 4130 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2019-01-01 to 2020-12-31. It is a Occultation measurement and covers the time 2020-09-14T23:17:54.000 to 2020-09-14T23:40:02.500.','public','2026-03-13T16:38:34.502024','2026-03-13T16:38:34.502029','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','db713fe6-96ec-429e-b4f7-71aecc5fdf51','NASA Data.json','eff6494a235752fbc4833ae0e7913e1d77c7aeeed1b7414b45fb9e6c26d99610','1.1','2026-03-13T16:38:34.502024','2026-03-13T16:38:34.502029','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('8fe98057-50fe-45f4-848e-a4450ce8af6c','Laborshed - Medical Premium Cost Share','Laborshed dataset containing data that covers the current and desired shares of healthcare premiums between employees and employers in all laborsheds in Iowa.','public','2026-03-28T22:00:46.984594','2026-03-28T22:00:46.984599','data.iowa.gov','svqueen',NULL,'9f5d30cd-2c4e-4dab-9d58-32a5dff53fc1','Iowa metadata','f3ef3893b5f248f86ba9b251a408718e4ad6b455ed2978b27298c6affd01a4d9','1.1','2026-03-28T22:00:46.984594','2026-03-28T22:00:46.984599','Economic Statistics',NULL,0,'state-of-iowa'),('8ff18113-014e-4be7-b97d-87a082167647','Continuous Fixed Station Water Quality Measurements in Cape Lookout National Seashore, August 2009 (Certified)','This dataset represents continuous water quality measurements that were taken at a fixed point in Cape Lookout National Seashore during the month of August, 2009 as a part of the Fixed Station Water Quality Monitoring protocol that was developed by the Southeast Coast I&M Network (SECN). The measurements were taken by a YSI 6600 ESD Multi-Parameter Long Term Water Quality Monitoring Datasonde unit that serves as the standard fixed station water quality monitoring equipment for all similar operations conducted by the SECN. The following parameters were measured at 15 minute intervals during the time period that has been specified: Water Temperature, Specific Conductivity, Salinity, Dissolved Oxygen (DO), DO Concentration, Shallow Depth, pH Level, and Turbidity. Any anomalies noted regarding these parameters have also been noted in separate fields.  Please note that these measurements have been certified by network personnel.','public','2026-03-26T05:27:48.104779','2026-03-26T05:27:48.104784','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','32dab45c-bee7-400a-ad85-4f150838bc16','DOI NPS DCAT-US','8e02f5a56212efc854e96a7cdec41975783be1b522767304679c62d7c58a34ed','1.1','2026-03-26T05:27:48.104779','2026-03-26T05:27:48.104784','Vector Dataset','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('9042228b-aae9-40f6-b477-d251e81a1307','Retrospective stepwise prioritization of chemicals detected in Great Lakes tributaries (2008–2018)','Supplementary material and data links for \"Retrospective stepwise prioritization of chemicals detected in Great Lakes tributaries (2008–2018)\". \n\nThis dataset is associated with the following publication:\nMaloney, E., S. Corsi, M. Pronschinske, L. DeCicco, J. Frisch, N. Fuller, A. Baldwin, K. Kimbrough, M. Edwards, S. Hummel, N. Garcia Reyero, and D. Villeneuve. Retrospective stepwise prioritization of chemicals detected in Great Lakes tributaries (2008–2018).   ENVIRONMENTAL TOXICOLOGY AND CHEMISTRY. Society of Environmental Toxicology and Chemistry, Pensacola, FL, USA, 44(7): 2048-2069, (2025).','public','2026-03-26T12:49:13.925755','2026-03-26T12:49:13.925759','U.S. Environmental Protection Agency','Daniel Villeneuve','020:00','63db8e46-9107-4828-9695-a5831be5a084','EPA ScienceHub','b9a23f066bf3ddcab901ae0194075b3f9f947d32c8636e59e3e034462cff5b6d','1.1','2026-03-26T12:49:13.925755','2026-03-26T12:49:13.925759',NULL,'020:000',0,'epa-gov'),('907776f0-b63d-4ca6-bb22-6678d734ef02','BLM ID Range Improvement Poly','This geodatabase of point, line and polygon features is an effort to consolidate all of the range improvement locations on BLM-managed land in Idaho into one database. Currently, the polygon feature class has some data for all of the BLM field offices except the Coeur d\'Alene and Cottonwood field offices. Range improvements are structures intended to enhance rangeland resources, including wildlife, watershed, and livestock management. Examples of range improvements include water troughs, spring headboxes, culverts, fences, water pipelines, gates, wildlife guzzlers, artificial nest structures, reservoirs, developed springs, corrals, exclosures, etc. These structures were first tracked by the Bureau of Land Management (BLM) in the Job Documentation Report (JDR) System in the early 1960s, which was predominately a paper-based tracking system. In 1988 the JDRs were migrated into and replaced by the automated Range Improvement Project System (RIPS), and version 2.0 is currently being used today. It tracks inventory, status, objectives, treatment, maintenance cycle, maintenance inspection, monetary contributions and reporting. Not all range improvements are documented in the RIPS database; there may be some older range improvements that were built before the JDR tracking system was established. There also may be unauthorized projects that are not in RIPS. Official project files of paper maps, reports, NEPA documents, checklists, etc., document the status of each project and are physically kept in the office with management authority for that project area. In addition, project data is entered into the RIPS system to enable managers to access the data to track progress, run reports, analyze the data, etc. Before Geographic Information System technology most offices kept paper atlases or overlay systems that mapped the locations of the range improvements. The objective of this geodatabase is to migrate the location of historic range improvement projects into a GIS for geospatial use with other data and to centralize the range improvement data for the state. This data set is a work in progress and does not have all range improvement projects that are on BLM lands. Some field offices have not migrated their data into this database, and others are partially completed. New projects may have been built but have not been entered into the system. Historic or unauthorized projects may not have case files and are being mapped and documented as they are found. Many field offices are trying to verify the locations and status of range improvements with GPS, and locations may change or projects that have been abandoned or removed on the ground may be deleted. Attributes may be incomplete or inaccurate. This data was created using the standard for range improvements set forth in Idaho IM 2009-044, dated 6/30/2009. However, it does not have all of the fields the standard requires. Fields that are missing from the polygon feature class that are in the standard are: ALLOT_NO, POLY_TYPE, MGMT_AGCY, ADMIN_ST, and ADMIN_OFF. The polygon feature class also does not have a coincident line feature class, so some of the fields from the polygon arc feature class are included in the polygon feature class: COORD_SRC, COORD_SRC2, DEF_FET, DEF_FEAT2, ACCURACY, CREATE_DT, CREATE_BY, MODIFY_DT, MODIFY_BY, GPS_DATE, and DATAFILE. There is no National BLM standard for GIS range improvement data at this time.  For more information contact us at blm_id_stateoffice@blm.gov.','public','2026-03-24T12:06:05.928494','2026-03-24T12:06:05.928500','Bureau of Land Management','Bureau of Land Management, id_so_information','010:04','206b3538-2761-4d06-8348-5392fdc6050d','DOI BLM DCAT-US','b96e33a969c128f7b57a89a2e5ebea95ce2f23aa1d83580d98e8b8611fb32798','1.1','2026-03-24T12:06:05.928494','2026-03-24T12:06:05.928500','geospatial','010:000',0,'doi-gov'),('907f072e-0059-4add-b7aa-baab29aac0d2','LP MOON ER LEVEL 4 ELECTRON DATA V1.0','Lunar Prospector Electron Reflectometer    (ER) Level 2 Data (CODMAC Level 4). Time ordered values of derived    quantities from electron reflection, including calculated effective    electron reflection coefficient.','public','2026-03-13T19:03:22.999542','2026-03-13T19:03:22.999547','planetary plasma interactions','Planetary Data System','026:00','96b2121c-a81e-402e-9425-8d4037e4580a','NASA Data.json','0d65d28a6530285b16adbd5e1a70e4a37600b10eb87afdf240fa2d884a2a3805','1.1','2026-03-13T19:03:22.999542','2026-03-13T19:03:22.999547','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('90a935b4-79bd-41c1-83a1-1da26b68bffe','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RPCMIP 5 EXT1 V1.0','This archive contains derived data from the RPC-MIP instrument on-board ROSETTA Orbiter acquired during the ROSETTA EXTENSION 1 mission phase. Observations are performed in the vicinity of comet 67P/C-G. It also contains documentation which describes the RPC-MIP experiment. The data archived in this data set conform to the Planetary Data System Standards, Version 3.6.','public','2026-03-13T18:47:15.837186','2026-03-13T18:47:15.837191','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','58ef2674-5aac-46ea-b26f-405e26c6b20b','NASA Data.json','32b21321a20339203c9a231736fed2bcbf2088865bff7de6c6b89cabc686416d','1.1','2026-03-13T18:47:15.837186','2026-03-13T18:47:15.837191','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('90ea2197-df69-404d-91b1-0690c49abdaa','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 3 1070 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 3 phase 2015-07-01 to 2015-10-21. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-10-01T03:05:50.000 to 2015-10-01T09:59:30.000.','public','2026-03-13T16:44:51.514190','2026-03-13T16:44:51.514194','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','311b7458-c054-4fe2-86d8-97af72995cdf','NASA Data.json','4712ceadfe3af6863ffd793cf9b6d14707858ef382f957edcad850be4f436cb3','1.1','2026-03-13T16:44:51.514190','2026-03-13T16:44:51.514194','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('90f99f14-b7df-4a7d-a66b-4548fef8d0f4','MARS EXPRESS MARS MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 3 3392 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2010-01-01 to 2012-12-31. It is a Global Gravity measurement and covers the time 2012-09-06T03:03:47.000 to 2012-09-06T05:45:10.500.','public','2026-03-13T16:52:06.834794','2026-03-13T16:52:06.834807','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','10f62dd9-e5e4-46a1-bd84-87a6394fc241','NASA Data.json','77f3d49cf2a756f1489ca602cdeaef49ecf8eb23349d7f9bfb92245180bf5a7e','1.1','2026-03-13T16:52:06.834794','2026-03-13T16:52:06.834807','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('9104c219-0a48-4e7e-9b02-d17cd5d58611','MARS EXPRESS MARS MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 3 3289 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2010-01-01 to 2012-12-31. It is a Global Gravity measurement and covers the time 2012-05-16T11:02:25.000 to 2012-05-16T12:39:16.500.','public','2026-03-13T17:38:08.788697','2026-03-13T17:38:08.788705','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','f2cb79fb-dca9-44ad-badf-3cfbe0188454','NASA Data.json','1b16a7c31d6078bbbc0c3c9abc919a5d94e134670098e0fcd60b90cf054a975f','1.1','2026-03-13T17:38:08.788697','2026-03-13T17:38:08.788705','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('9125d796-03f6-4fa6-a6c3-1872f7a0ae81','Data from: Rapid formation of abiotic CO2 after adding phenolic gallic acid, to agricultural soils','<p dir=\"ltr\">Abiotic efflux of CO<sub>2</sub> from soil is typically attributed to weathering of carbonates but also may be from basic biological and chemical processes in the soil such as concurrent oxidation of organic matter and reduction of metal oxides. However, little is known about how such reactions vary due to differences in the soil environment . An experiment was conducted to measure CO<sub>2</sub> emissions formed during 4-h incubations of soil from different management systems (n = 5), archived benchmark soils from sites across the U.S. (n = 18), and samples of reagent-grade metal oxides (n = 4). Treatments included water, pH 4 phthalate buffer, glucose (0.029 M), or gallic acid (0.025 M). Gallic acid is a simple phenolic constituent of root exudates found in the soil that can result in redox reactions producing CO<sub>2</sub>. Data may be used to understand processes contributing to abiotic sources of CO<sub>2</sub> from agricultural land.</p>','public','2026-03-13T22:49:14.865377','2026-03-13T22:49:14.865384','Agricultural Research Service','Halvorson, Jonathan J.','005:18','e70cbc4c-ff93-4be6-b75b-7728a9cb5ca6','USDA JSON','ea883bc39fee04d727929f38958221703eb5a9ac1c5a610e83a895758883be4e','1.1','2026-03-13T22:49:14.865377','2026-03-13T22:49:14.865384',NULL,'005:040',0,'usda-gov'),('91302978-a804-4f57-8525-344ea079d562','myUSCIS - command-center','Admin application for feature toggles to control production lauches of forms and features. Also contains other troubleshooting tools for developers or supporting the application. (Permanent)','non-public','2026-03-22T11:53:38.576816','2026-03-22T11:53:38.576821','Unspecified','Open Data (MGMT)','024:030','531e4b6c-d519-4a85-9ab3-c7680e7d1946','DHS datajson source','63771c734f8bb17d5cdf89d2c15e00ebc5952495a3193facb4a484d7046fd2f5','1.1','2026-03-22T11:53:38.576816','2026-03-22T11:53:38.576821',NULL,'024:000',0,'dhs-gov'),('91345355-38e6-4596-ba24-7b2a1f53c252','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSIWAC 4 PRL-MTP009 RDR-INF-REFL V1.0','This CODMAC level 4 data set contains solar stray-light corrected, in-field stray-light corrected,  radiometric calibrated and geometric distortion corrected  (resampled) image data in reflectance units (normalized  and thus without unit),  acquired by the OSIRIS Wide Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft  during the PRELANDING mission phase, covering the period  from 2014-10-24T10:00:00.000 to 2014-11-21T23:24:59.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V1.0 is the first version of this dataset: Lien corrected dataset after September 2019 PSA/PDS external peer review.','public','2026-03-13T17:50:54.559970','2026-03-13T17:50:54.559975','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','ef24f3db-c46d-476a-a723-ccf3121bca9d','NASA Data.json','3032cce32929d13c6f2e20b075e05751c86838f709ac5978d5275f942fbf8edc','1.1','2026-03-13T17:50:54.559970','2026-03-13T17:50:54.559975','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('914086fe-20a5-40ca-8b23-9a183f1d236e','DS1 IDS (PLASMA WAVE SPECTROMETER) DATA V1.0','This data set present plasma wave spectrometer data from the IDS instrument flown aboard the Deep Space 1 spacecraft. The data are observations of Comet 19P/Borrelly 1 obtained during the flyby of 22 September 2001.','public','2026-03-13T18:50:40.030055','2026-03-13T18:50:40.030061','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','16b1639a-35c9-461f-9045-e6f0e93991be','NASA Data.json','1a1dc9a55822175d83f8968841912ed56d95b08e6937beea0a6dd077e9c58fb8','1.1','2026-03-13T18:50:40.030055','2026-03-13T18:50:40.030061','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('9163b2ea-3cac-4249-907f-30f92b800029','MARS EXPRESS SUN MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 4 3562 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2013-01-01 to 2014-12-31. It is a Solar Conjunction measurement and covers the time 2013-04-22T13:23:18 to 2013-04-23T17:29:04.000.','public','2026-03-13T18:57:26.155396','2026-03-13T18:57:26.155401','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','62e9b8d5-1c1d-48cb-8bb6-56c2847ed05d','NASA Data.json','9b6e873ac4ed621e37c3a6954908c5fded7988ed8a390d03fda0791fbf429e82','1.1','2026-03-13T18:57:26.155396','2026-03-13T18:57:26.155401','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('9164ccfa-e435-49ea-933c-64fafcaac739','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RPCMAG 2 ESC4 RAW V9.0','This dataset contains EDITED RAW DATA (CODMAC LEVEL 2) of theCOMET ESCORT 4 Phase from October 21, 2015 until January 12, 2016of the ROSETTA orbiter magnetometer RPCMAG. Observations are done inthe vicinity of comet 67P/CHURYUMOV-GERASIMENKO 1 (1969 R1).The current version of the dataset is V9.0.The difference to the datasets of earlier versions is mainly a significantlyimproved sensor temperature model, more detailed documentation about magneticdisturbance sources, more data handling information for the user andalso an improved quality flagging system.This applies mainly to CALIBRATED and RESAMPLED datasets. The RAW dataset,however, has been updated as well in order provide all datasets at thesame stage, although RAW data proper did not change.','public','2026-03-13T18:03:56.616808','2026-03-13T18:03:56.616817','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','80bcfdb0-96cc-4c19-9e0f-6b979217f8ae','NASA Data.json','0da84ca98d0244609176d0bd40288804bd92698c2b9238b67b7b603a49adca5c','1.1','2026-03-13T18:03:56.616808','2026-03-13T18:03:56.616817','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('917a8a43-e7cc-4162-bf42-c4607ff7b1c3','ARECIBO VENUS RADIO TELESCOPE RESAMPLED 12.6 CM RADAR V1.0','The Arecibo 12.6 cm radar data set for Venus consists of scaled radar backscatter cross section images generated from data obtained in 1983 and 1988. The images are in raster format (one image per record, with no embedded labels). The original images are in 16-bit, unsigned integer, most-significant-byte-first format. Since the volume of the entire set of 16-bit images would have exceeded the capacity of the CD-ROM, some of the images have been scaled to 8-bit versions. Specifically, the entire set of 1988 images are in the scaled 8-bit format, while all the 1983 images are in the original 16-bit format. Both the 16-bit and the 8-bit images were provided by Don Campbell, Cornell University.','public','2026-03-13T19:39:47.997632','2026-03-13T19:39:47.997638','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','4ca1404e-34d0-4221-a95f-1134a36d8bba','NASA Data.json','00393f27e96bea77cc3dffd75fef8d7229e5254a894f8e5b5ce39a4662b00b73','1.1','2026-03-13T19:39:47.997632','2026-03-13T19:39:47.997638','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('918dddaf-0de9-47c0-9eff-dc0ad1a3cca5','Hydrographic and Impairment Statistics Database: NPS-WSR Mulchatna Wild and Scenic River','Hydrographic and Impairment Statistics (HIS) is a National Park Service (NPS) Water Resources Division (WRD) project established to track certain goals created in response to the Government Performance and Results Act of 1993 (GPRA). One water resources management goal established by the Department of the Interior under GRPA requires NPS to track the percent of its managed surface waters that are meeting Clean Water Act (CWA) water quality standards. This goal requires an accurate inventory that spatially quantifies the surface water hydrography that each bureau manages and a procedure to determine and track which waterbodies are or are not meeting water quality standards as outlined by Section 303(d) of the CWA. This project helps meet this DOI GRPA goal by inventorying and monitoring in a geographic information system for the NPS: (1) CWA 303(d) quality impaired waters and causes; and (2) hydrographic statistics based on the United States Geological Survey (USGS) National Hydrography Dataset (NHD). Hydrographic and 303(d) impairment statistics were evaluated based on a combination of 1:24,000 (NHD) and finer scale data (frequently provided by state GIS layers).','public','2026-03-29T06:06:11.372805','2026-03-29T06:06:11.372810','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','46d96313-4794-4d6e-a7a6-89ec4143a680','DOI NPS DCAT-US','cbac144a014d9c0406e2924b0624aaa28e084b5fee7ad78f5720228265a8290b','1.1','2026-03-29T06:06:11.372805','2026-03-29T06:06:11.372810','geospatial','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('91947edc-95a6-4bad-ac5c-5dae67442f24','ROSETTA-ORBITER EARTH RPCICA 2 EAR2 UNCALIBRATED V3.0','This dataset contains RAW DATA from the RPCICA instrument onmission ROSETTA during the second Earth swingby. RPC-ICA was on, butdid not obtain any useful measurements.Data set version 3 replaces a previously delivered data set.Important changes are the the expansion of data to a uniform resolution,Inclusion of the mode variable and new quality flags in the data andmoving information about software version, BAD_HV_MASK and SHADOW_MASKto the label.','public','2026-03-13T17:06:01.004050','2026-03-13T17:06:01.004058','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','021fc18f-7324-4d2a-9498-99067e6e6338','NASA Data.json','5ab64a92a69ad56aaf3310a4eab4b6c797c14fd1c4adc45639ba1f251fd54833','1.1','2026-03-13T17:06:01.004050','2026-03-13T17:06:01.004058','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('91ab9f93-db45-4fde-bec0-ef80a6282bc4','MARS EXPRESS MARS MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 8 4268 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2021-01-01 to 2022-12-31. It is a Occultation measurement and covers the time 2022-05-25T07:45:18.000 to 2022-05-25T10:00:03.000.','public','2026-03-13T18:00:16.653205','2026-03-13T18:00:16.653211','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','2e3b1853-f1bd-40cc-9764-56d4b30868bb','NASA Data.json','5a4804661c48e03876a4365849dae393305d85e44aadda90121878d5b8176ab1','1.1','2026-03-13T18:00:16.653205','2026-03-13T18:00:16.653211','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('91d85528-76a2-42cc-a8e4-6c0a9528bbf1','Continuous Fixed Station Water Quality Measurements in Canaveral National Seashore, November 2007 (Certified)','This dataset represents continuous water quality measurements that were taken at a fixed point in Canaveral National Seashore during the month of November, 2007 as a part of the Fixed Station Water Quality Monitoring protocol that was developed by the Southeast Coast I&M Network (SECN). The measurements were taken by a YSI 6600 ESD Multi-Parameter Long Term Water Quality Monitoring Datasonde unit that serves as the standard fixed station water quality monitoring equipment for all similar operations conducted by the SECN. The following parameters were measured at 30 minute intervals during the time period that has been specified: Water Temperature, Specific Conductivity, Salinity, Dissolved Oxygen (DO), DO Concentration, Shallow Depth, pH Level, and Turbidity. Any anomalies noted regarding these parameters have also been noted in separate fields. Please note that these measurements have been certified by network personnel.','public','2026-03-26T05:31:37.131850','2026-03-26T05:31:37.131855','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','a363ede0-e03c-4eba-8bd3-e6769583458e','DOI NPS DCAT-US','22b70f7584b0d442a131d3749f2d61b3f24c81c86ca977b4b42178134b3494b6','1.1','2026-03-26T05:31:37.131850','2026-03-26T05:31:37.131855','Vector Dataset','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('91ef85e4-d2d9-426b-9c95-0cf3ae5fad3b','MARS EXPRESS MARS MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 3 3356 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2010-01-01 to 2012-12-31. It is a Global Gravity measurement and covers the time 2012-07-21T06:19:11.000 to 2012-07-21T09:55:22.500.','public','2026-03-13T19:51:53.611531','2026-03-13T19:51:53.611536','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','2df8a212-4b4c-4ae3-9a24-76832942541b','NASA Data.json','28b897d66e57829cc866ee6939621d88c6f152505e2c782dc21f331b1c1dab86','1.1','2026-03-13T19:51:53.611531','2026-03-13T19:51:53.611536','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('927d9fdf-1584-4f00-956c-88836e00cc6c','MARS EXPRESS SUN MRS 1/2/3                                     EXTENDED MISSION 8 4404 V1.0','This is a Mars Express                                     Radio Science data set, collected                                     during the extended mission phase                                     2023-01-01 to 2023-12-31.                                     It is a Solar Conjunction                                     measurement and covers the time                                     2023-12-22T22:07:48.000 to                                     2023-12-22T23:17:02.000.','public','2026-03-13T18:50:17.827913','2026-03-13T18:50:17.827921','geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','d5aea820-2880-4b29-9fbe-4a46cd9bf463','NASA Data.json','b0b49b9afa8440b127cd9c1250f8dc6cff9e00d87c49efaed435a370387e14c6','1.1','2026-03-13T18:50:17.827913','2026-03-13T18:50:17.827921','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('9297a97e-106c-4039-a65b-ed4f64931cdb','ROSETTA-ORBITER EARTH OSIWAC 4 EAR1 RDR-REFLECT V1.0','This CODMAC level 4 data set contains radiometric calibrated and geometric distortion corrected (resampled)  image data in reflectance units (normalized and thus without unit),  acquired by the OSIRIS Wide Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft  during the EARTH SWING-BY 1 mission phase, covering the period  from 2004-10-17T00:00:00.000 to 2005-04-04T23:59:59.000. The prime target is planet Earth. This version V1.0 is the first version of this dataset.','public','2026-03-13T18:59:16.553563','2026-03-13T18:59:16.553569','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','bdc6f7b2-b66f-473e-a5ed-423cd61da731','NASA Data.json','2efd5752993d5440dfc1e574973584b683202244b9b8d60df970f0fd20600051','1.1','2026-03-13T18:59:16.553563','2026-03-13T18:59:16.553569','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('92c3d157-3192-4ad0-91fa-7a528956b759','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 1 0570 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 1 phase 2014-11-20 to 2015-03-10. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-02-09T11:06:40.000 to 2015-02-09T22:33:38.000.','public','2026-03-13T17:02:52.423490','2026-03-13T17:02:52.423496','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','266eb746-de0b-4f40-a318-3ff7eada5cd0','NASA Data.json','5ed98b252b2b5bbc8c66709825ef9add4d75ce2ad43a632a50cc63f8f900c0b5','1.1','2026-03-13T17:02:52.423490','2026-03-13T17:02:52.423496','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('92e48ca5-b512-4944-8feb-8f5b7358c7cf','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSINAC 4 EXT3-MTP035 RDR-STR-REFL V1.0','This CODMAC level 4 data set contains solar stray light corrected, radiometric calibrated and geometric distortion corrected (resampled) image data in in reflectance units (normalized and thus without unit), acquired by the OSIRIS Narrow Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft during the ROSETTA EXTENSION 3 mission phase, covering the period from 2016-09-26T06:40:00.000 to 2016-10-01T00:00:00.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V1.0 is the first version of this dataset: Lien corrected dataset after October 2018 PSA/PDS external peer review.','public','2026-03-13T17:25:09.321695','2026-03-13T17:25:09.321702','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','f9d04a35-7780-4541-b2d4-c96ca5e96491','NASA Data.json','7e70c83b7dea721542c55c15ddafed2e2b9e71d274b06134f5eddb63f2c6c875','1.1','2026-03-13T17:25:09.321695','2026-03-13T17:25:09.321702','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('92eab661-56af-4bac-bf66-2769b8239ce4','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P MIRO 4 EXT3 V2.0','This data set contains Spectroscopic and Continuum level 4 data, in the form of table files, taken during the ROSETTA EXTENSION 3 phase of the Rosetta mission to comet 67P/CHURYUMOV-GERASIMENKO by the MIRO instrument. The major updates with this version (V2.0) are the addition of a Level 4 continuum data product and the elimination of separate geometry files for the spectroscopic data.','public','2026-03-13T17:36:30.095095','2026-03-13T17:36:30.095103','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','b348c430-b88e-4a46-ad08-3539c509c118','NASA Data.json','282ae923bd4c5814cf54857be8b8a9d434c6f38d720f9a6d0cff78c1e68ced1a','1.1','2026-03-13T17:36:30.095095','2026-03-13T17:36:30.095103','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('92ef471d-49f6-414a-90d5-a315bbca221b','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSIWAC 3 PRL-MTP008 RDR V3.0','This CODMAC level 3 data set contains radiometric calibrated image data in W/m^2/sr/nm, acquired by the OSIRIS Wide Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft during the PRELANDING mission phase, covering the period from 2014-09-23T10:00:00.000 to 2014-10-24T09:59:59.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V3.0 supersedes previous deliveries of the same dataset with the following changes since the last version: Lien corrected dataset after the July and October 2018 PSA/PDS external peer reviews. Updated documentation and ancillary files, added document on bandpass filter. Updated SCIENCE_USER_GUIDE_V03.PDF to include one section about FAQ and one section about image data quality. Added shutter backtravel and readout issues to image quality map. Updated DATA_QUALITY_ID keyword in image header. Improved handling of images with missing packets. Included FITs files. Browse products changed to the same size as the original image.','public','2026-03-13T18:14:19.820719','2026-03-13T18:14:19.820723','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','afd5fa1e-a032-4161-b13a-e4d7f8831750','NASA Data.json','1030cd74d37dc0ab8e57d2cecc096c9a4e12692dd603fc8e08c3420e28e49e55','1.1','2026-03-13T18:14:19.820719','2026-03-13T18:14:19.820723','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('930cedf7-3b90-4994-ac0f-55916d6291f8','ROSETTA-ORBITER COMET ESCORT 1 OSIWAC 2 EDR MTP013 V2.0','This data set contains images acquired by the OSIRIS Wide Angle Camera during the COMET ESCORT 1 phase of the Rosetta mission at the comet 67P, covering the period from 2015-02-10T23:25:00.000 to 2015-03-10T23:24:59.000. This version V2.0 supersedes previous deliveries of the same dataset.','public','2026-03-13T18:59:43.826638','2026-03-13T18:59:43.826644','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','d537ae18-4a2c-454c-810c-2fa87f286725','NASA Data.json','5f8f9449d18a54766b19174a23b09608fdb883f7fa6d0c4bbf46fe7a71ed0b3d','1.1','2026-03-13T18:59:43.826638','2026-03-13T18:59:43.826644','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('9327c210-f3ee-4e06-bd00-b720535e7623','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RPCICA 4 PRL PHYS-MASS V1.0','This dataset contains RESAMPLED CALIBRATED DATA separated into4 physical mass ranges, corresponding to H+, He++, He+ and heavier ions(mass 1, 2, 4, 16 amu and above), from the RPCICA instrumenton mission ROSETTA during the prelanding phase.Data contains measurements of an undisturbed solar wind untilRosetta was close enough to the comet to obtain measurements ofthe solar wind interaction with the atmosphere of target comet 67P.','public','2026-03-13T18:51:45.440108','2026-03-13T18:51:45.440128','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','43dbf687-52ac-49e7-b165-b2bbeb9da4ec','NASA Data.json','62936e56cb5fad8f30712038e5b7a209e351bd2a204cb08005cb773ba430e26a','1.1','2026-03-13T18:51:45.440108','2026-03-13T18:51:45.440128','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('937419e5-5b2e-43ef-8fb5-74c8cb51ac96','ULY JUP GRB SOLAR X-RAY/COSMIC GAMMA-RAY RAW COUNT RATE','The archived data consist of count                                    rates from the sum of two hemispherical                                    detectors covering 4 pi steradians and                                    operating continuously. The detectors                                    are 3 mm thick CsI scintillators                                    coupled to photomultiplier tubes. The                                    nominal energy range is 25-150 keV, but                                    the below table should be consulted to                                    find the accurate thresholds for any day                                    of the mission. Although the prime                                    objectives of this investigation are the                                    study of solar and cosmic x- and                                    gamma-ray bursts, it should be noted                                    that the experiment is also sensitive                                    to solar protons and electrons. The                                    former deposit energy directly in the                                    scintillator if they are energetic                                    enough, while the latter may produce                                    x- radiation locally by bremsstrahlung.                                    Thus although the counting rates are                                    generally stable at about 500 c/s over                                    the long term, there are periods of                                    weeks to a month or so when the rates                                    increase considerably due to particles.                                    Examples may be found in March 1991                                    (solar protons) and February 1992                                    (particles in the Jovian magnetosphere).                                    The time resolution of the data takes                                    on one of four values depending on the                                    telemetry rate and instrument operating                                    mode: 0.25, 0.5, 1, or 2 seconds.','public','2026-03-13T19:34:00.908818','2026-03-13T19:34:00.908824','planetary plasma interactions','Planetary Data System','026:00','269d3d69-bbc2-4539-912b-dc64fae64f27','NASA Data.json','d4829285b3418a1227af27a4000b65fbade514a29fcdeaeb73c867e5d64134b3','1.1','2026-03-13T19:34:00.908818','2026-03-13T19:34:00.908824','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('938c91d9-38e9-4d9d-97fd-c06b1cd604fb','IHW COMET HALLEY METEOR ETA AQUARID VISUAL DATA V1.0','NASA\'s International Halley Watch (IHW) has created a Comet Halley Archive. The collection of data spans the full wavelength range as submitted by scientists to the IHW. The observations belong to one of the following Disciplines: Amateur, Astrometry, Infrared Studies, Large-Scale Phenomena, Meteor Studies, Near-Nucleus Studies, Photometry and Polarimetry, Radio Studies, and Spectroscopy and Spectrophotometry. The data collected by these nine disciplines were augmented by Spacecraft measurements. The data were submitted to IHW, but the evaluation and selection for the Archive has been the primary responsibility of the Discipline Specialist Teams for each network in cooperation with the Lead Center. The visual data for Eta Aquarid contains 579 observations, spanning dates 1984 April 27 through 1987 May 11.','public','2026-03-13T18:59:28.921617','2026-03-13T18:59:28.921622','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','bee8dbb0-fca6-46b2-ba73-a5720633d962','NASA Data.json','adafa40562792b71e6213dbda43c31c011277cd55c2ce72c9508ae469be272d8','1.1','2026-03-13T18:59:28.921617','2026-03-13T18:59:28.921622','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('93e81968-045d-4443-95bf-273d41472a5f','MARS EXPRESS SUN MRS 1/2/3                                     EXTENDED MISSION 8 4372 V1.0','This is a Mars Express                                     Radio Science data set, collected                                     during the extended mission phase                                     2023-01-01 to 2023-12-31.                                     It is a Solar Conjunction                                     measurement and covers the time                                     2023-11-29T05:05:00.000 to                                     2023-11-29T09:32:39.000.','public','2026-03-13T19:10:48.124403','2026-03-13T19:10:48.124409','geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','d9fa8512-ccfc-41cd-bde1-941ce0cb1b2d','NASA Data.json','838c080ff80fcf212af7ba40095b5916e76d434849735c4df7dbaf4fc0115447','1.1','2026-03-13T19:10:48.124403','2026-03-13T19:10:48.124409','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('93eb6bc9-bc0e-492f-9f57-98a099b028f9','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 2 0724 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 2 phase 2015-03-11 to 2015-06-30. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-04-22T02:01:55.000 to 2015-04-22T07:49:24.500.','public','2026-03-13T16:56:35.747534','2026-03-13T16:56:35.747539','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','2403800c-86b3-445c-bf25-21ed25dbb2d2','NASA Data.json','be6d8162aa298e2b7a6a697180797ad417a83fd67970172663c95323e1c3a6dc','1.1','2026-03-13T16:56:35.747534','2026-03-13T16:56:35.747539','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('942360d2-e994-4fc5-9f12-0bedb26c35b7','Continuous Fixed Station Water Quality Measurements in Timucuan Ecological and Historic Preserve, November 2008 (Certified)','This dataset represents continuous water quality measurements that were taken at a fixed point in Timucuan Ecological and Historic Preserve during the month of November, 2008 as a part of the Fixed Station Water Quality Monitoring protocol that was developed by the Southeast Coast I&M Network (SECN). The measurements were taken by a YSI 6600 ESD Multi-Parameter Long Term Water Quality Monitoring Datasonde unit that serves as the standard fixed station water quality monitoring equipment for all similar operations conducted by the SECN. The following parameters were measured at 30 minute intervals during the time period that has been specified: Water Temperature, Specific Conductivity, Salinity, Dissolved Oxygen (DO), DO Concentration, Shallow Depth, pH Level, and Turbidity. Any anomalies noted regarding these parameters have also been noted in separate fields. Please note that these measurements have been certified by network personnel.','public','2026-03-26T05:30:09.014229','2026-03-26T05:30:09.014237','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','9f70d2d3-8015-4fc0-997c-44ec7e730ad1','DOI NPS DCAT-US','a08b9ef6bbf39cc246885e2a0512b23de713a6b766ea1987261e241ea2c23821','1.1','2026-03-26T05:30:09.014229','2026-03-26T05:30:09.014237','Vector Dataset','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('94275efb-62df-4ca0-805a-604a9c539a10','ROSETTA-ORBITER COMET ESCORT 3 OSINAC 2 EDR MTP020 V1.0','This data set contains images acquired by the OSIRIS Narrow Angle Camera during the COMET ESCORT 3 phase of the Rosetta mission at the comet 67P, covering the period from 2015-08-25T23:25:00.000 to 2015-09-22T23:24:59.000.','public','2026-03-13T17:11:25.433368','2026-03-13T17:11:25.433376','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','598efa1e-c2a9-41e7-a187-56df729227a5','NASA Data.json','a5d906db2d1c6607c9c46e045276f85ac8c07888d2a56898628900d2bfbb495c','1.1','2026-03-13T17:11:25.433368','2026-03-13T17:11:25.433376','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('94426ece-1d1a-4e09-8960-f1d4afd18cb4','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 3 1033 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 3 phase 2015-07-01 to 2015-10-21. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-09-14T21:19:30.000 to 2015-09-15T05:26:13.500.','public','2026-03-13T18:46:58.018744','2026-03-13T18:46:58.018751','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','186daca0-cb86-4bea-989d-7921f96d69c3','NASA Data.json','61b4101b4c4e7f7248592258fdb7d439c5776d985b8c1dee49f8a9fc19471061','1.1','2026-03-13T18:46:58.018744','2026-03-13T18:46:58.018751','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('947df8f0-b063-4861-a625-e657421618f6','Statewide Laborshed Trends - Commute Data','A subset of the statewide laborshed trends dataset that contains respondents\' miles and minutes willing to travel for employment','public','2026-03-28T22:00:32.649860','2026-03-28T22:00:32.649866','data.iowa.gov','svqueen',NULL,'f2477d20-c54b-4a2e-a012-038110c936a2','Iowa metadata','bba1d4a4f3a1f728d99c7c896342e3c80b094f2d72e271ca4a666a497d426060','1.1','2026-03-28T22:00:32.649860','2026-03-28T22:00:32.649866','Economic Statistics',NULL,0,'state-of-iowa'),('9496e9ef-977b-4b2c-9603-2246eb7e73b2','NEW HORIZONS  SDC PLUTO ENCOUNTER  RAW V3.0','This data set contains Raw data taken by the New Horizons  Student Dust Counter  instrument during the  Pluto encounter  mission phase. This is VERSION 3.0 of this data set.   This data set contains SDC observations taken during the  the Approach (Jan-Jul, 2015), Encounter, Departure, and  Transition mission sub-phases, including flyby observations  taken on 14 July, 2015, and departure and calibration data  through late October, 2016. This data set completes the  Pluto mission phase deliveries for SDC.   This is version 3.0 of this data set. Changes since version 2.0  include the final batch of Pluto mission phase data, downlinked  between the end of January, 2016 and late in October, 2016, including  a Stim calibration in July. Also, updates were made to the  documentation and catalog files, primarily to implement suggestions  from the V2.0 peer review. A new table of SDC Ram (velocity)  ancillary data has been provided, and the SDC on/off and Stim tables  have been extended in time to cover the new data.','public','2026-03-13T17:47:43.129466','2026-03-13T17:47:43.129472','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','102cae53-033f-45f9-9ee9-a56fd16820ba','NASA Data.json','499b1aad8c018fc0720c68db929d0d643f0ba7ee18b6687a3f7308ce1d661b4e','1.1','2026-03-13T17:47:43.129466','2026-03-13T17:47:43.129472','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('94b1666e-2866-4747-a750-eee9b3bb2b10','HRRR Meteorology, Energy, and Transmission (MET) Toolkit','The HRRR MET (Meteorology, Energy, and Transmission) Toolkit is the National Laboratory of the Rockies\' (NLR) new flagship atmospheric dataset, designed to support comprehensive long-term planning and operations across the entire power sector. Serving as the direct successor to the legacy WIND Toolkit, this dataset provides a continuously updatable, high-fidelity meteorological record covering the Continental United States (CONUS). To ensure a seamless transition for modelers conducting multi-decadal grid integration and capacity expansion studies, the HRRR MET Toolkit is delivered at an hourly resolution on the exact same 2-km horizontal grid as the original WIND Toolkit.\n\nRepackaged from the National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration\'s (NOAA) operational High-Resolution Rapid Refresh (HRRR) forecasts, the dataset bridges the critical gap between historical industry baselines and modern operational weather data. Spanning from 2015 to the present with planned annual extensions, it overcomes the technical barriers of native weather models by providing spatial regridding, temporal gap-filling, and vertical interpolation at key energy-relevant heights. By delivering highly accurate, validation-backed data across a comprehensive suite of atmospheric variables -including temperature, pressure, humidity, and wind characteristics - the HRRR MET Toolkit provides a highly accessible and strictly standardized foundation for modern power system modeling.','public','2026-03-26T12:42:58.961119','2026-03-26T12:42:58.961124','National Laboratory of the Rockies (NLR)','Nicola Bodini','019:20','8d14d1dd-ec40-4ae6-b3d8-badf4bcb2e48','OpenEI data.json','5f066ff43981abde6a1df7a299053bad502dedeee94069f575b3e5ff181c7475','1.1','2026-03-26T12:42:58.961119','2026-03-26T12:42:58.961124',NULL,'019:000',0,'doe-gov'),('94f6859b-df21-4546-a05c-9de8aab62fea','BLM ID Boise District Orchard Training Area Military Proposed Poly','This is the boundary of the Orchard Training Area (OTA) in the Morley Nelson Snake River Birds of Prey (BOP) National Conservation Area (NCA). This data set is limited to the BOP area. The Orchard Training area is a training area for the Idaho Army National Guard. This is a field training area (maneuver area) for non-active duty Idaho National Guard. A 1979 Memorandum of Understanding (MOU) between BLM and the Idaho Army National Guard allows for continued military use of this area. There is public access to the Orchard Training Area and recreation and grazing is allowed in this area. This area contains the Orchard Training Area Impact Area and the Artillery Impact Area. Current to September 2009. Data Attributes include: District Name, Field Office Name, District Code, Field Office Code, Area Name and Acres.','public','2026-03-25T12:34:49.834597','2026-03-25T12:34:49.834601','Bureau of Land Management','Bureau of Land Management, blm_id_stateoffice','010:04','3465a40c-d8af-42d5-9f8d-720e95a0c020','DOI BLM DCAT-US','8639d081d715e026c9b8bfce05c07cd366a5f7671c6d95b66446cca47bf9407c','1.1','2026-03-25T12:34:49.834597','2026-03-25T12:34:49.834601','geospatial','010:000',0,'doi-gov'),('95078462-9462-48d7-964c-f0ab4bb6807f','Violence Reduction Data Portal Visualizations Replaced by Violence Reduction Dashboard','Announcement of violence reduction data portal visualizations replaced by violence reduction dashboard launched in 2021.','public','2026-03-29T04:50:09.621709','2026-03-29T04:50:09.621714','data.cityofchicago.org','Maria Fiorillo',NULL,'cff27de7-0000-4352-a66d-0e8d144e60df','Chicago JSON','002e2465c425b41e2117f6d759aa8a33e264fb132b1aba45bcccc5dcb414d1c0','1.1','2026-03-29T04:50:09.621709','2026-03-29T04:50:09.621714','Health & Human Services',NULL,0,'city-of-chicago'),('9528746e-75e1-4153-98d1-baeadf818b0c','NEW HORIZONS  LORRI JUPITER ENCOUNTER  RAW V3.0','This data set contains Raw data taken by the New Horizons  Long Range Reconnaissance Imager  instrument during the  Jupiter encounter  mission phase. This is VERSION 3.0 of this data set.   LORRI science observations for the Jupiter Phase include  observations of the Jovian system: the Jovian atmosphere and  clouds including full disk rotation movie and resolved images of  selected features like the Great Red Spot and the Little Red Spot;  Jovian ring system and associated small satellites; the Galilean  satellites with particular attention to Io under both sunlit and  eclipse conditions, and eclipse observations of both Europa and  Ganymede; the small irregular satellites Elara, Himalia,  Callirrhoe. Additional observations were taken to test and/or  characterize and/or calibrate the modes and performance of the  LORRI.   LORRI V3.0 provides a few updates from LORRI V2.0. The lossy images  were recalibrated, including expanding the \'bad\' pixel designation  of 8x8 boxes affected by the first 34 pixels of header information  in the calibrated quality map. Also, updates were made to the  documentation and catalog files, primarily to resolve liens from the  V2.0 peer review. No new observations were added with Version 3.0','public','2026-03-13T19:44:28.958379','2026-03-13T19:44:28.958385','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','f3fc2815-561f-4ae3-a2ed-a403f5076cf0','NASA Data.json','9af25edbc8729ba51b23304c3e56dbaebc1fc619e9031ef5e9ab0eaa24d03211','1.1','2026-03-13T19:44:28.958379','2026-03-13T19:44:28.958385','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('956d450c-181c-40f7-817c-f616f4da7715','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSINAC 5 ESC1-MTP011 DDR-GEO V1.0','This CODMAC level 5 data set contains derived data products that include pixel-precise georeferencing information, acquired by the OSIRIS Narrow Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft during the COMET ESCORT 1 mission phase, covering the period from 2014-12-19T23:25:00.000 to 2015-01-13T23:24:59.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V1.0 is the first version of this dataset: Lien corrected dataset after October 2018 PSA/PDS external peer review.','public','2026-03-13T17:20:45.336675','2026-03-13T17:20:45.336681','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','1c62a39a-10c6-4497-b4de-4117caa7892f','NASA Data.json','5aed3a8505b463bb413545f4ff3b2a230f4bb9516a59f359d3980891f665756f','1.1','2026-03-13T17:20:45.336675','2026-03-13T17:20:45.336681','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('957ce7f1-d239-4af7-bdd4-495c1a6e1445','BLM ID District Office Administrative Unit Boundary','<div style=\'text-align:Left;\'><div><div style=\'font-size:12pt\'><p><span>This data set shows the Idaho BLM District boundaries and names as per the Organization Refinement for FY 2004, which became official on October 1, 2003 (FY04), plus subsequent edits. This dataset has been updated over time. A Bureau of Land Management (BLM) Administrative Unit is a geographic area in which an organizational unit of the BLM has distinct jurisdictional responsibility for land and resource management activities occurring on the public lands, the maintained rights of the United States (i.e. mineral estate) and actions relating to the Trust responsibilities of the U.S. Government as stipulated in Law or Treaty. District Offices are the middle tier of BLM\'s three-tier organization, providing coordination, oversight and support to the lowest level, the Field Office, and overseen by the State Office.  For more information contact us at blm_id_stateoffice@blm.gov.</span></p></div></div></div>','public','2026-03-18T11:12:00.675581','2026-03-18T11:12:00.675588','Bureau of Land Management','Bureau of Land Management, id_so_information','010:04','3e7af677-9eb7-467c-b59f-05b5e76b4c7b','DOI BLM DCAT-US','a1ccf45e3b9b6a5688bf6e9f332e6ac1fd8842be16845005f9307e53ff796a62','1.1','2026-03-18T11:12:00.675581','2026-03-18T11:12:00.675588','geospatial','010:000',0,'doi-gov'),('9615dd20-379e-436a-af12-2a437c0120f6','Total Receipts for Highways by Governmental Unit (REC-C)','Total receipts for highways by State, local, and federal spending from the Federal Highway Administration\'s Office of Policy Information\'s Highway Statistics Series.','public','2026-03-27T12:57:51.851972','2026-03-27T12:57:51.851977','Federal Highway Administration','Office of Highway Policy Information','021:15','5c09a301-ac4e-409f-961e-d82dea75f9fd','DOT Socrata Data.json','5bd84d36b1f88c9163d734fa6400967d417b8f4a4b0457286b41a7366cc02253','1.1','2026-03-27T12:57:51.851972','2026-03-27T12:57:51.851977','Roadways and Bridges','021:009',0,'dot-gov'),('9620e148-7efa-4efd-8e13-c91364338175','MARS EXPRESS SUN MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 3 2737 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2010-01-01 to 2012-12-31. It is a Solar Conjunction measurement and covers the time 2011-01-22T16:32:30 to 2011-01-23T18:59:57.500.','public','2026-03-13T16:56:10.969671','2026-03-13T16:56:10.969679','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','819ce129-baf2-4d57-94a4-4d3bce3184bc','NASA Data.json','d59e832f293a28a426b7173c00f56998ae82ba53570d2ea43bc871c4169b3d09','1.1','2026-03-13T16:56:10.969671','2026-03-13T16:56:10.969679','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('962881cc-bd63-4b8e-84f8-a92520ab29d8','EPOXI C/GARRADD (2009 P1) - HRIV RAW IMAGES V1.0','This dataset contains raw clear-filter images of comet C/Garradd (2009 P1) acquired by the High Resolution Visible CCD (HRIV) from 20 February through 09 April 2012 during the Cruise 3 phase of the EPOXI mission.','public','2026-03-13T17:14:50.434281','2026-03-13T17:14:50.434287','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','96037921-41dc-46ef-85a7-fd800f26ec59','NASA Data.json','65ea356224d89fc6d71c148062127809e2b56f2694fb7672d4c4fff4a486b5e9','1.1','2026-03-13T17:14:50.434281','2026-03-13T17:14:50.434287','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('9647a4aa-f6d1-421a-8a82-2698ac26385b','Laborshed - Education Beyond High School','Laborshed dataset that contains data that estimates counts and percentages of those who have educational attainment beyond or below the high school level in all laborshed areas in Iowa.','public','2026-03-28T22:02:24.822474','2026-03-28T22:02:24.822480','data.iowa.gov','svqueen',NULL,'0c636592-097b-4d27-ba4a-99c8529c3f58','Iowa metadata','2662fce8087c081b19d700da7b428e5089826095e593fe8ac8b5a042076fea9c','1.1','2026-03-28T22:02:24.822474','2026-03-28T22:02:24.822480','Economic Statistics',NULL,0,'state-of-iowa'),('964a3cd1-c1c7-40a6-be24-fa099d703f5d','US Forest Atlas FIA Forest Type Groups Softwoods (Image Service)','<p><span style=\'background-color:rgb(255,255,255); color:rgb(76,76,76); font-family:&quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px;\'><span style=\'display:inline !important; float:none; font-style:normal; font-variant-caps:normal; font-variant-ligatures:normal; font-weight:400; letter-spacing:normal; text-align:left; text-decoration-color:initial; text-decoration-style:initial; text-indent:0px; text-transform:none; word-spacing:0px;\'>This Softwood type dataset portrays 16 forest type groups across the contiguous United States. These data were derived from MODIS composite images from the 2002 and 2003 growing seasons in combination with nearly 100 other geospatial data layers, including elevation, slope, aspect, ecoregions, and PRISM climate data. The dataset was developed as a collaborative effort between the USFS Forest Inventory and Analysis and Forest Health Monitoring programs and the USFS Remote Sensing.</span></span></p>','public','2026-03-13T22:49:17.200766','2026-03-13T22:49:17.200772','U.S. Forest Service','USFSEnterpriseContent','005:96','7095cff5-eb97-4e5d-90d6-56610087b912','USDA JSON','b33bd9917192c8f215d58fa97374c5a2c39dd0b58c0c289e96aa9b094f10b663','1.1','2026-03-13T22:49:17.200766','2026-03-13T22:49:17.200772','geospatial','005:059',0,'usda-gov'),('965d45b5-c8d4-49ce-bd1d-3959368e153e','Air Gap Data from CO-OPS','The Center for Operational Oceanographic Products and Services (CO-OPS) of the National Ocean Service (NOS), an organizational element of NOAA, operates and maintains a network of downward-looking long-range microwave sensors for determining the instantaneous clearance or air gap below bridges that span navigable waterways in the U.S.  These observations are part of the National Physical Oceanographic Real-Time System (PORTS) Program.  The data collected are used to ensure safety of navigation, improve economic efficiency, and protect coastal resources. Included in this data collection are preliminary 6-minute air gap observations from various bridges spanning navigable waterways in the U.S.','public','2026-03-17T19:40:37.363830','2026-03-17T19:40:37.363841',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2fc460b1-ca0f-4d94-93e2-18e71c522894','NOS CO-OPS',NULL,NULL,'2026-03-17T19:40:37.363830','2026-03-17T19:40:37.363841',NULL,NULL,NULL,'noaa-gov'),('968e5edf-aef5-44fd-b5cb-3ea90f292325','MARS EXPRESS ASPERA-3 RAW EDR ELECTRON SPECTROMTR EXT4 V1.0','This data set contains Mars Express ASPERA-3 Electron         Spectrometer (ELS) data for the fourth mission extension         (January 1, 2013 - Dec. 31, 2014). These data are provided         in raw units of counts/accumulation.','public','2026-03-13T18:50:40.010084','2026-03-13T18:50:40.010089','planetary plasma interactions','Planetary Data System','026:00','5277abd7-9a59-4f11-9534-44a483cacbf3','NASA Data.json','c813444105a1c91160fc47cc885bc55b0f0ee90fcca4615807e030d71284054e','1.1','2026-03-13T18:50:40.010084','2026-03-13T18:50:40.010089','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('96ac624b-0fbf-49a8-8dab-f3d941ae9cef','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSIWAC 4 EXT1-MTP026 RDR-INFLDSTR V1.0','This CODMAC level 4 data set contains solar stray-light corrected, in-field stray-light corrected,  radiometric calibrated and geometric distortion corrected  (resampled) image data in W/m^2/sr/nm,  acquired by the OSIRIS Wide Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft  during the ROSETTA EXTENSION 1 mission phase, covering the period  from 2016-02-09T23:25:00.000 to 2016-03-08T23:24:59.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V1.0 is the first version of this dataset: Lien corrected dataset after September 2019 PSA/PDS external peer review.','public','2026-03-13T16:41:48.993218','2026-03-13T16:41:48.993223','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','9abdd4d8-4f01-459c-ab09-4c644c527713','NASA Data.json','e31ad2de111f424e42c9a65ae911ff294944918dcf10837307b3efef759f1762','1.1','2026-03-13T16:41:48.993218','2026-03-13T16:41:48.993223','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('96eb5d39-623d-4625-9683-0cef96852eea','ROSETTA-ORBITER CHECKOUT OSINAC 3 CR4A RDR V2.0','This CODMAC level 3 data set contains radiometric calibrated image data in W/m^2/sr/nm,  acquired by the OSIRIS Narrow Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft  during the CRUISE 4-1 mission phase, covering the period  from 2008-01-28T00:00:00.000 to 2008-08-03T23:59:59.000. The prime objective was commissioning / calibration. Several targets of opportunity were observed, but none of them is identifiable as prime target. This version V2.0 supersedes previous deliveries of the same dataset with the following changes since the last version: Reprocessed dataset after October 2018 PSA/PDS external peer review.','public','2026-03-13T17:48:14.096612','2026-03-13T17:48:14.096617','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','982a05ca-313f-49f0-b1f2-47ffd909b9a7','NASA Data.json','6f9937ff5e2d6a9b69a2c8fe2e563fe965b4b425d947b29c2b7279fc265ae06b','1.1','2026-03-13T17:48:14.096612','2026-03-13T17:48:14.096617','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('96f4bcc5-e4a7-4511-a38f-a7bc91ac39d8','\"LATEX CTD - d94i052.nc - 27.56N, 93.0W - 1994-07-31\"','The Louisiana-Texas Shelf Physical Oceanography Program (LATEX) was sponsored by the Minerals Management Service (MMS) of the U.S. Department of the Interior. Of its three study units, the Texas-Louisiana Shelf Circulation and Transport Processes Study (LATEX A or LATEX Shelf) was conducted by the Texas A&M University System. The LATEX A field program ran from April 1992 to December 1994. The study area encompassed the Texas-Louisiana continental shelf offshore of approximately the 10-m isobath, from the Mississippi River to the Rio Grande. The five major field components were: moored current meter measurements, drifting buoys, hydrography, acoustic Doppler current profiling (Acoustic Doppler Current Profiler (ADCP)), and meteorological buoys.','public','2026-03-26T19:15:40.202231','2026-03-26T19:15:40.202238',NULL,NULL,NULL,'f7d880b2-a74b-48a5-9c7f-a5deb8f4a7c1','ioos',NULL,NULL,'2026-03-26T19:15:40.202231','2026-03-26T19:15:40.202238',NULL,NULL,NULL,'noaa-gov'),('96f825b3-ebc7-48af-b8c7-e8f9811d7f10','Fripp Island, SC','Timeseries data from \'Fripp Island, SC\' (hohonu_10046_fripp_island)','public','2026-03-26T19:16:35.819303','2026-03-26T19:16:35.819308',NULL,NULL,NULL,'379f99c7-962f-4882-a844-2e3bbcdfdfa1','ioos',NULL,NULL,'2026-03-26T19:16:35.819303','2026-03-26T19:16:35.819308',NULL,NULL,NULL,'noaa-gov'),('9722750e-58aa-4cdd-ab45-a69549bfe61a','Laborshed - In/Out Commute','Laborshed dataset that contains information about the commute patterns of employees in every laborshed area in Iowa.','public','2026-03-28T22:02:30.631626','2026-03-28T22:02:30.631630','data.iowa.gov','svqueen',NULL,'dac4dbb7-c88a-45a8-9953-a639bc5ab49e','Iowa metadata','9a55ea48e0aaea39ebcb953c9a5e54af4ad813ecf272ceb25dc11424ead17fb9','1.1','2026-03-28T22:02:30.631626','2026-03-28T22:02:30.631630','Economic Statistics',NULL,0,'state-of-iowa'),('973e601f-39a6-4a95-b971-8b4d5639c7b4','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSINAC 2 ESC2-MTP016 EDR V3.0','This CODMAC level 2 data set contains uncalibrated image data in DN unit, acquired by the OSIRIS Narrow Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft during the COMET ESCORT 2 mission phase, covering the period from 2015-05-05T23:25:00.000 to 2015-06-02T23:24:59.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V3.0 supersedes previous deliveries of the same dataset with the following changes since the last version: Lien corrected dataset after the July and October 2018 PSA/PDS external peer reviews. Updated documentation and ancillary files, added document on bandpass filter. Updated SCIENCE_USER_GUIDE_V03.PDF to include one section about FAQ and one section about image data quality. Added shutter backtravel and readout issues to image quality map. Updated DATA_QUALITY_ID keyword in image header. Improved handling of images with missing packets. Included FITs files. Browse products changed to the same size as the original image.','public','2026-03-13T17:51:54.009481','2026-03-13T17:51:54.009486','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','693bf638-c04c-4312-9c56-74f26963c6a0','NASA Data.json','9102232d9b35f355a8f1e7ca8e6aff939952dea936fa5b9eab0c6ba35a24ef60','1.1','2026-03-13T17:51:54.009481','2026-03-13T17:51:54.009486','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('974150a2-a829-4dd9-b163-37b2db8a1378','Continuous Fixed Station Water Quality Measurements in Timucuan Ecological and Historic Preserve, June 2008 (Certified)','This dataset represents continuous water quality measurements that were taken at a fixed point in Timucuan Ecological and Historic Preserve during the month of June, 2008 as a part of the Fixed Station Water Quality Monitoring protocol that was developed by the Southeast Coast I&M Network (SECN). The measurements were taken by a YSI 6600 ESD Multi-Parameter Long Term Water Quality Monitoring Datasonde unit that serves as the standard fixed station water quality monitoring equipment for all similar operations conducted by the SECN. The following parameters were measured at 30 minute intervals during the time period that has been specified: Water Temperature, Specific Conductivity, Salinity, Dissolved Oxygen (DO), DO Concentration, Shallow Depth, pH Level, and Turbidity. Any anomalies noted regarding these parameters have also been noted in separate fields. Please note that these measurements have been certified by network personnel.','public','2026-03-26T05:33:23.886174','2026-03-26T05:33:23.886180','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','cfe18a71-dce6-4af2-8efb-14d6df95f834','DOI NPS DCAT-US','7d53ed0538c75c3b7c8aa0a696afb48d5416f49d08a1fb6f74fc5eb2ba164b6e','1.1','2026-03-26T05:33:23.886174','2026-03-26T05:33:23.886180','Vector Dataset','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('97431f08-7e37-43d6-aeb0-12d31c5b4cf7','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 PRELANDING 0340 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the PRELANDING phase 2014-01-21 to 2014-11-18. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2014-10-06T15:55:30.000 to 2014-10-06T22:32:15.000.','public','2026-03-13T19:45:20.073094','2026-03-13T19:45:20.073100','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','950f9019-07d3-4c24-83e5-345196b42191','NASA Data.json','5dc023a282ecbd98e20e4638688cfabfb6cccbd93c0f0ffa29c8054fd86071a5','1.1','2026-03-13T19:45:20.073094','2026-03-13T19:45:20.073100','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('97559488-70ae-4170-af45-10432d6a7614','MARS EXPRESS MARS MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 6 3893 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2017-01-01 to 2018-12-31. It is a Occultation measurement and covers the time 2017-02-02T15:46:49.000 to 2017-02-02T16:08:58.949.','public','2026-03-13T17:26:08.004523','2026-03-13T17:26:08.004528','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','e16a6783-ab69-4a00-9167-1ad4c33cb6f2','NASA Data.json','52fb1c81332f0dbb55ae97394dec9b4bb25eaf0aa3afb1e07cef133f308d8564','1.1','2026-03-13T17:26:08.004523','2026-03-13T17:26:08.004528','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('975e17ee-7571-42f6-ad76-f3b06f515579','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSIWAC 5 EXT1-MTP027 DDR-GEO V1.0','This CODMAC level 5 data set contains derived data products that include pixel-precise georeferencing information, acquired by the OSIRIS Wide Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft during the ROSETTA EXTENSION 1 mission phase, covering the period from 2016-03-08T23:25:00.000 to 2016-04-05T23:24:59.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V1.0 is the first version of this dataset: Lien corrected dataset after October 2018 PSA/PDS external peer review.','public','2026-03-13T17:46:00.912818','2026-03-13T17:46:00.912826','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','0dfc1630-a2f3-466e-9862-0c04882d1d72','NASA Data.json','9cc94edfc52a21d16e87514462da4cb11c59913826705384e37db1bb31ca0fd9','1.1','2026-03-13T17:46:00.912818','2026-03-13T17:46:00.912826','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('97825626-2630-41c9-aeba-e9b0755efdf0','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P NAVCAM 3 ROSETTA EXTENSION 3 MTP032 V1.0','This dataset contains ROSETTA NAVCAM RADIOMETRICALLY CALIBRATED DATA of the ROSETTA EXTENSION 3 MTP032 Phase from 27 Jul. 2016, 06:04:22 to 09 Aug. 2016, 23:17:53 when at the vicinity of target 67P/CG.','public','2026-03-13T18:27:01.089445','2026-03-13T18:27:01.089451','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','c59e2a0b-dee2-4645-a742-7ad8825fac2f','NASA Data.json','cbcdac7a94547c1867a7274a5eae84e56cbc1740799b08d5bcc6c18b12ff08bd','1.1','2026-03-13T18:27:01.089445','2026-03-13T18:27:01.089451','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('97da095e-089a-4487-9e0c-6f3a3468f0ee','BLM ID CADNSDI PLSS Intersected','The fully intersected data is the atomic level of the PLSS that is similar to the coverage or the smallest pieces used to build the PLSS. Polygons may overlap in this feature class.     For more information contact us at blm_id_stateoffice@blm.gov.','public','2026-03-19T11:32:31.304378','2026-03-19T11:32:31.304384','Bureau of Land Management','Bureau of Land Management, blm_id_infoaccesscenter','010:04','73b066ae-109f-4609-8dcb-0e4624a51889','DOI BLM DCAT-US','31395642c6b35b363dd8c18c8c74e536c6256cec48c58616a793c54b1d8ebf0f','1.1','2026-03-19T11:32:31.304378','2026-03-19T11:32:31.304384','geospatial','010:000',0,'doi-gov'),('97e3bac9-4d11-4b4a-8f1b-43693722dac6','VOYAGER 2 SATURN MAGNETOMETER RESAMPLED DATA 9.60 SEC','This data set includes Voyager 2 Saturn encounter magnetometer data that have been resampled at a 9.6 second sample rate. The data set is composed of 6 columns: 1) ctime - this column contains the data acquisition time. The time is always output in the ISO standard spacecraft event time format (yyyy-mm-dd-Thh:mm:ss.sss) but is stored internally in Cline time which is measured in seconds after 00:00:00.000 Jan 01, 1966, 2) br - this column contains the radial component of the magnetic field, 3) bphi - this column contains the phi component of the magnetic field, 4) btheta - this column contains the theta component of the magnetic field, 5) bmag - this column contains the magnitude of the magnetic field, 6) flag - a flag value that indicates either software error or spacecraft hardware interference reduced confidence in this record (flag value of 1 is bad , 0 is good or unchecked). All magnetic field observations are measured in nanoTeslas. The coordinate system for this dataset is Minus Saturn Longitude System (-SLS). All of the magnetic field data are calibrated (see the instrument calibration description for more details). The SLS coordinate system is defined in Desch and Kaiser, 1981 and the reference documents for this dataset are: Ness et al, 1982 Acuna,Connerney,and Ness, 1983 Connerney,Acuna,and Ness, 1983 Behannon,Lepping,and Ness, 1983','public','2026-03-13T17:19:19.058236','2026-03-13T17:19:19.058241','Planetary Plasma Interactions','Planetary Data System','026:00','844156c2-39f7-4df9-b89a-8c46574cb4e4','NASA Data.json','78a11f6caf904fca0afdfa96d93db880b8c1e2a9d8879fbc6414bac259e50264','1.1','2026-03-13T17:19:19.058236','2026-03-13T17:19:19.058241','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('97f72094-2e70-4260-833b-fae844f080f4','SMAP_L1A_RADAR_RECEIVE_ONLY_V002','SMAP Level 1A Radar Receive Only Product Version 2','public','2026-03-13T22:33:32.197418','2026-03-13T22:33:32.197423','NASA/JPL/SMAP;ASF','Earthdata Forum','026:00','89e768bf-1f36-4ded-88db-aae877887672','NASA Data.json','d4220f19cb394221082a6abc8783428fa5c3d0ad900f766889691b74c3645cd8','1.1','2026-03-13T22:33:32.197418','2026-03-13T22:33:32.197423','Earth Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('980aba02-3f77-44b5-a2cc-dbf57eb30259','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSINAC 5 PRL-MTP006 DDR-GEO V1.0','This CODMAC level 5 data set contains derived data products that include pixel-precise georeferencing information, acquired by the OSIRIS Narrow Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft during the PRELANDING mission phase, covering the period from 2014-08-01T10:00:00.000 to 2014-09-02T09:59:59.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V1.0 is the first version of this dataset: Lien corrected dataset after October 2018 PSA/PDS external peer review.','public','2026-03-13T16:40:12.862570','2026-03-13T16:40:12.862576','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','745b3a80-b226-484a-bc45-a385d3145e8f','NASA Data.json','78420014a0be306583c04c222a3bdec3fd60965c99d786cb566a66a4e27693eb','1.1','2026-03-13T16:40:12.862570','2026-03-13T16:40:12.862576','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('981ca807-00bc-402b-bc12-bb0aca3d9e7f','NEW HORIZONS  SDC KEMCRUISE1  CALIBRATED V2.0','This data set contains Calibrated data taken by the  New Horizons Student Dust Counter instrument during the  CRUISE TO FIRST KBO ENCOUNTER mission phase.  This is VERSION 2.0 of this data set.   This data set contains data acquired by the spacecraft between  10/17/2016 and 08/13/2018. This is the complete dataset.','public','2026-03-13T17:53:47.028286','2026-03-13T17:53:47.028292','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','d846a661-f9f3-403a-93c0-f13a53514b44','NASA Data.json','61cd6ce03a099c7fb83667c96bf72a3b3d95de33303f932978a6fc9ca8d36962','1.1','2026-03-13T17:53:47.028286','2026-03-13T17:53:47.028292','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('982f41d6-d944-42b1-b19f-799c27258c89','Ordinance 20040624-009','Ordinance 20040624-009','public','2026-03-25T14:44:10.355899','2026-03-25T14:44:10.355904','data.austintexas.gov','Haileigh.Meyers@austintexas.gov',NULL,'ba77beee-df79-47d1-83fa-ca7e83c3e65f','City of Austin Data.json','35f96252b1f5d5d58bb0c759fd6b177a676e525c75679a8d7b9cb5013ffcd6ad','1.1','2026-03-25T14:44:10.355899','2026-03-25T14:44:10.355904',NULL,NULL,0,'city-of-austin'),('98380a04-4aeb-44aa-b0f7-464801ebf416','NEW HORIZONS  LORRI PLUTO CRUISE  RAW V2.0','This data set contains Raw data taken by the New Horizons  Long Range Reconnaissance Imager  instrument during the  pluto cruise  mission phase. This is VERSION 2.0 of this data set. The spacecraft was in hibernation for much of the Pluto Cruise mission phase, and the focus for LORRI during Annual CheckOuts (ACOs) one through four (ACO1-4) was preparation for the Pluto Encounter in 2015, including functionaltests, calibrations, and encounter rehearsals. Science observations performedby LORRI during this phase included the following targets: KBO objects KBO 2005 FY9 (Makemake) and KBO 2003 EL61 (Haumea); Centaur object Chariklo; the planets Jupiter, Uranus, and Neptune. The ACO tests also had LORRI observing several other targets: Pluto; the star field that will be visible 3 days before Pluto closest approach in 2015; the M7 star field; the star Vega. A full functional test was performed during ACO1 in 2007, with ACO \'Lite\' tests performed during ACO2-4 in 2008, 2009 and 2010. Specific tests and calibrations performed during ACOs included the following: scattered light test (2007, 2008, 2010); Pluto OpNav test (2007, 2008); lamp tests (2007, 2008, 2009, 2010); star tracker calibration test (2008); GNC mosaic settling test (2008); LEISA-LORRI ridealong (2008); scattered light dither test (2010).  The changes in Version 2.0 were re-running of the ancillary data  in the data product, updated geometry from newer SPICE kernels,  minor editing of the documentation, catalogs, etc., and resolution  of liens from the December, 2014 review, plus those from the May,  2016 review of the Pluto Encounter data sets.   The lossy images from Version 1.0 were recalibrated, including  expanding the \'bad\' pixel designation of 8x8 boxes affected by the  first 34 pixels of header information in the calibrated quality map.   No new observations were added with this version (V2.0).','public','2026-03-13T18:24:14.586603','2026-03-13T18:24:14.586609','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','39fe0614-f256-48d8-a4ba-42f3331f5a7c','NASA Data.json','db1db80f1e496525b3d218ddce9b379376394c2f11f8dc74f59532a5ba7c8e3b','1.1','2026-03-13T18:24:14.586603','2026-03-13T18:24:14.586609','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('983e5283-12a3-4213-9e7e-f6683a0f6443','APL_wifi','wifi usage at Austin Public Library in session count and data usages (gigabytes)','public','2026-03-25T14:19:19.923126','2026-03-25T14:19:19.923133','data.austintexas.gov','Austin Public Library Owners',NULL,'83816de4-239f-43f6-9e17-5df3fdea39c3','City of Austin Data.json','633be2558421dd689ca28c06f36dbbbcdf49856d747b7251b7dba69e8b696716','1.1','2026-03-25T14:19:19.923126','2026-03-25T14:19:19.923133','Recreation and Culture',NULL,0,'city-of-austin'),('988789b5-d1cd-4562-8204-7150c2e070ac','CACFP DCH Provider Applications, PY19-PY25','<b>This dataset includes raw data from the latest site-level application submitted to TDA for participation as a Day Care Home (DCH) in the Child and Adult Care Food Program (CACFP) for program years 2018-2019 (PY19) to 2024-2025 (PY25), regardless of application approval status.  </b>\n\nDay Care Home providers may be considered \"sites\" for the purposes of reporting. \n\nThis dataset is part of a collection of<b><a href=https://data.texas.gov/stories/en/s/7ke6-qib4 target=\"_blank\"> expanded raw data</a> </b>from the <i>Texas Department of Agriculture, Food & Nutrition Division\'s</i> meal program database, <i>TX-UNPS</i>. \n\nFor <b>final approved application datasets that combine sponsor and site information</b>, please refer to the <b><a href=https://data.texas.gov/stories/s/iekx-7mdi target=_blank\"> Child and Adult Care Food Program Data</a> </b>overview page. \n\nAn overview of all TDA Food and Nutrition data available on the Texas Open Data Portal can be found at our <b><a href=https://data.texas.gov/stories/s/TDA-Data-Overview-Food-and-Nutrition-Programs-Open/nk79-w2cs/ target=\"_blank\">TDA Data Overview - Food and Nutrition Open Data</a></b> page.\n\n<b>About the Agency</b>\n\nThe <i>Texas Department of Agriculture (TDA)</i> administers 12 <i>U.S. Department of Agriculture (USDA)</i> nutrition programs in Texas including the <i>National School Lunch Program (NSLP)</i> and <i>School Breakfast Program (SBP)</i>, the <i>Child and Adult Care Food Program (CACFP)</i>, and summer meal programs. TDA’s Food and Nutrition division provides technical assistance and training resources to partners operating the programs and oversees the USDA reimbursements they receive to cover part of the cost associated with serving food in their facilities. By working to ensure these partners serve nutritious meals and snacks, the division adheres to its mission — Feeding the Hungry and Promoting Healthy Lifestyles.\n\nFor more information on these programs, please visit <a href=https://squaremeals.org/ target=\"_blank\">our website</a>.','public','2026-03-25T14:47:20.251010','2026-03-25T14:47:20.251015','data.austintexas.gov','CDelgadoReyes',NULL,'1d9a276b-94ee-4b97-81de-c636268b6d1a','City of Austin Data.json','109ad60085539e390c77b88fa912dddb1ac914164010737fa74d201115cadb95','1.1','2026-03-25T14:47:20.251010','2026-03-25T14:47:20.251015',NULL,NULL,0,'city-of-austin'),('98b23b7b-d9a8-4d53-9412-c2cfbd614cf1','HO NOFA Special Set-Aside Waitlist','Homeownership Development Notice of Funding Availability Special Set-Aside Waitlist','public','2026-03-29T04:08:33.187654','2026-03-29T04:08:33.187659','data.oregon.gov','James Kwasnik',NULL,'e8d5d14e-160d-4140-9a52-4f87f6f54de0','oregon json','35901de78f6393b91c2311fdcf56cd465ef91a372ea20961c4bab521266ad523','1.1','2026-03-29T04:08:33.187654','2026-03-29T04:08:33.187659','Health & Human Services',NULL,0,'state-of-oregon'),('98c3b140-8787-4228-baa4-38c743466405','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 3 1021 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 3 phase 2015-07-01 to 2015-10-21. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-09-08T21:24:45.000 to 2015-09-09T00:17:15.000.','public','2026-03-13T19:51:03.166968','2026-03-13T19:51:03.166973','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','ce943fd2-45f1-4015-bc89-76063fc27acd','NASA Data.json','107c775039bb369195ad1db064fc9ba3e16c284ff1298df081e0d0cea4d30f23','1.1','2026-03-13T19:51:03.166968','2026-03-13T19:51:03.166973','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('98e3f5ef-718f-42be-9e90-be2759aa1ff7','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RPCLAP 5ESC1 NEL V1.0','This data set contains DERIVEDdata from Rosetta RPC-LAP, acquired during the COMET ESCORT 1 missionphase where the primary target was the comet 67P/CHURYUMOV-GERASIMENKO 1(1969 R1). It contains electron density at higher time resolution thanin the DERIV2 data sets.','public','2026-03-13T17:02:35.942973','2026-03-13T17:02:35.942980','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','61b17e2a-3161-4bcc-9cdf-7e5474ffc273','NASA Data.json','323c4668d73d1b99cedbe22e8b3a5c8588b14124ae8aecc87edeaf5109bc0617','1.1','2026-03-13T17:02:35.942973','2026-03-13T17:02:35.942980','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('99347ca1-c6ef-44ba-a00d-7fe699e870b7','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSIWAC 4 EXT3-MTP032 RDR-REFLECT V1.0','This CODMAC level 4 data set contains radiometric calibrated and geometric distortion corrected (resampled) image data in reflectance units (normalized and thus without unit), acquired by the OSIRIS Wide Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft during the ROSETTA EXTENSION 3 mission phase, covering the period from 2016-07-26T23:25:00.000 to 2016-08-09T23:24:59.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V1.0 is the first version of this dataset: Lien corrected dataset after October 2018 PSA/PDS external peer review.','public','2026-03-13T17:17:43.014982','2026-03-13T17:17:43.014990','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','52e5efb7-3553-40f1-bfae-39f4259f02b0','NASA Data.json','cbdd9b8c476615ad8941ec6b7368bc5a28e0c64fe50b3ab97e997c0e7a8bca14','1.1','2026-03-13T17:17:43.014982','2026-03-13T17:17:43.014990','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('9973c65d-b510-4d20-85f7-1cbd8f61b668','AIRS/Aqua L1B Near Real Time (NRT) Infrared (IR) geolocated and calibrated radiances in BUFR format V005 (AIRIBRAD_NRT_BUFR) at GES DISC','WARNING: On 2021/09/23 the EOS Aqua executed a Deep Space Maneuver (DSM). In the DSM, the spacecraft is turned such that the normal Earth field of regard is deep space. The thermal impact of the DSM caused a shift of the centroids of spectral response functions (SRF) of about 1% of the width of the SRF, equivalent to a frequency shift of 9 parts per million. This shift is reflected in the “spectral_freq” parameter (observed frequencies) in the L1b v5 files for each 6 minute granule. The magnitude of the effect on brightness temperatures (BT) depends on the spectral gradient of each channel. Maximum BT shifts are approximately +- 0.5 K, although many channels experience far smaller BT shifts. Approximately 1803 channels have BT shifts of less than 0.1 K and 575 channels are now shifted in BT by more than 0.1 K, while 231 of these channels have BT shifts greater than 0.2 K. Users of the L1b v5 product who are concerned that these shifts may impact their science investigations and applications are encouraged to switch to the AIRS L1c v6.7.4 product, which, among many other improvements, converts the spectra to a fixed frequency grid. END OF WARNING. This product is a 324-channel subset of the AIRIBRAD_NRT_005 product in which the AMSU footprints from AIRABRAD_NRT_005 product are also included and converted to binary Universal Form for the Representation of meteorological data (BUFR). The AIRS and AMSU Level 1B products differ from routine processing in 2 ways to meet the three hour latency requirements of the Land Atmosphere NRT Capability Earth Observing System (LANCE): (1) The NRT granules are produced without previous or subsequent granules if those granules are not available within 5 minutes, (2) the predictive ephemeris/attitude data are used rather than the definitive ephemeris/attitude. The consequences of these differences are described in the AIRS Near Real Time (NRT) data products document. The Atmospheric Infrared Sounder (AIRS) is a grating spectrometer (R = 1200) aboard the second Earth Observing System (EOS) polar-orbiting platform, EOS Aqua. In combination with the Advanced Microwave Sounding Unit (AMSU) and the Humidity Sounder for Brazil (HSB), AIRS constitutes an innovative atmospheric sounding group of visible, infrared, and microwave sensors.','public','2026-03-13T19:06:47.155152','2026-03-13T19:06:47.155157','NASA/GSFC/SED/ESD/TISL/GESDISC','Tess Jaffe','026:00','c7cc3b86-7320-42fe-8455-c61bb727e354','NASA Data.json','a96029d4179144cc77eafa8d74029d77c9752a251f4eb0ff004d9dfb7f60090c','1.1','2026-03-13T19:06:47.155152','2026-03-13T19:06:47.155157','Earth Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('997552c1-783a-4166-92cb-ea0aa7306496','Continuous Fixed Station Water Quality Measurements in Timucuan Ecological and Historic Preserve, July 2008 (Certified)','This dataset represents continuous water quality measurements that were taken at a fixed point in Timucuan Ecological and Historic Preserve during the month of July, 2008 as a part of the Fixed Station Water Quality Monitoring protocol that was developed by the Southeast Coast I&M Network (SECN). The measurements were taken by a YSI 6600 ESD Multi-Parameter Long Term Water Quality Monitoring Datasonde unit that serves as the standard fixed station water quality monitoring equipment for all similar operations conducted by the SECN. The following parameters were measured at 30 minute intervals during the time period that has been specified: Water Temperature, Specific Conductivity, Salinity, Dissolved Oxygen (DO), DO Concentration, Shallow Depth, pH Level, and Turbidity. Any anomalies noted regarding these parameters have also been noted in separate fields. Please note that these measurements have been certified by network personnel.','public','2026-03-26T05:33:31.107852','2026-03-26T05:33:31.107860','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','b0c9ad7d-e578-4530-b019-d6e357a6ae3f','DOI NPS DCAT-US','0aacb1a0456372efb00ddfbf65a72f43029739a142478eeefe0bf31bcd02d4cf','1.1','2026-03-26T05:33:31.107852','2026-03-26T05:33:31.107860','Vector Dataset','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('99846524-3de5-4773-826d-8e27047bbebd','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P NAVCAM 3 ROSETTA EXTENSION 3 MTP031 V1.0','This dataset contains ROSETTA NAVCAM RADIOMETRICALLY CALIBRATED DATA of the ROSETTA EXTENSION 3 MTP031 Phase from 29 Jun. 2016, 06:04:23 to 26 Jul. 2016, 23:17:53 when at the vicinity of target 67P/CG.','public','2026-03-13T17:04:38.458612','2026-03-13T17:04:38.458618','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','ce4a9f9b-73b4-454c-8037-72c9ebce54ad','NASA Data.json','8ff7a4c0be4e53564bb50de6c56a92b2944d3aacef08411f4893a28c5d03a1e5','1.1','2026-03-13T17:04:38.458612','2026-03-13T17:04:38.458618','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('9994c8a1-cdf0-4293-92a1-ba4421dd7e64','Fugro Cruise C16215 Line 1599, 300 kHz VMADCP','Program of vessel mount Acoustic Doppler Current Profiler (ADCP) measurements comprising a combination of 300kHz and 75kHz ADCP data collected in the vicinity of the Loop Current and drilling blocks between 2004 and 2007.','public','2026-03-26T19:17:38.106796','2026-03-26T19:17:38.106803',NULL,NULL,NULL,'3aa115f4-ebdc-4398-a8b6-2bb4909737a2','ioos',NULL,NULL,'2026-03-26T19:17:38.106796','2026-03-26T19:17:38.106803',NULL,NULL,NULL,'noaa-gov'),('99da3956-4d5e-48ca-9577-5f712175a061','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 ROSETTA EXTENSION 1 1379 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the ROSETTA EXTENSION 1 phase 2016-01-01 to 2016-04-05. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2016-01-29T01:16:50.000 to 2016-01-29T09:03:01.500.','public','2026-03-13T17:25:59.445779','2026-03-13T17:25:59.445784','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','694579b4-3aff-4ec8-901b-38be96401ce2','NASA Data.json','1593f7bac9932d93a01f3257a451c0409c6fb28d2dfe0b79a1942502df6ef738','1.1','2026-03-13T17:25:59.445779','2026-03-13T17:25:59.445784','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('99eb263f-ffe2-4d54-906c-66f9bd802511','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSINAC 3 ESC4-MTP023 RDR V3.0','This CODMAC level 3 data set contains radiometric calibrated image data in W/m^2/sr/nm, acquired by the OSIRIS Narrow Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft during the COMET ESCORT 4 mission phase, covering the period from 2015-11-17T23:25:00.000 to 2015-12-15T23:24:59.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V3.0 supersedes previous deliveries of the same dataset with the following changes since the last version: Lien corrected dataset after the July and October 2018 PSA/PDS external peer reviews. Updated documentation and ancillary files, added document on bandpass filter. Updated SCIENCE_USER_GUIDE_V03.PDF to include one section about FAQ and one section about image data quality. Added shutter backtravel and readout issues to image quality map. Updated DATA_QUALITY_ID keyword in image header. Improved handling of images with missing packets. Included FITs files. Browse products changed to the same size as the original image.','public','2026-03-13T18:20:10.812661','2026-03-13T18:20:10.812666','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','aa0cd138-733f-49e5-b30b-79d23d719010','NASA Data.json','37a2196000538814e724d1ec0d19bf526b4168469e07c281f5270a35bfae8cef','1.1','2026-03-13T18:20:10.812661','2026-03-13T18:20:10.812666','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('99f423da-8850-45e0-b497-459e9a42e6f2','NRC 828','NRC Small Business Subcontracting Plan Review. Fillable form in Adobe Portable Document Format (PDF) with information submitted by NRC stakeholder - licensee, applicant, or NRC employee/contractor.','non-public','2026-03-20T19:43:34.113828','2026-03-20T19:43:34.113833','Nuclear Regulatory Commission','Tira Patterson','429:00','20248180-962b-4cb9-b952-3d9e207c383d','NRC Data.json Harvest Source','665a61a62ef0618d4c55499ed4b97fefa1bac1188904d7e5c089f4ca51fac8e5','1.1','2026-03-20T19:43:34.113828','2026-03-20T19:43:34.113833',NULL,'000:000',0,'nrc-gov'),('9a66580c-48f9-486c-8253-776a842eebb8','Texas 4.2 Work Zone Data Feed Example','This dataset provides archived lane closure occurrences within the Texas Department of Transportation (TxDOT) highway system in a tabular format.\n\nThe ITS JPO has collections from 23 states including Texas covering various parts of the time period from 10/2019 to 08/2024 depending on when the feed was active. The data is split into two archive files, the raw data contains the collection of .json or .geojson files exactly as they were on the individual state’s WZDx feed at the time of collection. The processed data is organized by work zone, so that as information about the work zone changed through feed updates they would be collected in a single file for that work zone. To request access fill out the form here.','public','2026-03-25T12:39:17.284660','2026-03-25T12:39:17.284664','Federal Highway Administration','Elina Zlotchenko','021:15','aa8939ce-45e9-48ba-9a46-9e18d1e33e60','DOT Socrata Data.json','b051e2dd61f97db1ea6e7ff48798de3b9d6988dd46f8fcaffd3f590b06ab89a3','1.1','2026-03-25T12:39:17.284660','2026-03-25T12:39:17.284664','Roadways and Bridges','021:042',0,'dot-gov'),('9a9b76c5-5aff-48ff-a720-d5f35af97450','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSIWAC 4 EXT3-MTP033 RDR-REFLECT V1.0','This CODMAC level 4 data set contains radiometric calibrated and geometric distortion corrected (resampled) image data in reflectance units (normalized and thus without unit), acquired by the OSIRIS Wide Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft during the ROSETTA EXTENSION 3 mission phase, covering the period from 2016-08-09T23:25:00.000 to 2016-09-02T06:39:59.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V1.0 is the first version of this dataset: Lien corrected dataset after October 2018 PSA/PDS external peer review.','public','2026-03-13T18:11:27.174402','2026-03-13T18:11:27.174407','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','c55833bc-a4a9-4c2c-b59b-661461dda399','NASA Data.json','b7484694238d99e8ca99e7af67049ff4874d699e5c91bc5474d2ac2ed5badfc4','1.1','2026-03-13T18:11:27.174402','2026-03-13T18:11:27.174407','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('9ab5542d-6b3b-446f-862c-d90978fcbec7','ROSETTA-ORBITER CHECK RPCMAG 2 CVP RAW V9.0','This dataset contains EDITED RAW DATA (CODMAC LEVEL 2) of the twocommissioning phases CVP1 and CVP2 and of the interference campaign of theROSETTA orbiter magnetometer RPCMAG. Included are data from the time intervalMarch 17, 2004 until October 14, 2004.The current version of the dataset is V9.0.The difference to the datasets of earlier versions is mainly a significantlyimproved sensor temperature model, more detailed documentation about magneticdisturbance sources, more data handling information for the user andalso an improved quality flagging system.This applies mainly to CALIBRATED and RESAMPLED datasets. The RAW dataset,however, has been updated as well in order provide all datasets at thesame stage, although RAW data proper did not change.','public','2026-03-13T18:27:26.837098','2026-03-13T18:27:26.837103','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','92bbd66c-7a8d-4403-a969-f7ddea9953db','NASA Data.json','755f42aa3e6cf10e618f96431205ae19222bedae375c3e9fb1d67703dab6bd06','1.1','2026-03-13T18:27:26.837098','2026-03-13T18:27:26.837103','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('9ac6f3c4-6861-4674-b10e-5c1751eed49d','ODYSSEY THEMIS IR PBT V2.0','The THEMIS IR-PBT data set contains the spatially registered, infrared brightness temperature images derived from the projected radiance (IR-GEO) products. Each image header includes basic parameters describing the observation and image specific details of processing.','public','2026-03-13T20:09:44.645027','2026-03-13T20:09:44.645032','Imaging','Planetary Data System','026:00','8a04fb4c-7602-400d-82a2-399a41fcea77','NASA Data.json','bb80186fa8c87226cc7c34e3ab76e8f5825fe20f3cb76d88fec40ba7ebaa5668','1.1','2026-03-13T20:09:44.645027','2026-03-13T20:09:44.645032','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('9ae4b74e-4d59-40cf-96f3-2180727ef869','MARS EXPRESS SUN MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 5 3758 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2015-01-01 to 2016-12-31. It is a Solar Conjunction measurement and covers the time 2015-06-06T12:03:01 to 2015-06-06T17:54:00.','public','2026-03-13T17:22:05.845830','2026-03-13T17:22:05.845836','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','1ed78d35-6d5c-4f94-82f7-c7bf3004d253','NASA Data.json','b9715c9ca540eac54191ea41a310f959e9d12f336b6e8f018ab94efd8cc2782d','1.1','2026-03-13T17:22:05.845830','2026-03-13T17:22:05.845836','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('9b09a25d-3a26-445d-acc8-c604314c0d8f','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 2 0715 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 2 phase 2015-03-11 to 2015-06-30. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-04-18T08:15:10.000 to 2015-04-18T10:29:07.500.','public','2026-03-13T19:14:03.087353','2026-03-13T19:14:03.087358','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','727c66bb-a249-4e08-8c7e-ed803771d668','NASA Data.json','7d4a049e31b275007173e5c4e3a23211f5e863566c2eb61fd242a0c482ff7eca','1.1','2026-03-13T19:14:03.087353','2026-03-13T19:14:03.087358','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('9b408c09-8aad-4920-bae0-38864cc87ba2','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 PRELANDING 0285 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the PRELANDING phase 2014-01-21 to 2014-11-18. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2014-09-10T09:59:25.000 to 2014-09-10T17:11:27.000.','public','2026-03-13T16:52:57.098216','2026-03-13T16:52:57.098225','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','8bc92944-d91f-4664-b765-2041fdb7cf30','NASA Data.json','b6eedc04a67624bfc04c37af80fcbbf3acc89d14067130e9f41bd12fded86dab','1.1','2026-03-13T16:52:57.098216','2026-03-13T16:52:57.098225','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('9b52bc63-0f8e-4438-9bc2-43ad12c5eb6b','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 2 0678 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 2 phase 2015-03-11 to 2015-06-30. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-03-28T15:53:05.000 to 2015-03-28T19:00:13.000.','public','2026-03-13T20:03:19.797012','2026-03-13T20:03:19.797017','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','4a328561-6af7-4f86-89b3-f4cd4b98c606','NASA Data.json','00190008bb2aa725d4617fe6123b2f7f78099881dbad74921b4c8f12d1aff520','1.1','2026-03-13T20:03:19.797012','2026-03-13T20:03:19.797017','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('9b5527e4-6441-4267-843f-fb070470a3b7','ROSETTA-ORBITER COMET PRELANDING OSIWAC 3 RDR MTP 005 V1.0','This data set contains calibrated images acquired by the OSIRIS Wide AngleCamera during the prelanding phase of the Rosetta mission at the comet 67P,covering the period from 2014-07-02 to 2014-08-01.','public','2026-03-13T17:40:17.998199','2026-03-13T17:40:17.998206','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','8656f83b-243b-48fa-a938-42604822f5f5','NASA Data.json','2dbbbd7d8060aef4b593fd82bfb5de2706a190f1953213cefe6c51ebd804f729','1.1','2026-03-13T17:40:17.998199','2026-03-13T17:40:17.998206','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('9b7db436-dd63-4d57-8c1b-f3dd8bcb3d23','Temporal_mismatch','Temporal_mismatch. This dataset is not publicly accessible because: Property of the University of NC Institute for Marine Sciences. It can be accessed through the following means: Data are available for multiple purposes through HydroShare http://www.hydroshare.org/resource/671fefb82cc94504a6734717d8aae48d. Format: YSI sonde data owned and operated by UNC IMS. \n\nThis dataset is associated with the following publication:\nCronin-Golomb, O., K. Meyers, W. Salls, and B. Schaeffer. Quantifying temporal mismatches in satellite and in-situ data for aquatic environments..   Remote Sensing Letters. Taylor & Francis Group, London,  UK, 17(4): 404-415, (2026).','public','2026-03-23T12:00:55.763013','2026-03-23T12:00:55.763018','U.S. Environmental Protection Agency','Blake Schaeffer','020:00','6133635d-bfc1-4cdc-924c-8918d821a527','EPA ScienceHub','c03352e808427e062fd24572615b3584edd2714d2813b3685e7d124c4570a3e3','1.1','2026-03-23T12:00:55.763013','2026-03-23T12:00:55.763018',NULL,'020:000',0,'epa-gov'),('9b84b96a-b4ae-4625-a63c-2af9539573b1','Prioritizing Chemical Candidates from Non-targeted Analysis Using Metadata, Spectral Similarity, and Hazard Scoring within INTERPRET NTA','Supporting information for \"Prioritizing Chemical Candidates from Non-targeted Analysis Using Metadata, Spectral Similarity, and Hazard Scoring within INTERPRET NTA\"','public','2026-03-16T10:41:50.928586','2026-03-16T10:41:50.928590','U.S. Environmental Protection Agency','Antony Williams','020:00','18a01a65-df25-4c1e-9d1f-c24462f31870','EPA ScienceHub','a08d56676c735ba9728bb663e0676236d0549e2188dbe659e85cccfc16c712d4','1.1','2026-03-16T10:41:50.928586','2026-03-16T10:41:50.928590',NULL,'020:000',0,'epa-gov'),('9bc0b0ef-a826-413e-ad40-ed6cb18814df','Visual Resource Inventory data from the NPS Enjoy the View program, February 2026','This data package contains results from visual resources  inventories conducted at various National Park Service (NPS) units as a part of the National Park Service Enjoy the View program, which collects geospatial data, digital photographs, descriptions of the viewpoint and the viewed landscape, and ratings for scenic quality and view importance.\n\nThis data package contains data from scenic quality and view importance assessments conducted by NPS staff and contractors between 2013-11-13 and 2026-02-06 using standardized methodologies to evaluate the visual resources of the parks. The data within this package includes detailed descriptions of viewpoints, landscape elements, and ratings based on various factors affecting scenic quality and view importance, and are intended to be used with separate geographic location and photographic data available to internal staff.\n\nData from the Enjoy the View program support park planning, resource condition assessments, and visual resource management. The package is updated periodically and may not include the most recent inventory results. For general background on the visual resources inventory, visit the NPS Inventory & Mapping - Scenic Views web page at https://www.nps.gov/subjects/scenicviews/inventory-and-mapping.htm.','public','2026-03-18T02:25:00.923591','2026-03-18T02:25:00.923598','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','a633cdcd-d1b9-4bcf-b9a2-94a0cf3cabc3','DOI NPS DCAT-US','ade9c3f38aaa0f7132643b76223e938975d01e98a06b4d053b15fee95feeb96c','1.1','2026-03-18T02:25:00.923591','2026-03-18T02:25:00.923598','Data Package','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('9becc7d9-29df-42d3-a961-4cffe6d5d14e','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSINAC 4 ESC3-MTP020 RDR-INF-REFL V1.0','This CODMAC level 4 data set contains solar stray-light corrected, in-field stray-light corrected,  radiometric calibrated and geometric distortion corrected  (resampled) image data in reflectance units (normalized  and thus without unit),  acquired by the OSIRIS Narrow Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft  during the COMET ESCORT 3 mission phase, covering the period  from 2015-08-25T23:25:00.000 to 2015-09-22T23:24:59.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V1.0 is the first version of this dataset: Lien corrected dataset after September 2019 PSA/PDS external peer review.','public','2026-03-13T19:00:26.038552','2026-03-13T19:00:26.038557','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','b63412ed-51ed-4e30-9330-f915a0c89ed6','NASA Data.json','4daab89d30402c1c619d55a91ded98c086c8c2362a1e0d18f2c62c47a17283b0','1.1','2026-03-13T19:00:26.038552','2026-03-13T19:00:26.038557','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('9c22c465-2df0-4887-b8a5-2799414263a0','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P NAVCAM 2 COMET ESCORT 1 MTP013 V1.0','This dataset contains ROSETTA NAVCAM RAW DATA of the Escort Phase from 10th Feb 2015 to 10th Mar 2015 when at the vicinity of target 67P/CG.','public','2026-03-13T19:22:56.982257','2026-03-13T19:22:56.982262','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','71a49900-8ec5-417e-8815-85f08e681b7d','NASA Data.json','47ed48eade5628854455e88fd3e7d0c341fd358d4211b42ecc0d6c36b3df7809','1.1','2026-03-13T19:22:56.982257','2026-03-13T19:22:56.982262','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('9c37bb88-bbc3-481c-acfe-a2b802b3b6d4','VOYAGER 2 JUP LOW ENERGY CHARGED PARTICLE CALIB. BR 15MIN','THIS BROWSE DATA CONSISTS OF RESAMPLED DATA FROM THE LOW ENERGY CHARGED PARTICLE (LECP) EXPERIMENT ON VOYAGER 2 WHILE THE SPACECRAFT WAS IN THE VICINITY OF JUPITER. THIS INSTRUMENT MEASURES THE INTENSITIES OF IN-SITU CHARGED PARTICLES (>26 KEV ELECTRONS AND >30 KEV IONS) WITH VARIOUS LEVELS OF DISCRIMINATION BASED ON ENERGY, MASS SPECIES, AND ANGULAR ARRIVAL DIRECTION. A SUBSET OF ALMOST 100 LECP CHANNELS ARE INCLUDED WITH THIS DATA SET. THE LECP DATA ARE GLOBALLY CALIBRATED TO THE EXTENT POSSIBLE (SEE BELOW) AND THEY ARE TIME AVERAGED TO ABOUT 15 MINUTE TIME INTERVALS WITH THE EXACT BEGINNING AND ENDING TIMES FOR THOSE INTERVALS MATCHING THE LECP INSTRUMENTAL CYCLE PERIODS (THE ANGULAR SCANNING PERIODS). THE LECP INSTUMENT HAS A ROTATING HEAD FOR OBTAINING ANGULAR ANISOTROPY MEASUREMENTS OF THE MEDIUM ENERGY CHARGED PARTICLES THAT IT MEASURES. THE CYCLE TIME FOR THE ROTATION IF VARIABLE, BUT DURING ENCOUNTERS IT IS ALWAYS FASTER THAN 15 MINUTES. FOR THIS BROWSE DATA SET ONLY SCAN AVERAGE DATA IS GIVEN (NO ANGULAR INFORMATION). THE DATA IS IN THE FORM OF \'RATE\' DATA WHICH HAS NOT BEEN CONVERTED TO THE USUAL PHYSICAL UNITS. THE REASON IS THAT SUCH A CONVERSION WOULD DEPEND ON UNCERTAIN DETERMINATIONS SUCH AS THE MASS SPECIES OF THE PARTICLES AND THE LEVEL OF BACKGROUND. BOTH MASS SPECIES AND BACKGROUND ARE GENERALLY DETERMINED FROM CONTEXT DURING THE STUDY OF PARTICULAR REGIONS. TO CONVERT \'RATE\' TO \'INTENSITY\' FOR A PARTICULAR CHANNEL ONE PERFORMS THE FOLLOWING TASKS: 1) DECIDE ON THE LEVEL OF BACKGROUND CONTAMINATION AND SUBTRACT THAT OFF THE GIVEN RATE LEVEL. BACKGROUND IS TO BE DETERMINED FROM CONTEXT AND FROM MAKING USE OF SECTOR 8 RATES (SECTOR 8 HAS A 2 mm AL SHIELD COVERING IT). 2) DIVIDE THE BACKGROUND CORRECTED RATE BY THE CHANNEL GEOMETRIC FACTOR AND BY THE ENERGY BANDPASS OF THE CHANNEL. THE GEOMETRIC FACTOR IS FOUND IN ENTRY \'channel_geometric_ factor\' AS ASSOCIATED WITH EACH CHANNEL \'channel_id\'. TO DETERMINE THE ENERGY BANDPASS, ONE MUST JUDGE THE MASS SPECIES OF THE OF THE DETECTED PARTICLES (FOR IONS BUT NOT FOR ELECTRONS). THE ENERGY BAND PASSES ARE GIVEN IN ENTRIES \'minimum_instrument_parameter\' and \'maximum_instrument_ parameter\' IN TABLE \'FPLECPENERGY\', AND ARE GIVEN IN THE FORM \'ENERGY/NUCLEON\'. FOR CHANNELS THAT BEGIN THEIR NAMES WITH THE DESIGNATIONS \'CH\' THESE BANDPASSES CAN BE USED ON MASS SPECIES THAT ARE ACCEPTED INTO THAT CHANNEL (SEE ENTRIES \'minimum_instrument_parameter\' and \'maximum_instrument_ parameter\' IN TABLE \'FPLECPCHANZ\', WHICH GIVE THE MINIMUM AND MAXIMUM \'Z\' VALUE ACCEPTED -- THESE ENTRIES ARE BLANK FOR ELECTRON CHANNELS). FOR OTHER CHANNELS THE GIVEN BANDPASS REFERS ONLY TO THE LOWEST \'Z\' VALUE ACCEPTED. THE BANDPASSES FOR OTHER \'Z\' VALUES ARE NOT ALL KNOWN, BUT SOME ARE GIVEN IN THE LITERATURE (E.G. KRIMIGIS ET AL., 1979). THE FINAL PRODUCT OF THESE INSTRUCTIONS WILL BE THE PARTICLE INTENSITY WITH THE UNITS: COUNTS/(CM**2.STR.SEC.KEV). SOME CHANNELS ARE SUBJECT TO SERIOUS CONTAMINATIONS, AND MANY OF THESE CONTAMINATIONS CANNOT BE REMOVED EXCEPT WITH A REGION-BY-REGION ANALYSIS, WHICH HAS NOT BEEN DONE FOR THIS DATA. THUS, TO USE THIS DATA IT IS ABSOLUTELY VITAL THAT THE CONTAMINATION TYPES (\'contamination_id\' , \'contamination_desc\') AND THE LEVELS OF CONTAMINATION (\'data_quality_id\' CORRESPONDING TO THE DEFINITIONS \'data_quality_desc\') BE CAREFULLY EXAMINED FOR ALL REGIONS OF STUDY. A DEAD TIME CORRECTION PROCEDURE HAS BEEN APPLIED IN AN ATTEMPT TO CORRECT THE LINEAR EFFECTS OF DETECTOR OVERDRIVE (PULSE-PILEUP). THIS PROCEDURE DOES NOT FIX SEVERELY OVERDRIVEN DETECTORS. A PROCEDURE IS AVAILABLE FOR CORRECTING VOYAGER 2 LECP ELECTRON CONTAMINATION OF LOW ENERGY ION CHANNELS, BUT ITS EFFECTIVENESS HAS BEEN EVALUATED ONLY FOR THE URANUS DATA SET. THUS, CORRECTIONS U HAVE BEEN APPLIED ONLY TO THE URANUS DATA SET.','public','2026-03-13T18:07:54.567948','2026-03-13T18:07:54.567954','Planetary Plasma Interactions','Planetary Data System','026:00','e063ef41-afb6-48ee-a62b-05f4b9df2a8f','NASA Data.json','7f68f6ddebad13e6d0acd4242ac1bf9485a61b0c2ec082ce4519bb4f4863338f','1.1','2026-03-13T18:07:54.567948','2026-03-13T18:07:54.567954','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('9c589855-7892-49ba-b190-1f61b806006c','ROSETTA-ORBITER CHECK RPCLAP2 CVP1 EDITED2 V1.0','This data set contains EDITEDdata from Rosetta RPC-LAP, acquired during the COMMISSIONING 1 missionphase where there was no primary target. It contains uncalibrated rawdata, i.e. the digital output of the instrument.','public','2026-03-13T18:55:12.347185','2026-03-13T18:55:12.347192','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','3e3bec38-6b98-4813-aff2-4f64fb376e41','NASA Data.json','2b408ff7c7313868c2a2891b7243f592493de057cc14f7999324e3c95d5877bd','1.1','2026-03-13T18:55:12.347185','2026-03-13T18:55:12.347192','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('9c660455-7284-445c-ba52-c13cca599f69','LRO MOON LASER ALTIMETER 5 SHADR V1.0','This data set contains spherical harmonic topographic (shape) and gravity potential models from the Lunar Orbiter Laser Altimeter  instrument, LRO Laser Ranging, and radio tracking.','public','2026-03-13T17:54:39.888975','2026-03-13T17:54:39.888980','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','8a82a43b-f59c-4759-9be8-2eb2f2850467','NASA Data.json','83cd4f842e3e9487908c41a784a20592d115f7eef414bd3d182cf1fbe9bc471c','1.1','2026-03-13T17:54:39.888975','2026-03-13T17:54:39.888980','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('9ccc93a0-fff9-4531-b4a5-f21f7afc3284','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 1 0499 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 1 phase 2014-11-20 to 2015-03-10. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2014-12-22T00:23:55.000 to 2014-12-22T12:18:15.000.','public','2026-03-13T19:00:46.432997','2026-03-13T19:00:46.433003','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','57138029-f501-448f-9a80-50ece966b251','NASA Data.json','ebb901cfd705a96bfba72b056395216631f74b79c7f07c4f406158bcf6d10ef8','1.1','2026-03-13T19:00:46.432997','2026-03-13T19:00:46.433003','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('9cd9b55f-2fd2-4063-8be6-0c28dfa7761e','EPA Facility Registry Service (FRS): ER_SIC','To improve public health and the environment, the United States Environmental Protection Agency (USEPA) collects information about facilities, sites, or places subject to environmental regulation or of environmental interest. These data are considered sensitive and are restricted to internal use only. The download file and map service are accessible only on the EPA intranet. EPA Category: Mission Sensitive, NARA Category: Critical Infrastructure.','public','2026-03-27T15:37:42.643339','2026-03-31T16:40:00.464293',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2b7e3330-f924-406a-acfe-e43395c3f526','Environmental Dataset Gateway ISO Geospatial Metadata',NULL,NULL,'2026-03-27T15:37:42.643339','2026-03-31T16:40:00.464293',NULL,NULL,NULL,'epa-gov'),('9d20174e-a4c9-4db9-9078-4633272ad73e','2026 Open Data Annual Report -- Look Forward','Look Forward page provided the future plans for Maryland\'s Open Data program.','public','2026-03-15T02:20:16.962045','2026-03-15T02:20:16.962051','opendata.maryland.gov','Helen Bai',NULL,'f0c82c3e-bcd0-47c1-8f86-1d53698da7aa','md json','c5620eca77042b381553d29cc53b6dfb9c0f872957127b6a831c4fbb711ae06e','1.1','2026-03-15T02:20:16.962045','2026-03-15T02:20:16.962051',NULL,NULL,0,'state-of-maryland'),('9d32fc18-d3be-42d4-8d5c-4e2a280a0a28','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSIWAC 4 PRL-MTP001 RDR V2.0','This CODMAC level 4 data set contains radiometric calibrated and geometric distortion corrected (resampled) image data in W/m^2/sr/nm, acquired by the OSIRIS Wide Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft during the PRELANDING mission phase, covering the period from 2014-01-20T10:00:00.000 to 2014-05-07T12:47:59.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V2.0 supersedes previous deliveries of the same dataset with the following changes since the last version: Lien corrected dataset after October 2018 PSA/PDS external peer review. Updated documentation and ancillary files, added document on bandpass filter. Updated SCIENCE_USER_GUIDE_V03.PDF to include one section about FAQ and one section about image data quality. Added shutter backtravel and readout issues to image quality map. Updated DATA_QUALITY_ID keyword in image header. Improved handling of images with missing packets.','public','2026-03-13T17:44:20.785826','2026-03-13T17:44:20.785831','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','d6835e8e-ceb4-4e67-a125-e009462894ba','NASA Data.json','323c527dd0a54a7a1097dac23a61ce6708860552d3f5314bc1b9a362dc1c6b2b','1.1','2026-03-13T17:44:20.785826','2026-03-13T17:44:20.785831','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('9d3b2a6e-931a-46e7-956f-dd9fc65679fe','MARS EXPRESS MARS MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 3 3450 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2010-01-01 to 2012-12-31. It is a Global Gravity measurement and covers the time 2012-12-24T02:20:11.000 to 2012-12-24T04:20:10.500.','public','2026-03-13T20:08:49.733872','2026-03-13T20:08:49.733881','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','613d8686-ac3a-4319-a80c-f25f4b5d663d','NASA Data.json','22123f4645e885d384786bfbc45316239468b4a96982a3b15515bc67c34ff248','1.1','2026-03-13T20:08:49.733872','2026-03-13T20:08:49.733881','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('9d9ccfe7-7ac4-4a5b-8ede-f5195a470afc','ICPS - EPMS Card Agent','This data set represents EPMS Card Agent information obtained from the CLAIMS 3 LAN and ELIS systems as an incoming system interface and persists in the Card Management (formerly NPS) database.','non-public','2026-03-22T11:52:40.375248','2026-03-22T11:52:40.375253','Unspecified','Open Data (MGMT)','024:030','99a38f19-c854-4f57-84f8-e0e99204076f','DHS datajson source','7380ab657abcf2cd8f8377edfc7a5d46dcc11363992df2245ea591de523b9028','1.1','2026-03-22T11:52:40.375248','2026-03-22T11:52:40.375253',NULL,'024:000',0,'dhs-gov'),('9e030c78-fd37-4d1e-9b39-5aaccde05e82','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSINAC 2 EXT3-MTP031 EDR V3.0','This CODMAC level 2 data set contains uncalibrated image data in DN unit, acquired by the OSIRIS Narrow Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft during the ROSETTA EXTENSION 3 mission phase, covering the period from 2016-06-28T23:25:00.000 to 2016-07-26T23:24:59.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V3.0 supersedes previous deliveries of the same dataset with the following changes since the last version: Lien corrected dataset after the July and October 2018 PSA/PDS external peer reviews. Updated documentation and ancillary files, added document on bandpass filter. Updated SCIENCE_USER_GUIDE_V03.PDF to include one section about FAQ and one section about image data quality. Added shutter backtravel and readout issues to image quality map. Updated DATA_QUALITY_ID keyword in image header. Improved handling of images with missing packets.','public','2026-03-13T16:42:42.182626','2026-03-13T16:42:42.182633','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','5ac87e9d-d1b3-44d1-9b71-3914ec81f5a0','NASA Data.json','90c8dc55958d80a0e16a852cf2b2ce7c103c1b093ae2c9d5984dab9239ffa84f','1.1','2026-03-13T16:42:42.182626','2026-03-13T16:42:42.182633','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('9e0b9cc6-556c-44a1-84e3-37774c5d5ef8','Steep Slope 2 ft','<p><strong>Overview</strong></p><p>This Feature Service provides detailed geographic information on steep slope areas within the state of Connecticut. This layer was derived from the 2023 Digital Elevation Model from the <a target=\'_blank\' href=\'https://maps.cteco.uconn.edu/data/flight2023/\' rel=\'nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer\'>2023 Spring imagery and lidar capture</a>. It is developed to support planning, environmental management, and risk assessment related to slope stability.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Details about layer development: <a target=\'_blank\' href=\'https://github.com/ctgisoffice/steep_slopes\' rel=\'nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer\'>https://github.com/ctgisoffice/steep_slopes</a></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Feature Layers</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Steep Slope 10 ft</strong>: This layer maps areas with steep slopes derived from a 10-feet per pixel DEM, providing details such as slope percentage, municipality, and council of governments (COG) region. It offers data for assessing terrain steepness over larger vertical intervals.</li><li><strong>Steep Slope 2 ft</strong>: This layer captures steep slopes derived from a 10-feet per pixel DEM, allowing for more detailed slope analysis at a smaller vertical resolution. Similar attribute details like slope percent, municipality, and COG are included, supporting higher-resolution terrain studies.</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Geographic Coverage</strong></p><p>The data covers the landscape of Connecticut, focusing on areas with significant slope gradients that may impact land use and development.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p style=\'line-height:125%;\'><span><strong>Classifications</strong></span></p><ul><li><p style=\'margin-bottom:0in; margin-right:0in; margin-top:0in;\'><span>Agency: OPM</span></p></li><li><p style=\'margin-bottom:0in; margin-right:0in; margin-top:0in;\'><span>Sensitivity: Public</span></p></li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p style=\'line-height:125%;\'><span><strong>Currency </strong>(time)</span></p><ul><li><p style=\'margin-bottom:0in; margin-right:0in; margin-top:0in;\'><span>Created Data: 2026</span></p></li><li><p style=\'margin-bottom:0in; margin-right:0in; margin-top:0in;\'><span>Update Frequency (estimated): none</span></p></li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p style=\'line-height:125%;\'><span><strong>Lineage</strong></span></p><ul><li><span>Originated: D</span>erived from the 2023 Digital Elevation Model from the <a target=\'_blank\' href=\'https://maps.cteco.uconn.edu/data/flight2023/\' rel=\'nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer\'>2023 Spring imagery and lidar capture</a></li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p style=\'line-height:125%;\'><strong>Attributes</strong></p><ul><li><p style=\'line-height:125%;\'><strong>Slope_Percent </strong>- The category of percent steep slope. Moderate (10%-15%), Steep (15%-20%), Very Steep (20%+).</p></li><li><p style=\'line-height:125%;\'><strong>Muni </strong>- Municipality</p></li><li><p style=\'line-height:125%;\'><strong>COG </strong>- Council of Governments</p></li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p>','public','2026-03-29T03:53:16.276478','2026-03-29T03:53:16.276483','State of Connecticut','ctgisoffice',NULL,'3f95eae5-db3d-4fa4-b737-8e283b686793','Connecticut Data.json','8b7b8fcb8e70567e102a8f4b6f02c41dd055d8e5c8ed815fd785b2c99f6fe807','1.1','2026-03-29T03:53:16.276478','2026-03-29T03:53:16.276483','geospatial',NULL,0,'state-of-connecticut'),('9e290e50-c015-4f6a-ab29-365b355e5313','2025 FTB EITC Summary of CA Residents Year Comparison','Produced by the Economic & Statistical Research Bureau, year-end tabulations of tax filings statistics for the Earned Income Tax Credit, (EITC), Young Child Tax Credit (YCTC) and Foster Youth Tax Credit (FYTC) provide credit use by county, preparer type, credit amount allowed number of dependents and a many other useful cross-sections.','public','2026-03-23T13:52:22.367719','2026-03-23T13:52:22.367723','California Franchise Tax Board','FTB Open Data',NULL,'666ff76f-512f-40a7-a9dc-cd98dfacbe58','State of California','41457a2cf1daa025463e9e76cd362376c17c027209c5a0f788ea1140405430fd','1.1','2026-03-23T13:52:22.367719','2026-03-23T13:52:22.367723','Economy and Demographics',NULL,0,'ca-gov'),('9e717543-87a0-4a89-b8f0-3dccce8e56b2','VOYAGER 2 SOLAR WIND MAGNETIC FIELD HGCOORDS 48SEC AVG V1.0','This dataset contains Voyager 2 magnetometer data from the      interplanetary cruise averaged to 48 second samples in Heliographic      coordinates.','public','2026-03-13T19:51:38.418855','2026-03-13T19:51:38.418861','planetary plasma interactions','Planetary Data System','026:00','01ca28fd-b7d4-4859-958c-6d868bb75c67','NASA Data.json','b6cf8c0680f550d5f668e11ca8d2b7f4e2ef9abe3ffcd5570e37824601c5b47a','1.1','2026-03-13T19:51:38.418855','2026-03-13T19:51:38.418861','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('9e95c30f-9ba8-4fd1-b343-b88e25e552de','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P VIRTIS 2 ESCORT 2 MTP017 V1.0','This release contains the digital numbers (DN) contained in the telemetry (TM) packages of the VIRTIS instrument on board of the spacecraft Rosetta. This volume contains data at the vicinity of comet 67P, from the ESCORT 2 MTP017 phase, which occurred from 2015-06-03 to 2015-07-01','public','2026-03-13T20:06:49.096196','2026-03-13T20:06:49.096203','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','a8ac4a88-5c04-4082-968a-f165d2a38be3','NASA Data.json','ad41ad48b6ee863df7f19f2863295625522d595c0ed0316fe111b723843003c7','1.1','2026-03-13T20:06:49.096196','2026-03-13T20:06:49.096203','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('9ecd0e0f-71b8-48ff-8883-28fb2a9461a3','CLEMENTINE LWIR BRIGHTNESS TEMPERATURE V1.0','The Clementine Long-WaveInfrared (LWIR) Brightness Temperature data set containscalibrated brightness temperature images that provide informationon physical properties of the lunar surface.','public','2026-03-13T17:02:00.397758','2026-03-13T17:02:00.397763','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','00d21074-3420-4b43-bf39-506c5ae95b37','NASA Data.json','19f61e1f88972598d3e4472af0d0b128a61239208b79c1f58678642d6fc83ca4','1.1','2026-03-13T17:02:00.397758','2026-03-13T17:02:00.397763','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('9ef8b9de-57cb-4b58-99fb-333d1ea43685','MER 1 MI RADIOMETRICALLY CALIBRATED RDR V1.0','This archive volume is one of a set of volumes containing raw andderived data from the Mars Exploration Rover mission. This volumecontains \'science\' data products, which were generated by theinstrument team for archiving, as distinguished from \'operations\' dataproducts, which were generated by the Multi-Mission Image ProcessingFacility (MIPL) at JPL for using during mission operations. For moreinformation about science vs. operations products, see the text fileSCI_VS_OPS.TXT in the DOCUMENT directory.','public','2026-03-13T17:36:13.980732','2026-03-13T17:36:13.980736','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','b87e1af0-afb0-4e0b-8d11-e3d69cce4040','NASA Data.json','fc225fc040db99140317f45c15d03d1140fb0cd0617fb6abce32199f861d7db8','1.1','2026-03-13T17:36:13.980732','2026-03-13T17:36:13.980736','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('9f02bf0c-9b07-4484-9639-338d288f1e1a','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSIWAC 4 ESC1-MTP011 RDR V2.0','This CODMAC level 4 data set contains radiometric calibrated and geometric distortion corrected (resampled) image data in W/m^2/sr/nm, acquired by the OSIRIS Wide Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft during the COMET ESCORT 1 mission phase, covering the period from 2014-12-19T23:25:00.000 to 2015-01-13T23:24:59.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V2.0 supersedes previous deliveries of the same dataset with the following changes since the last version: Lien corrected dataset after October 2018 PSA/PDS external peer review. Updated documentation and ancillary files, added document on bandpass filter. Updated SCIENCE_USER_GUIDE_V03.PDF to include one section about FAQ and one section about image data quality. Added shutter backtravel and readout issues to image quality map. Updated DATA_QUALITY_ID keyword in image header. Improved handling of images with missing packets.','public','2026-03-13T17:12:00.436008','2026-03-13T17:12:00.436017','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','ca415d35-732d-4270-a558-730bafa11705','NASA Data.json','8ca6daf179f50bb53dbf5585b457fdff2f6efeb89a81d8eef134a6992bec76eb','1.1','2026-03-13T17:12:00.436008','2026-03-13T17:12:00.436017','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('9f2e6ded-d1fc-4ac8-ac82-9469095aa77b','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSIWAC 4 ESC1-MTP013 RDR-INF-REFL V1.0','This CODMAC level 4 data set contains solar stray-light corrected, in-field stray-light corrected,  radiometric calibrated and geometric distortion corrected  (resampled) image data in reflectance units (normalized  and thus without unit),  acquired by the OSIRIS Wide Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft  during the COMET ESCORT 1 mission phase, covering the period  from 2015-02-10T23:25:00.000 to 2015-03-10T23:24:59.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V1.0 is the first version of this dataset: Lien corrected dataset after September 2019 PSA/PDS external peer review.','public','2026-03-13T18:32:22.083034','2026-03-13T18:32:22.083038','Small Bodies','Tess Jaffe','026:00','865f770c-e201-47e6-ab9b-cbdc989c772f','NASA Data.json','38c989f469ab5bbbb156cadcc22e1e63a88e93bd4e648cdb0014786ac57d70bc','1.1','2026-03-13T18:32:22.083034','2026-03-13T18:32:22.083038','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('9f60ba4a-eca1-40ad-9e88-a68201438fea','MARS EXPRESS MARS MRS 1/2/3                                     EXTENDED MISSION 8 4345 V1.0','This is a Mars Express                                     Radio Science data set, collected                                     during the extended mission phase                                     2023-01-01 to 2023-12-31.                                     It is a Occultation                                     measurement and covers the time                                     2023-10-08T07:21:02.100 to                                     2023-10-08T07:43:10.100.','public','2026-03-13T19:00:06.260185','2026-03-13T19:00:06.260192','geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','01d73b26-07bd-46c0-93d1-449d8d69ea47','NASA Data.json','a558c032d1ce217724042fb4d16d3c7a6deb1125d16022ee439d0c4e6db2238b','1.1','2026-03-13T19:00:06.260185','2026-03-13T19:00:06.260192','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('9f759b75-a462-4549-a088-a8ea58312380','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 3 1094 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 3 phase 2015-07-01 to 2015-10-21. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-10-11T10:17:05.000 to 2015-10-11T17:28:21.500.','public','2026-03-13T17:38:20.182733','2026-03-13T17:38:20.182739','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','959a7d2d-2531-4fd6-8911-b81de0bb8623','NASA Data.json','ed521da83ec29eda85ac4ffac977e5ea923e852a4c7b7110310640e168101930','1.1','2026-03-13T17:38:20.182733','2026-03-13T17:38:20.182739','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('9f9339f9-ce6b-4d83-9e7c-5dae036a1adc','MARS EXPRESS SUN MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 7 4069 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2019-01-01 to 2020-12-31. It is a Solar Conjunction measurement and covers the time 2019-09-22T10:10:00.000 to 2019-09-22T13:20:00.000.','public','2026-03-13T17:02:40.410700','2026-03-13T17:02:40.410706','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','0094778b-7ef3-4d13-8d73-00e3f45bad85','NASA Data.json','11c355fe18b0b448ab8184dee7c9f375b165a750f3f1a08473ab557a5a585bfd','1.1','2026-03-13T17:02:40.410700','2026-03-13T17:02:40.410706','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('9fa03897-4762-48cc-a2eb-3b08c2469894','Data from: Physical and microbial root-zone factors underlying tomato wilt in long-term biofloc aquaponic systems','<p dir=\"ltr\"><u>Experimental Aquaponics Systems</u></p><p dir=\"ltr\">Twelve independent aquaponics systems were established in a double poly greenhouse located at the EW Shell Fisheries Center in Auburn, AL. Each aquaponics system consisted of a 700L fish tank stocked with 40 tilapia and a 1 m<sup>2</sup> grow bed filled with pea gravel substrate. The systems were run for two years which involved tilapia grow out from March to November in 2023 and 2024. Fingerlings were stocked in March (20-50 g) and grown to 400-500 g at which point they were harvested (November). In 2024, a partial harvest was carried out in September to ensure fish mass in the tanks did not exceed 20 kg/ m3 of water. Cherry tomatoes were cultivated in the grow beds with two crops per year (4 crops in total). More specific detail on the operational parameters of these systems can be found in our prior publications:</p><p dir=\"ltr\">https://doi.org/10.1016/j.aquaculture.2025.743286</p><p dir=\"ltr\">https://doi.org/10.1016/j.biteb.2025.102439</p><p dir=\"ltr\">Four experimental conditions were tested with three independent aquaponics system replicates for each condition. These conditions involved testing two factors: allowing natural sunlight penetration into the fish tanks (versus covering them to block light) and running the systems in coupled versus decoupled operation. Coupled operation allows water to recirculate from the fish tank to the grow bed and then back to the fish tank. Decoupled operation allows water to flow from the fish tank to the grow bed and then to a sump. Water is recirculated between the sump and grow bed. When water from the fish tank is used for irrigation, this causes the sump to overflow into a drain. The net effect is one-way flow from fish tank to grow bed. As both factors were tested in a full factorial design, this resulted in the four experimental treatments: Light decoupled, Light coupled, Dark decoupled, and Dark coupled.</p><p dir=\"ltr\">An ebb and flow irrigation cycle was achieved using a bell siphon in 2023. This system was prone to clogging and was switched to a timer-controlled flow regime in 2024 (30 minutes on, 30 minutes off). Also, 6 tomato plants per grow bed were used in 2023 while 5 tomato plants per bed were planted in 2024 to provide more space for each plant. The Favorita F1 varietal from Johnny’s Seeds was used in all trials except for Spring of 2023 where the Washington varietal was used. Ripe tomatoes were harvested from each system multiple times per week in response to plant production levels. Fruits were weighed for each system. Cumulative tomato yields were tracked for each system and divided by the number of plants in the system.</p><p dir=\"ltr\">In 2023, solids removal between the fish tank and grow bed consisted of a series of foam filter materials (Pentair PF7 and PF17C). In 2024, radial flow separators (RFS) were installed to remove large solid particulates (mostly fecal matter) followed by one layer of foam filter material (Pentair PF7 only). This change was implemented in response to high levels of solids deposition on filter material and in grow beds in the 2023 trial. Sludge removal from the RFS was carried out several times per week. Volumes and total suspended solids (TSS) in removed material were recorded to understand how effectively the RFS was removing solids across the different system types.</p>','public','2026-03-13T22:47:15.314151','2026-03-13T22:47:15.314157','Agricultural Research Service','Higgins, Brendan, T','005:18','95889826-a2a9-46df-95b9-0b9bbaf223f8','USDA JSON','341f548dfa41496e9b8c76ce1509d884085e878f7d1d54d1b97ab7630fac07c4','1.1','2026-03-13T22:47:15.314151','2026-03-13T22:47:15.314157',NULL,'005:040',0,'usda-gov'),('9fcf2888-2f02-4f95-9fff-2884ba51acc2','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 1 0447 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 1 phase 2014-11-20 to 2015-03-10. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2014-11-20T13:47:20.000 to 2014-11-20T20:23:15.000.','public','2026-03-13T17:01:31.695763','2026-03-13T17:01:31.695770','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','2b888c60-e31c-46ff-9358-984caefb4335','NASA Data.json','15ef4e90d1017f1c34bbc541363a95fe0110d5aaa2b77d94477ab854f6a8af22','1.1','2026-03-13T17:01:31.695763','2026-03-13T17:01:31.695770','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('9feb8823-f3b9-4220-8b07-82b1ea227088','ROSETTA-ORBITER COMET PRELANDING OSINAC 2 EDR MTP 008 V1.0','This data set contains raw EDR images acquired by the OSIRIS Narrow AngleCamera during the prelanding phase of the Rosetta mission at the comet 67P,covering the period from 2014-09-23 to 2014-10-24.','public','2026-03-13T17:03:46.969878','2026-03-13T17:03:46.969884','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','c385e455-b18d-47fa-af31-9f898e138913','NASA Data.json','836aaa04b072cae48f48d6c82658792ec9df2500f394347da1f3e856535f487c','1.1','2026-03-13T17:03:46.969878','2026-03-13T17:03:46.969884','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('9ff8604c-6ddd-4a79-aeb7-1966f13116a4','BLM ID Right of Way Poly','These are Rights-of-Ways (ROW) on Idaho BLM land (and some other Federal agency land) as shown on Bureau of Land Management (BLM) Master Title Plats (MTP). Every GIS ROW feature has a \"CASEFILE\" value, also known as the serial number of the ROW. The ROW data that was digitized is what was present on the MTP at the time of the digitizing done for that township. The project was performed over several years. Therefore, the \"early\" townships digitized are more out of date regarding ROWs compared to the ones more recently digitized. Unfortunately, there is no attribute that indicates the digitizing sequence. Any updates to this ROW feature class should be sent to the BLM Idaho State Office GIS staff for incorporation into the statewide GIS ROW feature classes for improvement over time. For more information contact us at blm_id_stateoffice@blm.gov.','public','2026-03-26T12:41:03.732347','2026-03-26T12:41:03.732355','Bureau of Land Management','Bureau of Land Management, blm_id_stateoffice','010:04','be837139-0f24-4a30-9a8f-6326228d1497','DOI BLM DCAT-US','86a17fe542f1963afc6ae3bb31ad91573c33f94dbe04eb959ba3d3c03919a0dd','1.1','2026-03-26T12:41:03.732347','2026-03-26T12:41:03.732355','geospatial','010:000',0,'doi-gov'),('a00b6d50-a1cc-46a1-8016-668e1a536841','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSIWAC 2 ESC3-MTP018 EDR V3.0','This CODMAC level 2 data set contains uncalibrated image data in DN unit, acquired by the OSIRIS Wide Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft during the COMET ESCORT 3 mission phase, covering the period from 2015-06-30T23:25:00.000 to 2015-07-28T23:24:59.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V3.0 supersedes previous deliveries of the same dataset with the following changes since the last version: Lien corrected dataset after the July and October 2018 PSA/PDS external peer reviews. Updated documentation and ancillary files, added document on bandpass filter. Updated SCIENCE_USER_GUIDE_V03.PDF to include one section about FAQ and one section about image data quality. Added shutter backtravel and readout issues to image quality map. Updated DATA_QUALITY_ID keyword in image header. Improved handling of images with missing packets. Included FITs files. Browse products changed to the same size as the original image.','public','2026-03-13T17:59:47.430785','2026-03-13T17:59:47.430791','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','941312f9-aae3-49a9-9c9f-4f6ee7bfda6e','NASA Data.json','f40f5988691f3904e62e462111aaf7c13d7b0b890064a23e09c8ccd08d8bce81','1.1','2026-03-13T17:59:47.430785','2026-03-13T17:59:47.430791','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('a00d434a-0437-4585-8a6e-a57d395a2f12','ROSETTA-ORBITER SW RPCMAG 3 CR2 CALIBRATED V9.0','This dataset contains CALIBRATED (CODMAC LEVEL 3) DATA of the CRUISE 2 (CR2)phase of the ROSETTA orbiter magnetometer RPCMAG.Included are data from the time interval June 1, 2005 until July 8, 2006.The current version of the dataset is V9.0.The difference to the datasets of earlier versions is mainly a significantlyimproved sensor temperature model, more detailed documentation about magneticdisturbance sources, more data handling information for the user andalso an improved quality flagging system.','public','2026-03-13T17:34:53.686233','2026-03-13T17:34:53.686241','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','576ac908-455d-485c-9631-3ca8da5c2db4','NASA Data.json','c3fcc24585cf7b943402eac02747c2c0bde2a438251c80c924674d062cce742b','1.1','2026-03-13T17:34:53.686233','2026-03-13T17:34:53.686241','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('a0411962-c8e1-456f-83fb-dfa59a6de125','Alaska Department of Natural Resources North Slope Rehabilitation Assessment Sites','This layer was developed by ABR for this project, using data provided by BP Alaska, Inc,. ConocoPhillips, Inc., and Hilcorp Alaska, LLC. It shows the locations of selected sites on the North Slope where ABR has conducted land rehabilitation planning, treatments and/or monitoring. Each site is shown as a polygon representing its approximate size and shape. The data provided for each site also include site type (e.g., exploratory well site, spill) and operator (BP/Hilcorp or CPAI). Permission should be obtained from the site owner(s) before making any of this information available to the public. Several of these sites are described in the accompanying Guidance Document for land rehabilitation planning.','public','2026-03-13T22:36:14.483133','2026-03-13T22:36:14.483139','U.S. Fish and Wildlife Service','Todd Sutherland','010:18','a87a6d9b-e248-4608-b337-22af510765bb','DOI FWS DCAT-US','4f263415e6aad95e9f5bb36893fda1aa1069f68d799678598d90695d1f65c02a','1.1','2026-03-13T22:36:14.483133','2026-03-13T22:36:14.483139','geospatial','010:028',0,'doi-gov'),('a05aff2b-c6b1-47d5-898a-ad969f705a6a','BLM ID Grazing Pastures','This feature class depicts the boundaries of the livestock grazing pastures under the jurisdiction of the Idaho Bureau of Land Management. A pasture is a sub-unit of a grazing allotment; each allotment is comprised of at least one pasture. An allotment is an area of land designated and managed for grazing of livestock. An allotment may include private and state lands, in addition to public lands under the jurisdiction of the Bureau of Land Management and/or other federal agencies. All allotments and pastures are recorded and tracked in BLM\'s Rangeland Administrative System (RAS). This GIS feature class provides a spatial component to pastures and allotments.    For more information contact us at blm_id_stateoffice@blm.gov.','public','2026-03-25T12:35:46.149727','2026-03-25T12:35:46.149732','Bureau of Land Management','Bureau of Land Management, id_so_information','010:04','58a46eff-319a-42fc-86b3-688e72f12ca4','DOI BLM DCAT-US','a599b11a6ea76667128663c3449970e7f8f1616e1af03a47f3e07a3ce869384a','1.1','2026-03-25T12:35:46.149727','2026-03-25T12:35:46.149732','geospatial','010:000',0,'doi-gov'),('a06f1467-edd2-4f37-9122-2d15d390f1e9','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P VIRTIS 2 ESCORT 1 MTP010 V2.0','This release contains the digital numbers (DN) contained in the telemetry (TM) packages of the VIRTIS instrument on board of the spacecraft Rosetta. This volume contains data at the vicinity of comet 67P, from the ESCORT 1 MTP010 phase, which occurred from 2014-11-22 to 2014-12-20. This version of the dataset (2.0) is produced by a fixed EGSE software. The old version of the software produced incomplete products, reduced by one line','public','2026-03-13T20:04:55.053493','2026-03-13T20:04:55.053500','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','eef82d45-ca68-4c94-b78c-1281fec04884','NASA Data.json','50e602b71c111a2c67ca1054410d31e22db8020c3cbbdc75e55a4bfb1a2476c5','1.1','2026-03-13T20:04:55.053493','2026-03-13T20:04:55.053500','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('a08d5fba-1819-46c6-930b-f0447f739fa2','MARS EXPRESS MARS MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 8 4282 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2021-01-01 to 2022-12-31. It is a Occultation measurement and covers the time 2022-06-05T02:15:24.000 to 2022-06-05T04:45:04.000.','public','2026-03-13T19:30:40.392685','2026-03-13T19:30:40.392692','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','7f9cd9fe-407f-4338-b9d1-a261b54dd802','NASA Data.json','0bbaebef3fe2b5e72afb7f557017f16f26bd59a8035d039c8e97953cd72e0189','1.1','2026-03-13T19:30:40.392685','2026-03-13T19:30:40.392692','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('a093b4d7-987c-43e1-be9e-98ad5d4915db','NEAR MSI IMAGES FOR CRUISE2','NEAR EDR volume sets contain a single data set, from one instrument and one mission phase (defined in the phase table in /AAREADME.TXT).','public','2026-03-13T18:20:22.637465','2026-03-13T18:20:22.637470','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','b919db21-3802-4da2-bfbf-2e8ed7f8ffcd','NASA Data.json','708f23e55eda6a438a37635c2e1ed2bbef27036c6c1047134a77e36b9e75cb7c','1.1','2026-03-13T18:20:22.637465','2026-03-13T18:20:22.637470','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('a0ac6c82-6146-42c0-ac93-11bc4a90992f','CASSINI SATURN UVIS SOLAR STELLAR BRIGHTNESS TIME SERIES 1.2','Photometric observations of stellar occultations by Saturnian rings, satellites, atmospheres, and Jovian atmosphere.','public','2026-03-13T19:16:49.868713','2026-03-13T19:16:49.868720','Planetary Atmospheres','Planetary Data System','026:00','8d5c770c-84e9-43e0-a694-5efd845e7663','NASA Data.json','24438edfaccb422b00e6c45c0fb93935e1fa09a3806615796d4fca12471461e2','1.1','2026-03-13T19:16:49.868713','2026-03-13T19:16:49.868720','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('a0af1891-b88e-4acd-b39b-cf3082cd46ba','GALILEO VENUS AND EARTH SOLID STATE IMAGING 2 RAW EDR V1','not applicable','public','2026-03-13T17:29:50.374638','2026-03-13T17:29:50.374643','Imaging','Planetary Data System','026:00','50e3e28d-0cea-4078-bfff-3c436e9dd07d','NASA Data.json','5e8fb68738c87089ee44130a21260f51951cea09d53d95e829fa3ae57e1aecf5','1.1','2026-03-13T17:29:50.374638','2026-03-13T17:29:50.374643','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('a13765d4-6c0a-458c-a55a-f44d6ad4259b','ROSETTA-ORBITER CHECKOUT OSINAC 4 CVP1 RDR V1.0','This CODMAC level 4 data set contains radiometric calibrated and geometric distortion corrected (resampled) image data in W/m^2/sr/nm,  acquired by the OSIRIS Narrow Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft  during the COMMISSIONING 1 mission phase, covering the period  from 2004-03-05T00:00:00.000 to 2004-06-06T23:59:59.000. The prime objective was commissioning / calibration. Several targets of opportunity were observed, but none of them is identifiable as prime target. This version V1.0 is the first version of this dataset.','public','2026-03-13T16:52:06.858119','2026-03-13T16:52:06.858125','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','06651ba6-c711-4f41-90f2-3eafe42c9751','NASA Data.json','ac25083c8ca922b5d9481e08c115be195bc7c23bbaa47ecd03c919d703692adb','1.1','2026-03-13T16:52:06.858119','2026-03-13T16:52:06.858125','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('a16a1386-8a96-4759-ac89-c4965f171fe9','EGIS - Enterprise Gateway Integration Services-Denaturalization Service (DNATZ)','Denaturalization service supports the tracking of cases that should be reviewed to remove citizenship due to fraudulent or criminal activities.','non-public','2026-03-22T11:54:35.620100','2026-03-22T11:54:35.620107','Unspecified','Open Data (MGMT)','024:030','dd2f6322-0c52-4945-9385-23e8c0fc7b8b','DHS datajson source','e4f2acb763aa4ebe9931e3bd37754ce0ffd77a0ad0252d4173017f018296339c','1.1','2026-03-22T11:54:35.620100','2026-03-22T11:54:35.620107',NULL,'024:000',0,'dhs-gov'),('a1711af8-319c-4ce5-b2ad-d112695159f9','Okeanos Explorer (EX1501): Ship Shakedown and Patch							Test','Multibeam and single beam data will be collected 24 hours a day\n					and XBT casts will be conducted at an interval defined by prevailing\n					oceanographic conditions, but not to exceed 6 hours. Additionally, EK 60 and\n					sub-bottom profile data will be collected 24 hours per day. A new EK80\n					instrument will be tested. The Okeanos Explorer will continue to host NASA\'s\n					Maritime Aerosol Network sensors to provide ship-borne aerosol optical depth\n					measurements from sun photometers for NASA.','public','2026-03-28T23:17:14.833118','2026-03-28T23:17:14.833124',NULL,NULL,NULL,'4ca23842-15e1-4f30-8940-2aedecc13394','NCDDC OER',NULL,NULL,'2026-03-28T23:17:14.833118','2026-03-28T23:17:14.833124',NULL,NULL,NULL,'noaa-gov'),('a1722f97-193d-4962-a78c-4ec1602bee55','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 3 1056 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 3 phase 2015-07-01 to 2015-10-21. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-09-25T03:07:15.000 to 2015-09-25T09:27:57.000.','public','2026-03-13T18:46:20.405942','2026-03-13T18:46:20.405947','Small Bodies','Tess Jaffe','026:00','4284b06c-1d46-4d3e-847b-191af6c512bf','NASA Data.json','c3e46aaa8b0d0e88cbb95cdcf0950ef85670c397708a75ab09ab92f8e8d92b6f','1.1','2026-03-13T18:46:20.405942','2026-03-13T18:46:20.405947','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('a1a0eed1-ed70-4b83-acdd-45619b0afbe9','TNO AND CENTAUR COLORS V10.0','This data set is intended to include published broadband colors of centaurs and Transneptunian Objects (TNOs) published through March 2014. It includes some comets with Centaur orbits. It supersedes all versions of the TNO colors data set EAR-A-3-RDR-TNO-PHOT.','public','2026-03-13T17:07:38.516211','2026-03-13T17:07:38.516216','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','22c0475c-42ca-4c4e-844f-a25aac580d57','NASA Data.json','7773e21cacd3a390000e058508f7ab2e0906ccce05bfe93fd44119c6b0a222fc','1.1','2026-03-13T17:07:38.516211','2026-03-13T17:07:38.516216','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('a1aea78c-07b9-4a2e-81fb-8498ca9521ff','2024 High Injury Network','<strong>A. SUMMARY</strong> \nThis dataset includes street segments that were identified to be on the 2024 High Injury Network (HIN). The HIN shows the street corridors that had the highest concentration of severe and fatal injuries in the years 2020 to 2024. \n\nUsing the High Injury Network, San Francisco is better able to prioritize city resources to implement engineering, education, and enforcement activities that serve to make the streets safer. \n\n<strong>B. HOW THE DATASET IS CREATED</strong> \nThis dataset is sourced from traffic crash data from the San Francisco Police Department, hospital data from Zuckerberg San Francisco General Hospital (ZSFG), and ambulance operator data from American Medical Response (AMR) and the San Francisco Fire Department Emergency Medical Services (EMS). These data are linked using a non-probabilistic deterministic method to match records between these three data sources. Once they are matched, any details about the crash circumstances are defaulted to come from the San Francisco Police Department (SFPD), and the final injury severity determination is sourced from ZSFG Hospital. The dataset also includes un-matched SFPD severe and fatal crash victims that had associated geolocations, as well as un-linked ZSFG Hospital data from the Trauma Registry that had linked geolocation data from the ambulance operators’ pick- up locations. \n\nSan Francisco’s street centerline data layer is corridorized into segments that are at least 0.25 miles long along segments that share the same street name. Then, the point data of Killed or Severely Injured (KSI) is plotted onto the map and a KSI per mile per corridor is calculated based on a count of points that geographically intersect a given corridor. \n\nThe base map for the HIN is created by filtering corridors based on minimum length. Any corridor that is less than 0.25 miles in total length is excluded from eligibility onto the network. Then, corridors are selected based on a minimum cutpoint of “greater than or equal to 10 KSI per mile per corridor.” \n\nAdditional processing of the map includes finding street segments of the base HIN map that are greater than 500 feet away from the last on-HIN KSI on that street. These “stubs” are removed before producing the final HIN map in order to further prioritize city resources on the streets with the highest 5-year incidence of severe injuries and fatalities. \n\n<strong>C. UPDATE PROCESS</strong> \nThis dataset will not need to be updated once published. \n\n<strong>D. HOW TO USE THIS DATASET</strong> \nThis dataset only includes street segments that were identified to be on the High Injury Network. \n\n<strong>E. RELATED DATASETS</strong> \n<u><a href=\"https://data.sfgov.org/d/ubvf-ztfx\">Traffic Crashes Resulting in Injury</a></u> \n<u><a href=\"https://data.sfgov.org/d/8gtc-pjc6\">Traffic Crashes Resulting in Injury: Parties Involved</a></u> \n<u><a href=\"https://data.sfgov.org/d/nwes-mmgh\">Traffic Crashes Resulting in Injury: Victims Involved</a></u> \n<u><a href=\"https://data.sfgov.org/d/dau3-4s8f\">Traffic Crashes Resulting in Fatality </a></u> \n<u><a href=\"https://data.sfgov.org/d/8vtn-qytr\">2022 High Injury Network </a></u> \n \n<strong>F. KNOWN USES</strong> \n* San Francisco County Transportation Authority\n* Public health injury prevention professionals \n* SFMTA staff\n* Transit Advocates \n* Pedestrian advocates\n* Bicycling advocates\n* Senior health centers and residential centers\n* Automobile insurance companies\n* California Office of Traffic Safety','public','2026-03-29T05:01:05.620386','2026-03-29T05:01:05.620390','data.sfgov.org','OpenData',NULL,'f8403695-534b-4397-b1f6-be50d99980d6','SFO JSON','844b9ebaae710cb40e369a61201465e7521d914ba9831c6bfecf44780290452c','1.1','2026-03-29T05:01:05.620386','2026-03-29T05:01:05.620390','Health and Social Services',NULL,0,'city-of-san-francisco'),('a1b52d80-e611-47b0-b821-c3771fa123f6','Help America Vote Verification (HAVV) Transactions by State - Week Ending March 14, 2026','This dataset represents the results of the 4-digit match performed using the Social Security - Help America Vote Verification (HAVV) system. Report for week ending March 14, 2026.','public','2026-03-31T17:20:22.192020','2026-03-31T17:20:22.192025','Social Security Administration','Open Data','016:00','0bc76a9e-7d91-4cc2-abab-26e53d90f107','SSA JSON','161b5706a1ae04580fe3ae77fefb1710cbcea918b5dc0e8e115c1612466951d9','1.1','2026-03-31T17:20:22.192020','2026-03-31T17:20:22.192025',NULL,'016:000',0,'ssa-gov'),('a20b236e-6c7a-48e6-8a42-bcfffd3ea26b','IHW COMET IRPHOT EDITED REDUCED DATA RECORD GZ V1.0','In preparation for the concerted international study of Comet Halley, the IHW conducted a trial run with observations of Comet Crommelin, largely during February and March of 1984.','public','2026-03-13T17:49:15.095461','2026-03-13T17:49:15.095468','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','452b5463-36a1-403d-915f-5fce13652dc2','NASA Data.json','3ff53548ae55067de1ae096c5edf6897d13ffafa28d9b0874f6a370afef3222d','1.1','2026-03-13T17:49:15.095461','2026-03-13T17:49:15.095468','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('a223c3ad-3bf9-4130-a35f-01d0610502d2','ROSETTA-ORBITER/ROSETTA-LANDER 67P CONSERT 2 SDL V2.0','This archive contains raw data from the CONSERT instrument onboard ROSETTA Orbiter and Lander, acquired during SDL (Separation, Descent and Landing) comet phase. The primary target is the comet 67P/CHURYUMOV-GERASIMENKO. It also contains documentation which describes the CONSERT experiment. The data archived in this data set conform to the Planetary Data System (PDS) Standards, Version 3.6. This data set supersedes RO/RL-C-CONSERT-2-SDL-V1.0.','public','2026-03-13T16:43:27.122136','2026-03-13T16:43:27.122145','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','73d014c1-3218-4741-9e5c-7d324de1ccb4','NASA Data.json','b7f754c9e16740ef8b4938226c398467a6982c4b8098b284296b1dbe622f6b60','1.1','2026-03-13T16:43:27.122136','2026-03-13T16:43:27.122145','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('a223cd86-73a3-4b32-af4d-9c86bad1416d','Data for ioos-station-wmo-42937-20171211_1742-20171211_1742','Current profile data from Downward-looking Teledyne RDI 38 kHz Ocean Observer ADCP, ADCP #0 on Maersk Viking, 28.78N, 88.23W, 2017/12/11 through 2018/02/15','public','2026-03-26T19:17:28.053014','2026-03-26T19:17:28.053020',NULL,NULL,NULL,'f1b5006c-461e-4b7f-8e85-779f06426b2f','ioos',NULL,NULL,'2026-03-26T19:17:28.053014','2026-03-26T19:17:28.053020',NULL,NULL,NULL,'noaa-gov'),('a250ba25-9236-49b9-951d-b7dd51a15cd8','Data for Projecting and valuing climate change impacts on anxiety and depression in the contiguous United States','The data saved here are for a forthcoming article, Projecting and valuing climate change impacts on anxiety and depression in the contiguous United States. \n\nThis dataset is associated with the following publication:\nBelova, A., K. Munson, D. Keeler, M. Sluder, A. Kiesel, M.C. Sarofim, R. Silva, S. Anenberg, S. Clayton, and C.A. Gould. Projecting and valuing climate change impacts on anxiety and depression in the contiguous USA: a damage function approach.   The Lancet Planetary Health. Elsevier B.V., Amsterdam,  NETHERLANDS, 10(2): 101426, (2026).','public','2026-03-28T13:39:44.219129','2026-03-28T13:39:44.219134','U.S. Environmental Protection Agency','Caitlin Gould','020:00','c44fbfa6-998b-4072-8ba2-2bf52f06d450','EPA ScienceHub','189c17d12c2314a516ea000f8ae87048531f8dea4297e38524cb262146977c00','1.1','2026-03-28T13:39:44.219129','2026-03-28T13:39:44.219134',NULL,'020:000',0,'epa-gov'),('a26513ef-b26f-4cf4-84ab-cfbabcd3fe0c','Long Lake, AK (1001)','Timeseries data from \'Long Lake, AK (1001)\' (gov_usda_nrcs_sntl_1001)','public','2026-03-26T19:15:15.477112','2026-03-26T19:15:15.477119',NULL,NULL,NULL,'af4c94c9-d4b9-42a8-8b9d-db7a5b1cb9bd','ioos',NULL,NULL,'2026-03-26T19:15:15.477112','2026-03-26T19:15:15.477119',NULL,NULL,NULL,'noaa-gov'),('a2a0a83d-98e4-4988-aa8d-6b7c1a0ac377','ACS Table B21005 - Employment','American Community Survey Table B21005 employment dataset that covers labor force estimates at the 1 year and 5 year timeframe.','public','2026-03-28T21:58:25.229870','2026-03-28T21:58:25.229875','data.iowa.gov','svqueen',NULL,'987b7c6e-6f73-4177-b000-5f0b145ae45d','Iowa metadata','a3e7d3595ba6b2fe2df555f8ee41700e55798c2c610f8ee64436675ee3f99e18','1.1','2026-03-28T21:58:25.229870','2026-03-28T21:58:25.229875','Economic Statistics',NULL,0,'state-of-iowa'),('a2b66a5b-76be-4b99-bff4-a1bcdfc32309','EGIS - Enterprise Gateway Integration Services-Customer Profile Management System Support Service (CPMS-SS)','Customer Profile Management System Support Services (CPMS SS) enables USCIS to maintain a repository of the cards, booklets, and encounter data and to expose this data to subscribing systems. It decreases benefit applicant burden by reducing the need to have their fingerprints taken multiple times and facilitates information sharing with other agencies. CPMS SS improves risk and eligibility decisions by increasing the quantity, quality, and timeliness of information available to adjudicators.','non-public','2026-03-22T11:56:03.209183','2026-03-22T11:56:03.209188','Unspecified','Open Data (MGMT)','024:030','55d50197-d8a2-4804-bbc6-d99b1e4eca20','DHS datajson source','3cf845e9ade631e59a9d975b847be3fd5389e24f5d9cec44284b9462df44aa27','1.1','2026-03-22T11:56:03.209183','2026-03-22T11:56:03.209188',NULL,'024:000',0,'dhs-gov'),('a2bc6d1c-b396-48ac-8ed7-0cb83965a44f','BLM ID Administrative Unit Office Locations','<div style=\'text-align:Left;font-size:12pt\'><div><div><div><p><span>Point features used to show the locations of BLM offices. Each office in this feature class is represented by a point, regardless of whether the office is co-located with others at the same location. One physical location may administer more than one administrative unit, and have multiple offices co-located in that location. Therefore, point features may be coincident. The feature class includes attributes to store feature level metadata information. Several attributes document the origin and characteristics of the points. The Bureau of Land Management uses a multiple tier organization to manage the land. With some exceptions, the land that the BLM manages is served by field offices. Most of these field offices are managed by district offices, which in turn are managed by State Offices.    For more information contact us at blm_id_stateoffice@blm.gov.</span></p></div></div></div></div>','public','2026-03-18T11:11:00.554776','2026-03-18T11:11:00.554783','Bureau of Land Management','Bureau of Land Management, id_so_information','010:04','f3562514-bc2b-4135-ab74-0bd896ef34e5','DOI BLM DCAT-US','1129349a2352598c95cedfab3898fd61ed4551ca152c7cb07538fa0de4658e96','1.1','2026-03-18T11:11:00.554776','2026-03-18T11:11:00.554783','geospatial','010:000',0,'doi-gov'),('a2bf54fc-ac29-4103-b0df-9a6017b0770d','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSIWAC 4 PRL-MTP007 RDR V2.0','This CODMAC level 4 data set contains radiometric calibrated and geometric distortion corrected (resampled) image data in W/m^2/sr/nm, acquired by the OSIRIS Wide Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft during the PRELANDING mission phase, covering the period from 2014-09-02T10:00:00.000 to 2014-09-23T09:59:59.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V2.0 supersedes previous deliveries of the same dataset with the following changes since the last version: Lien corrected dataset after October 2018 PSA/PDS external peer review. Updated documentation and ancillary files, added document on bandpass filter. Updated SCIENCE_USER_GUIDE_V03.PDF to include one section about FAQ and one section about image data quality. Added shutter backtravel and readout issues to image quality map. Updated DATA_QUALITY_ID keyword in image header. Improved handling of images with missing packets.','public','2026-03-13T17:43:44.539694','2026-03-13T17:43:44.539702','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','81cc7ff2-84c9-4652-ad43-b7600d44872c','NASA Data.json','060fd9024099e752357581d18441d830e46f3f090083e7b873a2ae7966023e32','1.1','2026-03-13T17:43:44.539694','2026-03-13T17:43:44.539702','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('a2c1e249-07cd-4654-b26f-7aea28879ab4','MTA Pulse Survey: Beginning 2025','The Pulse Survey dataset provides customer sentiment and satisfaction results across MTA service modes. The dataset is organized as survey output records (not individual-level responses) and includes fields such as month, time period, mode, bus type, question text, category, measure, score grain, score type, score, and sample size.','public','2026-03-14T22:31:13.756294','2026-03-28T22:51:42.825142','data.ny.gov','NY Open Data',NULL,'d8df9d20-3b7a-45b3-b845-121260e0f377','NY State JSON','bf973c574baf693ceda96377612c9e5b6c5a07b05dec549cc77ff05ed028687b','1.1','2026-03-14T22:31:13.756294','2026-03-28T22:51:42.825142','Transportation',NULL,0,'state-of-new-york'),('a2fac14d-8ea2-4a48-86f2-c4984b517fe6','WILLOW RIVER NEAR WABASCA','Timeseries data from \'WILLOW RIVER NEAR WABASCA\' (ca_hydro_07JA003)','public','2026-03-26T19:17:47.158717','2026-03-26T19:17:47.158723',NULL,NULL,NULL,'a60635a5-37f0-42af-a4c4-69968a8b6e9c','ioos',NULL,NULL,'2026-03-26T19:17:47.158717','2026-03-26T19:17:47.158723',NULL,NULL,NULL,'noaa-gov'),('a3108cc7-2c92-4e25-9812-a92f806463d7','FAST Eddy Sys 2  Transect 115, 150kHz kHz VMADCP','Program of vessel mount ADCP measurements comprising a combination of 75kHz and 150kHz ADCP data collected in the vicinity of the Loop Current and drilling blocks between 2009 and 2020.','public','2026-03-26T19:16:20.121871','2026-03-26T19:16:20.121877',NULL,NULL,NULL,'e4dfd75f-5399-4333-8d71-1422c28ea956','ioos',NULL,NULL,'2026-03-26T19:16:20.121871','2026-03-26T19:16:20.121877',NULL,NULL,NULL,'noaa-gov'),('a337b38d-40e7-41a3-8d55-2ce5a8699053','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 PRELANDING 0369 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the PRELANDING phase 2014-01-21 to 2014-11-18. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2014-10-19T04:22:05.000 to 2014-10-19T08:19:24.000.','public','2026-03-13T17:31:22.509834','2026-03-13T17:31:22.509840','Small Bodies','Tess Jaffe','026:00','9022512d-d13f-4a63-931b-416d2e64990d','NASA Data.json','a88ba9ff6933ddf1442e4c907075ec1d0c010b1eba236d39baf61e4a119a62fb','1.1','2026-03-13T17:31:22.509834','2026-03-13T17:31:22.509840','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('a34c071e-21a9-4425-afa6-0c711541445e','NEW HORIZONS  ALICE PLUTO CRUISE  RAW V2.0','This data set contains Raw data taken by the New Horizons  Alice Ultraviolet Imaging Spectrograph  instrument during the  pluto cruise  mission phase. This is VERSION 2.0 of this data set.   ALICE Activities Overview at Annual CheckOuts (ACOs) during the  Pluto Cruise mission phase started with the standard WakeUp  sequence (memory/code checks, aperture door performance test,  pixelhack issue verification, 24 hours of decontamination and  three one hour dark observations) and finished with the standard  Button-Up sequence (code and parameter refresh). Other activities  (with targets as noted) were calibrations for flux (Spica,  rho-Leo, gamma-Grus, HD93521, Sun in Solar OCcultation Channel,  SOCC), flatfield (rho-Leo), airglow scattered light and SOCC  pointing calibrations (Spica, zeta-Pup), SOCC flat (Sun), dark sky  stares, spinning dark observations (in some cases the Sun strobes  through the slit), pointing and short wavelength calibration  (HD93521), InterPlanetary Medium (IPM) histograms and pixellist  observations, dual target tests (HD214680 : 8 Lac, HD214168 : 10  Lac), MEV Solar Wind (HEET) baseine observation, Pluto encounter  rehearsals, and instrument interference tests.   The changes in Version 2.0 were re-running of the ancillary data  in the data product, updated geometry from newer SPICE kernels,  minor editing of the documentation, catalogs, etc., and resolution  of liens from the December, 2014 review, plus those from the May,  2016 review of the Pluto Encounter data sets.   New observations added with this version (V2.0) include IPM  histogram scans in December, 2014, which failed.','public','2026-03-13T18:12:25.945791','2026-03-13T18:12:25.945795','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','70a8d549-d0ee-4aa7-acd4-11633c742ee1','NASA Data.json','9e512cc4daf1c41ae55eac5b987a75e772e1f900065400a90bfbc5650683af2a','1.1','2026-03-13T18:12:25.945791','2026-03-13T18:12:25.945795','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('a386df49-fcd6-4b1e-8b96-0a122c3767d8','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 1 0634 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 1 phase 2014-11-20 to 2015-03-10. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-03-10T13:46:00.000 to 2015-03-10T15:57:40.000.','public','2026-03-13T18:22:08.939873','2026-03-13T18:22:08.939889','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','67a98718-2bfa-496c-a733-45e796545581','NASA Data.json','e0416a2cc9bac8ddf6602ac5e052836f1932dbb48664506f0c7f07fbb7c51085','1.1','2026-03-13T18:22:08.939873','2026-03-13T18:22:08.939889','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('a38cff84-2591-444a-83c2-31ffa76f0d87','Vocal Anuran Monitoring in Southeast Coast Network Parks - Data packages','Data were collected during implementation of the Southeast Coast Network’s Landbird Community Monitoring Protocol.  Automated recording devices (ARDs) captured bird vocalizations at spatially-balanced random sampling locations during the April-May breeding season.  A subset of of recorded audio were reviewed and all discernible bird vocalizations were reviewed and classified to species.  \n\n----Supplemental Information: Avian taxonomy follows 61st supplement (Chesser et al., 2020) to the Check-list of North American Birds, 7th edition (American Ornithological Union [AOU], 1998).  Citations: AOU. 1998. Check-list of North American Birds, 7th ed. American Ornithologists’ Union, Washington, DC, USA.; Byrne, M. W., C. J. Wright, E. Thompson, and C. D. Jones. 2014. Protocol for monitoring landbird communities in Southeast Coast Network Parks. Natural Resource Report NPS/SECN/NRR—2014/853. National Park Service, Fort Collins, Colorado.; Chesser, RT, SW Billerman, KJ Burns, C Cicero, JL Dunn, AW Kratter, IJ Lovette, NA Mason, PC Rasmussen, JV Remsen Jr, DF Stotz, and K Winker.  2020.  Sixty-first Supplement to the American Ornithological Society’s Check-list of North American Birds.  The Auk, Volume 137, Issue 3, 1 July 2020.  https://doi.org/10.1093/auk/ukaa030;','public','2026-03-26T05:33:51.402875','2026-03-26T05:33:51.402880','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','69a57ff5-69a6-484d-85df-9e62148cbc67','DOI NPS DCAT-US','bd2abfef9d780381c22a61cb9f734850e86492ede776453a72a8767165c6eec9','1.1','2026-03-26T05:33:51.402875','2026-03-26T05:33:51.402880','Generic Dataset','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('a3a25b52-130b-4824-8ad6-f96609c7a6aa','Rusting Rivers observations: geographic coordinates and maps','This tabular dataset is a collection of geographic points where rusting is suspected based on the manual interpretation of high-resolution satellite imagery. Point locations have not been validated with ground surveys. \n\nThis collection of points represents three independent interpretations that varied in scope and scale, and thus duplicate point locations exist. Some points are characterized as seeps (point sources where rusting is suspected to originate, often on hillslopes) and starts (the first visible sign of rusting in a headwater stream).  \n\nImagery sources include: IKONOS, SPOT5, GeoEye, WorldView-2, WorldView-3, and ESRI basemap. Imagery acquisition dates are not specified. \n\nObservations are plotted on two maps showing 1) land use designation, and 2) physical geographic boundaries.\n\nFurther information:\nO’Donnell, J.A., Carey, M.P., Koch, J.C. et al. Metal mobilization from thawing permafrost to aquatic ecosystems is driving rusting of Arctic streams. Commun Earth Environ 5, 268 (2024). https://doi.org/10.1038/s43247-024-01446-z\nO\'Donnell, J. A. et al. (2025). NOAA Arctic Report Card 2025 : Rusting Rivers. https://doi.org/10.25923/f3tr-5759\n\nContact: kenneth_hill@nps.gov or jon_odonnell@nps.gov\n \nLast updated March 2026','public','2026-03-29T06:36:56.907342','2026-03-29T06:36:56.907349','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','937bfdf5-14ec-4bb3-b9ec-3a46100d733e','DOI NPS DCAT-US','dfa7af1d84e987c1ffce9ddabbaacce19bf5b6cf9742bcf9f9f430b90c30941e','1.1','2026-03-29T06:36:56.907342','2026-03-29T06:36:56.907349','Tabular Dataset','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('a3a4e946-81e1-42a6-9cd8-fc8360294564','MPF LANDER MARS IMAGER FOR MARS PATHFINDER 2 EDR V1.0','Mars Pathfinder bounced down and rolled to a stop on the surface of Mars on July 4, 1997. It landed in an ancient floodplain in the Ares Vallis region of Chryse Planitia at 19.17 degrees North latitude, and 33.21 degrees West longitude. (See below for details.)','public','2026-03-13T16:47:17.808006','2026-03-13T16:47:17.808013','Imaging','Planetary Data System','026:00','34814fbe-6153-4101-8213-4ab8068bd343','NASA Data.json','481fbb88a5e025c1ff25a3aa5cca84e3b1ea813602eb09f7e3b185546004da6e','1.1','2026-03-13T16:47:17.808006','2026-03-13T16:47:17.808013','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('a3cb7e22-5042-4490-891e-9e7b98ceca35','MARS EXPRESS MARS MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 8 4296 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2021-01-01 to 2022-12-31. It is a Occultation measurement and covers the time 2022-06-17T08:05:41.000 to 2022-06-17T10:37:53.000.','public','2026-03-13T17:11:55.902984','2026-03-13T17:11:55.902990','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','3a0647ab-7a97-4fe3-9f0e-c607c20a5c63','NASA Data.json','8d314833c33d065b84447926205797919ec594e413f8eb252d1164a3c80767c5','1.1','2026-03-13T17:11:55.902984','2026-03-13T17:11:55.902990','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('a3d6c6c1-82ea-4df1-8748-459664ad9766','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RPCLAP 2ESC2 EDITED2 V1.0','This data set contains EDITEDdata from Rosetta RPC-LAP, acquired during the COMET ESCORT 2 missionphase where the primary target was the comet 67P/CHURYUMOV-GERASIMENKO 1(1969 R1). It contains uncalibrated raw data, i.e. the digital output ofthe instrument. This version reorganizes the data into fewer files withlonger time series and sorted by type of measurement. It also supersedesprevious versions that were split into MTPs. The version number startsover from V1.0 due to a change in naming convention.','public','2026-03-13T18:48:25.955623','2026-03-13T18:48:25.955629','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','f412064a-9dde-46e3-ad49-c3d02e75daa9','NASA Data.json','6d48ed3d3d7660cbcaedb97f1532160cc38f4188b048287523423622193ed772','1.1','2026-03-13T18:48:25.955623','2026-03-13T18:48:25.955629','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('a3fb4fc6-a28a-4ab2-98d8-92c3cd60fe2d','MARS EXPRESS MARS MRS 1/2/3                                     EXTENDED MISSION 8 4310 V1.0','This is a Mars Express                                     Radio Science data set, collected                                     during the extended mission phase                                     2023-01-01 to 2023-12-31.                                     It is a Occultation                                     measurement and covers the time                                     2023-07-29T06:42:02.100 to                                     2023-07-29T07:04:10.100.','public','2026-03-13T19:24:14.667817','2026-03-13T19:24:14.667823','geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','b0e44946-79d4-42da-b731-6c86524c04cb','NASA Data.json','1e85e6ea8cdebb68aa24f0878cf70af2b3eca8f11aaaf1903682f2f932905e61','1.1','2026-03-13T19:24:14.667817','2026-03-13T19:24:14.667823','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('a41dc0b5-2267-4353-8fb0-0bc9ec1c2b1e','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSINAC 5 ESC2-MTP017 DDR-GEO V1.0','This CODMAC level 5 data set contains derived data products that include pixel-precise georeferencing information, acquired by the OSIRIS Narrow Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft during the COMET ESCORT 2 mission phase, covering the period from 2015-06-02T23:25:00.000 to 2015-06-30T23:24:59.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V1.0 is the first version of this dataset: Lien corrected dataset after October 2018 PSA/PDS external peer review.','public','2026-03-13T17:06:11.906052','2026-03-13T17:06:11.906057','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','5c882f29-b515-4c2f-99c4-f4948e6600e3','NASA Data.json','0b572278503ec365e0010d577c2b3c3a6c7b7fd2eaad9175215a1cef8924df72','1.1','2026-03-13T17:06:11.906052','2026-03-13T17:06:11.906057','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('a42b6936-9c16-4300-b137-e0341d0d4d33','MARS EXPRESS MARS MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 3 3359 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2010-01-01 to 2012-12-31. It is a Global Gravity measurement and covers the time 2012-08-06T06:42:05.000 to 2012-08-06T09:55:58.500.','public','2026-03-13T19:09:47.594394','2026-03-13T19:09:47.594402','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','d56e6dbc-913a-41d9-81f7-fc83993446a8','NASA Data.json','438e1c2660e97d8c0e8b993d4aba76a2e74e6084acf04941fd571a40fbb7bc2f','1.1','2026-03-13T19:09:47.594394','2026-03-13T19:09:47.594402','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('a45b6917-63b5-4c16-a989-0c81970cbf0d','Flexible Operation of Natural Gas Power Plants in Texas: Startup and Shutdown Durations and Nitrogen Dioxide Emissions','This dataset provides insights into historical flexible operation of natural gas power plants in Texas, with a focus on startup and shutdown events. The dataset includes tables summarizing startup and shutdown durations as well as nitrogen oxide (NOx) emission factors during these events, and compares these emission factors with those observed during all other operating phases (referred to here as “steady-state operation”). The dataset is derived using the U.S. Environmental Protection Agency (EPA)’s Clean Air Markets Program Data (CAMPD). Historical hourly data from 2015–2024, including electricity generation, heat input, and NOx emission factors, are used for natural gas combined cycle units, combustion turbine units, and steam turbine units in Texas.This work was authored by the National Laboratory of the Rockies, operated by the Alliance for Energy Innovation, LLC, for the U.S Department of Energy (DOE) under contract no. DE-AC36-08GO28308. Funding was provided by the U.S. Department of Energy as part of its Grid Modernization Laboratory Consortium, a strategic partnership between DOE and the national laboratories to bring together leading experts, technologies, and resources to collaborate on the goal of modernizing the nation’s grid. The views expressed in the dataset&nbsp;do not necessarily represent the views of the DOE or the U.S. Government.','public','2026-03-27T12:55:13.319564','2026-03-31T14:23:23.198393','National Laboratory of the Rockies','Yun Li','019:20','e9125b77-b323-4f8b-906a-a3a085254f47','OpenEI data.json','4734508dd3dc52219689b90f2da006af4c8af938cca13ac00e75239692aa42fb','1.1','2026-03-27T12:55:13.319564','2026-03-31T14:23:23.198393',NULL,'019:000',0,'doe-gov'),('a472885f-a22a-4f22-97bc-f9d629d98753','ROSETTA-ORBITER ROSETTA EXTENSION 1 OSIWAC 3 RDR MTP025 V1.0','This data set contains images acquired by the OSIRIS Wide Angle Camera during the ROSETTA EXTENSION 1 phase of the Rosetta mission at the comet 67P, covering the period from 2016-01-12T23:25:00.000 to 2016-02-09T23:24:59.000.','public','2026-03-13T18:14:44.981598','2026-03-13T18:14:44.981602','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','bdfca533-4c35-456f-8296-0919f9814ea4','NASA Data.json','06305941cb2833c01155acdafa76ab40a446129da8d4fe05e4919aa63cf7dff2','1.1','2026-03-13T18:14:44.981598','2026-03-13T18:14:44.981602','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('a4789586-1437-475d-8c6e-5d0bade75f0f','NIMS EXPERIMENT DATA RECORDS: GASPRA/IDA ENCOUNTERS','NIMS Experiment Data Record (EDR) files contain raw data from the Galileo Orbiter Near-Infrared Mapping Spectrometer (CARLSONETAL1992). This raw data requires considerable processing before it is readily amenable to science analysis. The EDRs comprise the base dataset from which spectral image cubes will be created by continually evolving software using successively more accurate calibration and geometry data.','public','2026-03-13T17:05:50.172955','2026-03-13T17:05:50.172960','Imaging','Planetary Data System','026:00','e689bea3-2796-49f4-86dd-ec2a59ddb4b9','NASA Data.json','74fcd34ac89f9c1d95bb79967feb9e94df50b4869698ae342cafacef522823df','1.1','2026-03-13T17:05:50.172955','2026-03-13T17:05:50.172960','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('a47eeab2-e8ad-40a6-ab81-acba3d65d463','Laborshed - Benefits','Laborshed dataset that contains information about the current and desired benefits of those within a given laborshed, broken out by various demographic groups.','public','2026-03-28T22:00:25.137631','2026-03-28T22:00:25.137636','data.iowa.gov','svqueen',NULL,'0c22db93-40c4-41c5-8ec2-86e2ed64e14c','Iowa metadata','93ce513fe500cbb04435ef9d8428a9a259d28c020e54f686a596470b8cfd5401','1.1','2026-03-28T22:00:25.137631','2026-03-28T22:00:25.137636','Economic Statistics',NULL,0,'state-of-iowa'),('a48fb084-5394-4050-b077-fff942226a02','SMALL PLANETARY SATELLITE COLORS V1.0','This data set is intended to include published colors of small planetary satellites published up through December 2003. Small planetary satellites are defined as all those except the Moon, the Galilean satellites, Titan, and Triton.','public','2026-03-13T18:41:42.716647','2026-03-13T18:41:42.716652','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','6082c8ed-a794-4cae-b1e3-28c367b2b214','NASA Data.json','eded9a9be0a3fc0eb135d4f13a229592c8809e42e7f03cb3e6a572b9ac9923fa','1.1','2026-03-13T18:41:42.716647','2026-03-13T18:41:42.716652','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('a49358aa-2e8d-4284-8c6d-4e3c1dba6a28','Historic Zoning Map from 1936','This historic 1936 zoning map was digitized and georeferenced to Washington, D.C. It is from the Washingtoniana Map Collection at the District of Columbia Public Library’s DIG DC site. The 1936 map depicts the 1920 regulations amended to 1936 and was published for the DC Zoning Commission by Rufus Lusk. This map breaks the residential zone into six different categories regulating the type of housing allowed in an area. This map also includes regulations on residential lot occupancy. It is used in the Office of Zoning\'s Historic Web Viewer . More information this map and other content found on the DC Public Library DIG DC website .','public','2026-04-01T08:49:40.884757','2026-04-01T08:49:40.884764','D.C. Office of the Chief Technology Officer','DCGISopendata',NULL,'1f849ab9-eb66-488c-9324-21be5874a4b2','DC data','c753f3dc67bc942c4096b3eccba0cd913af7302b065c8cf23d5e3cd9f6dc66ab','1.1','2026-04-01T08:49:40.884757','2026-04-01T08:49:40.884764','geospatial',NULL,0,'district-of-columbia'),('a4acfac4-a070-4816-b1a0-a7308626569a','MARS EXPRESS MARS MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 8 4177 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2021-01-01 to 2022-12-31. It is a Occultation measurement and covers the time 2021-01-09T10:08:33.100 to 2021-01-09T10:30:41.750.','public','2026-03-13T16:54:44.438317','2026-03-13T16:54:44.438322','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','02910064-541a-4582-8494-559eb053a402','NASA Data.json','d155c653d309be9ab772ac0a3e81a1c1d91b73e1046540079e671a942c7962db','1.1','2026-03-13T16:54:44.438317','2026-03-13T16:54:44.438322','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('a4b375d8-ed4b-4dd9-9bc3-d6522d94d627','MER 2 MARS NAVCAM 3 RADIOMETRIC RDR SCI V1.0','This data set contains radiometrically calibrated MER-2 Navcam data. The calibration has removed bias, dark current, and flatfield effects from the raw Navcam data, resulting in estimated radiance-on-sensor data in units of W/m^2/nm/sr. No geometric or camera-model calibrations or transformations have been applied.','public','2026-03-13T19:21:20.724632','2026-03-13T19:21:20.724638','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','251320b8-edad-47c5-8daa-2175aedebab1','NASA Data.json','d05c34219fcd7a2ea4314b9dadea22257c515775637560259bb6426de3ee96ff','1.1','2026-03-13T19:21:20.724632','2026-03-13T19:21:20.724638','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('a4d413aa-3e82-479a-b5e4-35271d3dd122','2026 Open Data Annual Report -- References','Look Forward page provided the future plans for Maryland\'s Open Data program.','public','2026-03-15T02:19:50.273914','2026-03-15T02:19:50.273920','opendata.maryland.gov','Helen Bai',NULL,'6d9f4def-2bd1-4331-b09b-4eac5d5d800f','md json','a36876af9e741295ec4f3b4550b45ed9bf39c28dcc4d3d0cfb691745bb6a0117','1.1','2026-03-15T02:19:50.273914','2026-03-15T02:19:50.273920',NULL,NULL,0,'state-of-maryland'),('a4e84672-2d20-4aea-a40d-3157855d61b6','Sand Hill Bluff 1 (SHB001)','Timeseries data from \'Sand Hill Bluff 1 (SHB001)\' (saic_shb001)','public','2026-03-26T19:14:44.393587','2026-03-26T19:14:44.393593',NULL,NULL,NULL,'8cf16a32-c217-4a27-9f12-45944c65fd5e','ioos',NULL,NULL,'2026-03-26T19:14:44.393587','2026-03-26T19:14:44.393593',NULL,NULL,NULL,'noaa-gov'),('a4f5259a-f517-4e51-9682-046f969aaac0','Continuous Fixed Station Water Quality Measurements in Canaveral National Seashore, November 2006 (Certified)','This dataset represents continuous water quality measurements that were taken at a fixed point in Canaveral National Seashore during the month of November, 2006 as a part of the Fixed Station Water Quality Monitoring protocol that was developed by the Southeast Coast I&M Network (SECN). The measurements were taken by a YSI 6600 ESD Multi-Parameter Long Term Water Quality Monitoring Datasonde unit that serves as the standard fixed station water quality monitoring equipment for all similar operations conducted by the SECN. The following parameters were measured at 30 minute intervals during the time period that has been specified: Water Temperature, Specific Conductivity, Salinity, Dissolved Oxygen (DO), DO Concentration, Shallow Depth, pH Level, and Turbidity. Any anomalies noted regarding these parameters have also been noted in separate fields. Please note that these measurements have been certified by network personnel.','public','2026-03-26T05:30:32.657669','2026-03-26T05:30:32.657673','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','301bf89d-ec15-4810-9b9c-8f055edd638b','DOI NPS DCAT-US','f5948f7aa88d373790b0da8ff51d4bb9176a3e49a4d838169c0732fea1077208','1.1','2026-03-26T05:30:32.657669','2026-03-26T05:30:32.657673','Vector Dataset','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('a554ab8d-5d04-47da-86c1-f7f76f2c270d','EGIS - Enterprise Gateway Integration Services-Encryption as a Service (EaaS)','EGIS Encryption (EaaS) is a simple network-based service offering  encryption and decryption on given payloads intended to simplify and standardize the encryption/decryption process for data that must be secured. ','non-public','2026-03-22T11:54:51.712062','2026-03-22T11:54:51.712067','Unspecified','Open Data (MGMT)','024:030','9a81cdee-cc3c-4fb7-b2ad-223792cf1b34','DHS datajson source','8fe13af7f5a16eb2403770084fd3f91be5e0dc625ea914f06ad7950f0c1fd3e0','1.1','2026-03-22T11:54:51.712062','2026-03-22T11:54:51.712067',NULL,'024:000',0,'dhs-gov'),('a5a87752-a329-4e5f-bf40-52e133f7f017','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 1 0478 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 1 phase 2014-11-20 to 2015-03-10. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2014-12-07T00:56:55.000 to 2014-12-07T13:18:09.500.','public','2026-03-13T16:42:57.442467','2026-03-13T16:42:57.442473','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','bc546ce5-bbad-4904-a86a-4fc0b98def94','NASA Data.json','7b34db8bd1346ddfe3564e2639bebfd6955835fe3a9c2aca0ee3dedaf6048bdd','1.1','2026-03-13T16:42:57.442467','2026-03-13T16:42:57.442473','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('a5b042f6-570a-4a21-babf-af228997bbd9','ROSETTA-ORBITER EARTH RPCMAG 4 EAR3 RESAMPLED V9.0','This dataset contains RESAMPLED DATA (CODMAC LEVEL 4) of the THIRD EARTHSWINGBY (EAR3) of the ROSETTA orbiter magnetometer RPCMAG.The closest approach (CA) took place on November 13, 2009 at 07:45.Additionally data from the Payload Checkout PC10 are added.The current version of the dataset is V9.0.The difference to the datasets of earlier versions is mainly a significantlyimproved sensor temperature model, more detailed documentation about magneticdisturbance sources, more data handling information for the user andalso an improved quality flagging system.','public','2026-03-13T19:42:21.240355','2026-03-13T19:42:21.240361','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','6a7ccb77-5e6f-48a1-99a6-8d45866fa7f9','NASA Data.json','91dc4ee146c239aefc34093ffecd1c4139707b53820420fcd548ce00a02cb84d','1.1','2026-03-13T19:42:21.240355','2026-03-13T19:42:21.240361','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('a5f14bf1-cb72-4832-bad7-5452779c61db','Stratigraphic and electron microprobe data for Holocene tephra from Makushin Volcano, Alaska, and for interbedded tephra from other volcanoes located among or near the islands of the eastern Aleutians','Stratigraphic and electron microprobe data for Holocene tephra from Makushin Volcano, Alaska, and for interbedded tephra from other volcanoes located among or near the islands of the eastern Aleutians, Raw Data File 2026-12, summarizes tephrostratigraphy and electron probe microanalytical (EPMA) data from Makushin Volcano and regional tephras in the Unalaska Island area. The data were collected by scientists from the Alaska Volcano Observatory (AVO) and the Cascades Volcano Observatory during fieldwork from 2011 to 2024. Additional EPMA analyses from this time interval are reported in Larsen and others (2020). Makushin Volcano is part of the Makushin Volcanic Field (McConnell and others, 1998) in the north central part of Unalaska Island, Alaska, approximately 1,290 km southwest of Anchorage and 20 km west of the City of Unalaska and the Port of Dutch Harbor. Makushin erupted explosively to produce two large-volume, explosive Holocene deposits with ages of 9,040 (Makushin Valley) and 7,900 (Driftwood) cal. yr B.P. Since then, Makushin Volcano has erupted numerous times, though individual eruptions have been significantly less voluminous than those of the early Holocene events. The most recent eruption in 1995 produced small ash plumes but left no clearly preserved deposits. Eruptions from volcanoes on neighboring islands also deposited significant tephra fall on Unalaska Island. Tephra from the Okmok II caldera-forming eruption about 2050 years ago is 1-2 cm thick and drapes the area near Dutch Harbor and the City of Unalaska. Tephra from two large explosive eruptions of the Akutan volcano also covered the area 1,600 and 8,700 years ago. Tephra from the older Akutan eruption is up to 40 cm thick in the City of Unalaska. An additional, older silicic tephra sample originated from a distant volcano, but its provenance remains undetermined. Data in this report are included in the public Geologic Database of Information on Volcanoes in Alaska (GeoDIVA; Cameron and others, 2022, http://doi.org/10.14509/geodiva). These data and accompanying discussion are released as a DGGS Raw Data File, and all publication components are available from the DGGS website at: http://doi.org/10.14509/32059.','public','2026-03-29T05:07:03.163868','2026-03-29T05:07:03.163873',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2781a8ee-0071-4877-be4c-8cb10ce8d7c5','Alaska Division of Geological and Geophysical Surveys',NULL,NULL,'2026-03-29T05:07:03.163868','2026-03-29T05:07:03.163873',NULL,NULL,NULL,'state-of-alaska'),('a622bb8e-12ba-407f-82ef-f7ca569cc9d3','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 PRELANDING 0218 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the PRELANDING phase 2014-01-21 to 2014-11-18. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2014-08-18T07:16:15.000 to 2014-08-18T13:13:58.000.','public','2026-03-13T17:14:02.384171','2026-03-13T17:14:02.384179','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','c3664bfe-5d21-473b-ad34-1c4b4585959f','NASA Data.json','9b56fe9f2ad961efdce8bea018d926af3b852a7a9aa4a4f421634ca33a6e0779','1.1','2026-03-13T17:14:02.384171','2026-03-13T17:14:02.384179','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('a6457923-c0e4-4ae8-a8c7-53c5484b8b49','ICE PLASMA WAVE ELECTRIC FIELD MEASUREMENT DATA','The Plasma Wave Data were submitted to National Space Science Data Center after the Principal Investigator\'s death (Scarf) by S. Chang of TRW. For the electric field data, the time interval submitted was Sept 9 - 14, 1985 was included. That information, as well as an explanation of the reformatted data is detailed.','public','2026-03-13T18:45:53.872734','2026-03-13T18:45:53.872740','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','6c2b03c1-bb1b-445f-b073-d51217d290e9','NASA Data.json','a0021bb448a2c651f1b276c66b0c62baf48e7bbc482650a36b9edad921324362','1.1','2026-03-13T18:45:53.872734','2026-03-13T18:45:53.872740','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('a649be86-e9f2-441d-a2e4-3f26904210bc','ULY JUP COSPIN HIGH FLUX TELESCOPE HIGH                                        RES. ION FLUX','This data set contains ion flux data                                       recorded by the COSPIN High Flux                                       Telescope (HFT) during the Ulysses                                       Jupiter encounter 1992-Jan-25 to                                       1992-Feb-18','public','2026-03-13T19:48:46.236974','2026-03-13T19:48:46.236980','planetary plasma interactions','Planetary Data System','026:00','f3e30187-0911-45d4-bd41-5f5616417e6b','NASA Data.json','977d9dfc9b82be2f422910e78f6bc579f2b1858a7cf97fdd9ab30c7339038f02','1.1','2026-03-13T19:48:46.236974','2026-03-13T19:48:46.236980','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('a68b97d5-afd9-48fa-8b90-f32ee6b3ad2c','ROSETTA-ORBITER EARTH OSIWAC 4 EAR2 RDR-STRLIGHT V1.0','This CODMAC level 4 data set contains solar stray light corrected, radiometric calibrated and geometric distortion corrected (resampled) image data in W/m^2/sr/nm,  acquired by the OSIRIS Wide Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft  during the EARTH SWING-BY 2 mission phase, covering the period  from 2007-09-13T00:00:00.000 to 2008-01-27T23:59:59.000. The prime target is planet Earth. This version V1.0 is the first version of this dataset.','public','2026-03-13T17:11:50.167585','2026-03-13T17:11:50.167590','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','be27f2ee-3055-4136-b395-1e59cdff0bc8','NASA Data.json','18eec08eb3a6ba9833f683773477a0e9b206c7ece2cda39be3161b609041d150','1.1','2026-03-13T17:11:50.167585','2026-03-13T17:11:50.167590','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('a69901cb-fb44-4bd4-ba83-127b996460cb','Continuous Fixed Station Water Quality Measurements in Canaveral National Seashore, May 2006 (Certified)','This dataset represents continuous water quality measurements that were taken at a fixed point in Canaveral National Seashore during the month of May, 2006 as a part of the Fixed Station Water Quality Monitoring protocol that was developed by the Southeast Coast I&M Network (SECN). The measurements were taken by a YSI 6600 ESD Multi-Parameter Long Term Water Quality Monitoring Datasonde unit that serves as the standard fixed station water quality monitoring equipment for all similar operations conducted by the SECN. The following parameters were measured at 30 minute intervals during the time period that has been specified: Water Temperature, Specific Conductivity, Salinity, Dissolved Oxygen (DO), DO Concentration, Shallow Depth, pH Level, and Turbidity. Any anomalies noted regarding these parameters have also been noted in separate fields. Please note that these measurements have been certified by network personnel.','public','2026-03-26T05:29:29.809066','2026-03-26T05:29:29.809073','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','366416a0-79df-4dd9-8938-7969a57969fe','DOI NPS DCAT-US','04c3d04f767b2f85a80d8522e8af9d5fd6e1b71187709237df9cba3c3bd596ce','1.1','2026-03-26T05:29:29.809066','2026-03-26T05:29:29.809073','Vector Dataset','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('a69d6a43-7f1c-41c8-9207-184721789df0','RegionalCenter CatchmentAreas','<p><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255);color:rgb(76,76,76);font-family:&quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif;font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;display:inline !important;float:none;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">The State of California, Department of Developmental Services oversees and organizes services for individuals with developmental disabilities in California. This is achieved through a network of 21 non-profit, community-based agencies called regional centers. These regional centers are responsible for evaluating individuals, determining their eligibility for services, and providing case management. The Regional Center Catchment Areas were developed to capture the extent of services associated with a regional center. This data, when added to the DDS Regional Center Lookup helps current and future consumers of the DDS Regional Center services in determining which Regional Center to contact according to their location within an associated catchment (service) area. When an address is entered into the Regional Center Lookup application, a zonal search of the catchment area and the address location returns the appropriate Regional Center name and a link with contact information. </span></span><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.dds.ca.gov/rc/lookup-rcs-by-county/\">Regional Center Lookup : CA Department of Developmental Services</a></p>','public','2026-03-23T14:07:31.486785','2026-03-23T14:07:31.486790','California Department of Developmental Services','Department of Developmental Services',NULL,'741812cb-079d-4467-97df-2f67d6879864','State of California','eb877c154d70e9ea7d88103cf8296bf3f7afba0542520d3f404f3a083e7fe19e','1.1','2026-03-23T14:07:31.486785','2026-03-23T14:07:31.486790','Health and Human Services',NULL,0,'ca-gov'),('a6a3c1ea-b01c-44cc-837b-b40c97e205f9','Continuous Fixed Station Water Quality Measurements in Timucuan Ecological and Historic Preserve, June 2008 (Certified)','This dataset represents continuous water quality measurements that were taken at a fixed point in Timucuan Ecological and Historic Preserve during the month of June, 2008 as a part of the Fixed Station Water Quality Monitoring protocol that was developed by the Southeast Coast I&M Network (SECN). The measurements were taken by a YSI 6600 ESD Multi-Parameter Long Term Water Quality Monitoring Datasonde unit that serves as the standard fixed station water quality monitoring equipment for all similar operations conducted by the SECN. The following parameters were measured at 30 minute intervals during the time period that has been specified: Water Temperature, Specific Conductivity, Salinity, Dissolved Oxygen (DO), DO Concentration, Shallow Depth, pH Level, and Turbidity. Any anomalies noted regarding these parameters have also been noted in separate fields. Please note that these measurements have been certified by network personnel.','public','2026-03-26T05:29:45.167148','2026-03-26T05:29:45.167153','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','66349e7b-53fd-4729-b892-7d744748450c','DOI NPS DCAT-US','7611fe1f552f747d18cf286a40817f05edd610742742cb245be1aaafbe15d155','1.1','2026-03-26T05:29:45.167148','2026-03-26T05:29:45.167153','Vector Dataset','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('a6c5cb65-810c-4200-a7da-e6afb71c6ec1','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 PRELANDING 0388 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the PRELANDING phase 2014-01-21 to 2014-11-18. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2014-10-26T14:54:00.000 to 2014-10-26T21:30:32.000.','public','2026-03-13T18:45:37.217321','2026-03-13T18:45:37.217325','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','9b045a34-9e52-4656-adb8-7e52d0c7089a','NASA Data.json','0a092a65dec0d66cdc0862df7294d38145f6e74089f1650dcc3de25d4558dfbf','1.1','2026-03-13T18:45:37.217321','2026-03-13T18:45:37.217325','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('a717794d-e3ec-454d-9337-c3e20f232e68','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 4 1211 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 4 phase 2015-10-22 to 2015-12-31. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-11-25T10:48:15.000 to 2015-11-25T15:06:28.000.','public','2026-03-13T18:32:36.491310','2026-03-13T18:32:36.491316','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','3dc9a85d-17f9-4222-9578-161526c75390','NASA Data.json','73d195f7313f73220a15e179ceebb426c1149c1cdee396d37de64bd6605e0982','1.1','2026-03-13T18:32:36.491310','2026-03-13T18:32:36.491316','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('a726b559-aad2-4312-a6e2-10231df66068','Data from: Laboratory evaluation of two insecticide-incorporated nets for the management of <i>Prostephanus truncatus</i>','<p dir=\"ltr\"><i>Insects</i></p><p dir=\"ltr\">Adult <i>P. truncatus </i>were obtained from insect colonies kept in the Laboratory of Entomology and Agricultural Zoology (LEAZ), at the Department of Agriculture, Crop Production and Rural Environment, University of Thessaly, Greece, on whole maize kernels, at 26°C and 55% relative humidity (RH) and continuous darkness.</p><p dir=\"ltr\"><i>Insecticide-Incorporated Netting</i></p><p dir=\"ltr\">The experiments were carried out in plastic petri dishes 90 mm in diameter (50.4 cm<sup>2 </sup>bottom surface). The inside of each petri dish was covered with two types of LLIN (0.4% deltamethrin, D-Terrence, Vestergaard INC., Lausanne Switzerland; and 0.34% alpha-cypermethrin, Carifend, BASF Ag, Ludwigshafen, Germany) and a polytetraflurorethylene preparation (Fluon, 60 wt% dispersion in water, Sigma-Aldrich Chemie GmbH, Steinheim, Germany) to prevent insects from escaping. An additional series of dishes with physically identical control netting were prepared without an insecticide treatment to serve as the control. Twenty <i>P. truncatus</i> were then exposed on the insecticide-treated netting in petri dishes for 60, 90, 120, 240 min, 1, 3, and 5 days.</p><p dir=\"ltr\"><i>Mortality and Recovery</i></p><p dir=\"ltr\">After exposure, insects were evaluated for mortality and individual <i>P. truncatus</i> that remained alive or knocked down (not dead) were then place into clean Petri dish arenas with a small amount of clean cracked maize kernels and evaluated for delayed mortality after 7 days. Using a stereomicroscope (SMZ-18, Nikon Inc., Tokyo, Japan) under 60× magnification, <i>P. truncatus</i> were classified as alive (moving normally, is able to right itself when flipped over, no twitching), affected (moving sluggishly or erratically, unable to right itself, twitching of antennae or legs may be present), or dead (completely immobile even after prodding) according to prior published definitions. There were three 3 replicates for each time treatment and netting type and 3 subreplicates for a total of 9 replicates for each treatment combination.</p><p dir=\"ltr\"><i>Explanation of files</i></p><p dir=\"ltr\">The file \"Greece Net Data 2023_All\" includes the raw mortality ratings, whereas \"Greece Net Data 2023_Recovery\" includes calculated recovery values by <i>P. truncatus</i>, where recovery was calculated to \"alive\" from the initial reading (0 d) in \"Greece Net Data 2023_All\".</p>','public','2026-03-13T22:47:30.466696','2026-03-13T22:47:30.466703','Agricultural Research Service','Morrison, William R.','005:18','695757f3-3a08-495a-a362-f1685134540b','USDA JSON','bbc9b98d81a2de52fd054049a3ff0d01d973644feaba7693d842f283c84ef229','1.1','2026-03-13T22:47:30.466696','2026-03-13T22:47:30.466703',NULL,'005:040',0,'usda-gov'),('a74c2bec-1e46-479d-aae3-d81b313bb38f','DC COVID 19 Outbreaks','<div style=\"text-align:Left;\"><div><div><p>Retired on March 2, 2022. Data and metadata are provided as-is archive.</p><p><span>The data describes COVID-19 outbreaks that occur at various setting types. Data are presented by setting type (school building, university, office building, etc.) by week.</span></p></div></div></div>','public','2026-04-01T08:42:08.967039','2026-04-01T08:42:08.967043','Office of the Chief Technology Officer','DCGISopendata',NULL,'f4058bf3-789c-4ac6-86c9-ea5ccaaba164','DC data','fea1018a2f6eaf7507802f118651e90699c4af5b8b54e29b10a3cc468b0ee363','1.1','2026-04-01T08:42:08.967039','2026-04-01T08:42:08.967043','geospatial',NULL,0,'district-of-columbia'),('a79aaa69-9207-4ef9-9b39-e3ec99aa72e6','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P VIRTIS 2 EXTENSION 3 MTP033 V2.0','This release contains the digital numbers (DN) contained in the telemetry (TM) packages of the VIRTIS instrument on board of the spacecraft Rosetta. This volume contains data at the vicinity of comet 67P, from the EXTENSION 3 MTP033 phase, which occurred from 2016-08-10 to 2016-09-02. This version of the dataset (2.0) is produced by a fixed EGSE software. The old version of the software produced incomplete products, reduced by one line','public','2026-03-13T17:15:40.857818','2026-03-13T17:15:40.857823','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','370b451c-65ff-45ea-89c8-cc19e2374d3b','NASA Data.json','138cb762ae67fc77875344a01a8c0a087922aca866a09d217e67424cf98ef49e','1.1','2026-03-13T17:15:40.857818','2026-03-13T17:15:40.857823','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('a7e131c6-e866-47da-aff6-d247e2c93b1d','Employment Benefit Analysis: How Premiums are Paid','The Employment Benefit Analysis was published in 2023. The data reported was collected through an employer survey in the State of Iowa.\n\nThis dataset shows how employers reported that the premiums of the health insurance offered to employees is covered. The information is provided by type of coverage (either single or family). The ways premiums are covered include: 100% employee paid, 100% employer paid, or shared by the employer and employee. The data can be viewed by area (statewide, county, or LWDA), by industry of the employer, and by employer size.','public','2026-03-28T21:59:39.211979','2026-03-28T21:59:39.211986','data.iowa.gov','Katie Green',NULL,'56350493-bfc8-46e6-b9b8-b1eae38fbed8','Iowa metadata','d247b507a18b1ea45d3a07ca4179d212fe01f6186ecc72b2cd989930d4936298','1.1','2026-03-28T21:59:39.211979','2026-03-28T21:59:39.211986','Workforce',NULL,0,'state-of-iowa'),('a7f28acd-969b-477f-b377-7c6fd206c1f5','CASSINI RSS RAW DATA SET - SCC10 V1.0','The Cassini Radio Science Solar Corona Characterization Experiment (SCC10) Raw Data Archive is a time-ordered collection of radio science raw data acquired from October 5 to November 14, 2012, during the Cassini Extended Mission.','public','2026-03-13T18:01:42.883601','2026-03-13T18:01:42.883607','Planetary Atmospheres','Planetary Data System','026:00','dc16d3b0-92b0-4078-b8a9-73bc16acae55','NASA Data.json','1f889cebc1fa8bbb15195c1e59a4a431884dc1bd6a7da3935a52e2ecfccbad61','1.1','2026-03-13T18:01:42.883601','2026-03-13T18:01:42.883607','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('a80171da-e4d2-4b52-bac3-f224a785e000','MARINER 10 MERC PLS DDR ELECTRON MOMENTS V1.0','Mariner 10 Plasma Experiment (PLS) derived ELECTRON MOMENTS data at    Mercury.','public','2026-03-13T18:28:07.916898','2026-03-13T18:28:07.916904','planetary plasma interactions','Planetary Data System','026:00','8765e714-ca5f-4f8a-b870-c9f03c5783d1','NASA Data.json','fa0b840d85020e7be973406ddfaafa4847c36e9a1311981c43835c845621a3a1','1.1','2026-03-13T18:28:07.916898','2026-03-13T18:28:07.916904','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('a885d611-f00b-4564-8b59-703b088d907a','NEW HORIZONS PEPSSI KEM1 CALIBRATED V6.0','This data set contains Calibrated data taken by the New Horizons Pluto Energetic Particle Spectrometer Science Investigation instrument during the KEM1 ENCOUNTER mission phase. This is VERSION 6.0 of this data set. This version includes data acquired by the spacecraft between 08/14/2018 and 04/10/2022. It only includes data downlinked before 05/01/2022. Future datasets may include more data acquired by the spacecraft after 08/13/2018 but downlinked after 04/30/2022. This dataset contains PEPSSI Plasma Rolls, approach and departure observations of Arrokoth, and post-Arrokoth data. In all FITS data files in this dataset, non-finite (NaN and Inf) values have been replaced with INVALID_CONSTANT values.','public','2026-03-13T18:26:46.632508','2026-03-13T18:26:46.632514','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','38f510ab-e08d-4ac8-9c32-560bbea5eb7e','NASA Data.json','75c31ee4fc5c371379561134dc00b9499c6f2d8487045db6320da0dbf5cd90ab','1.1','2026-03-13T18:26:46.632508','2026-03-13T18:26:46.632514','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('a8c501fc-158e-4868-925d-06aa097aeb22','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSINAC 4 EXT3-MTP035 RDR-INFLDSTR V1.0','This CODMAC level 4 data set contains solar stray-light corrected, in-field stray-light corrected,  radiometric calibrated and geometric distortion corrected  (resampled) image data in W/m^2/sr/nm,  acquired by the OSIRIS Narrow Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft  during the ROSETTA EXTENSION 3 mission phase, covering the period  from 2016-09-26T06:40:00.000 to 2016-10-01T00:00:00.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V1.0 is the first version of this dataset: Lien corrected dataset after September 2019 PSA/PDS external peer review.','public','2026-03-13T19:26:33.866521','2026-03-13T19:26:33.866527','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','9e530bc8-eb2d-4046-92c5-ea1d80530c90','NASA Data.json','cc95212ab3c4e77dfa7e62409bf87be166a65b68bbd2f1be3543b5491c9b05c7','1.1','2026-03-13T19:26:33.866521','2026-03-13T19:26:33.866527','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('a8f2fede-1a57-41e4-92e0-9f2b16ba1f16','CalHeatScore Live Data for API Use','<p style=\'background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255); border:0px solid currentcolor; box-sizing:border-box; color:rgb(74, 74, 74); font-family:&quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px; font-style:normal; font-variant-caps:normal; font-variant-ligatures:normal; font-weight:400; letter-spacing:normal; margin:0px 0px 1.5rem; text-align:start; text-decoration-color:initial; text-decoration-style:initial; text-indent:0px; text-transform:none; word-spacing:0px;\'><span style=\'font-family:Arial; font-size:14px;\'>CalHeatScore is a heat-health ranking system that translates 7-day weather forecasts into easy-to-understand heat scores ranging from 0-4 to indicate increasing levels of health risks due to extreme heat at the zip code level. This layer contains the 7-day forecast of heat scores, updated daily at 5 and 8am Pacific Time. Click on this link to go directly to the </span><a style=\'background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255); border:0px solid currentcolor; box-sizing:border-box; color:rgb(0, 97, 155); font-family:&quot;Noto Serif&quot;, serif; font-size:16.8px; font-style:normal; font-variant-caps:normal; font-variant-ligatures:normal; font-weight:400; letter-spacing:normal; line-height:1.5; text-align:start; text-decoration:none; text-indent:0px; text-transform:none; word-spacing:0px;\' target=\'_blank\' href=\'https://experience.arcgis.com/experience/7fe16481f14646b4a167861962ab57a7/page/Homepage/\' rel=\'nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer\'><span style=\'font-family:Arial; font-size:14px;\'><span style=\'border:0px solid currentcolor; box-sizing:border-box; line-height:1.5;\'>CalHeatScore mapping tool</span></span></a><span style=\'background-color:rgb(255,255,255); color:rgb(59,59,59); font-family:Arial; font-size:14px;\'><span style=\'border:0px solid currentcolor; box-sizing:border-box; font-style:normal; font-variant-caps:normal; font-variant-ligatures:normal; font-weight:400; letter-spacing:normal; line-height:1.5; text-align:start; text-decoration-color:initial; text-decoration-style:initial; text-indent:0px; text-transform:none; word-spacing:0px;\'>.&nbsp;</span></span></p><p style=\'background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255); border:0px solid currentcolor; box-sizing:border-box; color:rgb(74, 74, 74); font-family:&quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px; font-style:normal; font-variant-caps:normal; font-variant-ligatures:normal; font-weight:400; letter-spacing:normal; margin:0px 0px 1.5rem; text-align:start; text-decoration-color:initial; text-decoration-style:initial; text-indent:0px; text-transform:none; word-spacing:0px;\'><span style=\'font-family:Arial; font-size:14px;\'>Data Definitions for the layer:</span></p><p style=\'background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255); border:0px solid currentcolor; box-sizing:border-box; color:rgb(74, 74, 74); font-family:&quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px; font-style:normal; font-variant-caps:normal; font-variant-ligatures:normal; font-weight:400; letter-spacing:normal; margin:0px 0px 1.5rem; text-align:start; text-decoration-color:initial; text-decoration-style:initial; text-indent:0px; text-transform:none; word-spacing:0px;\'><span style=\'font-family:Arial; font-size:14px;\'><span style=\'border:0px solid currentcolor; box-sizing:border-box; line-height:1.5;\'>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; ZIP_CODE = Zip code identifier</span></span></p><p style=\'background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255); border:0px solid currentcolor; box-sizing:border-box; color:rgb(74, 74, 74); font-family:&quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px; font-style:normal; font-variant-caps:normal; font-variant-ligatures:normal; font-weight:400; letter-spacing:normal; margin:0px 0px 1.5rem; text-align:start; text-decoration-color:initial; text-decoration-style:initial; text-indent:0px; text-transform:none; word-spacing:0px;\'><span style=\'font-family:Arial; font-size:14px;\'><span style=\'border:0px solid currentcolor; box-sizing:border-box; line-height:1.5;\'>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Date = Date associated with CHS Day 0</span></span></p><p style=\'background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255); border:0px solid currentcolor; box-sizing:border-box; color:rgb(74, 74, 74); font-family:&quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px; font-style:normal; font-variant-caps:normal; font-variant-ligatures:normal; font-weight:400; letter-spacing:normal; margin:0px 0px 1.5rem; text-align:start; text-decoration-color:initial; text-decoration-style:initial; text-indent:0px; text-transform:none; word-spacing:0px;\'><span style=\'font-family:Arial; font-size:14px;\'><span style=\'border:0px solid currentcolor; box-sizing:border-box; line-height:1.5;\'>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; CHS Day 0 = &nbsp;The CalHeatScore on the day associated with the Date field</span></span></p><p style=\'background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255); border:0px sol','public','2026-03-23T13:50:33.219575','2026-03-23T13:50:33.219579','California Office of Environmental Health Hazard Assessment','felicia.chiang_oehha',NULL,'7028cf77-78c1-4622-9832-28542ca57c50','State of California','e15913c9012b2098f7eff85e29ac439a9ccc461ce6c59a7b5b12771248f2dc13','1.1','2026-03-23T13:50:33.219575','2026-03-23T13:50:33.219579',NULL,NULL,0,'ca-gov'),('a8fbaa9e-649b-4740-9360-d0d67b9783af','GALILEO NIMS SPECTRAL IMAGE CUBES: JUPITER OPERATIONS','The natural form of imaging spectrometer data is the spectral image cube. It is normally in band sequential format, but has a dual nature. It is a series of \'images\' of the target, each in a different wavelength, in ascending order. It is also a set of spectra, each at a particular line and sample, over the target area. Each spectrum describes a small portion of the area. When transformed into cubes, the data may be analyzed spatially, an image at a time, or spectrally, a spectrum at a time, or in more complex spatial-spectral fashion.','public','2026-03-13T19:32:55.810390','2026-03-13T19:32:55.810394','Imaging','Planetary Data System','026:00','f996835f-7176-4e91-9675-94b92478f639','NASA Data.json','ad340418278e099fab3923355854bda9d227999f82f029903b5199f56814c173','1.1','2026-03-13T19:32:55.810390','2026-03-13T19:32:55.810394','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('a93acb8f-0141-4cd3-8107-0d974e586362','Continuous Fixed Station Water Quality Measurements in Cape Lookout National Seashore, May 2008 (Certified)','This dataset represents continuous water quality measurements that were taken at a fixed point in Cape Lookout National Seashore during the month of May, 2008 as a part of the Fixed Station Water Quality Monitoring protocol that was developed by the Southeast Coast I&M Network (SECN). The measurements were taken by a YSI 6600 ESD Multi-Parameter Long Term Water Quality Monitoring Datasonde unit that serves as the standard fixed station water quality monitoring equipment for all similar operations conducted by the SECN. The following parameters were measured at 15 minute intervals during the time period that has been specified: Water Temperature, Specific Conductivity, Salinity, Dissolved Oxygen (DO), DO Concentration, Shallow Depth, pH Level, and Turbidity. Any anomalies noted regarding these parameters have also been noted in separate fields.  Please note that these measurements have been certified by network personnel.','public','2026-03-26T05:34:50.404458','2026-03-26T05:34:50.404463','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','ec32e383-53d6-4e26-97e3-b725c0d1424f','DOI NPS DCAT-US','62f167adf4c13b0a5ae9094ecdb24f1e17a084d5e5bb07d03c4208fc9a0ac071','1.1','2026-03-26T05:34:50.404458','2026-03-26T05:34:50.404463','Vector Dataset','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('a9623a9f-6d5b-42e2-8dd8-782ecef16280','CASSINI RSS RAW DATA SET - SAGR10 V1.0','The Cassini Radio Science Saturn Gravity Science Experiment (SAGR10) Raw Data Archive is a time-ordered collection of radio science raw data acquired on January 10, 11 and 12, 2010, during the Cassini Extended Mission.','public','2026-03-13T19:06:01.356015','2026-03-13T19:06:01.356021','Planetary Atmospheres','Planetary Data System','026:00','3a665dfa-3fb5-4bf5-bb7c-f6310fb7f396','NASA Data.json','afef0a9b1ae3a36bee70b711bb5c8cc21c097aa9f782ee71cdbd2c5603ed9bae','1.1','2026-03-13T19:06:01.356015','2026-03-13T19:06:01.356021','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('a9624740-21cc-467f-a538-a964ce7270a2','2025 Estuarine Nutrient Enrichment Water Quality Monitoring Data Package','Residential, agricultural, and urban expansion in the Northeast has resulted in an increase in anthropogenic nutrient loading to the region’s coastal zone. Estuaries can generally assimilate some degree of enrichment without major ecological ramifications, but excessive nutrient inputs typically lead to dense blooms of phytoplankton and fast-growing macroalgae and loss of seagrasses. Protecting the ecological integrity of park estuaries depends on implementing a scientifically-based monitoring program that is capable of diagnosing local causes of nutrient enrichment, detecting changes in nutrient loads, and determining if nutrient inputs are near to exceeding thresholds that would result in shifts in ecosystem structure and function. The current database includes data from NCBN\'s Estuarine Nutrient Enrichment Water Quality sampling protocol for 2006 to 2025 at Assateague Island National Seashore, Cape Cod National Seashore, Colonial National Historical Park, Fire Island National Seashore, Gateway National Recreation Area, and George Washington National Monument.','public','2026-03-15T01:45:30.246011','2026-03-15T01:45:30.246021','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','7fa6aa55-71b6-4ddf-9d50-a4ae454d2930','DOI NPS DCAT-US','9dc6062c864cef3518806cb5d9f4c04940783ee36b1b056f77432987d37a77de','1.1','2026-03-15T01:45:30.246011','2026-03-15T01:45:30.246021','Data Package','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('a9887373-dada-42b7-969f-c2516e64908e','Exposure Activities Event Setting','<div style=\"text-align:Left;\"><div><div><p style=\"margin:0 0 11;\">Retired on March 2, 2022. Data and metadata are provided as-is archive.</p><p style=\"margin:0 0 11;\"><span>The “event setting” demonstrates cumulative data since July 31, 2020 of positive cases interviewed who reported attending an event with five or more attendees and identified its setting type (i.e. fully outdoors, fully indoors, or both indoors and outdoors) during their exposure period.</span></p><p><span>Note: Data subject to change on a daily basis. Data are restricted to positive cases with a completed contact tracing interview. Possible exposure data are collected during the contact tracing interview as self-reported activities occurring within the 2-week period before the date of symptom onset for symptomatic individuals or the date of test sample collection for asymptomatic individuals. Data collection methods were altered starting the week of Dec 11 for gym/fitness and sports, so should not be compared to previous values.</span></p><p><span>* High to Moderate Exposure Activity Types are not exhaustive and include travel, personal care, faith events, work, dining out, social events, gym/fitness, and sports.</span></p><p><span>Data is updated on a weekly basis.</span></p></div></div></div>','public','2026-04-01T08:42:09.003405','2026-04-01T08:42:09.003409','Office of the Chief Technology Officer','DCGISopendata',NULL,'d9808251-2a1a-4a9c-a512-1e6a89d94d73','DC data','a52074d23247ecb679d4bbd0931465a71596182dbd257081d00db638071e6744','1.1','2026-04-01T08:42:09.003405','2026-04-01T08:42:09.003409','geospatial',NULL,0,'district-of-columbia'),('a98de8a4-c95d-499e-8711-e85e88947ac1','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 PRELANDING 0294 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the PRELANDING phase 2014-01-21 to 2014-11-18. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2014-09-14T17:13:03.000 to 2014-09-14T23:35:10.000.','public','2026-03-13T22:35:06.398748','2026-03-13T22:35:06.398755','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','1764a01f-7414-4865-8199-e57985fa5b4d','NASA Data.json','c219d80dec8296d6d7b88c3d9f738bb3a1038f0722aa66483f7aa19d990d057d','1.1','2026-03-13T22:35:06.398748','2026-03-13T22:35:06.398755','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('a9c1e9e0-d800-4d46-a887-77fbb9ac70c3','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 PRELANDING 0368 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the PRELANDING phase 2014-01-21 to 2014-11-18. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2014-10-18T15:17:40.000 to 2014-10-18T21:30:09.500.','public','2026-03-13T17:35:21.919461','2026-03-13T17:35:21.919467','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','dd55bfa7-8630-4839-bab3-416484128d0c','NASA Data.json','01bf7626e8089d31d963df89b2db6a0b08c04d6dbf3dfac3b14565514d