53b82-584a-44df-973a-8fda38327d5d','NASA Data.json','751c12a4de23b965521552374dd2ea6bf02724ed4c8f33501e4b060b23de5438','1.1','2026-03-13T18:04:23.671852','2026-03-13T18:04:23.671858','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('ca4938bc-5dab-43ba-bca7-aadaa47947ff','ROSETTA-ORBITER PRELANDING OSIWAC 3 RDR MTP009 V2.0','This data set contains images acquired by the OSIRIS Wide Angle Camera during the PRELANDING phase of the Rosetta mission at the comet 67P, covering the period from 2014-10-24T10:00:00.000 to 2014-11-21T23:24:59.000. This version V2.0 supersedes previous deliveries of the same dataset.','public','2026-03-13T18:45:09.500624','2026-03-13T18:45:09.500630','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','a4cabb8c-75b3-46ca-85ea-c8f00efc6acf','NASA Data.json','95bcd48eba1ffc9b24a005c208d3abe20d02c6d32e72dadb50809b182d9e10d5','1.1','2026-03-13T18:45:09.500624','2026-03-13T18:45:09.500630','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('ca5207dd-8758-4340-b24c-a6b5faf238b7','Continuous Fixed Station Water Quality Measurements in Canaveral National Seashore, July 2007 (Certified)','This dataset represents continuous water quality measurements that were taken at a fixed point in Canaveral National Seashore during the month of July, 2007 as a part of the Fixed Station Water Quality Monitoring protocol that was developed by the Southeast Coast I&M Network (SECN). The measurements were taken by a YSI 6600 ESD Multi-Parameter Long Term Water Quality Monitoring Datasonde unit that serves as the standard fixed station water quality monitoring equipment for all similar operations conducted by the SECN. The following parameters were measured at 30 minute intervals during the time period that has been specified: Water Temperature, Specific Conductivity, Salinity, Dissolved Oxygen (DO), DO Concentration, Shallow Depth, pH Level, and Turbidity. Any anomalies noted regarding these parameters have also been noted in separate fields. Please note that these measurements have been certified by network personnel.','public','2026-03-26T05:31:24.899090','2026-03-26T05:31:24.899095','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','bd3f0f0e-da89-4f08-a79d-3f8ce6321361','DOI NPS DCAT-US','49366b1c066c63af9bc1fd407ea17e8ef335667016d0f8e9b62e6b761a0c88f8','1.1','2026-03-26T05:31:24.899090','2026-03-26T05:31:24.899095','Vector Dataset','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('ca60bbbd-5718-48ef-a847-6dee178a0bac','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSINAC 4 EXT3-MTP031 RDR-INFLDSTR V1.0','This CODMAC level 4 data set contains solar stray-light corrected, in-field stray-light corrected,  radiometric calibrated and geometric distortion corrected  (resampled) image data in W/m^2/sr/nm,  acquired by the OSIRIS Narrow Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft  during the ROSETTA EXTENSION 3 mission phase, covering the period  from 2016-06-28T23:25:00.000 to 2016-07-26T23:24:59.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V1.0 is the first version of this dataset: Lien corrected dataset after September 2019 PSA/PDS external peer review.','public','2026-03-13T19:27:06.105904','2026-03-13T19:27:06.105909','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','eced61b6-9302-4020-937e-90805ab75c59','NASA Data.json','3b80d6f90cc62dd2de055b6366c4762cc920e062ce16171373e56d4c5e64a2ea','1.1','2026-03-13T19:27:06.105904','2026-03-13T19:27:06.105909','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('ca692a51-bb05-4fb8-902e-9f367adf1dfe','MARS EXPRESS MARS MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 3 3303 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2010-01-01 to 2012-12-31. It is a Global Gravity measurement and covers the time 2012-07-27T08:58:48.000 to 2012-07-27T12:04:30.500.','public','2026-03-13T18:53:40.277516','2026-03-13T18:53:40.277522','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','4f8d05df-838f-48b8-bd3c-1c9f54f64ead','NASA Data.json','9543c43b7b1d1bb3c554c880fae1beff5ee0955e0e44a29f8561a65594931e33','1.1','2026-03-13T18:53:40.277516','2026-03-13T18:53:40.277522','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('ca6e8fba-f47f-4493-8f38-73e3e73ce0d4','Ecosys EcoMapProvinces 2025','<DIV STYLE=\"text-align:Left;\"><DIV><P><SPAN>The Ecomap 2025 contains a feature class for five different levels of the National Hierarchical Framework of Ecological Units (the Hierarchy. FSM 2060): Ecological Domains, Ecological Divisions, Ecological Provinces, Ecological Sections, and Ecological Subsections. The Ecomap 2025 data set describes the ecological hierarchy within the conterminous United States. Each feature class contains polygons attributed with the code and name of the ecological unit along with the codes and names of broader scale units into which a given ecological unit is nested. It contains regional geographic delineations for analysis of ecological relationships across ecological units. ECOMAP is the term used for a USDA Forest Service initiative to map ecological units and encourage their use in ecosystem-based approaches to forest and range land conservation and management. This is a collaborative effort with many partners. It is coordinated at the national and regional levels by USDA Forest Service staff and implemented in cooperation with State forestry agencies and others. ECOMAP mapping criteria are outlined in the National Hierarchical Framework of Ecological Units (Cleland et al. 1997, FSM 2060). The framework systematically divides the country into progressively smaller areas that have similar geophysical and biological characteristics and ecological processes.</SPAN></P></DIV></DIV>','public','2026-03-13T22:49:20.816151','2026-03-13T22:49:20.816157','U.S. Forest Service','USFSEnterpriseContent','005:96','f4a8ddcb-f05e-4aae-9975-17c5ed335ec8','USDA JSON','bef70db903dad0e9ead898a160f4eb4a8442f0c73c2c83671ee4beac90e73b89','1.1','2026-03-13T22:49:20.816151','2026-03-13T22:49:20.816157','geospatial','005:059',0,'usda-gov'),('caa4a14d-1c20-4fd2-a415-8bcd60b2f120','BLM ID CADNSDI PLSS Township','In the Public Land Survey System a Township refers to a unit of land, that is nominally six miles on a side, usually containing 36 sections. For more information contact us at blm_id_stateoffice@blm.gov.','public','2026-03-19T11:33:06.345671','2026-03-19T11:33:06.345677','Bureau of Land Management','Bureau of Land Management, blm_id_infoaccesscenter','010:04','ffca10d8-b4d4-48da-82bf-b89b520a02ce','DOI BLM DCAT-US','267fa9aafc30f5158e8364729ba215ad6184ded55b5bb274adb84966f7787607','1.1','2026-03-19T11:33:06.345671','2026-03-19T11:33:06.345677','geospatial','010:000',0,'doi-gov'),('cae49eda-fff4-4f14-bd9b-6db35db45f76','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 ROSETTA EXTENSION 1 1413 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the ROSETTA EXTENSION 1 phase 2016-01-01 to 2016-04-05. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2016-02-09T14:38:15.000 to 2016-02-09T22:22:30.500.','public','2026-03-13T17:21:27.177894','2026-03-13T17:21:27.177902','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','0204f685-1719-4e0a-9592-8bd7c5f43d72','NASA Data.json','ef1136ec88c3fe49001995363b92ef6fdb640f4c099f6e675b7f9d3ce2f84484','1.1','2026-03-13T17:21:27.177894','2026-03-13T17:21:27.177902','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('cae7d71a-1a96-434f-8f44-31c1a62c3fc0','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 3 1074 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 3 phase 2015-07-01 to 2015-10-21. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-10-02T21:13:05.000 to 2015-10-03T00:17:27.000.','public','2026-03-13T19:53:26.244466','2026-03-13T19:53:26.244471','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','05927894-76a8-4743-9189-46641b9495f0','NASA Data.json','3c1a1147cd5d1b72220d590317b94a4cc507e0332fc833a27d4b9ff4ff3c7a23','1.1','2026-03-13T19:53:26.244466','2026-03-13T19:53:26.244471','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('cb04fc61-40e0-4acf-b364-c2e7f7e1cc4b','WILMINGTON INT\'L AIRPORT, NC (KILM)','Timeseries data from \'WILMINGTON INT\'L AIRPORT, NC (KILM)\' (gov_noaa_awc_kilm)','public','2026-03-26T19:14:53.053912','2026-03-26T19:14:53.053918',NULL,NULL,NULL,'e6b1da7a-4c5e-4151-8ccf-406609f64803','ioos',NULL,NULL,'2026-03-26T19:14:53.053912','2026-03-26T19:14:53.053918',NULL,NULL,NULL,'noaa-gov'),('cb1eace4-a6fd-4566-b3c9-6e19e2698146','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSIWAC 4 ESC2-MTP017 RDR-REFLECT V1.0','This CODMAC level 4 data set contains radiometric calibrated and geometric distortion corrected (resampled) image data in reflectance units (normalized and thus without unit), acquired by the OSIRIS Wide Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft during the COMET ESCORT 2 mission phase, covering the period from 2015-06-02T23:25:00.000 to 2015-06-30T23:24:59.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V1.0 is the first version of this dataset: Lien corrected dataset after October 2018 PSA/PDS external peer review.','public','2026-03-13T18:57:44.550733','2026-03-13T18:57:44.550740','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','df84829c-9998-4a47-890f-c7ae597d755c','NASA Data.json','f4d3cbc465f25a61d148c9d67d326ca001f50967d0b5892813ba6925642f9a61','1.1','2026-03-13T18:57:44.550733','2026-03-13T18:57:44.550740','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('cb214cf9-e4a1-44d0-b0d7-e354fdc4602d','Ordinance 20070322-004','Ordinance 20070322-004','public','2026-03-25T14:27:02.606086','2026-03-25T14:27:02.606091','data.austintexas.gov','Haileigh.Meyers@austintexas.gov',NULL,'785dc546-e5d2-48f1-b6e0-187e25ffa6f8','City of Austin Data.json','4276b1d531430cdef6e843f4110890d02221c94b7c09686863cf7f93534ee1bc','1.1','2026-03-25T14:27:02.606086','2026-03-25T14:27:02.606091',NULL,NULL,0,'city-of-austin'),('cb22106d-0d9d-45de-8546-14f5c94d66ec','MARS EXPRESS MARS MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 8 4197 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2021-01-01 to 2022-12-31. It is a Occultation measurement and covers the time 2021-03-24T22:28:20.500 to 2021-03-24T22:50:28.549.','public','2026-03-13T19:23:37.859046','2026-03-13T19:23:37.859053','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','e193d0e3-62d3-461e-b7e5-7aae055efd68','NASA Data.json','6afbf128fe2ebcec4d2f1558197a00b7b1bef86334ef244887ac53fedf8ddd23','1.1','2026-03-13T19:23:37.859046','2026-03-13T19:23:37.859053','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('cb268a81-18ea-4e48-98c0-d81d8950dca6','Narcotics Activity Hex Centroids','This dataset represents summarized police activity related to narcotics, including specific actions, values of narcotics seized, cash seized, guns seized, and arrests. Data is aggregated by hex grid and displayed as the centroid point for each grid cell. Source datasets are geocoded differently, so events near the perimeter of grid cells may be counted in the neighboring cell from where it actually occured.','public','2026-03-30T19:40:12.913623','2026-03-30T19:40:12.913630','City of Philadelphia','Philly Stat 360',NULL,'bbbcc1f0-4e7c-49f0-979a-86513f61db5f','Phila data json','db049eb9f033b9575992e9fbc54e4d871ef8fb65d521a90bb3ff8a026c5bbc78','1.1','2026-03-30T19:40:12.913623','2026-03-30T19:40:12.913630',NULL,NULL,0,'city-of-philadelphia'),('cb47cea7-5cb4-4769-be6f-908e7c2b8821','Utah FORGE: Laboratory Data for Emergent Pore Pressure Heterogeneity Controlling Slip Timing and Microseismicity','Included are experimental data recorded from shear experiments that explore the effects of pore pressure heterogeneity on microseismic character and fault slip timing resulting from shear reactivation of laboratory faults. Raw mechanical and acoustic data from 15 experiments are included alongside two MATLAB scripts (uniform and non-uniform pore pressure profiles) that import and plot the data, as well as use it to calculate shear and normal stress.\n\nExperiments are performed on 2.5-3 inch long granitoid cores from the Utah FORGE EGS demonstration site, containing a single inclined fracture with small-scale roughness added to the fracture surface. The raw data included here were recorded from an aluminum triaxial pressure vessel (TEMCO) configured with three independent servo-controlled pumps, with DI water used as the working fluid. The pumps control confining pressure, upstream pore pressure, and axial pressure, with each pump connected to a LabView interface to record applied pressures, cumulative injected water volumes, and pump flow rates. The downstream outlet from the fracture is closed to allow pressurization, which is measured by an external pressure transducer. A linear variable differential transformer (LVDT) attached to the axial piston measures axial displacement, from which we calculate shear displacement along the fracture. Additionally, P-wave transducers are used to record acoustic signatures, where acoustic emission events and maximum amplitudes are compared against seismic moment and shear slip velocity.\n\nFluid injection rates range between 0.05 mL/min, 0.25 mL/min, and 0.75 mL/min for each experiment. Triggered shear displacement is used as a proxy for seismic moment and is indexed against cumulative injection volume and rate. Each experiment is performed under constant shear stress conditions, and the sample is fully saturated with DI water. Axial and confining stresses are applied to 3 MPa through pressure-stepping in 500 kPa increments. The pore pressure is held constant at 200 kPa prior to initiating the experiment, and initial axial displacement is recorded. The axial stress is then increased to initiate shear mobilization during the loading phase (run-in) until a peak steady state is achieved. The initial shear stress is reduced to approximately 60, 80, or 90% of the peak shear strength by decreasing the axial stress, then held constant for the duration of each experiment.','public','2026-03-21T11:56:06.953962','2026-03-21T11:56:06.953966','Pennsylvania State University','Matthew Roseboom','019:20','2ca3f5a5-c967-4fff-9292-28624fc23f38','OpenEI data.json','9c4c3da018761b2cb52694c6e1224e62966c56d2d5952d6bb574a7051d237143','1.1','2026-03-21T11:56:06.953962','2026-03-21T11:56:06.953966',NULL,'019:006',0,'doe-gov'),('cb5b837f-03bb-47d6-8b9b-879223036f46','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 3 0870 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 3 phase 2015-07-01 to 2015-10-21. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-07-01T03:27:20.000 to 2015-07-01T04:55:17.000.','public','2026-03-13T18:12:18.066210','2026-03-13T18:12:18.066216','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','67d8c67b-21c7-4055-9d09-f15c376a1aee','NASA Data.json','d1b73cd1c3827917e0d49be2a4aa7ab57dfe5003be785d96034707bc199c456a','1.1','2026-03-13T18:12:18.066210','2026-03-13T18:12:18.066216','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('cb6665dd-15de-4fd1-bc02-6cf0ce39c77c','Cape Lookout National Seashore (CALO) Park Boundary (Includes Harkers Island/Visitor Center Section)','Brief Description: This dataset represents the Cape Lookout National Seashore (CALO) boundary with the Harkers Island/Visitor Center section intact.\n\nFull Description: This boundary dataset depicts a hybrid version of Cape Lookout National Seashore (CALO). The boundary is the resulting output of merging the most current NPS administrative boundary with a customized version of the Harkers Island/Visitor Center section of the park that is omitted from the current administrative boundary.','public','2026-03-27T05:28:36.406109','2026-03-27T05:28:36.406115','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','213308b4-1d8b-4189-9e42-6ed72d25421b','DOI NPS DCAT-US','8a08e5fdb672f47cde3755e53effa35b9e49f9425328881ad2ed929caf771f37','1.1','2026-03-27T05:28:36.406109','2026-03-27T05:28:36.406115','Vector Dataset','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('cb7c134f-4a0d-4c2f-968e-12d3d4c4ef66','ROSETTA-ORBITER EARTH OSIWAC 4 EAR2 RDR-STR-REFL V1.0','This CODMAC level 4 data set contains solar stray light corrected, radiometric calibrated and geometric distortion corrected (resampled) image data in in reflectance units  (normalized and thus without unit),  acquired by the OSIRIS Wide Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft  during the EARTH SWING-BY 2 mission phase, covering the period  from 2007-09-13T00:00:00.000 to 2008-01-27T23:59:59.000. The prime target is planet Earth. This version V1.0 is the first version of this dataset.','public','2026-03-13T19:58:17.793011','2026-03-13T19:58:17.793018','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','a9ec0bf1-bd5e-43ea-a7c8-78c8002868c4','NASA Data.json','647e20a6336b98b27185c079606cd9a1bf69d42faa927aa16c3d5257edfd93dc','1.1','2026-03-13T19:58:17.793011','2026-03-13T19:58:17.793018','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('cba09988-da07-40db-be3a-ee1c8ddf6bfc','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 4 1270 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 4 phase 2015-10-22 to 2015-12-31. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-12-20T01:36:25.000 to 2015-12-20T06:43:34.000.','public','2026-03-13T17:44:03.826427','2026-03-13T17:44:03.826433','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','ef3d3277-4f13-49ba-b5a6-5a086acd6f2c','NASA Data.json','4e7f936ec65aade89c3157595d211ab7d724976f5e6e9461044cbec2e9462eef','1.1','2026-03-13T17:44:03.826427','2026-03-13T17:44:03.826433','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('cbe3cd49-fa2c-4884-acfa-75bd8c869b29','MARS EXPRESS SUN MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 7 4049 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2019-01-01 to 2020-12-31. It is a Solar Conjunction measurement and covers the time 2019-09-04T01:27:10.000 to 2019-09-04T04:35:53.500.','public','2026-03-13T19:13:01.611030','2026-03-13T19:13:01.611035','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','a5f486ad-ee29-404e-95e4-c22160889286','NASA Data.json','165294164028932087cf294b968ab2cf5103e4cfc03a6c38ca67fe3cc07edb42','1.1','2026-03-13T19:13:01.611030','2026-03-13T19:13:01.611035','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('cbf408c9-59a0-49d1-80ca-1d003d6518d8','MARS EXPRESS MARS MRS 1/2/3                                     EXTENDED MISSION 8 4341 V1.0','This is a Mars Express                                     Radio Science data set, collected                                     during the extended mission phase                                     2023-01-01 to 2023-12-31.                                     It is a Occultation                                     measurement and covers the time                                     2023-09-17T01:21:19.000 to                                     2023-09-17T01:43:27.200.','public','2026-03-13T18:45:24.630359','2026-03-13T18:45:24.630367','geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','f45fe704-785d-4515-864b-e577300b0634','NASA Data.json','f24acc07a39ba554965841bceee792c61375e3167585ce22190e5ceb24e27b97','1.1','2026-03-13T18:45:24.630359','2026-03-13T18:45:24.630367','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('cc05cbd8-144d-4450-8b19-1213ba18d486','EGIS - Enterprise Gateway Integration Services (overall)','Acts as a conduit for the exchange of information between systems within USCIS, the U.S. Department of Homeland Security (DHS), external government agencies, and authorized third parties.','non-public','2026-03-22T11:52:22.901727','2026-03-22T11:52:22.901732','Unspecified','Open Data (MGMT)','024:030','aea12541-9c0b-4a27-b252-2a2ef4030a57','DHS datajson source','2d2efabe00b219525eff508bed0fd94346ed2c705540e17c6de6bc659eccf0dd','1.1','2026-03-22T11:52:22.901727','2026-03-22T11:52:22.901732',NULL,'024:000',0,'dhs-gov'),('cc1e086e-710f-408c-bd6c-e4b2a4169421','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSIWAC 4 ESC3-MTP020 RDR-STR-REFL V1.0','This CODMAC level 4 data set contains solar stray light corrected, radiometric calibrated and geometric distortion corrected (resampled) image data in in reflectance units (normalized and thus without unit), acquired by the OSIRIS Wide Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft during the COMET ESCORT 3 mission phase, covering the period from 2015-08-25T23:25:00.000 to 2015-09-22T23:24:59.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V1.0 is the first version of this dataset: Lien corrected dataset after October 2018 PSA/PDS external peer review.','public','2026-03-13T17:58:13.936947','2026-03-13T17:58:13.936952','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','c3c076c5-fe71-4c04-b492-fe83f0838eb4','NASA Data.json','90ba6eb8062711e57c12ecb30dc0e86efbe739cdd3cd047436f431a06d3eb395','1.1','2026-03-13T17:58:13.936947','2026-03-13T17:58:13.936952','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('cc2c5cf7-40c0-493f-bceb-1fdf0f042ff6','Continuous Fixed Station Water Quality Measurements in Timucuan Ecological and Historic Preserve, March 2008 (Certified)','This dataset represents continuous water quality measurements that were taken at a fixed point just outside of Timucuan Ecological and Historic Preserve during the month of March, 2008 as a part of the Fixed Station Water Quality Monitoring protocol that was developed by the Southeast Coast I&M Network (SECN). The measurements were taken by a YSI 6600 ESD Multi-Parameter Long Term Water Quality Monitoring Datasonde unit that serves as the standard fixed station water quality monitoring equipment for all similar operations conducted by the SECN. The following parameters were measured at 30 minute intervals during the time period that has been specified: Water Temperature, Specific Conductivity, Salinity, Dissolved Oxygen (DO), DO Concentration, Shallow Depth, pH Level, and Turbidity. Any anomalies noted regarding these parameters have also been noted in separate fields. Please note that these measurements have been certified by network personnel.','public','2026-03-26T05:34:16.865209','2026-03-26T05:34:16.865214','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','ec71d277-794f-41ed-bd8c-db3f72445e4a','DOI NPS DCAT-US','54a105c728d2bff8f46fb4958a6247b0247be9866ffd990fb241986b134763b2','1.1','2026-03-26T05:34:16.865209','2026-03-26T05:34:16.865214','Vector Dataset','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('cc31c069-b4a4-4307-9bdc-80cec8951a27','GO JUP HIC DERIVED ENERGETIC ION COMPOSITION V1.0','This data set provides energetic (MeV) ion fluxes for a variety of        different Z values (carbon, oxygen, sulfur) derived from the        Heavy Ion Counter (HIC) instrument on the Galileo spacecraft.        The data set includes all recorded intervals at Jupiter.','public','2026-03-13T20:00:03.244273','2026-03-13T20:00:03.244281','planetary plasma interactions','Planetary Data System','026:00','6b5713be-e9ad-4b82-936a-2925fe0f4500','NASA Data.json','26c27ba4f471d2e66edd3e05dcc033dcc8978b2e42ab9e73d18acf17dc3dcea9','1.1','2026-03-13T20:00:03.244273','2026-03-13T20:00:03.244281','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('cc7974e4-1227-49f3-b12d-8f84160beb90','BLM ID CADNSDI PLSS State Boundary Line','<div style=\'text-align:Left;font-size:12pt\'><div><div><p><span>This dataset portrays the state boundary based on the 2010 Cadastral National Spatial Data Infrastructure (CADNSDI) Geographic Coordinate Data Base (GCDB) distribution. The GCDB was acquired from a Premier Data contract in coordination with the BLM state GCDB Data Stewards to deliver a standardized GCDB product. This product would be capable, where GCDB data exists, to identify the State borders. Where GCDB data does not exist, in cases or rivers, lakes, and unsurveyed terrain, then alternative sources were used to identify the state boundary. Alternative sources include original 24K USGS Maps and US Forest Service Cartographic Feature File (CFF) PLSS data.</span></p></div></div></div>','public','2026-03-18T11:14:26.958928','2026-03-18T11:14:26.958934','Bureau of Land Management','Bureau of Land Management, blm_id_stateoffice','010:04','b91b64af-4f02-4ece-b3a2-5b09aebce27b','DOI BLM DCAT-US','db52b38563531bb9f72b15fc0be557421a7feb12d5d6e7ebaa7e45eb6a7508fc','1.1','2026-03-18T11:14:26.958928','2026-03-18T11:14:26.958934','geospatial','010:000',0,'doi-gov'),('cca8ef69-4a57-4adb-84ca-1d2ec6dd1eec','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 3 1082 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 3 phase 2015-07-01 to 2015-10-21. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-10-06T10:16:30.000 to 2015-10-06T17:30:23.000.','public','2026-03-13T19:46:57.421714','2026-03-13T19:46:57.421721','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','80453cb5-b1d2-4475-9c71-e6b8abd568d0','NASA Data.json','ffa011b36e52e31e9c82b53adaabcadb14fafa1d7b662edef027fcb378929679','1.1','2026-03-13T19:46:57.421714','2026-03-13T19:46:57.421721','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('ccc55233-de69-4e49-968a-c3da7b0f7c67','BLM Natl Recreation Site Points','This feature class represents the point features that show the physical locations of BLM National Recreation Sites. The general types of recreation point features targeted by this feature class include information center sites, water-based sites, overnight sites, day use sites, restrooms, water access, recreational access, parking areas, airplane landing strips, etc.\n\nThis dataset is based on an interim data standard and will be republished in the future.\n\nThis dataset is a subset of the official national dataset, containing features and attributes intended for public release and has been optimized for online map service performance. ','public','2026-03-18T11:10:39.467370','2026-03-18T11:10:39.467375','Bureau of Land Management','Bureau of Land Management, dbyrd','010:04','269d8f64-067f-4628-8d95-cd45c7910af9','DOI BLM DCAT-US','2cb03d30756b7be3ce65316ba21aef488dbb4c6d1d2e2d7f190ea3fa751bb292','1.1','2026-03-18T11:10:39.467370','2026-03-18T11:10:39.467375','geospatial','010:000',0,'doi-gov'),('ccc9fd31-6aa3-42a1-8496-0fffd15a6120','HPMS Roadway Sample 2019','State DOTs provide the Highway Performance Monitoring System (HPMS) with the location limits of highway sections used to represent statewide aggregations based on a statistically valid Sample Panel.','public','2026-03-28T13:34:49.044641','2026-03-28T13:34:49.044649','Federal Highway Administration','Office of Highway Policy Information','021:15','82c00efb-564f-4207-a35d-19bd157d12eb','DOT Socrata Data.json','307e0ba6f719144e468ca2e034ff2f2549a3024adc552ea55b807ddee2571d28','1.1','2026-03-28T13:34:49.044641','2026-03-28T13:34:49.044649','Roadways and Bridges','021:009',0,'dot-gov'),('cd2556ff-2790-4351-aa22-4ff79abee544','Employment Benefit Analysis: Employers Offering Benefits 2023','The Employment Benefit Analysis was published in 2023. The data reported was collected through an employer survey in the State of Iowa.\n\nThis dataset shows the percentage of employers who reported providing benefits to their employees. The data can be viewed by area (statewide, county, or LWDA), by industry of the employer, and by employer size.','public','2026-03-28T21:59:50.745118','2026-03-28T21:59:50.745123','data.iowa.gov','Katie Green',NULL,'e98f442e-11a3-4e8d-8fc0-7e8a960240fa','Iowa metadata','458f94277375936938ca8bd9c977cfedbf7470f98d875693636873094b822e2a','1.1','2026-03-28T21:59:50.745118','2026-03-28T21:59:50.745123','Workforce',NULL,0,'state-of-iowa'),('cd659c6f-6039-45ae-880a-403ac35ad1e3','Employment Benefit Analysis: Benefits Offered to Full-Time or Part-Time Employees 2023','The Employment Benefit Analysis was published in 2023. The data reported was collected through an employer survey in the State of Iowa.\n\nThis dataset shows the percentage of employers who reported they offer benefits to only full-time employees, only part-time employees, or to both full-time and part-time employees. The data can be viewed by area (statewide, county, or LWDA), by industry of the employer, and by employer size.','public','2026-03-28T21:58:46.631333','2026-03-28T21:58:46.631338','data.iowa.gov','Katie Green',NULL,'5a20ba66-a930-4cc1-b34e-0cf70455b406','Iowa metadata','545a56e7eb152944b3afc3cedbe8d5206c8424011352ebb81f0739bd1e6dbb94','1.1','2026-03-28T21:58:46.631333','2026-03-28T21:58:46.631338','Workforce',NULL,0,'state-of-iowa'),('cd7635f0-b337-41e1-be54-d53987473afc','GALILEO ORBITER A MAG RDR IDA HIGH RES V1.0','Galileo Orbiter Magnetometer (MAG) calibrated high-resolution data      from the Ida flyby in spacecraft, EME-50, RTN and Ida Solar      Ecliptic (IaSE) coordinates. These data cover the interval      1993-08-28 15:56 to 1993-08-28 17:50.','public','2026-03-13T19:43:08.333332','2026-03-13T19:43:08.333340','planetary plasma interactions','Planetary Data System','026:00','a5a1a9e7-eaab-45cd-852c-c25bbe6cca11','NASA Data.json','992147cafe3823783a2334964eed9b8f2b9f433c234430057c96ea1637ab25dd','1.1','2026-03-13T19:43:08.333332','2026-03-13T19:43:08.333340','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('cd86f081-1c33-4152-ba4a-1bc6117a5914','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RPCMAG 2 EXT2 RAW V9.0','This dataset contains EDITED RAW DATA (CODMAC LEVEL 2) of theEXTENDED MISSION PHASE 2 (EXT2) from April 6 until June 29, 2016of the ROSETTA orbiter magnetometer RPCMAG. Observations are done inthe vicinity of comet 67P/CHURYUMOV-GERASIMENKO 1 (1969 R1).The current version of the dataset is V9.0.The difference to the datasets of earlier versions is mainly a significantlyimproved sensor temperature model, more detailed documentation about magneticdisturbance sources, more data handling information for the user andalso an improved quality flagging system.This applies mainly to CALIBRATED and RESAMPLED datasets. The RAW dataset,however, has been updated as well in order provide all datasets at thesame stage, although RAW data proper did not change.','public','2026-03-13T18:04:49.102826','2026-03-13T18:04:49.102831','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','46d7026e-392b-40a8-b307-3e330bb8a511','NASA Data.json','2490bc83fb22973da1faf790701aeffce7e3c7a5420c38b96053c806a19ec180','1.1','2026-03-13T18:04:49.102826','2026-03-13T18:04:49.102831','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('cd8a576b-9b60-43e7-82b2-852a6411b2d8','GALILEO ORBITAL OPERATIONS SOLID STATE IMAGING RAW EDR V1.0','This data set has been generated by NASA\'s Galileo Project in order to distribute the images acquired by the Solid State Imaging (SSI) camera to the scientists and later to the Planetary Data System (PDS). This collection resides on volumes GO_0017 thru GO_0022. Included are all images of Jupiter, its satellites, stars and calibrations, acquired during the Jupiter Orbital Operations which comprise the Prime Mission and the Galileo Europa Mission (GEM) phases. These phases extended from June, 1996 thru February, 2000 and included SCLKs from 346405900 thru 527365602.','public','2026-03-13T16:42:01.876071','2026-03-13T16:42:01.876077','Imaging','Planetary Data System','026:00','e0818c4d-fc5c-4dc9-9e2c-29c33a78fec1','NASA Data.json','8d1366adcf42328a06bb2ee96acbe7578d69127c426ad1db598dfd560097a36a','1.1','2026-03-13T16:42:01.876071','2026-03-13T16:42:01.876077','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('cdcb2b40-41be-4dcc-a329-ec03b46acebe','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSIWAC 4 EXT3-MTP034 RDR V2.0','This CODMAC level 4 data set contains radiometric calibrated and geometric distortion corrected (resampled) image data in W/m^2/sr/nm, acquired by the OSIRIS Wide Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft during the ROSETTA EXTENSION 3 mission phase, covering the period from 2016-09-02T06:40:00.000 to 2016-09-26T06:39:59.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V2.0 supersedes previous deliveries of the same dataset with the following changes since the last version: Lien corrected dataset after October 2018 PSA/PDS external peer review. Updated documentation and ancillary files, added document on bandpass filter. Updated SCIENCE_USER_GUIDE_V03.PDF to include one section about FAQ and one section about image data quality. Added shutter backtravel and readout issues to image quality map. Updated DATA_QUALITY_ID keyword in image header. Improved handling of images with missing packets.','public','2026-03-13T16:49:02.833544','2026-03-13T16:49:02.833551','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','01945602-28ea-4306-9f78-e73709e0b075','NASA Data.json','e537f03798241362bfcc4ea148399d5fb492f14762bc51f603f0259791590e61','1.1','2026-03-13T16:49:02.833544','2026-03-13T16:49:02.833551','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('cddd8a05-e88e-42ed-89c1-2778a2e958a1','ROSETTA-ORBITER EARTH OSIWAC 4 EAR1 RDR-STR-REFL V1.0','This CODMAC level 4 data set contains solar stray light corrected, radiometric calibrated and geometric distortion corrected (resampled) image data in in reflectance units  (normalized and thus without unit),  acquired by the OSIRIS Wide Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft  during the EARTH SWING-BY 1 mission phase, covering the period  from 2004-10-17T00:00:00.000 to 2005-04-04T23:59:59.000. The prime target is planet Earth. This version V1.0 is the first version of this dataset.','public','2026-03-13T18:02:38.441573','2026-03-13T18:02:38.441579','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','aa420d90-e452-474c-adcb-5cbd0644ac08','NASA Data.json','9b9d6c8f2b66a0eafc22b770ac5c0db2632425a8e92eb42138322da024a23ac2','1.1','2026-03-13T18:02:38.441573','2026-03-13T18:02:38.441579','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('cdffe0e8-27d6-40d7-b7ea-b933b57e46d6','DID(IT) - Telework Data','ePulse contains USCIS employee\'s telework schedule data.','non-public','2026-03-22T11:53:52.094032','2026-03-22T11:53:52.094039','Unspecified','Open Data (MGMT)','024:030','db20d7f1-05ef-4aa1-8467-437d9326fe28','DHS datajson source','35b03da8e67641a6371ef8c992f415eced75e95b27e91a10215e1cae88d80ff5','1.1','2026-03-22T11:53:52.094032','2026-03-22T11:53:52.094039',NULL,'024:000',0,'dhs-gov'),('ce26fbaf-ab0a-4f20-b70e-34c84b5b9908','Continuous Fixed Station Water Quality Measurements in Timucuan Ecological and Historic Preserve, May 2008 (Certified)','This dataset represents continuous water quality measurements that were taken at a fixed point in Timucuan Ecological and Historic Preserve during the month of May, 2008 as a part of the Fixed Station Water Quality Monitoring protocol that was developed by the Southeast Coast I&M Network (SECN). The measurements were taken by a YSI 6600 ESD Multi-Parameter Long Term Water Quality Monitoring Datasonde unit that serves as the standard fixed station water quality monitoring equipment for all similar operations conducted by the SECN. The following parameters were measured at 30 minute intervals during the time period that has been specified: Water Temperature, Specific Conductivity, Salinity, Dissolved Oxygen (DO), DO Concentration, Shallow Depth, pH Level, and Turbidity. Any anomalies noted regarding these parameters have also been noted in separate fields. Please note that these measurements have been certified by network personnel.','public','2026-03-26T05:29:45.154352','2026-03-26T05:29:45.154357','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','b4becc4d-3e92-479c-9a80-e3595ddd8356','DOI NPS DCAT-US','9ba8f205b52344d3090783e24d0e32dbcc8af5e9847421df22bcb1d471f13765','1.1','2026-03-26T05:29:45.154352','2026-03-26T05:29:45.154357','Vector Dataset','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('ce280522-2732-42b9-847d-b1d7764df52b','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSINAC 4 EXT3-MTP034 RDR-STRLIGHT V1.0','This CODMAC level 4 data set contains solar stray light corrected, radiometric calibrated and geometric distortion corrected (resampled) image data in W/m^2/sr/nm, acquired by the OSIRIS Narrow Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft during the ROSETTA EXTENSION 3 mission phase, covering the period from 2016-09-02T06:40:00.000 to 2016-09-26T06:39:59.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V1.0 is the first version of this dataset: Lien corrected dataset after October 2018 PSA/PDS external peer review.','public','2026-03-13T19:28:01.667518','2026-03-13T19:28:01.667523','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','cc4b36bf-52cf-4b58-8bb1-4d1b567d1798','NASA Data.json','09af7ad0510960f9ed2666c6f57c9bc74c379533b7d5d78aa62706763936d8e8','1.1','2026-03-13T19:28:01.667518','2026-03-13T19:28:01.667523','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('ce2be263-f0b5-4716-a11c-920fef810b2a','ROSETTA-ORBITER COMET ESCORT 3 OSIWAC 3 RDR MTP021 V1.0','This data set contains images acquired by the OSIRIS Wide Angle Camera during the COMET ESCORT 3 phase of the Rosetta mission at the comet 67P, covering the period from 2015-09-22T23:25:00.000 to 2015-10-20T23:24:59.000.','public','2026-03-13T18:49:22.854531','2026-03-13T18:49:22.854536','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','ec0dd9a4-2f09-4a33-be6c-810a646df69f','NASA Data.json','edbe2f52c6de12c4fb14bb2de755acd0bda63bbcc48fbfab17abff6b5dc7fbff','1.1','2026-03-13T18:49:22.854531','2026-03-13T18:49:22.854536','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('ce58efa2-783c-4848-b363-4a80950a7549','MARS EXPRESS MARS MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 3 3319 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2010-01-01 to 2012-12-31. It is a Global Gravity measurement and covers the time 2012-06-20T09:12:03.000 to 2012-06-20T12:39:55.500.','public','2026-03-13T18:58:27.459104','2026-03-13T18:58:27.459112','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','f35e58df-16b6-4035-bd2e-4cc0b8e7f908','NASA Data.json','7e4c8237f85a4f2d3910f3fb62a61ac2b461eff79295b3aaafc799c5ea280c71','1.1','2026-03-13T18:58:27.459104','2026-03-13T18:58:27.459112','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('ce95ce60-c414-4d46-8f23-1d4fae0b38df','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 PRELANDING 0223 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the PRELANDING phase 2014-01-21 to 2014-11-18. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2014-08-19T19:00:25.000 to 2014-08-20T01:37:20.500.','public','2026-03-13T18:54:13.502757','2026-03-13T18:54:13.502761','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','4f45ff3b-fa83-4661-b400-cf41f5e3aa29','NASA Data.json','28ebe1e153b36b1f3a6f201c4e562dd73102463cff30fb69d310b08beb6bcede','1.1','2026-03-13T18:54:13.502757','2026-03-13T18:54:13.502761','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('ce9ee473-bc3b-45f2-bcdb-7af7145d0a53','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 3 0905 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 3 phase 2015-07-01 to 2015-10-21. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-07-18T21:18:10.000 to 2015-07-19T02:54:06.500.','public','2026-03-13T17:39:51.110825','2026-03-13T17:39:51.110832','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','ffb381a5-8c6e-4ac3-841f-530470e1b9d8','NASA Data.json','707ca6808307fbbb4ba01ce185617e4496c3cd762c4fd4a333080f45a778024f','1.1','2026-03-13T17:39:51.110825','2026-03-13T17:39:51.110832','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('cea573de-278e-4f91-a92e-a630446d1d0f','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 3 0944 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 3 phase 2015-07-01 to 2015-10-21. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-08-05T10:09:25.000 to 2015-08-05T17:26:49.500.','public','2026-03-13T17:59:24.128947','2026-03-13T17:59:24.128952','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','15a4d5a5-07ae-463a-a1a3-e79658928606','NASA Data.json','cb61b38f6df9c56a612894580e8b8be3e387a96c29ccd61e0365ce967de98996','1.1','2026-03-13T17:59:24.128947','2026-03-13T17:59:24.128952','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('cf52683c-2b12-4988-95dc-181866121955','BLM ID CADNSDI PLSS Conflicted Areas','The conflicted areas feature class is a depiction of known overlaps or gaps resulting from two or more different surveys of the same area, this may also include an indication of canceled or suspended surveys. For more information contact us at blm_id_stateoffice@blm.gov.','public','2026-03-18T11:13:33.904784','2026-03-18T11:13:33.904789','Bureau of Land Management','Bureau of Land Management, blm_id_infoaccesscenter','010:04','e1bc9fc4-9bde-4daf-aa7a-8b326b62e7a6','DOI BLM DCAT-US','64186e5a577a944ea219cf7b18bceeb1d65c0d4b6ad9a4ceb5512868fe84de86','1.1','2026-03-18T11:13:33.904784','2026-03-18T11:13:33.904789','geospatial','010:000',0,'doi-gov'),('cf662ce6-d207-4057-8d2e-ae2daf11e77e','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 PRELANDING 0252 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the PRELANDING phase 2014-01-21 to 2014-11-18. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2014-08-28T12:44:05.000 to 2014-08-28T18:04:19.000.','public','2026-03-13T17:52:32.639547','2026-03-13T17:52:32.639553','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','ce5aff11-03ae-440d-9036-12519e80e9e4','NASA Data.json','c9ecb7708f54c49bac045afbe49e8fbb3f078a98c0c8cc05f2d16eadce635dd2','1.1','2026-03-13T17:52:32.639547','2026-03-13T17:52:32.639553','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('cfd0084a-0d27-4a86-8eec-43695f5a7e04','ROSETTA-ORBITER CHECK RSI 1/2/3 COMMISSIONING 1 0009 V1.0','This is a Commissioning measurement covering the time 2004-05-06T20:11:29.500 to 2004-05-07T02:16:28.500.','public','2026-03-13T18:12:39.386951','2026-03-13T18:12:39.386958','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','6ca865b8-22e1-4128-923f-b7c7ae0c16ac','NASA Data.json','da7a8aa0a79dded436f521db93c4e8246010aa1a60e7d407a5634cf7ced8179a','1.1','2026-03-13T18:12:39.386951','2026-03-13T18:12:39.386958','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('d00e5e58-84dd-4907-a195-69cee4a6a1c7','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 1 0463 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 1 phase 2014-11-20 to 2015-03-10. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2014-11-28T15:43:10.000 to 2014-11-28T19:54:07.500.','public','2026-03-13T19:34:38.323950','2026-03-13T19:34:38.323957','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','b6e759fd-81a2-4af3-934a-7a04fc19c25c','NASA Data.json','86662b5a7a1a5ee7df3dafa6d87211890e68535ad3fba1a11db8cdc3f7704bb6','1.1','2026-03-13T19:34:38.323950','2026-03-13T19:34:38.323957','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('d04c5e16-e15b-4654-bf35-389c6c099510','MRO CONTEXT CAMERA EXPERIMENT DATA RECORD  LEVEL 0 V1.0','The CTX Experiment Data Record (EDR)Archive, a collection of image data from the Context Camera on theMars Reconnaissance Orbiter spacecraft.','public','2026-03-13T17:44:43.572480','2026-03-13T17:44:43.572485','Imaging','Planetary Data System','026:00','894fae82-0b1a-45f5-8610-adb6e5bf9240','NASA Data.json','32da18b79015a345f8c51fdfb9f0731191092a0fe1c95bd630c8c7660fa294c3','1.1','2026-03-13T17:44:43.572480','2026-03-13T17:44:43.572485','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('d0601a8c-5402-4b67-8d9d-9a3c5c72b59b','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSINAC 4 EXT3-MTP033 RDR-INFLDSTR V1.0','This CODMAC level 4 data set contains solar stray-light corrected, in-field stray-light corrected,  radiometric calibrated and geometric distortion corrected  (resampled) image data in W/m^2/sr/nm,  acquired by the OSIRIS Narrow Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft  during the ROSETTA EXTENSION 3 mission phase, covering the period  from 2016-08-09T23:25:00.000 to 2016-09-02T06:39:59.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V1.0 is the first version of this dataset: Lien corrected dataset after September 2019 PSA/PDS external peer review.','public','2026-03-13T17:13:48.146604','2026-03-13T17:13:48.146609','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','4c1e53a3-219c-4c26-9bf1-afd3e31d8567','NASA Data.json','20658ae31fc0fe3513b25a751897053e1b86a2fe0aad37cf9894f779bf9977ae','1.1','2026-03-13T17:13:48.146604','2026-03-13T17:13:48.146609','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('d06b5f68-24b0-45a4-9f49-f3ec07f2320c','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSINAC 5 PRL-MTP009 DDR-GEO V1.0','This CODMAC level 5 data set contains derived data products that include pixel-precise georeferencing information, acquired by the OSIRIS Narrow Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft during the PRELANDING mission phase, covering the period from 2014-10-24T10:00:00.000 to 2014-11-21T23:24:59.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V1.0 is the first version of this dataset: Lien corrected dataset after October 2018 PSA/PDS external peer review.','public','2026-03-13T17:09:10.243970','2026-03-13T17:09:10.243974','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','9bad7ab9-17f3-4aab-90e5-d5c6492cec3e','NASA Data.json','44d7da7508d98817757b2efb573e8438e5edff1ffbd7aa15ac01fdccbcc3d47a','1.1','2026-03-13T17:09:10.243970','2026-03-13T17:09:10.243974','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('d0755f58-a311-4c23-bb95-740e849e1275','Licenses and Inspections: BEE Case Inspections','This dataset contains details and locations related to investigations conducted by the Business Education and Enforcement (BEE) Program, a program run by the Department of Licenses and Inspections Quality of Life and the Commerce Department. The program educates businesses on the law, ensures the businesses have the proper licenses and permits, and tells the businesses to fix any issues that are not meeting the standards required in Philadelphia. Learn more at [Philly Stat 360](https://philly-stat-360.phila.gov/pages/bee~)','public','2026-03-30T19:40:12.611159','2026-03-30T19:40:12.611165','City of Philadelphia','ligisteam@phila.gov',NULL,'966ceafc-c957-4f81-9b8f-0521c2fc6e13','Phila data json','76a256e96c7a5c153aeb9d19280198fc54154dff62fa4d6c1881ba464b8d45b5','1.1','2026-03-30T19:40:12.611159','2026-03-30T19:40:12.611165',NULL,NULL,0,'city-of-philadelphia'),('d07755e3-70b1-4475-bedb-dd463888c2d1','NEW HORIZONS      PEPSSI KEM2      RAW V1.0','This data set contains Raw data taken by the      New Horizons Pluto Energetic Particle Spectrometer Science Investigation      instrument during the KEM1 ENCOUNTER and KEM2 CRUISE mission      phases. This is VERSION 1.0 of this data set.      This version includes data acquired by the spacecraft between      08/14/2018 and 04/10/2023. It only includes data downlinked before      05/01/2023 and after 04/30/2023. Future datasets may include more data      acquired by the spacecraft after 08/13/2018 but downlinked after      04/30/2023.      This dataset contains observations from prior to, during, and after      the ASTEROID 486958 Arrokoth (2014 MU69) encounter.','public','2026-03-13T18:12:57.696910','2026-03-13T18:12:57.696916','small bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','b9649003-15ea-4437-9070-c5369c763910','NASA Data.json','c3940b10c70b7b316a723061de9653c4a72333cbd1ac53aa2c2c2fe485f5d95b','1.1','2026-03-13T18:12:57.696910','2026-03-13T18:12:57.696916','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('d07c0015-0a19-4ba4-98c6-8068e4d11874','MARS EXPRESS MARS MARSIS EXPERIMENT DATA RECORD EXT 6 V1.0','This dataset contains the                    scientific telemetry produced by the MARSIS                    instrument after editing for duplicated and                    corrupted packets, together with geometric                    information computed on ground to locate                    observations in space and time. Both subsurface                    and ionosphere sounding data are included in                    the dataset.','public','2026-03-13T19:46:03.082617','2026-03-13T19:46:03.082625','planetary plasma interactions','Planetary Data System','026:00','5678e6d6-d306-4a0e-aea9-ddf37a5b536a','NASA Data.json','a24b301f6d2c41da53f3b90894094fb6ec4f99a4ac45cbc4369b9ced435e6333','1.1','2026-03-13T19:46:03.082617','2026-03-13T19:46:03.082625','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('d08011a4-9587-4d18-9d70-316f157fcb8b','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSIWAC 4 EXT1-MTP025 RDR-STRLIGHT V1.0','This CODMAC level 4 data set contains solar stray light corrected, radiometric calibrated and geometric distortion corrected (resampled) image data in W/m^2/sr/nm, acquired by the OSIRIS Wide Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft during the ROSETTA EXTENSION 1 mission phase, covering the period from 2016-01-12T23:25:00.000 to 2016-02-09T23:24:59.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V1.0 is the first version of this dataset: Lien corrected dataset after October 2018 PSA/PDS external peer review.','public','2026-03-13T19:55:42.517173','2026-03-13T19:55:42.517178','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','c6894e76-d667-40f6-aa73-5f9d86a000d6','NASA Data.json','5d2b263f68ddd0a3caab404dcb01c955cdb27509b5952fc470e7648602edb9b4','1.1','2026-03-13T19:55:42.517173','2026-03-13T19:55:42.517178','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('d0c251da-f2db-4863-9934-ab280d942f2b','MARS EXPRESS MARS MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 4 3531 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2013-01-01 to 2014-12-31. It is a Global Gravity measurement and covers the time 2013-03-03T08:13:51.000 to 2013-03-03T10:12:39.500.','public','2026-03-13T19:21:33.581336','2026-03-13T19:21:33.581341','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','66a68340-a15f-4e09-b211-82d7f257db01','NASA Data.json','2ab020bec6aba81284a8ad57a7ca89fc2a79ea90321ef5c6900c8e99e98cee64','1.1','2026-03-13T19:21:33.581336','2026-03-13T19:21:33.581341','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('d0c3cc4f-853f-40a6-96a9-13863b363088','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RPCICA 4 PRL CORR-CTS V1.0','This dataset contains corrected and RESAMPLED RAW DATA fromthe RPCICA instrument on mission ROSETTA during the prelanding phase.The data has been corrected for cross-talk using an automatic algorithm,and noise has been treated to be even regardless of onward noisesuppression. The data is the same as L4 CORR but in counts, not physicalunits. The data may due to noise treatment have negative values.Data contains measurements of an undisturbed solar wind untilRosetta was close enough to the comet to obtain measurements ofthe solar wind interaction with the atmosphere of target comet 67P.','public','2026-03-13T17:28:55.591929','2026-03-13T17:28:55.591935','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','d10e08d1-88ef-45dd-bc21-f4e9bee6fe9c','NASA Data.json','fa84c27bbaeb18a01a1d348bfec0918a16224b9ce135970fa00b175a1d33066a','1.1','2026-03-13T17:28:55.591929','2026-03-13T17:28:55.591935','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('d11553e4-fda4-4a47-b9f9-a9242c1bed34','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 2 0786 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 2 phase 2015-03-11 to 2015-06-30. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-05-18T04:45:20.000 to 2015-05-18T06:45:10.000.','public','2026-03-13T20:01:18.802909','2026-03-13T20:01:18.802916','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','0067d6bc-651e-4b8a-9feb-78684f2a2bf1','NASA Data.json','262be883d96284fe4389bcd5579e027e63cb6c885ef41333d3bf0afc6f972595','1.1','2026-03-13T20:01:18.802909','2026-03-13T20:01:18.802916','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('d161e219-6fb2-4b3d-b194-6ae8033d8929','MARS EXPRESS MARS MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 8 4219 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2021-01-01 to 2022-12-31. It is a Occultation measurement and covers the time 2021-04-20T10:07:45.500 to 2021-04-20T11:40:52.629.','public','2026-03-13T17:45:54.352958','2026-03-13T17:45:54.352963','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','dfab397d-f7a2-4a6e-9b5b-0078fa7299c2','NASA Data.json','38e6d9b02b8922133007d63ccd0fef8e0627e686938a12ca53f88933c4353cb8','1.1','2026-03-13T17:45:54.352958','2026-03-13T17:45:54.352963','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('d166855d-4666-407e-b05f-569e05d563eb','EPOXI 103P/HARTLEY2 ENCOUNTER - MRI PHOTOMETRY V1.0','This dataset contains clear-filter, CN, OH, C2, and dust-continuum photometric measurements of comet 103/P Hartley 2 derived from calibrated images acquired by the Medium Resolution Visible CCD (MRI) from 01 October through 26 November 2010, during the Hartley 2 encounter phase of the EPOXI mission. Two different methods were used: simple circular aperture photometry and azimuthal averaged aperture photometry, which removed stars. The results and uncertainties for both procedures are included in this dataset.','public','2026-03-13T17:30:08.285831','2026-03-13T17:30:08.285836','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','ed57336e-0eb4-40df-9074-1888bfa82ec6','NASA Data.json','705451ccf74a4ec1a47e3526defcdbaa33e8083150bd48976d4243b9e7879ae3','1.1','2026-03-13T17:30:08.285831','2026-03-13T17:30:08.285836','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('d173c2b7-3238-429e-9113-5a4de0ee671e','MOC DSDP ARCHIVE','This data set contains portions of the MOC Decompressed Standard Data Product (DSDP) Archive, a collection of decompressed images from the Mars Orbiter Camera on the Mars Global Surveyor spacecraft. Images are stored with PDS labels, but are otherwise unprocessed and uncalibrated.','public','2026-03-13T17:25:20.783014','2026-03-13T17:25:20.783019','Imaging','Planetary Data System','026:00','e457c6a4-2227-4785-b740-8029a5ba5249','NASA Data.json','f2521ba84d1bbe12672d867f1a50d6ef1cc9b65ecd47a492226820619b245828','1.1','2026-03-13T17:25:20.783014','2026-03-13T17:25:20.783019','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('d182190c-5077-4937-be47-3a8ff922ba2a','Laborshed - Employment Status','Laborshed dataset that covers counts and percentages of the employment status groups for all laborshed areas in Iowa.','public','2026-03-28T21:57:58.487301','2026-03-28T21:57:58.487307','data.iowa.gov','svqueen',NULL,'808e1ff2-f5dc-414a-9f76-736f07b9f5b7','Iowa metadata','94b1db821d695852963ca20b73bdd20941c7c85326c5774a448fb525cb003439','1.1','2026-03-28T21:57:58.487301','2026-03-28T21:57:58.487307','Economic Statistics',NULL,0,'state-of-iowa'),('d19172ec-3ddb-4126-82a8-4f360f11beef','MARS EXPRESS SUN MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 5 3757 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2015-01-01 to 2016-12-31. It is a Solar Conjunction measurement and covers the time 2015-06-05T11:18:01 to 2015-06-05T14:29:00.','public','2026-03-13T18:50:55.102844','2026-03-13T18:50:55.102850','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','04ff2363-c42f-4618-a31e-862ab7d13df6','NASA Data.json','9d324550cdf5c79d7872cc331bf7d5a8c53874b9ffc41ce81fdece85b175b784','1.1','2026-03-13T18:50:55.102844','2026-03-13T18:50:55.102850','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('d1a6f968-30ed-4ecc-b34c-a076efbf10f4','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P VIRTIS 3 ESCORT 3 MTP018 V2.0','This release contains the calibrated data of the VIRTIS instrument on board of the spacecraft Rosetta. This volume contains data from the ESCORT 3 MTP018 phase, which occurred from 2015-07-01 to 2015-07-29 when at the vicinity of comet 67P. This data set V2.0 supersedes V1.0. It includes major updates on the data and documentation.','public','2026-03-13T16:46:28.056308','2026-03-13T16:46:28.056313','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','5a13ed5a-48c5-4aa7-ac95-702068e0bc12','NASA Data.json','46f8a19444f112d3182fafbcd4d673c246ab6bb1a9c052294d6bbc196e18c9e0','1.1','2026-03-13T16:46:28.056308','2026-03-13T16:46:28.056313','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('d1a731da-676b-4700-bc8f-9419b981501f','Hydrographic and Impairment Statistics Database: FOMC','Hydrographic and Impairment Statistics (HIS) is a National Park Service (NPS) Water Resources Division (WRD) project established to track certain goals created in response to the Government Performance and Results Act of 1993 (GPRA). One water resources management goal established by the Department of the Interior under GRPA requires NPS to track the percent of its managed surface waters that are meeting Clean Water Act (CWA) water quality standards. This goal requires an accurate inventory that spatially quantifies the surface water hydrography that each bureau manages and a procedure to determine and track which waterbodies are or are not meeting water quality standards as outlined by Section 303(d) of the CWA. This project helps meet this DOI GRPA goal by inventorying and monitoring in a geographic information system for the NPS: (1) CWA 303(d) quality impaired waters and causes; and (2) hydrographic statistics based on the United States Geological Survey (USGS) National Hydrography Dataset (NHD). Hydrographic and 303(d) impairment statistics were evaluated based on a combination of 1:24,000 (NHD) and finer scale data (frequently provided by state GIS layers).','public','2026-03-29T06:06:37.013822','2026-03-29T06:06:37.013829','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','5be4a9aa-a9ed-4f4c-a7eb-17aab4a59411','DOI NPS DCAT-US','63b8922f710c26151dee05111aec1a62c2dfc0abb2b3f3f3b2c05818316f34c0','1.1','2026-03-29T06:06:37.013822','2026-03-29T06:06:37.013829','geospatial','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('d1c9e37a-45b1-4d4d-a7e1-b338d344e5b6','VG2 URA PRA EDITED RDR HIGH RATE                                      60MS V1.0','This data set (VG2-U-PRA-2-RDR-HIGHRATE-60MS-V1.0) contains dataacquired by the Voyager-2 Planetary Radio Astronomy (PRA) instrumentduring the Uranus encounter.  Since the PRA instrument is able toobserve planetary phenomenon at much larger ranges than other fieldsand particles experiments, thus the PRA data cover a variable andlonger encounter period. PRA lowband data provided here cover theentire Uranus Encounter Phase (1985-10-24 to 1988-07-14).','public','2026-03-13T19:03:09.630367','2026-03-13T19:03:09.630373','planetary plasma interactions','Planetary Data System','026:00','637c4383-c76e-484e-bde9-ff5c74e8ebb9','NASA Data.json','a3989f85bced7d77249240ffa6dc0d5e242a62621d20b71a27fff327324ab42f','1.1','2026-03-13T19:03:09.630367','2026-03-13T19:03:09.630373','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('d1cbc389-72f5-4bcc-a0cf-af66c10ac562','MARS EXPRESS MARS MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 7 3999 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2019-01-01 to 2020-12-31. It is a Occultation measurement and covers the time 2019-04-28T08:36:03.299 to 2019-04-28T08:58:10.149.','public','2026-03-13T18:17:22.585994','2026-03-13T18:17:22.585999','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','764c99bd-2cdd-4b39-ba8c-a97fd0b017ea','NASA Data.json','501950bc43bdd1e586bb3706faf16f3f7d09679a4815895e1bdb42f0bca5b33d','1.1','2026-03-13T18:17:22.585994','2026-03-13T18:17:22.585999','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('d1d75f6f-b235-49d6-87fb-9846d7c088ff','State of Maryland Users\' Guide to Uploading Data','A guide to uploading and formatting your data and metadata in the State\'s Internal and Open Data Portals.','public','2026-03-22T03:22:52.639536','2026-03-22T03:22:52.639541','opendata.maryland.gov','J.B. Churchill',NULL,'1973f170-15e9-400c-b878-aabf023a929c','md json','4ec14c8aaa7f012328ac98c5896821aa224245253afa4f9b1517cd1ff67df86b','1.1','2026-03-22T03:22:52.639536','2026-03-22T03:22:52.639541','Administrative',NULL,0,'state-of-maryland'),('d1d8c673-55cb-457b-b64e-9a791325e5bd','GALILEO JUPITER PWS DERIVED PLASMA DENSITY FULL RES V1.0','Plasma electron number density      from Jupiter\'s magnetosphere, derived from measurements of radio      and plasma waves obtained by Galileo','public','2026-03-13T16:56:37.138595','2026-03-13T16:56:37.138600','planetary plasma interactions','Planetary Data System','026:00','ca4c0deb-a5e8-4b54-956a-5e2ab788d3fd','NASA Data.json','8e9653223803e21d853b01f54fedae41d0f58f0aa539cc5d50fbe9922fe68cb4','1.1','2026-03-13T16:56:37.138595','2026-03-13T16:56:37.138600','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('d21c449c-f893-4119-b7b4-38884c463e58','Noble Jim Thompson Current Profile Time Series','Current profile data from Downward-looking ADCP #00 on MODU Noble Jim Thompson, 2.922000e+01N, 8.795000e+01W, 2007/08/21 20:32 through 2007/10/10 13:03','public','2026-03-26T19:17:27.902913','2026-03-26T19:17:27.902919',NULL,NULL,NULL,'d4d8d81c-b5bb-4119-b365-86c7353b3e08','ioos',NULL,NULL,'2026-03-26T19:17:27.902913','2026-03-26T19:17:27.902919',NULL,NULL,NULL,'noaa-gov'),('d2f9d455-7495-4958-9c4e-1ff97c63af89','PHOENIX MARS ATMOSPHERIC STRUCTURE EXP REDUCED DATA V1.0','The purpose of this report is to describe the methodology used to produce Reduced Data Records (RDRs) for the Phoenix Atmospheric Structure Experiment (ASE) from its Experimental Data Records (EDRs). These RDRs include vertical profiles of atmospheric density, pressure, and temperature.','public','2026-03-13T18:24:28.432777','2026-03-13T18:24:28.432785','Planetary Atmospheres','Planetary Data System','026:00','aecae935-744a-49d4-b01e-15de752930e2','NASA Data.json','020720b8fb63b4436d9a64e4e6dc8b96a775da1885869c75ed84ba5b6a06ece8','1.1','2026-03-13T18:24:28.432777','2026-03-13T18:24:28.432785','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('d30bb039-b6b8-4772-8b9d-a4498fc7d7aa','ROSETTA-ORBITER SW RPCMAG 2 PRL RAW V9.0','This dataset contains EDITED RAW DATA (CODMAC LEVEL 2) of thePRELANDING Phase (PRL) from March 23,2014 until November 21, 2014of the ROSETTA orbiter magnetometer RPCMAG. Observations are done inthe vicinity of comet 67P/CHURYUMOV-GERASIMENKO 1 (1969 R1).The current version of the dataset is V9.0.The difference to the datasets of earlier versions is mainly a significantlyimproved sensor temperature model, more detailed documentation about magneticdisturbance sources, more data handling information for the user andalso an improved quality flagging system.This applies mainly to CALIBRATED and RESAMPLED datasets. The RAW dataset,however, has been updated as well in order provide all datasets at thesame stage, although RAW data proper did not change.','public','2026-03-13T18:24:02.723233','2026-03-13T18:24:02.723240','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','1e1458c5-f76e-4b31-8cb0-dadcec641821','NASA Data.json','c8683f6e2594f0f41eddeda6d8f33d3c78c2a620bdb7d94dfcf43b350b85bf75','1.1','2026-03-13T18:24:02.723233','2026-03-13T18:24:02.723240','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('d336d255-9612-486d-8e1b-a435105b0dcd','ROSETTA-ORBITER CHECKOUT OSIWAC 4 CR2 RDR-REFLECT V1.0','This CODMAC level 4 data set contains radiometric calibrated and geometric distortion corrected (resampled)  image data in reflectance units (normalized and thus without unit),  acquired by the OSIRIS Wide Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft  during the CRUISE 2 mission phase, covering the period  from 2005-04-05T00:00:00.000 to 2006-07-28T23:59:59.000. The prime objective was commissioning / calibration. Several targets of opportunity were observed, but none of them is identifiable as prime target. This version V1.0 is the first version of this dataset.','public','2026-03-13T16:57:58.498330','2026-03-13T16:57:58.498336','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','d33aa3d5-8982-404e-9ae5-03a4ffa8bd65','NASA Data.json','15ef737cb83031d974e0532b72e7c24d3a048ad563c1be942f3f188888acd71a','1.1','2026-03-13T16:57:58.498330','2026-03-13T16:57:58.498336','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('d3646635-c4cf-4472-ba42-3e1629e96853','NRC 823C','NRC Health Center Consent for 2009-2010 H1N1 Inactivated Influenza (Flu Shot). Fillable form in Adobe Portable Document Format (PDF) with information submitted by NRC stakeholder - licensee, applicant, or NRC employee/contractor.','non-public','2026-03-20T19:44:02.857254','2026-03-20T19:44:02.857258','Nuclear Regulatory Commission','Ilka Solorio','429:00','7dd1c315-3676-4088-a0e3-7c016184516b','NRC Data.json Harvest Source','be06a50441213387ab5fb7cfdfc7c64fd19f4bc06782fb74b355561f38249b17','1.1','2026-03-20T19:44:02.857254','2026-03-20T19:44:02.857258',NULL,'000:000',0,'nrc-gov'),('d3919941-b6b9-4153-8721-c78aa03c423b','ODYSSEY THEMIS IR RDR V1.0','The THEMIS IR-RDR data set contains the calibrated thermal infrared observations. Each qube header includes basic parameters describing the observation and file specific details of the calibration process.','public','2026-03-13T17:50:04.971522','2026-03-13T17:50:04.971527','Imaging','Planetary Data System','026:00','fe532fbf-8a37-42e5-9d76-cb41f7b1183d','NASA Data.json','8c53d5bea797e7c03d8e77a012d1dc33a3c9195955f864e84298e2c1cca0f19b','1.1','2026-03-13T17:50:04.971522','2026-03-13T17:50:04.971527','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('d39e0207-a1ee-4a8a-aa89-9144b8c71db3','ROSETTA-ORBITER EARTH OSINAC 2 EAR1 EDR V2.0','This CODMAC level 2 data set contains uncalibrated image data in DN unit,  acquired by the OSIRIS Narrow Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft  during the EARTH SWING-BY 1 mission phase, covering the period  from 2004-10-17T00:00:00.000 to 2005-04-04T23:59:59.000. The prime target is planet Earth. This version V2.0 supersedes previous deliveries of the same dataset with the following changes since the last version: Reprocessed dataset after October 2018 PSA/PDS external peer review.','public','2026-03-13T18:27:41.244920','2026-03-13T18:27:41.244926','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','57d3c3aa-1c22-4980-baab-5254796526b9','NASA Data.json','063f2219cb1bc41ed0bc99dd44f58982fa4faf0e8cbe35718a859cb4c8bd76fc','1.1','2026-03-13T18:27:41.244920','2026-03-13T18:27:41.244926','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('d3cb4f53-5d09-4e63-b9f0-a47e48e665da','MOLA MISSION EXPERIMENT GRIDDED DATA RECORD','The Mars Global Surveyor spacecraft includes a laser altimeter instrument. The primary objective of the Mars Orbiter Laser Altimeter (MOLA) is to determine globally the topography of Mars at a level suitable for addressing problems in geology and geophysics. The MOLA Experiment Gridded Data Record (EGDR) is a topographic map of Mars based on altimetry data acquired by the MOLA instrument and accumulated over the course of the mission. The Mission Experiment Gridded Data Record (MEGDR), consists of data accumulated over the whole primary mission.','public','2026-03-13T19:58:56.095598','2026-03-13T19:58:56.095603','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','1fa062fe-5a44-416b-ab15-38cb32a5b0ed','NASA Data.json','abd75a095c1887bd0ce93c0e415d2a98b813d9958998b5d6c3035d5aafb84345','1.1','2026-03-13T19:58:56.095598','2026-03-13T19:58:56.095603','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('d4247c49-a3ac-46d7-be3a-20458c1f3bb5','VOYAGER 1 SOLAR WIND MAGNETIC FIELD HGCOORDS HOUR AVGS V1.0','This dataset contains Voyager 1 magnetometer data from the      interplanetary cruise averaged to 1 hour samples in Heliographic      coordinates.','public','2026-03-13T17:03:23.364643','2026-03-13T17:03:23.364648','planetary plasma interactions','Planetary Data System','026:00','ba365c25-0400-41c2-87de-aefcfd5d9984','NASA Data.json','e25c315cb33549272144c1f79806306ae6ac8579c8124b7845267c42aa583809','1.1','2026-03-13T17:03:23.364643','2026-03-13T17:03:23.364648','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('d42d4ad8-db63-4932-8e4d-b12db17cf189','BLM ID Ground Transportation Linear Features','The purpose of the BLM ID Ground Transportation Linear Features (GTLF) is to provide a standardized transportation information for use in BLM programs and analysis. The ground transportation linear features gathered, inventoried, analyzed and recorded in a Travel Management Plan (TMP). The TMP analyzes transportation options and incorporates public participation to assist in determining travel routes, modes of travel, season of use on selected and surrounding BLM managed lands. The BLM ID only maintains only GTLF routes that have been recorded in a TMP. All other data is considered Non-BLM authoritive, administered and maintained transportation data and is provided only as spatial and tabular reference material. The BLM ID GTLF contains external routes that provides connectivity to BLM managed lands. The purpose for collecting and maintaining an Idaho state-wide route connectivity is to provide a broad overview of the transportation network for properly focused analysis or inventory purposes and to provide connectivity between BLM managed routes and the broader transportation networks.','public','2026-03-25T12:33:07.323106','2026-03-25T12:33:07.323112','Bureau of Land Management','Bureau of Land Management, blm_id_stateoffice','010:04','ae4acc3f-e30f-4317-a99e-cd984350badf','DOI BLM DCAT-US','b56b4d2dc9691be44895a9481639314c6a9f2b6d524bd91ae54c282c2b940d30','1.1','2026-03-25T12:33:07.323106','2026-03-25T12:33:07.323112','geospatial','010:000',0,'doi-gov'),('d43ae981-d5bd-4dbd-ac96-fdb0f09799ef','ROSETTA-ORBITER COMET ESCORT OSINAC 3 RDR MTP 019 V1.0','This data set contains calibrated images acquired by the OSIRIS Narrow AngleCamera during the escort phase of the Rosetta mission at the comet 67P,covering the period from 2015-07-28 to 2015-08-25.','public','2026-03-13T19:24:39.796772','2026-03-13T19:24:39.796779','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','b7305df2-1a50-4989-8f6e-3b2e235dabcc','NASA Data.json','47d66d8ca071804d49f96200814440a23e09cf80b2076f0aa275b1f9af97986b','1.1','2026-03-13T19:24:39.796772','2026-03-13T19:24:39.796779','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('d4464f0e-6ef6-4fe1-ad1b-1f6b5b2c7b39','ARCSIX P-3B In-Situ Trace Gas Data','ARCSIX_TraceGas_AircraftInSitu_P3B_Data is the in-situ trace gas data collected onboard the P-3B aircraft during the Arctic Radiation-Cloud-Aerosol-Surface Interaction EXperiment (ARCSIX) campaign. Data from the PICARRO G2401-m Gas Concentration Analyzer and the 2B Technologies Model 205 Ozone Monitor are featured in this collection. Data collection for this product is complete. The ARCSIX campaign is a NASA field investigation aimed at quantifying the contributions of surface properties, clouds, aerosol particles, and precipitation to the Arctic summer surface radiation budget and sea ice melt during the early melt season. Based out of Greenland, ARCSIX completed two deployments from May – June 2024 and July - August 2024 utilizing the NASA P-3B, LaRC G-III, and SPEC-Learjet aircraft. The P-3B was equipped with in situ and remote sensing payloads to acquire measurements of aerosols, cloud, and radiation properties. The high-flying LaRC G-III was equipped with remote sensing instrumentation, including the HALO, and HSRL, along with the AVAPS dropsonde system. The SPEC-Learjet acquired measurements of cloud microphysics. Data were also collected at the Thule High Arctic Atmospheric Observatory (THAAO) in Pituffik, Greenland. The primary objective of ARCSIX was to enhance long-term space-based monitoring and predictive capabilities of Arctic sea ice, cloud, and aerosols by validating and improving remote sensing algorithms and model parameterizations in the Arctic. ARCSIX science questions focused on examining the impact of the predominant summer Arctic cloud types on the radiative surface energy budget, what processes control the evolution and maintenance of the predominant cloud types in the summertime Arctic, and how do the two-way interactions between surface properties and atmospheric forcings affect sea ice evolution?','public','2026-03-13T16:48:46.350179','2026-03-13T16:48:46.350184','NASA/LARC/SD/ASDC','Earthdata Forum','026:00','bca14b16-3b94-41a2-bea9-daacdd4fbb84','NASA Data.json','99dfaa413a0130fba11e88611887831c9239ca5e79fdc5f7c22c6956f1892692','1.1','2026-03-13T16:48:46.350179','2026-03-13T16:48:46.350184','Earth Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('d49c1d0b-9076-4170-9ba8-a8dbaf9d5135','ROSETTA-LANDER CAL PTOLEMY 3 PDCS V1.0','This archive contains calibrated data from the PTOLEMY instrument onboard ROSETTA Lander, acquired during the PDCS mission phase. It also contains documentation which describes the PTOLEMY experiment. The data archived in this data set conform to the Planetary Data System (PDS) Standards, Version 3.6.','public','2026-03-13T17:48:12.965662','2026-03-13T17:48:12.965668','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','95ebaa0d-d280-4c14-912a-dace7b19b924','NASA Data.json','ef5dacea8a4ece4626d271ca874ecb2e7c4e956dcf0bda9c3cd2c8dcf8671435','1.1','2026-03-13T17:48:12.965662','2026-03-13T17:48:12.965668','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('d49eded6-b24c-4ba4-abbc-31d232822208','EPOXI EARTH OBS - HRII CALIBRATED SPECTRA V2.0','This dataset contains calibrated, 1.05- to 4.8-micron spectra of Earth acquired by the High Resolution Infrared Spectrometer (HRII) during the EPOCh and Cruise 2 phases of the EPOXI mission. Five sets of observations were acquired on 18-19 March, 28-29 May and 04-05 June 2008 and on 27-28 March and 04-05 October 2009 to characterize Earth as an analog for extrasolar planets. Each observing period lasted approximately 24 hours, and spectra were acquired twice every 2 hours. During the observing period in May 2008, the Moon transited across Earth as seen from the spacecraft. HRII spectra were not acquired during the first attempt of an Earth south polar observation on 27-28 September 2009 because fault protection turned that instrument off; the full sequence was successfully rerun on 04-05 October 2009. Version 2 corrects an error in the IR absolute calibration that previously inflated all spectra by a factor of 2.','public','2026-03-13T19:43:58.695430','2026-03-13T19:43:58.695437','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','3014a089-84d4-4322-82e8-21fcf86a0767','NASA Data.json','ced193697263db410e56d44dd7b3d83b50f8c6236351668ce72fb8029a6447c5','1.1','2026-03-13T19:43:58.695430','2026-03-13T19:43:58.695437','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('d4aac58d-af66-4db8-895e-91f7d29d990a','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSINAC 4 PRL-MTP009 RDR-INF-REFL V1.0','This CODMAC level 4 data set contains solar stray-light corrected, in-field stray-light corrected,  radiometric calibrated and geometric distortion corrected  (resampled) image data in reflectance units (normalized  and thus without unit),  acquired by the OSIRIS Narrow Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft  during the PRELANDING mission phase, covering the period  from 2014-10-24T10:00:00.000 to 2014-11-21T23:24:59.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V1.0 is the first version of this dataset: Lien corrected dataset after September 2019 PSA/PDS external peer review.','public','2026-03-13T16:58:04.249544','2026-03-13T16:58:04.249551','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','05d31de9-0364-44eb-8667-ea393841269c','NASA Data.json','522f7b049af1c2eb311c4ce39e633b4061b1a0e8129ef7aaf82b2c0d119b6c74','1.1','2026-03-13T16:58:04.249544','2026-03-13T16:58:04.249551','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('d4b797ca-a020-481d-84b3-ff21b21c884a','In Vitro Confirmation of Estrogenic and Antiandrogenic Pesticide Bioactivity using Schild Regression Analysis','Experimental results from in vitro analysis for Confirmation of Estrogenic and Antiandrogenic Pesticide Bioactivity using Schild Regression Analysis. \n\nThis dataset is associated with the following publication:\nBoxberger, C., L. Gray, N. Evans, J. Conley, and E. Medlock Kakaley. In Vitro Confirmation of Estrogenic and Antiandrogenic Pesticide Bioactivity using Schild Regression Analysis.   TOXICOLOGY AND APPLIED PHARMACOLOGY. Elsevier B.V., Amsterdam,  NETHERLANDS, 504: 117523, (2025).','public','2026-03-23T12:01:03.609027','2026-03-23T12:01:03.609032','U.S. Environmental Protection Agency','Justin Conley','020:00','92d42032-4f8f-4505-b303-5506f0c418f5','EPA ScienceHub','804ddb299f004a7dd154bfec1742706a24e8d212cd8828e301de885535ba3052','1.1','2026-03-23T12:01:03.609027','2026-03-23T12:01:03.609032',NULL,'020:000',0,'epa-gov'),('d5a00180-e32c-409d-81c4-86815d34cc6d','Employment Benefit Analysis: Paid Leave Time Offered','The Employment Benefit Analysis was published in 2023. The data reported was collected through an employer survey in the State of Iowa.\n\nThis dataset shows the average and median time (in days or hours) by type of paid leave, which is offered by employers to their employees (both in full-time and part-time status) in their first year of employment. The data can be viewed by area (statewide, county, or LWDA), by industry of the employer, and by employer size.','public','2026-03-28T22:02:16.260259','2026-03-28T22:02:16.260265','data.iowa.gov','Katie Green',NULL,'0a4245b3-1036-49c2-b19d-5084bd61d713','Iowa metadata','3fda1af654bda4baf7dfabbb7b2d3f28f31f8bf8e372270a0a6cd1f6da87e13e','1.1','2026-03-28T22:02:16.260259','2026-03-28T22:02:16.260265','Workforce',NULL,0,'state-of-iowa'),('d5a55ba4-8bc7-4ad5-b0f9-5f3012005d5e','Continuous Fixed Station Water Quality Measurements in Canaveral National Seashore, June 2007 (Certified)','This dataset represents continuous water quality measurements that were taken at a fixed point in Canaveral National Seashore during the month of June, 2007 as a part of the Fixed Station Water Quality Monitoring protocol that was developed by the Southeast Coast I&M Network (SECN). The measurements were taken by a YSI 6600 ESD Multi-Parameter Long Term Water Quality Monitoring Datasonde unit that serves as the standard fixed station water quality monitoring equipment for all similar operations conducted by the SECN. The following parameters were measured at 30 minute intervals during the time period that has been specified: Water Temperature, Specific Conductivity, Salinity, Dissolved Oxygen (DO), DO Concentration, Shallow Depth, pH Level, and Turbidity. Any anomalies noted regarding these parameters have also been noted in separate fields. Please note that these measurements have been certified by network personnel.','public','2026-03-26T05:31:19.556240','2026-03-26T05:31:19.556246','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','d7256a81-9590-404b-b340-d5f33b1de6b1','DOI NPS DCAT-US','854e4cd18df8f3fa556e03897ab1d833402916b3a4873710cbe9360970939286','1.1','2026-03-26T05:31:19.556240','2026-03-26T05:31:19.556246','Vector Dataset','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('d5b95bc8-07fe-4f47-88f7-2e4258f09b4a','NEW HORIZONS LEISA JUPITER ENCOUNTER V1.1','This data set contains Calibrated data taken by the New Horizons Linear Etalon Imaging Spectral Array instrument during the Jupiter encounter mission phase.','public','2026-03-13T17:52:03.956431','2026-03-13T17:52:03.956438','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','5fc8a8d1-c80d-4ff9-a522-7139ff1ab729','NASA Data.json','a73634f3b73bed8b25efdb4bef8d209352fba0797c73673a466edc37ace9a6c4','1.1','2026-03-13T17:52:03.956431','2026-03-13T17:52:03.956438','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('d5dd1a71-8839-418f-b98f-883ab4001e25','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 4 1203 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 4 phase 2015-10-22 to 2015-12-31. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-11-19T16:05:45.000 to 2015-11-19T16:46:50.500.','public','2026-03-13T19:23:25.704507','2026-03-13T19:23:25.704513','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','770ebc7c-8fab-473f-94a3-e5710563559a','NASA Data.json','1d5477296a6268a770d5541faba192f156f311ecb99c45d4b695a89648018f62','1.1','2026-03-13T19:23:25.704507','2026-03-13T19:23:25.704513','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('d5dfad19-e86a-4d04-96f2-08a6b45bc91b','EGIS - Enterprise Gateway Integration Services-Visa Support Services (VSS)','VSS supports cooperative efforts between the governments of the United States and Canada to secure the homelands of both countries and enhance the flow of legitimate travel and trade. ','non-public','2026-03-22T11:55:06.184472','2026-03-22T11:55:06.184477','Unspecified','Open Data (MGMT)','024:030','c008e10f-46c9-49fa-81f4-e3a1b76f73bb','DHS datajson source','f5d14d8b6f14c345646b4b207c0bfe2e9d4673f306e033ccdde5dc4cab7278c2','1.1','2026-03-22T11:55:06.184472','2026-03-22T11:55:06.184477',NULL,'024:000',0,'dhs-gov'),('d5f8f265-33ae-4118-9ebe-31b8abcac460','ROSETTA-ORBITER CHECKOUT OSIWAC 4 RVM1 RDR-STR-REFL V1.0','This CODMAC level 4 data set contains solar stray light corrected, radiometric calibrated and geometric distortion corrected (resampled) image data in in reflectance units  (normalized and thus without unit),  acquired by the OSIRIS Wide Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft  during the RENDEZVOUS MANOEUVRE 1 mission phase, covering the period  from 2010-09-04T00:00:00.000 to 2011-07-13T23:59:59.000. The prime objective was commissioning / calibration. Several targets of opportunity were observed, but none of them is identifiable as prime target. This version V1.0 is the first version of this dataset.','public','2026-03-13T18:48:31.345381','2026-03-13T18:48:31.345387','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','010df622-8b81-441e-8c80-7c92500234e9','NASA Data.json','2ff8c097b0e17449ba4f662b49efa87af82bac0c76ecd574526a5cf301b31993','1.1','2026-03-13T18:48:31.345381','2026-03-13T18:48:31.345387','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('d6563557-e5fb-490e-945d-bfdb983a0591','DC COVID 19 Cases by Ward','<div style=\"text-align:Left;\"><div><div><p>Retired on March 2, 2022. Data and metadata are provided as-is archive.</p><p><span>District of Columbia COVID-19 positive cases and total tests reported by Ward. Due to rapidly changing nature of COVID-19, data for March 2020 is limited.</span></p><p><strong>General Guidelines for Interpreting Disease Surveillance Data</strong></p><p><span>During a disease outbreak, the health department will collect, process, and analyze large amounts of information to understand and respond to the health impacts of the disease and its transmission in the community. The sources of disease surveillance information include contact tracing, medical record review, and laboratory information, and are considered protected health information. When interpreting the results of these analyses, it is important to keep in mind that the disease surveillance system may not capture the full picture of the outbreak, and that previously reported data may change over time as it undergoes data quality review or as additional information is added. These analyses, especially within populations with small samples, may be subject to large amounts of variation from day to day. Despite these limitations, data from disease surveillance is a valuable source of information to understand how to stop the spread of COVID19.</span></p></div></div></div>','public','2026-04-01T08:42:46.888198','2026-04-01T08:42:46.888205','Office of the Chief Technology Officer','DCGISopendata',NULL,'e388635f-c193-49a8-87ed-9e341e4425bf','DC data','e2af7e4e1be1252ecf534d08a6ca7373d5823818ad7de65ddea711b97173faa1','1.1','2026-04-01T08:42:46.888198','2026-04-01T08:42:46.888205','geospatial',NULL,0,'district-of-columbia'),('d65e4f81-c4cf-4569-b963-77d5589cb15a','HPMS Roadway Sections 2020','These data are the road section attributes from the Highway Performance Monitoring System (HPMS). The HPMS Field Manual, and corresponding section dataset, identify records by their Data Item.','public','2026-03-28T13:37:26.325079','2026-03-28T13:37:26.325085','Federal Highway Administration','Office of Highway Policy Information','021:15','4e528d35-0fdf-41fa-a5f3-cdbe7a4d5450','DOT Socrata Data.json','ac13c2397826f76576a3fe976413bdca09e5ad6e307280437631bbf7b08c17f7','1.1','2026-03-28T13:37:26.325079','2026-03-28T13:37:26.325085','Roadways and Bridges','021:009',0,'dot-gov'),('d67f8fb3-37da-4961-9c5e-530457d11a7a','Medicare Alternative Payment Model Adoption','The Medicare Alternative Payment Model (APM) Adoption data set provides information on the amount and percent of Medicare payments flowing through APMs, including downside risk models. The data is segmented according to the categories of the HCP-LAN APM framework, which provides a common, industry framework for classifying payment models. The Framework classifies APMs in four categories and eight subcategories, specifying decision rules to standardize classification efforts. ','public','2026-03-17T16:52:04.272082','2026-03-17T16:52:04.272120','Centers for Medicare & Medicaid Services','Medicare Alternative Payment Model Adoption - CMMI','009:38','a47ffb1d-cf37-4233-b3e4-92cecee463af','Healthdata.gov','9a8e353d766c600e8295a3278d7748d782c2040d3315e3ab675e1512e9608317','1.1','2026-03-17T16:52:04.272082','2026-03-17T16:52:04.272120','Medicare','009:000',0,'hhs-gov'),('d692b59e-dff1-4310-b3e2-b9233e6e7107','VO1/VO2 MARS INFRARED THERMAL MAPPER RESAMPLED DATA V1.0','This data set contains the Infrared Thermal Mapping (IRTM) data of Mars acquired by the Viking orbiters. The database contains the time, geometry, and radiative parameters obtained by the IRTM instrument. Included in the database for each measurement are model temperatures of Mars represent the average Martian response to the temporal variation of insolation. The reference \'Thermal and Albedo Mapping of Mars during the Viking Primary Mission\', Journal of Geophysical Research, Vol. 82, No. 28, 1977, describes how the thermal emission and reflected energy measured by the various channels on the Infrared Thermal Mapper are used to reveal wide variations in the Martian surface properties. There is a description of how the surface thermal inertias are mapped and correlated with the surficial geologic units. The derivation of model and surface temperatures are described. The data set includes latitude and longitude for each measured point, as well as emission angle, solar incidence angle, the position of the sun, and other parameters that help to locate the position of the spacecraft relative to Mars. (For further information see the Confidence_Level_Note).','public','2026-03-13T19:01:23.391717','2026-03-13T19:01:23.391722','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','d8ea546b-9c4f-492e-8154-3e1de037f0ab','NASA Data.json','5e3af9bfc534c4880dc529314798670ab3edf110ff3396a5ae4c1de0861e23c2','1.1','2026-03-13T19:01:23.391717','2026-03-13T19:01:23.391722','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('d6c000f0-58a6-4ba9-ba6a-5131bfe5cbed','Hydrographic and Impairment Statistics Database: NPS-WSR John Wild and Scenic River','Hydrographic and Impairment Statistics (HIS) is a National Park Service (NPS) Water Resources Division (WRD) project established to track certain goals created in response to the Government Performance and Results Act of 1993 (GPRA). One water resources management goal established by the Department of the Interior under GRPA requires NPS to track the percent of its managed surface waters that are meeting Clean Water Act (CWA) water quality standards. This goal requires an accurate inventory that spatially quantifies the surface water hydrography that each bureau manages and a procedure to determine and track which waterbodies are or are not meeting water quality standards as outlined by Section 303(d) of the CWA. This project helps meet this DOI GRPA goal by inventorying and monitoring in a geographic information system for the NPS: (1) CWA 303(d) quality impaired waters and causes; and (2) hydrographic statistics based on the United States Geological Survey (USGS) National Hydrography Dataset (NHD). Hydrographic and 303(d) impairment statistics were evaluated based on a combination of 1:24,000 (NHD) and finer scale data (frequently provided by state GIS layers).','public','2026-03-29T06:06:39.659882','2026-03-29T06:06:39.659889','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','b339b27d-e1cc-4c29-aebd-44e5e728c37e','DOI NPS DCAT-US','1b19623a7834eb6a0efaa9f54b01819828bc78b475822904704a80e8d9939297','1.1','2026-03-29T06:06:39.659882','2026-03-29T06:06:39.659889','geospatial','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('d6e1448e-ee06-425a-af7e-e935d690b4b6','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSIWAC 4 PRL-MTP004 RDR-REFLECT V1.0','This CODMAC level 4 data set contains radiometric calibrated and geometric distortion corrected (resampled) image data in reflectance units (normalized and thus without unit), acquired by the OSIRIS Wide Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft during the PRELANDING mission phase, covering the period from 2014-06-04T10:50:00.000 to 2014-07-02T08:34:59.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V1.0 is the first version of this dataset: Lien corrected dataset after October 2018 PSA/PDS external peer review.','public','2026-03-13T19:08:50.960778','2026-03-13T19:08:50.960783','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','a229074e-241e-4118-8a7c-f73a2662c56b','NASA Data.json','d914fe21731b65c8ad42f37a57a9bf1fa7f5ed5453a7cc214d4a933d7b214d1b','1.1','2026-03-13T19:08:50.960778','2026-03-13T19:08:50.960783','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('d70ea662-1f56-44ff-af80-9b517305c128','MGN V RDRS DERIVED MOSAIC IMAGE DATA RECORD FULL RES V1.0','This data set contains the Magellan Full-resolution Mosaic Image Data Records (F-MIDR) which consists of SAR mosaics generated from F-BIDRs (i.e., with 75 meters / pixel). Each F-MIDR is in a sinusoidal equal area projection and has an origin at 0 degrees latitude, with the central meridian defined as the longitude bisecting the mosaic. Each F-MIDR has 7168 lines (aligned with latitude) by 8192 samples, arranged on the CD-ROM as 56 1024 x 1024 files. F-MIDRs have been generated for key terrains on the planet, regions where highest spatial resolution is required for analysis.','public','2026-03-13T18:31:43.009627','2026-03-13T18:31:43.009633','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','a53be336-d239-4bab-961c-dc6e3e6edf3a','NASA Data.json','8b7f018223c2e1d1a05e8df3a099f76d431e73067343223445b1078d15813692','1.1','2026-03-13T18:31:43.009627','2026-03-13T18:31:43.009633','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('d715272c-9f65-4912-b2a6-8e9004793fc0','NEW HORIZONS  LEISA PLUTO CRUISE  CALIBRATED V1.0','This data set contains Calibrated data taken by the New Horizons  Linear Etalon Imaging Spectral Array  instrument during the  pluto cruise  mission phase. This is VERSION 1.0 of this data set.   The spacecraft was in hibernation for much of the Pluto Cruise  mission phase, and the focus for RALPH (which includes both MVIC and  LEISA sensors) during Annual CheckOuts one through eight (ACO1-8) was  preparation for the Pluto Encounter in 2015, including functional tests,  and calibrations. Observations performed during this phase for LEISA were  for the Pluto Encounter Rehearsal in 2013, a test of the Sun in the Solar  Illumination Assembly (SIA), Vega and Arcturus calibrations, and other  calibrations (stray light, dark, flat fields, interference with other  instruments).','public','2026-03-13T19:40:52.841810','2026-03-13T19:40:52.841817','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','f99b3d43-019b-4c8f-8160-3b92e0e43a92','NASA Data.json','b83adc760f10c00b9f7a6c5c2677f244020a47a484f5a8667f1f0f591490f06c','1.1','2026-03-13T19:40:52.841810','2026-03-13T19:40:52.841817','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('d72df159-5983-441c-a74f-e0bfc18aa3b3','CASSINI RSS RAW DATA SET - SROC12 V1.0','The Cassini Radio Science Saturn Ring and Atmospheric Occultation experiments (SROC12) Raw Data Archive is a time-ordered collection of radio science raw data acquired on April 27 and June 18, 2010, during the Cassini Extended Mission.','public','2026-03-13T17:53:33.053563','2026-03-13T17:53:33.053569','Planetary Atmospheres','Planetary Data System','026:00','206fdb2a-07cb-4e14-9787-031da9027e1d','NASA Data.json','c33e6ff5a15ee68c0ed79c6d9c80dc5ff1d3d0037b2a060968d840479dab6d4c','1.1','2026-03-13T17:53:33.053563','2026-03-13T17:53:33.053569','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('d7bbd748-ad32-421f-ad5d-34a7e9930f55','NEW HORIZONS      SWAP KEM2      RAW V1.0','This data set contains Raw data taken by the      New Horizons Solar Wind Around Pluto instrument during the      KEM1 ENCOUNTER and KEM2 CRUISE mission phases.      This is VERSION 1.0 of this data set.      This version includes data acquired by the spacecraft between      08/14/2018 and 04/30/2023. It only includes data downlinked before      05/01/2023 and after 04/30/2022. Future datasets may include more      data acquired by the spacecraft after 08/13/2018 but downlinked after      04/30/2023.      This dataset includes SWAP observations and plasma rolls taken after the      Arrokoth encounter.','public','2026-03-13T18:11:03.457260','2026-03-13T18:11:03.457267','small bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','73a7f867-aee8-47c8-8d81-5dcf44bd11dc','NASA Data.json','9fe32c38e39a90b6dfa3d3217f59a0f0ee6fff7228c723fe7cc205dbb160e208','1.1','2026-03-13T18:11:03.457260','2026-03-13T18:11:03.457267','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('d8046893-8bf9-4e84-a5b4-034c27e99359','MARS EXPRESS MARS MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 7 4157 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2019-01-01 to 2020-12-31. It is a Occultation measurement and covers the time 2020-11-26T11:12:12.399 to 2020-11-26T11:34:20.549.','public','2026-03-13T18:08:35.549106','2026-03-13T18:08:35.549112','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','01142f41-5e0e-407a-9ccb-2107bdd0259c','NASA Data.json','ec69fd7d963d5a20b27d4d0423ce170767db030833eec8ea66332b082d92ff5e','1.1','2026-03-13T18:08:35.549106','2026-03-13T18:08:35.549112','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('d84a2061-c536-4087-91a8-546a0b1a7427','EGIS - Enterprise Gateway Integration Services-Payment Service (PMT)','The Payments Service (PMT) is an intermediary between USCIS and Pay.gov for payment transactions required for benefit processing. PMT also consumes Pay.gov settlement information and distributes transaction status to parties interested in payment failures. PMT does not store or retain PII or information regarding financial accounts.','non-public','2026-03-22T11:53:50.916645','2026-03-22T11:53:50.916650','Unspecified','Open Data (MGMT)','024:030','11a2e5a1-7774-4546-9ad4-e9c3b33ec407','DHS datajson source','342ab7dde0239efa331118cbcdd859144781798d0df3c974cffcd4f0ffafd7a8','1.1','2026-03-22T11:53:50.916645','2026-03-22T11:53:50.916650',NULL,'024:000',0,'dhs-gov'),('d84df86b-3e23-41b2-992a-1f6c6b8ef18c','ROSETTA-ORBITER LUTETIA VIRTIS 2 AST2 V1.0','This release contains the digital numbers (DN) contained in the telemetry (TM) packages of the VIRTIS instrument on board of the spacecraft Rosetta. This volume contains data from the Lutetia Fly-by phase, which occurred on 25-04/10-07/2010.','public','2026-03-13T17:30:24.984626','2026-03-13T17:30:24.984631','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','f2852191-ed0b-481a-9363-23fd16292170','NASA Data.json','9854208e67a2b6029da5d4ac6d7b940aaf7c36f893da1ce0c8b1c3ceea90ee29','1.1','2026-03-13T17:30:24.984626','2026-03-13T17:30:24.984631','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('d8ee4b9d-0693-4fff-b7f5-5a8f652418aa','Continuous Fixed Station Water Quality Measurements in Cape Lookout National Seashore, August 2008 (Certified)','This dataset represents continuous water quality measurements that were taken at a fixed point in Cape Lookout National Seashore during the month of August, 2008 as a part of the Fixed Station Water Quality Monitoring protocol that was developed by the Southeast Coast I&M Network (SECN). The measurements were taken by a YSI 6600 ESD Multi-Parameter Long Term Water Quality Monitoring Datasonde unit that serves as the standard fixed station water quality monitoring equipment for all similar operations conducted by the SECN. The following parameters were measured at 15 minute intervals during the time period that has been specified: Water Temperature, Specific Conductivity, Salinity, Dissolved Oxygen (DO), DO Concentration, Shallow Depth, pH Level, and Turbidity. Any anomalies noted regarding these parameters have also been noted in separate fields.  Please note that these measurements have been certified by network personnel.','public','2026-03-26T05:28:44.861408','2026-03-26T05:28:44.861413','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','4367360c-d1d6-4d5b-92b9-4c629588bf2c','DOI NPS DCAT-US','6f541f5e4a78fc2ddcbf284727ea76b5f9fd27e27b8c5ec084445fded47f56cd','1.1','2026-03-26T05:28:44.861408','2026-03-26T05:28:44.861413','Vector Dataset','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('d9039911-d536-49a4-b7f7-72be01a1c6b9','CASSINI RSS RAW DATA SET - ENGR6 V1.0','The Cassini Radio Science Enceladus Gravity Science Experiment (ENGR6) Raw Data Archive is a time-ordered collection of radio science raw data acquired on April 27 and 28, 2010, during he Cassini Extended Mission.','public','2026-03-13T20:01:24.562190','2026-03-13T20:01:24.562195','Planetary Atmospheres','Planetary Data System','026:00','2ee34ab0-93e3-419e-8456-079fd02ccf7b','NASA Data.json','20eede586ce6a290c1777537be0d0f34b5b2dc3eadd33172e2d736ece4613dd6','1.1','2026-03-13T20:01:24.562190','2026-03-13T20:01:24.562195','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('d91b4ab5-3be2-41b5-932d-bd0cf883374b','CPMS - Customer Profile Management System','The Customer Profile Management System (CPMS) is the repository of biometric & background check data for USCIS. CPMS provides the capability to store and reuse biometric images and biographic information about applicants, and initiates background check requests about those applicants. CPMS records biometric and biographic data collected by other USCIS systems, and then uses a combination of biometric and biographic identifiers to determine an applicant’s identity in CPMS.  CPMS performs biometric vetting to determine which biometrics can be reused based on that identity, and verifies the identity of qualified applicants by sending newly captured fingerprints to DHS-IDENT for verification against previously captured fingerprint images. Once an identity is verified, CPMS requests background checks from FBI and, depending on the form type, DoD or a foreign partner country. Knowledge of both biometric identification and biographic identifiers at each stage of the process provides a person-centric view of applicants’ interactions with USCIS throughout the immigration process. CPMS provides USCIS along with ICE and CBP the capability to search for biometric and biographic information on immigrant applicants. Based on encounters at an Application Service Center (ASC), other locations around the globe and from benefit cards issued by USCIS systems, CPMS contains over 64 million identities, of which 27 million are derived from benefit cards, 4 million are derived from encounters without fingerprints, and the remainder are derived from encounters with full biometric data collection. Encounters with biometric matches are reported to IDENT to be shared among DHS components.','non-public','2026-03-22T11:51:27.421320','2026-03-22T11:51:27.421325','Unspecified','Open Data (MGMT)','024:030','49f96fa3-75df-46a0-98ce-2b4b4a30824b','DHS datajson source','89095a806172a5f85325c2c061116251e155e0670206d2098dd4fbc3f79bf38d','1.1','2026-03-22T11:51:27.421320','2026-03-22T11:51:27.421325',NULL,'024:000',0,'dhs-gov'),('d9227d95-cce2-4136-92a4-7e50ce441788','MER 1 MARS PANORAMIC CAMERA SOLAR RDR OPS V1.0','not applicable','public','2026-03-13T18:55:27.269690','2026-03-13T18:55:27.269695','Imaging','Planetary Data System','026:00','c00e1a7b-560f-4a74-935d-126dad861ed8','NASA Data.json','50b734086ca64d54665f7beca568f44bb7444169a290afee8c9d00f5a2a008e4','1.1','2026-03-13T18:55:27.269690','2026-03-13T18:55:27.269695','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('d94469b6-3a04-4be1-ae85-1c86c959d19c','GO JUP HIC SURVEY ENERGETIC ION COUNT RATE V1.0','This data set provides energetic (MeV) ion count rates and events        measured by the Heavy Ion Counter (HIC) instrument on the Galileo        spacecraft. The data are derived from the raw real-time science (RTS)        data.  There are two basic types of data files associated with the        full-rate reduced data: Detector Count Rates and Events        (Pulse Heights).','public','2026-03-13T18:32:17.186691','2026-03-13T18:32:17.186697','planetary plasma interactions','Planetary Data System','026:00','8ad3dd10-6391-426a-aee7-d5bed3a95bf5','NASA Data.json','f38287d4f42dbb27cf35b52a800232356e4cef0f635082132e47c3c2e113a0cf','1.1','2026-03-13T18:32:17.186691','2026-03-13T18:32:17.186697','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('d95880cd-73b5-43d0-aa7a-f404ff383467','DID(IT) - Position Data','ePulse contains data on USCIS vacancies and details.','non-public','2026-03-22T11:53:09.512289','2026-03-22T11:53:09.512294','Unspecified','Open Data (MGMT)','024:030','b9a10d5e-784f-47a3-a8c4-8513ec5755bf','DHS datajson source','6f52a8c9b497111aa013bdc99f8260549169e0c8df65d7996bc33a706008c910','1.1','2026-03-22T11:53:09.512289','2026-03-22T11:53:09.512294',NULL,'024:000',0,'dhs-gov'),('d96c218b-798f-4796-aab6-d764fe016d91','MARS EXPRESS MARS MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 4 3636 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2013-01-01 to 2014-12-31. It is a Global Gravity measurement and covers the time 2013-11-03T21:11:56.000 to 2013-11-04T00:08:08.500.','public','2026-03-13T19:08:21.095959','2026-03-13T19:08:21.095964','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','ce4014aa-cf27-41df-be60-a7fd6854e9a2','NASA Data.json','7a710ea4c8484c1bef172d432a4245b3ce20d2a5b55ba1ad5f3b842165b3f277','1.1','2026-03-13T19:08:21.095959','2026-03-13T19:08:21.095964','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('d96d2e03-b42e-43cc-9161-32b0e4b4b229','MARS EXPRESS MARS MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 4 3591 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2013-01-01 to 2014-12-31. It is a Global Gravity measurement and covers the time 2013-06-18T04:59:57.000 to 2013-06-18T07:05:01.500.','public','2026-03-13T19:19:08.717496','2026-03-13T19:19:08.717503','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','a506c364-ec1d-4eb8-833e-24ebce6e4794','NASA Data.json','cb0885e673c62ec6e049e826ae088057222393351da416aa45c6e0d8d2d8df2f','1.1','2026-03-13T19:19:08.717496','2026-03-13T19:19:08.717503','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('d96f74bc-cd43-4fba-b34f-4a2af2eeb561','GO JUPITER PWS EDITED EDR 1KHZ WAVEFORM RECEIVER V1.0','This data set includes wideband waveform measurements from the      Galileo plasma wave receiver obtained during Jupiter orbital      operations. These data were obtained during selected observation      periods near perijove, satellite encounters and other select times.      These measurements are electric waveforms obtained by rapidly      sampling the potential at the input to the receiver from the      electric dipole antenna.  The sample rates are 201,600/s, 25,200/s,      or 3,150/s taken through bandpass filters of 80, 10, or 1 kHz,      respectively.','public','2026-03-13T19:16:12.101743','2026-03-13T19:16:12.101748','planetary plasma interactions','Planetary Data System','026:00','0e522db7-c8a9-47b0-ae68-0d0e90126ef3','NASA Data.json','510ae5ff9c6926819f5f97a644ad7836e49bd36a67d3aa6e38848e0b80813fc7','1.1','2026-03-13T19:16:12.101743','2026-03-13T19:16:12.101748','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('d97068a1-28c6-4b5e-9280-c9df8f4b3fe9','ROSETTA-ORBITER PRELANDING OSINAC 3 RDR MTP001 V2.0','This data set contains images acquired by the OSIRIS Narrow Angle Camera during the PRELANDING phase of the Rosetta mission at the comet 67P, covering the period from 2014-01-20T10:00:00.000 to 2014-05-07T12:47:59.000. This version V2.0 supersedes previous deliveries of the same dataset.','public','2026-03-13T17:00:24.046000','2026-03-13T17:00:24.046004','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','c7d28321-58a0-488a-b0fe-955a7acb1bcb','NASA Data.json','de2862d539c5c91a0af1dcd08b6c67cca48e373bf81a8ecb350c029c6fac41c2','1.1','2026-03-13T17:00:24.046000','2026-03-13T17:00:24.046004','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('d971ac0b-c597-4aac-a0eb-8926b6341fc3','MARS EXPRESS MARS MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 7 4127 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2019-01-01 to 2020-12-31. It is a Occultation measurement and covers the time 2020-09-12T01:00:00.000 to 2020-09-12T01:50:00.000.','public','2026-03-13T19:45:13.702216','2026-03-13T19:45:13.702222','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','eda3bc70-2071-473a-b184-12f34f1f609c','NASA Data.json','1a1e3df0979d08a5b03bd750490623bec91dd8cabc64e08e3b8c23eb24d87f60','1.1','2026-03-13T19:45:13.702216','2026-03-13T19:45:13.702222','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('d99f2aff-409b-410b-ab9e-cfa64896a203','MSL CHEMCAM REMOTE MICRO IMAGING CAMERA EDR V1.0','The MSL ChemCam RMI EDR data set consists of all uncalibrated data collected by the ChemCam Remote Micro-Imager on the Mars Science Laboratory rover. The imager software inherited from Rosetta includes autoexposure algorithms, with typically four different exposures made, and the best image is kept. For a typical rock analysis scenario a full 1024x1024 pixel image is taken prior to LIBS analysis, and an image of only the analysis spot (e.g., 128x128) is taken subsequent to analysis.','public','2026-03-13T18:09:46.745661','2026-03-13T18:09:46.745666','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','9815edb8-c03a-4323-a4c6-7ad708dc6485','NASA Data.json','f0f255b8c0d279604818b9e62cd5761a605ffc8d436ab07fecf6455dd6da2975','1.1','2026-03-13T18:09:46.745661','2026-03-13T18:09:46.745666','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('d9a4da41-580c-47cf-b439-080c7ad528a4','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 4 1177 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 4 phase 2015-10-22 to 2015-12-31. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-11-12T20:25:40.000 to 2015-11-13T01:00:33.000.','public','2026-03-13T17:27:18.462224','2026-03-13T17:27:18.462231','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','630e441d-e555-4d9b-bb79-218c94374f68','NASA Data.json','4e036272641a01143eb78583d7635de819d90a1867819420d6db409df49ddd9a','1.1','2026-03-13T17:27:18.462224','2026-03-13T17:27:18.462231','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('d9a6751a-ce14-4c56-8258-a37e4845f7be','FIRST Front Porch Data','This data represents the FOIA requests made via the FIRST website along with the data returned to the requestor.','non-public','2026-03-22T11:52:39.100811','2026-03-22T11:52:39.100816','Unspecified','Open Data (MGMT)','024:030','a17ce0fa-bd88-4b1b-aded-8c0ff249d371','DHS datajson source','fe2cc0f1a9b5ae701404ff715ffe124e77f44ca1f86a8f34dfa5d6a53cbeef59','1.1','2026-03-22T11:52:39.100811','2026-03-22T11:52:39.100816',NULL,'024:000',0,'dhs-gov'),('da1fc4fb-e7b1-42cd-95b3-e9b9ec2dd52e','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSINAC 4 EXT1-MTP027 RDR-REFLECT V1.0','This CODMAC level 4 data set contains radiometric calibrated and geometric distortion corrected (resampled) image data in reflectance units (normalized and thus without unit), acquired by the OSIRIS Narrow Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft during the ROSETTA EXTENSION 1 mission phase, covering the period from 2016-03-08T23:25:00.000 to 2016-04-05T23:24:59.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V1.0 is the first version of this dataset: Lien corrected dataset after October 2018 PSA/PDS external peer review.','public','2026-03-13T20:06:20.871124','2026-03-13T20:06:20.871131','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','543d381b-98f0-46f9-b7a8-ecc86d364639','NASA Data.json','0a8148f562c09b960f580cd6636c3170563531d23d445d2a1428de99555ccbbe','1.1','2026-03-13T20:06:20.871124','2026-03-13T20:06:20.871131','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('da40adbb-9ca6-491e-857d-95a46663b2d5','BLM ID CADNSDI PLSS State Boundary Line','<div style=\'text-align:Left;font-size:12pt\'><div><div><p><span>This dataset portrays the state boundary based on the 2010 Cadastral National Spatial Data Infrastructure (CADNSDI) Geographic Coordinate Data Base (GCDB) distribution. The GCDB was acquired from a Premier Data contract in coordination with the BLM state GCDB Data Stewards to deliver a standardized GCDB product. This product would be capable, where GCDB data exists, to identify the State borders. Where GCDB data does not exist, in cases or rivers, lakes, and unsurveyed terrain, then alternative sources were used to identify the state boundary. Alternative sources include original 24K USGS Maps and US Forest Service Cartographic Feature File (CFF) PLSS data.</span></p></div></div></div>','public','2026-03-18T11:11:22.046361','2026-03-18T11:11:22.046368','Bureau of Land Management','Bureau of Land Management, blm_id_stateoffice','010:04','b91b64af-4f02-4ece-b3a2-5b09aebce27b','DOI BLM DCAT-US','db52b38563531bb9f72b15fc0be557421a7feb12d5d6e7ebaa7e45eb6a7508fc','1.1','2026-03-18T11:11:22.046361','2026-03-18T11:11:22.046368','geospatial','010:000',0,'doi-gov'),('da6d9b13-0116-4e99-af9f-41c2e60b7f0b','VG2 NEP CRS RESAMPLED SUMMARY D2 RATE ELEC 96SEC V1.0','Counting rate from the D2 detector in the Cosmic Ray      System (CRS) electron telescope (TET) on Voyager 2 during      the Neptune encounter.      The D2 detector nominally responds to      electrons with kinetic energies above approximately 2.5 MeV      (see detector description for details).','public','2026-03-13T17:57:33.395655','2026-03-13T17:57:33.395661','planetary plasma interactions','Planetary Data System','026:00','ef396c19-019a-4325-a756-5d8ae6971ea0','NASA Data.json','243bbd7e780fb89b38ee38c5816c6484078d36b6f0e444bf1e9c6291dafac01d','1.1','2026-03-13T17:57:33.395655','2026-03-13T17:57:33.395661','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('da9ff444-56e5-42b0-905e-df7f13422fd0','ASTEROID DENSITIES','This data set contains a tabulation of asteroid masses, diameters, and bulk densities compiled by D. T. Britt and published in Table 1 of Britt, et al. (2002) [BRITTETAL2002] in the \'Asteroids III\' volume.','public','2026-03-13T16:54:03.359708','2026-03-13T16:54:03.359713','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','e1e38296-4fee-4477-814a-38d28fe6b9b2','NASA Data.json','8fd73520c67abe758396af4a37afc93d31fb714f51878c3050ae65aa799fc367','1.1','2026-03-13T16:54:03.359708','2026-03-13T16:54:03.359713','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('daa6c687-e281-41c8-a78e-7d37e9efec29','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 2 0769 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 2 phase 2015-03-11 to 2015-06-30. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-05-12T12:09:40.000 to 2015-05-12T15:17:18.500.','public','2026-03-13T19:26:52.517883','2026-03-13T19:26:52.517890','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','3ad2936e-04df-4b75-a6cc-7e85509b2938','NASA Data.json','29b435db88f842093d42e5a8d8a4351c6b53762a437ad97c43fd6626c7e61376','1.1','2026-03-13T19:26:52.517883','2026-03-13T19:26:52.517890','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('daca9c45-6738-4532-a8f9-6a3df51e8006','(41033 / FRP2) Fripp Nearshore, NC','Timeseries data from \'(41033 / FRP2) Fripp Nearshore, NC\' (org_cormp_frp2)','public','2026-03-26T19:16:40.757257','2026-03-26T19:16:40.757264',NULL,NULL,NULL,'8020bd0c-1e78-4a64-aaa6-f3d87bb5b41f','ioos',NULL,NULL,'2026-03-26T19:16:40.757257','2026-03-26T19:16:40.757264',NULL,NULL,NULL,'noaa-gov'),('dacd84a2-e74f-4319-95c7-90cab955a7f8','Okeanos Explorer (EX1601): Transit and Mission Patch							Test','Normal underway operations and mapping patch testing.\n					Bathymetric mapping of either the Murray or Molokai Fracture Zones during the\n					transit to Hawaii is planned, as allowed by equipment shakedown priorities and\n					prevailing sea conditions. CTD casts may be requested at strategic locations\n					along the fracture zone. New equipment in need of shakedown testing includes a\n					new Very Small Aperture Terminal (VSAT) antenna, a new Keyboard-Video-Monitor\n					(KVM) system, new Doppler speed log, four new EK 60 single beam sonars, two new\n					ADCPs, new digital file storage systems, and a newly installed Underway\n					CTD.','public','2026-03-28T23:17:12.056479','2026-03-28T23:17:12.056487',NULL,NULL,NULL,'68cd9a03-3616-4165-aea6-0e6f198d8cd7','NCDDC OER',NULL,NULL,'2026-03-28T23:17:12.056479','2026-03-28T23:17:12.056487',NULL,NULL,NULL,'noaa-gov'),('daf20e3f-387f-4480-8cb3-a6519b1823a0','CCD OBSERVATIONS V1.0','Charged Coupled Device (CCD) cameras from ESO were used by groups to observe the outburst of comet Halley using a variety of telescopes and chip sets.','public','2026-03-13T18:18:56.884401','2026-03-13T18:18:56.884407','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','4bbca4ff-06fc-4cc3-b639-07a5dbdd436f','NASA Data.json','005ef1428fcf3329af2a01bf0638695c1ac8a60ada6a3d294428708ae894b7a9','1.1','2026-03-13T18:18:56.884401','2026-03-13T18:18:56.884407','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('db2dbcbd-dc07-461e-8c6f-4c0f79bfa71a','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSINAC 4 ESC1-MTP013 RDR-STR-REFL V1.0','This CODMAC level 4 data set contains solar stray light corrected, radiometric calibrated and geometric distortion corrected (resampled) image data in in reflectance units (normalized and thus without unit), acquired by the OSIRIS Narrow Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft during the COMET ESCORT 1 mission phase, covering the period from 2015-02-10T23:25:00.000 to 2015-03-10T23:24:59.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V1.0 is the first version of this dataset: Lien corrected dataset after October 2018 PSA/PDS external peer review.','public','2026-03-13T19:04:05.074503','2026-03-13T19:04:05.074508','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','e1a1d2d5-42b0-4c9b-bc51-6494ecfc6f83','NASA Data.json','dd4adc7cd8a5ca1f8ccd35309b13b76f1f87be350d40b753b216251ff23460e2','1.1','2026-03-13T19:04:05.074503','2026-03-13T19:04:05.074508','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('db44c919-ce8e-4ea0-b704-5333d1f4706a','Coastal Mapping Program of  Port of Weedon Island/St. Petersburg, FL, FL2322B-CS-N','These data provide an accurate high-resolution shoreline compiled from imagery of  Port of Weedon Island/St. Petersburg, FL .  This vector shoreline data is based on an office interpretation of imagery that may be suitable as a geographic information system (GIS) data layer. This metadata describes information for both the line and point shapefiles. The NGS attribution scheme \'Coastal Cartographic Object Attribute Source Table (C-COAST)\' was developed to conform the attribution of various sources of shoreline data into one attribution catalog. C-COAST is not a recognized standard, but was influenced by the International Hydrographic Organization\'s S-57 Object-Attribute standard so the data would be more accurately translated into S-57.  This resource is a member of  https://inport.nmfs.noaa.gov/inport/item/39808','public','2026-03-19T20:04:20.871882','2026-03-19T20:04:20.871889',NULL,NULL,NULL,'74e0f69c-48c1-4deb-8766-6e90a05ed180','NOS NGS',NULL,NULL,'2026-03-19T20:04:20.871882','2026-03-19T20:04:20.871889',NULL,NULL,NULL,'noaa-gov'),('db66c886-2715-43c4-bec4-55556a69a8eb','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 4 1198 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 4 phase 2015-10-22 to 2015-12-31. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-11-21T22:12:05.000 to 2015-11-22T04:28:41.000.','public','2026-03-13T17:41:34.560543','2026-03-13T17:41:34.560550','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','211459c2-ecca-48a4-9916-c8c1084ac371','NASA Data.json','468c444223933b0453e7bc13b3377f349b8832cad5de81a74dd6abc4fd24bdae','1.1','2026-03-13T17:41:34.560543','2026-03-13T17:41:34.560550','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('db7b3dbf-4a54-44aa-99f6-1a4e9102c073','Accident Type (including Highway-Rail Crossings) (3.08)','This is the page for Accident Type (including Highway-Rail Crossings) (3.08).','public','2026-03-24T12:08:50.290376','2026-03-26T12:43:40.176671','Federal Railroad Administration','FRA Safety Data Team','021:27','1663b03f-1411-488b-abdf-e0c1a7dbf2db','DOT Socrata Data.json','53ebd80794f58e1f1284341c6ac094697b90229f1e4c7d2ac01eb63e55826931','1.1','2026-03-24T12:08:50.290376','2026-03-26T12:43:40.176671','Railroads','021:037',0,'dot-gov'),('db87c7ae-8f99-482e-ba62-7a07501418a1','RIVKIN THREE MICRON ASTEROID DATA V3.0','This data set is a collection of 3-micron spectra of 33 asteroids and Phobos and Deimos obtained by Andy Rivkin and collaborators. Nearly all these data have been published.','public','2026-03-13T19:07:03.468017','2026-03-13T19:07:03.468023','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','9fd9d8db-7dbd-43c8-9fa3-cbf8864845c0','NASA Data.json','ba9c7d7bd17f78b84e7a7c7daf1ab5d1af3538f253bf641c9638ea7859b315be','1.1','2026-03-13T19:07:03.468017','2026-03-13T19:07:03.468023','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('db970258-99d0-46e5-8897-5c040f633f30','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 2 0821 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 2 phase 2015-03-11 to 2015-06-30. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-06-01T09:28:15.000 to 2015-06-01T14:36:32.000.','public','2026-03-13T19:14:58.910219','2026-03-13T19:14:58.910224','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','1b11e608-5f68-4aa4-9ec0-bbecd7cf0ee3','NASA Data.json','763a6d484fca6749833b9023a83dd630a14fd6abd740da6dff863132983cd14d','1.1','2026-03-13T19:14:58.910219','2026-03-13T19:14:58.910224','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('dccdd2e6-bcc0-406d-95c7-6befb3ab2aaa','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSINAC 4 EXT2-MTP030 RDR-REFLECT V1.0','This CODMAC level 4 data set contains radiometric calibrated and geometric distortion corrected (resampled) image data in reflectance units (normalized and thus without unit), acquired by the OSIRIS Narrow Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft during the ROSETTA EXTENSION 2 mission phase, covering the period from 2016-05-31T23:25:00.000 to 2016-06-28T23:24:59.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V1.0 is the first version of this dataset: Lien corrected dataset after October 2018 PSA/PDS external peer review.','public','2026-03-13T19:33:00.402300','2026-03-13T19:33:00.402305','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','cd203c97-932d-4574-9d38-2f6e6114fb8e','NASA Data.json','b850a89efe28375601804933b5de9d8966859cf0d4c496c3d696639a88e99da8','1.1','2026-03-13T19:33:00.402300','2026-03-13T19:33:00.402305','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('dccf1727-d92b-4e89-82ac-d8d7657ff5c6','Estuarine and Nearshore Marine Sediment Quality Measurements in Timucuan Ecological and Historic Preserve (2008)','This dataset represents sediment quality measurements that were taken in Timucuan Ecological and Historic Preserve during 2008 as a part of the marine water and sediment quality assessment protocol that was developed by the Southeast Coast I&M Network (SECN). The protocol is modeled after the EPA\'s National Coastal Assessment Program (www.epa.gov/emap/nca) and it consists of conducting sediment sampling every 10 years based on a probabilistic sampling design that was also designed by the EPA. Thirty sites were selected within the Nassau River, Pumpkin Hill Creek, Intracoastal Waterway (Sisters Creek), Cedar Point Creek, Clapboard Creek, Pablo Creek, and St. Johns River at which sediments were sampled using a Van Veen sampler and composited for analysis as described in the National Coastal Assessment Quality Assurance Project Plan (www.epa.gov/emap/nca/html/docs/qaprojplan.html). The final analyses of the sediment samples were conducted by GPL Laboratories, LLC (now Centauri Labs); please refer to their website (www.centaurilabs.com) or the documents listed in the Cross Reference section for more information about the analytical process. Please note that each sampling location contains multiple sediment parameters that are recorded individually.','public','2026-03-26T05:31:55.605370','2026-03-26T05:31:55.605375','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','3994cb27-5100-418a-b1f3-46c82ca857e8','DOI NPS DCAT-US','fcc1c4c05058bddc7e506f0cba42738041328bb497ceacbcd253e02dbe253906','1.1','2026-03-26T05:31:55.605370','2026-03-26T05:31:55.605375','Vector Dataset','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('dce4f542-6548-4183-9500-23cf0629e34f','MARS EXPRESS MARS PFS EDR FIRST EXTENSION MISSION DATA V1.0','The Mars Express PFS data set contains raw (CODMAC Level 2) measurements from the Planetary Fourier Spectrometer collected during the first extension Mars orbit phases.','public','2026-03-13T18:35:46.283843','2026-03-13T18:35:46.283851','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','b67ab876-e230-4643-9117-3894f55e6d74','NASA Data.json','d2e694e0955409392e7ef5597a2e3e108fd03f90fb340a5422fa4e99772c50e0','1.1','2026-03-13T18:35:46.283843','2026-03-13T18:35:46.283851','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('dce93878-d873-4246-9ad6-d02af76bc2f4','MO MARS RADIO SCIENCE 1 ORIGINAL/INTERMEDIATE DATA REC V1.0','The data set consists of several CD-WO volumes which contain radiometric and open loop data acquired from the Mars Observer spacecraft during its Cruise between Earth and Mars. The basic data are supplemented by ancillary data including DSN weather files and media calibrations, spacecraft maneuver information, and operations schedules. There are fourteen data types.','public','2026-03-13T16:44:51.537412','2026-03-13T16:44:51.537420','Engineering','Planetary Data System','026:00','b4f77b72-7a5a-43ac-88d7-77566f0785fe','NASA Data.json','b4b4b6b520798b0ca959b34c86597c5c1bbb09644f9ae2580f5840712b1497d2','1.1','2026-03-13T16:44:51.537412','2026-03-13T16:44:51.537420','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('dcfed4ab-ba98-4c01-b104-7de408c47301','Monthly Enrollment - Test0318','test','public','2026-03-20T17:38:37.163747','2026-03-20T17:38:37.163751','Centers for Medicare & Medicaid Services','Medicaid.gov','009:38','ae1c822c-c95f-4d0a-97c8-971c2d7474a0','Healthdata.gov','984cfc3a57a6999870514e500f8d252d8086fb7b0749a6384dd7133e4ef6045a','1.1','2026-03-20T17:38:37.163747','2026-03-20T17:38:37.163751','Enrollment','009:076',0,'hhs-gov'),('dd2a249b-7dd2-469d-97b6-75e20a605dff','Parking Violations Issued in February 2026','<p>Parking citation locations in the District of Columbia. The <a href=\'https://visionzero.dc.gov\' target=\'_blank\' rel=\'nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer\'>Vision Zero</a> data contained in this layer pertain to parking violations issued by the District of Columbia\'s Metropolitan Police Department (MPD) and partner agencies with the authority. For example, the District Department of Transportation\'s (DDOT) traffic control officers write parking violations to prevent congestion through enforcement and control at intersections. Parking violation locations are summarized ticket counts based on time of day, week of year, year, and category of violation. Data was originally extracted from the District Department of Motor Vehicle\'s eTIMS meter work order management system. Data was then loaded into the DC GIS, where the Office of the Chief Technology Officer (OCTO) geocoded citation data to the street segment level. Data are visualized using the street segment centroid coordinates.</p>','public','2026-03-25T08:06:38.232359','2026-03-25T08:06:38.232364','District Department of Transportation','DCGISopendata',NULL,'08909633-3c0a-43e5-9c51-56abe696ee18','DC data','0a18cb13ffa042552983f0bed6dde7cbb405cfe97fd376ee40ff70a2c9ba5f7d','1.1','2026-03-25T08:06:38.232359','2026-03-25T08:06:38.232364','geospatial',NULL,0,'district-of-columbia'),('dd94a57e-6166-4823-9f0d-447dbcf4b6a9','Continuous Fixed Station Water Quality Measurements in Canaveral National Seashore, February 2009 (Certified)','This dataset represents continuous water quality measurements that were taken at a fixed point in Canaveral National Seashore during the month of February, 2009 as a part of the Fixed Station Water Quality Monitoring protocol that was developed by the Southeast Coast I&M Network (SECN). The measurements were taken by a YSI 6600 ESD Multi-Parameter Long Term Water Quality Monitoring Datasonde unit that serves as the standard fixed station water quality monitoring equipment for all similar operations conducted by the SECN. The following parameters were measured at 30 minute intervals during the time period that has been specified: Water Temperature, Specific Conductivity, Salinity, Dissolved Oxygen (DO), DO Concentration, Shallow Depth, pH Level, and Turbidity. Any anomalies noted regarding these parameters have also been noted in separate fields. Please note that these measurements have been certified by network personnel.','public','2026-03-26T05:32:33.272632','2026-03-26T05:32:33.272637','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','d6195f0b-9f62-4098-9939-ea2d25163d09','DOI NPS DCAT-US','54ebf23d068af80434d857cecf94c263426ca8e8a3a23364e04f73bc60a82b86','1.1','2026-03-26T05:32:33.272632','2026-03-26T05:32:33.272637','Vector Dataset','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('dda01218-0c6d-4b43-b21d-020ffc7a6c9a','ROSETTA-ORBITER X SREM 5 EARTH 1 V1.0','This data set contains derived electron and proton flux energies in MeV from the Standard Radiation Environment Monitor (SREM) instrument on the Rosetta spacecraft. These are CODMAC Level 5 derived data, and measure the radiation in the spacecraft environment during the EARTH 1 mission phase.','public','2026-03-13T18:30:37.226411','2026-03-13T18:30:37.226416','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','ab0ce1ca-f7bf-4b21-b754-da645912ea1b','NASA Data.json','b2522aad262412b23fdc3585509a64a100cb66a5352de84aedcd369537618de3','1.1','2026-03-13T18:30:37.226411','2026-03-13T18:30:37.226416','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('ddb806b2-0219-4dae-aac9-d2e6a61189ba','MEX EXT6 SPICAM MARS CLEANED IR RDR V1.0','The Mars Express SPICAM level 1A IR data set contains clean measurements from the infrared SPICAM spectrometer collected during the nominal MARS phases','public','2026-03-13T18:43:48.082229','2026-03-13T18:43:48.082233','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','efd31cd2-c83b-4d52-bb11-6a73de40455a','NASA Data.json','ae5c68a3fd4fe1e932a74c17f0d96509f6071524a4cfbb99e83dcc3bb5611424','1.1','2026-03-13T18:43:48.082229','2026-03-13T18:43:48.082233','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('ddbbd069-b3f8-48fb-a31e-670aed2cb226','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P ROSINA 2 ESC3 V2.0','This data set contains CODMAC level 2 science data acquired by the COPS, DFMS and RTOF ROSINA sensors between 2015-07-01 and 2015-10-20 during the Escort phase 3 of the Rosetta mission at the comet 67P/CG. V2.0 : Some missing DFMS PDS files were added and corrupted files have been removed.','public','2026-03-13T18:53:23.247418','2026-03-13T18:53:23.247424','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','d556c493-a7f3-4304-8639-164fc33ce375','NASA Data.json','303e669fd147dc427dc48b26342f78d96674e50a92887ff1874b55529c03f880','1.1','2026-03-13T18:53:23.247418','2026-03-13T18:53:23.247424','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('ddca0c02-f9fd-47dd-82bd-c50980106b9f','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSIWAC 4 ESC3-MTP021 RDR-STRLIGHT V1.0','This CODMAC level 4 data set contains solar stray light corrected, radiometric calibrated and geometric distortion corrected (resampled) image data in W/m^2/sr/nm, acquired by the OSIRIS Wide Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft during the COMET ESCORT 3 mission phase, covering the period from 2015-09-22T23:25:00.000 to 2015-10-20T23:24:59.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V1.0 is the first version of this dataset: Lien corrected dataset after October 2018 PSA/PDS external peer review.','public','2026-03-13T17:56:02.088921','2026-03-13T17:56:02.088926','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','0b4a9f68-fa08-4ad6-8e97-d52d2dbd4273','NASA Data.json','35bc08102f2b49cdff72cd68e701aa2db565a2479d65d7e0047cd7de5728b487','1.1','2026-03-13T17:56:02.088921','2026-03-13T17:56:02.088926','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('de395cbb-eb44-43dd-b770-9dafccf1fd2e','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 PRELANDING 0387 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the PRELANDING phase 2014-01-21 to 2014-11-18. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2014-10-26T04:02:05.000 to 2014-10-26T14:37:06.500.','public','2026-03-13T17:15:54.764793','2026-03-13T17:15:54.764798','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','17b691b0-621d-46af-b631-2ebe22811970','NASA Data.json','9f8f120af4100ee6084ae63f5390bb9194b842f50da8c1274ca1466bff042bd5','1.1','2026-03-13T17:15:54.764793','2026-03-13T17:15:54.764798','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('de7e830e-5bc0-470b-90fe-30e2170cd405','GO JUPITER EPD REFORMATTED HIGH RES SECTOR V1.0','This data set contains two versions of three different data file  types.  One version is a corrected form of the other (\'C\').  The  corrected data are adjusted for minute gaps in between the detector  cycles.  This data ranges from the Io flyby (December 1995) to end of  mission. All available motor positions are provided.  Step 0, which  looks behind the background shield, is included for an indication of  the background penetration of the detector.  The rates reported are in  units of (counts/sec), pitch and phase angles are in (radians). The  sectors are ordered in time','public','2026-03-13T18:37:48.739939','2026-03-13T18:37:48.739947','planetary plasma interactions','Planetary Data System','026:00','58ea4862-e50f-4026-a06d-b212610d8631','NASA Data.json','994b05c9b903aa895e423fe2374ad10d8c032762304811e31b8b6e5a5383b635','1.1','2026-03-13T18:37:48.739939','2026-03-13T18:37:48.739947','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('de9a9839-26fd-4e02-be98-1cc571f99a95','Peregrine Falcon Predicted Habitat - CWHR B129 [ds2099]','<div style=\'text-align:Left;\'><div><div><p><span>CWHR Predicted Habitat Models represent areas of predicted suitable habitat for each species within its range. These models are built from the following principal inputs: </span></p><p><span>1) a statewide, best-available vegetation map (FVEG);  </span></p><p><span>2) GIS data representing a species’ range;  </span></p><p><span>3) the CWHR database of habitat suitability values for over 700 terrestrial vertebrate species. </span></p><p><span>Habitat suitability ranks of Low (non-zero values less than 0.34), Medium (0.34-0.66), and High (greater than 0.66) are based on the maximum suitability value across the 3 species life requisites: reproduction, feeding, and cover. Note that previous versions of these Predicted Habitat Models used an average across the 3 life requisites in order to obtain an overall suitability score for each habitat type and stage class.  Habitat suitability scores were developed based on habitat patch sizes greater than 40 acres in size and are best interpreted for habitat patches greater than 200 acres in size. The FVEG landcover dataset is an aggregation of multiple statewide landcover and regional vegetation mapping efforts, conducted at different points in time (approximately 1990 up to time of publishing) and at various resolutions, compiled by the California Department of Forestry and Fire Protection (CALFIRE). FVEG uses the most current and consistent data available for each region of the state. Decision rules were developed that controlled which layers were given priority in areas of overlap. Crosswalks were used to attribute the various data sources according to the CWHR habitat-type classification system. Attributing FVEG with CWHR habitat types allows for the extraction of areas with non-zero suitability values for each species within the bounds of its range, creating a series of maps of predicted suitable habitat which are species-specific. Because FVEG is an amalgam of disparate landcover assessment efforts across the state, the predictive power for determining suitable habitat will vary between species, and possibly even regionally for species which are widely distributed. While these maps represent CDFW’s best estimate of the presence of suitable habitat for any given species in the CWHR system, these maps are also limited by several factors: 1) the accuracy and resolution of vegetation maps in a given region; 2) the dynamic nature of the landscape in which fire and other disturbance events alter conditions at a greater frequency than mapping efforts can track; 3) the currency of expert knowledge, particularly as species adapt to changing land and climate conditions and the shifting of other species’ ranges; 4) the frequency of species-specific surveys across a representative sample of a species’ entire range; 5) metapopulation dynamics, which describes the shifting of populations within their environment as result of numerous types of interactions and responses. </span></p><p><span>CWHR GIS data representing predicted suitable habitat should not be used to indicate the presence or absence of a particular species at any specific site. CWHR predicted habitat models are named according to the 4-character alpha-numeric CWHR ID assigned to each species (5 characters in the case of subspecies or other sub-taxa). There is also a “CWHR Revision Tracking Table” containing a record for each species, its CWHR ID, scientific name, common name, and range and habitat model data revision history. CWHR species range models, predicted habitat models, and GIS data of the statewide distribution of all CWHR habitat types, along with the CWHR revision tracking table, are available for download at </span><a href=\'https://www.wildlife.ca.gov/Data/CWHR\' target=\'_blank\' style=\'text-decoration:underline;\' rel=\'nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer\'><span>https://www.wildlife.ca.gov/Data/CWHR</span></a><span>. </span></p></div></div></div>','public','2026-03-23T13:53:13.289271','2026-03-23T13:53:13.289276','California Department of Fish and Wildlife','BIOS_Admin',NULL,'bc928cef-1023-4d8e-8a4c-87199fb707ca','State of California','e18d26583e1b5fce87987e8d61de90b13e015ade2ae097d22416db98b568d909','1.1','2026-03-23T13:53:13.289271','2026-03-23T13:53:13.289276','Natural Resources',NULL,0,'ca-gov'),('deb6f41d-2dac-49ac-8b20-c073a445993d','ODYSSEY THEMIS VIS GEO V2.0','The THEMIS VIS-GEO data set contains the spatially registered, visible images derived from the calibrated radiance (VIS-RDR) products. Each image file is accompanied by a detached PDS label describing the data format, contents, and processing history.','public','2026-03-13T16:56:18.575075','2026-03-13T16:56:18.575080','Imaging','Planetary Data System','026:00','338ac5e7-fd0a-4397-bb64-6210f2ec4d5f','NASA Data.json','56d35205839f714b5ab8fed5dbdca4dd47c7b6100c314ba9e39ca80ca067b85b','1.1','2026-03-13T16:56:18.575075','2026-03-13T16:56:18.575080','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('def7e5c2-5ea3-4aa7-aa59-45571ddb70b9','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 1 0574 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 1 phase 2014-11-20 to 2015-03-10. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-02-11T01:55:55.000 to 2015-02-11T10:32:28.000.','public','2026-03-13T18:46:43.709708','2026-03-13T18:46:43.709716','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','2a1fdecd-fb89-49dc-a60a-c67dbf303a2b','NASA Data.json','521dfa32003d538758d691aeb6c67cb38044450cbd7cd275946d85c30e58cfcc','1.1','2026-03-13T18:46:43.709708','2026-03-13T18:46:43.709716','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('defa85c5-ed1a-4326-aa3f-7cc01854fdb6','MEX EXT 4 SPICAM MARS IR EDR-RAW V1.0','The Mars Express SPICAM level 0B IR data set contains raw measurements from the infrared SPICAM spectrometer collected during the extension 4 MARS phases','public','2026-03-13T17:11:11.521788','2026-03-13T17:11:11.521796','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','b4524622-c75b-4470-8d03-063f2b12aa7d','NASA Data.json','1ef9a59eb20bf273098f1ace6e8341f9b261e5b347fd21d0a6884f2c2db0833e','1.1','2026-03-13T17:11:11.521788','2026-03-13T17:11:11.521796','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('df011ccd-687a-4695-9649-6bd3bc3bf50b','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 3 1067 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 3 phase 2015-07-01 to 2015-10-21. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-09-29T21:00:55.000 to 2015-09-30T00:17:26.000.','public','2026-03-13T20:05:42.648399','2026-03-13T20:05:42.648405','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','170ab189-f65f-4aaa-9b62-bdc80188ec2d','NASA Data.json','b366905ac55c191df87600f9fba6f966d57c26958abd00b91cfb636246592f14','1.1','2026-03-13T20:05:42.648399','2026-03-13T20:05:42.648405','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('df24f687-7501-4c2d-8911-394d0c792570','SRFCEA Array, Station RBHW4, Bottom Temperature','Timeseries data from \'SRFCEA Array, Station RBHW4, Bottom Temperature\' (org_secoora_srfcea_rbhw4)','public','2026-03-26T19:16:59.406176','2026-03-26T19:16:59.406182',NULL,NULL,NULL,'e832bd2f-5730-416b-9287-78dccf3680c6','ioos',NULL,NULL,'2026-03-26T19:16:59.406176','2026-03-26T19:16:59.406182',NULL,NULL,NULL,'noaa-gov'),('df47f9fd-24f1-4393-b2f7-e0938f96485e','Continuous Fixed Station Water Quality Measurements in Timucuan Ecological and Historic Preserve, November 2008 (Certified)','This dataset represents continuous water quality measurements that were taken at a fixed point just outside of Timucuan Ecological and Historic Preserve during the month of November, 2008 as a part of the Fixed Station Water Quality Monitoring protocol that was developed by the Southeast Coast I&M Network (SECN). The measurements were taken by a YSI 6600 ESD Multi-Parameter Long Term Water Quality Monitoring Datasonde unit that serves as the standard fixed station water quality monitoring equipment for all similar operations conducted by the SECN. The following parameters were measured at 30 minute intervals during the time period that has been specified: Water Temperature, Specific Conductivity, Salinity, Dissolved Oxygen (DO), DO Concentration, Shallow Depth, pH Level, and Turbidity. Any anomalies noted regarding these parameters have also been noted in separate fields. Please note that these measurements have been certified by network personnel.','public','2026-03-26T05:34:02.494173','2026-03-26T05:34:02.494179','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','fbd0e4a5-922e-47b5-94c9-a795cfd2ee50','DOI NPS DCAT-US','cc38d77573ccc4c01f701e022777532ed2f5579f35b773486e9e4e37a36caba0','1.1','2026-03-26T05:34:02.494173','2026-03-26T05:34:02.494179','Vector Dataset','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('df4d67c3-05a8-4a09-bedc-3e3a4bb7e8a2','NEAR NIS SPECTRA FOR EROS/ORBIT','This data set contains the NEAR infrared spectrometer (NIS) data for the EROS/ORBIT phase. The data set begins on 2000-01-11T00:00:00.000 and ends 2001-02-12T23:59:59.999 . The data are raw telemetry data, provided in engineering units, that have been reformatted into FITS file format (NASA Office of Science and Technology (NOST), 100-1.0). In addition to the raw spectrometer data, a calibration file and algorithm are available. This data set is archived as a set of CDROM images as a part of the NEAR EDR volume set.','public','2026-03-13T17:48:37.353678','2026-03-13T17:48:37.353683','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','00167bf9-e83a-4f9b-825f-b689f9584d88','NASA Data.json','a2c492fe1211587f3b411f593d71edf62cb3e3a951ba345d34806b8239af9d7a','1.1','2026-03-13T17:48:37.353678','2026-03-13T17:48:37.353683','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('dfae8269-b3a3-48e1-b9f6-62dfc231704b','Ecosys EcoMapDomains 2025','<DIV STYLE=\"text-align:Left;\"><DIV><P><SPAN>The Ecomap 2025 contains a feature class for five different levels of the National Hierarchical Framework of Ecological Units (the Hierarchy. FSM 2060): Ecological Domains, Ecological Divisions, Ecological Provinces, Ecological Sections, and Ecological Subsections. The Ecomap 2025 data set describes the ecological hierarchy within the conterminous United States. Each feature class contains polygons attributed with the code and name of the ecological unit along with the codes and names of broader scale units into which a given ecological unit is nested. It contains regional geographic delineations for analysis of ecological relationships across ecological units. ECOMAP is the term used for a USDA Forest Service initiative to map ecological units and encourage their use in ecosystem-based approaches to forest and range land conservation and management. This is a collaborative effort with many partners. It is coordinated at the national and regional levels by USDA Forest Service staff and implemented in cooperation with State forestry agencies and others. ECOMAP mapping criteria are outlined in the National Hierarchical Framework of Ecological Units (Cleland et al. 1997, FSM 2060). The framework systematically divides the country into progressively smaller areas that have similar geophysical and biological characteristics and ecological processes.</SPAN></P></DIV></DIV>','public','2026-03-13T22:49:38.956844','2026-03-13T22:49:38.956853','U.S. Forest Service','USFSEnterpriseContent','005:96','7d3d72c6-752b-49e2-9759-ea4c2f9dd6e2','USDA JSON','d51b797ba1e7bd4536a71b112768dcf888dcf20b0233b802c740d5587e6fc83c','1.1','2026-03-13T22:49:38.956844','2026-03-13T22:49:38.956853','geospatial','005:059',0,'usda-gov'),('dfc5a27d-9527-4377-bf38-73cd4e237285','Continuous Fixed Station Water Quality Measurements in Canaveral National Seashore, September 2008 (Certified)','This dataset represents continuous water quality measurements that were taken at a fixed point in Canaveral National Seashore during the month of September, 2008 as a part of the Fixed Station Water Quality Monitoring protocol that was developed by the Southeast Coast I&M Network (SECN). The measurements were taken by a YSI 6600 ESD Multi-Parameter Long Term Water Quality Monitoring Datasonde unit that serves as the standard fixed station water quality monitoring equipment for all similar operations conducted by the SECN. The following parameters were measured at 30 minute intervals during the time period that has been specified: Water Temperature, Specific Conductivity, Salinity, Dissolved Oxygen (DO), DO Concentration, Shallow Depth, pH Level, and Turbidity. Any anomalies noted regarding these parameters have also been noted in separate fields. Please note that these measurements have been certified by network personnel.','public','2026-03-26T05:32:01.986873','2026-03-26T05:32:01.986878','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','353c043a-1739-4e8a-8b01-7cb8613a6ed2','DOI NPS DCAT-US','f943438b36d9481c40e4ade0a7afdf4fc61ca7f4e11134e288266d7e9ab28a76','1.1','2026-03-26T05:32:01.986873','2026-03-26T05:32:01.986878','Vector Dataset','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('dfd132d6-d34c-4e1c-b859-60d1ad6ba1c8','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 3 1017 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 3 phase 2015-07-01 to 2015-10-21. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-09-06T10:06:30.000 to 2015-09-06T17:30:25.000.','public','2026-03-13T19:34:47.085955','2026-03-13T19:34:47.085963','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','6dcb491e-035f-4b5c-913b-1c9e8661369c','NASA Data.json','fdd0699b3e983eeef673ce2ad0768296f8f05544f467b10f72402e0105d46e7a','1.1','2026-03-13T19:34:47.085955','2026-03-13T19:34:47.085963','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('dfe6ab02-6b7a-4b31-a5f0-286752f28977','Continuous Fixed Station Water Quality Measurements in Canaveral National Seashore, October 2005 (Certified)','This dataset represents continuous water quality measurements that were taken at a fixed point in Canaveral National Seashore during the month of October, 2005 as a part of the Fixed Station Water Quality Monitoring protocol that was developed by the Southeast Coast I&M Network (SECN). The measurements were taken by a YSI 6600 ESD Multi-Parameter Long Term Water Quality Monitoring Datasonde unit that serves as the standard fixed station water quality monitoring equipment for all similar operations conducted by the SECN. The following parameters were measured at 30 minute intervals during the time period that has been specified: Water Temperature, Specific Conductivity, Salinity, Dissolved Oxygen (DO), DO Concentration, Shallow Depth, pH Level, and Turbidity. Any anomalies noted regarding these parameters have also been noted in separate fields. Please note that these measurements have been certified by network personnel.','public','2026-03-26T05:29:13.350075','2026-03-26T05:29:13.350079','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','80fb77ae-4eaa-4f90-9deb-5161daa06db2','DOI NPS DCAT-US','1ba142c0e9932e4c92e0ce3a4116a69c98c05e49d6b88d185cae67cfb4531e9f','1.1','2026-03-26T05:29:13.350075','2026-03-26T05:29:13.350079','Vector Dataset','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('e01016a8-c9be-4461-8d65-449c991a6772','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 1 0492 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 1 phase 2014-11-20 to 2015-03-10. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2014-12-17T03:34:15.000 to 2014-12-17T12:51:56.000.','public','2026-03-13T17:23:56.189325','2026-03-13T17:23:56.189335','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','565d9846-eee2-4095-9a2d-9b11d99c49cf','NASA Data.json','f2a6e4f6c0ac0b09e526987dd43a333750a8952c040c0dfe0da71ab64269c77f','1.1','2026-03-13T17:23:56.189325','2026-03-13T17:23:56.189335','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('e014625b-3964-4fb6-8155-3dbc7b53db87','Continuous Fixed Station Water Quality Measurements in Canaveral National Seashore, January 2006 (Certified)','This dataset represents continuous water quality measurements that were taken at a fixed point in Canaveral National Seashore during the month of January, 2006 as a part of the Fixed Station Water Quality Monitoring protocol that was developed by the Southeast Coast I&M Network (SECN). The measurements were taken by a YSI 6600 ESD Multi-Parameter Long Term Water Quality Monitoring Datasonde unit that serves as the standard fixed station water quality monitoring equipment for all similar operations conducted by the SECN. The following parameters were measured at 30 minute intervals during the time period that has been specified: Water Temperature, Specific Conductivity, Salinity, Dissolved Oxygen (DO), DO Concentration, Shallow Depth, pH Level, and Turbidity. Any anomalies noted regarding these parameters have also been noted in separate fields. Please note that these measurements have been certified by network personnel.','public','2026-03-26T05:29:28.585103','2026-03-26T05:29:28.585108','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','77fe1ead-cbdf-496a-ae7e-8416496165ac','DOI NPS DCAT-US','9a5ad4d96aad20e481f1a7a39c3e1390f262e93364f06fb589626fe346e28d4f','1.1','2026-03-26T05:29:28.585103','2026-03-26T05:29:28.585108','Vector Dataset','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('e027931a-f796-438f-a819-839f05b045fe','MARS EXPRESS MARS MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 7 4024 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2019-01-01 to 2020-12-31. It is a Occultation measurement and covers the time 2019-07-28T02:35:00.000 to 2019-07-28T04:25:00.000.','public','2026-03-13T17:07:48.119550','2026-03-13T17:07:48.119559','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','30c6e30b-b088-47b9-a496-fe68b537d694','NASA Data.json','7a34f226b83eb8aea579cef2cdb9bf51901a17c9f54d5f4918caa2fa3bba1d3f','1.1','2026-03-13T17:07:48.119550','2026-03-13T17:07:48.119559','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('e0327387-dabb-408f-895c-9340807471a4','SHIP C NR ANCHORAGE AK (USGS 15276000)','Timeseries data from \'SHIP C NR ANCHORAGE AK (USGS 15276000)\' (gov_usgs_nwis_15276000)','public','2026-03-26T19:16:41.844302','2026-03-26T19:16:41.844308',NULL,NULL,NULL,'16446e2c-cff4-4e4c-b8a1-11e479848e84','ioos',NULL,NULL,'2026-03-26T19:16:41.844302','2026-03-26T19:16:41.844308',NULL,NULL,NULL,'noaa-gov'),('e0462595-1a0f-4775-b2c1-a2ba19bfa419','P445.3 (PLUTO) OCCULTATION V1.0','The dataset include simultaneous imaging obtained at the MMT in the infrared (H-band, 1.65 micron) and visible (unfiltered, approximately 0.24-1.24 micron) of Pluto occulting the star P445.3 (2UCAC 25823784) on 2007 March 18. The measurements included in the dataset were obtained continuously from 10:10:00 to 11:30:00 UTC. The midpoint of the occultation, at the MMT, was 10:53:49+/-00:01. The event was grazing and gives information about the atmosphere of Pluto to a depth of 1348 km above the surface. Images from the other observing sites for this event are not contained within this dataset, however lightcurve tables are included.','public','2026-03-13T19:41:59.842029','2026-03-13T19:41:59.842037','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','4a5bd84e-9201-41ec-8e3b-54024b09c66b','NASA Data.json','a0aa1d2f7a75234d05632972221a4ed3d45201110eb042ec8463b4506854e0c8','1.1','2026-03-13T19:41:59.842029','2026-03-13T19:41:59.842037','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('e048af78-5f9e-4418-80e2-de8eade472ec','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 1 0483 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 1 phase 2014-11-20 to 2015-03-10. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2014-12-11T04:10:05.000 to 2014-12-11T12:41:36.000.','public','2026-03-13T16:40:52.628257','2026-03-13T16:40:52.628262','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','2a7e9de3-a7b3-4063-b026-9ea20473c913','NASA Data.json','c7efdb7bffa07e22566442044dd088eb0568ca5b32c8073dfa17d788250a4110','1.1','2026-03-13T16:40:52.628257','2026-03-13T16:40:52.628262','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('e06ff608-1a0f-46a8-a261-5d0f4fac97c3','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 3 1118 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 3 phase 2015-07-01 to 2015-10-21. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-10-21T10:20:25.000 to 2015-10-21T17:22:10.500.','public','2026-03-13T16:42:33.431821','2026-03-13T16:42:33.431829','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','395d8858-b807-4ea7-bf62-fe3faddc4c19','NASA Data.json','6e9767244b9b9bed04e8e68edf0d322dee4ff43c2c30cb020306fd606c4b6083','1.1','2026-03-13T16:42:33.431821','2026-03-13T16:42:33.431829','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('e088e29c-42f3-457d-8270-c42377dce3af','ROSETTA-ORBITER COMET ESCORT OSINAC 2 EDR MTP 019 V1.0','This data set contains raw EDR images acquired by the OSIRIS Narrow AngleCamera during the escort phase of the Rosetta mission at the comet 67P,covering the period from 2015-07-28 to 2015-08-25.','public','2026-03-13T17:19:29.436989','2026-03-13T17:19:29.436993','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','66c5ad59-0af8-42c0-965c-30e8bffcae73','NASA Data.json','efc95f8eea195e008c6732f81f323f3cf4ad0baf3586e127acfb58f352ddc286','1.1','2026-03-13T17:19:29.436989','2026-03-13T17:19:29.436993','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('e0b57643-2f27-4f7b-9e57-f31a363002c7','MARS EXPRESS SUN MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 7 4079 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2019-01-01 to 2020-12-31. It is a Solar Conjunction measurement and covers the time 2019-10-03T03:24:07.000 to 2019-10-03T06:33:33.500.','public','2026-03-13T17:01:10.766999','2026-03-13T17:01:10.767005','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','c2025870-7d34-4aca-b735-697993ceb9f5','NASA Data.json','f3d65f3e3b8271df073f2c2421e967ffc3743176ff76757c884a1059c8022c77','1.1','2026-03-13T17:01:10.766999','2026-03-13T17:01:10.767005','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('e0d3e03e-4da0-4f4b-b5c5-4ae366a55bf4','ROSETTA-ORBITER EARTH RPCICA 3 EAR2 CALIB V1.0','This dataset contains CALIBRATED DATA from the RPCICA instrument onmission ROSETTA during the second Earth swingby. RPC-ICA was on, butdid not obtain any useful measurements.','public','2026-03-13T18:33:56.783767','2026-03-13T18:33:56.783772','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','f70dea0c-3112-49a7-9f20-30310f1e49b0','NASA Data.json','0f5d9c1153d9e3330c2a3dca19d2b41d453ce177e2109dbb28be17c573b43e14','1.1','2026-03-13T18:33:56.783767','2026-03-13T18:33:56.783772','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('e0efc5ec-563b-4409-9469-c333fd5acedd','Continuous Fixed Station Water Quality Measurements in Canaveral National Seashore, December 2005 (Certified)','This dataset represents continuous water quality measurements that were taken at a fixed point in Canaveral National Seashore during the month of December, 2005 as a part of the Fixed Station Water Quality Monitoring protocol that was developed by the Southeast Coast I&M Network (SECN). The measurements were taken by a YSI 6600 ESD Multi-Parameter Long Term Water Quality Monitoring Datasonde unit that serves as the standard fixed station water quality monitoring equipment for all similar operations conducted by the SECN. The following parameters were measured at 30 minute intervals during the time period that has been specified: Water Temperature, Specific Conductivity, Salinity, Dissolved Oxygen (DO), DO Concentration, Shallow Depth, pH Level, and Turbidity. Any anomalies noted regarding these parameters have also been noted in separate fields. Please note that these measurements have been certified by network personnel.','public','2026-03-26T05:29:27.471787','2026-03-26T05:29:27.471792','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','f216d644-fdc6-4556-8625-43bdafacc515','DOI NPS DCAT-US','3e89eb5ad9452d4d585c55b5fac1c7e18b5073949d0763cc4b81b7408213f8fb','1.1','2026-03-26T05:29:27.471787','2026-03-26T05:29:27.471792','Vector Dataset','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('e0fb06c7-2b8d-4183-924a-7261cbf27503','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSIWAC 4 ESC1-MTP012 RDR-INF-REFL V1.0','This CODMAC level 4 data set contains solar stray-light corrected, in-field stray-light corrected,  radiometric calibrated and geometric distortion corrected  (resampled) image data in reflectance units (normalized  and thus without unit),  acquired by the OSIRIS Wide Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft  during the COMET ESCORT 1 mission phase, covering the period  from 2015-01-13T23:25:00.000 to 2015-02-10T23:24:59.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V1.0 is the first version of this dataset: Lien corrected dataset after September 2019 PSA/PDS external peer review.','public','2026-03-13T18:10:11.503514','2026-03-13T18:10:11.503522','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','2a91bd00-08be-43b9-805c-9f4f59daecdd','NASA Data.json','4db5ce4086ed7b8b5030374af4d7aeaaa7b88161046e243d924330d1e04f633a','1.1','2026-03-13T18:10:11.503514','2026-03-13T18:10:11.503522','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('e1698343-4a51-49fb-acc9-3b96a5469111','Laborshed - OES Wages','Laborshed dataset containing OES wage records for occupations in a given laborshed, for every laborshed in Iowa.','public','2026-03-28T21:57:48.481665','2026-03-28T21:57:48.481669','data.iowa.gov','svqueen',NULL,'e1634ab4-945f-42fe-a0d3-f766cc3c724d','Iowa metadata','a7914b85fbdc975aa194202216fbae6c00ead0d21420b77c985993649a2efdfc','1.1','2026-03-28T21:57:48.481665','2026-03-28T21:57:48.481669','Economic Statistics',NULL,0,'state-of-iowa'),('e1a3ac9b-db36-44e8-954f-bf692351a43d','ARCSIX P-3B Aircraft Multi-function Airborne Raman Lidar (MARLi) Data','ARCSIX_AircraftRemoteSensing_P3B_MARLi_Data contains data collected by the Multi-function Airborne Raman Lidar (MARLi) onboard the P-3B aircraft during the Arctic Radiation-Cloud-Aerosol-Surface Interaction EXperiment (ARCSIX) campaign. Data collection for this product is complete. The ARCSIX campaign is a NASA field investigation aimed at quantifying the contributions of surface properties, clouds, aerosol particles, and precipitation to the Arctic summer surface radiation budget and sea ice melt during the early melt season. Based out of Greenland, ARCSIX completed two deployments from May – June 2024 and July - August 2024 utilizing the NASA P-3B, LaRC G-III, and SPEC-Learjet aircraft. The P-3B was equipped with in situ and remote sensing payloads to acquire measurements of aerosols, cloud, and radiation properties. The high-flying LaRC G-III was equipped with remote sensing instrumentation, including the HALO, and HSRL, along with the AVAPS dropsonde system. The SPEC-Learjet acquired measurements of cloud microphysics. Data were also collected at the Thule High Arctic Atmospheric Observatory (THAAO) in Pituffik, Greenland. The primary objective of ARCSIX was to enhance long-term space-based monitoring and predictive capabilities of Arctic sea ice, cloud, and aerosols by validating and improving remote sensing algorithms and model parameterizations in the Arctic. ARCSIX science questions focused on examining the impact of the predominant summer Arctic cloud types on the radiative surface energy budget, what processes control the evolution and maintenance of the predominant cloud types in the summertime Arctic, and how do the two-way interactions between surface properties and atmospheric forcings affect sea ice evolution?','public','2026-03-13T16:48:10.930702','2026-03-13T16:48:10.930708','NASA/LARC/SD/ASDC','Earthdata Forum','026:00','c0642487-d996-4955-8fd6-498f99a75a1b','NASA Data.json','80718bac6a5be2d173d41072a1b59f3521ca7e2ed55e914bb27b028d226aa7ce','1.1','2026-03-13T16:48:10.930702','2026-03-13T16:48:10.930708','Earth Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('e1ecb4fa-95ec-4401-abf8-3db405a0cf6b','FTB EITC Summary of CA Residents Year Comparison Feb 2026','Produced by the Economic & Statistical Research Bureau, monthly tabulations of tax filings statistics for the Earned Income Tax Credit (EITC), Young Child Tax Credit (YCTC) and Foster Youth Tax Credit (FYTC) provide credit use by county, preparer type, credit amount allowed number of dependents and a many other useful cross-sections','public','2026-03-23T13:57:09.440528','2026-03-23T13:57:09.440535','California Franchise Tax Board','FTB Open Data',NULL,'aa51f752-4e06-4b27-8a5f-8679437faef8','State of California','5536554185409800c0524efafac94c2a5801326b7b39f82b4a2ec6a54267065b','1.1','2026-03-23T13:57:09.440528','2026-03-23T13:57:09.440535','Economy and Demographics',NULL,0,'ca-gov'),('e20ab121-f836-40ff-bfb1-91acec25fb92','VG1 JUP PLS PLASMA DERIVED ION MOMENTS                                         96.0 SEC V1.1','This data set contains the best estimates of the total ion     density at Jupiter during the Voyager 1 encounter in the PLS     voltage range (10-5950 eV/Q).','public','2026-03-13T18:25:41.931800','2026-03-13T18:25:41.931806','planetary plasma interactions','Planetary Data System','026:00','2d194966-99b3-4ae8-8bb9-8238ab134cb2','NASA Data.json','8fc6b1162e9357569de62128c45ac4c7ba707ed21dc064a746cc3276a24cab6e','1.1','2026-03-13T18:25:41.931800','2026-03-13T18:25:41.931806','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('e2291b89-1fc0-4d7a-bca0-0d90c7aac84b','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RPCMAG 2 ESC2 RAW V9.0','This dataset contains EDITED RAW DATA (CODMAC LEVEL 2) of theCOMET ESCORT 2 Phase from March 11, 2015 until June 30, 2015of the ROSETTA orbiter magnetometer RPCMAG. Observations are done inthe vicinity of comet 67P/CHURYUMOV-GERASIMENKO 1 (1969 R1).The current version of the dataset is V9.0.The difference to the datasets of earlier versions is mainly a significantlyimproved sensor temperature model, more detailed documentation about magneticdisturbance sources, more data handling information for the user andalso an improved quality flagging system.This applies mainly to CALIBRATED and RESAMPLED datasets. The RAW dataset,however, has been updated as well in order provide all datasets at thesame stage, although RAW data proper did not change.','public','2026-03-13T18:03:05.452681','2026-03-13T18:03:05.452686','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','d2fedc5e-fae1-43c9-b5a7-486fc04d4f7f','NASA Data.json','2434ab868d711823860cfca6336accd10e2b9bd4468fc114f459cd41d6eb6fdf','1.1','2026-03-13T18:03:05.452681','2026-03-13T18:03:05.452686','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('e27dd6f7-65f4-4ff2-80c5-6f2f238d47bd','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RPCLAP 3ESC2 CALIB2 V1.0','This data set containsCALIBRATED data from Rosetta RPC-LAP, acquired during the COMET ESCORT 2mission phase where the primary target was the comet67P/CHURYUMOV-GERASIMENKO 1 (1969 R1). It contains instrument outputs involts and amperes, calibrated and corrected for instrument offsets.','public','2026-03-13T18:52:23.747644','2026-03-13T18:52:23.747651','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','1a9b4664-2be2-4905-8a57-fac5b778ee2d','NASA Data.json','9bfb8a583606e7fe027de662be0ff66cffe078dd068a10426903dec6b61584ca','1.1','2026-03-13T18:52:23.747644','2026-03-13T18:52:23.747651','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('e2df816d-828f-4de2-9ffd-ca3673deb73d','NEAR GRS SPECTRA FOR EROS SURFACE PHASE','This data set contains Gamma Ray Spectrometer (GRS) observations made during the Eros surface phase of the NEAR mission. Only the GRF sensor made observations from the surface of Eros.','public','2026-03-13T19:23:47.464124','2026-03-13T19:23:47.464129','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','5698e3a8-e13e-4164-b6cf-b5213e0a33b8','NASA Data.json','9fa2d7bfc0634483f28aaded5a940ba015791c5b79db6f2d208c2a12a7fba35b','1.1','2026-03-13T19:23:47.464124','2026-03-13T19:23:47.464129','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('e2e44ae4-d8ce-4dbe-a338-e7fb18d73d3d','NEOWISE DIAMETERS AND ALBEDOS V1.0','This PDS data set represents a compilation of published diameters, optical albedos, near-infrared albedos, and beaming parameters for minor planets detected by NEOWISE during the fully cryogenic, 3-band cryo, post-cryo and NEOWISE-Reactivation Year 1 operations. It contains data covering near-Earth asteroids, Main Belt asteroids, active Main Belt objects, Hildas, Jupiter Trojans, Centaurs, and Jovian and Saturnian irregular satellites. Methodology for physical property determination is described in the referenced articles.','public','2026-03-13T20:08:20.813621','2026-03-13T20:08:20.813626','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','1a31706b-d324-434f-bd14-62ab7a5c23f6','NASA Data.json','b1dbcaff5ffeff8ea9db99b50d5e076ecbc27499822c39767e43abe200b97d10','1.1','2026-03-13T20:08:20.813621','2026-03-13T20:08:20.813626','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('e34eb7e8-4abc-442e-898a-d332762059b3','MSL MARS HAZARD AVOIDANCE CAMERA 2 EDR V1.0','Unknown','public','2026-03-13T17:52:39.899979','2026-03-13T17:52:39.899986','Imaging','Planetary Data System','026:00','88a929d3-9a12-43b8-8a27-653d380187ee','NASA Data.json','084946c297529db38a1471d72f317b17a0d72a5fa8e90c602169c7d3d6050d00','1.1','2026-03-13T17:52:39.899979','2026-03-13T17:52:39.899986','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('e3616f21-1fe7-46d6-be23-14fb3ff0ca76','HPMS Statewide Summaries 2019','The Highway Performance Management System (HPMS) Statewide Summaries table contains demographic and system length estimates for all Urban and Rural public roads, functionally classified as minor collector in rural areas or local in any area, summarized by State. In addition, this dataset contains daily vehicle-miles traveled (VMT) estimates for all public roads located in Small Urban areas, functionally classified as minor collector or local.','public','2026-03-28T13:37:14.072258','2026-03-28T13:37:14.072263','Federal Highway Administration','Office of Highway Policy Information','021:15','5bbedbba-303b-4cc4-a884-8ea10db8d410','DOT Socrata Data.json','87ae793b74b307ccaf9171dfb7c36390b72fa19e7d3a57b87bac91c48109dd88','1.1','2026-