G310000 - TPDES Oil and Gas Extraction, TXG340000 - Petroleum Bulk Stations and Terminals, TXG500000 - Quarries in Certain Water Quality Protection Areas, TXG640000 - Water Treatment Plant, TXG870000 - Pesticides, and TXG920000 - Concentrated Animal Feeding Operation.','public','2026-03-25T14:22:39.920615','2026-03-25T14:22:39.920621','data.austintexas.gov','TCEQ Information Resources Division',NULL,'25d6015d-1989-4470-af18-a99889e02c43','City of Austin Data.json','cff270554b28937c167303e3a328d61f9971200554d74218df0390f80c4ca8f6','1.1','2026-03-25T14:22:39.920615','2026-03-25T14:22:39.920621',NULL,NULL,0,'city-of-austin'),('e39c0683-8502-425b-b370-3022c14ded8b','MARS EXPRESS MARS MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 5 3879 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2015-01-01 to 2016-12-31. It is a Occultation measurement and covers the time 2016-12-31T02:52:01 to 2016-12-31T03:40:00.','public','2026-03-13T19:59:34.029706','2026-03-13T19:59:34.029712','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','6fc0a213-fa24-40f0-9292-0dee3805ea96','NASA Data.json','d16474d4c9efc4ffd45fa628fa5400a0b450e2f480e8c28b20ba346d10fff924','1.1','2026-03-13T19:59:34.029706','2026-03-13T19:59:34.029712','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('e3cfae9b-d380-4811-b730-b4c328b506d2','ROSETTA-ORBITER EARTH RPCLAP2 EAR2 EDITED2 V1.0','This data set contains EDITEDdata from Rosetta RPC-LAP, acquired during the EARTH SWING-BY 2 missionphase where the primary target was the planet EARTH. It containsuncalibrated raw data, i.e. the digital output of the instrument.','public','2026-03-13T18:05:38.351114','2026-03-13T18:05:38.351119','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','417ec1ec-6b8e-45f5-98f0-4a4cdc0a23bf','NASA Data.json','c637ea39ca9efbfa71ec47cfa23522229224cdf67f7a0250ad420fb0c4810107','1.1','2026-03-13T18:05:38.351114','2026-03-13T18:05:38.351119','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('e3d0a413-23a8-457d-9505-35b5ee01aa2f','Walton-Smith CTD, WS23203, WS23203_WS23203_Stn.ROME5, 2023-07-25, 27.6513N 82.8372W','Walton-Smith Conductivity, Temperature, Depth (CTD) - WS23203 - WS23203_WS23203_Stn.ROME5 - 2023-07-25 - 27.6513N 82.8372W. Hydrographic Measurements in the Gulf of Mexico. flags: 1 = good; 3 =  mean ÃÂ± 3*standard deviation; 4 = mean ÃÂ± 5*standard deviation; 9 = missing. other','public','2026-03-26T19:15:49.765525','2026-03-26T19:15:49.765534',NULL,NULL,NULL,'6c6ee9ad-2036-42a7-88d4-548ed4c4cde9','ioos',NULL,NULL,'2026-03-26T19:15:49.765525','2026-03-26T19:15:49.765534',NULL,NULL,NULL,'noaa-gov'),('e4106af9-2c83-41a3-a53d-30e592ca4fd9','Application of Transcriptomics Concentration-Response Modeling for Prioritization of Contaminants Detected in Tributaries of the North American Great Lakes','Raw data associated with the manuscript titled Application of Transcriptomics Concentration-Response Modeling for Prioritization of Contaminants Detected in Tributaries of the North American Great Lakes (Cavallin et al., 2025). \n\nThis dataset is associated with the following publication:\nCavallin, J., K. Bush, S. Corsi, L. DeCicco, K. Flynn, A. Kasparek, M. Hazemi, E. Maloney, P. Schumann, and D. Villeneuve. Application of transcriptomics concentration-response modeling for prioritization of contaminants detected in tributaries of the North American Great Lakes.   ENVIRONMENTAL TOXICOLOGY AND CHEMISTRY. Society of Environmental Toxicology and Chemistry, Pensacola, FL, USA, 44(5): 1310-1321, (2025).','public','2026-03-24T12:14:56.512556','2026-03-24T12:14:56.512560','U.S. Environmental Protection Agency','Jenna Cavallin','020:00','5007dd42-04b5-42d7-9c56-4d1f088c2410','EPA ScienceHub','90370418dde0054134023bc60c4e90acd9e0837ef88e372aff4b0a8ca48d40c5','1.1','2026-03-24T12:14:56.512556','2026-03-24T12:14:56.512560',NULL,'020:000',0,'epa-gov'),('e471ae37-72f3-4365-b3ee-064232510ffb','Laborshed - Occupational Reports','Laborshed dataset that contains estimates and counts for occupations within each laborshed area in Iowa. This data represents the main table on the occupations report dashboard.','public','2026-03-28T22:00:37.754519','2026-03-28T22:00:37.754524','data.iowa.gov','svqueen',NULL,'c8823d92-8a19-4467-bef0-6f4a8f5ac589','Iowa metadata','754206619d20536f3c90afffda0f3bbd006f90060443cfa2fdee612d938a47f5','1.1','2026-03-28T22:00:37.754519','2026-03-28T22:00:37.754524','Economic Statistics',NULL,0,'state-of-iowa'),('e4824a29-9446-454c-a110-748f2318ae22','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 ROSETTA EXTENSION 1 1382 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the ROSETTA EXTENSION 1 phase 2016-01-01 to 2016-04-05. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2016-01-30T05:35:00.000 to 2016-01-30T09:01:21.500.','public','2026-03-13T19:25:49.896395','2026-03-13T19:25:49.896402','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','99b998a7-d4c9-4fcf-b7c0-dd53693797d3','NASA Data.json','9582260fc8442b6966943f50df7dea9ad2d302809b63fb794798d84a090a780b','1.1','2026-03-13T19:25:49.896395','2026-03-13T19:25:49.896402','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('e4c8a9c1-5abd-4b53-9a56-85e2269218f8','CLEMENTINE MOON SPICE KERNELS V1.0','This data set includes the complete set of Clementine SPICE data files (``kernel files\'\'), which can be accessed using SPICE software. The SPICE data contains geometric and other ancillary information needed to recover the full value of science instrument data. In particular SPICE kernels provide spacecraft and planetary ephemerides, instrument mounting alignments, spacecraft orientation, spacecraft sequences of events, and data needed for relevant time conversions.','public','2026-03-13T19:01:04.907241','2026-03-13T19:01:04.907246','Navigation and Ancillary Information Facility','Planetary Data System','026:00','8ff8908b-b416-4a1a-923d-ac2514108019','NASA Data.json','b63b999209af98728a3d940bf062e2f9982ba2337c55584734ae02a9331d4701','1.1','2026-03-13T19:01:04.907241','2026-03-13T19:01:04.907246','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('e4e110e5-53bf-42db-82b5-86c20f3fa808','DID(IT) - Digital Innovation & Development - Information Technology- Fugitives and Absconders Search Report: Fugitive and Absconder Information','Fugitive and Absconder Information','non-public','2026-03-22T11:53:36.013739','2026-03-22T11:53:36.013744','Unspecified','Open Data (MGMT)','024:030','c5e11d47-472b-4eeb-9619-939fe3d898ce','DHS datajson source','a403c9a038ad7d82d05e5520091feecff4726d5f55ce567a911056cd9fe52a39','1.1','2026-03-22T11:53:36.013739','2026-03-22T11:53:36.013744',NULL,'024:000',0,'dhs-gov'),('e51c16e8-c8a7-4a0c-a2db-6dde46afb2fe','IHW COMET NNSN CALIB EXPERIMENT DATA RECORD CROMMELIN V1.0','In preparation for the concerted international study of Comet Halley, the IHW conducted a trial run with observations of Comet Crommelin, largely during February and March of 1984.','public','2026-03-13T18:29:01.326380','2026-03-13T18:29:01.326388','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','3ebcfb1a-e6ca-434f-9a24-e719308f0a9c','NASA Data.json','9b0b4e16d6fd5b128bdea99b07604763f0ddbdc3674324cecb8861a19e86f853','1.1','2026-03-13T18:29:01.326380','2026-03-13T18:29:01.326388','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('e53cde39-5534-4427-873f-67bf52f508aa','MARS EXPRESS MARS MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 5 3810 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2015-01-01 to 2016-12-31. It is a Occultation measurement and covers the time 2015-09-05T11:21:45.050 to 2015-09-05T11:45:36.949.','public','2026-03-13T18:59:35.612251','2026-03-13T18:59:35.612257','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','88faeb4d-c824-4220-8845-cd0eef6d72ce','NASA Data.json','acbaa14845628b7c09ff5f45028b80017942ef27489579898a6244b3c4d6bfaa','1.1','2026-03-13T18:59:35.612251','2026-03-13T18:59:35.612257','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('e53d09da-7f15-4715-a01e-3ccdf50ea25b','ULY JUP MAGNETIC FIELD JOVIGRAPHIC SYS III LH COORDS 60 AVGS','The data set covers the period Jan 25                                      through Feb 18, 1992 (days 25 to 48                                      inclusive).','public','2026-03-13T18:30:18.649565','2026-03-13T18:30:18.649570','planetary plasma interactions','Planetary Data System','026:00','fc341f11-b64c-4304-ae2f-07df712f8a52','NASA Data.json','c6de2b5ae7c49c470a730df8ecfab649c10d788475178fce028a1954a58dab93','1.1','2026-03-13T18:30:18.649565','2026-03-13T18:30:18.649570','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('e5409a0c-4e74-405c-9371-d42415289e85','PIONEER 10 JUPITER GEIGER TUBE TELESCOPE HIGH-RES DATA V1.0','Pioneer 10 geiger tube telescope data.','public','2026-03-13T18:56:21.045576','2026-03-13T18:56:21.045583','planetary plasma interactions','Planetary Data System','026:00','3e1f0f2f-bcb6-48ba-a5f3-2493bb4a7967','NASA Data.json','ae9fc1f200d385f1bd44ed1196cd77bf1ff2020db55aecd1d5215f04d4d7d04a','1.1','2026-03-13T18:56:21.045576','2026-03-13T18:56:21.045583','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('e58f9a7d-7489-48c4-92d0-8921ec984d38','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P SREM 2 ESCORT 3 MTP021 V1.0','This data set contains count rates (1/s) as measured by the Standard Radiation Environment Monitor (SREM) instrument on the Rosetta spacecraft, along with their standard deviations. The primary target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko. These are CODMAC Level 2 Experiment Data Record data, and provide a measure of the radiation in the spacecraft environment during the Medium Term Plan 21 period of the ESCORT 3 mission phase.','public','2026-03-13T18:03:15.620353','2026-03-13T18:03:15.620358','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','8197e0ec-1ce5-48d6-a22c-7fa92927839b','NASA Data.json','8f21d1c69cddfa137ec962f210e5da3b465c073ac6c8ff2b57df02335fb3ec8f','1.1','2026-03-13T18:03:15.620353','2026-03-13T18:03:15.620358','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('e612b30b-28e6-42e5-95f8-8d21727f3850','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSINAC 4 PRL-MTP003 RDR-INF-REFL V1.0','This CODMAC level 4 data set contains solar stray-light corrected, in-field stray-light corrected,  radiometric calibrated and geometric distortion corrected  (resampled) image data in reflectance units (normalized  and thus without unit),  acquired by the OSIRIS Narrow Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft  during the PRELANDING mission phase, covering the period  from 2014-05-07T12:48:00.000 to 2014-06-04T10:49:59.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V1.0 is the first version of this dataset: Lien corrected dataset after September 2019 PSA/PDS external peer review.','public','2026-03-13T19:40:43.544866','2026-03-13T19:40:43.544872','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','0b7f5964-7b8b-4a90-bf9b-afd57e92550a','NASA Data.json','84894c3943ef0362fbf830eb2b645a0e0b32c60d2e6f2901234928a6dc0c3adb','1.1','2026-03-13T19:40:43.544866','2026-03-13T19:40:43.544872','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('e6ba4b4e-0c4e-4718-ab47-5bc2256f7108','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 ROSETTA EXTENSION 1 1403 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the ROSETTA EXTENSION 1 phase 2016-01-01 to 2016-04-05. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2016-02-06T20:17:50.000 to 2016-02-06T21:50:06.500.','public','2026-03-13T19:22:45.848313','2026-03-13T19:22:45.848317','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','a025fa69-e228-42e8-ad46-dc9ba2e9d250','NASA Data.json','f51f7e08527ad54eb8d7ce8bd08d3af2e0b6f365e99a4ba9dec722cc5688339d','1.1','2026-03-13T19:22:45.848313','2026-03-13T19:22:45.848317','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('e6d42004-c9d7-4366-be5a-13bcb53d124e','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 4 1239 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 4 phase 2015-10-22 to 2015-12-31. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-12-06T01:46:15.000 to 2015-12-06T07:21:51.500.','public','2026-03-13T17:22:55.937859','2026-03-13T17:22:55.937864','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','0daa1b7d-2ea8-4c36-95ce-4d21e157dea0','NASA Data.json','fb8d8eac82110efdccf68477329c9dbda0d4e963883f0df1876911605f5e2831','1.1','2026-03-13T17:22:55.937859','2026-03-13T17:22:55.937864','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('e71800b0-e247-4525-95f2-6d129d1c2bb6','Ensatina Predicted Habitat - CWHR A012 [ds1979]','<div style=\'text-align:Left;\'><div><div><p><span>CWHR Predicted Habitat Models represent areas of predicted suitable habitat for each species within its range. These models are built from the following principal inputs: </span></p><p><span>1) a statewide, best-available vegetation map (FVEG);  </span></p><p><span>2) GIS data representing a species’ range;  </span></p><p><span>3) the CWHR database of habitat suitability values for over 700 terrestrial vertebrate species. </span></p><p><span>Habitat suitability ranks of Low (non-zero values less than 0.34), Medium (0.34-0.66), and High (greater than 0.66) are based on the maximum suitability value across the 3 species life requisites: reproduction, feeding, and cover. Note that previous versions of these Predicted Habitat Models used an average across the 3 life requisites in order to obtain an overall suitability score for each habitat type and stage class.  Habitat suitability scores were developed based on habitat patch sizes greater than 40 acres in size and are best interpreted for habitat patches greater than 200 acres in size. The FVEG landcover dataset is an aggregation of multiple statewide landcover and regional vegetation mapping efforts, conducted at different points in time (approximately 1990 up to time of publishing) and at various resolutions, compiled by the California Department of Forestry and Fire Protection (CALFIRE). FVEG uses the most current and consistent data available for each region of the state. Decision rules were developed that controlled which layers were given priority in areas of overlap. Crosswalks were used to attribute the various data sources according to the CWHR habitat-type classification system. Attributing FVEG with CWHR habitat types allows for the extraction of areas with non-zero suitability values for each species within the bounds of its range, creating a series of maps of predicted suitable habitat which are species-specific. Because FVEG is an amalgam of disparate landcover assessment efforts across the state, the predictive power for determining suitable habitat will vary between species, and possibly even regionally for species which are widely distributed. While these maps represent CDFW’s best estimate of the presence of suitable habitat for any given species in the CWHR system, these maps are also limited by several factors: 1) the accuracy and resolution of vegetation maps in a given region; 2) the dynamic nature of the landscape in which fire and other disturbance events alter conditions at a greater frequency than mapping efforts can track; 3) the currency of expert knowledge, particularly as species adapt to changing land and climate conditions and the shifting of other species’ ranges; 4) the frequency of species-specific surveys across a representative sample of a species’ entire range; 5) metapopulation dynamics, which describes the shifting of populations within their environment as result of numerous types of interactions and responses. </span></p><p><span>CWHR GIS data representing predicted suitable habitat should not be used to indicate the presence or absence of a particular species at any specific site. CWHR predicted habitat models are named according to the 4-character alpha-numeric CWHR ID assigned to each species (5 characters in the case of subspecies or other sub-taxa). There is also a “CWHR Revision Tracking Table” containing a record for each species, its CWHR ID, scientific name, common name, and range and habitat model data revision history. CWHR species range models, predicted habitat models, and GIS data of the statewide distribution of all CWHR habitat types, along with the CWHR revision tracking table, are available for download at </span><a href=\'https://www.wildlife.ca.gov/Data/CWHR\' target=\'_blank\' style=\'text-decoration:underline;\' rel=\'nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer\'><span>https://www.wildlife.ca.gov/Data/CWHR</span></a><span>. </span></p></div></div></div>','public','2026-03-23T13:57:55.896149','2026-03-23T13:57:55.896154','California Department of Fish and Wildlife','BIOS_Admin',NULL,'e954e279-aa70-4222-a89f-3126ee8e205a','State of California','5205bd613a32252c266af4175997ca21465d06bc23c3f3593d5b8b16f1aa8dc5','1.1','2026-03-23T13:57:55.896149','2026-03-23T13:57:55.896154','Natural Resources',NULL,0,'ca-gov'),('e71c5011-9886-480e-90b0-a4a1d952bb26','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P SREM 5 PRELANDING MTP007 V1.0','This data set contains derived electron and proton flux energies in MeV from the Standard Radiation Environment Monitor (SREM) instrument on the Rosetta spacecraft, which had the primary target of comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko. These are CODMAC Level 5 derived data, and measure the radiation in the spacecraft environment during the Medium Term Plan 7 period of the PRELANDING mission phase.','public','2026-03-13T18:54:28.299725','2026-03-13T18:54:28.299731','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','a834773b-b2d7-4767-9a80-ea1260794fc7','NASA Data.json','bf0b6820ed2957c8b256be37d6ceaca1febf0f297d2154940b157bd05a85430d','1.1','2026-03-13T18:54:28.299725','2026-03-13T18:54:28.299731','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('e754b34e-b798-4ce0-858e-2591e3e0f88f','ROSETTA-ORBITER COMET ESCORT 1 OSINAC 3 RDR MTP011 V2.0','This data set contains images acquired by the OSIRIS Narrow Angle Camera during the COMET ESCORT 1 phase of the Rosetta mission at the comet 67P, covering the period from 2014-12-19T23:25:00.000 to 2015-01-13T23:24:59.000. This version V2.0 supersedes previous deliveries of the same dataset.','public','2026-03-13T17:47:06.659466','2026-03-13T17:47:06.659472','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','b4c90c1f-7093-4c24-b091-f5839f9437c8','NASA Data.json','d8fbffc504aaec0ad069bc66eeb9a2d4346dffae57899790987af61018a73928','1.1','2026-03-13T17:47:06.659466','2026-03-13T17:47:06.659472','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('e76635d2-02fa-46c3-8075-69b4fe02aeb4','US Forest Atlas FIA Forest Type Groups All Alaska (Image Service)','<p><span style=\'background-color:rgb(255,255,255); color:rgb(20,20,20); font-family:&quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px;\'><span style=\'display:inline !important; float:none; font-style:normal; font-variant-caps:normal; font-variant-ligatures:normal; font-weight:400; letter-spacing:normal; text-align:start; text-decoration-color:initial; text-decoration-style:initial; text-indent:0px; text-transform:none; word-spacing:0px;\'>This dataset portrays the forest type group for Alaska. Each group is a subset of the National Forest Type dataset which portrays 28 forest type groups across the contiguous United States. These data were derived from MODIS composite images from the 2002 and 2003 growing seasons in combination with nearly 100 other geospatial data layers, including elevation, slope, aspect, ecoregions, and PRISM climate data.</span></span></p>','public','2026-03-13T22:50:01.598857','2026-03-13T22:50:01.598862','U.S. Forest Service','USFSEnterpriseContent','005:96','3b5198c8-5965-46f3-afcb-fee20e778ec2','USDA JSON','0d5acc2c3735083855d616275029325ce8fb930950b989887dae1975d03f46c3','1.1','2026-03-13T22:50:01.598857','2026-03-13T22:50:01.598862','geospatial','005:059',0,'usda-gov'),('e78e9dfe-0d33-4a4f-9f88-07b0c1009c94','SMAP_L1C_SIGMA_NAUGHT_HIGH_RES_METADATA_V002','SMAP Level 1C Sigma Naught High Res Product Metadata Version 2','public','2026-03-13T22:33:30.015249','2026-03-13T22:33:30.015257','NASA/JPL/SMAP;ASF','Earthdata Forum','026:00','7c5efd17-f18b-4797-a783-c5d5c27db12f','NASA Data.json','fa0b07545b4496eaa8c87d42512618d75f3230eade084d74e380f83231113d42','1.1','2026-03-13T22:33:30.015249','2026-03-13T22:33:30.015257','Earth Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('e7b5d032-c587-4a1c-ac93-30ac2110e475','BLM CO Lands Inventoried with Wilderness Characteristics','This feature dataset represents the spatial extent and boundaries of inventoried and managed BLM Lands with Wilderness Characteristics. This dataset also also provides BLM and the public with information about naturalness, opportunities for solitude and/or primitive recreation, supplemental values and proximity to Wilderness Areas or Wilderness Study Areas.\n\nBLM Inventoried Lands with Wilderness Characteristics is consistent with Section 201 of the Federal Land Policy and Management Act (FLPMA), which requires the BLM Colorado Inventoried Lands with Wilderness Characteristics is consistent with Section 201 of the Federal Land Policy and Management Act (FLPMA), which requires the Secretary of the Interior to “prepare and maintain on a continuing basis an inventory of all public lands and their resource and other values,” and the BLM Land Use Planning Handbook, BLM Colorado has identified and begun an assessment of BLM-managed lands with wilderness characteristics outside of existing WSAs. BLM Manual 6310 - Conducting Wilderness Characteristics Inventory on BLM Lands, provides the guidance from which BLM performs the wilderness characteristic inventory process.','public','2026-03-25T12:30:12.241073','2026-03-25T12:30:12.241080','Bureau of Land Management','Bureau of Land Management, pkeller','010:04','9e56b632-e453-4981-8d53-082d3173a777','DOI BLM DCAT-US','c922a03d639741471f2c6a3f7cd3f70b1e72ff72988a1225e41f2d1f338b182d','1.1','2026-03-25T12:30:12.241073','2026-03-25T12:30:12.241080','geospatial','010:000',0,'doi-gov'),('e7d0f6d0-7e8b-4253-8652-fa72cca7c9c9','Commercial Harvest Sites','Locations of commercial shellfish harvest sites (shellfish harvesters, shellstock shippers, and shucker packers) in Washington State.  Also displayed on the Commercial Shellfish Map Viewer here:  <a href=\'https://fortress.wa.gov/doh/oswpviewer/index.html\' target=\'_blank\' rel=\'nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer\'>https://fortress.wa.gov/doh/oswpviewer/index.html</a>  Relay and wet storage sites are not included.','public','2026-03-22T03:12:47.054728','2026-03-22T03:12:47.054733','Washington State Department of Health','WADOHAdmin',NULL,'236c1558-53bd-4445-8776-e8f437d5c26d','WA JSON','534c14d32c93e9cf6eb2caf997117d1ae8e3d5a3e603172e4516342d25707378','1.1','2026-03-22T03:12:47.054728','2026-03-22T03:12:47.054733','geospatial',NULL,0,'state-of-washington'),('e7d21df4-872c-4d2a-b17e-eb36b1a18100','EIGHT COLOR ASTEROID SURVEY V4.0','This data set contains the reflectance spectra and associated data of the Eight Color Asteroid Survey (ECAS), including results for 589 asteroids.','public','2026-03-13T17:59:35.465233','2026-03-13T17:59:35.465239','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','704dc114-56e0-4a31-ae9a-50b56b949bec','NASA Data.json','473b13093fa8603ca382aa3418c02ae685781308623c0f788f0e771fdf1bea8f','1.1','2026-03-13T17:59:35.465233','2026-03-13T17:59:35.465239','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('e7f63b40-e599-4104-a492-6ecfac8799bd','NEW HORIZONS REX POST-LAUNCH CHECKOUT RAW V2.0','This data set contains Raw data taken by the New Horizons Radio Science Experiment instrument during the post-launch checkout mission phase. This is VERSION 2.0 of this data set. The REX datasets over the mission include calibrations using known radio sources, Jupiter, and cold sky measurements; operational readiness tests (ORTs); internal test pattern calibration; and prime science radiometry and occultation observations during the Pluto Encounter.','public','2026-03-13T18:45:45.692479','2026-03-13T18:45:45.692483','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','6e845ff6-62c3-4309-a4ff-47b1b45f737a','NASA Data.json','b80686e27dce9363ec4639fb407ee10b0b8c16625ec588c119757c95f2139e25','1.1','2026-03-13T18:45:45.692479','2026-03-13T18:45:45.692483','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('e834eb6e-5cc0-4ee3-9d0f-010296515ed2','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 PRELANDING 0365 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the PRELANDING phase 2014-01-21 to 2014-11-18. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2014-10-17T03:27:05.000 to 2014-10-17T15:03:46.500.','public','2026-03-13T18:51:08.942712','2026-03-13T18:51:08.942720','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','7a57387f-8616-438b-8d97-b07f2c86b049','NASA Data.json','74ecb69cfb92519b20d9998830b58e168ecb8983381ae5d2469f4e03da90ec90','1.1','2026-03-13T18:51:08.942712','2026-03-13T18:51:08.942720','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('e8440f5d-6037-471d-9dd1-11e1e106db4b','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RPCIES 5 ESC3 V1.0','This dataset contains DERIVED DATA of the Rosetta RPCIES instrument taken during the comet escort 3 phase (ESC3). The target of this phase was comet 67P/CHURYUMOV-GERASIMENKO 1 (1969 R1). Included are the data taken between 01 Jul 2015 and 21 Oct 2015.','public','2026-03-13T17:03:57.820159','2026-03-13T17:03:57.820166','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','98c475f4-a656-46c1-950e-782178076574','NASA Data.json','daa72c78c4fc3eaf8db3cd16a0c0ebd9176b53e353d45a671786c3dc1d074cb6','1.1','2026-03-13T17:03:57.820159','2026-03-13T17:03:57.820166','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('e860eb06-d3d6-41f9-8778-7b621b0beada','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RPCLAP 5ESC2 NEL V1.0','This data set contains DERIVEDdata from Rosetta RPC-LAP, acquired during the COMET ESCORT 2 missionphase where the primary target was the comet 67P/CHURYUMOV-GERASIMENKO 1(1969 R1). It contains electron density at higher time resolution thanin the DERIV2 data sets.','public','2026-03-13T17:09:36.304572','2026-03-13T17:09:36.304581','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','8fb66b19-ac4c-4b77-8996-bbe5612124cb','NASA Data.json','e23c490c0d028a26d301d68aaf57b7159c96db19f23f15aa8b7bcf17f6582358','1.1','2026-03-13T17:09:36.304572','2026-03-13T17:09:36.304581','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('e885e465-25af-451b-9fa0-e047015476b0','Laborshed - Wages','Laborshed dataset containing wage data from the main survey. Data covers payment types and wages for all laborsheds in Iowa.','public','2026-03-28T22:00:03.205171','2026-03-28T22:00:03.205176','data.iowa.gov','svqueen',NULL,'406ee90c-fa19-45db-ae88-632d16417422','Iowa metadata','172a6543d79b22b8675f3159f47d79945a6b7fa8bcea57717bb167bc60495146','1.1','2026-03-28T22:00:03.205171','2026-03-28T22:00:03.205176','Economic Statistics',NULL,0,'state-of-iowa'),('e8902c8e-3c93-4896-8d8c-9b3063a53181','EPOXI 103P/HARTLEY2 ENCOUNTER - MRI CALIBRATED IMAGES V1.0','This dataset contains calibrated images of comet 103/P Hartley 2 acquired by the Medium Resolution Visible CCD (MRI) from 05 September through 26 November 2010 during the Hartley 2 encounter phase of the EPOXI mission. Clear-filter and CN images of the comet were acquired throughout this phase; OH, C2, and dust continuum images were only acquired for several days spanning closest approach.','public','2026-03-13T18:14:55.718953','2026-03-13T18:14:55.718958','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','ea0ffec6-a005-4fd9-9617-3e153c120c92','NASA Data.json','996ea72d10cdb41e530174bc9820f5fbb829cb28c261fce64bfc62a42a4d68aa','1.1','2026-03-13T18:14:55.718953','2026-03-13T18:14:55.718958','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('e897abb0-356d-41b2-85d2-392b991ece74','ROSETTA-ORBITER SW RPCMAG 2 RVM1 RAW V9.0','This dataset contains EDITED RAW DATA (CODMAC LEVEL 2) of theRENDEZVOUS MANOEUVRE 1 (RVM1) from November 22, 2010 until December 06, 2010of the ROSETTA orbiter magnetometer RPCMAG.The current version of the dataset is V9.0.The difference to the datasets of earlier versions is mainly a significantlyimproved sensor temperature model, more detailed documentation about magneticdisturbance sources, more data handling information for the user andalso an improved quality flagging system.This applies mainly to CALIBRATED and RESAMPLED datasets. The RAW dataset,however, has been updated as well in order provide all datasets at thesame stage, although RAW data proper did not change.','public','2026-03-13T18:44:47.116367','2026-03-13T18:44:47.116372','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','404a187a-11da-4570-9ad3-5c91a65ec572','NASA Data.json','9b941df0c860e6ded26b5b48511a7ec1488c0df9fa7af3d74acfdfb313a435e2','1.1','2026-03-13T18:44:47.116367','2026-03-13T18:44:47.116372','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('e89c86e5-6fb3-4ccf-936c-90dbfb6eb034','MARS EXPRESS SUN MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 5 3728 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2015-01-01 to 2016-12-31. It is a Solar Conjunction measurement and covers the time 2015-04-27T04:24:45.000 to 2015-04-27T09:26:52.500.','public','2026-03-13T18:03:52.471122','2026-03-13T18:03:52.471128','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','064fd848-5d38-4b89-86da-5efba3329eaf','NASA Data.json','c5c96642868eea743923ecef25c83831d6bcc8ab30143502d597c55d1c01199d','1.1','2026-03-13T18:03:52.471122','2026-03-13T18:03:52.471128','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('e8a20255-66f8-4f36-ad2d-9d7dd55b1487','Suicide Incidents, Fatalities, and Injuries','This is the report for suicide incidents, fatalities and injuries.','public','2026-03-26T12:45:14.030120','2026-03-26T12:45:14.030125','Federal Railroad Administration','FRA Safety Data Team','021:27','beca0f3d-fe68-457e-a1c7-73fa2653f4d2','DOT Socrata Data.json','8cfd009a8a49e8c536f57aab459420093e3eb3d416ede70fa0736c08b1f0b225','1.1','2026-03-26T12:45:14.030120','2026-03-26T12:45:14.030125','Railroads','021:037',0,'dot-gov'),('e9013a46-8995-46f1-94b5-3a1c2db369ee','MARS EXPRESS SUN MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 5 3791 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2015-01-01 to 2016-12-31. It is a Solar Conjunction measurement and covers the time 2015-07-09T07:05:01 to 2015-07-09T10:19:00.','public','2026-03-13T19:09:35.075206','2026-03-13T19:09:35.075213','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','c2209cb4-e00f-4dab-a9f6-f8cbbdd195b0','NASA Data.json','9e7b140a5ef78d5d1f1f8dc10b6937472e17e43ee66493823709fb151b111990','1.1','2026-03-13T19:09:35.075206','2026-03-13T19:09:35.075213','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('e9366d2b-9419-4f2d-a282-2a506d24bae6','NEW HORIZONS  LEISA PLUTO CRUISE  RAW V1.0','This data set contains Raw data taken by the New Horizons  Linear Etalon Imaging Spectral Array  instrument during the  pluto cruise  mission phase. This is VERSION 1.0 of this data set.   The spacecraft was in hibernation for much of the Pluto Cruise  mission phase, and the focus for RALPH (which includes both MVIC and  LEISA sensors) during Annual CheckOuts one through eight (ACO1-8) was  preparation for the Pluto Encounter in 2015, including functional tests,  and calibrations. Observations performed during this phase for LEISA were  for the Pluto Encounter Rehearsal in 2013, a test of the Sun in the Solar  Illumination Assembly (SIA), Vega and Arcturus calibrations, and other  calibrations (stray light, dark, flat fields, interference with other  instruments).','public','2026-03-13T18:48:38.596161','2026-03-13T18:48:38.596165','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','a24339ef-bd17-4ba6-92eb-3db7e7e6ebe6','NASA Data.json','10e052bba11b0c2db38bf790383a9989720c7bf38e436a6beb998b54d5f36388','1.1','2026-03-13T18:48:38.596161','2026-03-13T18:48:38.596165','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('e93ef3f3-e30f-450f-a2a1-b437ea8c420a','DAWN FC2 CALIBRATED VESTA IMAGES V1.0','Abstract : Framing Camera 2 is one of two identical units flying on Dawn spacecraft. This dataset includes the Reduced Data Record (RDR) version of all available images acquired during the Vesta Encounter (Approach, Survey, Transfer to HAMO, HAMO, Transfer to LAMO, LAMO, Transfer to HAMO2, HAMO-2, and Transfer to Ceres). In addition to the imagery, anciliary information is stored within the image headers, as well as a detailed account of all the reference files used for the calibration. Calibration files needed for further processing are archived as a separate data set.','public','2026-03-13T19:27:50.245831','2026-03-13T19:27:50.245836','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','e29fc72c-3194-48a9-bd13-3208473d0aed','NASA Data.json','bcd5b8a7d201ebcb54ab211d07dc82a9ea31007660d5e6e9110955a40a8f6b77','1.1','2026-03-13T19:27:50.245831','2026-03-13T19:27:50.245836','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('e95a2187-d6fe-40b0-9c88-12200d5ff663','MARS EXPRESS MARS MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 3 3255 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2010-01-01 to 2012-12-31. It is a Global Gravity measurement and covers the time 2012-05-31T07:17:45.000 to 2012-05-31T10:35:15.500.','public','2026-03-13T19:50:04.185603','2026-03-13T19:50:04.185609','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','7eba02da-dec5-45db-b8de-338a272f38d8','NASA Data.json','560227c97d5cf972c0f0918c105c42b5f5b7fb754ba60930a118f827dae27b26','1.1','2026-03-13T19:50:04.185603','2026-03-13T19:50:04.185609','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('e99d6db6-a42b-46ac-8314-def896baccb0','\"Deepwater CTD - 00596937.bdo.nc - 21.58N, -86.28W - 1970-04-21\"','The Minerals Management Service (MMS) of the U. S. Department of the Interior funded the Deepwater Physical Oceanography Reanalysis and Synthesis of Historical Data Study in the Gulf of Mexico. MMS awarded the contract to the Texas A&M Research Foundation in July 1998. The basic study area is bounded by the shelf edge and the 25DGN latitude, which is the southern boundary; it extends from sea surface to sea floor. MMS has four objectives for the study. First is to create an inventory of physical oceanographic data and compile it into a single database on a CD-ROM. Second is to conduct analyses and interpretations of the physical oceanographic data to identify physical processes and phenomena. Third is to produce a climatology of the processes from available data and analyses and to prioritize the processes in terms of importance to improved understanding, simulation, and prediction of deepwater circulation. Fourth is to provide criteria and constraints useful in design of future field observations and numerical modeling efforts. Study results will provide MMS with information needed to direct its resources more efficiently and effectively in the review and assessment of potential environmental impacts of offshore oil and gas operations in the deepwater Gulf of Mexico.','public','2026-03-26T19:15:29.610643','2026-03-26T19:15:29.610649',NULL,NULL,NULL,'c510bd13-e46b-4c22-8584-e47d69a24197','ioos',NULL,NULL,'2026-03-26T19:15:29.610643','2026-03-26T19:15:29.610649',NULL,NULL,NULL,'noaa-gov'),('e9c2d3a4-ed69-4262-81e1-208f3826d3d5','DDS RegionalCenters','<p><span style=\'background-color:rgb(255,255,255); color:rgb(76,76,76); font-family:&quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px;\'><span style=\'display:inline !important; font-style:normal; font-variant-caps:normal; font-variant-ligatures:normal; font-weight:400; letter-spacing:normal; text-align:start; text-decoration-color:initial; text-decoration-style:initial; text-indent:0px; text-transform:none; word-spacing:0px;\'>The State of California, Department of Developmental Services oversees and organizes services for individuals with developmental disabilities in California. This is achieved through a network of 21 non-profit, community-based agencies called regional centers. These regional centers are responsible for evaluating individuals, determining their eligibility for services, and providing case management.  For more information, please see the Department of Developmental Services website at </span></span><a href=\'https://www.dds.ca.gov/\' rel=\'nofollow ugc\'>Home : CA Department of Developmental Services</a></p>','public','2026-03-23T14:07:41.823270','2026-03-23T14:07:41.823275','California Department of Developmental Services','Department of Developmental Services',NULL,'d24ffdd4-5cf0-4d0b-ab34-b76bc0beac9c','State of California','2c983075d598f8d8276d3d06f376aa33f819334746a07a50e4594178c71c15fe','1.1','2026-03-23T14:07:41.823270','2026-03-23T14:07:41.823275','Health and Human Services',NULL,0,'ca-gov'),('e9c4ebdb-e747-4ccf-88b9-432af058e252','\"NEGOM CTD - n9l05s09.nc - 29.72N, 86.89W - 2000-00-01\"','The Northeastern Gulf of Mexico Physical Oceanography Program (NEGOM) is supported by the Minerals Management Service (MMS) of the U.S. Department of the Interior. Through a contract between MMS and the Texas A&M Research Foundation, several components of the Texas A&M University System are conducting the Chemical Oceanography and Hydrography study of NEGOM (NEGOM-COH). This report covers activities from October 1997 through June 1998. Data were collected from hydrographic and acoustic Doppler current profiler (ADCP) surveys conducted in the Gulf of Mexico over the continental shelf and upper slope between the Mississippi delta and Tampa Bay in water depths of 10 to 1000 m. Additionally, historical and concurrent data from other programs in this region were collected. Two hydrographic/ADCP surveys, N1 and N2, were conducted with 94 and 98 hydrographic sampling stations and with 80 and 97 expendable bathythermograph stations on respective cruises. Each survey also included continuous ADCP measurements along the cruise track. At each hydrographic sampling station continuous profiles were made of conductivity, temperature, pressure, downwelling irradiance, fluorescence, and light transmission. Up to twelve water samples were taken at each station and analyzed for dissolved oxygen and six nutrients: nitrate, nitrite, phosphate, silicate, ammonium, and urea. At 51 stations on cruise N1 and 61 on N2, water samples were filtered and analyzed for phytoplankton pigments at the surface and from the chlorophyll maximum and the low light regime immediately below it. Pigments were determined using high performance liquid chromatography. At 60 stations on each cruise, water samples were filtered and analyzed for particulate matter concentrations at surface, middle, and bottom water depths and for particulate organic carbon concentrations at surface and bottom water depths. Bottle salinity was measured at every station on the first cruise and at the shallowest and deepest stations on each cross-shelf line on the second. The instrumentation as well as calibration and sampling procedures are described in this report. The collected data were subjected to stringent quality assurance/quality control procedures.','public','2026-03-26T19:14:37.246094','2026-03-26T19:14:37.246100',NULL,NULL,NULL,'c22217d2-8480-4686-b725-130608b55a54','ioos',NULL,NULL,'2026-03-26T19:14:37.246094','2026-03-26T19:14:37.246100',NULL,NULL,NULL,'noaa-gov'),('e9e439df-fffd-4dc3-9683-35d98ff6d197','GALILEO JUPITER PLASMA RESAMPLED                                       BROWSE SPECTRA V1.0','This data set contains spin averaged count rates from selected ion      and electron channels from the Plasma Science experiment (PLS)      onboard the Galileo spacecraft during the Jupiter orbital operations      phase. Effects due to spacecraft charging and to background from high      energy penetrating radiation have not been removed.','public','2026-03-13T16:40:55.173766','2026-03-13T16:40:55.173772','planetary plasma interactions','Planetary Data System','026:00','333d8c01-1359-4a7c-8dfc-aa2e83ee163a','NASA Data.json','3406e7f9fd9a12ed08dd8a882d8be5e1194cc96ea05de60677c177ff0da892a9','1.1','2026-03-13T16:40:55.173766','2026-03-13T16:40:55.173772','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('e9f73037-efae-4239-8b73-47922f5e819d','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 4 1179 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 4 phase 2015-10-22 to 2015-12-31. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-11-13T15:11:40.000 to 2015-11-13T16:56:22.000.','public','2026-03-13T22:35:54.722588','2026-03-13T22:35:54.722597','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','0e9de36f-971a-437d-bf74-4e4d549fb3da','NASA Data.json','ff62b6ebce6929504bd24161557fd44828ca21db73258ea7d4fd8acd7333c06a','1.1','2026-03-13T22:35:54.722588','2026-03-13T22:35:54.722597','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('ea1d0ff5-1c93-42f5-ab36-02c84b2783e7','AIRSAR_TOPSAR_DEM_P','AIRSAR topographic SAR digital elevation model PTIF product','public','2026-03-13T18:35:27.434671','2026-03-13T18:35:27.434678','NASA/JPL/RDC;ASF','Earthdata Forum','026:00','12625272-ac60-41ea-afee-7e5530160f76','NASA Data.json','5cb8267cfc2eb6cc8fedeb194f0ab1af8138d9900547c43c5b7d87985b129c00','1.1','2026-03-13T18:35:27.434671','2026-03-13T18:35:27.434678','Earth Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('ea35bfb4-943c-4c34-b99a-fcb09c1b22fd','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 1 0590 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 1 phase 2014-11-20 to 2015-03-10. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-02-19T08:35:00.000 to 2015-02-19T10:34:39.000.','public','2026-03-13T18:19:46.685192','2026-03-13T18:19:46.685199','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','56d658d4-cb48-4e53-948e-e80021a69725','NASA Data.json','aa4d0517812cb07df69f839ed2121b29157fc7b411e1dd2be3a9046cb5db3660','1.1','2026-03-13T18:19:46.685192','2026-03-13T18:19:46.685199','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('ea7669a9-9295-4163-8c17-55b7992df17d','Continuous Fixed Station Water Quality Measurements in Canaveral National Seashore, October 2006 (Certified)','This dataset represents continuous water quality measurements that were taken at a fixed point in Canaveral National Seashore during the month of October, 2006 as a part of the Fixed Station Water Quality Monitoring protocol that was developed by the Southeast Coast I&M Network (SECN). The measurements were taken by a YSI 6600 ESD Multi-Parameter Long Term Water Quality Monitoring Datasonde unit that serves as the standard fixed station water quality monitoring equipment for all similar operations conducted by the SECN. The following parameters were measured at 30 minute intervals during the time period that has been specified: Water Temperature, Specific Conductivity, Salinity, Dissolved Oxygen (DO), DO Concentration, Shallow Depth, pH Level, and Turbidity. Any anomalies noted regarding these parameters have also been noted in separate fields. Please note that these measurements have been certified by network personnel.','public','2026-03-26T05:30:29.413975','2026-03-26T05:30:29.413979','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','97d0d189-7bc5-4d8d-816b-44aef4105aad','DOI NPS DCAT-US','e79717f71f44d39d44dc55a6aca912656dd8d14fce76c615f7eb17ba883a59a3','1.1','2026-03-26T05:30:29.413975','2026-03-26T05:30:29.413979','Vector Dataset','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('ea7a074a-d9d8-4fc5-9aaf-77695a722a47','AIRSAR_TOPSAR_DEM_L','AIRSAR topographic SAR digital elevation model LTIF product','public','2026-03-13T19:01:51.515368','2026-03-13T19:01:51.515374','NASA/JPL/RDC;ASF','Earthdata Forum','026:00','9b0aa87b-4d35-4091-85ca-d9e8556311c8','NASA Data.json','79c6ca698cc6cc0dbb6060e45f754bbe86ed37a2b5db2216c26159ae34d01845','1.1','2026-03-13T19:01:51.515368','2026-03-13T19:01:51.515374','Earth Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('ea8e3614-459d-4bd2-b496-34d9d5303f61','EX2107: Windows to the Deep 2021: Southeast U.S. (ROV and Mapping)','The Windows to the Deep 2021: Southeast U.S. ROV and Mapping expedition (EX-21-07) was a combined mapping and remotely operated vehicle (ROV) expedition to the Blake Plateau and Florida Straits that took place between October 26 and November 15, 2021. Operations during this 21-days at sea expedition included a combination of ROV dives in support of NOAA Ocean Exploration and its partner priorities. The primary focus of this expedition was the Blake Plateau, including its escarpment, off the coast of the Southeast U.S., but three dives were also conducted in the western and central Florida Straits due to weather conditions. Overall, 14 dives were completed, including two explorations of the water column, several dives to mound and ridgelike structures likely to be bioherms, two deeper dives to explore the steep Blake Escarpment, and one dive to document a lone sinkhole in the southeast region of the Blake Plateau. ROV dives were conducted from 300 m to 3650 meters water depth for a total of 47 hours of bottom time, and 15,800 square km were mapped using EM 304 multibeam sonar. All data associated with this expedition have been archived and are publicly available through the NOAA Archives.','public','2026-03-28T23:17:13.193133','2026-03-28T23:17:13.193139',NULL,NULL,NULL,'99d41c32-66a1-4d08-bf56-46c4be505558','NCDDC OER',NULL,NULL,'2026-03-28T23:17:13.193133','2026-03-28T23:17:13.193139',NULL,NULL,NULL,'noaa-gov'),('eabe5722-e807-4bf0-9d83-078df843c3f7','IHW COMET HALLEY RADIO CONTINUUM ARRAY DATA V1.0','NASA\'s International Halley Watch (IHW) has created a Comet Halley Archive. The collection of data spans the full wavelength range as submitted by scientists to the IHW. The observations belong to one of the following Disciplines: Amateur, Astrometry, Infrared Studies, Large-Scale Phenomena, Meteor Studies, Near-Nucleus Studies, Photometry and Polarimetry, Radio Studies, and Spectroscopy and Spectrophotometry. The data collected by these nine disciplines were augmented by Spacecraft measurements. The data were submitted to IHW, but the evaluation and selection for the Archive has been the primary responsibility of the Discipline Specialist Teams for each network in cooperation with the Lead Center. The data from the Radio Studies Continuum Subnetwork has one data file stored as a 2-d array for 1986 April 12.','public','2026-03-13T18:30:57.454174','2026-03-13T18:30:57.454179','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','2aea9809-f365-4e08-9ed0-c3889b85e3e3','NASA Data.json','4577167cd5353070c1e80566b21ead01353becf8b9b91b1a4db28541b5fb1a67','1.1','2026-03-13T18:30:57.454174','2026-03-13T18:30:57.454179','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('eac1ac30-8acb-43b2-8b93-2a10a1218c76','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 2 0826 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 2 phase 2015-03-11 to 2015-06-30. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-06-04T20:58:25.000 to 2015-06-05T06:22:14.500.','public','2026-03-13T16:37:38.494199','2026-03-13T16:37:38.494204','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','a8c8ad26-4fd5-4f66-a3cf-ef1af7f02e19','NASA Data.json','e82effbb48a309e7dee9d9eee80adb701d9e6736b922465fff529e03cc277153','1.1','2026-03-13T16:37:38.494199','2026-03-13T16:37:38.494204','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('eae00426-935b-41fe-938a-086258d5cfef','MARS EXPRESS SUN MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 7 4027 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2019-01-01 to 2020-12-31. It is a Solar Conjunction measurement and covers the time 2019-08-10T01:30:00.000 to 2019-08-10T05:25:00.000.','public','2026-03-13T16:45:21.215953','2026-03-13T16:45:21.215958','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','970c027a-bde3-40d4-a61d-849cac970d64','NASA Data.json','a9a8fddab7277da1573fdb65c2eb15acd3dfab5167b4ef4f0bd0ca23cf4234c3','1.1','2026-03-13T16:45:21.215953','2026-03-13T16:45:21.215958','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('eaea4b82-ece9-4f15-8b39-fa1f38f95c02','HUYGENS TRAJECTORY','Unknown','public','2026-03-13T19:25:08.602363','2026-03-13T19:25:08.602368','Planetary Atmospheres','Planetary Data System','026:00','c92d2b60-6de0-43dd-a7ea-b201630cfeb5','NASA Data.json','a7145e0fa7b47c3d2c2597d383bd87dbd65d2c8c659027a1ba79a6b3ab2b5cc7','1.1','2026-03-13T19:25:08.602363','2026-03-13T19:25:08.602368','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('eaf09c81-8c4d-4e00-96f7-a14612fa4de8','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RPCMIP/RPCLAP 5 ESC2 V1.0','This archive contains cross-calibrated data from the RPC-MIP and RPC-LAP instruments on-board ROSETTA Orbiter acquired during the COMET ESCORT 2 mission phase. Observations are performed in the vicinity of comet 67P/C-G. It also contains documentation which describes the RPC-MIP experiment. The data archived in this data set conform to the Planetary Data System Standards, Version 3.6.','public','2026-03-13T17:05:34.683917','2026-03-13T17:05:34.683922','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','d6871ab3-1fa2-4e09-bbb1-53cd7186b2fb','NASA Data.json','2c3097b02d0dfc80dbdf8a14c0907b5d9ae0ca7da209476417e148cca68857f2','1.1','2026-03-13T17:05:34.683917','2026-03-13T17:05:34.683922','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('eb034baa-5838-4156-a40d-d0e6460fbe99','MARS EXPRESS MARSIS REDUCED DATA SUBSURFACE EXT 2 V1.0','This dataset contains subsurface                    sounding data from the MARS EXPRESS MARS MARSIS                    EXPERIMENT DATA RECORD V2.0 Data Set that have                    been uncompressed, corrected for Automated Gain                    Control, aligned to a reference altitude and,                    except for data acquired using the SS2 mode, range                    processed after correcting for the distortion of                    the transmitted signal caused by the ionosphere.','public','2026-03-13T16:56:54.038533','2026-03-13T16:56:54.038539','planetary plasma interactions','Planetary Data System','026:00','b0045759-05d5-4349-80dc-a4b956837c16','NASA Data.json','aba154e4381337d5071c55e730a5b5abcaac07273c96ddb843a196560c0300cf','1.1','2026-03-13T16:56:54.038533','2026-03-13T16:56:54.038539','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('eb6ccdc4-afb5-4f88-9bc4-78d70d11863b','Highway-Rail Grade Crossing Incidents Within Quiet Zones Summary Report','This is the report page for Highway-Rail Grade Crossing Incidents Within Quiet Zones Summary Report.','public','2026-03-26T12:45:53.558371','2026-03-26T12:45:53.558377','Federal Railroad Administration','FRA Safety Data Team','021:27','4c94e4c5-4657-40a5-b4a2-c82c9b2fa112','DOT Socrata Data.json','03a5f95b0b29fb7aab1cc5a49f1632e7d46e0481d9c45caf676da11cbd66f5a9','1.1','2026-03-26T12:45:53.558371','2026-03-26T12:45:53.558377','Railroads','021:037',0,'dot-gov'),('eb804749-4e30-4a76-a02e-994598dbc6e9','HPMS Roadway Sample 2022','State DOTs provide the Highway Performance Monitoring System (HPMS) with the location limits of highway sections used to represent statewide aggregations based on a statistically valid Sample Panel.','public','2026-03-28T13:37:31.031644','2026-03-28T13:37:31.031649','Federal Highway Administration','Office of Highway Policy Information','021:15','41f64020-10c0-4d4e-b1d7-f789f2f8a15f','DOT Socrata Data.json','e05c8dfdf6b3890edcb0bc1514f2ec1035e1180a2d72c940dafda7d94b95f29c','1.1','2026-03-28T13:37:31.031644','2026-03-28T13:37:31.031649','Roadways and Bridges','021:009',0,'dot-gov'),('eb9c8ae1-4050-42cc-a365-b08dfe096759','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 3 0934 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 3 phase 2015-07-01 to 2015-10-21. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-08-02T03:05:00.000 to 2015-08-02T09:50:46.500.','public','2026-03-13T19:11:41.922857','2026-03-13T19:11:41.922862','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','c1a9c007-8754-4da4-9bcc-3a33d45ac694','NASA Data.json','1f63d4ddcc71c15e0cbaf397e6ab740a122acdcb2ee02200f7c4af78a77e1ad4','1.1','2026-03-13T19:11:41.922857','2026-03-13T19:11:41.922862','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('ebbee95c-1a31-4ec5-917e-c604b1bfb295','ROSETTA-ORBITER SUN RSI 1/2/3 CRUISE 2 0021 V1.0','This is a Solar Conjunction measurement covering the time 2006-03-28T00:29:04.500 to 2006-03-28T02:38:57.500.','public','2026-03-13T18:11:38.305457','2026-03-13T18:11:38.305462','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','b1825034-4aa2-40a6-9535-c113614391d3','NASA Data.json','cf1a28e353004596374bd5e3f5d686dbe7176bd1da4b764a2f9b7ddf1bd1a56f','1.1','2026-03-13T18:11:38.305457','2026-03-13T18:11:38.305462','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('ebcf6ad4-f786-421f-8dc5-f334441fc94d','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSIWAC 4 ESC3-MTP018 RDR-INFLDSTR V1.0','This CODMAC level 4 data set contains solar stray-light corrected, in-field stray-light corrected,  radiometric calibrated and geometric distortion corrected  (resampled) image data in W/m^2/sr/nm,  acquired by the OSIRIS Wide Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft  during the COMET ESCORT 3 mission phase, covering the period  from 2015-06-30T23:25:00.000 to 2015-07-28T23:24:59.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V1.0 is the first version of this dataset: Lien corrected dataset after September 2019 PSA/PDS external peer review.','public','2026-03-13T19:05:05.119382','2026-03-13T19:05:05.119387','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','7489a267-90be-485f-945f-58c4a7f0dfb9','NASA Data.json','dd5c8cdebca388713d35b14e0e377c886a1c72d3056e25fbf8d5f023d5234e2a','1.1','2026-03-13T19:05:05.119382','2026-03-13T19:05:05.119387','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('ebe27cb3-036a-47cf-9419-82be92ecf40c','IHW COMET HALLEY PHOTOMETRIC MAGNITUDES V1.0','NASA\'s International Halley Watch (IHW) has created a Comet Halley Archive. The collection of data spans the full wavelength range as submitted by scientists to the IHW. The observations belong to one of the following Disciplines: Amateur, Astrometry, Infrared Studies, Large-Scale Phenomena, Meteor Studies, Near-Nucleus Studies, Photometry and Polarimetry, Radio Studies, and Spectroscopy and Spectrophotometry. The data collected by these nine disciplines were augmented by Spacecraft measurements. The data were submitted to IHW, but the evaluation and selection for the Archive has been the primary responsibility of the Discipline Specialist Teams for each network in cooperation with the Lead Center. The Photometry and Polarimetry Network collected 3318 magnitudes for the Broadband Photometry Subnetwork. These data span the dates from 1981 December 02 to 1988 May 19.','public','2026-03-13T19:00:56.916549','2026-03-13T19:00:56.916555','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','553e3b25-6962-437d-bd52-b376424d0bc9','NASA Data.json','bdc23f8cc39d773ee53ea90414abc18984b26eab0e6eea357c3899b0b25308d0','1.1','2026-03-13T19:00:56.916549','2026-03-13T19:00:56.916555','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('ec0cc109-7294-421e-ac35-cd6be1ba231d','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 3 0964 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 3 phase 2015-07-01 to 2015-10-21. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-08-15T21:32:05.000 to 2015-08-16T05:22:29.500.','public','2026-03-13T16:48:28.824940','2026-03-13T16:48:28.824945','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','689479d1-dbd4-425a-b1f4-279fe2719c55','NASA Data.json','d21c119841e0fb257cecdff8ed3be8f1590cbd9afb1ef38e960ab55b91e0b41c','1.1','2026-03-13T16:48:28.824940','2026-03-13T16:48:28.824945','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('ec1b6bb8-c2ca-4d74-b0b6-c15e003d5e9f','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSIWAC 4 PRL-MTP002 RDR-STR-REFL V1.0','This CODMAC level 4 data set contains solar stray light corrected, radiometric calibrated and geometric distortion corrected (resampled) image data in in reflectance units (normalized and thus without unit), acquired by the OSIRIS Wide Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft during the PRELANDING mission phase, covering the period from 2014-01-20T10:00:00.000 to 2014-05-07T12:47:59.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V1.0 is the first version of this dataset: Lien corrected dataset after October 2018 PSA/PDS external peer review.','public','2026-03-13T19:19:37.037498','2026-03-13T19:19:37.037503','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','7aa9f3cd-18a2-48e7-be6b-52615d2860a8','NASA Data.json','e16626b356fcab8415dfab039273ce7da28b7cd31819795dc38472ae15ba853d','1.1','2026-03-13T19:19:37.037498','2026-03-13T19:19:37.037503','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('ec28fe62-814e-48ea-9354-0cf127ae325f','COVID-19 Reported Patient Impact and Hospital Capacity by Facility','The following datasets provides facility data for hospital utilization aggregated on a weekly basis','public','2026-03-18T17:21:46.016510','2026-03-18T17:21:46.016516','OCDO','HealthData.gov Team','009:00','d9613358-56eb-48ce-b609-997cad3ef5c6','Healthdata.gov','de99230cbe8667eaa29e0cb32c597d7550cff2bf33b05c2705adf4f6ef8afb65','1.1','2026-03-18T17:21:46.016510','2026-03-18T17:21:46.016516','Hospital','009:037',0,'hhs-gov'),('ec3fa7e5-6cb1-424a-81ad-876e3352634c','Continuous Fixed Station Water Quality Measurements in Timucuan Ecological and Historic Preserve, February 2008 (Certified)','This dataset represents continuous water quality measurements that were taken at a fixed point just outside of Timucuan Ecological and Historic Preserve during the month of February, 2008 as a part of the Fixed Station Water Quality Monitoring protocol that was developed by the Southeast Coast I&M Network (SECN). The measurements were taken by a YSI 6600 ESD Multi-Parameter Long Term Water Quality Monitoring Datasonde unit that serves as the standard fixed station water quality monitoring equipment for all similar operations conducted by the SECN. The following parameters were measured at 30 minute intervals during the time period that has been specified: Water Temperature, Specific Conductivity, Salinity, Dissolved Oxygen (DO), DO Concentration, Shallow Depth, pH Level, and Turbidity. Any anomalies noted regarding these parameters have also been noted in separate fields. Please note that these measurements have been certified by network personnel.','public','2026-03-26T05:32:40.684831','2026-03-26T05:32:40.684836','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','716a8895-af3e-4c96-9e89-9c35b1783038','DOI NPS DCAT-US','9d11afbc9388dec3e60bcaa0b1577240c66a615ea1ae9c529b994eed102fb9d1','1.1','2026-03-26T05:32:40.684831','2026-03-26T05:32:40.684836','Vector Dataset','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('ed0a5dbf-b22f-4f2e-b602-a0e15ac66c9f','BLM ID Boise District Orchard Training Area Military Proposed Poly','This is the boundary of the Orchard Training Area (OTA) in the Morley Nelson Snake River Birds of Prey (BOP) National Conservation Area (NCA). This data set is limited to the BOP area. The Orchard Training area is a training area for the Idaho Army National Guard. This is a field training area (maneuver area) for non-active duty Idaho National Guard. A 1979 Memorandum of Understanding (MOU) between BLM and the Idaho Army National Guard allows for continued military use of this area. There is public access to the Orchard Training Area and recreation and grazing is allowed in this area. This area contains the Orchard Training Area Impact Area and the Artillery Impact Area. Current to September 2009. Data Attributes include: District Name, Field Office Name, District Code, Field Office Code, Area Name and Acres.','public','2026-03-25T12:31:58.443666','2026-03-25T12:31:58.443671','Bureau of Land Management','Bureau of Land Management, blm_id_stateoffice','010:04','3465a40c-d8af-42d5-9f8d-720e95a0c020','DOI BLM DCAT-US','8639d081d715e026c9b8bfce05c07cd366a5f7671c6d95b66446cca47bf9407c','1.1','2026-03-25T12:31:58.443666','2026-03-25T12:31:58.443671','geospatial','010:000',0,'doi-gov'),('ed104c42-aeae-42bb-941e-79707fbf55ab','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 2 0853 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 2 phase 2015-03-11 to 2015-06-30. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-06-22T09:35:55.000 to 2015-06-22T18:06:25.500.','public','2026-03-13T17:20:06.250437','2026-03-13T17:20:06.250443','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','e5e3350d-380a-43c0-85cd-770ff25402d7','NASA Data.json','96ddf1b174115cc8fdd7a89f87db739bfdffa661b05fd302b91802901769f14f','1.1','2026-03-13T17:20:06.250437','2026-03-13T17:20:06.250443','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('ed13cad8-c6d7-4d34-ada3-27436232a366','BLM ID Surface Management Agency','This spatial data contains Surface Management Agency (SMA) information for Idaho from the Idaho Bureau of Land Management (BLM). For federal government lands, this data displays the managing agency of the surface of the land, which does not mean the agency \"owns\" the land. SMA is sometimes referred to as \"ownership\", although this term is inaccurate when describing public lands. This Surface Management Agency data should not be used to depict boundaries (for example National Forest, National Park, National Wildlife Refuge, or Indian Reservation boundaries among others). Attribute information for the federal and private lands are from the BLM Master Title Plats (MTPs), the BLM case files, and corresponding federal Orders and official documents. Please note that because these official sources are strictly used, OTHER NON-BLM FEDERAL AGENCY LANDS MAY NOT BE ATTRIBUTED CORRECTLY unless the proper documents have been filed with the BLM and the land actions have been noted on the MTPs.Starting in the spring of 2011 a field called Agency Name field is intended to indicate the managing agency for polygons coded as OTHER in the Management Agency field. The Agency Name field will not be used for the 100K Map Series published by the BLM for use by the public as all agencies in this field are not included in H-1553 Publication Standards Manual Handbook and, therefore, have no BLM Cartographic Standard. Except for polygons coded as OTHER in the Management Agency field, all managing agency information in the Agency Name field should be the same as that of the Management Agency field. The only intended difference between the Agency Name field and the Management Agency field is where the Management Agency is OTHER. In this case, the Agency Name will contain an abbreviation for an agency that is not represented in the H-1553 Publication Standards Manual Handbook. Examples of the agencies there are BIA (Bureau of Indian Affairs), USGS (United States Geological Survey), and FAA (Federal Aviation Administration) Attribute information for the State lands is received primarily through cooperation with the Idaho Department of Lands. This information might not reflect all State agency lands completely. A detailed analysis of State owned lands has not been done since June 2011; therefore, recent changes in ownership of State lands may not be reflected. Inclusion of State land information into this dataset is supplemental and should not be viewed as the authoritative source of State lands; please contact State agencies for questions about State lands. This data does not depict land management arrangements between government agencies such as Memorandums of Understanding or other similar agreements. When this data was originally generated in the early 2000\'s, the primary source of the geometry was the BLM Geographic Coordinate Database (GCDB), if it was available. In areas where GCDB was/is unavailable, the spatial features are taken from a variety of sources including the BLM Idaho Resource Base Data collection, BLM Idaho Master Title Plat AutoCad files, US Geological Survey Digital Line Graphs (DLGs), and US Forest Service Cartographic Feature Files (CFFs), among others (see Process Steps). It should be stressed that the geometry of a feature may not be GCDB-based in the first place, the geometry may shift away from GCDB due to a variety of reasons (topology procedures, automated software processes such as projections, etc.), and the GCDB-based features are not necessarily currently being edited to match improved GCDB. Therefore this data should NOT be considered actual GCDB data. For the latest Idaho GCDB spatial data, please contact the BLM Idaho State Office Cadastral Department at 208-373-4000. The BLM in Idaho creates and maintains this spatial data. Official actions that affect the managing agency happen often and changes to correct errors are always being made. Nevada SMA data was acquired from the BLM Nevada web site and clipped to the area that is managed by Idaho BLM Boise District.','public','2026-03-26T12:42:03.486542','2026-03-26T12:42:03.486546','Bureau of Land Management','Bureau of Land Management, blm_id_infoaccesscenter','010:04','d0020294-4152-4b5d-be9f-03793ca0e6e3','DOI BLM DCAT-US','401417da35291d12210600798d5ba08ba2f45c04e4edb8e2eb6bc49ebfdda3e5','1.1','2026-03-26T12:42:03.486542','2026-03-26T12:42:03.486546','geospatial','010:000',0,'doi-gov'),('ed1503ee-0c47-4fa0-8328-96c6b89a4a7e','Estuarine and Nearshore Marine Sediment Quality Measurements in Canaveral National Seashore (2009)','This dataset represents sediment quality measurements that were taken in Canaveral National Seashore during 2009 as a part of the marine water and sediment quality assessment protocol that was developed by the Southeast Coast I&M Network (SECN). The protocol is modeled after the EPA\'s National Coastal Assessment Program (www.epa.gov/emap/nca) and it consists of conducting sediment sampling every 10 years based on a probabilistic sampling design that was also designed by the EPA. Thirty sites were selected within and throughout Mosquito Lagoon at which sediments were sampled using a Van Veen sampler and composited for analysis as described in the National Coastal Assessment Quality Assurance Project Plan (www.epa.gov/emap/nca/html/docs/qaprojplan.html). The final analyses of the sediment samples were conducted by GPL Laboratories, LLC (now Centauri Labs); please refer to their website (www.centaurilabs.com) or the documents listed in the Cross Reference section for more information about the analytical process. Please note that each sampling location contains multiple sediment parameters that are recorded individually.','public','2026-03-26T05:32:17.930452','2026-03-26T05:32:17.930457','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','4ec16e61-e189-44db-92f5-102fdcafa013','DOI NPS DCAT-US','8ea71116b098b2a8f576a3223a1ae28fa28bfe39cf79ba585d2f7fb510e2dccd','1.1','2026-03-26T05:32:17.930452','2026-03-26T05:32:17.930457','Vector Dataset','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('ed1adb7c-eff3-48e8-864a-9b76089ba56a','Moving Violations Issued in January 2026','<p>Moving citation locations in the District of Columbia. The <a href=\'https://visionzero.dc.gov\' target=\'_blank\' rel=\'nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer\'>Vision Zero</a> data contained in this layer pertain to moving violations issued by the District of Columbia\'s Metropolitan Police Department (MPD) and partner agencies with the authority. For example, DC\'s enforcement camera program cites speeders, blocking the box, and other moving offenses. Moving violation locations are summarized ticket counts based on time of day, week of year, year, and category of violation. Data was originally extracted from the District Department of Motor Vehicle\'s eTIMS meter work order management system. Data was then loaded into the DC GIS, where the Office of the Chief Technology Officer (OCTO) geocoded citation data to the street segment level. Data are visualized using the street segment centroid coordinates.</p>','public','2026-03-25T08:38:34.817130','2026-03-25T08:38:34.817135','District Department of Transportation','DCGISopendata',NULL,'87cbfd5a-4a1a-409a-9b14-d628887add3c','DC data','6e8d5113ff8b6000d9d3b5894b24acb0d740259fe12ca6a28f47f24e922130e7','1.1','2026-03-25T08:38:34.817130','2026-03-25T08:38:34.817135','geospatial',NULL,0,'district-of-columbia'),('ed41d5d1-b44e-4ebf-9786-31ffba2402b2','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RPCMIP 3 PRL1 V2.0','This archive contains data from the RPC-MIP instrument onboard ROSETTA Orbiter, acquired during the prelanding part 1 phase at the vicinity of the comet 67P/CG. It also contains documentation which describes the MIP experiment. This is V2.0 updated after Science Review.','public','2026-03-13T18:38:05.775829','2026-03-13T18:38:05.775837','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','8722f676-815f-40aa-93c6-1b61cd896255','NASA Data.json','9bce0b58054f1c3280bcbd61c4119439142ec9b7c2c5f73cf02142bcf7f34294','1.1','2026-03-13T18:38:05.775829','2026-03-13T18:38:05.775837','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('ed509072-b4d9-4da2-b3d3-df0d9c143710','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P/CAL ALICE 2 EXT1 V2.0','This data set contains CODMAC Level 2 data acquired by the Rosetta Orbiter ALICE UV Spectrometer during the comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko Rosetta Extension 1 mission phase, which took place between 2016-01-01 and 2016-04-05. The current V2.0 data set supersedes the previous V1.0 data set with improved documentation.','public','2026-03-13T19:01:40.580901','2026-03-13T19:01:40.580907','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','c3733193-8064-4a54-9f63-6fc1336a1204','NASA Data.json','95b7f2b0ec7f07df38cabb47932c9b5a1081c254afb25f1128603eb860e7e31c','1.1','2026-03-13T19:01:40.580901','2026-03-13T19:01:40.580907','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('ed5fce31-dc2e-4d7e-a377-70c4b62c2fa7','Continuous Fixed Station Water Quality Measurements in Canaveral National Seashore, February 2007 (Certified)','This dataset represents continuous water quality measurements that were taken at a fixed point in Canaveral National Seashore during the month of February, 2007 as a part of the Fixed Station Water Quality Monitoring protocol that was developed by the Southeast Coast I&M Network (SECN). The measurements were taken by a YSI 6600 ESD Multi-Parameter Long Term Water Quality Monitoring Datasonde unit that serves as the standard fixed station water quality monitoring equipment for all similar operations conducted by the SECN. The following parameters were measured at 30 minute intervals during the time period that has been specified: Water Temperature, Specific Conductivity, Salinity, Dissolved Oxygen (DO), DO Concentration, Shallow Depth, pH Level, and Turbidity. Any anomalies noted regarding these parameters have also been noted in separate fields. Please note that these measurements have been certified by network personnel.','public','2026-03-26T05:30:39.706550','2026-03-26T05:30:39.706565','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','ac188090-2622-453a-81d1-dcb019f4c3ee','DOI NPS DCAT-US','a3c011fa007546f114647262a48926d18af570a9ff9bfb70faa06d60e56e6a45','1.1','2026-03-26T05:30:39.706550','2026-03-26T05:30:39.706565','Vector Dataset','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('ed8601c4-e8e9-414d-9165-71da078212a9','\"LATEX CTD - d94j099.nc - 28.71N, 94.67W - 1994-11-08\"','The Louisiana-Texas Shelf Physical Oceanography Program (LATEX) was sponsored by the Minerals Management Service (MMS) of the U.S. Department of the Interior. Of its three study units, the Texas-Louisiana Shelf Circulation and Transport Processes Study (LATEX A or LATEX Shelf) was conducted by the Texas A&M University System. The LATEX A field program ran from April 1992 to December 1994. The study area encompassed the Texas-Louisiana continental shelf offshore of approximately the 10-m isobath, from the Mississippi River to the Rio Grande. The five major field components were: moored current meter measurements, drifting buoys, hydrography, acoustic Doppler current profiling (Acoustic Doppler Current Profiler (ADCP)), and meteorological buoys.','public','2026-03-26T19:15:07.190691','2026-03-26T19:15:07.190697',NULL,NULL,NULL,'dd29c866-61ca-4e2d-9ec6-b0e3f478839b','ioos',NULL,NULL,'2026-03-26T19:15:07.190691','2026-03-26T19:15:07.190697',NULL,NULL,NULL,'noaa-gov'),('eda9bb98-303a-4f30-a924-029b0ccb7c37','LP MOON GAMMA RAY SPECTROMETER 3 RDR V1.0','This data set contains processed LP-GRS time-series data that are used as the fundamental data for deriving composition measurements of the lunar surface using either energy window techniques or the full modeling of the neutron and gamma ray transport processes. These data have been processed to eliminate bad data as well as to make corrections due to time variations in the cosmic ray flux, LP-GRS gain, LP-GRS orientation, and altitude above the lunar surface.','public','2026-03-13T19:27:45.476626','2026-03-13T19:27:45.476635','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','0e9c26f7-85e7-485f-a321-ba2cabfc9e95','NASA Data.json','5db5575aaa20a89176176c39324e0278f282f3a921e3b6494d4f5a74ce52f8c8','1.1','2026-03-13T19:27:45.476626','2026-03-13T19:27:45.476635','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('edc8ba51-5b25-4a9c-ba8a-5cfe121f879a','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P SREM 2 ESCORT 2 MTP017 V1.0','This data set contains count rates (1/s) as measured by the Standard Radiation Environment Monitor (SREM) instrument on the Rosetta spacecraft, along with their standard deviations. The primary target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko. These are CODMAC Level 2 Experiment Data Record data, and provide a measure of the radiation in the spacecraft environment during the Medium Term Plan 17 period of the ESCORT 2 mission phase.','public','2026-03-13T19:38:10.425475','2026-03-13T19:38:10.425483','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','3de74f15-6ba1-475b-930b-6643c23768d5','NASA Data.json','d689079dd39eb0fa06001ce68a224ef75e72a6f2b0cedf6e15d9d451c3983418','1.1','2026-03-13T19:38:10.425475','2026-03-13T19:38:10.425483','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('ede3309f-e63f-4865-9754-2e2f247e1c78','Occupational Licensing Training Search Portal','Find training requirements for obtaining or renewing a license, TCEQ approved training providers, and the courses each one offers.','public','2026-03-25T14:33:40.523487','2026-03-25T14:33:40.523493','data.austintexas.gov','TCEQ Information Resources Division',NULL,'2180f763-001f-41fd-9e12-ff5f46fb684c','City of Austin Data.json','17cfbf10de4d644bc707c12b1bd715b64b4e6e834ca81b2f149c6803c16abd22','1.1','2026-03-25T14:33:40.523487','2026-03-25T14:33:40.523493',NULL,NULL,0,'city-of-austin'),('edf069c7-ab40-4fd2-af54-c42b38c1bcb9','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 2 0765 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 2 phase 2015-03-11 to 2015-06-30. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-05-10T22:16:40.000 to 2015-05-11T01:46:20.000.','public','2026-03-13T18:16:11.487290','2026-03-13T18:16:11.487295','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','cb54eef7-4994-4826-a654-204323cadb26','NASA Data.json','0e81c22188b482e29cc037b7fb0dba731dd2a5bb7da781d15f02a83714e9ae9e','1.1','2026-03-13T18:16:11.487290','2026-03-13T18:16:11.487295','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('edf0c98a-90e2-4c55-87ff-52b871604a42','PHOENIX MARS ROBOTIC ARM CAMERA 2 EDR  VERSION 1.0','The Robotic Arm Camera (RAC)  experiment on the Mars Phoenix Lander consists of one instrument  component plus command electronics. This RAC Imaging Operations EDR  data set contains raw data from the Robotic Arm Camera (RAC).','public','2026-03-13T17:45:24.712953','2026-03-13T17:45:24.712960','Imaging','Planetary Data System','026:00','9463a504-3a66-4b30-98f9-27e580268247','NASA Data.json','d5e24f3e4756274e3bf4bd1f2eb120e38d01ad2979a6827c3030e0341382788a','1.1','2026-03-13T17:45:24.712953','2026-03-13T17:45:24.712960','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('ee1a3c0a-62f8-4e87-949f-ef4f63fd2c5f','HPMS Statewide Summaries 2020','The Highway Performance Management System (HPMS) Statewide Summaries table contains demographic and system length estimates for all Urban and Rural public roads, functionally classified as minor collector in rural areas or local in any area, summarized by State. In addition, this dataset contains daily vehicle-miles traveled (VMT) estimates for all public roads located in Small Urban areas, functionally classified as minor collector or local.','public','2026-03-28T13:39:10.437272','2026-03-28T13:39:10.437278','Federal Highway Administration','Office of Highway Policy Information','021:15','161b5d9b-e130-4f8a-8ae7-5d6a4a474e34','DOT Socrata Data.json','672f998af5d4423053ee2da2a59f8ac3fc8fdaca43f7ec49fa094a43badf0845','1.1','2026-03-28T13:39:10.437272','2026-03-28T13:39:10.437278','Roadways and Bridges','021:009',0,'dot-gov'),('ee4f35df-94c3-4aaf-a697-4c3e4a5c618b','ROSETTA-ORBITER COMET ESCORT 3 OSINAC 2 EDR MTP018 V2.0','This data set contains images acquired by the OSIRIS Narrow Angle Camera during the COMET ESCORT 3 phase of the Rosetta mission at the comet 67P, covering the period from 2015-06-30T23:25:00.000 to 2015-07-28T23:24:59.000. This version V2.0 supersedes previous deliveries of the same dataset.','public','2026-03-13T16:49:05.707950','2026-03-13T16:49:05.707955','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','3ceacb14-3414-4fe5-a1cd-82cbfe4cceab','NASA Data.json','f2be23c7ac6ca2b2b14690c63e95e001c476d0b3034696ce9decec1adc969596','1.1','2026-03-13T16:49:05.707950','2026-03-13T16:49:05.707955','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('ee6fb0f5-0dae-4d80-b18b-29f49e5a297d','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RPCICA 3 EXT2 CALIB V1.0','This dataset contains CALIBRATED DATA from the RPCICA instrument onmission ROSETTA during Rosetta extension 2.Data contains measurements of solar wind interactionwith the atmosphere of target comet 67P.','public','2026-03-13T16:54:24.389917','2026-03-13T16:54:24.389922','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','5eea2f34-1b99-4325-a5c7-67c097b9c50e','NASA Data.json','0c6f45669286418baf44748c8891b29f51aee867bca7a8f797f8f2b065ef4d2b','1.1','2026-03-13T16:54:24.389917','2026-03-13T16:54:24.389922','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('ee8dc655-6a0a-4b75-8575-3c304827c26b','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P MIDAS 3 ESC2 SAMPLES V3.0','The Micro-Imaging Dust Analysis System (MIDAS) is an instrument on theROSETTA Orbiter that will provide 3D images and statistical parametersof pristine cometary particles, collected in the vicinity of comet67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko. This data set includes all data from theCOMET ESCORT 2 mission phase.This release supersedes version 2.0.','public','2026-03-13T16:57:30.963900','2026-03-13T16:57:30.963906','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','38baf8b0-9523-46b5-be7f-e939627db8e5','NASA Data.json','82db337807918ce66d0d0d71f62bff717e2a00663ed2dd97cac75a06b267167c','1.1','2026-03-13T16:57:30.963900','2026-03-13T16:57:30.963906','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('eebfed2e-bd40-4461-9209-d4c781682df7','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSINAC 4 PRL-MTP002 RDR-REFLECT V1.0','This CODMAC level 4 data set contains radiometric calibrated and geometric distortion corrected (resampled) image data in reflectance units (normalized and thus without unit), acquired by the OSIRIS Narrow Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft during the PRELANDING mission phase, covering the period from 2014-01-20T10:00:00.000 to 2014-05-07T12:47:59.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V1.0 is the first version of this dataset: Lien corrected dataset after October 2018 PSA/PDS external peer review.','public','2026-03-13T18:46:38.346095','2026-03-13T18:46:38.346100','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','b24b5a56-7e1d-4925-a2fe-8a65c7da7e83','NASA Data.json','5982148df1e5a163757ff6654cbcc51cb191fa13756f9313f02bbf0eb26de5df','1.1','2026-03-13T18:46:38.346095','2026-03-13T18:46:38.346100','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('eec2cfb3-0b6b-4df2-a1ec-c7677e5e3526','Texas Commission on Environmental Quality - Occupational Licensing Training','Find training requirements for obtaining or renewing a license, TCEQ approved training providers, and the courses each one offers.','public','2026-03-25T14:42:59.746326','2026-03-25T14:42:59.746335','data.austintexas.gov','TCEQ Information Resources Division',NULL,'2b2c6271-34d4-43b4-a110-950123929959','City of Austin Data.json','55150e1299b18251005fde4a640f03fab9a0c7665b6d6ead28c65310ab5f6109','1.1','2026-03-25T14:42:59.746326','2026-03-25T14:42:59.746335',NULL,NULL,0,'city-of-austin'),('eedbb99c-c79d-4593-a7cc-5fd488fd52a4','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RPCICA 4 ESC1 CORR-CTS V1.0','This dataset contains corrected and RESAMPLED RAW DATA fromthe RPCICA instrument on mission ROSETTA during Comet escort 1.The data has been corrected for cross-talk using an automatic algorithm,and noise has been treated to be even regardless of onward noisesuppression. The data is the same as L4 CORR but in counts, not physicalunits. The data may due to noise treatment have negative values.Data contains measurements of solar wind interactionwith the atmosphere of target comet 67P.','public','2026-03-13T16:45:42.840524','2026-03-13T16:45:42.840529','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','ff31119a-b2e2-4e12-8b3f-2ef48af0e83b','NASA Data.json','b56be4bec8946742f8a77843be949e962fec5616ae19862c0eafcf5e1abed87f','1.1','2026-03-13T16:45:42.840524','2026-03-13T16:45:42.840529','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('eedf4975-870d-4e92-80b2-08e5fb52121c','STOOKE SMALL BODIES MAPS V3.0','These maps of small solar system bodies have been prepared by Philip Stooke of the University of Western Ontario. This data set includes 270 map sheets of six asteroids, five planetary satellites, and three comets, all prepared from spacecraft images. This data set was updated in 2015 with the addition of 44 new map sheets.','public','2026-03-13T17:37:19.426547','2026-03-13T17:37:19.426553','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','78df6879-7e59-41c9-b61c-e20f4b198575','NASA Data.json','cb6fc2e943418c5fc79f4152bfbf5b1b8956d9324b5e4bd37403077e7b296dbc','1.1','2026-03-13T17:37:19.426547','2026-03-13T17:37:19.426553','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('eee4d77b-4c2c-47e6-809e-731fe8d4df62','NHTSA Vehicle Recalls Completion Rates','NHTSA Vehicle Recalls Completion Rates','public','2026-03-27T12:59:15.565862','2026-03-27T12:59:15.565867','National Highway Traffic Safety Administration','NHTSA-Datahub','021:18','73b6c94c-3c2a-498f-9c0d-bbfbe5f4a6d8','DOT Socrata Data.json','7c47e97c08789ece2d94ffa9a05f1b35e25d4e96f394155b868dab24450c0868','1.1','2026-03-27T12:59:15.565862','2026-03-27T12:59:15.565867','Automobiles','021:031',0,'dot-gov'),('eefde2ba-64f7-4fec-b43f-5b8c6bd23626','AIRSAR_TOPSAR_C-BAND_DEM_AND_STOKES','AIRSAR topographic SAR digital elevation model C_Stokes product','public','2026-03-13T18:35:40.791841','2026-03-13T18:35:40.791849','NASA/JPL/RDC;ASF','Earthdata Forum','026:00','0f2f8f7b-e286-4dc3-88fe-6bebeabaa9ae','NASA Data.json','0a813a47cce623b120cd7476d12220c7a2f3bdbabd43e25ff6e43d190ae5641c','1.1','2026-03-13T18:35:40.791841','2026-03-13T18:35:40.791849','Earth Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('ef091009-8a86-4ca4-82a4-6177aff05294','DID(IT) - Digital Innovation & Development - Information Technology-electronic Working Reporting Tracking System: Requests for A-Files','Requests for A-Files accurately records and tracks A-File requests at the NRC and the actions taken to respond to those requests. ','non-public','2026-03-22T11:55:49.212965','2026-03-22T11:55:49.212970','Unspecified','Open Data (MGMT)','024:030','809196a6-0409-4e01-bb2a-7b61412337d2','DHS datajson source','f0df61d5a5514bd0deab6d66eab09b2a2313aa05563dff8f9ddf76ba710f31a8','1.1','2026-03-22T11:55:49.212965','2026-03-22T11:55:49.212970',NULL,'024:000',0,'dhs-gov'),('ef0bd5f4-06c4-4fcd-97a0-079b62e18172','Hydrographic and Impairment Statistics Database: NPS-WSR Housatonic Wild and Scenic River','Hydrographic and Impairment Statistics (HIS) is a National Park Service (NPS) Water Resources Division (WRD) project established to track certain goals created in response to the Government Performance and Results Act of 1993 (GPRA). One water resources management goal established by the Department of the Interior under GRPA requires NPS to track the percent of its managed surface waters that are meeting Clean Water Act (CWA) water quality standards. This goal requires an accurate inventory that spatially quantifies the surface water hydrography that each bureau manages and a procedure to determine and track which waterbodies are or are not meeting water quality standards as outlined by Section 303(d) of the CWA. This project helps meet this DOI GRPA goal by inventorying and monitoring in a geographic information system for the NPS: (1) CWA 303(d) quality impaired waters and causes; and (2) hydrographic statistics based on the United States Geological Survey (USGS) National Hydrography Dataset (NHD). Hydrographic and 303(d) impairment statistics were evaluated based on a combination of 1:24,000 (NHD) and finer scale data (frequently provided by state GIS layers).','public','2026-03-29T06:05:42.923802','2026-03-29T06:05:42.923807','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','63416205-c6f7-44ce-905f-78633889a268','DOI NPS DCAT-US','30a837d3e2cdff3ab59e9bde810a07490e547afddcad31b424b499f648a39527','1.1','2026-03-29T06:05:42.923802','2026-03-29T06:05:42.923807','geospatial','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('ef1ddf00-80f5-4ff5-ba92-17424905f62e','Wetland Delineation Field Data Collection Application','Database designed for deployment on iOS mobile devices for collecting wetland determination data.','public','2026-03-25T05:11:45.433446','2026-03-28T05:45:23.068931','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','2d385aff-21ce-4929-9c10-1c1b95cd984f','DOI NPS DCAT-US','940ba68416c6443fe9c8031a756d42caef2168475a29ca8b3897872917eca118','1.1','2026-03-25T05:11:45.433446','2026-03-28T05:45:23.068931','Relational Database','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('ef2dc7c3-db69-417d-91da-21976684fb15','V15/V16 VENUS ROE 5 OCC ELECTRON DENS V1.0','This dataset contains 29 ionospheric electron density profiles (EDS files)derived from Venera 15 and 16 radio occultation data. A total of 155profiles are believed to be available and it is hoped that all willeventually be archived.','public','2026-03-13T19:57:42.742936','2026-03-13T19:57:42.742942','planetary plasma interactions','Planetary Data System','026:00','82dda54e-0e8b-40d4-b3d6-5cc6b4ca7725','NASA Data.json','b5f8d801d41b6f3e9186560ccb9e50eb9a0cd7c74563f1f0a88ae2bb3300cafd','1.1','2026-03-13T19:57:42.742936','2026-03-13T19:57:42.742942','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('ef3b714c-807a-46c0-902d-439dddd2fc1a','ROSETTA-ORBITER CHECKOUT OSINAC 3 CR2 RDR V2.0','This CODMAC level 3 data set contains radiometric calibrated image data in W/m^2/sr/nm,  acquired by the OSIRIS Narrow Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft  during the CRUISE 2 mission phase, covering the period  from 2005-04-05T00:00:00.000 to 2006-07-28T23:59:59.000. The prime objective was commissioning / calibration. Several targets of opportunity were observed, but none of them is identifiable as prime target. This version V2.0 supersedes previous deliveries of the same dataset with the following changes since the last version: Reprocessed dataset after October 2018 PSA/PDS external peer review.','public','2026-03-13T22:43:36.342324','2026-03-13T22:43:36.342330','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','d50bca99-953d-41a6-8739-ebdcc938b42b','NASA Data.json','4fb8a17df03ea3b7499ffd7ec9969ea9863e33d4f34f5955c0a1b0c35b26f6d9','1.1','2026-03-13T22:43:36.342324','2026-03-13T22:43:36.342330','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('ef46a07f-d0e3-4c44-8fe7-2ac7f8aaea3e','EX2107: Windows to the Deep 2021: Southeast U.S. (ROV and Mapping)','The Windows to the Deep 2021: Southeast U.S. ROV and Mapping expedition (EX-21-07) was a combined mapping and remotely operated vehicle (ROV) expedition to the Blake Plateau and Florida Straits that took place between October 26 and November 15, 2021. Operations during this 21-days at sea expedition included a combination of ROV dives in support of NOAA Ocean Exploration and its partner priorities. The primary focus of this expedition was the Blake Plateau, including its escarpment, off the coast of the Southeast U.S., but three dives were also conducted in the western and central Florida Straits due to weather conditions. Overall, 14 dives were completed, including two explorations of the water column, several dives to mound and ridgelike structures likely to be bioherms, two deeper dives to explore the steep Blake Escarpment, and one dive to document a lone sinkhole in the southeast region of the Blake Plateau. ROV dives were conducted from 300 m to 3650 meters water depth for a total of 47 hours of bottom time, and 15,800 square km were mapped using EM 304 multibeam sonar. All data associated with this expedition have been archived and are publicly available through the NOAA Archives.','public','2026-03-28T23:16:55.430666','2026-03-28T23:16:55.430673',NULL,NULL,NULL,'c59162e9-5dfd-4161-b415-28bc82f3d60b','NCDDC OER',NULL,NULL,'2026-03-28T23:16:55.430666','2026-03-28T23:16:55.430673',NULL,NULL,NULL,'noaa-gov'),('ef80ea23-bde5-45a0-aa98-c97c6b36a901','COMET HALLEY ARCHIVE - INFRARED PHOTOMETRY','The INFRARED PHOTOMETRY Network contains 2204 observations of Comet Halley spanning dates from 1984 Sep 14 through 1988 Apr 08.','public','2026-03-13T17:46:17.949563','2026-03-13T17:46:17.949568','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','c3a3bcaa-5c6d-4091-b647-5fb989992efd','NASA Data.json','70bc762005d8e8c8d620b0f87cc5dec233cbeb92b6dc50ee525ae31cb9745bc3','1.1','2026-03-13T17:46:17.949563','2026-03-13T17:46:17.949568','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('efacfa36-fe52-4e91-b628-93905f80b07a','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P SREM 5 ESCORT 2 MTP016 V1.0','This data set contains derived electron and proton flux energies in MeV from the Standard Radiation Environment Monitor (SREM) instrument on the Rosetta spacecraft, which had the primary target of comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko. These are CODMAC Level 5 derived data, and measure the radiation in the spacecraft environment during the Medium Term Plan 16 period of the ESCORT 2 mission phase.','public','2026-03-13T19:15:40.007855','2026-03-13T19:15:40.007860','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','2aa93008-4d0d-4490-8f84-9ec8a24d0034','NASA Data.json','e90b34d9ba5b75b65bcf679a094a6a9fb70e47a33fd67fcee29d6ddf67a809d5','1.1','2026-03-13T19:15:40.007855','2026-03-13T19:15:40.007860','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('efbaef13-7b14-4520-a58f-28cb466e8545','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 PRELANDING 0229 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the PRELANDING phase 2014-01-21 to 2014-11-18. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2014-08-21T18:51:30.000 to 2014-08-22T01:19:27.500.','public','2026-03-13T18:48:01.356560','2026-03-13T18:48:01.356569','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','16382e36-938f-4bf2-a894-d5feeccfa936','NASA Data.json','cf1042decb0ae4a54c0ff6ebb98fd9d2a2f444e116a416a1d50c96e5c46b56d7','1.1','2026-03-13T18:48:01.356560','2026-03-13T18:48:01.356569','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('efe63856-0f25-4471-bf52-67390699da59','FTB EITC Summary of CA Residents Jan 2026','Produced by the Economic & Statistical Research Bureau, monthly tabulations of tax filings statistics for the Earned Income Tax Credit (EITC), Young Child Tax Credit (YCTC) and Foster Youth Tax Credit (FYTC) provide credit use by county, preparer type, credit amount allowed number of dependents and a many other useful cross-sections','public','2026-03-23T13:57:19.985173','2026-03-23T13:57:19.985178','California Franchise Tax Board','FTB Open Data',NULL,'d08fd5ce-287e-4a44-9244-2993a565a080','State of California','8b32bb12c330800c3b83c59c01e3cc9375ebfafee780ad1323c6f5c85d13a0bd','1.1','2026-03-23T13:57:19.985173','2026-03-23T13:57:19.985178','Economy and Demographics',NULL,0,'ca-gov'),('f00f087b-c4fc-48d4-bfe3-af0c0fb42deb','MARS EXPRESS MARS MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 3 3376 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2010-01-01 to 2012-12-31. It is a Global Gravity measurement and covers the time 2012-12-01T01:39:26.000 to 2012-12-01T04:49:05.500.','public','2026-03-13T18:20:32.401949','2026-03-13T18:20:32.401956','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','99553313-1d5a-4827-9662-0aeabaf7122b','NASA Data.json','da969c348cc032f87bf75675625939ebc569cdda5e650dce39b8c6ab285115f8','1.1','2026-03-13T18:20:32.401949','2026-03-13T18:20:32.401956','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('f016d56f-c363-4f9a-9796-ad6abc97f366','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 PRELANDING 0206 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the PRELANDING phase 2014-01-21 to 2014-11-18. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2014-08-14T13:46:35.000 to 2014-08-14T19:06:07.500.','public','2026-03-13T18:54:49.787805','2026-03-13T18:54:49.787810','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','b1472b07-91ee-4315-98ee-54b44f89dba3','NASA Data.json','0fdd1e74ed073641d73b82e06f8a7cee293bccd301f6817d921a411e27bb8a97','1.1','2026-03-13T18:54:49.787805','2026-03-13T18:54:49.787810','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('f01e78c4-489a-4ab5-8c4a-1d61a52092d4','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 4 1140 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 4 phase 2015-10-22 to 2015-12-31. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-10-29T20:05:10.000 to 2015-10-29T22:35:14.000.','public','2026-03-13T17:06:51.390289','2026-03-13T17:06:51.390294','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','500d3646-cc3f-42b2-82bf-82c450a8ba02','NASA Data.json','bfec4849820ac5b98a47ae2e30087a21dfa6a4849d9d309d6166f01e49c4a9f0','1.1','2026-03-13T17:06:51.390289','2026-03-13T17:06:51.390294','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('f0455e16-ee80-42c7-8837-52d552c35035','MARS EXPRESS MARSIS REDUCED DATA SUBSURFACE EXT 3 V1.0','This dataset contains subsurface                    sounding data from the MARS EXPRESS MARS MARSIS                    EXPERIMENT DATA RECORD V2.0 Data Set that have                    been uncompressed, corrected for Automated Gain                    Control, aligned to a reference altitude and,                    except for data acquired using the SS2 mode, range                    processed after correcting for the distortion of                    the transmitted signal caused by the ionosphere.','public','2026-03-13T18:04:10.521140','2026-03-13T18:04:10.521146','planetary plasma interactions','Planetary Data System','026:00','f61702a0-7eaa-49d9-abab-cc16319c6c8b','NASA Data.json','63043bbfb11b560b044a53df5754d9335132510f8ac6ac563dc8df4780520bb2','1.1','2026-03-13T18:04:10.521140','2026-03-13T18:04:10.521146','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('f07a8016-fdd3-4a11-bf4c-6144d093fcc8','Great Smoky Mountains National Park 1991-2025 Noland Divide Water Quality Monitoring Data from the GRSM_ND Project as of 2026-03-04','This data package was created 2026-03-04 09:45:35 by NPSTORET and includes selected project, location, and result data.\n\nData contained in the Great Smoky Mountains National Park NPSTORET back-end file (GRSM_NPSTORET_BE_20260302.ACCDB) were filtered to include:\n\nOrganization:\n- GRSM: Great Smoky Mountains National Park\nProject:\n- GRSM_ND: GRSM Noland Divide Water Quality Monitoring\nStation:\n- Include Trip QC And All Station Visit Results\nValue Status:\n- Accepted or Certified (exported as Final) or Final\n\nThe data package is organized into five data tables:\n- Projects.csv - describes the purpose and background of the monitoring efforts\n- Locations.csv - documents the attributes of the monitoring locations/stations\n- Results.csv - contains the field measurements, observations, and/or lab analyses for each sample/event/data grouping\n- HUC.csv - enumerates the domain of allowed values for 8-digit and 12-digit hydrologic unit codes utilized by the Locations data table\n- Characteristics.csv - enumerates the domain of characteristics available in NPSTORET to identify what was sampled, measured or observed in Results\n\nPeriod of record for filtered data is 1991-07-05 to 2025-12-22.  This data package is a snapshot in time of one National Park Service project. The most current data for this project, which may be more or less extensive than that in this data package, can be found on the Water Quality Portal at:\n\nhttps://www.waterqualitydata.us/data/Result/search?project=GRSM_ND&mimeType=csv&zip=yes&dataProfile=biological&providers=STORET','public','2026-03-19T03:35:17.895922','2026-03-19T03:35:17.895928','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','42e1fb34-8021-4f15-9090-88ca55dd0915','DOI NPS DCAT-US','5b3d2dcb0279c7f4c45b0d31a1a1f0babb883cad6f3c18c21b1104aa34ab9858','1.1','2026-03-19T03:35:17.895922','2026-03-19T03:35:17.895928','Data Package','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('f0a29f24-c44d-40d1-9f8d-69c8c0520021','BLM OR Leases and Claims Polygon Hub','LSE_CLM_POLY: This dataset is a spatial representation of Leases and Claims (LSE_CLM).  It is a portion of the total encumbrance data category that includes information about entities, rights, and restrictions relating to the use of Federal minerals.  This dataset contains Leases and Claims within Oregon and Washington BLM-administered lands (surface and subsurface) and over mineral estate in areas of split estate (i.e., areas where the BLM administers Federal mineral estate, but the surface is not owned by the BLM).','public','2026-03-18T11:12:26.027987','2026-03-18T11:12:26.027996','Bureau of Land Management','Bureau of Land Management, gkrosts','010:04','a0b82dc5-e974-4ab4-83d9-1ee5a024ac62','DOI BLM DCAT-US','e0f9474e33ce06b29278355c6d6d0f2cb42ef52a35626398f5b98f4f9257614c','1.1','2026-03-18T11:12:26.027987','2026-03-18T11:12:26.027996','geospatial','010:000',0,'doi-gov'),('f0a793d8-3f48-4f95-9dd8-af7f491512c8','MARS EXPRESS MARS MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 3 3371 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2010-01-01 to 2012-12-31. It is a Global Gravity measurement and covers the time 2012-08-19T03:02:23.000 to 2012-08-19T05:56:00.500.','public','2026-03-13T17:14:45.464699','2026-03-13T17:14:45.464704','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','b757a587-f0f1-40df-81a7-de4008435119','NASA Data.json','3f41826057568fc16297061494da61822651bc61744c67fa4798a4a3c7e5f8a0','1.1','2026-03-13T17:14:45.464699','2026-03-13T17:14:45.464704','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('f0c40873-c917-4e68-a8cf-e1129824d302','Vegetation - Mojave Desert National Preserve [ds3128]','<div style=\'text-align:Left;\'><div><div><p style=\'margin:0 0 0 0;\'><span>This study presents a comprehensive vegetation mapping inventory project undertaken in Mojave National Preserve (MOJA) and Castle Mountains National Monument (CAMO), two areas within the National Park Service’s Mojave Desert Network (MOJN). Covering a combined area of over 1.6 million acres along the California-Nevada border, these sites encompass diverse desert ecosystems, including valleys, washes, sand dunes, volcanic formations, and Joshua tree forests. The project, initiated in 2010 by the National Park Service’s Vegetation Mapping Inventory (VMI), aimed to document and classify the plant communities in these areas. </span></p><p style=\'margin:0 0 0 0;\'><span /><span /></p><p style=\'margin:0 0 0 0;\'><span>The project unfolded over six phases between 2011 and 2021, starting with a review of existing vegetation data and the development of a comprehensive work plan. In collaboration with the California Native Plant Society (CNPS) and the University of Nevada, Las Vegas (UNLV), field data were collected from 630 plots and observation points, supplemented by 588 samples from previous studies. The data were used to classify 67 plant alliances and two landform types, ultimately identifying 136 plant associations within MOJA and CAMO. </span></p><p style=\'margin:0 0 0 0;\'><span /><span /></p><p style=\'margin:0 0 0 0;\'><span>The vegetation map for the project, covering the entire 1.6-million-acre area, was created using a hybrid mapping approach that combined manual and automated techniques. The map was based on 2018 National Agriculture Imagery Program (NAIP) basemap data and was validated through ground-based verification efforts. The accuracy of the final vegetation map was assessed at 91%, with a Kappa value of 92%, indicating a high level of reliability. The minimum mapping unit is 1.2 acres (0.5 hectares). </span></p><p style=\'margin:0 0 0 0;\'><span /><span /></p><p style=\'margin:0 0 0 0;\'><span>The final products of this project include a spatial geodatabase, digital field photos, metadata, a classification report, and a field key to the vegetation alliances. These resources provide a valuable tool for ongoing research and conservation efforts in these ecologically significant areas. </span></p><p style=\'margin:0 0 0 0;\'><span /></p><p><span>More information can be found in the project report, which is bundled with the vegetation map published for BIOS here: </span><span style=\'text-decoration:underline;\'>https://filelib.wildlife.ca.gov/Public/BDB/GIS/BIOS/Public_Datasets/3100_3199/ds3128.zip</span></p><p style=\'margin:0 0 0 0;\'><span /></p><p style=\'margin:0 0 0 0;\'><span /></p><p style=\'margin:0 0 0 0;\'><span /></p></div></div></div>','public','2026-03-23T14:02:04.779226','2026-03-23T14:02:04.779231','California Department of Fish and Wildlife','BIOS_Admin',NULL,'981a5fd1-005b-4dae-86a1-f3b1a51e99fd','State of California','84d57a8dd148e922316fe2d5211f4127238ac8c5cc3709a8206b3d3ea6993e8b','1.1','2026-03-23T14:02:04.779226','2026-03-23T14:02:04.779231','Natural Resources',NULL,0,'ca-gov'),('f104d384-f330-424d-89d8-8fae22fa07aa','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 PRELANDING 0288 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the PRELANDING phase 2014-01-21 to 2014-11-18. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2014-09-11T17:24:29.000 to 2014-09-12T01:05:11.000.','public','2026-03-13T18:15:51.116472','2026-03-13T18:15:51.116478','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','4dd66c8a-059e-497e-bf52-fbb6c9fd0394','NASA Data.json','107dc25bbbafd67fb716a902fe0df8a04451180b2157c4d4b8e46b2688d2b999','1.1','2026-03-13T18:15:51.116472','2026-03-13T18:15:51.116478','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('f14fdb86-b939-4214-bba5-2050967ae8e5','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 4 1197 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 4 phase 2015-10-22 to 2015-12-31. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-11-21T07:42:20.000 to 2015-11-21T16:43:24.000.','public','2026-03-13T19:56:01.714780','2026-03-13T19:56:01.714786','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','a2e58f1e-d466-448e-b3d6-fd75dd89dacf','NASA Data.json','0a332c9e3d058ba9a368cfac5e8bfbe75c5c2978665d1c52ea06d9e76221eb15','1.1','2026-03-13T19:56:01.714780','2026-03-13T19:56:01.714786','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('f1582270-839c-4167-bd56-8f4449ffdef5','VG1/VG2 SATURN IRIS 3 RDR V1.0','The data set contains measurements from both the infrared interferometer spectrometer and the broadband reflected solar radiometer and ancillary data. The data set is ordered by time as measured by the Flight Data System Count (FDSC). This represents the data frame number, modulo 60. Also included is pointing and other information on the geometry associated with a given data record.','public','2026-03-13T16:50:39.165970','2026-03-13T16:50:39.165978','Planetary Atmospheres','Planetary Data System','026:00','aa859b43-8046-428e-9d1f-0b0d2119a66f','NASA Data.json','9508bfa45465695a8b4f9f617f7403e511ff73d73d4fc1869a3f43aaafb57909','1.1','2026-03-13T16:50:39.165970','2026-03-13T16:50:39.165978','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('f17ef925-9912-4a5d-8e32-60ef1b31e808','NEAR NLR DATA FOR CRUISE4','NEAR EDR volume sets contain a single data set, from one instrument and one mission phase (defined in the phase table in /AAREADME.TXT).','public','2026-03-13T17:14:22.525096','2026-03-13T17:14:22.525101','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','eaa722c4-7df4-4fb9-844b-57b8111f1abe','NASA Data.json','9b6852d5cde32a1af53f167f230a76b0133488d30091c97530ed1617e4dd32c9','1.1','2026-03-13T17:14:22.525096','2026-03-13T17:14:22.525101','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('f197ad65-7013-4f37-90b5-c5930ad7132a','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P ROSINA 4 EXT1 V2.0','This data set contains CODMAC level 4 science data acquired by the ROSINA COPS sensor between 2016-01-13 and 2016-04-05 during the Extension phase 1 of the Rosetta mission to comet 67P/CG. V2.0: Minor species (CH4, NH3, HCN, H2CO, C2H6, CH3OH, H2S, C2H5OH, OCS, CS2) detected by DFMS were added.','public','2026-03-13T17:04:23.054336','2026-03-13T17:04:23.054342','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','7ac99bf8-b984-4618-9fe6-20f0ebb7830f','NASA Data.json','02ea8242666bbd2ce047e0db1eb7c688763d103e779b042f13325b59d5db48c4','1.1','2026-03-13T17:04:23.054336','2026-03-13T17:04:23.054342','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('f1995047-ae9b-4058-91c8-65d09893a7da','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 4 1199 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 4 phase 2015-10-22 to 2015-12-31. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-11-22T07:44:00.000 to 2015-11-22T16:41:41.000.','public','2026-03-13T17:04:16.482022','2026-03-13T17:04:16.482030','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','1464a24f-5a03-416a-a44b-5bf0684ac644','NASA Data.json','c2aa1ddc9cbf350e4a58d8ef1bf482951ef023f62981db6e1d03f32f92d4462c','1.1','2026-03-13T17:04:16.482022','2026-03-13T17:04:16.482030','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('f1b3966e-53b8-4f62-a7b6-25adaa6e653d','IRAS MINOR PLANET SURVEY V6.0','The Supplemental IRAS Minor Planet Survey (SIMPS) presents additional and revised diameters and albedos for asteroids detected by the 1983 IRAS mission. SIMPS is considered to supersede the diameters and albedos of the original 1992 IRAS Minor Planet Survey (IMPS).','public','2026-03-13T18:09:28.534155','2026-03-13T18:09:28.534162','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','c7986e5d-fde5-4ae0-a885-bee40736f222','NASA Data.json','0d1036409140ed0fd0dffef7d6d591fc433937a07ee24d34d4ff18539ee0fbc7','1.1','2026-03-13T18:09:28.534155','2026-03-13T18:09:28.534162','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('f1cf43da-3555-41e1-90c6-bb38231cd337','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 1 0567 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 1 phase 2014-11-20 to 2015-03-10. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-02-07T03:35:40.000 to 2015-02-07T08:54:12.000.','public','2026-03-13T18:55:57.792053','2026-03-13T18:55:57.792058','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','d084a717-1a95-4dc2-a9a9-0aeb381c699c','NASA Data.json','cb8729e4a2d556229774ab95df92b68b9a3025815d8bbf7288024081c890153a','1.1','2026-03-13T18:55:57.792053','2026-03-13T18:55:57.792058','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('f1f968a2-6063-4105-8f18-549609019074','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSIWAC 4 EXT1-MTP026 RDR-STRLIGHT V1.0','This CODMAC level 4 data set contains solar stray light corrected, radiometric calibrated and geometric distortion corrected (resampled) image data in W/m^2/sr/nm, acquired by the OSIRIS Wide Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft during the ROSETTA EXTENSION 1 mission phase, covering the period from 2016-02-09T23:25:00.000 to 2016-03-08T23:24:59.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V1.0 is the first version of this dataset: Lien corrected dataset after October 2018 PSA/PDS external peer review.','public','2026-03-13T17:13:04.840544','2026-03-13T17:13:04.840550','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','8e0d36f9-29ec-4207-8a5d-6af61f622e7f','NASA Data.json','a46b394c07c6ec34482923f346120248bd0acc30cee085d98376de71d8d2e5a1','1.1','2026-03-13T17:13:04.840544','2026-03-13T17:13:04.840550','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('f1fed9fd-55a9-41a4-9263-f591714de11e','Parking Violations Issued in January 2026','<p>Parking citation locations in the District of Columbia. The <a href=\'https://visionzero.dc.gov\' target=\'_blank\' rel=\'nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer\'>Vision Zero</a> data contained in this layer pertain to parking violations issued by the District of Columbia\'s Metropolitan Police Department (MPD) and partner agencies with the authority. For example, the District Department of Transportation\'s (DDOT) traffic control officers write parking violations to prevent congestion through enforcement and control at intersections. Parking violation locations are summarized ticket counts based on time of day, week of year, year, and category of violation. Data was originally extracted from the District Department of Motor Vehicle\'s eTIMS meter work order management system. Data was then loaded into the DC GIS, where the Office of the Chief Technology Officer (OCTO) geocoded citation data to the street segment level. Data are visualized using the street segment centroid coordinates.</p>','public','2026-03-25T08:06:48.864701','2026-03-25T08:06:48.864707','District Department of Transportation','DCGISopendata',NULL,'6f815538-e7dd-4f34-af4f-187c83cbf5df','DC data','3131f4692ead6bd2cc46ba601d302eeb67ac6b7dddea33ff2685664e2ae17ae6','1.1','2026-03-25T08:06:48.864701','2026-03-25T08:06:48.864707','geospatial',NULL,0,'district-of-columbia'),('f26142fe-2dc0-40be-9341-25d855f38d1f','ROSETTA-ORBITER CHECK GIADA 2 CR5 CRUISE5 V1.0','Payload Checkout 12 (PC12) was an active checkout where a target independent opportunity to perform interactive operations and to request spacecraft pointing was given to all Rosetta payload teams. All Rosetta payload took part in this scenario The Active Payload Checkout 12 ran for 23 consecutive days starting on the 23th April 2010 until the 14th May 2010.During PC12 GIADA performs only a passive test (GD01) similar to the previous Passive Payload Checkouts. This passive test (GD01), which includes standard procedures and full functional verification, was executed by switching on Main and Redundant I/Fs in sequence and executing similar procedures for the two cases. The data reported in this data set have been converted from ADC counts to engineering values. The quality of the Housekeeping and Calibration data is good. Scientific data are due to noise, as no grain event is expected during this mission phase. These data must be only considered to evaluate GIADA behaviour and not as real scientific data. Data reported by GDS and IS are due to noise as no dust event is expected during this mission phase. MBS frequency changes, once normalised for frequency vs. temperature dependence, if present, are due to deposition of contaminants existing in the S/C environment. Housekeeping and Calibration data from all GIADA sub-systems are useful to evaluate instrument health and behaviour when compared with similar data acquired during other mission phases.','public','2026-03-13T17:50:07.960898','2026-03-13T17:50:07.960905','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','13894410-7cb9-4160-83e6-972fdd48f8b7','NASA Data.json','cda9d9b3297cda911fafff0afc1c92b5951bfc093471d8e548edf914a9630baa','1.1','2026-03-13T17:50:07.960898','2026-03-13T17:50:07.960905','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('f27ffd65-12e8-407d-b13d-f4f829004933','Hydrographic and Impairment Statistics Database: NPS-WSR Virgin Wild and Scenic River','Hydrographic and Impairment Statistics (HIS) is a National Park Service (NPS) Water Resources Division (WRD) project established to track certain goals created in response to the Government Performance and Results Act of 1993 (GPRA). One water resources management goal established by the Department of the Interior under GRPA requires NPS to track the percent of its managed surface waters that are meeting Clean Water Act (CWA) water quality standards. This goal requires an accurate inventory that spatially quantifies the surface water hydrography that each bureau manages and a procedure to determine and track which waterbodies are or are not meeting water quality standards as outlined by Section 303(d) of the CWA. This project helps meet this DOI GRPA goal by inventorying and monitoring in a geographic information system for the NPS: (1) CWA 303(d) quality impaired waters and causes; and (2) hydrographic statistics based on the United States Geological Survey (USGS) National Hydrography Dataset (NHD). Hydrographic and 303(d) impairment statistics were evaluated based on a combination of 1:24,000 (NHD) and finer scale data (frequently provided by state GIS layers).','public','2026-03-29T06:05:40.300556','2026-03-29T06:05:40.300563','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','d62a00ee-0a3a-4fc2-a830-ab8f6beffdb5','DOI NPS DCAT-US','abad2d3d9850f1f11669e721d4c9570f87798041cdb38e3593e12fd96412097c','1.1','2026-03-29T06:05:40.300556','2026-03-29T06:05:40.300563','geospatial','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('f2913fe7-54aa-435f-9b20-1312d67c14a7','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P NAVCAM 2 COMET ESCORT 1 MTP012 V1.1','This dataset contains ROSETTA NAVCAM RAW DATA of the Escort Phase from 13th Jan 2015 to 10th Feb 2015 when at the vicinity of target 67P/CG. This data set V1.1 supersedes the V1.0. It includes updates of the Browse images, adding of the FITS version, clarification of calibration target, document updates and resolve other minor outstanding errata.','public','2026-03-13T16:47:24.023048','2026-03-13T16:47:24.023053','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','e4422859-069e-47b6-ab99-6f7bf901f5fa','NASA Data.json','2b2252c39d77f2672189a3d558aa242ee1c2fa378dc148f4f623e5ffb4fc3d9a','1.1','2026-03-13T16:47:24.023048','2026-03-13T16:47:24.023053','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('f2baf3fc-3acd-46d4-b631-70d3144d2fd8','Data from: Temperature effects on development and population growth of two parasitoids (Hymenoptera) of the coffee berry borer (<i>Hypothenemus hampei</i>)','<p dir=\"ltr\">These data are from a study that evaluated the thermal biology of two key parasitoids of <i>Hypothenemus hampei (</i>Coffee berry borer; Coleoptera: Curculionidae): the larval-pupal ectoparasitoid <i>Prorops nasuta</i> (Hymenoptera: Bethylidae) and the adult endoparasitoid <i>Phymastichus coffea</i> (Hymenoptera: Eulophidae). Using age-stage, two-sex life tables across eight constant temperatures, we quantified temperature effects on development, survival, fecundity, and population growth. We identified 22-25°C as the optimal range for survival, and fecundity peaked at 25°C . Life-table parameters indicate maximal population growth at 25°C for both parasitoids. Development failed at extreme temperatures (32 and 35°C), highlighting upper thermal limits relevant to mass-rearing and field releases for both parasitoids. Degree-day models were developed to estimate the potential number of generations across Colombian coffee-growing regions. We predict 5.5-11.6 annual generations of <i>P. nasuta</i> and 2.2-8.6 of <i>P. coffea</i>, depending on local temperature regimes. These results identify optimal temperature ranges for rearing and deploying <i>P. nasuta</i> and <i>P. coffea</i> and provide spatially relevant predications for their establishment potential in Colombian coffee-growing regions. Regions with mean temperatures between 22-28°C are expected to support the greatest efficacy of augmentative biological control programs targeting the coffee berry borer.</p>','public','2026-03-13T22:49:08.920908','2026-03-13T22:49:08.920915','Agricultural Research Service','Johnson, Melissa, A.','005:18','d4a3e51a-3255-4774-ae7f-4118f2854b5d','USDA JSON','83a9209d9e9d6bf0fdb1ecc11d8bb884ec6cc30e01f65f1fb40099d04b32df5e','1.1','2026-03-13T22:49:08.920908','2026-03-13T22:49:08.920915','geospatial','005:040',0,'usda-gov'),('f2f991bf-f2db-4cb0-a56d-695ceeaea298','Estuarine and Nearshore Marine Sediment Quality Measurements in Cumberland Island National Seashore (2007)','This dataset represents sediment quality measurements that were taken in Cumberland Island National Seashore during 2007 as a part of the marine water and sediment quality assessment protocol that was developed by the Southeast Coast I&M Network (SECN). The protocol is modeled after the EPA\'s National Coastal Assessment Program (www.epa.gov/emap/nca) and it consists of conducting sediment sampling every 10 years based on a probabilistic sampling design that was also designed by the EPA. Thirty sites were selected within the Cumberland River, Mud Creek, Brickhill River, Cumberland Sound and St. Marys River at which sediments were sampled using a Van Veen sampler and composited for analysis as described in the National Coastal Assessment Quality Assurance Project Plan (www.epa.gov/emap/nca/html/docs/qaprojplan.html). The final analyses of the sediment samples were conducted by GPL Laboratories, LLC (now Centauri Labs); please refer to their website (www.centaurilabs.com) or the documents listed in the Cross Reference section for more information about the analytical process. Please note that each sampling location contains multiple sediment parameters that are recorded individually.','public','2026-03-26T05:34:57.747739','2026-03-26T05:34:57.747743','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','38173301-c0e3-409d-98a5-2183c0f460af','DOI NPS DCAT-US','08a4cb9369f9c8feb6e02cb7afbe05f2f3b590ff83910d46d8dad5a0335bb048','1.1','2026-03-26T05:34:57.747739','2026-03-26T05:34:57.747743','Vector Dataset','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('f308bc7b-13c5-45f5-a41f-c095cb36e59a','Continuous Fixed Station Water Quality Measurements in Canaveral National Seashore, July 2008 (Certified)','This dataset represents continuous water quality measurements that were taken at a fixed point in Canaveral National Seashore during the month of July, 2008 as a part of the Fixed Station Water Quality Monitoring protocol that was developed by the Southeast Coast I&M Network (SECN). The measurements were taken by a YSI 6600 ESD Multi-Parameter Long Term Water Quality Monitoring Datasonde unit that serves as the standard fixed station water quality monitoring equipment for all similar operations conducted by the SECN. The following parameters were measured at 30 minute intervals during the time period that has been specified: Water Temperature, Specific Conductivity, Salinity, Dissolved Oxygen (DO), DO Concentration, Shallow Depth, pH Level, and Turbidity. Any anomalies noted regarding these parameters have also been noted in separate fields. Please note that these measurements have been certified by network personnel.','public','2026-03-26T05:32:14.321749','2026-03-26T05:32:14.321753','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','ce6fd07b-16c0-4806-b015-18847c239b23','DOI NPS DCAT-US','c1cf2134a159f9f2f2114182bc7fabc0a42d73ab44c3d26ec3969227ea087e9d','1.1','2026-03-26T05:32:14.321749','2026-03-26T05:32:14.321753','Vector Dataset','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('f30bb901-5132-4189-a73e-bc9d57f6c702','MARINER9 IRIS RDR V1.0','The dataset contains measurements from the infrared interferometer spectrometer and ancillary data. Each record of the dataset consists of a header and a spectral observation of Mars geometry of the observation. The dataset is ordered by time as measured by the Data Acquisition System (DAS) time (1 DAS count is approximately 1.2 sec.). Two IRIS frames are completed every 35 DAS counts calibration observation (alternately of interstellar space and an internal calibration blackbody), and is therefore absent from the calibrated dataset.','public','2026-03-13T19:19:22.016062','2026-03-13T19:19:22.016067','Planetary Atmospheres','Planetary Data System','026:00','05e1f5eb-2187-4fe8-bc16-87ca05b2436e','NASA Data.json','0b30a8574e9856c2d2c839d452bb5aeacb5cb38ae2834ff2829b3e08ea703fed','1.1','2026-03-13T19:19:22.016062','2026-03-13T19:19:22.016067','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('f30bd9a1-c1e0-4c24-bea7-8b6fdfa616df','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 2 0699 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 2 phase 2015-03-11 to 2015-06-30. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-04-09T09:52:05.000 to 2015-04-09T20:40:16.000.','public','2026-03-13T19:50:21.734047','2026-03-13T19:50:21.734054','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','4f057356-d4d5-47c4-ba74-0a61c9870355','NASA Data.json','e31b169778472a1fd95b1bb7f42270aa7fb4ca4954b6e4a7001092b53763ca5d','1.1','2026-03-13T19:50:21.734047','2026-03-13T19:50:21.734054','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('f383e7f1-40e5-4928-b479-0719242255ab','ROSETTA-ORBITER CHECKOUT OSINAC 4 CR4A RDR V1.0','This CODMAC level 4 data set contains radiometric calibrated and geometric distortion corrected (resampled) image data in W/m^2/sr/nm,  acquired by the OSIRIS Narrow Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft  during the CRUISE 4-1 mission phase, covering the period  from 2008-01-28T00:00:00.000 to 2008-08-03T23:59:59.000. The prime objective was commissioning / calibration. Several targets of opportunity were observed, but none of them is identifiable as prime target. This version V1.0 is the first version of this dataset.','public','2026-03-13T16:39:58.190115','2026-03-13T16:39:58.190121','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','f4ba3d06-4485-4caa-b961-270e0acfeef3','NASA Data.json','ba2d49ce008c8473fdd0200cb88d6fe55214dd8eb9b4e5420217f95c3eaaf32b','1.1','2026-03-13T16:39:58.190115','2026-03-13T16:39:58.190121','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('f3b3c727-02c7-4c56-8911-cf5089a2e013','CASSINI RSS RAW DATA SET - SROC11 V1.0','The Cassini Radio Science Saturn Ring and Atmospheric Occultation experiments (SROC11) Raw Data Archive is a time-ordered collection of radio science raw data acquired on January 26-27, 2010, during the Cassini Extended Mission.','public','2026-03-13T19:41:45.592121','2026-03-13T19:41:45.592127','Planetary Atmospheres','Planetary Data System','026:00','1c9fc955-3a26-4fa6-bd3b-f5e1ba6af193','NASA Data.json','21c3a8e7c4390705e69581fc86474d5f33822a27c47f044d636231c6c1917231','1.1','2026-03-13T19:41:45.592121','2026-03-13T19:41:45.592127','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('f3c0efc6-5694-46da-8d68-66ea33bd05fd','Coastal Mapping Program of  Intracoastal Waterway, Western Bogue Sound to Bear Inlet, NC, NC1901D-TB-C','These data provide an accurate high-resolution shoreline compiled from imagery of  Intracoastal Waterway, Western Bogue Sound to Bear Inlet, NC .  This vector shoreline data is based on an office interpretation of imagery that may be suitable as a geographic information system (GIS) data layer. This metadata describes information for both the line and point shapefiles. The NGS attribution scheme \'Coastal Cartographic Object Attribute Source Table (C-COAST)\' was developed to conform the attribution of various sources of shoreline data into one attribution catalog. C-COAST is not a recognized standard, but was influenced by the International Hydrographic Organization\'s S-57 Object-Attribute standard so the data would be more accurately translated into S-57.  This resource is a member of  https://inport.nmfs.noaa.gov/inport/item/39808','public','2026-03-19T20:04:12.898343','2026-03-19T20:04:12.898348',NULL,NULL,NULL,'027714d0-3375-450d-b35e-5b6334f69f42','NOS NGS',NULL,NULL,'2026-03-19T20:04:12.898343','2026-03-19T20:04:12.898348',NULL,NULL,NULL,'noaa-gov'),('f3e329b8-de2b-4e4a-907d-224eea886fa4','Continuous Fixed Station Water Quality Measurements in Canaveral National Seashore, May 2007 (Certified)','This dataset represents continuous water quality measurements that were taken at a fixed point in Canaveral National Seashore during the month of May, 2007 as a part of the Fixed Station Water Quality Monitoring protocol that was developed by the Southeast Coast I&M Network (SECN). The measurements were taken by a YSI 6600 ESD Multi-Parameter Long Term Water Quality Monitoring Datasonde unit that serves as the standard fixed station water quality monitoring equipment for all similar operations conducted by the SECN. The following parameters were measured at 30 minute intervals during the time period that has been specified: Water Temperature, Specific Conductivity, Salinity, Dissolved Oxygen (DO), DO Concentration, Shallow Depth, pH Level, and Turbidity. Any anomalies noted regarding these parameters have also been noted in separate fields. Please note that these measurements have been certified by network personnel.','public','2026-03-26T05:31:15.459387','2026-03-26T05:31:15.459392','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','a116a881-f4c3-4d82-95d7-6c7fb3a22412','DOI NPS DCAT-US','a4bea56ab7f9cc9b1d6513f7156144082608dd35eddd5e7e5e566a01d0d11c45','1.1','2026-03-26T05:31:15.459387','2026-03-26T05:31:15.459392','Vector Dataset','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('f405e0ae-783e-45f2-9a10-16c8f605f388','Laborshed - Model Estimates','Laborshed dataset that contains counts of those who are likely to change or accept employment laborshed area. These estimates are given for every laborshed area in Iowa.','public','2026-03-28T21:59:22.809846','2026-03-28T21:59:22.809851','data.iowa.gov','svqueen',NULL,'502792ad-d224-4caf-a8e3-2f89338f149c','Iowa metadata','afcd0fa9f3733eaa61d7065772fef88c357551d15378953a06977aa01c9d34bc','1.1','2026-03-28T21:59:22.809846','2026-03-28T21:59:22.809851','Economic Statistics',NULL,0,'state-of-iowa'),('f437f6f1-53e9-4d4e-8baa-28b6fb543a0e','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 PRELANDING 0320 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the PRELANDING phase 2014-01-21 to 2014-11-18. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2014-09-27T05:32:05.000 to 2014-09-27T16:08:51.500.','public','2026-03-13T18:29:16.294476','2026-03-13T18:29:16.294482','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','4637bc02-fe6e-4b15-a10e-c57dfee87cc9','NASA Data.json','a2ecfeaa498620f8d983778015211034aa22d900e01fba7ebeeed4a80417b042','1.1','2026-03-13T18:29:16.294476','2026-03-13T18:29:16.294482','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('f43924c8-54f8-44f4-a459-54d007970c42','IHW COMET PPFLX CALIBRATED REDUCED DATA RECORD GZ V1.0','In preparation for the concerted international study of Comet Halley, the IHW conducted a trial run with observations of Comet Crommelin, largely during February and March of 1984.','public','2026-03-13T16:39:57.032498','2026-03-13T16:39:57.032505','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','637ac617-58bb-4a29-88e4-beade45739eb','NASA Data.json','74565ad9c6fee953981c7ceab8ac22bc22c24b2ae8f915cd7d62f4ff5a1d50c3','1.1','2026-03-13T16:39:57.032498','2026-03-13T16:39:57.032505','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('f44a04f3-b220-40c7-90f1-a788699348ec','Floodplains Outline from 2020','<div style=\'text-align:Left;\'><div><div><p><span>The Digital Flood Insurance Rate Map (DFIRM) Database depicts flood risk information and supporting data used to develop the risk data. The primary risk classifications used are the 1-percent-annual-chance flood event, the 0.2-percent-annual-chance flood event, and areas of minimal flood risk. The DFIRM Database is derived from Flood Insurance Studies (FISs), previously published Flood Insurance Rate Maps (FIRMs), flood hazard analyses performed in support of the FISs and FIRMs, and new mapping data, where available. The FISs and FIRMs are published by the Federal Emergency Management Agency (FEMA). The file is georeferenced to earth\'s surface using the UTM projection and coordinate system. The specifications for the horizontal control of DFIRM data files are consistent with those required for mapping at a scale of 1:12000. Insurance applications include enforcement of the mandatory purchase requirement of the Flood Disaster Protection Act, which ... requires the purchase of flood insurance by property owners who are being assisted by Federal programs or by Federally supervised, regulated or insured agencies or institutions in the acquisition or improvement of land facilities located or to be located in identified areas having special flood hazards, Section 2 (b) (4) of the Flood Disaster Protection Act of 1973. In addition to the identification of Special Flood Hazard Areas (SFHAs), the risk zones shown on the FIRMs are the basis for the establishment of premium rates for flood coverage offered through the NFIP. The DFIRM Database presents the flood risk information depicted on the FIRM in a digital format suitable for use in electronic mapping applications. The DFIRM database is a subset of the Digital FIS database that serves to archive the information collected during the FIS.</span></p></div></div></div>','public','2026-04-01T08:50:11.813636','2026-04-01T08:50:11.813640','Federal Emergency Management Agency','DCGISopendata',NULL,'dbe56099-26f5-4d07-b32e-7ab6f48a4da2','DC data','32b695c384cd54034278e6897f9bd48b32b59cde9baed2a3157c68f3490328ad','1.1','2026-04-01T08:50:11.813636','2026-04-01T08:50:11.813640','geospatial',NULL,0,'district-of-columbia'),('f469bf01-7484-4635-a5f3-2da10d2c4155','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSINAC 4 EXT2-MTP030 RDR V2.0','This CODMAC level 4 data set contains radiometric calibrated and geometric distortion corrected (resampled) image data in W/m^2/sr/nm, acquired by the OSIRIS Narrow Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft during the ROSETTA EXTENSION 2 mission phase, covering the period from 2016-05-31T23:25:00.000 to 2016-06-28T23:24:59.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V2.0 supersedes previous deliveries of the same dataset with the following changes since the last version: Lien corrected dataset after October 2018 PSA/PDS external peer review. Updated documentation and ancillary files, added document on bandpass filter. Updated SCIENCE_USER_GUIDE_V03.PDF to include one section about FAQ and one section about image data quality. Added shutter backtravel and readout issues to image quality map. Updated DATA_QUALITY_ID keyword in image header. Improved handling of images with missing packets.','public','2026-03-13T18:00:43.921915','2026-03-13T18:00:43.921921','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','008dff77-2a52-4835-a3bd-a267ba737e73','NASA Data.json','c164fe57254696cdcd3cea68782c4f9d0296f3ce84f92b7046680a2bf66ed0d8','1.1','2026-03-13T18:00:43.921915','2026-03-13T18:00:43.921921','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('f46ab28a-636b-4293-9b63-b501bd41b5f7','HPMS Roadway Sample 2018','State DOTs provide the Highway Performance Monitoring System (HPMS) with the location limits of highway sections used to represent statewide aggregations based on a statistically valid Sample Panel.','public','2026-03-28T13:32:46.323490','2026-03-28T13:32:46.323495','Federal Highway Administration','Office of Highway Policy Information','021:15','141f761f-83f4-4ace-9313-25cc2c0129ce','DOT Socrata Data.json','a6e88da9ee63733d4d4d2480b1bc5d342e3dff87b45be053b3f970686d53ccc8','1.1','2026-03-28T13:32:46.323490','2026-03-28T13:32:46.323495','Roadways and Bridges','021:009',0,'dot-gov'),('f4d03a8e-ad8d-490b-ba56-3ecad5359ab6','Data from: Combination of serial plating and long-read sequencing to detect and quantify live Shiga-toxin producing <i>Escherichia coli</i>','<p dir=\"ltr\">Consumption of food contaminated with Shiga toxin-producing <i>Escherichia coli</i> (STEC) causes millions of illnesses in the United States annually. Long-read sequencing could be used to reduce the time needed to test food for STEC, but sequencing is not quantitative and cannot differentiate between live and dead bacteria. Therefore, this study investigated combining serial plating with long-read sequencing to quantify only live STEC in a sample. Ground beef was inoculated with STEC and stomached. The liquid was filtered to remove eukaryotic cells and then centrifuged to pellet the bacteria. Serial dilutions of the pellet were plated on selective agar and then single colonies were selected for sequencing. During initial experiments where sample processing was conducted at room temperature, a 1 log increase in STEC concentration from the initial inoculated amount was observed. Subsequent experiments kept samples and reagents cold, and the amount of STEC recovered did not significantly differ from the amount inoculated. The DNA extracted from a single colony provided enough data to identify all virulence genes of interest multiple times. The amount of STEC in a sample could be quantified down to 1 cfu g<sup>-1</sup>. The ability of this method to quantify STEC in samples would improve risk assessment and guide mitigation in industry.</p>','public','2026-03-13T22:44:34.110737','2026-03-13T22:44:34.110745','Agricultural Research Service','Counihan, Katrina, L.','005:18','8c88843e-4563-46f0-b0be-3e91dc95c363','USDA JSON','090a91c8ac0b2dd5e8d36bcf05a45b479d78966d1b0c8d60b6feb8b340ddc668','1.1','2026-03-13T22:44:34.110737','2026-03-13T22:44:34.110745',NULL,'005:040',0,'usda-gov'),('f505958f-d9c1-4b1b-87b0-4af4d7d93ba7','Nitrogen Screening Project - Sensitive Vegetation','This geodatabase contains vegetation data utilized in the Nitrogen Screening project.  It includes LANDFIRE, NWI and NLCD datasets of nitrogen-sensitive vegetation clipped to Inventory & Monitoring Parks.The original data were retrieved on an indivual park basis from the USGS-NPS Vegetation Characterization Surveys (available before June 2009) and merged. Only the vegetation types believed to be N-sensitive are included in this dataset.','public','2026-03-26T05:35:05.953277','2026-03-26T05:35:05.953282','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','b68e8771-1b15-490e-9bd9-5a56f7299862','DOI NPS DCAT-US','443a0acdc55f55cbb42e242e522e1435bf04acdc6987241203b2fb5a8396c66f','1.1','2026-03-26T05:35:05.953277','2026-03-26T05:35:05.953282','geospatial','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('f5296c79-5a87-4507-aaf2-e1293a840497','NEW HORIZONS  SWAP JUPITER ENCOUNTER  CALIBRATED V4.0','This data set contains Calibrated data taken by the New Horizons  Solar Wind Around Pluto  instrument during the  Jupiter encounter  mission phase. This is VERSION 4.0 of this data set.   During the Jupiter mission phase, SWAP made near-continuous  science observations, taking data between 2 and 12 times per hour.  Inbound to Jupiter, real-time science mode data were taken twice  per hour, then 12 measurements were recorded per hour in the  Jupiter tail. The Jupiter tail observations continue until about  100 days after closest approach, which corresponds to about 2200  RJ downstream.   The changes in Version 4.0 were re-running of the ancillary data  in the data product, updated geometry from newer SPICE kernels,  minor editing of the documentation, catalogs, etc., and resolution  of liens from the December, 2014 review, plus those from the May,  2016 review of the Pluto Encounter data sets. No new observations  were added with Version 4.0.','public','2026-03-13T16:50:17.311317','2026-03-13T16:50:17.311325','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','064ede0a-55ac-4d44-8fd0-facdf4d0a54d','NASA Data.json','48f1063e4236d5335fe8e06280b7f48a20ecf5a98fbfd1b647a8b805c4693b3a','1.1','2026-03-13T16:50:17.311317','2026-03-13T16:50:17.311325','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('f5503826-8a78-4d83-9867-722dc0e1abf4','US Forest Atlas FIA Forest Type Groups Hardwoods (Image Service)','<p><span style=\'background-color:rgb(255,255,255); color:rgb(76,76,76); font-family:&quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px;\'><span style=\'display:inline !important; float:none; font-style:normal; font-variant-caps:normal; font-variant-ligatures:normal; font-weight:400; letter-spacing:normal; text-align:left; text-decoration-color:initial; text-decoration-style:initial; text-indent:0px; text-transform:none; word-spacing:0px;\'>This Hardwoods type dataset portrays 12 forest type groups across the contiguous United States. These data were derived from MODIS composite images from the 2002 and 2003 growing seasons in combination with nearly 100 other geospatial data layers, including elevation, slope, aspect, ecoregions, and PRISM climate data. The dataset was developed as a collaborative effort between the USFS Forest Inventory and Analysis and Forest Health Monitoring programs and the USFS Remote Sensing.</span></span></p>','public','2026-03-13T22:49:44.714431','2026-03-13T22:49:44.714438','U.S. Forest Service','USFSEnterpriseContent','005:96','646455a4-cc31-4ef7-9483-1679eb5d31fb','USDA JSON','8c2f8bd55e61f987d95405006a4fcd5dae478d0bd4678bec4a14ac9e649162d6','1.1','2026-03-13T22:49:44.714431','2026-03-13T22:49:44.714438','geospatial','005:059',0,'usda-gov'),('f57b96b1-742e-4387-a3e0-12950956f6c0','MARS EXPRESS SUN MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 5 3740 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2015-01-01 to 2016-12-31. It is a Solar Conjunction measurement and covers the time 2015-05-18T03:03:25.000 to 2015-05-18T08:53:26.000.','public','2026-03-13T19:11:59.440835','2026-03-13T19:11:59.440840','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','1b53b1f3-5bdd-4b0f-af6d-bc34aef782f5','NASA Data.json','f3d63ed63218e9cb2aef3f93d9e6344f862a441729012b2db63e667c33d6728f','1.1','2026-03-13T19:11:59.440835','2026-03-13T19:11:59.440840','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('f583b2db-4aad-4cc0-89c9-8f924985e272','Gulf of Mexico Scalars CICESE Mooring Y7 WH 300 KHZ (DOWN) delta_t 360 (20090608-20110506)','Phsyical Oceanographic Circulation Study','public','2026-03-26T19:14:45.966507','2026-03-26T19:14:45.966514',NULL,NULL,NULL,'f4d392ec-6f05-464e-9df7-f6261f2a73fc','ioos',NULL,NULL,'2026-03-26T19:14:45.966507','2026-03-26T19:14:45.966514',NULL,NULL,NULL,'noaa-gov'),('f594f1fa-2e0d-4af0-b98e-44d93255052e','Continuous Fixed Station Water Quality Measurements in Canaveral National Seashore, April 2008 (Certified)','This dataset represents continuous water quality measurements that were taken at a fixed point in Canaveral National Seashore during the month of April, 2008 as a part of the Fixed Station Water Quality Monitoring protocol that was developed by the Southeast Coast I&M Network (SECN). The measurements were taken by a YSI 6600 ESD Multi-Parameter Long Term Water Quality Monitoring Datasonde unit that serves as the standard fixed station water quality monitoring equipment for all similar operations conducted by the SECN. The following parameters were measured at 30 minute intervals during the time period that has been specified: Water Temperature, Specific Conductivity, Salinity, Dissolved Oxygen (DO), DO Concentration, Shallow Depth, pH Level, and Turbidity. Any anomalies noted regarding these parameters have also been noted in separate fields. Please note that these measurements have been certified by network personnel.','public','2026-03-26T05:31:30.584676','2026-03-26T05:31:30.584680','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','119fc678-dda8-40f3-bcf9-cb8471a05716','DOI NPS DCAT-US','a02ceca1b15607a3babdfb3ad5be7e34a1613818aaf26777ef31c731a18926cc','1.1','2026-03-26T05:31:30.584676','2026-03-26T05:31:30.584680','Vector Dataset','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('f5c676a9-bfbc-4f3b-93ae-2d60a8c4f6fa','MARS EXPRESS MARS MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 5 3698 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2015-01-01 to 2016-12-31. It is a Occultation measurement and covers the time 2015-02-21T01:49:26 to 2015-02-22T14:28:20.999.','public','2026-03-13T16:40:36.421041','2026-03-13T16:40:36.421046','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','d603fb23-5dfe-4230-b335-5d0ef8d0886a','NASA Data.json','9f17e2aee66d87321dde18c56a809ba447df6d7ea23176732d5ed5b2f957b95e','1.1','2026-03-13T16:40:36.421041','2026-03-13T16:40:36.421046','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('f5e95318-e159-4cb5-a1e8-e2465e4b0eff','Report Card WSIF Supplemental Accountability 2024 Annual','This file contains Washington School Improvement Framework (WSIF) 2024 Annual Supplemental Accountability data for Federal School Accountability under the Every Student Succeeds Act.','public','2026-03-22T03:13:22.034230','2026-03-22T03:13:22.034235','data.wa.gov','OSPI Data',NULL,'b131af51-2e36-4c55-bd42-150da8ab8763','WA JSON','8b0d6f54bbca05c94da5301eeaccf1c8e44e10a1c02aa14ea73b87c547e61700','1.1','2026-03-22T03:13:22.034230','2026-03-22T03:13:22.034235','education',NULL,0,'state-of-washington'),('f606b52c-3d7b-4a96-b763-6eb04a193cc1','GALILEO ORBITER EARTH MAG RDR EARTH2 HIGHRES V1.0','Galileo Orbiter Magnetometer (MAG) calibrated              high-resolution data from the Earth-2 flyby in              spacecraft, GSE, and GSM coordinates. These data              cover the interval 1992-11-03 to 1992-12-19.','public','2026-03-13T17:50:28.963342','2026-03-13T17:50:28.963347','planetary plasma interactions','Planetary Data System','026:00','4d48566e-334c-425f-969c-f3609eb1d1e2','NASA Data.json','10b15a5804beb751c29404dfc7aaa21c5dbaed2552d96325a51c98e89aed40d7','1.1','2026-03-13T17:50:28.963342','2026-03-13T17:50:28.963347','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('f6153999-5e42-49cd-b038-f11faf771c20','EGIS - Enterprise Gateway Integration Services-Verification Services (VS)','VS supports the VIS applications by connecting to various endpoints to support business processing. The Verification Service is a composite service which allows the Verification Information System to query the immigration status of an immigrant across several USCIS and DoS systems for verification or validation purposes. This service is also heavily used for ACA.','non-public','2026-03-22T11:51:53.699647','2026-03-22T11:51:53.699653','Unspecified','Open Data (MGMT)','024:030','a64270f7-3bfc-4d24-beaa-ef2a2a82a80f','DHS datajson source','da5741246aee46ac96dbaabde596e0195acf2c9f772d06fc8f838d3b79350abc','1.1','2026-03-22T11:51:53.699647','2026-03-22T11:51:53.699653',NULL,'024:000',0,'dhs-gov'),('f61e19d0-e720-4a4c-91c5-fcf95178c956','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSIWAC 4 EXT1-MTP027 RDR-REFLECT V1.0','This CODMAC level 4 data set contains radiometric calibrated and geometric distortion corrected (resampled) image data in reflectance units (normalized and thus without unit), acquired by the OSIRIS Wide Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft during the ROSETTA EXTENSION 1 mission phase, covering the period from 2016-03-08T23:25:00.000 to 2016-04-05T23:24:59.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V1.0 is the first version of this dataset: Lien corrected dataset after October 2018 PSA/PDS external peer review.','public','2026-03-13T16:45:10.779908','2026-03-13T16:45:10.779913','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','6418fe96-b74a-41b1-98c9-955863532f3f','NASA Data.json','62874166ff13c2860b2e3a89be3ba389eba9694417c0eaa7b662ea305f51e567','1.1','2026-03-13T16:45:10.779908','2026-03-13T16:45:10.779913','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('f620587a-9869-4d71-92fb-9406c1c46353','Detailed data for all results shown in paper \"Acute BTEX Inhalation Activates Sensitive Transcriptomic Pathways in Mouse Respiratory Tract\"','This dataset shows all detailed data backing up all results (tables, figures, results text) shown in the main paper and supplemental files of the paper intended for submission to Environmental Science and Pollution Research \"Acute BTEX Inhalation Activates Sensitive Transcriptomic Pathways in Mouse Respiratory Tract\" by T. W. Jackson et al.','public','2026-03-21T12:04:11.830313','2026-03-21T12:04:11.830318','U.S. Environmental Protection Agency','Stephen Gavett','020:00','36f41657-a18f-4e4c-a7af-d06d39d7c957','EPA ScienceHub','eb91385979f3eadeaac7b59e7ab7d7022667b2abeb6b28247735342c767ab130','1.1','2026-03-21T12:04:11.830313','2026-03-21T12:04:11.830318',NULL,'020:000',0,'epa-gov'),('f63383bf-1260-443f-b8b0-42604f5ff026','Coast Range Newt Predicted Habitat - CWHR A007 [ds1974]','<div style=\'text-align:Left;\'><div><div><p><span>CWHR Predicted Habitat Models represent areas of predicted suitable habitat for each species within its range. These models are built from the following principal inputs: </span></p><p><span>1) a statewide, best-available vegetation map (FVEG);  </span></p><p><span>2) GIS data representing a species’ range;  </span></p><p><span>3) the CWHR database of habitat suitability values for over 700 terrestrial vertebrate species. </span></p><p><span>Habitat suitability ranks of Low (non-zero values less than 0.34), Medium (0.34-0.66), and High (greater than 0.66) are based on the maximum suitability value across the 3 species life requisites: reproduction, feeding, and cover. Note that previous versions of these Predicted Habitat Models used an average across the 3 life requisites in order to obtain an overall suitability score for each habitat type and stage class.  Habitat suitability scores were developed based on habitat patch sizes greater than 40 acres in size and are best interpreted for habitat patches greater than 200 acres in size. The FVEG landcover dataset is an aggregation of multiple statewide landcover and regional vegetation mapping efforts, conducted at different points in time (approximately 1990 up to time of publishing) and at various resolutions, compiled by the California Department of Forestry and Fire Protection (CALFIRE). FVEG uses the most current and consistent data available for each region of the state. Decision rules were developed that controlled which layers were given priority in areas of overlap. Crosswalks were used to attribute the various data sources according to the CWHR habitat-type classification system. Attributing FVEG with CWHR habitat types allows for the extraction of areas with non-zero suitability values for each species within the bounds of its range, creating a series of maps of predicted suitable habitat which are species-specific. Because FVEG is an amalgam of disparate landcover assessment efforts across the state, the predictive power for determining suitable habitat will vary between species, and possibly even regionally for species which are widely distributed. While these maps represent CDFW’s best estimate of the presence of suitable habitat for any given species in the CWHR system, these maps are also limited by several factors: 1) the accuracy and resolution of vegetation maps in a given region; 2) the dynamic nature of the landscape in which fire and other disturbance events alter conditions at a greater frequency than mapping efforts can track; 3) the currency of expert knowledge, particularly as species adapt to changing land and climate conditions and the shifting of other species’ ranges; 4) the frequency of species-specific surveys across a representative sample of a species’ entire range; 5) metapopulation dynamics, which describes the shifting of populations within their environment as result of numerous types of interactions and responses. </span></p><p><span>CWHR GIS data representing predicted suitable habitat should not be used to indicate the presence or absence of a particular species at any specific site. CWHR predicted habitat models are named according to the 4-character alpha-numeric CWHR ID assigned to each species (5 characters in the case of subspecies or other sub-taxa). There is also a “CWHR Revision Tracking Table” containing a record for each species, its CWHR ID, scientific name, common name, and range and habitat model data revision history. CWHR species range models, predicted habitat models, and GIS data of the statewide distribution of all CWHR habitat types, along with the CWHR revision tracking table, are available for download at </span><a href=\'https://www.wildlife.ca.gov/Data/CWHR\' target=\'_blank\' style=\'text-decoration:underline;\' rel=\'nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer\'><span>https://www.wildlife.ca.gov/Data/CWHR</span></a><span>. </span></p></div></div></div>','public','2026-03-23T13:58:43.545216','2026-03-23T13:58:43.545221','California Department of Fish and Wildlife','BIOS_Admin',NULL,'77039ee4-a6db-47a8-9c5f-985317f3b1d4','State of California','26409024ac0026db3c036f3e23be7ed89323ae0cab5922726b13e612e170841f','1.1','2026-03-23T13:58:43.545216','2026-03-23T13:58:43.545221','Natural Resources',NULL,0,'ca-gov'),('f65035be-115d-4305-ba4a-de13e19297b3','Austin Facilities Management 2026 Projects','Current AFM CIP and deferred maintenance projects','public','2026-03-25T14:25:57.898720','2026-03-25T14:25:57.898726','data.austintexas.gov','Tomi.Coleman@austintexas.gov',NULL,'c3bb8fb3-b503-4b5e-ab4e-3b92e742f00f','City of Austin Data.json','cabbef32212a313a9db0e3e7ca1d0bbc94ba7b49e10199b82805846c63775777','1.1','2026-03-25T14:25:57.898720','2026-03-25T14:25:57.898726','Building and Development',NULL,0,'city-of-austin'),('f662fda0-9319-4707-ae68-906c3adacb29','Statewide Laborshed Trends - Main Data','Statewide historical laborshed trends over time. Contains demographic, economic, and other labor supply data from 2009 to the most recent statewide data release.','public','2026-03-28T21:59:38.629278','2026-03-28T21:59:38.629283','data.iowa.gov','svqueen',NULL,'b923a372-94f4-494b-b524-9f419c8973c4','Iowa metadata','bed34a276817cc41e6f1d1c4571f76229e7ec95be8fe5e2d2c8e0b6d2e62fda1','1.1','2026-03-28T21:59:38.629278','2026-03-28T21:59:38.629283','Economic Statistics',NULL,0,'state-of-iowa'),('f6914183-6e35-4a23-97ab-69e8b3924d75','VG2 URA CRS RESAMPLED SUMMARY D2 RATE                                       ELEC 96SEC V1.0','Counting rate from the D2 detector inthe Cosmic Ray System (CRS) electron telescope (TET) on Voyager 2 duringthe Uranus encounter. The D2 detector nominally responds to electrons withkinetic energies above approximately 2.5 MeV.','public','2026-03-13T18:19:54.101034','2026-03-13T18:19:54.101040','planetary plasma interactions','Planetary Data System','026:00','fd5febb8-251d-4361-916f-ff5d85c96363','NASA Data.json','ce5472d5f61fd3620c99729789532cf47bdbb53b9e2082d39654fcf04db9bb08','1.1','2026-03-13T18:19:54.101034','2026-03-13T18:19:54.101040','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('f692146f-111c-48b6-bed8-18b94138c85a','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSINAC 4 PRL-MTP004 RDR-REFLECT V1.0','This CODMAC level 4 data set contains radiometric calibrated and geometric distortion corrected (resampled) image data in reflectance units (normalized and thus without unit), acquired by the OSIRIS Narrow Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft during the PRELANDING mission phase, covering the period from 2014-06-04T10:50:00.000 to 2014-07-02T08:34:59.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V1.0 is the first version of this dataset: Lien corrected dataset after October 2018 PSA/PDS external peer review.','public','2026-03-13T16:49:57.973324','2026-03-13T16:49:57.973330','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','4be78408-8ec4-4873-abe8-5de02dbfd68b','NASA Data.json','112574cac08b868df980127d721965cae7db106f4559e23f8c3c29c856399008','1.1','2026-03-13T16:49:57.973324','2026-03-13T16:49:57.973330','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('f6b028e7-04ea-4928-8409-884cf143dfbd','ROSETTA-ORBITER CHECKOUT OSINAC 4 CR2 RDR V1.0','This CODMAC level 4 data set contains radiometric calibrated and geometric distortion corrected (resampled) image data in W/m^2/sr/nm,  acquired by the OSIRIS Narrow Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft  during the CRUISE 2 mission phase, covering the period  from 2005-04-05T00:00:00.000 to 2006-07-28T23:59:59.000. The prime objective was commissioning / calibration. Several targets of opportunity were observed, but none of them is identifiable as prime target. This version V1.0 is the first version of this dataset.','public','2026-03-13T18:44:41.373067','2026-03-13T18:44:41.373073','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','959277d8-44e7-4f38-b2fd-5653e96d5f14','NASA Data.json','1bec9fd5e3dfbc601d6f3ac48c26a1e4b77c225dfea671561677d3fb8fe44c6c','1.1','2026-03-13T18:44:41.373067','2026-03-13T18:44:41.373073','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('f6ea83fc-fb10-4ae3-95df-cbb921aee178','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RPCIES 5 EXT1 V1.0','This dataset contains DERIVED DATA of the Rosetta RPCIES instrument taken during the mission extension 2 (EXT2). The target of this phase was comet 67P/CHURYUMOV-GERASIMENKO 1 (1969 R1). Included are the data taken between 06 Apr 2016 and 30 Jun 2016.','public','2026-03-13T17:28:01.655186','2026-03-13T17:28:01.655191','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','e88f3c46-0f87-4906-ba00-62589f93ff1d','NASA Data.json','a385ac21f1b146f2afca7c9399ccc56f81d18ddefab5596008f71a49a7c5815a','1.1','2026-03-13T17:28:01.655186','2026-03-13T17:28:01.655191','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('f70fead1-2ea6-44e4-9d4e-76d2dca56c53','Exposure Activities All Activity Trends','<div style=\"text-align:Left;\"><div><div><p style=\"margin:0 0 11;\">Retired on March 2, 2022. Data and metadata are provided as-is archive.</p><p style=\"margin:0 0 11;\"><span>The “All Activity Trend” shows the number of positive cases that were interviewed (bar graph) and the percentage of those interviewed who reported each select high to moderate exposure activity types (i.e. personal care, dining out, social-related activities, work, travel, gym/fitness, sports, and faith-related events) during their exposure period (trend lines) on a weekly basis.Note: Data subject to change on a daily basis. Data are restricted to positive cases with a completed contact tracing interview. Possible exposure data are collected during the contact tracing interview as self-reported activities occurring within the 2-week period before the date of symptom onset for symptomatic individuals or the date of test sample collection for asymptomatic individuals. Data collection methods were altered starting the week of Dec 11 for gym/fitness and sports, so should not be compared to previous values.</span></p><p style=\"margin:0 0 11;\"><span>* High to Moderate Exposure Activity Types are not exhaustive and include travel, personal care, faith events, work, dining out, social events, gym/fitness, and sports.</span></p><p style=\"margin:0 0 11;\"><span>Data is updated on a weekly basis.</span></p></div></div></div>','public','2026-04-01T08:42:25.477836','2026-04-01T08:42:25.477842','Office of the Chief Technology Officer','DCGISopendata',NULL,'745eb814-3503-4bbd-8355-d5c3e0d80037','DC data','f28110409e5a2b282071b45c4fee2e88c0c2f0d6007e527d95b8ccb81ab357c2','1.1','2026-04-01T08:42:25.477836','2026-04-01T08:42:25.477842','geospatial',NULL,0,'district-of-columbia'),('f71c1b89-e72b-4fad-b5ae-9d0fc868511c','Coastal Mapping Program of  Ports of Bangor and Keyport, WA, WA2502A-CS-N','These data provide an accurate high-resolution shoreline compiled from imagery of  Ports of Bangor and Keyport, WA .  This vector shoreline data is based on an office interpretation of imagery that may be suitable as a geographic information system (GIS) data layer. This metadata describes information for both the line and point shapefiles. The NGS attribution scheme \'Coastal Cartographic Object Attribute Source Table (C-COAST)\' was developed to conform the attribution of various sources of shoreline data into one attribution catalog. C-COAST is not a recognized standard, but was influenced by the International Hydrographic Organization\'s S-57 Object-Attribute standard so the data would be more accurately translated into S-57.  This resource is a member of  https://inport.nmfs.noaa.gov/inport/item/39808','public','2026-03-26T20:18:38.072865','2026-03-26T20:18:38.072871',NULL,NULL,NULL,'f053b54f-071a-4090-bf0d-272814e3c2fa','NOS NGS',NULL,NULL,'2026-03-26T20:18:38.072865','2026-03-26T20:18:38.072871',NULL,NULL,NULL,'noaa-gov'),('f7702f63-d4c3-4edc-8c56-158973207bea','Structure from motion images collected during marine debris surveys at coral reef sites entangled with derelict fishing nets at Pearl and Hermes Atoll in the Northwestern Hawaiian Islands in 2018 and 2021','The photographs described in this dataset were collected using a Structure from Motion (SfM) approach during in-water marine debris swim surveys conducted by snorkelers in search of derelict fishing nets. Surveys were conducted by the NOAA Fisheries, Ecosystem Sciences Division (ESD) at Pearl and Hermes Atoll in the Northwestern Hawaiian Islands (NWHI). Initial surveys occurred from September 24 - October 3, 2018 during an ESD-led marine debris removal mission aboard the NOAA Ship Oscar Elton Sette, and follow-up surveys occurred from September 13-14, 2021 on a joint mission with non-profit organization Papahanaumokuakea  Marine Debris Project aboard the M/V IMUA.\n\nDuring the 2018 mission, only a subset of marine debris surveys resulted in a SfM survey. Fishing nets were located during swim surveys and selected for SfM if the net was interacting with coral or hard substrate, the depth of the net was within ~1- 4 m of the surface, and the area of the net fit within the 9 sq. meter SFM survey plot. During a SFM survey, a permanent 3 x 3 m plot was established around the center of the fishing net, and the net was photographed using a back and forth swim pattern (\"before\" photos) for later processing using a SfM approach. The net was then removed and the same area was photographed again in the same way (\"after\" photos). A nearby (>50 m distant) paired control site was also photographed using the same method (\"control\" photos).\n\nDuring the 2021 mission, relocation of all paired sites where \"after\" and \"control\" photos were taken in 2018 was attempted; if found, the permanent 3 x 3m plot was reimaged using the same SfM approach. Only a subset of 2018 sites were successfully relocated in 2021 (12 \"after\" sites, 8 \"control\" sites), and five new nearby \"control\" sites had to be established to fulfill the paired study design.','public','2026-03-21T23:13:28.100789','2026-03-21T23:13:28.100794',NULL,NULL,NULL,'100139bc-0311-4d1c-b357-dc1fe249c249','NMFS PIFSC',NULL,NULL,'2026-03-21T23:13:28.100789','2026-03-21T23:13:28.100794',NULL,NULL,NULL,'noaa-gov'),('f77c6f39-0904-4d2d-a02e-020c8ac7c7bd','ROSETTA-ORBITER LUTETIA OSINAC 4 AST2 RDR-REFLECT V1.0','This CODMAC level 4 data set contains radiometric calibrated and geometric distortion corrected (resampled)  image data in reflectance units (normalized and thus without unit),  acquired by the OSIRIS Narrow Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft  during the LUTETIA FLY-BY mission phase, covering the period  from 2010-05-17T00:00:00.000 to 2010-09-03T23:59:59.000. The prime target is asteroid 21 Lutetia. This version V1.0 is the first version of this dataset.','public','2026-03-13T17:11:37.426409','2026-03-13T17:11:37.426417','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','aa172fae-3add-45d8-bcd7-0fbf3b74f021','NASA Data.json','55e5742b2dbc45a03f013b24ebaafad5eff73722967d84ce72c88511d96082f7','1.1','2026-03-13T17:11:37.426409','2026-03-13T17:11:37.426417','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('f794ee33-81b4-4016-9987-adb2b6d64b34','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 2 0673 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 2 phase 2015-03-11 to 2015-06-30. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-03-25T17:57:20.000 to 2015-03-25T21:16:24.500.','public','2026-03-13T16:50:17.285540','2026-03-13T16:50:17.285545','Small Bodies','Tess Jaffe','026:00','68eece83-215a-4373-808e-aea3a33e923b','NASA Data.json','3330e9676f7b5a0220d82c92df161158051c9fe2731d2c53310e626c086b9277','1.1','2026-03-13T16:50:17.285540','2026-03-13T16:50:17.285545','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('f7ad3c2d-9d60-4c07-a67d-100accd10f84','ROSETTA-LANDER 67P PTOLEMY 3 RBD V1.0','This archive contains calibrated data from the PTOLEMY instrument onboard ROSETTA Lander, acquired during the RBD mission phase. The primary target is the comet 67P/CHURYUMOV-GERASIMENKO. It also contains documentation which describes the PTOLEMY experiment. The data archived in this data set conform to the Planetary Data System (PDS) Standards, Version 3.6.','public','2026-03-13T19:36:09.744083','2026-03-13T19:36:09.744089','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','db6f1f6d-fecc-46b1-b1d1-27e86895b8b8','NASA Data.json','8205ccdce0583343888dbc43e9517b228ddd11ed3415b61b17f817b03b5af661','1.1','2026-03-13T19:36:09.744083','2026-03-13T19:36:09.744089','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('f7c2ffd5-b72f-4449-a2b9-8308a430a030','ROSETTA-ORBITER COMET ESCORT OSIWAC 3 RDR MTP 013 V1.0','This data set contains calibrated images acquired by the OSIRIS Wide AngleCamera during the escort phase of the Rosetta mission at the comet 67P,covering the period from 2015-02-10 to 2015-03-10.','public','2026-03-13T17:35:13.468664','2026-03-13T17:35:13.468669','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','4fa16e5c-c1a4-404b-9747-beb8f9cdd4b1','NASA Data.json','a1ccee2dc237622a2c377ec9b922930d50ae0050a89e1be0e21d8b3e964f8713','1.1','2026-03-13T17:35:13.468664','2026-03-13T17:35:13.468669','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('f7f8f7a3-9281-49ef-8f00-9d8ec6ba053f','Hydrographic and Impairment Statistics Database: NPS-WSR Kobuk Wild and Scenic River','Hydrographic and Impairment Statistics (HIS) is a National Park Service (NPS) Water Resources Division (WRD) project established to track certain goals created in response to the Government Performance and Results Act of 1993 (GPRA). One water resources management goal established by the Department of the Interior under GRPA requires NPS to track the percent of its managed surface waters that are meeting Clean Water Act (CWA) water quality standards. This goal requires an accurate inventory that spatially quantifies the surface water hydrography that each bureau manages and a procedure to determine and track which waterbodies are or are not meeting water quality standards as outlined by Section 303(d) of the CWA. This project helps meet this DOI GRPA goal by inventorying and monitoring in a geographic information system for the NPS: (1) CWA 303(d) quality impaired waters and causes; and (2) hydrographic statistics based on the United States Geological Survey (USGS) National Hydrography Dataset (NHD). Hydrographic and 303(d) impairment statistics were evaluated based on a combination of 1:24,000 (NHD) and finer scale data (frequently provided by state GIS layers).','public','2026-03-29T06:06:47.869576','2026-03-29T06:06:47.869583','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','9a9b4cd3-9d80-4b1f-8968-833575e57d04','DOI NPS DCAT-US','5eba77d74b604ff963de8961ae5caf895832d7d9ccceadacf28849994329b3c1','1.1','2026-03-29T06:06:47.869576','2026-03-29T06:06:47.869583','geospatial','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('f8630830-2e6b-4fad-a480-0af8ee0a9f68','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSINAC 4 ESC4-MTP024 RDR-INF-REFL V1.0','This CODMAC level 4 data set contains solar stray-light corrected, in-field stray-light corrected,  radiometric calibrated and geometric distortion corrected  (resampled) image data in reflectance units (normalized  and thus without unit),  acquired by the OSIRIS Narrow Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft  during the COMET ESCORT 4 mission phase, covering the period  from 2015-12-15T23:25:00.000 to 2016-01-12T23:24:59.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V1.0 is the first version of this dataset: Lien corrected dataset after September 2019 PSA/PDS external peer review.','public','2026-03-13T17:57:47.477997','2026-03-13T17:57:47.478004','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','6f49445d-1abc-4919-b661-b0abbb116e14','NASA Data.json','ca0a3ec1db2301037d4004d5584eeb6885783f0379a5bebc35b5900512b71a96','1.1','2026-03-13T17:57:47.477997','2026-03-13T17:57:47.478004','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('f864fd38-9fec-43f1-87e8-4f95aa12e4b7','ARCSIX Learjet In-Situ Cloud Data','ARCSIX_Cloud_AircraftInSitu_Learjet_Data is the in-situ cloud data collected onboard the Learjet aircraft during the Arctic Radiation-Cloud-Aerosol-Surface Interaction EXperiment (ARCSIX) campaign. Data from the 2D-Gray Particle Probe (2D-Gray), 2D-Stereo Particle Probe (2DS), Fast Cloud Droplet Probe (FCDP), High Volume Precipitation Spectrometer (HVPS), and the Nevzorov Water Vapor Probe are featured in this collection. Data collection for this product is complete. The ARCSIX campaign is a NASA field investigation aimed at quantifying the contributions of surface properties, clouds, aerosol particles, and precipitation to the Arctic summer surface radiation budget and sea ice melt during the early melt season. Based out of Greenland, ARCSIX completed two deployments from May – June 2024 and July - August 2024 utilizing the NASA P-3B, LaRC G-III, and SPEC-Learjet aircraft. The P-3B was equipped with in situ and remote sensing payloads to acquire measurements of aerosols, cloud, and radiation properties. The high-flying LaRC G-III was equipped with remote sensing instrumentation, including the HALO, and HSRL, along with the AVAPS dropsonde system. The SPEC-Learjet acquired measurements of cloud microphysics. Data were also collected at the Thule High Arctic Atmospheric Observatory (THAAO) in Pituffik, Greenland. The primary objective of ARCSIX was to enhance long-term space-based monitoring and predictive capabilities of Arctic sea ice, cloud, and aerosols by validating and improving remote sensing algorithms and model parameterizations in the Arctic. ARCSIX science questions focused on examining the impact of the predominant summer Arctic cloud types on the radiative surface energy budget, what processes control the evolution and maintenance of the predominant cloud types in the summertime Arctic, and how do the two-way interactions between surface properties and atmospheric forcings affect sea ice evolution?','public','2026-03-13T16:46:23.417347','2026-03-13T16:46:23.417353','NASA/LARC/SD/ASDC','Earthdata Forum','026:00','ce889c77-ae3b-4833-ba68-bf52ebed757b','NASA Data.json','022e17335c3b02bf17dab9b9df1537de3cab4d7b8913bc71611aedc8640e66a7','1.1','2026-03-13T16:46:23.417347','2026-03-13T16:46:23.417353','Earth Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('f86a7d9d-1063-4475-9257-ab6c1994f155','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 ROSETTA EXTENSION 1 1384 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the ROSETTA EXTENSION 1 phase 2016-01-01 to 2016-04-05. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2016-01-30T20:13:15.000 to 2016-01-30T23:14:37.000.','public','2026-03-13T16:57:40.117340','2026-03-13T16:57:40.117349','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','b351dfcd-bdf6-42a4-892d-f3dc47daac3e','NASA Data.json','3a1265d8d668d2ff866562531fec5bb130adcff5277105db758114390121bf51','1.1','2026-03-13T16:57:40.117340','2026-03-13T16:57:40.117349','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('f87dac8c-e187-4acb-92e1-f63d7025c15b','Continuous Fixed Station Water Quality Measurements in Canaveral National Seashore, November 2008 (Certified)','This dataset represents continuous water quality measurements that were taken at a fixed point in Canaveral National Seashore during the month of November, 2008 as a part of the Fixed Station Water Quality Monitoring protocol that was developed by the Southeast Coast I&M Network (SECN). The measurements were taken by a YSI 6600 ESD Multi-Parameter Long Term Water Quality Monitoring Datasonde unit that serves as the standard fixed station water quality monitoring equipment for all similar operations conducted by the SECN. The following parameters were measured at 30 minute intervals during the time period that has been specified: Water Temperature, Specific Conductivity, Salinity, Dissolved Oxygen (DO), DO Concentration, Shallow Depth, pH Level, and Turbidity. Any anomalies noted regarding these parameters have also been noted in separate fields. Please note that these measurements have been certified by network personnel.','public','2026-03-26T05:32:22.392416','2026-03-26T05:32:22.392423','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','1dccf82a-8058-43c4-9586-38889aa12481','DOI NPS DCAT-US','e41a2d9e1f7541f6a62317fe340cd8eed69f57535b399ad5d0dc33e83c3ca03c','1.1','2026-03-26T05:32:22.392416','2026-03-26T05:32:22.392423','Vector Dataset','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('f898b59e-81ff-4e72-8fec-5c56c326e831','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P OSIWAC 3 ESC2-MTP014 RDR V3.0','This CODMAC level 3 data set contains radiometric calibrated image data in W/m^2/sr/nm, acquired by the OSIRIS Wide Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft during the COMET ESCORT 2 mission phase, covering the period from 2015-03-10T23:25:00.000 to 2015-04-08T11:24:59.000. The prime target is comet 67P/Churyumov-Gerasimenko 1 (1969 R1). This version V3.0 supersedes previous deliveries of the same dataset with the following changes since the last version: Lien corrected dataset after the July and October 2018 PSA/PDS external peer reviews. Updated documentation and ancillary files, added document on bandpass filter. Updated SCIENCE_USER_GUIDE_V03.PDF to include one section about FAQ and one section about image data quality. Added shutter backtravel and readout issues to image quality map. Updated DATA_QUALITY_ID keyword in image header. Improved handling of images with missing packets. Included FITs files. Browse products changed to the same size as the original image.','public','2026-03-13T19:29:03.963548','2026-03-13T19:29:03.963559','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','854a9582-6af7-4aa1-9f39-db52e38dacf0','NASA Data.json','6cdda6b1663a87f5ce27f224e2f8580cab4179eca55c0f3d5cebe6ab6aafed38','1.1','2026-03-13T19:29:03.963548','2026-03-13T19:29:03.963559','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('f8a1ad24-0ffc-410e-8ece-3df35bf3f017','ASTEROID ALBEDOS','This data set comprises a compilation of asteroid albedos for the convenience of the user. Most but not all of the albedos compiled here also appear in other PDS data sets.','public','2026-03-13T17:06:33.432702','2026-03-13T17:06:33.432707','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','8bcf851b-7a64-4b87-83ad-909a5c3ffb1f','NASA Data.json','0345a1a080951d8502969b90d3f7eb1bdfdb8dd522faeeb5c3dea173f4fb3d01','1.1','2026-03-13T17:06:33.432702','2026-03-13T17:06:33.432707','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('f9050035-e2ee-4fbe-bddb-4dfb7b15a9e5','Deepwater Horizon Response Air Sampling Data','The April 20, 2010, explosion and collapse of the BP Deepwater Horizon oil platform in the Gulf of Mexico resulted in the release of millions of barrels of oil into Gulf waters. The response to this disaster involved the efforts of tens of thousands of workers in a variety of capacities across Louisiana, Mississippi, Alabama, Florida, Texas, and in the Gulf of Mexico itself. The diverse work included oil and tar ball removal from beaches, oil skimming and booming near shores, burning of surface oil near the source of the oil release, surface application of dispersant by vessels and aircraft, and containment and recovery work on vessels at the release site. The nature of these activities raised concerns about potential occupational exposures to chemical and physical hazards and mental stressors.\n\nNIOSH investigators conducted health hazard evaluations (HHEs) of Deepwater Horizon Response onshore and offshore workers. The goals of the NIOSH HHE assessments were to describe acute health effects, evaluate occupational exposures in qualitative or quantitative assessments, and generate hypotheses regarding symptoms potentially related to work activities. Environmental air samples were collected in support of the goals.\n\nNIOSH investigators conducted the following exposure evaluations:\n\n- We conducted evaluations on board vessels releasing dispersant. These vessels were deployed to perform small‐scale releases of dispersant in an area with surface oil contamination.\n- We assessed exposures during in‐situ (i.e., on site) burns of surface oil.\n- We assessed exposures on fishing and shrimping trawlers in the Vessels of Opportunity (VoO) program that were assigned to remove surface oil by booming and skimming.\n- We assessed exposures aboard vessels located at the Deepwater Horizon incident site.\n- We assessed exposures during boom and vessel decontamination operations.','public','2026-03-18T17:18:39.310739','2026-03-18T17:18:39.310746','Centers for Disease Control and Prevention','Division of Field Studies and Evaluation, Hazard Evaluation and Technical Assistance Branch','009:20','76342afc-472d-4f59-8664-80846485e643','Healthdata.gov','8475baeb9acfca93b569128f345970e7e60d9ce4e78f5f16bbf5598a59e6daa1','1.1','2026-03-18T17:18:39.310739','2026-03-18T17:18:39.310746','National Institute for Occupational Safety and Health','009:034',0,'hhs-gov'),('f912979e-39d0-42eb-aeae-303312424d26','Continuous Fixed Station Water Quality Measurements in Timucuan Ecological and Historic Preserve, March 2008 (Certified)','This dataset represents continuous water quality measurements that were taken at a fixed point in Timucuan Ecological and Historic Preserve during the month of March, 2008 as a part of the Fixed Station Water Quality Monitoring protocol that was developed by the Southeast Coast I&M Network (SECN). The measurements were taken by a YSI 6600 ESD Multi-Parameter Long Term Water Quality Monitoring Datasonde unit that serves as the standard fixed station water quality monitoring equipment for all similar operations conducted by the SECN. The following parameters were measured at 30 minute intervals during the time period that has been specified: Water Temperature, Specific Conductivity, Salinity, Dissolved Oxygen (DO), DO Concentration, Shallow Depth, pH Level, and Turbidity. Any anomalies noted regarding these parameters have also been noted in separate fields. Please note that these measurements have been certified by network personnel.','public','2026-03-26T05:30:26.547778','2026-03-26T05:30:26.547783','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','edbacc57-b07d-4641-a986-ae63ad796726','DOI NPS DCAT-US','ef33e2f0e7774a61f5ba687f2864ea69c57f3b1a35e474fe19b48b95149326bb','1.1','2026-03-26T05:30:26.547778','2026-03-26T05:30:26.547783','Vector Dataset','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('f944b243-4c7d-421b-bfab-857705a4e964','VG2 NEP MAG RESAMP RDR HELIOGRAPHIC                                       COORDINATES 1.92SEC V1.0','This data set includes data from the Low Field Magnetometer (LFM)       during the inbound Neptune encounter beginning in the solar wind       and continuing until the first magnetopause crossing. The       magnetometer are given in Heliographic coordinates and the data have       been averaged from the 60ms instrument sample rate       to a 1.92 second resampled rate.','public','2026-03-13T19:29:20.171296','2026-03-13T19:29:20.171302','planetary plasma interactions','Planetary Data System','026:00','a95c73e3-31ba-4488-aa7e-02194ef55c3b','NASA Data.json','423bc691038d68298a7f33b0e1ca4ee8730f36b83d7e57a1ee84ce2efb713ba3','1.1','2026-03-13T19:29:20.171296','2026-03-13T19:29:20.171302','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('f98743a3-ebc4-4eae-897e-d79af9e680c6','MARS EXPRESS MARS MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 3 3293 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2010-01-01 to 2012-12-31. It is a Global Gravity measurement and covers the time 2012-05-20T12:02:13.000 to 2012-05-20T14:05:56.500.','public','2026-03-13T17:34:37.354176','2026-03-13T17:34:37.354184','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','07efaac3-4b20-44d8-8eb5-5ed091c17609','NASA Data.json','28ee226e7f0cae9b09317f2a85d5b1f45f6240ced7d22c918f722267cfed1055','1.1','2026-03-13T17:34:37.354176','2026-03-13T17:34:37.354184','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('f99090b8-66f0-4abf-8641-8fbaafa6267e','DID(IT) - Digital Innovation & Development - Information Technology-GoMaruHachi: Section 508 Issues','Section 508 issues created in USCIS GitHub Enterprise repositories','non-public','2026-03-22T11:54:50.566511','2026-03-22T11:54:50.566515','Unspecified','Open Data (MGMT)','024:030','c68f30e6-5400-4387-ae2a-6e1f7e95c6da','DHS datajson source','6fb36620c71ab5b43b895bc140e54fd27c7d72cda29477fdaea09d151ed442df','1.1','2026-03-22T11:54:50.566511','2026-03-22T11:54:50.566515',NULL,'024:000',0,'dhs-gov'),('f9a8e61c-739c-41d4-ad2b-c56b405f8c57','JOLTS Tableau - JOLTS Dataset','The Job Openings and Labor Turnover dataset contains levels, ranks, and rates for hires, openings, and total separations by geography and date.','public','2026-03-28T22:00:53.002913','2026-03-28T22:00:53.002918','data.iowa.gov','svqueen',NULL,'b301c3fe-1be1-4990-b947-74a9fe3894d4','Iowa metadata','c0cb647c5cceff1fbe64188cb378196855160ba42f972b329b578ae27fdb8234','1.1','2026-03-28T22:00:53.002913','2026-03-28T22:00:53.002918','Economic Statistics',NULL,0,'state-of-iowa'),('f9b45ed0-dab8-4d4d-9314-5346b23d27d9','NEW HORIZONS  MVIC PLUTO ENCOUNTER  CALIBRATED V3.0','This data set contains Calibrated data taken by the New Horizons  Multispectral Visible Imaging Camera  instrument during the  Pluto encounter  mission phase. This is VERSION 3.0 of this data set.   This data set contains MVIC observations taken during the  the Approach (Jan-Jul, 2015), Encounter, Departure, and  Transition mission sub-phases, including flyby observations  taken on 14 July, 2015, and departure and calibration data  through late October, 2016. This data set completes the  Pluto mission phase deliveries for MVIC.   This is version 3.0 of this dataset. Changes since version 2.0 include  the addition of data downlinked between the end of January, 2016 and the end of October, 2016, completing the delivery of all data covering the  Pluto Encounter and subsequent Calibration Campaign. It includes multi-  map observations from the Approach phase, observations of the moons, hi- res, full-frame observations from Pluto Encounter and Departure, and  ring search observations. There may be some overlap between prior  datasets and this dataset, due to only partial, windowed, or lossy data  in prior datasets. This dataset also includes functional tests from the Calibration Campaign, including calibration observations of the M6 and  M7 clusters, and HD205905.   Also, updates were made to the calibration files, documentation, and  catalog files.   For any data previously delivered as sub-frame windows, this delivery  will fill in the image data outside those windows.   Changes to the calibration involved only changes to the  spectrum-specific calibration constants provided in FITS headers and  in PDS labels; the calibrated Data Number values in the calibrated  data set, excluding image data outside the sub-frame windows  mentioned above, will not be substantively changed.','public','2026-03-13T19:44:17.624531','2026-03-13T19:44:17.624536','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','1da2dca4-e4e3-4675-a48c-da351873dbae','NASA Data.json','faf1b2f93766c3f194ada0eba2f58997c274d8a5af0bff34c7497844fb7dd72e','1.1','2026-03-13T19:44:17.624531','2026-03-13T19:44:17.624536','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('fa02fe4d-1c8e-4deb-bbb5-b568bb31b8bd','ROSETTA-ORBITER EARTH OSINAC 4 EAR2 RDR V1.0','This CODMAC level 4 data set contains radiometric calibrated and geometric distortion corrected (resampled) image data in W/m^2/sr/nm,  acquired by the OSIRIS Narrow Angle Camera on the Rosetta spacecraft  during the EARTH SWING-BY 2 mission phase, covering the period  from 2007-09-13T00:00:00.000 to 2008-01-27T23:59:59.000. The prime target is planet Earth. This version V1.0 is the first version of this dataset.','public','2026-03-13T18:49:38.239800','2026-03-13T18:49:38.239805','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','dad0be2a-8990-49c0-b183-9e3dc8a6b8a2','NASA Data.json','fca26554daf911366642c11f8b0eeebf5e96a55ff250392c41ed197d0513a558','1.1','2026-03-13T18:49:38.239800','2026-03-13T18:49:38.239805','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('fa1ba3d5-524c-4964-b551-aa1d98d8d0fc','VOYAGER 2 SOLAR WIND PLS 1 HOUR                                      AVERAGES V1.0','Voyager 2 plasma data of the solar wind, 1 hour averages.','public','2026-03-13T18:47:28.846305','2026-03-13T18:47:28.846332','planetary plasma interactions','Planetary Data System','026:00','75c1bee7-1db9-43ac-a932-c155390a9d99','NASA Data.json','d0340fb0c9c561866a46a028784e1c5c88259fdf80720f11024f1f40e20d2a2a','1.1','2026-03-13T18:47:28.846305','2026-03-13T18:47:28.846332','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('fa49aa8c-ffae-44d2-aca4-1c362dcdaa21','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 3 1078 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 3 phase 2015-07-01 to 2015-10-21. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-10-04T20:53:10.000 to 2015-10-05T05:22:30.000.','public','2026-03-13T20:06:01.995595','2026-03-13T20:06:01.995602','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','e9d02a03-55b1-4152-88b5-cdc2bfcc4bb2','NASA Data.json','8f8687e9819fc5a7b5e09b3999a359060f63b6af8c9293587173b03ab69c7604','1.1','2026-03-13T20:06:01.995595','2026-03-13T20:06:01.995602','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('fa539a70-42cc-4cdb-88f9-f2b0c66ce720','2023 NOAA Topobathy Lidar: Whitefish Point Lake Superior, MI','These lidar are processed Classified LAS 1.4 files, formatted to 983 individual 500 m x 500 m tiles. The project AOI covers approximately 161.5 square kilometers, and includes the area from Whitefish Point to Bay Mills, MI in Eastern Lake Superior, the eastern portion of which falls within and EPA\'s St. Marys River area of concern. Lidar was collected in August 2023. Tetra Tech established 4 ground control points that were used to calibrate the lidar to known ground positions.','public','2026-03-19T20:04:22.188541','2026-03-26T20:18:44.583176',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-03-19T20:04:22.188541','2026-03-26T20:18:44.583176',NULL,NULL,NULL,'noaa-gov'),('fa7efb17-2b31-439b-9012-1399ff38fb9f','ROSETTA-ORBITER SOLAR WIND RPCIES 2 CR5 V1.0','This dataset contains EDITED RAW DATA of the Rosetta RPCIES instrument taken during the Cruise 5 phase (CR5). Included are the data taken between 26 Apr 2010 and 02 May 2010.','public','2026-03-13T17:38:21.359125','2026-03-13T17:38:21.359129','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','fe81fbe4-4162-4a49-8b67-8b48348cb725','NASA Data.json','cbee1b4a34ed4babac79e6709a6af98b2f407ef2a9f008d00f7ac4e04856bc35','1.1','2026-03-13T17:38:21.359125','2026-03-13T17:38:21.359129','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('fae9bd86-fe7d-4ccb-bb4c-f9ca73b8f0f4','HPMS Roadway Sample 2023','State DOTs provide the Highway Performance Monitoring System (HPMS) with the location limits of highway sections used to represent statewide aggregations based on a statistically valid Sample Panel.','public','2026-03-28T13:37:50.603880','2026-03-28T13:37:50.603886','Federal Highway Administration','Office of Highway Policy Information','021:15','bd6cd9dd-a071-4174-b0e1-9f31c3cf6ceb','DOT Socrata Data.json','053505dd616ce96b093d0b23660cb174272cbc555dda41c16eafbd82e2063775','1.1','2026-03-28T13:37:50.603880','2026-03-28T13:37:50.603886','Roadways and Bridges','021:009',0,'dot-gov'),('fb063d09-067c-472b-a38a-cf064b78d6fe','ROSETTA-ORBITER COMET ESCORT OSINAC 3 RDR MTP 012 V1.0','This data set contains calibrated images acquired by the OSIRIS Narrow AngleCamera during the escort phase of the Rosetta mission at the comet 67P,covering the period from 2015-01-13 to 2015-02-10.','public','2026-03-13T18:28:42.675113','2026-03-13T18:28:42.675118','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','21dcc4cd-ffc0-4fba-9596-ab8f0bcf0ed9','NASA Data.json','d5b7cb1b6a175d39f8eda4e1d1c2c6d6ac8412ce6bc420de6608fd3c94325952','1.1','2026-03-13T18:28:42.675113','2026-03-13T18:28:42.675118','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('fb49fa27-729a-4e7c-857a-21354d635a7d','MARS EXPRESS MARS MARSIS                                      EXPERIMENT DATA RECORD V2.0','This dataset contains the                    scientific telemetry produced by the MARSIS                    instrument after editing for duplicated and                    corrupted packets, together with geometric                    information computed on ground to locate                    observations in space and time. Both subsurface                    and ionosphere sounding data are included in                    the dataset.','public','2026-03-13T17:27:46.416511','2026-03-13T17:27:46.416517','planetary plasma interactions','Planetary Data System','026:00','f91657dc-0fa4-4825-8608-a29901356015','NASA Data.json','7f972fe9f151d4b01f149704182e318e9143b1398e2cd786b7fdbd64e1897620','1.1','2026-03-13T17:27:46.416511','2026-03-13T17:27:46.416517','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('fb5d1402-9181-435f-ab6c-013af06c37ba','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 4 1274 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 4 phase 2015-10-22 to 2015-12-31. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-12-21T10:03:10.000 to 2015-12-21T14:12:23.000.','public','2026-03-13T19:52:16.785686','2026-03-13T19:52:16.785693','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','45da6ff2-a366-4fb1-a832-4a20497b5969','NASA Data.json','f72a094b591122c4cd645cf819989f0a4b99eafd05ff4a9fe586fe4477d6e347','1.1','2026-03-13T19:52:16.785686','2026-03-13T19:52:16.785693','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('fb6d38c0-e810-4c89-89c5-0f39fb967355','ROSETTA-ORBITER COMET ESCORT 2 OSINAC 2 EDR MTP015 V2.0','This data set contains images acquired by the OSIRIS Narrow Angle Camera during the COMET ESCORT 2 phase of the Rosetta mission at the comet 67P, covering the period from 2015-04-08T11:25:00.000 to 2015-05-05T23:24:59.000. This version V2.0 supersedes previous deliveries of the same dataset.','public','2026-03-13T19:12:10.988946','2026-03-13T19:12:10.988951','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','a1fd4912-b79f-4813-9104-aa1353593018','NASA Data.json','315708fdaf0ad743497c9d39184a23b21df7a43744416ec50a2b679731aec26d','1.1','2026-03-13T19:12:10.988946','2026-03-13T19:12:10.988951','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('fb9c8c80-023d-42cf-9fec-67b61598f7c6','Bat Activity Inventory at Pearl Harbor National Memorial - Acoustic Data - Dataset as delivered','We examined acoustic activity of the endangered Hawaiian hoary bat (\'ōpe\'ape\'a; Lasiurus semotus) at at Pearl Harbor National Memorial (PERL) located on Ford Island, O‘ahu, Hawaii. The study area was located at the Ford Island Chief Petty Officer\'s (CPO) Bungalows Neighborhood, which covers approximately 4 acres and includes five historic CPO bungalows. Bat echolocation vocalizations were recorded at four acoustic stations (PERL1 - PERL4) located between 20 and 25 m above sea level, that operated nightly from June 2024 through December 2024. At station PERL-1 a total of 176 nights were sampled acoustically with \'ōpe\'ape\'a activity detected on seven nights. A total of nine \'ōpe\'ape\'a echolocation call events, zero feeding buzzes, and zero occurrences of multiple bats were documented. At station PERL-2 a total of 173 nights were sampled acoustically with \'ōpe\'ape\'a activity detected on seven nights. A total of eight \'ōpe\'ape\'a echolocation call events, zero feeding buzzes, and zero occurrences of multiple bats were documented. At station PERL-3 a total of 148 nights were sampled acoustically with \'ōpe\'ape\'a activity detected on six nights. A total of six \'ōpe\'ape\'a echolocation call events, zero feeding buzzes, and zero occurrences of multiple bats were documented. And finally, at station PERL-4 a total of 164 nights were sampled acoustically with \'ōpe\'ape\'a activity detected on six nights. A total of seven \'ōpe\'ape\'a echolocation call events, zero feeding buzzes, and zero occurrences of multiple bats were documented.','public','2026-03-27T05:28:47.244538','2026-03-27T05:28:47.244545','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','eaa5d73c-e385-4407-919e-8a84f47d6e63','DOI NPS DCAT-US','60a4e4328d08e1d4e8044ea67ab0f3a92ba9c11834be467a7e3f811f6b044ac2','1.1','2026-03-27T05:28:47.244538','2026-03-27T05:28:47.244545','Generic Dataset','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('fbbb4c80-9eb1-4caa-bb0c-526d0f919305','EX2106: 2021 U.S. Blake Plateau Mapping 2 (Mapping)','From September 5 - September 28, 2021, NOAA Ocean Exploration conducted mapping operations on the Blake Plateau within U.S. waters, aiding in closing the gaps within this region. The second of two cruises focused on mapping this region, EX-21-06 collected 25,800 square kilometers of bathymetry and associated water column data, 25,790 square kilometers of which were within the U.S. Exclusive Economic Zone and Territorial Sea deeper than 200 m. The exploratory mapping operations conducted during this cruise will provide initial characterization of the region, as well as data to support further exploration with remotely operated vehicles planned for EX-21-07.','public','2026-03-28T23:17:23.468824','2026-03-28T23:17:23.468829',NULL,NULL,NULL,'5fbd965f-3c1c-420e-8a73-7111ebe90fb3','NCDDC OER',NULL,NULL,'2026-03-28T23:17:23.468824','2026-03-28T23:17:23.468829',NULL,NULL,NULL,'noaa-gov'),('fbe43318-99e1-4b8a-98a5-55830b88ceb7','MARS EXPRESS SUN MRS 1/2/3                                     EXTENDED MISSION 8 4383 V1.0','This is a Mars Express                                     Radio Science data set, collected                                     during the extended mission phase                                     2023-01-01 to 2023-12-31.                                     It is a Solar Conjunction                                     measurement and covers the time                                     2023-12-06T05:34:49.000 to                                     2023-12-06T08:54:41.000.','public','2026-03-13T19:33:47.241007','2026-03-13T19:33:47.241013','geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','075d13b2-c94d-4deb-950d-5b35b19a3881','NASA Data.json','876f9bdd0106b78e1705630ec9b5dee8385722333cf5c95bbdea09e6fbb4b27d','1.1','2026-03-13T19:33:47.241007','2026-03-13T19:33:47.241013','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('fbe4d30d-c2b2-4e6a-821d-82517910c5c6','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 PRELANDING 0193 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the PRELANDING phase 2014-01-21 to 2014-11-18. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2014-08-09T20:42:00.000 to 2014-08-10T02:13:13.000.','public','2026-03-13T16:49:22.314192','2026-03-13T16:49:22.314200','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','9437b6d9-72b8-461a-b8db-c12567f52e20','NASA Data.json','5d0d7b4c710f2d9030a58fcae2c7e98b47ac3c54285d57d3b519b69ba808d0cb','1.1','2026-03-13T16:49:22.314192','2026-03-13T16:49:22.314200','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('fc1b2368-c085-4a8a-b3f2-8f0a38a5ac49','V-safe Registration','Users of the V-safe data are required to adhere to the following standards for the analysis and reporting of research data. All research results must be presented and/or published in a manner that protects the confidentiality of participants. V-safe data will not be presented and/or published in any way in which an individual can be identified. Therefore, users will:\n<ol>\n<li>Not attempt to link or permit others to link the data with individually identified records in another database.</li>\n<li>Not attempt to learn the identity of any participant in the data and will not deliberately combine these data with other CDC or non-CDC data for the purpose of matching records to identify individuals. If you should inadvertently discover the identity of any participant, you will ensure the identity of any participant is kept confidential, and will not be used in any publications and/or presentations.</li>\n<li>Not imply or state, either in written or oral form, that interpretations based on analysis of the data reflect official CDC policies or positions.</li>\n<li>Understand that sub-national analyses are not appropriate for this national sample and will not be conducted. </li>\n<li>Understand that V-safe is a voluntary self-enrollment program requiring smartphone access; therefore, information from V-safe might not be representative or generalizable to the US population.</li></ol>\nBy clicking on the weblink below to download and use these V-safe data, you signify your agreement to comply with the above-stated terms.\n\nV-safe is a voluntary U.S. active safety surveillance system established by CDC to characterize local and systemic side effects of new vaccines administered after U.S. authorization or licensure. V-safe participants are not a random sample of all vaccinated persons in the United States and data might not be generalizable to the full U.S. vaccinated population. Participants may have been more likely to complete surveys if experiencing symptoms post-vaccination. All V-safe measures are self-reported, therefore there may be some misclassification of outcomes, vaccine-related information, or demographics.\n\nOccasional system outages and attrition over time may contribute to incomplete reporting. \n\nV-safe Registration public data includes de-identified demographic data for all participants that registered to V-safe from 10/20/2023 to 3/23/2025.  Corresponding protocol data (RSV for Adults, RSV for Pregnant Women, and COVID-19) can be downloaded at data.cdc.gov.  Please review the V-safe data user agreement before analyzing any V-safe data.','public','2026-03-20T17:36:12.029304','2026-03-20T17:36:12.029308','Centers for Disease Control and Prevention','Vsafe@cdc.gov','009:20','3f760b66-a7ec-4943-8e7a-05eb1e038a75','Healthdata.gov','553f55ca3c73431236c7cfab804ff57897f1a1f671371aeefb3e255c064a4826','1.1','2026-03-20T17:36:12.029304','2026-03-20T17:36:12.029308','National Center for Emerging and Zoonotic Infectious Diseases','009:028',0,'hhs-gov'),('fc240405-c724-4248-a610-6cad8c76fceb','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P ROSINA 2 ESC4 V2.0','This data set contains CODMAC level 2 science data acquired by the COPS, DFMS and RTOF ROSINA sensors between 2015-10-20 and 2016-02-09 during the Escort phase 4 of the Rosetta mission at the comet 67P/CG. V2.0 : Some missing DFMS PDS files were added and corrupted files have been removed.','public','2026-03-13T18:54:22.612535','2026-03-13T18:54:22.612541','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','97b493ea-841c-4099-93e3-4f02aa46eb35','NASA Data.json','4f99150f5774c27c6238913360e39daffa179b14b0944a4e70f00e09ea9a9374','1.1','2026-03-13T18:54:22.612535','2026-03-13T18:54:22.612541','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('fc244795-9e78-40a9-ba8e-22027e6439e4','myUSCIS - user-group-service','Stores user group assignments and roles.','non-public','2026-03-22T11:53:08.221398','2026-03-22T11:53:08.221402','Unspecified','Open Data (MGMT)','024:030','68f00f76-de33-4a06-b399-73bbc0ef14ed','DHS datajson source','d95c01d396463ee851c5f205db9f7e2bac989c2f4e50e84bd75668f65e7b3fab','1.1','2026-03-22T11:53:08.221398','2026-03-22T11:53:08.221402',NULL,'024:000',0,'dhs-gov'),('fc7959a2-547d-44bd-83f9-98cc471236ca','ROSETTA-ORBITER DUST MIDAS 3 PRL SAMPLES V1.0','The Micro-Imaging Dust Analysis System (MIDAS) is an instrument on theROSETTA Orbiter that will provide 3D images and statistical parametersof pristine cometary particles hitting the detector. This data setincludes all data from the PRELANDING mission phase.','public','2026-03-13T16:39:21.831376','2026-03-13T16:39:21.831382','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','edae4470-ccab-431c-a564-52d342d81874','NASA Data.json','5e44e925ae3c5c7354e48bbb30f3b2391e6fa1ec12494f39e55a9af18f22e567','1.1','2026-03-13T16:39:21.831376','2026-03-13T16:39:21.831382','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('fc7cd2dc-a411-41da-b7e8-4674a7b6a75a','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 ROSETTA EXTENSION 1 1317 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the ROSETTA EXTENSION 1 phase 2016-01-01 to 2016-04-05. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2016-01-06T21:29:05.000 to 2016-01-06T23:58:19.500.','public','2026-03-13T16:51:49.773560','2026-03-13T16:51:49.773566','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','6ad76c82-3a8e-4a97-b116-8ec8f8c74589','NASA Data.json','66f6f8d6f18981561921bb95370af3c5251a48288dd59120b5831a42ef9d3708','1.1','2026-03-13T16:51:49.773560','2026-03-13T16:51:49.773566','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('fc8c40f3-fb13-48ec-a47a-3f5fb84df379','Coastal Mapping Program of  Port of Anchorage, AK, AK2509-CS-N','These data provide an accurate high-resolution shoreline compiled from imagery of  Port of Anchorage, AK .  This vector shoreline data is based on an office interpretation of imagery that may be suitable as a geographic information system (GIS) data layer. This metadata describes information for both the line and point shapefiles. The NGS attribution scheme \'Coastal Cartographic Object Attribute Source Table (C-COAST)\' was developed to conform the attribution of various sources of shoreline data into one attribution catalog. C-COAST is not a recognized standard, but was influenced by the International Hydrographic Organization\'s S-57 Object-Attribute standard so the data would be more accurately translated into S-57.  This resource is a member of  https://inport.nmfs.noaa.gov/inport/item/39808','public','2026-03-19T20:04:12.694408','2026-03-19T20:04:12.694416',NULL,NULL,NULL,'74b5523b-0166-4180-ba67-4ee2e8024e9c','NOS NGS',NULL,NULL,'2026-03-19T20:04:12.694408','2026-03-19T20:04:12.694416',NULL,NULL,NULL,'noaa-gov'),('fcee1a43-296f-4254-9c7a-e71ede0e4501','TNO AND CENTAUR DIAMETERS, ALBEDOS, AND DENSITIES V4.0','This data set is a compilation of published diameters, albedos, and densities for Transneptunian Objects (TNOs) and Centaurs. A total of 190 objects are listed, many with more than one entry. This version covers published values through 31 March 2016.','public','2026-03-13T17:55:12.995576','2026-03-13T17:55:12.995582','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','30a543d2-2b66-445f-8fbe-2fbdc6b561d6','NASA Data.json','31938835f483392cea836318cf62c0034dba1e5d80030dc4f89f3fc9ec68d2ca','1.1','2026-03-13T17:55:12.995576','2026-03-13T17:55:12.995582','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('fd1317a4-d715-4859-b56a-0f897ed5f154','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 PRELANDING 0295 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the PRELANDING phase 2014-01-21 to 2014-11-18. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2014-09-15T06:17:02.000 to 2014-09-15T15:10:07.500.','public','2026-03-13T17:08:15.544337','2026-03-13T17:08:15.544342','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','eea68baa-11d2-44a3-81db-abd81dfe5b2f','NASA Data.json','0026b99d4ac7c5497f8c89b86ad2edeacb610b3706060fe22fdc9a2bfce272bb','1.1','2026-03-13T17:08:15.544337','2026-03-13T17:08:15.544342','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('fd1b9bac-5a78-4825-a98a-fd0dfc9c102b','Continuous Fixed Station Water Quality Measurements in Timucuan Ecological and Historic Preserve, August 2008 (Certified)','This dataset represents continuous water quality measurements that were taken at a fixed point in Timucuan Ecological and Historic Preserve during the month of August, 2008 as a part of the Fixed Station Water Quality Monitoring protocol that was developed by the Southeast Coast I&M Network (SECN). The measurements were taken by a YSI 6600 ESD Multi-Parameter Long Term Water Quality Monitoring Datasonde unit that serves as the standard fixed station water quality monitoring equipment for all similar operations conducted by the SECN. The following parameters were measured at 30 minute intervals during the time period that has been specified: Water Temperature, Specific Conductivity, Salinity, Dissolved Oxygen (DO), DO Concentration, Shallow Depth, pH Level, and Turbidity. Any anomalies noted regarding these parameters have also been noted in separate fields. Please note that these measurements have been certified by network personnel.','public','2026-03-26T05:29:56.997751','2026-03-26T05:29:56.997757','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','60e0ba39-1a4e-4c32-81b9-886da67e9f0c','DOI NPS DCAT-US','5646acc5923867a3e2a358cd18ba035ec28d6792c42b7f040915459b9662f8bf','1.1','2026-03-26T05:29:56.997751','2026-03-26T05:29:56.997757','Vector Dataset','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('fd2aea9e-51e9-446c-8337-f931a82440f9','myUSCIS - events','Temporarily stores event information for surfacing backend events to front end clients (for instance when we change the state of a feature toggle).','non-public','2026-03-22T11:53:49.793361','2026-03-22T11:53:49.793365','Unspecified','Open Data (MGMT)','024:030','c140d3ca-7832-47bd-b422-6d5e244c3e5f','DHS datajson source','221990d54c7209ccd66fac19e289f76a17345008ba2a393d855ba3ba6bd4cec9','1.1','2026-03-22T11:53:49.793361','2026-03-22T11:53:49.793365',NULL,'024:000',0,'dhs-gov'),('fd2e4b05-f631-459b-b11d-b058c82ab869','Chemical and physical data for analysis of nitrogen fluxes and nominal travel time in surface water','<p dir=\"ltr\">Data were collected from a former cranberry farm that was restored to a wetland in Plymouth, Massachusetts, called \"Tidmarsh\". Between 2016 and 2024, data included surface water discharges, total nitrogen and nitrate concentrations in surface water, and specific conductivity concentrations to determine surface water travel times. Data were used for the following objectives: (1) watershed-scale water quality modelling to determine sources of N to Tidmarsh, (2) weekly field measurements to quantify seasonal patterns of NO<sub>3</sub><sup>-</sup> retention by Tidmarsh, and (3) bi-monthly injections of a conservative tracer to quantify solute residence time and its effect on NO<sub>3</sub><sup>-</sup> retention by Tidmarsh.</p>','public','2026-03-13T22:44:21.956151','2026-03-13T22:44:21.956158','Agricultural Research Service','Kennedy, Casey, D.','005:18','11576647-3a69-417d-bd5b-04ab8bcdabe0','USDA JSON','084f3115f16da1472a57ded92a701254d28530effac99d16ad11e7f730db13b6','1.1','2026-03-13T22:44:21.956151','2026-03-13T22:44:21.956158',NULL,'005:040',0,'usda-gov'),('fd2f5c4c-8f37-4095-8a62-98d6493b2414','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 4 1295 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 4 phase 2015-10-22 to 2015-12-31. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-12-29T01:24:05.000 to 2015-12-29T04:12:45.000.','public','2026-03-13T18:55:39.613346','2026-03-13T18:55:39.613355','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','c5fa4108-8937-48b6-ad5d-a356803cd18e','NASA Data.json','3fb2347bb1a6b5527f0d865690b8073cefd30b5535d6830dcb567fc4174678d2','1.1','2026-03-13T18:55:39.613346','2026-03-13T18:55:39.613355','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('fd2fecbb-5595-4315-b45b-9a206319920b','Data from: Tillage in southeastern U.S. row crops reduces ground-nesting bee incidence and diversity compared to field edges','<p dir=\"ltr\">This dataset was collected to assess the response of ground-nesting bees to different agricultural management treatments while documenting key environmental variables. Data were collected from March 2021 to November 2022 at the E.V. Smith Research Center in Shorter, Alabama. The study site consisted of 96 experimental subplots arranged in a randomized block design within a long-established agricultural field. It provides valuable insights into the interactions between soil management practices, soil conditions, vegetation cover, and ground-nesting bee populations in agricultural landscapes. It may be useful for ecological modeling, particularly in understanding how management actions influence bee emergence. However, caution should be used in interpreting emergence trap data, as it does not represent floral visitation behavior.</p>','public','2026-03-13T22:46:57.244360','2026-03-13T22:46:57.244367','Agricultural Research Service','Campbell, Joshua, W.','005:18','ac8212d5-aeab-4b8d-b4da-f297db2c8147','USDA JSON','af0782da2a902bd316257e09a8cc1bcffab88599255043b249e3dccaa8e2dc34','1.1','2026-03-13T22:46:57.244360','2026-03-13T22:46:57.244367',NULL,'005:040',0,'usda-gov'),('fd3c8385-baf4-478b-9013-ac571c69dfce','Citywide Mobility Survey - Household 2024','The Citywide Mobility Survey (CMS) is NYC DOT\'s annual travel survey to assess the travel behavior, preferences, and attitudes of NYC residents. It is composed of 5 linked data tables.\n\nCitywide Mobility Survey (CMS) Household table contains data about the characteristics of the participant’s household, including household size, income, type of residence, number of vehicles, bicycles, and micromobility devices, package delivery location, and other demographic and transportation-related information.\n\n<b>Other 2024 Citywide Mobility Survey Datasets:</b>\n<a href=\"https://data.cityofnewyork.us/d/i2im-iqtt\">Citywide Mobility Survey - Person 2024 </a>\n<a href=\"https://data.cityofnewyork.us/d/naav-ygga\">Citywide Mobility Survey - Day 2024</a>\n<a href=\"https://data.cityofnewyork.us/d/wgnh-qwsg\">Citywide Mobility Survey - Trip 2024</a>\n<a href=\"https://data.cityofnewyork.us/d/qhkz-4dqm\">Citywide Mobility Survey - Vehicle 2024</a>\n\nSee all the <a href=\"https://data.cityofnewyork.us/browse?sortBy=relevance&pageSize=20&Data-Collection_Data-Collection=Citywide+Mobility+Survey\">Citywide Mobility Survey Data</a>, including past surveys.','public','2026-03-29T04:35:08.419531','2026-03-29T04:35:08.419537','data.cityofnewyork.us','NYC OpenData',NULL,'b19f4cef-3a38-49c2-ad74-7f707847c0be','NYC JSON','53c35d97a9f973f0557356a56902ce6e3f2b4130268e7c898b2b99b0ea6c65ee','1.1','2026-03-29T04:35:08.419531','2026-03-29T04:35:08.419537','Transportation',NULL,0,'city-of-new-york'),('fd3cf13e-6118-477e-8729-81e1fb76df0d','MARS EXPRESS MARS MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 6 3968 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2017-01-01 to 2018-12-31. It is a Occultation measurement and covers the time 2018-10-09T14:27:43.399 to 2018-10-09T14:57:16.399.','public','2026-03-13T17:35:31.655891','2026-03-13T17:35:31.655896','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','c9f1116f-6dd2-4e65-9069-1173ddaec1fc','NASA Data.json','6811dece265d637b2c8687bb68e2a07a70688405b651bb9a22a7571aebbbdb2c','1.1','2026-03-13T17:35:31.655891','2026-03-13T17:35:31.655896','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('fd69f69c-ad8f-45b8-b654-752a23a1c487','Code Cases Past 90 Days','<p><span style=\'background-color:rgb(255,255,255); color:rgb(74,74,74); font-family:&quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px;\'><span style=\'display:inline !important; float:none; font-style:normal; font-variant-caps:normal; font-variant-ligatures:normal; font-weight:400; letter-spacing:normal; text-align:start; text-decoration-color:initial; text-decoration-style:initial; text-indent:0px; text-transform:none; word-spacing:0px;\'>Provides data for code cases that were opened in the past 90 days based on district, address, and type of code case.</span></span></p>','public','2026-03-22T02:54:51.672121','2026-03-29T03:52:23.444308','Wake County','WakeCountyGovernment',NULL,'e6cabe69-7496-4769-af19-51153fa289f5','Wake County Open Data Json Harvest Source','e2d581abe76596233c473345b6cd1d0186e96bbd6b1409df74853eff24a997ab','1.1','2026-03-22T02:54:51.672121','2026-03-29T03:52:23.444308','geospatial',NULL,0,'wake-county'),('fd79a6de-757f-4662-85d0-6cf8bf7e82ef','CMOR METEOROID STREAM SURVEY V2.0','A seven-year radar survey of meteor showers has been carried out with the Canadian Meteor Orbit Radar (CMOR) from 2002-2008 (Brown et al. 2008, 2010). This survey resulted in the unambiguous detection and orbital characterization of 109 major and minor meteor showers. This data set includes a list of the detected meteor showers along with their orbital parameters.','public','2026-03-13T19:35:33.119734','2026-03-13T19:35:33.119739','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','a5b623e8-f90c-40ab-8fc3-70f0aae08f95','NASA Data.json','3c1606c1015de21943790a058ee11ce6df6a25df3894a1dca1c1e0933bc19476','1.1','2026-03-13T19:35:33.119734','2026-03-13T19:35:33.119739','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('fd8ef6fd-5941-44f6-92db-d673da85840b','Walton-Smith CTD, WS18120, WS18120_WS18120STN55, 2018-05-02, 25.3512N 81.1955W','Walton-Smith Conductivity, Temperature, Depth (CTD) - WS18120 - WS18120_WS18120STN55 - 2018-05-02 - 25.3512N 81.1955W. Hydrographic Measurements in the Gulf of Mexico. flags: 1 = good; 3 =  mean ÃÂ± 3*standard deviation; 4 = mean ÃÂ± 5*standard deviation; 9 = missing. other','public','2026-03-26T19:14:37.364086','2026-03-26T19:14:37.364094',NULL,NULL,NULL,'c18b3aed-96f9-453a-893e-8d816b3cd285','ioos',NULL,NULL,'2026-03-26T19:14:37.364086','2026-03-26T19:14:37.364094',NULL,NULL,NULL,'noaa-gov'),('fdfd6235-51cb-47c4-bc61-864a70f55ccb','JUNO J/SW JOVIAN AURORAL DISTRIBUTION DEF V1.0','This data set consists of all of the calibrated data collected by the JADE (Jovian Auroral Distributions Experiment) on-board the Juno spacecraft in units of DEF, with pitch angles included for JADE-E.','public','2026-03-13T17:17:27.664724','2026-03-13T17:17:27.664729','Planetary Plasma Interactions','Planetary Data System','026:00','2638c940-4d7e-4018-a41f-d64b712e8908','NASA Data.json','a81bd24226dcddd194502fd38f17dfb54f84402bf577b40bbe3bc92295def37c','1.1','2026-03-13T17:17:27.664724','2026-03-13T17:17:27.664729','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('fe0e52de-294b-4e11-ab49-ca8e6c1f919f','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RSI 1/2/3 COMET ESCORT 1 0560 V1.0','This is a Rosetta Radio Science data set, collected during the COMET ESCORT 1 phase 2014-11-20 to 2015-03-10. It is a Global Gravity measurement at the comet 67P and covers the time 2015-02-02T16:53:50.000 to 2015-02-02T22:45:14.500.','public','2026-03-13T17:21:00.483488','2026-03-13T17:21:00.483494','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','7effd1c8-fa07-4a49-9cf0-10abbe136090','NASA Data.json','a097b21209f94c1f71d5572b24e364cba525dd07711891b40ad39ac6dfb2d100','1.1','2026-03-13T17:21:00.483488','2026-03-13T17:21:00.483494','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('fe19da99-aa2f-4e27-a50a-fdc2f641a027','MARS EXPRESS MARS MRS 1/2/3 EXTENDED MISSION 4 3475 V1.0','This is a Mars Express Radio Science data set, collected during the extended mission phase 2013-01-01 to 2014-12-31. It is a Global Gravity measurement and covers the time 2013-02-03T09:08:21.000 to 2013-02-03T11:01:09.500.','public','2026-03-13T19:14:45.082582','2026-03-13T19:14:45.082587','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','682a5214-dfb6-4092-a04f-5bb0d83de2c7','NASA Data.json','c19bf70af7d010131d5807a75a8abd8d4902848907ec5e4878f241024f14dacb','1.1','2026-03-13T19:14:45.082582','2026-03-13T19:14:45.082587','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('fe2348b5-6c04-48cb-92a9-40d139ed1b7c','Coral Bleaching & Recovery Observations using Structure-from-Motion (SfM) Models from Main Hawaiian Islands Fixed Sites Surveyed from 2019 to 2021','Coral adult demographic data described in this dataset are derived from the GIS analysis of benthic photomosaic imagery. This data includes coral species identification, bleaching extent and severity, colony diameter, perimeter, and planar size.  The source imagery was collected using a Structure from Motion (SfM) approach during in-water surveys conducted by divers and is documented and described separately. The data was collected by the NOAA Pacific Islands Fisheries Science Center (PIFSC) Ecosystem Sciences Division (ESD; formerly the Coral Reef Ecosystem Division) and [on Hawaii Island] in partnership with State of Hawaii Department of Land and Natural Resources (DLNR), Division of Aquatic Resources (DAR) during the 2019 bleaching event in the Main Hawaiian Islands, and in subsequent years (2020, 2021) to assess recovery. The SfM surveys were conducted at fixed sites ranging in depth from 18-52\'. Sites were photographed using underwater cameras for later processing using one of two SfM approaches: using a spiral swim pattern (where divers take images continuously in a circular pattern covering a circle of 12m diameter), or within a defined box where divers swam back and forth to cover a 10 x 10m area. The photographs were processed using Agisoft Metashape software to generate orthomosaic images that were analyzed in ArcGIS for adult coral colony demographic metrics. Data was collected for each site within at least 10 randomly generated 0.49m2 quadrats. Additional quadrats were analyzed if necessary until the sample sizes per species of interest were met. If a species had very low density at a given site (< 10 patches recorded within the first 10 quadrats), it was dropped from further observations. However, the data for these patches remains in the raw data in order to provide presence/absence data. Therefore, data should be carefully analyzed to ensure accurate species density calculations are done. Two datasets are provided: an annotations file which provides coral demographic information of 6 target species at 12 fixed sites across 3 years, as well as a site metadata file which describes the site and surveys which were used to generate models for which annotation data was derived.\n\n Six species were assessed: Montipora capitata (MCAP), Montipora patula (MPAT), Porites lichen (PLIC), Porites lobata (PLOB), Porites lutea (PLUT), and Pocillopora meandrina (PMEA).  Annotations included coral species identification, maximum diameter measurement, planar area measurement, morphology, and, for sites surveyed in 2019, bleaching extent and bleaching severity. Each coral was annotated at the patch level, and patches composing individual colonies, also known as genets, were assigned a unique genet ID number. The same coral patches were tracked over each time point, unless mortality of a coral patch occurred.\n\nNote an update in methodology: The data was collected in two stages. During the first stage of data collection that was completed in 2021, for each coral patch, (>= 5cm in diameter), maximum diameter, ID (to lowest taxonomic level), morphology, bleaching extent (% of the patch with reduced pigmentation), and bleaching severity (1-3 from least to most severe) were recorded. In 2023 the methodology was updated for the second stage of data collection; the updated dataset includes measures of planar area and a \"genet\" (colony) identification column. The 2023 dataset was also collected following an update to the model process methodology (see Lineage).   Users should refer to the most updated dataset published in 2023.','public','2026-03-21T23:13:32.020531','2026-03-21T23:13:32.020537',NULL,NULL,NULL,'f59491a7-9eb5-49c6-858e-65b36f0665c7','NMFS PIFSC',NULL,NULL,'2026-03-21T23:13:32.020531','2026-03-21T23:13:32.020537',NULL,NULL,NULL,'noaa-gov'),('fe2fc89c-6ad9-40eb-9290-9aab003dc7ca','MARS EXPRESS MARS MRS 1/2/3                                     EXTENDED MISSION 8 4321 V1.0','This is a Mars Express                                     Radio Science data set, collected                                     during the extended mission phase                                     2023-01-01 to 2023-12-31.                                     It is a Occultation                                     measurement and covers the time                                     2023-08-13T03:01:00.200 to                                     2023-08-13T03:23:08.000.','public','2026-03-13T19:53:59.034685','2026-03-13T19:53:59.034690','geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','1f5b10ab-4ba4-4787-9bc0-1b744fca5751','NASA Data.json','0c19a3adfa2db24a0f725e427298c4aa84c8ec09750f5c3ab4723acc0c5aa50f','1.1','2026-03-13T19:53:59.034685','2026-03-13T19:53:59.034690','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('fe710a2c-9f1b-4c0b-9542-0c07c70f3cd6','Changes to CTA Ridership Datasets - 3/20/2026','Changes to CTA Ridership Datasets','public','2026-03-29T04:50:37.147198','2026-03-29T04:50:37.147203','data.cityofchicago.org','Maria Fiorillo',NULL,'04a612cb-e049-4de5-84a5-91f7f1c633d3','Chicago JSON','fde252258763837b8756f34874970e8a8481a6e96ef06e5e8437d6ae2593e75b','1.1','2026-03-29T04:50:37.147198','2026-03-29T04:50:37.147203','Transportation',NULL,0,'city-of-chicago'),('fe7b53ec-2cdf-488f-9286-e1c35a315e36','BLM ID Grazing Allotments','This feature class depicts the boundaries of the livestock grazing allotments under the jurisdiction of the Idaho Bureau of Land Management. A pasture is a sub-unit of a grazing allotment; each allotment is comprised of at least one pasture. An allotment is an area of land designated and managed for grazing of livestock. An allotment may include private and state lands, in addition to public lands under the jurisdiction of the Bureau of Land Management and/or other federal agencies. All allotments and pastures are recorded and tracked in BLM\'s Rangeland Administrative System (RAS). This GIS feature class provides a spatial component to pastures and allotments.  For more information contact us at blm_id_stateoffice@blm.gov.','public','2026-03-25T12:34:28.715694','2026-03-25T12:34:28.715700','Bureau of Land Management','Bureau of Land Management, id_so_information','010:04','f19e2f13-822f-466b-bc2d-d2ac2ac10e32','DOI BLM DCAT-US','0a2a2849f4bfce3b3b29f9c9ae69205671951b9ecdc71186749ecaea65080b68','1.1','2026-03-25T12:34:28.715694','2026-03-25T12:34:28.715700','geospatial','010:000',0,'doi-gov'),('fe7ef723-2567-49aa-b1d2-7f326623471b','AIRS/Aqua Granule map product V005 (AIRXAMAP) at GES DISC','The Atmospheric Infrared Sounder (AIRS) is a grating spectrometer (R = 1200) aboard the second Earth Observing System (EOS) polar-orbiting platform, EOS Aqua. In combination with the Advanced Microwave Sounding Unit (AMSU) and the Humidity Sounder for Brazil (HSB), AIRS constitutes an innovative atmospheric sounding group of visible, infrared, and microwave sensors. An AIRS granule has been set as 6 minutes of data, 30 footprints cross track by 45 lines along track. The AIRS Granule Map Product consists of images of granule coverage in PDF and JPG format. The images are daily ones but updated every 6 minutes to capture any new available granule. Granules are assembled by ascending, descending, in north and south hemisphere, and the maps are in global cylindrical projection and satellite projection for better view.','public','2026-03-13T18:49:39.533102','2026-03-13T18:49:39.533108','NASA/GSFC/SED/ESD/TISL/GESDISC','Earthdata Forum','026:00','3a90df4d-5ca5-4f8f-92e2-3e0f8604df39','NASA Data.json','630eb25f60ff67350321a3093a94dcae8be0b7867a5af894bb6e804e053f93c9','1.1','2026-03-13T18:49:39.533102','2026-03-13T18:49:39.533108','Earth Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('fe92c702-b5ae-4bf6-ad96-83c5a09bcf3f','BLM ID CADNSDI PLSS Second Division',' second division of the PLSS is quarter, quarter-quarter, sixteenth or government lot division of the PLSS. The second and third divisions are combined into this feature class as an intentional de-normalization of the PLSS hierarchical data. The polygons in this feature class represent the smallest division to the sixteenth that has been defined for the first division. For example In some cases sections have only been divided to the quarter. Divisions below the sixteenth are in the Special Survey or Parcel Feature Class.  For more information contact us at blm_id_stateoffice@blm.gov.','public','2026-03-19T11:31:30.097673','2026-03-19T11:31:30.097679','Bureau of Land Management','Bureau of Land Management, blm_id_infoaccesscenter','010:04','686f3f26-04fd-4e37-921b-cd34011d5e61','DOI BLM DCAT-US','926d7e5ca9b4dcb83f721d49cae9ecb52963cbb8e9ce90a5a6d5a80f0b0b259e','1.1','2026-03-19T11:31:30.097673','2026-03-19T11:31:30.097679','geospatial','010:000',0,'doi-gov'),('fe9d7a0f-cdcb-4818-bcb0-21b5bb5f261c','Key Watersheds in the Southeast Coast I&M Network (SECN) - Custom Drainage Basin Boundaries','This dataset contains custom drainage basin polygons that are composed of the various watersheds (HUC-10) or subwatersheds (HUC-12) that contain water features that flow or contribute to those that flow directly into SECN parks. The drainage basins have attributes that state the HUC-2/Region, HUC-4/Subregion, HUC-6/Basin, and HUC-8/Subbasin numbers and names as well as the HUC level that each drainage basin is composed of (Watershed or Subwatershed) for the particular park that they are associated with. The drainage basin polygons are essentially the merged versions of the individual watersheds/subwatersheds that they contain. If the individual watershed/subwatershed boundaries within a drainage basin are needed, please refer to the dataset titled \'Key Watersheds in the Southeast Coast I&M Network (SECN) - Individual Watershed/Subwatershed Boundaries\' in order to access the individual units that are found within each drainage basin. Note: for the purposes of this dataset and for the remainder of this metadata file, the term \"watershed\" will refer to individual watershed/subwatershed units while the term \"drainage basin\" will refer to the collection of individual watershed/subwatershed units that contribute to the condition of each park.','public','2026-03-26T05:32:59.705100','2026-03-26T05:32:59.705106','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','ab954350-13d8-4794-8ce9-27914c91b5e5','DOI NPS DCAT-US','bb5cf4ab1879a11ef64142f939447d893613ec2b460df977bf951bb358e82de4','1.1','2026-03-26T05:32:59.705100','2026-03-26T05:32:59.705106','geospatial','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('feb83470-991a-4841-9cb5-3eb9360249f4','MPF LANDER MARS IMP STEREO-DERIVED 3D POSITIONS V1.0','Three-dimensional position informationfor pixels in IMP (Imager for Mars Pathfinder) stereo-pair images.','public','2026-03-13T17:51:05.562792','2026-03-13T17:51:05.562798','Geosciences','Planetary Data System','026:00','80f00fda-2b86-4aa8-98b1-fb9635d70121','NASA Data.json','347cb79cb332c74fb29d80c21f043b5df3bef416db0782904d31601dee4ef255','1.1','2026-03-13T17:51:05.562792','2026-03-13T17:51:05.562798','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('fefb03d8-41fb-49e8-88c4-dfe9ae881744','Continuous Fixed Station Water Quality Measurements in Cape Lookout National Seashore, April 2009 (Certified)','This dataset represents continuous water quality measurements that were taken at a fixed point in Cape Lookout National Seashore during the month of April, 2009 as a part of the Fixed Station Water Quality Monitoring protocol that was developed by the Southeast Coast I&M Network (SECN). The measurements were taken by a YSI 6600 ESD Multi-Parameter Long Term Water Quality Monitoring Datasonde unit that serves as the standard fixed station water quality monitoring equipment for all similar operations conducted by the SECN. The following parameters were measured at 15 minute intervals during the time period that has been specified: Water Temperature, Specific Conductivity, Salinity, Dissolved Oxygen (DO), DO Concentration, Shallow Depth, pH Level, and Turbidity. Any anomalies noted regarding these parameters have also been noted in separate fields.  Please note that these measurements have been certified by network personnel.','public','2026-03-26T05:28:29.069093','2026-03-26T05:28:29.069098','National Park Service','NPS IRMA Help','010:24','d9d6f71d-2fa0-42bb-b4ac-4a7805687cbb','DOI NPS DCAT-US','f8e82f4f5f25fb4f61ae633daa662f35ce0591d8706f3e7e4e528cc071ef0c90','1.1','2026-03-26T05:28:29.069093','2026-03-26T05:28:29.069098','Vector Dataset','010:118',0,'doi-gov'),('ff0f4ff0-09b4-4067-bbea-9f9f921a9a05','Genes Required for Survival in Microgravity Revealed by Genome-Wide Yeast Deletion Collections Cultured during Spaceflight','Spaceflight is a unique environment with profound effects on biological systems including tissue redistribution and musculoskeletal stresses. However, the more subtle biological effects of spaceflight on cells and organisms are difficult to measure in a systematic, unbiased manner. Here we test the utility of the molecularly barcoded yeast deletion collection to provide a quantitative assessment of the effects of microgravity on a model organism. We developed robust hardware to screen, in parallel, the complete collection of ~4800 homozygous and ~5900 heterozygous (including ~1100 single-copy deletions of essential genes) yeast deletion strains, each carrying unique DNA that acts as strain identifiers. We compared strain fitness for the homozygous and heterozygous yeast deletion collections grown in spaceflight and ground, as well as plus and minus hyperosmolar sodium chloride, providing a second additive stressor. The genome-wide sensitivity profiles obtained from these treatments were then queried for their similarity to a compendium of drugs whose effects on the yeast collection have been previously reported. We found that the effects of spaceflight have high concordance with the effects of DNA-damaging agents and changes in redox state, suggesting mechanisms by which spaceflight may negatively affect cell fitness.','public','2026-03-13T19:18:46.636497','2026-03-13T19:18:46.636504','Open Science Data Repository','Open Science Data Repository Help Desk','026:00','538494a8-f1b9-4a6e-81b1-68ffbbea5133','NASA Data.json','0434aa24e0e44208bd5ab24ffdf4f151440933b2e7e8837ab0dbd6603b788391','1.1','2026-03-13T19:18:46.636497','2026-03-13T19:18:46.636504','Biological and Physical Sciences','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('ff152bcd-ae26-4e86-8ccf-e925b8634463','NRC 823S','NRC Heath Center Consent for Influenza Immunization. Fillable form in Adobe Portable Document Format (PDF) with information submitted by NRC stakeholder - licensee, applicant, or NRC employee/contractor.','non-public','2026-03-20T19:43:52.068637','2026-03-20T19:43:52.068643','Nuclear Regulatory Commission','Ilka Solorio','429:00','4d576212-8425-4aa4-b7a5-fe15384fdebd','NRC Data.json Harvest Source','5b1304ffec47d99fb24db9736d605dffc313480d7ad82777e221935d8aa509e8','1.1','2026-03-20T19:43:52.068637','2026-03-20T19:43:52.068643',NULL,'000:000',0,'nrc-gov'),('ff3e821a-d92b-4256-9b6b-6004ad2d102f','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P VIRTIS 3 EXTENSION 2 MTP030 V2.0','This release contains the calibrated data of the VIRTIS instrument on board of the spacecraft Rosetta. This volume contains data from the EXTENSION 2 MTP030 phase, which occurred from 2016-06-01 to 2016-06-29 when at the vicinity of comet 67P. This data set V2.0 supersedes V1.0. It includes major updates on the data and documentation.','public','2026-03-13T18:14:37.151015','2026-03-13T18:14:37.151022','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','bd911a44-f263-4cef-93b9-f3667f0d35e6','NASA Data.json','4c25521ec6c85815f0fb8c77f3816ed23fb6e9e191b5f39e70b93767fe1effb7','1.1','2026-03-13T18:14:37.151015','2026-03-13T18:14:37.151022','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('ff9cbfe1-7cad-4726-8e33-99cc238364d8','ROSETTA-ORBITER 67P RPCMAG 2 ESC3 RAW V9.0','This dataset contains EDITED RAW DATA (CODMAC LEVEL 2) of theCOMET ESCORT 3 Phase from July 1,2016 until October 20, 2016of the ROSETTA orbiter magnetometer RPCMAG. Observations are done inthe vicinity of comet 67P/CHURYUMOV-GERASIMENKO 1 (1969 R1).The current version of the dataset is V9.0.The difference to the datasets of earlier versions is mainly a significantlyimproved sensor temperature model, more detailed documentation about magneticdisturbance sources, more data handling information for the user andalso an improved quality flagging system.This applies mainly to CALIBRATED and RESAMPLED datasets. The RAW dataset,however, has been updated as well in order provide all datasets at thesame stage, although RAW data proper did not change.','public','2026-03-13T18:47:03.683090','2026-03-13T18:47:03.683096','Small Bodies','Planetary Data System','026:00','8d3f3810-5f3a-40b1-a039-d1f08a37a9ec','NASA Data.json','82ea65879be5797e68dcfaa3c3ba7dfc63491abee0cf9810a1f76165f8e349a3','1.1','2026-03-13T18:47:03.683090','2026-03-13T18:47:03.683096','Planetary Science','026:000',0,'nasa-gov'),('ffbfd1a2-e266-4982-bcb5-e8aae71ea88c','Walton-Smith CTD, WS15264, WS15264_WS15264sta41, 2015-09-23, 25.7333N 81.575W','Walton-Smith Conductivity, Temperature, Depth (CTD) - WS15264 - WS15264_WS15264sta41 - 2015-09-23 - 25.7333N 81.575W. Hydrographic Measurements in the Gulf of Mexico. flags: 1 = good; 3 =  mean ÃÂ± 3*standard deviation; 4 = mean ÃÂ± 5*standard deviation; 9 = missing. other','public','2026-03-26T19:14:46.156498','2026-03-26T19:14:46.156504',NULL,NULL,NULL,'e715912f-6861-41a0-a0ad-56a8c61d012a','ioos',NULL,NULL,'2026-03-26T19:14:46.156498','2026-03-26T19:14:46.156504',NULL,NULL,NULL,'noaa-gov'),('ffd87756-86b0-421d-b6a7-3c4e03f9cb1f','Data from: Application of visual soil evaluations in a semiarid region','<p dir=\"ltr\">A half-day workshop exploring visual soil evaluation methods was developed for land managers by the USDA-ARS Northern Great Plains Research Laboratory, Mandan, ND USA. Outcomes from workshops held between 2018 and 2023 found that attendees were able to quickly acquire skills necessary to effectively apply the Visual Evaluation of Soil Structure (VESS) assessment method under conditions unique to the workshop. Annual measurements of soil properties and crop yield were conducted on five cropping systems with different management but common soil type and compared to VESS assessments. Soil measurements included soil bulk density, sorptivity, soil pH, soil organic matter, soluble C, soluble N, and C mineralization, while crop measurements included spring wheat grain and straw yield. Field measurements of sorptivity were conducted at the same time soil samples were collected from the 0-10 cm depth for laboratory analyses. Soil pH was estimated from a 1:1 soil-water mixture, soil organic matter by loss-on-ignition, soluble C and N from water extracts, and C mineralization using a 24-hr incubation. Spring wheat grain and straw yield were measured using standard methods for hand sampling and biomass processing. Visual Evaluation of Soil Structure assessments were conducted by workshop attendees and the instructor. Data may be used to understand how visual soil evaluations conducted by land managers compare with traditional soil and crop measurements. Data are generally applicable to cropland under a semiarid to sub-humid continental climate for the following USDA soil types: Grassna, Linton, Mandan, Temvik, Williams, and Wilton.</p>','public','2026-03-13T22:48:25.977028','2026-03-13T22:48:25.977035','Agricultural Research Service','Liebig, Mark A.','005:18','3d803499-c469-4eca-bf47-44c355b79ee0','USDA JSON','1abda70604fb11087ee6cdc8bf631bb3433dde7e9b8963ebf285b67e6d852ec5','1.1','2026-03-13T22:48:25.977028','2026-03-13T22:48:25.977035',NULL,'005:040',0,'usda-gov');
